// Auto-generated for the Unit Board — 學測6000字 Level 6
window.L6_DASHBOARD_UNITS = [{"unit":1,"theme":"abbreviate – aesthetic","cards":[{"w":"abbreviate","p":"v.","d":"to make a word or name shorter","c":"縮寫；使簡短","s":"Many students abbreviate long words in their notes, so they can write down everything the teacher says in class.","t":"許多學生在筆記裡把長單字縮寫，這樣他們就能寫下老師上課說的每一句話。","h":1},{"w":"abbreviation","p":"n.","d":"a short form of a word or name","c":"縮寫；略語","s":"'Dept.' is a common abbreviation of 'department', and you can often see it on signs in big office buildings.","t":"Dept. 是 department 常見的縮寫，你常常可以在大型辦公大樓的標示上看到它。"},{"w":"be abbreviated to","p":"v.phr.","d":"to be made shorter as","c":"被縮寫為","s":"The name World Health Organization is abbreviated to WHO, and most people only know it by these three letters.","t":"世界衛生組織這個名稱被縮寫為WHO，大多數人只知道這三個字母。","a":"is abbreviated to"},{"w":"abbreviated","p":"adj.","d":"made shorter than usual","c":"縮短的；簡短的","s":"Because of the heavy rain, the school held an abbreviated sports day that ended before lunch instead of in the evening.","t":"因為大雨，學校舉辦了縮短版的運動會，在午餐前就結束，而不是到傍晚。"},{"w":"abide","p":"v.","d":"to accept and follow a rule; to bear","c":"遵守；忍受","s":"Everyone who lives in this building has to abide by the rules, so no loud music is allowed after ten at night.","t":"住在這棟大樓的每個人都必須遵守規定，所以晚上十點以後不准大聲放音樂。","h":1},{"w":"abide by","p":"v.phr.","d":"to obey a rule, law, or decision","c":"遵守；服從","s":"All players must abide by the rules of the game, or the referee will ask them to leave the field.","t":"所有球員都必須遵守比賽規則，否則裁判會要求他們離開球場。"},{"w":"cannot abide","p":"v.phr.","d":"to dislike something very much","c":"無法忍受","s":"My mother cannot abide people who talk loudly on their phones in quiet places like libraries and hospitals.","t":"我媽媽無法忍受在圖書館和醫院這類安靜場所大聲講電話的人。"},{"w":"law-abiding","p":"adj.","d":"always obeying the law","c":"守法的","s":"Most people in this small town are law-abiding citizens, so the police station is usually very quiet.","t":"這個小鎮大部分的人都是守法的公民，所以警察局通常很安靜。"},{"w":"aboriginal","p":"adj.","d":"belonging to the first people who lived in a place","c":"原住民的；土著的","s":"The museum in Taitung shows aboriginal clothes and tools, and visitors can learn how the tribes lived long ago.","t":"台東的博物館展示原住民的服裝和工具，參觀者可以了解部落很久以前的生活方式。","h":1},{"w":"Aborigine","p":"n.","d":"one of the first people who lived in Australia","c":"（澳洲）原住民","s":"The Aborigines of Australia have lived on the land for more than forty thousand years, and they have many ancient songs.","t":"澳洲的原住民已經在這片土地上生活了四萬多年，他們有許多古老的歌謠。","a":"Aborigines"},{"w":"aboriginal culture","p":"n.phr.","d":"the traditions and way of life of native people","c":"原住民文化","s":"Many young people are trying to protect aboriginal culture, so they learn the old songs and dances from their grandparents.","t":"許多年輕人努力保護原住民文化，所以他們向祖父母學習古老的歌曲和舞蹈。"},{"w":"origin","p":"n.","d":"the place or point where something begins","c":"起源；來源","s":"The origin of this festival is not clear, but some people say it started more than three hundred years ago.","t":"這個節慶的起源並不清楚，但有些人說它始於三百多年前。"},{"w":"abound","p":"v.","d":"to exist in very large numbers","c":"大量存在；盛產","s":"Wild flowers abound in the mountains in spring, so many families go hiking there to take pictures.","t":"春天時山上到處都是野花，所以許多家庭會去那裡健行拍照。","h":1},{"w":"abound with","p":"v.phr.","d":"to have a lot of something","c":"富於；充滿","s":"The lakes in this area abound with fish, and that is why so many people come here to go fishing on weekends.","t":"這一帶的湖泊有很多魚，這就是為什麼週末有那麼多人來這裡釣魚。"},{"w":"abounding","p":"adj.","d":"existing in great amounts","c":"大量的；充滿的","s":"The children were full of abounding energy after the long holiday, and they ran around the playground all morning.","t":"長假過後孩子們充滿旺盛的精力，整個早上都在操場上跑來跑去。"},{"w":"abstraction","p":"n.","d":"a general idea that is not about one real thing","c":"抽象概念；抽象","s":"For young children, numbers are an abstraction, so teachers often use apples and candies to help them count.","t":"對年幼的孩子來說，數字是一種抽象概念，所以老師常用蘋果和糖果幫助他們數數。","h":1},{"w":"abstract","p":"adj.","d":"based on ideas, not on real things","c":"抽象的","s":"Words like 'peace' and 'love' are abstract, and it is hard to draw a simple picture of them.","t":"像「和平」和「愛」這類字是抽象的，很難為它們畫出一張簡單的圖。"},{"w":"abstract art","p":"n.phr.","d":"art that uses shapes and colors instead of real objects","c":"抽象藝術","s":"The museum has a new room for abstract art, where the paintings are full of bright colors and strange shapes.","t":"博物館有一間新的抽象藝術展間，裡面的畫作充滿鮮豔的色彩和奇特的形狀。"},{"w":"abstract","p":"n.","d":"a short summary of a report or article","c":"摘要","s":"Before reading the whole science report, you should read the short abstract on the first page to see the main idea.","t":"在閱讀整份科學報告之前，你應該先讀第一頁的簡短摘要，了解主要內容。"},{"w":"abundance","p":"n.","d":"a very large amount of something","c":"豐富；大量","s":"There is an abundance of fresh fruit at the market in summer, so prices are usually lower then.","t":"夏天市場上有大量的新鮮水果，所以那時候價格通常比較低。","h":1},{"w":"in abundance","p":"phr.","d":"in large amounts; more than enough","c":"大量地；充足地","s":"During the rainy season water is found in abundance, but in winter the farmers often worry about their dry fields.","t":"雨季時水非常充足，但到了冬天農夫常常擔心田地乾旱。"},{"w":"abundant","p":"adj.","d":"existing in large amounts; more than enough","c":"豐富的；充足的","s":"Taiwan has abundant rain in summer, so the reservoirs are usually full by the end of September.","t":"台灣夏天雨量充沛，所以到九月底水庫通常都是滿的。"},{"w":"abundantly","p":"adv.","d":"in large amounts; very","c":"大量地；十分","s":"The teacher made it abundantly clear that phones are not allowed during the test, so everyone put theirs away.","t":"老師說得十分清楚，考試時不准使用手機，所以大家都把手機收起來了。"},{"w":"academy","p":"n.","d":"a school or college for special training","c":"學院；專科學校","s":"My cousin studies at a police academy in Taoyuan, where students must get up at six every morning to exercise.","t":"我表哥在桃園的警察學校讀書，那裡的學生每天早上六點就得起床運動。","h":1},{"w":"academic","p":"adj.","d":"connected with studying and schools","c":"學術的；學業的","s":"Her academic performance improved a lot this year because she joined a study group with her classmates.","t":"她今年的學業表現進步很多，因為她和同學組了讀書會。"},{"w":"academic","p":"n.","d":"a teacher or researcher at a university","c":"學者；大學教師","s":"Many academics from different universities attended the meeting, and they shared new research about climate change.","t":"許多來自不同大學的學者參加了會議，並分享了有關氣候變遷的新研究。","a":"academics"},{"w":"academically","p":"adv.","d":"in a way connected with study","c":"在學業上","s":"Although Ben is quiet in class, he is very strong academically and often gets the best grades in science.","t":"雖然阿班上課很安靜，但他在學業上很強，自然科常常拿最高分。"},{"w":"accessory","p":"n.","d":"an extra thing like a bag, belt, or phone case","c":"配件；飾品","s":"She bought a pink phone case as an accessory, and it matches the color of her school bag perfectly.","t":"她買了一個粉紅色手機殼當作配件，它和她書包的顏色完全搭配。","h":1},{"w":"accessory","p":"n.","d":"a person who helps someone do a crime","c":"從犯；共犯","s":"The man who drove the car for the thieves was punished as an accessory, although he never went inside the bank.","t":"那名替小偷開車的男子以從犯身分受罰，雖然他從未進入銀行。"},{"w":"access","p":"n.","d":"the right or chance to enter or use something","c":"進入；使用權","s":"Students can get access to the school library on weekends if they show their student card at the door.","t":"學生週末只要在門口出示學生證，就可以進入學校圖書館。"},{"w":"accessible","p":"adj.","d":"easy to reach, enter, or use","c":"容易到達的；無障礙的","s":"The new train station is accessible to people in wheelchairs because there are elevators at every exit.","t":"新火車站對坐輪椅的人來說很方便進出，因為每個出口都有電梯。"},{"w":"acclaim","p":"n.","d":"strong public praise","c":"讚譽；喝采","s":"The singer's new album received great acclaim from fans, and it stayed at the top of the music charts for weeks.","t":"這位歌手的新專輯獲得歌迷極高的讚譽，在音樂排行榜上蟬聯冠軍好幾週。","h":1},{"w":"acclaim","p":"v.","d":"to praise someone or something in public","c":"稱讚；讚揚","s":"Critics around the world acclaimed the young director's first film, and it won three prizes last year.","t":"世界各地的影評人都讚揚這位年輕導演的第一部電影，它去年還得了三個獎。","a":"acclaimed"},{"w":"critically acclaimed","p":"adj.phr.","d":"praised a lot by people who judge books or films","c":"備受好評的","s":"This critically acclaimed novel has been translated into twenty languages, and it will soon be made into a movie.","t":"這本備受好評的小說已被翻譯成二十種語言，而且很快就要被拍成電影。"},{"w":"acclaimed","p":"adj.","d":"praised by many people","c":"備受讚譽的；著名的","s":"An acclaimed chef from Japan opened a new restaurant downtown, so it is almost impossible to get a table this month.","t":"一位備受讚譽的日本主廚在市中心開了新餐廳，所以這個月幾乎訂不到位。"},{"w":"accordance","p":"n.","d":"the state of following a rule or wish","c":"依照；一致","s":"The old house was built in accordance with the safety rules of that time, but it needs a lot of repairs now.","t":"那棟老房子是依照當時的安全規定建造的，但現在需要大量整修。","h":1},{"w":"accordingly","p":"adv.","d":"in a way that fits the situation; so","c":"相應地；因此","s":"The weather report says it will be cold tomorrow, so please dress accordingly and bring a warm jacket.","t":"氣象報告說明天會很冷，所以請適當地穿著，並帶一件保暖外套。","h":1},{"w":"in accordance with","p":"phr.","d":"following a rule, law, or wish","c":"依照；根據","s":"In accordance with his wishes, the old man's money was given to the children's hospital after he died.","t":"依照老先生的遺願，他過世後錢被捐給了兒童醫院。","a":"In accordance with"},{"w":"accord","p":"n.","d":"an official agreement","c":"協議；一致","s":"The two countries signed a peace accord last year, and since then their people have been able to travel freely.","t":"兩國去年簽署了和平協議，從那以後兩國人民就能自由往來。"},{"w":"of one's own accord","p":"phr.","d":"without being asked or forced","c":"自願地；主動地","s":"Nobody told him to do it, but Tom cleaned the whole classroom of his own accord after the party.","t":"沒有人叫他做，但湯姆在派對後主動把整間教室打掃乾淨。","a":"of his own accord"},{"w":"according to","p":"phr.","d":"as said or shown by","c":"根據","s":"According to the weather report, a strong typhoon will reach Taiwan on Friday, so classes may be canceled.","t":"根據氣象報告，一個強烈颱風將在星期五抵達台灣，所以可能會停課。","a":"According to"},{"w":"accountable","p":"adj.","d":"responsible for your actions and able to explain them","c":"應負責的","s":"Leaders should be accountable for their decisions, so they must explain to the public why they spent the money.","t":"領導者應該為自己的決定負責，所以他們必須向大眾解釋為什麼花了那筆錢。","h":1},{"w":"be held accountable","p":"v.phr.","d":"to be made responsible for something bad","c":"被追究責任","s":"Drivers who cause accidents after drinking should be held accountable for the harm they do to other people.","t":"酒後肇事的駕駛應該為他們對別人造成的傷害被追究責任。"},{"w":"accountability","p":"n.","d":"the duty to explain and be responsible for your actions","c":"責任；問責","s":"The new rules bring more accountability to the government, because every spending plan must now be shown online.","t":"新規定讓政府更具問責性，因為現在每項支出計畫都必須公布在網路上。"},{"w":"account for","p":"v.phr.","d":"to explain the reason for something","c":"說明；解釋（原因）","s":"Can you account for the missing money, or should we call the manager to check the records again?","t":"你能說明那筆不見的錢的去向嗎？還是我們該請經理再檢查一次紀錄？"},{"w":"accumulate","p":"v.","d":"to collect more and more of something over time","c":"累積；積聚","s":"If you save a little money every week, you will accumulate enough to buy a new bike by the summer.","t":"如果你每週存一點錢，到夏天你就會累積足夠的錢買一台新腳踏車。","h":1},{"w":"accumulation","p":"n.","d":"the slow growth of an amount of something","c":"累積；堆積","s":"The accumulation of snow on the roads made driving dangerous, so the mountain highway was closed for two days.","t":"道路上的積雪讓開車變得危險，所以山區公路封閉了兩天。","h":1},{"w":"accumulated","p":"adj.","d":"collected over a period of time","c":"累積的","s":"Thanks to her accumulated experience as a nurse, she knew exactly what to do when the old man fainted.","t":"多虧她當護士累積的經驗，當那位老先生昏倒時，她完全知道該怎麼做。"},{"w":"cumulative","p":"adj.","d":"increasing by adding one amount after another","c":"累計的；漸增的","s":"The cumulative effect of sleeping too little every night can make students feel tired and sick.","t":"每晚睡太少的累積效應會讓學生感到疲倦甚至生病。"},{"w":"accusation","p":"n.","d":"a statement saying someone did something wrong","c":"指控；控告","s":"The student denied the accusation that he had cheated on the test, and he asked the teacher to check the video.","t":"那位學生否認他考試作弊的指控，並要求老師查看錄影。","h":1},{"w":"make an accusation","p":"v.phr.","d":"to say that someone did something wrong","c":"提出指控","s":"You should not make an accusation without any proof, because it can hurt a person's good name.","t":"你不應該在沒有任何證據的情況下提出指控，因為那可能傷害一個人的名聲。"},{"w":"accuse","p":"v.","d":"to say that someone has done something wrong","c":"指控；指責","s":"The shop owner accused the boy of stealing a candy bar, but the camera showed that he had paid for it.","t":"店老闆指控那個男孩偷了一條巧克力棒，但監視器顯示他已經付了錢。","a":"accused"},{"w":"be accused of","p":"v.phr.","d":"to be blamed for doing something wrong","c":"被指控…","s":"The famous singer was accused of copying another artist's song, but she said the music was her own idea.","t":"那位知名歌手被指控抄襲別的歌手的歌，但她說那首曲子是她自己的點子。","a":"was accused of"},{"w":"accustom","p":"v.","d":"to make someone get used to something","c":"使習慣","s":"Parents should accustom their children to going to bed early, so that they can wake up easily for school.","t":"父母應該讓孩子習慣早睡，這樣他們上學時才能輕鬆起床。","h":1},{"w":"be accustomed to","p":"v.phr.","d":"to be used to something","c":"習慣於","s":"My grandfather is accustomed to getting up at five, so he never needs an alarm clock even on holidays.","t":"我爺爺習慣五點起床，所以即使放假他也從來不需要鬧鐘。","a":"is accustomed to"},{"w":"accustom oneself to","p":"v.phr.","d":"to make yourself get used to something","c":"使自己習慣於","s":"It took me a whole month to accustom myself to the cold weather after I moved to Canada for school.","t":"我搬到加拿大念書後，花了整整一個月才讓自己習慣寒冷的天氣。","a":"accustom myself to"},{"w":"accustomed","p":"adj.","d":"usual; normal for a person","c":"慣常的；通常的","s":"Grandpa sat in his accustomed chair by the window and read the newspaper, just as he did every morning.","t":"爺爺坐在窗邊他慣常坐的椅子上看報紙，就像他每天早上一樣。"},{"w":"custom","p":"n.","d":"a traditional way of doing something","c":"習俗；風俗","s":"It is a Taiwanese custom to give red envelopes to children during the Lunar New Year holiday.","t":"在農曆新年期間給孩子紅包是台灣的習俗。"},{"w":"acne","p":"n.","d":"red spots on the face, common in teenagers","c":"粉刺；青春痘","s":"Many teenagers suffer from acne, so they wash their faces carefully and try not to eat too much fried food.","t":"許多青少年受青春痘困擾，所以他們會仔細洗臉，並盡量不吃太多油炸食物。","h":1},{"w":"acne cream","p":"n.phr.","d":"a cream that helps clear red spots on the skin","c":"青春痘藥膏","s":"The doctor gave me some acne cream, and after two weeks the red spots on my face were almost gone.","t":"醫生給了我一些青春痘藥膏，兩週後我臉上的紅點幾乎都消失了。"},{"w":"acne-prone","p":"adj.","d":"likely to get red spots easily","c":"易長痘痘的","s":"If you have acne-prone skin, you should choose a light face cream that does not contain any oil.","t":"如果你是容易長痘痘的肌膚，應該選擇不含油的清爽乳液。"},{"w":"acre","p":"n.","d":"a unit for measuring land, about 4,047 square meters","c":"英畝","s":"My uncle owns a farm of fifty acres in the countryside, where he grows rice and raises chickens.","t":"我叔叔在鄉下擁有一座五十英畝的農場，他在那裡種稻和養雞。","a":"acres","h":1},{"w":"acreage","p":"n.","d":"the size of a piece of land","c":"面積；英畝數","s":"The acreage of the national park is huge, so visitors usually need two or three days to see the main areas.","t":"這座國家公園的面積非常大，所以遊客通常需要兩三天才能看完主要區域。"},{"w":"acres of","p":"phr.","d":"a very large area or amount of","c":"大片的；大量的","s":"There were acres of green fields around the old house, and we could not see any other buildings at all.","t":"那棟老房子周圍有大片綠油油的田野，我們完全看不到其他建築物。"},{"w":"adaptation","p":"n.","d":"a film or play made from a book or story","c":"改編作品","s":"The new movie is an adaptation of a popular novel, but fans say the ending is quite different from the book.","t":"這部新電影是一部暢銷小說的改編作品，但書迷說結局和原著差很多。","h":1},{"w":"adaptation","p":"n.","d":"the process of changing to fit a new situation","c":"適應","s":"The thick fur of polar bears is an adaptation to the freezing weather of the Arctic, where it is cold all year.","t":"北極熊厚厚的毛是對北極嚴寒氣候的適應，那裡一整年都很冷。"},{"w":"adapt","p":"v.","d":"to change so that you fit a new place or situation","c":"適應；改編","s":"It took the new students a few weeks to adapt to life in the school dormitory.","t":"新生們花了幾個星期才適應學校宿舍的生活。"},{"w":"adaptable","p":"adj.","d":"able to change easily in new situations","c":"適應力強的","s":"Good workers are adaptable, so they can stay calm and learn quickly when plans suddenly change.","t":"好的員工適應力強，所以計畫突然改變時，他們能保持冷靜並快速學習。"},{"w":"adapter","p":"n.","d":"a small object that lets you connect a plug to a different kind of socket","c":"轉接頭","s":"Don't forget to bring a power adapter when you travel to England, because the plugs there are different.","t":"去英國旅行時別忘了帶電源轉接頭，因為那裡的插頭不一樣。"},{"w":"addiction","p":"n.","d":"the state of not being able to stop doing or taking something","c":"上癮；癮","s":"Phone addiction is a big problem among students, so some schools ask them to put their phones in boxes during class.","t":"手機成癮是學生間的一大問題，所以有些學校要求學生上課時把手機放進盒子裡。","h":1},{"w":"addict","p":"n.","d":"a person who cannot stop doing or taking something","c":"上癮的人","s":"My brother calls himself a coffee addict because he drinks at least four cups every day.","t":"我哥哥自稱是咖啡成癮者，因為他每天至少喝四杯。"},{"w":"be addicted to","p":"v.phr.","d":"to be unable to stop doing or using something","c":"對…上癮","s":"Some children are addicted to video games, and they play for hours without eating or sleeping.","t":"有些孩子對電玩上癮，他們一玩就是好幾個小時，不吃也不睡。","a":"are addicted to"},{"w":"addictive","p":"adj.","d":"making you want more and more of it","c":"使人上癮的","s":"Sugar can be quite addictive, so it is hard for many people to stop eating sweets once they start.","t":"糖可能很容易讓人上癮，所以很多人一開始吃甜食就很難停下來。"},{"w":"administer","p":"v.","d":"to give medicine or a test; to manage","c":"給予（藥物）；實施；管理","s":"Only a nurse or a doctor is allowed to administer this medicine, because the wrong amount can be dangerous.","t":"只有護理師或醫生可以給予這種藥，因為劑量錯誤可能很危險。","h":1},{"w":"administrate","p":"v.","d":"to manage a company, school, or other group","c":"管理；治理","s":"She was hired to administrate the new language center, so she plans the classes and manages the teachers.","t":"她受聘來管理新的語言中心，所以她負責規劃課程和管理老師。","h":1},{"w":"administer a test","p":"v.phr.","d":"to give a test to people","c":"實施測驗","s":"Teachers will administer a test to all the first-year students next Monday to check their English level.","t":"老師們下週一將對所有一年級學生實施測驗，檢查他們的英文程度。"},{"w":"administration","p":"n.","d":"the people or work of managing a school, company, or country","c":"行政；管理部門","s":"The school administration decided to change the lunch time, and the new schedule will start next month.","t":"學校行政單位決定更改午餐時間，新的時間表將從下個月開始。"},{"w":"administrator","p":"n.","d":"a person who manages an office or system","c":"管理人員","s":"If you forget your password, please email the system administrator, and she will help you set a new one.","t":"如果你忘記密碼，請寫信給系統管理員，她會幫你設定新密碼。"},{"w":"administrative","p":"adj.","d":"connected with managing an office or group","c":"行政的；管理的","s":"She does most of the administrative work in the office, such as answering emails and keeping records.","t":"她負責辦公室大部分的行政工作，例如回覆電子郵件和保存紀錄。"},{"w":"admiral","p":"n.","d":"a very high officer in the navy","c":"海軍上將","s":"The admiral gave orders to all the ships, and soon the whole navy was ready to leave the harbor.","t":"海軍上將向所有船艦下達命令，很快整支海軍就準備好離開港口。","h":1},{"w":"rear admiral","p":"n.phr.","d":"a navy officer just below a vice admiral","c":"海軍少將","s":"He became a rear admiral at forty-five, and he was one of the youngest officers ever to reach that rank.","t":"他四十五歲就成為海軍少將，是有史以來升到這個階級最年輕的軍官之一。"},{"w":"admiralty","p":"n.","d":"the government office that controls the navy","c":"海軍部","s":"In old times the British Admiralty was in charge of all the warships and sailors of the country.","t":"在過去，英國海軍部掌管全國所有的軍艦和水手。","a":"Admiralty"},{"w":"adolescence","p":"n.","d":"the time when a child is becoming an adult","c":"青春期","s":"During adolescence, many young people care a lot about what their friends think of them.","t":"在青春期，許多年輕人非常在意朋友對他們的看法。","h":1},{"w":"adolescent","p":"n.","d":"a young person who is becoming an adult; a teenager","c":"青少年","s":"As an adolescent, my brother spent most of his free time playing basketball with his friends after school.","t":"青少年時期，我哥哥放學後大部分的空閒時間都和朋友打籃球。"},{"w":"adolescent","p":"adj.","d":"connected with teenagers","c":"青少年的；青春期的","s":"Adolescent problems such as stress and lack of sleep are common, so the school hired a new counselor this year.","t":"壓力和睡眠不足等青少年的問題很常見，所以學校今年聘請了一位新的輔導老師。","a":"Adolescent"},{"w":"advisory","p":"adj.","d":"giving advice","c":"諮詢的；顧問的","s":"The president formed an advisory group of doctors to help him make decisions about public health.","t":"總統成立了一個醫生諮詢小組，協助他做公共衛生方面的決策。","h":1},{"w":"advisory","p":"n.","d":"an official warning or notice","c":"（官方）警告；公告","s":"The weather bureau issued a heat advisory, so people were told to drink more water and stay indoors at noon.","t":"氣象局發布了高溫警報，所以民眾被告知要多喝水，中午待在室內。"},{"w":"advise","p":"v.","d":"to tell someone what you think they should do","c":"建議；勸告","s":"The doctor advised me to get more sleep and drink less coffee before my exams.","t":"醫生建議我在考試前多睡一點、少喝咖啡。","a":"advised"},{"w":"adviser","p":"n.","d":"a person whose job is to give advice","c":"顧問；指導老師","s":"My school adviser helped me choose the right university courses, and she also wrote me a letter of recommendation.","t":"我的學校輔導老師幫我選擇合適的大學課程，還幫我寫了推薦信。"},{"w":"advice","p":"n.","d":"an opinion about what someone should do","c":"建議；忠告","s":"My grandmother always gives me good advice, so I talk to her whenever I have a problem at school.","t":"我奶奶總是給我很好的建議，所以我在學校遇到問題時都會跟她聊。"},{"w":"aesthetic","p":"adj.","d":"connected with beauty and art","c":"美學的；審美的","s":"The new library is useful, but it also has great aesthetic value because of its beautiful glass walls.","t":"新圖書館很實用，但因為它美麗的玻璃牆，也具有很高的美學價值。","h":1},{"w":"aesthetic","p":"n.","d":"a particular style or idea of beauty","c":"美感；風格","s":"The café has a simple, clean aesthetic, with white walls, wooden tables, and lots of green plants.","t":"這間咖啡館有簡單乾淨的風格，白色牆面、木頭桌子和許多綠色植物。"},{"w":"aesthetics","p":"n.","d":"the study of beauty and art","c":"美學","s":"She is studying aesthetics at university because she wants to understand why people find some things beautiful.","t":"她在大學研讀美學，因為她想了解為什麼人們覺得某些東西很美。"},{"w":"aesthetically","p":"adv.","d":"in a way that is beautiful to look at","c":"在美感上","s":"The new park is aesthetically pleasing, and it also gives children a safe place to play after school.","t":"新公園在視覺上令人賞心悅目，也提供孩子們放學後一個安全的遊戲場所。"}]},{"unit":2,"theme":"affectionate – applaud","cards":[{"w":"affectionate","p":"adj.","d":"showing love and caring in a gentle way","c":"親切的；深情的","s":"My grandmother is very affectionate, and she always hugs us and kisses our cheeks when we visit her.","t":"我奶奶非常慈愛，我們去看她時，她總是擁抱我們並親我們的臉頰。","h":1},{"w":"affection","p":"n.","d":"a feeling of liking and caring for someone","c":"喜愛；感情","s":"The old man looked at his dog with great affection, because they had lived together for fifteen years.","t":"老先生帶著深厚的感情看著他的狗，因為他們已經一起生活了十五年。"},{"w":"affectionately","p":"adv.","d":"in a loving and gentle way","c":"深情地；親暱地","s":"Everyone in the village affectionately calls the kind doctor 'Uncle Lee', even though he is not their real uncle.","t":"村裡每個人都親暱地叫那位好心的醫生「李伯伯」，雖然他不是他們真正的伯伯。"},{"w":"show affection","p":"v.phr.","d":"to let someone see that you love them","c":"表達愛意","s":"Some fathers do not know how to show affection, so they show their love by cooking or fixing things for their children.","t":"有些父親不知道如何表達愛意，所以他們用煮飯或替孩子修東西來表現愛。"},{"w":"affiliate","p":"n.","d":"a smaller group or company that belongs to a bigger one","c":"附屬機構；分會","s":"The TV station in our city is an affiliate of a national network, so it shows many of the same programs.","t":"我們城市的電視台是全國電視網的附屬台，所以它播出許多相同的節目。","h":1},{"w":"affiliate","p":"v.","d":"to connect a group closely with a larger one","c":"使隸屬；使加入","s":"The small hospital decided to affiliate itself with a big university, so it could get better doctors and machines.","t":"那家小醫院決定加入一所大型大學體系，這樣就能得到更好的醫生和設備。"},{"w":"be affiliated with","p":"v.phr.","d":"to be officially connected to a group","c":"隸屬於；與…有關聯","s":"Our school is affiliated with a famous university in Japan, so some of our students can study there for a year.","t":"我們學校隸屬於日本一所著名大學的合作體系，所以有些學生可以去那裡讀一年書。","a":"is affiliated with"},{"w":"affiliation","p":"n.","d":"an official connection with a group","c":"隸屬關係；從屬","s":"The speaker did not mention his political affiliation, because he wanted people to listen to his ideas first.","t":"那位講者沒有提到他的政治立場，因為他希望大家先聽他的想法。"},{"w":"affirm","p":"v.","d":"to say clearly and strongly that something is true","c":"確認；斷言","s":"The president stood in front of the cameras to affirm that the new train line will open next year.","t":"總統站在鏡頭前確認新的鐵路線將在明年通車。","h":1},{"w":"affirmation","p":"n.","d":"a statement that something is true; words that support you","c":"肯定；確認","s":"Every morning she reads a short affirmation like 'I can do this', and it helps her feel brave before school.","t":"她每天早上都會讀一句簡短的自我肯定的話，像是「我做得到」，這讓她上學前覺得更勇敢。"},{"w":"affirmative","p":"adj.","d":"saying or showing yes","c":"肯定的；贊成的","s":"When I asked if she wanted to join the trip, she gave an affirmative answer and started packing at once.","t":"當我問她要不要一起去旅行時，她給了肯定的回答，馬上就開始打包。"},{"w":"in the affirmative","p":"phr.","d":"with a yes answer","c":"肯定地","s":"Most students answered in the affirmative when the teacher asked if they wanted more time for the project.","t":"當老師問大家是否需要更多時間做報告時，大部分學生都給了肯定的答覆。"},{"w":"airtight","p":"adj.","d":"closed so tightly that no air can get in or out","c":"密閉的；不透氣的","s":"Store the tea leaves in an airtight jar, or they will lose their smell and taste after a few weeks.","t":"把茶葉存放在密封的罐子裡，否則過幾週後它們就會失去香氣和味道。","h":1},{"w":"airtight container","p":"n.phr.","d":"a box or jar that keeps air out","c":"密封容器","s":"Put the leftover rice in an airtight container and keep it in the fridge, so it will still be fresh tomorrow.","t":"把剩飯放進密封容器並放到冰箱，這樣明天還會很新鮮。"},{"w":"airtight","p":"adj.","d":"so strong that no one can find a weak point","c":"無懈可擊的","s":"The lawyer's argument was airtight, so the judge could not find a single reason to doubt it.","t":"那位律師的論點無懈可擊，所以法官找不到任何一個質疑的理由。"},{"w":"airway","p":"n.","d":"the passage from the nose and mouth to the lungs","c":"呼吸道","s":"The nurse checked the boy's airway first, because he could not breathe after the ball hit his throat.","t":"護理師先檢查男孩的呼吸道，因為球打到他的喉嚨後他無法呼吸。","h":1},{"w":"airways","p":"n.","d":"a company that carries people by plane (used in names)","c":"航空公司","s":"My uncle has worked for British Airways for twenty years, and he has flown to almost every big city in Europe.","t":"我叔叔在英國航空工作了二十年，他幾乎飛遍了歐洲的每個大城市。","a":"Airways"},{"w":"clear the airway","p":"v.phr.","d":"to remove something that blocks breathing","c":"清除呼吸道","s":"In the first-aid class, we learned how to clear the airway of a person who is choking on food.","t":"在急救課上，我們學會如何清除被食物噎到的人的呼吸道。"},{"w":"algebra","p":"n.","d":"a kind of math that uses letters like x and y","c":"代數","s":"My brother is good at algebra, so he helps me solve the problems with x and y in my math homework.","t":"我哥哥擅長代數，所以他會幫我解數學作業中有 x 和 y 的題目。","h":1},{"w":"algebraic","p":"adj.","d":"connected with or using algebra","c":"代數的","s":"The teacher wrote a long algebraic equation on the board, and then she showed us how to solve it step by step.","t":"老師在黑板上寫了一個很長的代數方程式，然後一步一步示範怎麼解。"},{"w":"algebra problem","p":"n.phr.","d":"a math question that uses letters for numbers","c":"代數題","s":"I spent an hour on one difficult algebra problem last night, and I finally found the answer just before midnight.","t":"我昨晚花了一個小時在一道困難的代數題上，終於在午夜前找到答案。"},{"w":"alienate","p":"v.","d":"to make someone feel unfriendly toward you or left out","c":"使疏遠；使不友好","s":"If you keep making jokes about your friends' mistakes, you will alienate them and end up feeling lonely.","t":"如果你一直拿朋友的錯誤開玩笑，你會疏遠他們，最後覺得很孤單。","h":1},{"w":"alienation","p":"n.","d":"the feeling of not belonging to a group","c":"疏離感；疏遠","s":"Many new immigrants feel a sense of alienation at first, because they do not speak the local language well.","t":"許多新移民一開始會有疏離感，因為他們不太會說當地的語言。"},{"w":"alienated","p":"adj.","d":"feeling that you do not belong","c":"被疏遠的；感到疏離的","s":"The quiet boy felt alienated from his classmates, so the teacher asked a few kind students to eat lunch with him.","t":"那個安靜的男孩覺得和同學們有距離，所以老師請幾位友善的學生和他一起吃午餐。"},{"w":"alien","p":"n.","d":"a creature from another planet; a person from another country","c":"外星人；外國人","s":"In the movie, an alien lands in a small town, and a group of children help him find a way to go home.","t":"在電影裡，一個外星人降落在一個小鎮，一群孩子幫他找到回家的方法。"},{"w":"align","p":"v.","d":"to put things in a straight line or in the right position","c":"對齊；使成一直線","s":"Please align the desks in neat rows before the exam starts, so that the teacher can walk between them easily.","t":"考試開始前請把桌子排整齊，這樣老師才能輕鬆地在中間走動。","h":1},{"w":"align with","p":"v.phr.","d":"to agree with or support a person or group","c":"與…結盟；與…一致","s":"The small country decided to align with its powerful neighbor, because it needed help to protect its borders.","t":"那個小國決定與強大的鄰國結盟，因為它需要幫忙保衛國界。"},{"w":"alignment","p":"n.","d":"the position of things in a straight line; agreement","c":"對齊；結盟；一致","s":"The mechanic checked the alignment of my car's wheels, because the car kept moving to the left on the highway.","t":"技師檢查了我車輪的定位，因為車子在高速公路上一直往左偏。"},{"w":"line","p":"n.","d":"a long thin mark; a row of people or things","c":"線；隊伍","s":"There was a long line of people outside the new bakery, and some of them had waited for more than an hour.","t":"新麵包店外面排了長長的隊伍，有些人已經等了超過一個小時。"},{"w":"allege","p":"v.","d":"to say someone did something wrong without proving it","c":"聲稱；指稱","s":"Some workers allege that the factory dumps dirty water into the river at night, but nobody has proof yet.","t":"有些工人聲稱工廠在夜裡把髒水排進河裡，但目前還沒有人有證據。","h":1},{"w":"alleged","p":"adj.","d":"said to be true but not yet proved","c":"據稱的；被指控的","s":"The police are still looking for the alleged thief, who was seen running out of the shop with a bag.","t":"警方仍在尋找那名涉嫌的小偷，有人看到他提著袋子跑出商店。"},{"w":"allegedly","p":"adv.","d":"according to what people say, without proof","c":"據稱；據說","s":"The famous actor allegedly hit a photographer outside the hotel, but he says it was only an accident.","t":"那位知名演員據稱在飯店外打了一名攝影師，但他說那只是意外。"},{"w":"allegation","p":"n.","d":"a statement that someone did wrong, without proof","c":"（未經證實的）指控","s":"The company said the allegation was false, and it promised to show all its records to the public.","t":"那家公司說這項指控是假的，並承諾向大眾公開所有紀錄。"},{"w":"alligator","p":"n.","d":"a large reptile with strong jaws, like a crocodile","c":"短吻鱷","s":"We saw a huge alligator lying in the sun by the river, so the guide told us to stay inside the boat.","t":"我們看到一隻巨大的短吻鱷躺在河邊曬太陽，所以導遊叫我們待在船上。","h":1},{"w":"crocodile","p":"n.","d":"a large reptile with a long nose and many sharp teeth","c":"鱷魚","s":"A crocodile can stay under the water for a long time, and then it suddenly jumps out to catch its food.","t":"鱷魚可以在水下待很久，然後突然跳出來抓食物。"},{"w":"crocodile tears","p":"n.phr.","d":"sadness that is not real","c":"鱷魚的眼淚（假慈悲）","s":"Don't believe him when he cries after breaking your toy, because those are just crocodile tears.","t":"他弄壞你的玩具後哭的時候別相信他，因為那只是鱷魚的眼淚。"},{"w":"altitude","p":"n.","d":"the height of a place above the sea","c":"高度；海拔","s":"The plane flew at an altitude of ten thousand meters, so we could see only clouds below us.","t":"飛機在一萬公尺的高度飛行，所以我們只能看到下方的雲。","h":1},{"w":"at high altitude","p":"phr.","d":"in a place far above the sea","c":"在高海拔處","s":"Water boils at a lower temperature at high altitude, so it takes longer to cook noodles on a high mountain.","t":"在高海拔處水的沸點較低，所以在高山上煮麵要花比較久的時間。"},{"w":"altitude sickness","p":"n.phr.","d":"illness caused by being very high above the sea","c":"高山症","s":"Several climbers got altitude sickness near the top of the mountain, so they had headaches and felt very weak.","t":"好幾位登山客在接近山頂時得了高山症，所以他們頭痛而且覺得非常虛弱。"},{"w":"aluminum","p":"n.","d":"a light, silver-colored metal","c":"鋁","s":"Most soda cans are made of aluminum, because it is light, strong, and easy to recycle.","t":"大部分汽水罐是用鋁做的，因為它輕、堅固又容易回收。","h":1},{"w":"aluminum foil","p":"n.phr.","d":"very thin metal paper used to wrap food","c":"鋁箔紙","s":"My mother wrapped the fish in aluminum foil before putting it in the oven, so it stayed soft and full of flavor.","t":"我媽媽把魚放進烤箱前先用鋁箔紙包起來，所以魚肉保持軟嫩、充滿風味。"},{"w":"aluminum can","p":"n.phr.","d":"a light metal container for drinks","c":"鋁罐","s":"Please wash each aluminum can before you put it in the recycling bin, or the bin will start to smell.","t":"把每個鋁罐放進回收桶前請先洗乾淨，否則回收桶會開始發臭。"},{"w":"ambiguity","p":"n.","d":"the state of having more than one possible meaning","c":"模稜兩可；歧義","s":"There was some ambiguity in the teacher's instructions, so half of the class wrote one page and the other half wrote two.","t":"老師的指示有些模稜兩可，所以班上一半的人寫了一頁，另一半寫了兩頁。","h":1},{"w":"ambiguous","p":"adj.","d":"having more than one possible meaning; not clear","c":"模稜兩可的；不明確的","s":"His answer was ambiguous, and I still do not know if he will come to my party or not.","t":"他的回答模稜兩可，我到現在還不知道他會不會來我的派對。"},{"w":"ambiguously","p":"adv.","d":"in a way that is not clear","c":"含糊地","s":"The rule was written so ambiguously that even the teachers could not agree on what it really meant.","t":"那條規定寫得如此含糊，連老師們都無法對它的真正意思達成共識。"},{"w":"unambiguous","p":"adj.","d":"very clear, with only one meaning","c":"明確的；毫不含糊的","s":"The sign at the pool gave an unambiguous message: no running, no pushing, and no food near the water.","t":"泳池的告示傳達了明確的訊息：禁止奔跑、禁止推擠，水邊禁止飲食。"},{"w":"amid","p":"prep.","d":"in the middle of; during","c":"在…之中；在…期間","s":"The mother held her baby tightly amid the crowd of people at the busy train station.","t":"在繁忙火車站的人群之中，那位母親緊緊抱著她的寶寶。","h":1},{"w":"amidst","p":"prep.","d":"in the middle of (a more formal form of amid)","c":"在…之中","s":"Amidst all the noise of the night market, I suddenly heard someone calling my name from far away.","t":"在夜市一片吵雜聲中，我突然聽到有人從遠處叫我的名字。","a":"Amidst","h":1},{"w":"in the midst of","p":"phr.","d":"in the middle of an event or place","c":"在…當中；正值…之際","s":"We were in the midst of dinner when the lights went out, so we finished eating by candlelight.","t":"我們正在吃晚餐的時候停電了，所以我們在燭光下吃完晚餐。"},{"w":"among","p":"prep.","d":"in a group of people or things; between more than two","c":"在…之中（三者以上）","s":"The new student felt shy at first, but soon she was happy among her new friends in the art club.","t":"新同學一開始很害羞，但很快她就在美術社和新朋友們在一起玩得很開心。"},{"w":"amongst","p":"prep.","d":"among (a more formal form)","c":"在…之中","s":"The old letter was found amongst some dusty books in the attic, and nobody knew who had written it.","t":"那封舊信是在閣樓裡一些積滿灰塵的書之中被發現的，沒有人知道是誰寫的。"},{"w":"alongside","p":"prep.","d":"next to; together with","c":"在…旁邊；與…一起","s":"The young doctor worked alongside the experienced nurses, and she learned a lot from them every day.","t":"那位年輕醫生和經驗豐富的護理師們一起工作，她每天都從她們身上學到很多。"},{"w":"amplify","p":"v.","d":"to make a sound louder; to make something stronger","c":"放大；擴大","s":"The band used big speakers to amplify their music, so people could hear it from the other side of the park.","t":"樂團用大型喇叭來放大音樂，所以公園另一頭的人都聽得到。","h":1},{"w":"amplifier","p":"n.","d":"a machine that makes sounds louder","c":"擴音器；擴大機","s":"The guitar player plugged his guitar into an amplifier, and suddenly the sound filled the whole hall.","t":"吉他手把吉他插上擴大機，突然間聲音充滿了整個大廳。"},{"w":"amplification","p":"n.","d":"the act of making something louder or stronger","c":"放大；擴大","s":"The old church is so large that the priest's voice needs some amplification, or people at the back cannot hear him.","t":"那座老教堂太大了，神父的聲音需要一些擴音，否則後面的人聽不到。"},{"w":"ample","p":"adj.","d":"more than enough","c":"充足的；充裕的","s":"There is ample time to finish the test, so please read every question carefully before you answer.","t":"有充裕的時間完成測驗，所以作答前請仔細閱讀每一題。"},{"w":"analogy","p":"n.","d":"a comparison between two things that are alike in some way","c":"類比；比喻","s":"The teacher used the analogy of a busy city to explain how all the parts of a cell work together.","t":"老師用一座繁忙城市作為類比，來解釋細胞的各個部分如何一起運作。","h":1},{"w":"draw an analogy","p":"v.phr.","d":"to compare two things to explain one of them","c":"做類比","s":"The writer drew an analogy between the human brain and a computer, and it made the article easy to understand.","t":"作者在人腦和電腦之間做了類比，讓這篇文章很容易理解。","a":"drew an analogy"},{"w":"analogous","p":"adj.","d":"similar in some way","c":"類似的；可比擬的","s":"Learning a language is analogous to learning to swim, because you cannot improve without a lot of practice.","t":"學語言和學游泳很類似，因為不經過大量練習就無法進步。"},{"w":"analytical","p":"adj.","d":"using careful thinking to study or understand something","c":"分析的；善於分析的","s":"Detectives need strong analytical skills, because they must study small details to find out who did the crime.","t":"偵探需要很強的分析能力，因為他們必須研究小細節來找出是誰犯案。","h":1},{"w":"analyze","p":"v.","d":"to study something carefully to understand it","c":"分析","s":"The scientists will analyze the water from the river, and they will tell the public if it is safe to drink.","t":"科學家將分析河裡的水，並告訴大眾它是否可以安全飲用。"},{"w":"analysis","p":"n.","d":"the careful study of something","c":"分析","s":"After a careful analysis of the test results, the doctor said that my grandfather was healthy.","t":"經過仔細分析檢查結果後，醫生說我爺爺很健康。"},{"w":"analyst","p":"n.","d":"a person whose job is to study information carefully","c":"分析師","s":"My aunt works as a news analyst, and she explains what is happening in the world on TV every night.","t":"我阿姨是一位新聞分析師，每天晚上在電視上解說世界上正在發生的事。"},{"w":"analytically","p":"adv.","d":"in a careful, logical way","c":"分析地；邏輯地","s":"Try to think about the problem analytically instead of guessing, and you will find the answer much faster.","t":"試著有條理地分析這個問題而不是用猜的，你會更快找到答案。"},{"w":"anchor","p":"n.","d":"a heavy metal object that keeps a ship in one place","c":"錨","s":"The sailors dropped the anchor near the island, and then they took a small boat to the beach.","t":"水手們在島附近抛下錨，然後搭小船到海灘上。","h":1},{"w":"anchor","p":"v.","d":"to stop a ship with an anchor; to fix something firmly","c":"下錨；固定","s":"The workers had to anchor the tent to the ground with strong ropes, because the wind was very strong.","t":"工人們必須用堅固的繩子把帳篷固定在地上，因為風非常大。"},{"w":"anchor","p":"n.","d":"a person who reads the news on TV","c":"新聞主播","s":"The news anchor looked serious as she told viewers about the typhoon that was coming toward Taiwan.","t":"新聞主播神情嚴肅地告訴觀眾，有一個颱風正朝台灣而來。"},{"w":"drop anchor","p":"v.phr.","d":"to let the anchor go down so the ship stops","c":"抛錨；停泊","s":"The ship will drop anchor in the quiet bay tonight, and the passengers can go swimming in the morning.","t":"這艘船今晚將在安靜的海灣停泊，乘客們早上可以去游泳。"},{"w":"animate","p":"v.","d":"to make something lively; to make drawings move in a film","c":"使有生氣；製作成動畫","s":"The artists spent three years trying to animate the old fairy tale, and the cartoon finally came out last month.","t":"藝術家們花了三年把這個古老童話製作成動畫，這部卡通終於在上個月上映。","h":1},{"w":"animated","p":"adj.","d":"full of energy; made as a cartoon","c":"活潑的；動畫的","s":"The children had an animated discussion about their favorite movies, and everyone wanted to speak at the same time.","t":"孩子們針對最喜歡的電影進行了熱烈的討論，每個人都想同時發言。"},{"w":"animation","p":"n.","d":"the making of cartoons; liveliness","c":"動畫；活力","s":"My cousin studies animation in college, and she hopes to work for a big film company that makes cartoons.","t":"我表姐在大學讀動畫，她希望能到一家製作卡通的大電影公司工作。"},{"w":"animated film","p":"n.phr.","d":"a movie made from moving drawings or computer pictures","c":"動畫電影","s":"This animated film is popular with both children and adults, because the story is funny and also very moving.","t":"這部動畫電影很受小孩和大人喜愛，因為故事既有趣又非常感人。"},{"w":"annoyance","p":"n.","d":"the feeling of being a little angry","c":"煩惱；惱怒","s":"To my great annoyance, the bus left just as I arrived at the stop, so I had to wait twenty minutes for the next one.","t":"令我非常惱火的是，我一到站公車就開走了，所以我得再等二十分鐘搭下一班。","h":1},{"w":"annoy","p":"v.","d":"to make someone a little angry","c":"使惱怒；打擾","s":"Please don't annoy your sister while she is studying, because she has an important test tomorrow.","t":"妹妹在念書的時候請不要吵她，因為她明天有一個重要的考試。"},{"w":"annoying","p":"adj.","d":"making you feel a little angry","c":"惱人的；煩人的","s":"The sound of the mosquito was so annoying that I could not fall asleep until two in the morning.","t":"蚊子的聲音太惱人了，我一直到凌晨兩點都睡不著。"},{"w":"annoyed","p":"adj.","d":"feeling a little angry","c":"惱怒的；不高興的","s":"My father was annoyed because the neighbors parked their car in front of our garage again.","t":"我爸爸很不高興，因為鄰居又把車停在我們的車庫前面。"},{"w":"anthem","p":"n.","d":"a special song for a country, group, or event","c":"國歌；頌歌；代表歌曲","s":"This rock song became the anthem of our basketball team, and we play it before every game to feel strong.","t":"這首搖滾歌曲成了我們籃球隊的代表歌曲，我們每場比賽前都會播放它來振奮士氣。","h":1},{"w":"national anthem","p":"n.phr.","d":"the official song of a country","c":"國歌","s":"Everyone stood up and sang the national anthem together before the big baseball game started on Saturday.","t":"星期六那場大型棒球比賽開始前，大家都站起來一起唱國歌。"},{"w":"school anthem","p":"n.phr.","d":"the official song of a school","c":"校歌","s":"At the graduation ceremony, the students sang the school anthem one last time, and many of them began to cry.","t":"在畢業典禮上，學生們最後一次唱校歌，許多人都哭了。"},{"w":"antibiotic","p":"n.","d":"a medicine that kills bacteria","c":"抗生素","s":"The doctor gave me an antibiotic for my ear infection, and he told me to take all the pills even if I felt better.","t":"醫生給了我治療耳朵感染的抗生素，並告訴我即使覺得好了也要把藥吃完。","h":1},{"w":"antibiotic","p":"adj.","d":"able to kill bacteria","c":"抗菌的；抗生的","s":"This antibiotic cream helps small cuts heal faster, so many parents keep it in the first-aid box.","t":"這種抗菌藥膏能幫助小傷口更快癒合，所以很多家長會把它放在急救箱裡。"},{"w":"take antibiotics","p":"v.phr.","d":"to use medicine that kills bacteria","c":"服用抗生素","s":"You should not take antibiotics for a cold, because a cold is caused by a virus, not by bacteria.","t":"感冒時你不應該服用抗生素，因為感冒是病毒引起的，不是細菌。"},{"w":"antibiotic resistance","p":"n.phr.","d":"when bacteria can no longer be killed by medicine","c":"抗藥性","s":"Many doctors are worried about antibiotic resistance, because some medicines no longer work against dangerous bacteria.","t":"許多醫生擔心抗藥性的問題，因為有些藥物已經對危險的細菌無效了。"},{"w":"anticipation","p":"n.","d":"a feeling of excitement about something that will happen","c":"期待；預期","s":"The fans waited outside the stadium with great anticipation, because their favorite singer was going to arrive soon.","t":"歌迷們滿懷期待地在體育場外等候，因為他們最喜歡的歌手很快就要到了。","h":1},{"w":"anticipate","p":"v.","d":"to expect something and get ready for it","c":"預期；預料","s":"We did not anticipate so much traffic on the highway, so we arrived at the wedding an hour late.","t":"我們沒有預料到高速公路上會這麼塞，所以我們晚了一個小時才到婚禮。"},{"w":"in anticipation of","p":"phr.","d":"because you expect something to happen","c":"預期…而；為…做準備","s":"Many people bought extra food and water in anticipation of the typhoon, so the shelves at the supermarket were almost empty.","t":"許多人為了颱風做準備而多買了食物和水，所以超市的貨架幾乎都空了。"},{"w":"anticipated","p":"adj.","d":"expected","c":"預期的；期待已久的","s":"The new phone was the most anticipated product of the year, so people waited in line all night to buy it on the first day.","t":"這支新手機是今年最令人期待的產品，所以人們整晚排隊，就為了在第一天買到它。"},{"w":"antonym","p":"n.","d":"a word with the opposite meaning of another word","c":"反義詞","s":"'Happy' is an antonym of 'sad', so you can use it when you want to describe the opposite feeling.","t":"happy 是 sad 的反義詞，所以當你想描述相反的感覺時可以用它。","h":1},{"w":"synonym","p":"n.","d":"a word with the same or almost the same meaning as another","c":"同義詞","s":"'Big' is a synonym of 'large', so you can use either word to describe a huge house.","t":"big 是 large 的同義詞，所以描述一棟很大的房子時你可以用任何一個字。"},{"w":"opposite","p":"n.","d":"a person or thing that is completely different","c":"相反的事物；對立面","s":"My sister loves parties and noise, but I am the opposite, because I prefer quiet evenings at home with a book.","t":"我姐姐喜歡派對和熱鬧，但我正好相反，我比較喜歡在家看書、度過安靜的夜晚。"},{"w":"applaud","p":"v.","d":"to clap your hands to show you like something; to praise","c":"鼓掌；讚揚","s":"The audience began to applaud when the young dancer finished, and some people even stood up to cheer.","t":"年輕舞者表演結束時，觀眾開始鼓掌，有些人甚至站起來歡呼。","h":1},{"w":"applause","p":"n.","d":"the sound of people clapping their hands","c":"掌聲","s":"The applause lasted for almost five minutes, and the singer had to come back on stage to sing another song.","t":"掌聲持續了將近五分鐘，歌手只好回到台上再唱一首歌。"},{"w":"a round of applause","p":"n.phr.","d":"a period of clapping for someone","c":"一陣掌聲","s":"Let's give a round of applause to our volunteers, because they worked very hard to make this event a success.","t":"讓我們給志工們一陣熱烈的掌聲，因為他們非常努力讓這次活動成功。"},{"w":"applaud sb for","p":"v.phr.","d":"to praise someone because of something they did","c":"為某事讚揚某人","s":"The principal applauded the students for their courage after they saved a little boy from the river.","t":"學生們從河裡救起一個小男孩後，校長讚揚學生們的勇氣。","a":"applauded the students for"}]},{"unit":3,"theme":"applicable – badge","cards":[{"w":"applicable","p":"adj.","d":"able to be used in a certain situation; relevant","c":"適用的；合適的","s":"The new rule is applicable to all students, so even seniors must wear their school uniforms on Fridays now.","t":"新規定適用於所有學生，所以現在連高三生星期五也必須穿制服。","h":1},{"w":"be applicable to","p":"v.phr.","d":"to be suitable for or able to be used for","c":"適用於","s":"This discount is applicable to online orders only, so you cannot use it when you buy things in the store.","t":"這個折扣只適用於網路訂單，所以你在店裡買東西時不能使用。","a":"is applicable to"},{"w":"apply","p":"v.","d":"to use a rule or idea in a situation; to ask formally for something","c":"應用；申請","s":"You can apply what you learned in math class when you count your change at the supermarket.","t":"在超市數找零時，你可以應用在數學課學到的東西。"},{"w":"application","p":"n.","d":"a formal request; the use of something","c":"申請（書）；應用","s":"She sent her application to three universities last month, and now she is waiting nervously for their answers.","t":"她上個月把申請書寄給三所大學，現在正緊張地等待他們的回覆。"},{"w":"inapplicable","p":"adj.","d":"not able to be used in a certain situation","c":"不適用的","s":"The old safety rules are inapplicable to electric cars, so the government is writing new ones this year.","t":"舊的安全規定不適用於電動車，所以政府今年正在制定新規定。"},{"w":"apprentice","p":"n.","d":"a young person who learns a skill by working for an expert","c":"學徒","s":"At sixteen, he became an apprentice to an old carpenter, and he learned how to make chairs and tables by hand.","t":"他十六歲時成為一位老木匠的學徒，學會了如何手工製作椅子和桌子。","h":1},{"w":"be apprenticed to","p":"v.phr.","d":"to work as a learner for a skilled person","c":"當…的學徒","s":"My grandfather was apprenticed to a tailor when he was young, so he can still make his own shirts today.","t":"我爺爺年輕時當過一位裁縫師的學徒，所以他到今天還能自己做襯衫。","a":"was apprenticed to"},{"w":"apprenticeship","p":"n.","d":"the time when you learn a job by working for an expert","c":"學徒期；學徒身分","s":"After a three-year apprenticeship at a famous bakery, Amy finally opened her own small cake shop.","t":"在一家知名麵包店當了三年學徒之後，艾咪終於開了自己的小蛋糕店。"},{"w":"approximate","p":"adj.","d":"almost correct or exact, but not completely","c":"大概的；近似的","s":"The approximate cost of the school trip is two thousand dollars, but the final price may change a little.","t":"校外旅行的大約費用是兩千元，但最後的價格可能會有些變動。","h":1},{"w":"approximately","p":"adv.","d":"about; close to an exact number","c":"大約；近乎","s":"The movie lasts approximately two hours, so we should have enough time to eat dinner after it ends.","t":"這部電影大約兩個小時，所以電影結束後我們應該有足夠的時間吃晚餐。"},{"w":"approximate","p":"v.","d":"to be close to something in amount or quality","c":"近似；接近","s":"The taste of this cheap coffee does not even approximate the rich flavor of the coffee in the café downtown.","t":"這種便宜咖啡的味道甚至比不上市中心那家咖啡館咖啡的濃郁風味。"},{"w":"approximation","p":"n.","d":"a number or idea that is close but not exact","c":"近似值；概算","s":"The number of birds in the park is only an approximation, because it is impossible to count every single one of them.","t":"公園裡鳥的數量只是一個概略的估計，因為不可能把每一隻都數清楚。"},{"w":"archaeology","p":"n.","d":"the study of old cultures by digging up and studying old things","c":"考古學","s":"My cousin studies archaeology at university, and this summer she will help dig up an old village in the mountains.","t":"我表姐在大學讀考古學，這個夏天她會幫忙挖掘山上的一座古老村落。","h":1},{"w":"archaeologist","p":"n.","d":"a person who studies very old cultures and objects","c":"考古學家","s":"The archaeologist found some broken pots and old coins, which showed that people lived there two thousand years ago.","t":"那位考古學家發現了一些破碎的陶罐和古錢幣，顯示兩千年前就有人住在那裡。"},{"w":"archaeological","p":"adj.","d":"connected with the study of old cultures","c":"考古的；考古學的","s":"Workers stopped building the new road because they found an important archaeological site under the ground.","t":"工人們停止興建新道路，因為他們在地底下發現了一處重要的考古遺址。"},{"w":"archive","p":"n.","d":"a collection of old records or documents","c":"檔案；檔案資料","s":"The museum has a large archive of old photos, so visitors can see what Taipei looked like a hundred years ago.","t":"博物館有大量的老照片檔案，所以參觀者可以看到台北一百年前的樣子。","h":1},{"w":"archives","p":"n.","d":"a place where old records are kept","c":"檔案室；檔案館","s":"The writer spent many days in the city archives, reading letters and newspapers from the time of the war.","t":"那位作家花了好幾天待在市立檔案館，閱讀戰爭時期的信件和報紙。"},{"w":"archive","p":"v.","d":"to store old documents or computer files in a safe place","c":"把…存檔；歸檔","s":"Please archive the old emails before you delete them, because we may need them again next year.","t":"刪除舊電子郵件前請先把它們存檔，因為我們明年可能還會用到。"},{"w":"arithmetic","p":"n.","d":"the part of math that uses adding, subtracting, multiplying, and dividing","c":"算術","s":"Young children learn simple arithmetic by counting their toys, and later they learn to add and subtract on paper.","t":"年幼的孩子透過數玩具來學習簡單的算術，之後才學會在紙上做加減法。","h":1},{"w":"arithmetic","p":"adj.","d":"connected with adding, subtracting, and other number work","c":"算術的","s":"The test has twenty arithmetic problems, and you are not allowed to use a calculator to solve them.","t":"這份測驗有二十道算術題，而且你不能用計算機解題。"},{"w":"mental arithmetic","p":"n.phr.","d":"doing math in your head without paper","c":"心算","s":"My grandmother is very good at mental arithmetic, so she can add up the prices at the market faster than the shop owner.","t":"我奶奶非常擅長心算，所以她在市場算價錢比老闆還快。"},{"w":"ascend","p":"v.","d":"to go up or climb","c":"上升；登上","s":"The climbers began to ascend the mountain at four in the morning, so they could see the sunrise from the top.","t":"登山客們清晨四點開始攀登那座山，這樣他們就能在山頂看到日出。","h":1},{"w":"ascent","p":"n.","d":"the act of going up; a path that goes up","c":"上升；攀登","s":"The ascent to the top of the tower took twenty minutes, because there were more than five hundred steps.","t":"登上塔頂花了二十分鐘，因為有五百多級台階。"},{"w":"in ascending order","p":"phr.","d":"arranged from the smallest to the largest","c":"由小到大排列","s":"Please put these numbers in ascending order, starting with the smallest one and ending with the biggest one.","t":"請把這些數字由小到大排列，從最小的開始，到最大的結束。"},{"w":"descend","p":"v.","d":"to go down","c":"下降；走下","s":"When the plane began to descend, the captain asked all the passengers to fasten their seat belts.","t":"當飛機開始下降時，機長請所有乘客繫好安全帶。"},{"w":"aspire","p":"v.","d":"to have a strong wish to achieve something","c":"渴望；立志","s":"Many students aspire to study abroad, so they practice English every day and save money for the trip.","t":"許多學生渴望出國念書，所以他們每天練英文，並為此存錢。","h":1},{"w":"aspire to","p":"v.phr.","d":"to hope strongly to reach a goal","c":"渴望達到；立志成為","s":"Young players aspire to the level of their sports heroes, so they train for hours after school every day.","t":"年輕球員們渴望達到他們運動偶像的水準，所以他們每天放學後訓練好幾個小時。"},{"w":"aspiration","p":"n.","d":"a strong hope to do or become something","c":"抱負；志向","s":"Her greatest aspiration is to become a doctor, because she wants to help sick children in poor countries.","t":"她最大的志向是成為醫生，因為她想幫助貧窮國家生病的孩子。"},{"w":"aspiring","p":"adj.","d":"hoping to become a certain kind of person","c":"有抱負的；想成為…的","s":"The famous writer gave some useful advice to a group of aspiring writers at the library last Saturday.","t":"那位知名作家上星期六在圖書館給了一群有志成為作家的人一些實用的建議。"},{"w":"assassinate","p":"v.","d":"to kill an important person, often for political reasons","c":"暗殺；行刺","s":"Several men planned to assassinate the king during the parade, but the guards discovered their plan in time.","t":"有幾個人計畫在遊行時暗殺國王，但侍衛及時發現了他們的計畫。","h":1},{"w":"assassination","p":"n.","d":"the murder of an important person","c":"暗殺","s":"The assassination of President Lincoln in 1865 shocked the whole country, and many people cried in the streets.","t":"1865 年林肯總統遭暗殺震驚全國，許多人在街上哭泣。"},{"w":"assassin","p":"n.","d":"a person who kills an important person","c":"刺客；暗殺者","s":"In the movie, the assassin hid on the roof of a tall building and waited for the president's car to pass.","t":"在電影裡，刺客躲在一棟高樓的屋頂上，等待總統的車經過。"},{"w":"asthma","p":"n.","d":"an illness that makes breathing difficult","c":"氣喘","s":"My little sister has asthma, so she cannot run for a long time, and she always carries her medicine with her.","t":"我妹妹有氣喘，所以她不能長時間跑步，而且她總是隨身帶著藥。","h":1},{"w":"asthmatic","p":"adj.","d":"having asthma; connected with asthma","c":"氣喘的；患氣喘的","s":"Dirty air is very dangerous for asthmatic children, so the school keeps them inside when the air quality is bad.","t":"髒空氣對有氣喘的孩子非常危險，所以空氣品質不好時學校會讓他們待在室內。"},{"w":"asthma attack","p":"n.phr.","d":"a sudden time when someone with asthma cannot breathe well","c":"氣喘發作","s":"Tom had an asthma attack during the race, so the teacher called an ambulance and gave him his medicine.","t":"湯姆在賽跑時氣喘發作，所以老師叫了救護車並給他吃藥。"},{"w":"astray","p":"adv.","d":"away from the right path or the right place","c":"迷路；離開正道","s":"Some of the letters went astray during the move, so we never got the bills from the electric company.","t":"搬家時有些信件寄丟了，所以我們一直沒收到電力公司的帳單。","h":1},{"w":"go astray","p":"v.phr.","d":"to get lost; to start doing wrong things","c":"走失；誤入歧途","s":"Parents worry that their teenagers may go astray if they spend too much time with the wrong friends.","t":"父母擔心如果青少年花太多時間和壞朋友在一起，可能會誤入歧途。"},{"w":"lead sb astray","p":"v.phr.","d":"to make someone do bad or wrong things","c":"把某人帶壞","s":"The older boys tried to lead him astray by asking him to skip class and play games at the internet café.","t":"那些年紀較大的男孩想把他帶壞，要他翹課去網咖打電動。","a":"lead him astray"},{"w":"stray","p":"adj.","d":"lost or without a home (used for animals)","c":"走失的；流浪的","s":"We found a stray dog near the school gate, so we gave it some water and called the animal shelter.","t":"我們在校門附近發現一隻流浪狗，所以我們給牠一些水並打電話給動物收容所。"},{"w":"astronaut","p":"n.","d":"a person who travels into space","c":"太空人","s":"The astronaut stayed on the space station for six months, and she did many science experiments there.","t":"那位太空人在太空站待了六個月，並在那裡做了許多科學實驗。","h":1},{"w":"astronautics","p":"n.","d":"the science of travel in space","c":"太空航行學","s":"He studied astronautics in college because he wanted to help build rockets that could fly to Mars.","t":"他在大學讀太空航行學，因為他想幫忙建造能飛到火星的火箭。"},{"w":"space suit","p":"n.phr.","d":"special clothes that astronauts wear in space","c":"太空衣","s":"Before going outside the space station, the astronaut put on his heavy space suit and checked the air supply.","t":"在走出太空站之前，太空人穿上沉重的太空衣並檢查空氣供應。"},{"w":"astronomer","p":"n.","d":"a scientist who studies stars and planets","c":"天文學家","s":"The astronomer used a powerful telescope to find a new planet that was far away from our sun.","t":"那位天文學家用一台強大的望遠鏡發現了一顆離我們的太陽很遠的新行星。","h":1},{"w":"astronomy","p":"n.","d":"the scientific study of stars, planets, and space","c":"天文學","s":"I became interested in astronomy after I saw the Milky Way on a camping trip in the mountains.","t":"我在山上露營看到銀河之後，就對天文學產生了興趣。","h":1},{"w":"astronomical","p":"adj.","d":"connected with the study of stars and planets","c":"天文的；天文學的","s":"The new astronomical center has a large telescope, and students can look at the moon there every Friday night.","t":"新的天文中心有一台大型望遠鏡，學生們每週五晚上都可以在那裡觀察月亮。"},{"w":"astronomical","p":"adj.","d":"extremely large (used for prices or numbers)","c":"天文數字的；極大的","s":"The rent for apartments near the train station is astronomical, so most young workers live farther away.","t":"火車站附近公寓的租金高得驚人，所以大多數年輕上班族住得比較遠。"},{"w":"attain","p":"v.","d":"to reach or succeed in getting something after hard work","c":"達到；獲得","s":"If you practice every day and never give up, you will attain your goal of running a full marathon.","t":"如果你每天練習而且永不放棄，你就能達成跑完全程馬拉松的目標。","h":1},{"w":"attainment","p":"n.","d":"success in reaching a goal; something you have achieved","c":"成就；達成","s":"The school is proud of the high academic attainment of its students, because many of them enter top universities.","t":"學校以學生們優異的學業成就為榮，因為他們之中有許多人進入頂尖大學。"},{"w":"attainable","p":"adj.","d":"possible to reach or achieve","c":"可達到的","s":"Set small goals that are attainable, and you will feel more confident each time you reach one of them.","t":"設定可以達成的小目標，每完成一個，你就會更有自信。"},{"w":"unattainable","p":"adj.","d":"impossible to reach or achieve","c":"無法達到的","s":"For a poor family in the past, owning a car was an unattainable dream, but now many families have two.","t":"對過去的窮人家來說，擁有一輛車是遙不可及的夢想，但現在許多家庭都有兩輛。"},{"w":"attendant","p":"n.","d":"a person whose job is to help or serve people","c":"服務員；侍者","s":"The parking lot attendant showed us where to park, and then he gave us a ticket for the car.","t":"停車場管理員告訴我們要停在哪裡，然後給了我們一張停車票。","h":1},{"w":"flight attendant","p":"n.phr.","d":"a person who serves passengers on a plane","c":"空服員","s":"The flight attendant brought me a blanket and some hot tea, because I said I felt cold during the flight.","t":"因為我說飛行途中覺得冷，空服員拿了一條毯子和一些熱茶給我。"},{"w":"attend","p":"v.","d":"to go to an event, a class, or a school","c":"出席；參加；上（學）","s":"More than two hundred people will attend the wedding, so the couple booked the biggest room in the hotel.","t":"超過兩百人將出席婚禮，所以新人預訂了飯店最大的廳。"},{"w":"attendance","p":"n.","d":"the act of being present at a class or event; the number of people who come","c":"出席；出席人數","s":"The teacher checks attendance every morning, and students who are late three times must stay after school.","t":"老師每天早上都會點名，遲到三次的學生必須放學後留下來。"},{"w":"audit","p":"n.","d":"an official check of a company's money records","c":"審計；查帳","s":"The yearly audit showed that someone had taken money from the company, so the police were called in.","t":"年度查帳顯示有人從公司拿走了錢，所以警方介入調查。","h":1},{"w":"audit","p":"v.","d":"to check money records officially; to attend a class without grades","c":"查帳；旁聽","s":"My father decided to audit a history class at the university, so he can learn without taking any tests.","t":"我爸爸決定到大學旁聽一門歷史課，這樣他可以學習而不用參加任何考試。"},{"w":"auditor","p":"n.","d":"a person whose job is to check money records","c":"審計員；查帳員","s":"The auditor spent two weeks checking every receipt, and she found several serious mistakes in the reports.","t":"那位審計員花了兩週檢查每一張收據，並在報告中發現好幾個嚴重錯誤。"},{"w":"auditorium","p":"n.","d":"a large room or building where people watch shows or listen to speeches","c":"禮堂；大廳","s":"The graduation ceremony will be held in the school auditorium, which has enough seats for all the parents.","t":"畢業典禮將在學校禮堂舉行，那裡有足夠的座位讓所有家長入座。","h":1},{"w":"audience","p":"n.","d":"the people who watch or listen to a show or speech","c":"觀眾；聽眾","s":"The audience laughed so loudly at the funny play that the actors had to stop and wait for a moment.","t":"觀眾被那齣有趣的戲逗得大笑，演員們不得不停下來等一會兒。"},{"w":"audio","p":"adj.","d":"connected with sound or recording sound","c":"聲音的；音訊的","s":"The museum gives visitors an audio guide, so they can listen to stories about each painting.","t":"博物館提供參觀者語音導覽，讓他們可以聆聽每幅畫背後的故事。"},{"w":"audible","p":"adj.","d":"loud enough to be heard","c":"聽得見的","s":"His voice was barely audible because of the loud music, so I asked him to say it again.","t":"因為音樂太大聲，他的聲音幾乎聽不見，所以我請他再說一次。"},{"w":"avert","p":"v.","d":"to stop something bad from happening","c":"避免；防止","s":"The pilot landed the plane safely in a field, and he was able to avert a terrible accident.","t":"機長把飛機安全地降落在田野上，成功避免了一場可怕的意外。","h":1},{"w":"avert one's eyes","p":"v.phr.","d":"to look away from something","c":"轉移視線；把目光移開","s":"The movie was so scary that I had to avert my eyes during the most frightening parts.","t":"那部電影太可怕了，在最嚇人的片段我不得不把目光移開。","a":"avert my eyes"},{"w":"avert a crisis","p":"v.phr.","d":"to stop a very serious problem from happening","c":"避免危機","s":"The two countries started talking again in order to avert a crisis, and soon the danger of war was over.","t":"兩國重新展開對話以避免危機，不久戰爭的危險就解除了。"},{"w":"aviation","p":"n.","d":"the design, building, and flying of airplanes","c":"航空；飛行","s":"The Wright brothers made the first powered flight in 1903, and it was the beginning of modern aviation.","t":"萊特兄弟在 1903 年完成第一次動力飛行，那是現代航空的開端。","h":1},{"w":"aviator","p":"n.","d":"a pilot, especially in the early days of flying","c":"飛行員","s":"The brave aviator flew alone across the ocean, and crowds of people were waiting for her when she landed.","t":"那位勇敢的飛行員獨自飛越大洋，她降落時一大群人正在等她。"},{"w":"aviation industry","p":"n.phr.","d":"the business of making and flying airplanes","c":"航空業","s":"Many workers in the aviation industry lost their jobs when people stopped traveling during the pandemic.","t":"疫情期間人們停止旅行時，許多航空業的員工失去了工作。"},{"w":"awesome","p":"adj.","d":"very good, great, or wonderful","c":"很棒的；令人驚嘆的","s":"The fireworks on New Year's Eve were awesome, and thousands of people took pictures of the colorful sky.","t":"跨年夜的煙火棒極了，成千上萬的人拍下了五彩繽紛的天空。","h":1},{"w":"awe","p":"n.","d":"a feeling of great respect mixed with surprise","c":"敬畏；驚嘆","s":"We looked at the huge waterfall in awe, because none of us had ever seen anything so powerful before.","t":"我們帶著敬畏看著那座巨大的瀑布，因為我們從來沒看過那麼壯觀的景象。"},{"w":"be in awe of","p":"v.phr.","d":"to respect and admire someone very much","c":"對…敬畏；非常欽佩","s":"The young players were in awe of the famous coach, so they listened carefully to every word he said.","t":"年輕球員們非常敬佩那位知名教練，所以他們仔細聆聽他說的每一個字。","a":"were in awe of"},{"w":"awful","p":"adj.","d":"very bad or unpleasant","c":"糟糕的；可怕的","s":"The food at the hotel was awful, so we went out to find a small noodle shop in the town.","t":"飯店的食物很難吃，所以我們出去找鎮上的一家小麵店。"},{"w":"awfully","p":"adv.","d":"very; extremely","c":"非常；極其","s":"I'm awfully sorry that I forgot your birthday, so please let me buy you dinner this weekend.","t":"我非常抱歉忘了你的生日，所以這個週末請讓我請你吃晚餐。"},{"w":"awhile","p":"adv.","d":"for a short time","c":"一會兒；片刻","s":"Let's sit down and rest awhile before we climb the last part of the mountain to the top.","t":"我們先坐下來休息一會兒，再爬最後一段山路登頂吧。","h":1},{"w":"for a while","p":"phr.","d":"for some time","c":"一段時間；一陣子","s":"I have not seen my old classmates for a while, so I am very excited about the class reunion next week.","t":"我已經一陣子沒見到老同學了，所以我對下週的同學會感到很興奮。"},{"w":"once in a while","p":"phr.","d":"sometimes, but not often","c":"偶爾；有時","s":"We usually cook at home, but once in a while we go to a nice restaurant to celebrate something special.","t":"我們通常在家煮飯，但偶爾會去好餐廳慶祝特別的事。"},{"w":"worthwhile","p":"adj.","d":"worth the time, money, or effort you spend","c":"值得的","s":"The trip was long and tiring, but it was worthwhile, because the view from the top was amazing.","t":"那趟旅程又長又累，但很值得，因為山頂的景色太棒了。"},{"w":"bachelor","p":"n.","d":"a man who has never been married","c":"單身漢","s":"My uncle is still a bachelor at forty, but he says he enjoys living alone and traveling whenever he likes.","t":"我叔叔四十歲了仍是單身漢，但他說他喜歡獨自生活，想去哪裡旅行就去哪裡。","h":1},{"w":"bachelor","p":"n.","d":"a person who has a first university degree","c":"學士","s":"She is a bachelor of science, and now she is studying for a higher degree in chemistry.","t":"她是理學學士，現在正在攻讀化學的更高學位。"},{"w":"bachelor's degree","p":"n.phr.","d":"the first degree you get from a university","c":"學士學位","s":"Most jobs at this company require a bachelor's degree, so my brother is finishing college before he applies.","t":"這家公司大多數的職位都要求學士學位，所以我哥哥要先完成大學學業再去應徵。"},{"w":"master's degree","p":"n.phr.","d":"a university degree you can get after a first degree","c":"碩士學位","s":"After working for three years, my sister went back to school to get a master's degree in business.","t":"工作三年後，我姐姐回到學校攻讀商業碩士學位。"},{"w":"backbone","p":"n.","d":"the line of bones down the middle of your back","c":"脊椎；脊柱","s":"The doctor said that sitting in a bad position for many hours can hurt your backbone over time.","t":"醫生說長時間用不良的姿勢坐著，久了會傷害你的脊椎。","h":1},{"w":"backbone","p":"n.","d":"the most important part that supports a group or system","c":"骨幹；支柱","s":"Small businesses are the backbone of Taiwan's economy, and they provide jobs for millions of people.","t":"中小企業是台灣經濟的骨幹，它們為數百萬人提供工作。"},{"w":"spine","p":"n.","d":"the line of bones down the middle of your back","c":"脊椎","s":"The rider fell off his horse and hurt his spine, so he had to stay in bed for three months.","t":"那位騎士從馬上摔下來傷了脊椎，所以他必須在床上躺三個月。"},{"w":"badge","p":"n.","d":"a small piece of metal or cloth with a name or sign that you wear","c":"徽章；名牌","s":"The police officer showed us his badge before he asked us some questions about the accident.","t":"警察在問我們一些關於事故的問題前，先出示了他的警徽。","h":1},{"w":"name badge","p":"n.phr.","d":"a small card with your name that you wear on your clothes","c":"名牌","s":"Every visitor must wear a name badge in the school building, so the guards know who is allowed inside.","t":"每位訪客在校舍內都必須配戴名牌，這樣警衛才知道誰可以進入。"},{"w":"badge of honor","p":"n.phr.","d":"something that shows you have done something good or brave","c":"榮譽的象徵","s":"For the old soldier, the scar on his arm was a badge of honor, and he was proud to tell its story.","t":"對那位老兵來說，手臂上的傷疤是一種榮譽的象徵，他很自豪地講述它的故事。"}]},{"unit":4,"theme":"banquet – breakup","cards":[{"w":"banquet","p":"n.","d":"a large formal dinner for many people, often with speeches","c":"宴會；盛宴","s":"After the championship game, the school held a banquet for the players, and every family was invited to join the celebration.","t":"冠軍賽結束後，學校為球員舉辦了一場宴會，每個家庭都受邀參加慶祝活動。","h":1},{"w":"banquet hall","p":"n.phr.","d":"a large room where big formal dinners are held","c":"宴會廳","s":"The hotel's banquet hall can hold five hundred guests, so many couples choose it for their wedding dinner in spring.","t":"這家飯店的宴會廳可以容納五百位賓客，所以許多新人選擇在春天來這裡辦婚宴。"},{"w":"wedding banquet","p":"n.phr.","d":"a big dinner party to celebrate a marriage","c":"婚宴；喜宴","s":"In Taiwan, guests usually bring a red envelope with money to a wedding banquet, and the bride changes her dress several times.","t":"在台灣，賓客參加婚宴通常會帶裝著錢的紅包，新娘也會換好幾套禮服。"},{"w":"hold a banquet","p":"v.phr.","d":"to organize a large formal dinner","c":"舉辦宴會","s":"The company decided to hold a banquet at the end of the year to thank its workers for their hard work and loyalty.","t":"公司決定在年底舉辦宴會，感謝員工一年來的辛勞與忠誠。"},{"w":"barbarian","p":"n.","d":"a rude, wild person from a culture thought to be uncivilized","c":"野蠻人","s":"In the old stories, the Romans called anyone who lived outside their empire a barbarian, even if that person was educated.","t":"在古老的故事中，羅馬人把任何住在帝國之外的人都稱為野蠻人，即使那個人受過教育。","h":1},{"w":"barbarian","p":"adj.","d":"belonging to a wild, uncivilized group of people","c":"野蠻的；蠻族的","s":"The museum shows how the so-called barbarian tribes actually made beautiful jewelry and traded with cities far away.","t":"博物館展示了那些所謂的蠻族部落其實如何製作精美的首飾，並與遠方的城市進行貿易。"},{"w":"barbaric","p":"adj.","d":"extremely cruel and violent","c":"殘暴的；野蠻的","s":"Many people think that keeping wild animals in tiny cages is barbaric, so the zoo is now building larger, more natural homes for them.","t":"許多人認為把野生動物關在狹小的籠子裡很殘暴，所以動物園現在正為它們建造更大、更自然的家。"},{"w":"bass","p":"n.","d":"the lowest male singing voice, or the low notes in music","c":"男低音；低音","s":"My uncle sings bass in the church choir, and his deep voice makes the whole room feel warm and full.","t":"我叔叔在教會詩班唱男低音，他低沉的聲音讓整個空間感覺溫暖又飽滿。","h":1},{"w":"bass","p":"adj.","d":"producing or relating to low musical sounds","c":"低音的","s":"Our neighbor turned the bass sound on his speakers up so high that our windows shook during the whole party.","t":"我們的鄰居把喇叭的低音開得太大聲，整場派對期間我們的窗戶都在震動。"},{"w":"bass guitar","p":"n.phr.","d":"a guitar with four thick strings that plays low notes","c":"貝斯；低音吉他","s":"She started learning the bass guitar last year because every band needs someone to play the low notes that hold the song together.","t":"她去年開始學貝斯，因為每個樂團都需要有人彈奏把整首歌撐起來的低音。"},{"w":"bassist","p":"n.","d":"a person who plays the bass guitar","c":"貝斯手","s":"The bassist in our school band is very quiet in class, but on stage he moves and smiles like a rock star.","t":"我們學校樂團的貝斯手在課堂上很安靜，但在舞台上他像搖滾明星一樣又動又笑。"},{"w":"batter","p":"v.","d":"to hit someone or something hard many times","c":"連續猛擊；重創","s":"Strong winds and heavy rain continued to batter the small fishing boats all night, and several of them sank before morning.","t":"強風和大雨整夜持續猛烈襲擊那些小漁船，其中幾艘在天亮前就沉了。","h":1},{"w":"batter","p":"n.","d":"a soft mix of flour, eggs, and milk used for cooking","c":"麵糊","s":"Pour the pancake batter into the hot pan slowly, and wait until small bubbles appear before you flip it over.","t":"把鬆餅麵糊慢慢倒進熱鍋裡，等到出現小泡泡再翻面。"},{"w":"batter","p":"n.","d":"the player who hits the ball in baseball","c":"打者；擊球員","s":"The batter swung at the first pitch and hit a home run, so the whole stadium stood up and cheered loudly.","t":"那位打者對第一球揮棒就打出全壘打，全場觀眾都站起來大聲歡呼。"},{"w":"battered","p":"adj.","d":"old and damaged from being used or hit a lot","c":"破舊的；受損的","s":"Grandpa still carries the same battered suitcase he bought forty years ago, although the handle is broken and the color has faded.","t":"爺爺仍然帶著四十年前買的那個破舊的行李箱，雖然把手壞了、顏色也褪了。"},{"w":"beautify","p":"v.","d":"to make a place or thing look more attractive","c":"美化","s":"The city plans to beautify the old riverside by planting flowers and adding benches where people can sit and relax.","t":"市政府計畫種花並增設長椅來美化舊河岸，讓人們可以坐下休息。","h":1},{"w":"beauty","p":"n.","d":"the quality of being very pleasing to look at","c":"美；美麗","s":"Tourists come from all over the world to enjoy the natural beauty of Taroko Gorge, especially in the early morning mist.","t":"觀光客從世界各地前來欣賞太魯閣峽谷的自然美景，尤其是在清晨的薄霧中。"},{"w":"beautiful","p":"adj.","d":"very pleasing to look at, hear, or experience","c":"美麗的","s":"The sunset over the ocean was so beautiful that everyone on the beach stopped talking and simply watched the sky change color.","t":"海上的夕陽如此美麗，海灘上的每個人都停止說話，只是靜靜看著天空變色。"},{"w":"beautifully","p":"adv.","d":"in a very pleasing or skillful way","c":"美麗地；出色地","s":"She played the piano beautifully at the concert, and even the strict music teacher had tears in her eyes.","t":"她在音樂會上琴聲優美動人，連嚴格的音樂老師都眼中含淚。"},{"w":"beautification","p":"n.","d":"the work of making a place look nicer","c":"美化（工程）","s":"The beautification of our neighborhood park took two years, but now families use it every evening for picnics and games.","t":"我們社區公園的美化工程花了兩年，但現在家庭每天傍晚都會來這裡野餐和玩遊戲。"},{"w":"beep","p":"n.","d":"a short, high electronic sound","c":"嗶聲","s":"When you hear the beep after the message, please leave your name and phone number, and I will call you back soon.","t":"聽到留言後的嗶聲時，請留下您的姓名和電話，我會儘快回電給您。","h":1},{"w":"beep","p":"v.","d":"to make a short, high electronic sound","c":"發出嗶聲","s":"The microwave will beep three times when the food is ready, so you do not need to stand there and watch it.","t":"食物好了時微波爐會嗶三聲，所以你不需要站在那裡盯著它。"},{"w":"beeper","p":"n.","d":"a small device that beeps to tell you someone wants to contact you","c":"呼叫器","s":"Before smartphones existed, doctors carried a beeper so the hospital could reach them quickly in an emergency.","t":"在智慧型手機出現之前，醫生會帶著呼叫器，這樣醫院在緊急時才能迅速聯絡到他們。"},{"w":"beforehand","p":"adv.","d":"before something happens; earlier","c":"事先；預先","s":"If you want to visit the famous restaurant on Saturday, you should call beforehand because it is always full on weekends.","t":"如果你想在星期六去那家有名的餐廳，你應該事先打電話，因為它週末總是客滿。","h":1},{"w":"before","p":"prep.","d":"earlier than a time or event","c":"在…之前","s":"Please finish your homework before dinner, and then you can watch television with the rest of the family tonight.","t":"請在晚餐之前完成功課，然後今晚你就可以和家人一起看電視。"},{"w":"know beforehand","p":"v.phr.","d":"to have information about something before it happens","c":"事先知道","s":"If we had known beforehand that the museum was closed on Mondays, we would not have traveled two hours to get there.","t":"如果我們事先知道博物館星期一休館，就不會花兩小時的車程去那裡了。","a":"known beforehand"},{"w":"in advance","p":"phr.","d":"before a particular time; ahead of time","c":"提前；事先","s":"Tickets for the concert must be bought in advance, since nothing will be sold at the door on the night of the show.","t":"演唱會的票必須提前購買，因為演出當晚現場不會售票。"},{"w":"beverage","p":"n.","d":"any kind of drink, especially one other than water","c":"飲料","s":"The price of the set meal includes a soup, a main dish, and one beverage of your choice, such as tea or juice.","t":"套餐價格包含一碗湯、一道主菜和一杯你選擇的飲料，例如茶或果汁。","h":1},{"w":"alcoholic beverage","p":"n.phr.","d":"a drink that contains alcohol, like beer or wine","c":"含酒精飲料","s":"In Taiwan, stores are not allowed to sell any alcoholic beverage to people under eighteen, and clerks often ask to see an ID card.","t":"在台灣，商店不得販售任何含酒精飲料給十八歲以下的人，店員常會要求查看身分證。"},{"w":"beverage company","p":"n.phr.","d":"a business that makes and sells drinks","c":"飲料公司","s":"A large beverage company is building a new factory near our town, which will create about two hundred jobs for local people.","t":"一家大型飲料公司正在我們鎮附近蓋新工廠，將為當地人創造大約兩百個工作機會。"},{"w":"bilateral","p":"adj.","d":"involving two groups or countries","c":"雙邊的","s":"The two countries signed a bilateral trade deal yesterday, so farmers on both sides can now sell fruit across the border more easily.","t":"兩國昨天簽署了一項雙邊貿易協定，所以雙方的農民現在可以更容易地把水果賣到邊境另一邊。","h":1},{"w":"bilateral agreement","p":"n.phr.","d":"an official deal made between two countries or groups","c":"雙邊協定","s":"Under the new bilateral agreement, students from either country can study at the other's universities without paying extra fees.","t":"根據新的雙邊協定，兩國任一方的學生都可以到對方的大學就讀，而不必額外付費。"},{"w":"unilateral","p":"adj.","d":"done by one side only, without agreement from others","c":"單方面的","s":"The manager's unilateral decision to cancel the trip made the whole team angry because nobody had been asked for an opinion.","t":"經理單方面決定取消旅行，讓整個團隊很生氣，因為沒有人被徵詢過意見。"},{"w":"multilateral","p":"adj.","d":"involving several countries or groups","c":"多邊的","s":"Climate change is a global problem, so it needs multilateral action in which many nations work together instead of alone.","t":"氣候變遷是全球性的問題，所以需要許多國家共同合作而非單獨行動的多邊行動。"},{"w":"lateral","p":"adj.","d":"relating to the side of something; sideways","c":"側面的；橫向的","s":"The coach asked the players to practice lateral movements, moving quickly from side to side without crossing their feet.","t":"教練要求球員練習橫向移動，快速地左右移動而不交叉雙腳。"},{"w":"blaze","p":"n.","d":"a large, strong fire","c":"烈火；火焰","s":"Firefighters worked for six hours to control the blaze in the old warehouse, and luckily nobody was hurt.","t":"消防員奮戰六小時才控制住舊倉庫的大火，幸運的是沒有人受傷。","h":1},{"w":"blaze","p":"v.","d":"to burn brightly and strongly","c":"熊熊燃燒","s":"The campfire continued to blaze long after midnight, so we sat around it, told stories, and roasted marshmallows.","t":"營火過了午夜仍持續熊熊燃燒，所以我們圍坐在旁邊說故事、烤棉花糖。"},{"w":"blazing","p":"adj.","d":"very hot or bright; burning strongly","c":"炎熱的；熾烈的","s":"Under the blazing summer sun, the workers took a break every hour and drank plenty of water to stay safe.","t":"在炎熱的夏日陽光下，工人們每小時休息一次並大量喝水以保安全。"},{"w":"blaze a trail","p":"v.phr.","d":"to be the first to do something new that others will follow","c":"開創先例；開闢新路","s":"The young scientist helped blaze a trail for women in engineering, and today many girls say she inspired them to study science.","t":"這位年輕的科學家為女性在工程領域開創先例，如今許多女孩說她激勵了她們去學科學。"},{"w":"bleach","p":"n.","d":"a strong chemical used to make things white or to kill germs","c":"漂白劑","s":"Be careful when you use bleach to clean the bathroom, because its strong smell can hurt your eyes and throat.","t":"用漂白劑清潔浴室時要小心，因為它刺鼻的味道會傷害你的眼睛和喉嚨。","h":1},{"w":"bleach","p":"v.","d":"to make something white or lighter in color","c":"漂白；使變白","s":"If you leave the colorful curtains in the strong sunlight all summer, the sun will slowly bleach them until they look grey.","t":"如果你讓彩色窗簾整個夏天曬在強烈的陽光下，陽光會慢慢把它們曬白到看起來灰灰的。"},{"w":"bleached","p":"adj.","d":"made white or pale by chemicals or the sun","c":"漂白的；褪色的","s":"Rising sea temperatures have left large areas of bleached coral near the island, which worries scientists and local divers.","t":"海水溫度上升使得島附近出現大片白化的珊瑚，這讓科學家和當地潛水員很擔心。"},{"w":"blond","p":"adj.","d":"having pale yellow hair","c":"金髮的","s":"My cousin was born with blond hair, but it slowly turned darker as she grew up, and now it is light brown.","t":"我表妹出生時是金髮，但隨著長大慢慢變深，現在是淺棕色。","h":1},{"w":"blonde","p":"n.","d":"a woman or girl with pale yellow hair","c":"金髮女子","s":"The actress is a natural blonde, but she dyed her hair black for the movie because she was playing a Chinese character.","t":"這位女演員是天生的金髮女子，但為了電影把頭髮染黑，因為她要演一個華人角色。"},{"w":"blond hair","p":"n.phr.","d":"hair that is pale yellow in color","c":"金色頭髮","s":"In the group photo, you can easily find Anna because her blond hair shines brightly next to all her dark-haired classmates.","t":"在團體照裡你可以很容易找到安娜，因為她的金色頭髮在一群黑髮同學旁邊顯得特別亮。"},{"w":"blot","p":"v.","d":"to dry a wet surface by pressing soft paper or cloth on it","c":"吸乾；用紙吸","s":"After you wash the lettuce, blot it gently with a clean paper towel so the salad dressing will stick to the leaves.","t":"洗好生菜後，用乾淨的紙巾輕輕吸乾水分，這樣沙拉醬才會附著在葉子上。","h":1},{"w":"blot","p":"n.","d":"a dirty mark or spot, especially of ink","c":"污漬；墨漬","s":"There was a large ink blot in the middle of my homework, so the teacher could not read the answer to question five.","t":"我的作業中間有一大塊墨水污漬，所以老師看不到第五題的答案。"},{"w":"blot out","p":"v.phr.","d":"to cover something so that it cannot be seen; to try to forget","c":"遮蔽；抹去（記憶）","s":"Thick grey clouds began to blot out the sun around noon, and by two o'clock the whole city was dark and rainy.","t":"中午左右厚厚的灰雲開始遮住太陽，到了兩點整個城市又暗又下雨。"},{"w":"ink blot","p":"n.phr.","d":"a spot made by ink that has spread on paper","c":"墨漬","s":"The psychologist showed the boy an ink blot and asked him what shape he saw, and he answered that it looked like a butterfly.","t":"心理學家給男孩看一個墨漬圖，問他看到什麼形狀，他回答說看起來像一隻蝴蝶。"},{"w":"blunt","p":"adj.","d":"not sharp; having a thick edge or point","c":"鈍的","s":"This kitchen knife is too blunt to cut the tomato cleanly, so could you sharpen it before we start cooking dinner?","t":"這把菜刀太鈍了，切不好番茄，可以在我們開始做晚餐前把它磨一磨嗎？","h":1},{"w":"blunt","p":"adj.","d":"saying exactly what you think, even if it is not polite","c":"直率的；直言不諱的","s":"My grandmother is very blunt; when she does not like your cooking, she tells you right away without a smile.","t":"我奶奶非常直率；她不喜歡你做的菜時，會馬上面無表情地告訴你。"},{"w":"blunt","p":"v.","d":"to make something weaker or less sharp","c":"使變鈍；減弱","s":"Cutting cardboard with your good scissors will quickly blunt the blades, so please use the old pair instead.","t":"用你的好剪刀剪紙板很快就會弄鈍刀刃，所以請改用舊的那把。"},{"w":"bluntly","p":"adv.","d":"in a direct way, without trying to be polite","c":"直率地；坦白地","s":"The coach told the team bluntly that they had lost because they were lazy in practice, and nobody dared to argue.","t":"教練直白地告訴球隊，他們輸球是因為練習時偷懶，沒有人敢反駁。"},{"w":"bluntness","p":"n.","d":"the habit of speaking in a very direct, honest way","c":"直率；坦率","s":"People who do not know him are often shocked by his bluntness, but his close friends appreciate that he never lies to them.","t":"不認識他的人常被他的直率嚇到，但他的好友很欣賞他從不對他們說謊。"},{"w":"bodily","p":"adj.","d":"relating to the human body","c":"身體的","s":"Sleep, food, and exercise are basic bodily needs, and students who ignore them often find it hard to focus in class.","t":"睡眠、食物和運動是基本的身體需求，忽略這些的學生常常很難在課堂上專心。","h":1},{"w":"bodily","p":"adv.","d":"by lifting or moving the whole body","c":"以整個身體；全身地","s":"The angry fan refused to leave his seat, so two security guards lifted him bodily and carried him out of the stadium.","t":"那位生氣的球迷拒絕離開座位，所以兩名警衛把他整個人抬起來，帶出體育場。"},{"w":"body","p":"n.","d":"the whole physical form of a person or animal","c":"身體","s":"Drinking enough water every day helps your body stay cool in hot weather and keeps your skin healthy, doctors say.","t":"醫生說，每天喝足夠的水有助於你的身體在炎熱天氣中保持涼爽，並讓皮膚健康。"},{"w":"bodily harm","p":"n.phr.","d":"physical injury to a person","c":"身體傷害","s":"The man was arrested for causing serious bodily harm to a shopkeeper during a fight over a parking space.","t":"那名男子因為在爭搶停車位的打架中對店主造成嚴重身體傷害而被逮捕。"},{"w":"bodyguard","p":"n.","d":"a person whose job is to protect someone important","c":"保鑣","s":"The famous singer always travels with a bodyguard, who walks beside her and keeps the crowds of fans at a safe distance.","t":"這位著名歌手出門總是帶著保鑣，他走在她身旁，讓成群的粉絲保持安全距離。"},{"w":"booklet","p":"n.","d":"a small, thin book with a paper cover that gives information","c":"小冊子","s":"The tourist center gives every visitor a free booklet with maps, bus times, and short descriptions of the main sights.","t":"遊客中心發給每位訪客一本免費的小冊子，裡面有地圖、公車時刻和主要景點的簡短介紹。","h":1},{"w":"book","p":"n.","d":"a set of printed pages fastened together inside a cover","c":"書","s":"My favorite book is about a boy who travels through time, and I have already read it four times since last summer.","t":"我最喜歡的書是關於一個穿越時空的男孩，從去年夏天以來我已經讀了四遍。"},{"w":"book","p":"v.","d":"to arrange to have a seat, room, or ticket at a future time","c":"預訂","s":"We should book the hotel rooms early because the city will be full of visitors during the lantern festival in February.","t":"我們應該早點預訂飯店房間，因為二月燈會期間這座城市會擠滿遊客。"},{"w":"instruction booklet","p":"n.phr.","d":"a small book that explains how to use something","c":"使用說明書","s":"Before you put the new bookshelf together, read the instruction booklet carefully so that you do not put the pieces in the wrong order.","t":"在組裝新書架之前，請仔細閱讀使用說明書，以免把零件裝錯順序。"},{"w":"bosom","p":"n.","d":"a woman's chest; the center of someone's feelings","c":"胸部；內心","s":"The mother held the crying baby close to her bosom and sang softly until he fell asleep in her arms.","t":"母親把哭泣的寶寶緊緊抱在胸前，輕聲唱歌直到他在她懷裡睡著。","h":1},{"w":"bosom friend","p":"n.phr.","d":"a very close friend you trust completely","c":"知己；摯友","s":"Lisa has been my bosom friend since elementary school, and we still tell each other everything, even though we live in different cities.","t":"麗莎從小學起就是我的知己，即使我們住在不同的城市，我們仍然什麼事都告訴對方。"},{"w":"in the bosom of","p":"phr.","d":"surrounded and protected by a loving group, such as a family","c":"在…的懷抱中","s":"After five hard years working abroad, he finally spent the New Year in the bosom of his family, eating hot pot and laughing all night.","t":"在國外辛苦工作五年後，他終於在家人的懷抱中過新年，整晚吃火鍋、開懷大笑。"},{"w":"boulevard","p":"n.","d":"a wide city street, often with trees along each side","c":"大道；林蔭大道","s":"The parade will move slowly down the main boulevard, so the police will close it to cars from eight in the morning.","t":"遊行隊伍會沿著主要大道緩緩前進，所以警方將從早上八點起禁止車輛通行。","h":1},{"w":"tree-lined boulevard","p":"n.phr.","d":"a wide street with rows of trees on both sides","c":"兩旁有樹的林蔭大道","s":"Every autumn, tourists walk along the tree-lined boulevard to take photos of the golden leaves falling onto the wide sidewalks.","t":"每年秋天，遊客沿著林蔭大道散步，拍下金黃的落葉飄到寬闊人行道上的照片。"},{"w":"stroll along the boulevard","p":"v.phr.","d":"to walk slowly and in a relaxed way down a wide street","c":"在大道上漫步","s":"On warm summer evenings, families like to stroll along the boulevard, stopping for ice cream and listening to the street musicians play.","t":"在溫暖的夏夜，家庭喜歡在大道上漫步，停下來買冰淇淋，聽街頭音樂家演奏。"},{"w":"boxing","p":"n.","d":"a sport in which two people fight with their fists wearing thick gloves","c":"拳擊","s":"My brother took up boxing to get fit, and after six months of training he is much stronger and more confident.","t":"我哥哥為了健身開始學拳擊，訓練六個月後他變得更強壯、更有自信。","h":1},{"w":"boxer","p":"n.","d":"a person who takes part in the sport of boxing","c":"拳擊手","s":"The young boxer trains five hours a day because he hopes to represent Taiwan at the next Olympic Games.","t":"這位年輕的拳擊手每天訓練五小時，因為他希望能代表台灣參加下一屆奧運。"},{"w":"box","p":"v.","d":"to fight someone with your fists as a sport","c":"打拳擊","s":"His grandfather used to box in the army, and he still shows the kids how to protect their faces with their hands.","t":"他爺爺以前在軍隊裡打拳擊，現在仍會教孩子們如何用手保護臉部。"},{"w":"boxing match","p":"n.phr.","d":"a boxing contest between two fighters","c":"拳擊比賽","s":"Thousands of fans stayed up until three in the morning to watch the boxing match live on television from Las Vegas.","t":"成千上萬的粉絲熬夜到凌晨三點，觀看從拉斯維加斯直播的拳擊比賽。"},{"w":"boxing ring","p":"n.phr.","d":"the square area with ropes around it where boxers fight","c":"拳擊台","s":"When the two fighters stepped into the boxing ring, the crowd became silent, and the only sound was the bell.","t":"當兩位選手踏上拳擊台時，觀眾安靜下來，唯一的聲音就是鈴聲。"},{"w":"boycott","p":"v.","d":"to refuse to buy, use, or take part in something as a protest","c":"拒買；聯合抵制","s":"Many customers decided to boycott the restaurant after a video showed the manager shouting at a young worker.","t":"在一支影片顯示經理對一位年輕員工大吼之後，許多顧客決定拒買那家餐廳。","h":1},{"w":"boycott","p":"n.","d":"the act of refusing to buy or use something as a protest","c":"聯合抵制","s":"The boycott of the shoe company lasted three months, and it ended only when the company promised to pay its workers fairly.","t":"對那家鞋業公司的聯合抵制持續了三個月，直到公司承諾公平支付員工薪資才結束。"},{"w":"call for a boycott","p":"v.phr.","d":"to publicly ask people to stop buying or using something","c":"呼籲抵制","s":"Several animal groups have started to call for a boycott of the circus because of the way it treats its elephants and tigers.","t":"好幾個動物保護團體開始呼籲抵制那個馬戲團，因為它對待大象和老虎的方式。"},{"w":"brace","p":"v.","d":"to get ready for something difficult or unpleasant","c":"做好準備（面對困難）","s":"Shop owners along the coast began to brace for the typhoon by covering their windows with wooden boards.","t":"沿海的店主開始用木板遮住窗戶，為颱風做好準備。","h":1},{"w":"brace","p":"n.","d":"something that supports or holds a part of the body or an object in place","c":"支架；護具","s":"After he hurt his knee playing basketball, the doctor told him to wear a brace for six weeks and avoid running.","t":"他打籃球傷了膝蓋後，醫生要他戴護具六週，並避免跑步。"},{"w":"braces","p":"n.","d":"metal wires fixed to the teeth to make them straight","c":"牙套；牙齒矯正器","s":"My sister got her braces last month, and now she cannot eat hard candy or chew gum for two whole years.","t":"我姐姐上個月裝了牙套，現在整整兩年不能吃硬糖或嚼口香糖。"},{"w":"brace yourself","p":"v.phr.","d":"to prepare yourself for a shock or something unpleasant","c":"做好心理準備","s":"Brace yourself before you look at the bill, because the repairs to the car cost much more than the mechanic first said.","t":"看帳單之前先做好心理準備，因為修車的費用比技工一開始說的貴得多。","a":"Brace yourself"},{"w":"bracelet","p":"n.","d":"a piece of jewelry worn around the wrist","c":"手鍊；手環","s":"She never takes off the silver bracelet her grandmother gave her, even when she swims or plays sports.","t":"她從不拿下奶奶送她的銀手鍊，即使游泳或運動時也戴著。"},{"w":"bra","p":"n.","d":"a piece of underwear that supports a woman's breasts","c":"胸罩","s":"The department store is having a sale this week, so my mother bought a new bra and some socks at half price.","t":"百貨公司這週在特價，所以我媽媽用半價買了一件新胸罩和幾雙襪子。","h":1},{"w":"brassiere","p":"n.","d":"the full, formal word for a bra","c":"胸罩（正式用語）","s":"The old shop sign still uses the word brassiere, which sounds very formal today because almost everyone just says bra.","t":"那家老店的招牌仍然用brassiere（胸罩）這個字，今天聽起來非常正式，因為幾乎每個人都只說 bra。"},{"w":"sports bra","p":"n.phr.","d":"a bra designed to be worn while exercising","c":"運動內衣","s":"Before the marathon, the coach reminded the women on the team to wear a comfortable sports bra and good running shoes.","t":"馬拉松前，教練提醒隊上的女生要穿舒適的運動內衣和好的跑鞋。"},{"w":"breadth","p":"n.","d":"the distance from one side of something to the other; width","c":"寬度","s":"The new bridge has a breadth of thirty meters, so it has room for four lanes of cars and two wide bicycle paths.","t":"新橋的寬度有三十公尺，所以有空間容納四線車道和兩條寬闊的自行車道。","h":1},{"w":"breadth of knowledge","p":"n.phr.","d":"a wide range of things that a person knows about","c":"知識的廣度","s":"The old professor's breadth of knowledge amazed us; he could talk about history, music, and science in a single conversation.","t":"老教授的知識廣度讓我們驚訝；他能在一次談話中聊歷史、音樂和科學。"},{"w":"broad","p":"adj.","d":"wide; including many different things","c":"寬的；廣泛的","s":"The river is so broad at this point that you can hardly see the people walking on the other side.","t":"這條河在這裡非常寬，你幾乎看不到對岸走路的人。"},{"w":"broaden","p":"v.","d":"to make something wider or to include more things","c":"拓寬；擴展","s":"Traveling to other countries can broaden your mind because you meet people whose ideas are very different from yours.","t":"到其他國家旅行可以開拓你的視野，因為你會遇到想法和你非常不同的人。"},{"w":"broadly","p":"adv.","d":"in a general way; widely","c":"大致上；廣泛地","s":"Broadly speaking, students who read for pleasure every day do better in writing than those who only read textbooks.","t":"大致上來說，每天為樂趣而閱讀的學生，寫作表現比只讀課本的學生好。","a":"Broadly"},{"w":"breakdown","p":"n.","d":"a time when a machine or system stops working","c":"故障；崩潰","s":"Our bus had a breakdown on the mountain road, so we waited two hours in the cold until another bus came to pick us up.","t":"我們的巴士在山路上故障了，所以我們在寒冷中等了兩小時，直到另一輛巴士來接我們。","h":1},{"w":"nervous breakdown","p":"n.phr.","d":"a time of serious mental illness caused by stress, when a person cannot live normally","c":"精神崩潰","s":"After working eighty hours a week for a year, the young lawyer suffered a nervous breakdown and had to rest at home for months.","t":"在一年內每週工作八十小時之後，這位年輕律師精神崩潰，不得不在家休養幾個月。"},{"w":"break down","p":"v.phr.","d":"to stop working (a machine or vehicle)","c":"（機器）故障","s":"The old washing machine finally broke down this morning, so I had to carry all our dirty clothes to the laundry down the street.","t":"舊洗衣機今天早上終於壞了，所以我得把所有髒衣服搬到街尾的洗衣店。","a":"broke down"},{"w":"break down","p":"v.phr.","d":"to lose control of your feelings and start crying","c":"情緒崩潰；崩潰大哭","s":"When the teacher read the kind letter from her former students, she broke down in front of the whole class and could not continue.","t":"當老師讀到以前學生寫來的溫暖信件時，她在全班面前崩潰大哭，無法繼續讀下去。","a":"broke down"},{"w":"breakup","p":"n.","d":"the end of a relationship, marriage, or group","c":"分手；破裂；解散","s":"After the breakup with her boyfriend, Mia spent more time with her friends and started learning to play the guitar.","t":"和男友分手後，米亞花更多時間和朋友在一起，並開始學彈吉他。","h":1},{"w":"break up","p":"v.phr.","d":"to end a romantic relationship","c":"分手","s":"The famous couple decided to break up after five years together, but they said they would always remain good friends.","t":"這對名人情侶在一起五年後決定分手，但他們說會永遠是好朋友。"},{"w":"break up","p":"v.phr.","d":"to separate into smaller pieces or parts","c":"分裂；弄碎","s":"The teacher asked us to break up the long article into short sections so that it would be easier to understand and remember.","t":"老師要我們把長文章分成幾個短段落，這樣比較容易理解和記憶。"},{"w":"break up with","p":"v.phr.","d":"to end a relationship with someone","c":"和某人分手","s":"She decided to break up with him because he kept lying about where he went on weekends and never apologized.","t":"她決定和他分手，因為他一直對週末去哪裡說謊，而且從不道歉。"}]},{"unit":5,"theme":"bribe – cashier","cards":[{"w":"bribe","p":"v.","d":"to give someone money or a gift so that they will do something dishonest for you","c":"賄賂；行賄","s":"The driver tried to bribe the police officer with two thousand dollars, but she refused the money and wrote him a bigger ticket.","t":"那位駕駛試圖用兩千元賄賂警察，但她拒收並開了一張更大的罰單給他。","h":1},{"w":"bribe","p":"n.","d":"money or a gift given to make someone do something dishonest","c":"賄賂；賄款","s":"The judge was sent to prison for ten years after reporters proved that he had accepted a bribe from a rich businessman.","t":"記者證明那位法官收了一名富商的賄賂後，他被判入獄十年。"},{"w":"bribery","p":"n.","d":"the crime of giving or taking bribes","c":"賄賂（行為）；行賄罪","s":"The mayor lost his job because of bribery, and three other officials in his office are now being questioned by the police.","t":"市長因為賄賂案丟了工作，他辦公室的另外三名官員現在正接受警方訊問。"},{"w":"take a bribe","p":"v.phr.","d":"to accept money or a gift in exchange for doing something dishonest","c":"收賄","s":"A good referee will never take a bribe, no matter how much money a team offers him to change the result of the game.","t":"好的裁判絕不會收賄，不管球隊給他多少錢要他改變比賽結果。"},{"w":"brink","p":"n.","d":"the edge of a cliff or steep place; the point just before something happens","c":"邊緣；（事情發生的）邊緣","s":"The hikers stood at the brink of the cliff and looked down at the river far below, holding tightly to the rope.","t":"登山客站在懸崖邊緣，緊抓著繩索，俯視下方遙遠的河流。","h":1},{"w":"on the brink of","p":"phr.","d":"very close to a bad or important situation","c":"瀕臨；在…的邊緣","s":"Because of years of hunting, the mountain tiger is now on the brink of extinction, and only about forty animals remain in the wild.","t":"由於多年來的獵捕，這種山地老虎現在瀕臨滅絕，野外只剩下大約四十隻。"},{"w":"the brink of war","p":"n.phr.","d":"the point at which a war is about to begin","c":"戰爭邊緣","s":"Fifty years ago, the two neighboring countries came to the brink of war over a small island, but a last-minute meeting kept the peace.","t":"五十年前，這兩個鄰國因為一座小島來到戰爭邊緣，但最後一刻的會談維持了和平。"},{"w":"broaden","p":"v.","d":"to make something wider or to include more things","c":"拓寬；擴展","s":"The government plans to broaden the narrow mountain road next year so that buses can finally reach the village safely.","t":"政府計畫明年拓寬那條狹窄的山路，這樣公車終於可以安全抵達村莊。","h":1},{"w":"broad","p":"adj.","d":"wide; including a large number of different things","c":"寬的；廣泛的","s":"The teacher has a broad smile on her face every morning, and students say it makes the classroom feel warm and friendly.","t":"老師每天早上臉上都掛著燦爛的笑容，學生說這讓教室感覺溫暖又友善。"},{"w":"broadly","p":"adv.","d":"in a general way; widely","c":"大致上；廣泛地","s":"The two reports reach broadly the same conclusion, although they use very different methods to collect their information.","t":"這兩份報告大致上得到相同的結論，雖然它們蒐集資料的方法非常不同。"},{"w":"breadth","p":"n.","d":"the distance from side to side; the wide range of something","c":"寬度；廣度","s":"What surprised the judges was the breadth of the young artist's work, which included paintings, photos, and even short films.","t":"讓評審驚訝的是這位年輕藝術家作品的廣度，包含繪畫、攝影，甚至短片。"},{"w":"broaden one's horizons","p":"v.phr.","d":"to learn about new things and gain wider experience","c":"開拓視野","s":"Studying abroad for a year helped my sister broaden her horizons, and she came home with new friends, new ideas, and better English.","t":"出國讀書一年幫助我姐姐開拓視野，她帶著新朋友、新想法和更好的英文回家。","a":"broaden her horizons"},{"w":"brochure","p":"n.","d":"a small book or folded paper with pictures that gives information about something","c":"小冊子；簡介","s":"I picked up a colorful brochure about the hot springs at the station, and now I really want to visit them this winter.","t":"我在車站拿了一本關於溫泉的彩色簡介手冊，現在我真的很想今年冬天去泡一泡。","h":1},{"w":"travel brochure","p":"n.phr.","d":"a small booklet that advertises trips and holiday places","c":"旅遊手冊","s":"The beach in the travel brochure looked clean and empty, but when we got there, it was crowded and covered with trash.","t":"旅遊手冊裡的海灘看起來乾淨又空曠，但我們到那裡時卻擠滿人，而且到處是垃圾。"},{"w":"pick up a brochure","p":"v.phr.","d":"to take a free information booklet from a place","c":"拿一本簡介","s":"If you are interested in the summer camp, you can pick up a brochure at the front desk and read about the activities and prices.","t":"如果你對夏令營有興趣，可以在櫃檯拿一本簡介，看看活動內容和價格。"},{"w":"broil","p":"v.","d":"to cook food under or over very strong direct heat","c":"烤（用高溫直接燒烤）","s":"My father likes to broil fish with a little salt and lemon, and the whole kitchen smells wonderful when it is done.","t":"我爸爸喜歡用一點鹽和檸檬來烤魚，烤好時整個廚房都香噴噴的。","h":1},{"w":"broiler","p":"n.","d":"the part of an oven that cooks food with strong heat from above; a young chicken for cooking","c":"烤箱上火；肉雞","s":"Put the cheese toast under the broiler for two minutes, but watch it carefully because it can burn very quickly.","t":"把起司吐司放在烤箱上火下烤兩分鐘，但要仔細看著，因為它很快就會燒焦。"},{"w":"broiled","p":"adj.","d":"cooked under or over strong direct heat","c":"烤的；炙烤的","s":"The restaurant is famous for its broiled chicken, which is cooked over a hot fire and served with rice and vegetables.","t":"這家餐廳以炙烤雞肉聞名，雞肉在旺火上烤熟，搭配米飯和蔬菜一起上桌。"},{"w":"brook","p":"n.","d":"a small river or stream","c":"小溪","s":"Behind my grandmother's house there is a clear brook where we used to catch tiny fish and cool our feet in summer.","t":"我奶奶家後面有一條清澈的小溪，我們以前夏天常在那裡抓小魚、泡腳消暑。","h":1},{"w":"babbling brook","p":"n.phr.","d":"a small stream that makes a soft, bubbling sound","c":"潺潺小溪","s":"We set up our tent beside a babbling brook, and the gentle sound of the water helped us fall asleep quickly that night.","t":"我們在一條潺潺小溪旁搭帳篷，輕柔的水聲讓我們那晚很快入睡。"},{"w":"mountain brook","p":"n.phr.","d":"a small stream that flows down a mountain","c":"山澗；山間小溪","s":"The water in the mountain brook is so cold and clean that hikers often fill their bottles there instead of carrying water up.","t":"山澗裡的水非常冰涼乾淨，登山客常在那裡裝水，而不是把水背上山。"},{"w":"broth","p":"n.","d":"thin soup made by boiling meat, bones, or vegetables in water","c":"高湯；清湯","s":"When I had a cold last week, my mother made me a bowl of hot chicken broth with ginger, and I felt better the next day.","t":"上週我感冒時，媽媽幫我煮了一碗加薑的熱雞湯，第二天我就覺得好多了。","h":1},{"w":"chicken broth","p":"n.phr.","d":"a thin soup made by boiling chicken in water","c":"雞高湯","s":"Many Taiwanese noodle shops cook their noodles in chicken broth rather than plain water because it gives the dish a richer taste.","t":"許多台灣麵店用雞高湯而不是白開水煮麵，因為這樣會讓這道菜更有滋味。"},{"w":"bone broth","p":"n.phr.","d":"a soup made by boiling animal bones for many hours","c":"大骨湯；骨頭高湯","s":"The chef cooks his bone broth for twelve hours, which is why the soup at his beef noodle shop tastes so deep and rich.","t":"這位主廚把大骨湯熬煮十二小時，這就是為什麼他牛肉麵店的湯頭如此濃郁。"},{"w":"brotherhood","p":"n.","d":"a feeling of friendship and support between people, as if they were brothers","c":"兄弟情誼；手足之情","s":"After living and training together for a year, the soldiers felt a strong sense of brotherhood that lasted for the rest of their lives.","t":"在一起生活和訓練一年後，這些士兵感受到強烈的兄弟情誼，這份情感持續了一輩子。","h":1},{"w":"brotherhood","p":"n.","d":"an organization of men with the same job, religion, or interest","c":"兄弟會；同業會","s":"The brotherhood of firefighters holds a dinner every year to honor members who died while saving others.","t":"消防員兄弟會每年舉辦晚宴，向為了救人而殉職的成員致敬。"},{"w":"brother","p":"n.","d":"a boy or man who has the same parents as you","c":"兄弟","s":"My older brother taught me how to ride a bicycle when I was six, and he ran beside me until I could balance alone.","t":"我六歲時哥哥教我騎腳踏車，他在旁邊跑，直到我能自己平衡。"},{"w":"brotherly","p":"adj.","d":"showing the kindness and love that a brother should show","c":"兄弟般的","s":"The older boys at the camp showed brotherly care for the younger ones, helping them carry bags and tie their shoes.","t":"營隊裡年紀較大的男孩對年紀小的孩子表現出兄弟般的關心，幫他們拿包包、綁鞋帶。"},{"w":"sisterhood","p":"n.","d":"a feeling of closeness and support among women","c":"姊妹情誼","s":"The women on the volleyball team have a deep sense of sisterhood, and they still meet for dinner ten years after graduating.","t":"排球隊的女生們有深厚的姊妹情誼，畢業十年後她們仍會聚餐。"},{"w":"bulky","p":"adj.","d":"large and heavy, and therefore hard to carry or move","c":"笨重的；龐大的","s":"The old television was so bulky that it took three people to carry it down the stairs and out to the truck.","t":"那台舊電視太笨重了，要三個人才能把它搬下樓梯、搬到卡車上。","h":1},{"w":"bulk","p":"n.","d":"the large size or main part of something","c":"大批；主體","s":"Students spend the bulk of their time at school sitting at desks, so teachers try to add short activities that let them move.","t":"學生在學校大部分的時間都坐在書桌前，所以老師會試著加入讓他們活動的短暫活動。"},{"w":"in bulk","p":"phr.","d":"in large amounts, usually at a cheaper price","c":"大量地（購買）","s":"Our family buys rice and toilet paper in bulk from the big store outside town because it saves us a lot of money.","t":"我們家從城外的大賣場大量購買米和衛生紙，因為這樣能省很多錢。"},{"w":"bureaucrat","p":"n.","d":"an official in a government office, especially one who follows rules too strictly","c":"官僚；公務員","s":"The young bureaucrat refused to accept my form because one box was empty, and he told me to come back the next week.","t":"那位年輕的公務員因為有一格沒填就拒收我的表格，還要我下週再來。","h":1},{"w":"bureaucracy","p":"n.","d":"a system of government with many rules and offices; too many official rules","c":"官僚體系；官僚作風","s":"It took my uncle six months and twelve different forms to open his small shop because of the city's slow bureaucracy.","t":"由於市政府緩慢的官僚體系，我叔叔花了六個月和十二份不同的表格才開了他的小店。"},{"w":"bureaucratic","p":"adj.","d":"involving many official rules and slow processes","c":"官僚的；繁文縟節的","s":"Getting a new passport used to be a bureaucratic nightmare, but now you can finish most of the steps online in ten minutes.","t":"以前辦新護照是一場官僚惡夢，但現在你可以在十分鐘內在線上完成大部分步驟。"},{"w":"bureau","p":"n.","d":"a government office or department","c":"局；處","s":"The weather bureau warned that a strong typhoon would hit the east coast tonight, so all schools in the area are closed tomorrow.","t":"氣象局警告今晚強颱將侵襲東海岸，所以該地區所有學校明天停課。"},{"w":"bypass","p":"v.","d":"to go around something instead of through it; to avoid a rule or step","c":"繞過；避開","s":"To save time, the taxi driver decided to bypass the crowded city center and take the new road along the river instead.","t":"為了節省時間，計程車司機決定繞過擁擠的市中心，改走河邊的新路。","h":1},{"w":"bypass","p":"n.","d":"a road that goes around a town so that traffic does not pass through it","c":"外環道；繞道","s":"Since the bypass opened last spring, far fewer trucks drive through our town, and the main street is much quieter now.","t":"自從外環道去年春天通車後，經過我們鎮上的卡車少了很多，大街現在安靜多了。"},{"w":"heart bypass","p":"n.phr.","d":"an operation that makes blood flow around a blocked part of the heart","c":"心臟繞道手術","s":"My grandfather had a heart bypass last year, and now he walks for thirty minutes every morning on the doctor's advice.","t":"我爺爺去年做了心臟繞道手術，現在他聽醫生的建議每天早上走路三十分鐘。"},{"w":"caffeine","p":"n.","d":"a chemical in coffee and tea that makes you feel more awake","c":"咖啡因","s":"Doctors say teenagers should not have too much caffeine, because it can make it hard for them to fall asleep at night.","t":"醫生說青少年不應攝取太多咖啡因，因為它會讓他們晚上難以入睡。","h":1},{"w":"caffeinated","p":"adj.","d":"containing caffeine","c":"含咖啡因的","s":"Energy drinks are heavily caffeinated, so our school has stopped selling them and now offers fruit juice and milk instead.","t":"能量飲料含大量咖啡因，所以我們學校已停止販售，現在改賣果汁和牛奶。"},{"w":"decaffeinated","p":"adj.","d":"having had most of the caffeine removed","c":"低咖啡因的；去咖啡因的","s":"My mother drinks only decaffeinated coffee after dinner, because a regular cup would keep her awake until two in the morning.","t":"我媽媽晚餐後只喝低咖啡因咖啡，因為一杯普通的咖啡會讓她清醒到凌晨兩點。"},{"w":"caffeine-free","p":"adj.","d":"containing no caffeine at all","c":"不含咖啡因的","s":"This herbal tea is completely caffeine-free, so it is a good choice for children or for anyone who wants a warm drink before bed.","t":"這種花草茶完全不含咖啡因，所以很適合孩子，或任何想在睡前喝杯熱飲的人。"},{"w":"calculator","p":"n.","d":"a small electronic machine used for doing math","c":"計算機","s":"Students may use a calculator during the science test, but they must put away their phones before the exam begins.","t":"學生在理化考試中可以使用計算機，但考試開始前必須把手機收起來。","h":1},{"w":"calculate","p":"v.","d":"to find an answer or amount by using numbers","c":"計算","s":"Before the trip, we sat down to calculate how much money we would need for train tickets, food, and two nights in a hotel.","t":"旅行前，我們坐下來計算火車票、食物和兩晚飯店需要多少錢。"},{"w":"calculation","p":"n.","d":"the process of using numbers to find an answer","c":"計算","s":"The engineer made a small mistake in her calculation, and because of that the bridge had to be checked again by another team.","t":"那位工程師在計算中犯了一個小錯，因此橋樑必須由另一個團隊重新檢查。"},{"w":"pocket calculator","p":"n.phr.","d":"a small calculator that is easy to carry","c":"袖珍計算機","s":"My grandfather still keeps a pocket calculator in his shirt pocket, although his phone can do the same job much faster.","t":"我爺爺的襯衫口袋裡仍放著一台袖珍計算機，雖然他的手機可以更快完成同樣的工作。"},{"w":"calligraphy","p":"n.","d":"the art of writing beautifully with a brush or special pen","c":"書法","s":"Every Saturday morning, my grandfather practices Chinese calligraphy for an hour, and he says it calms his mind like meditation.","t":"每個星期六早上，我爺爺都會練一小時中國書法，他說這像冥想一樣能讓他心靜。","h":1},{"w":"calligrapher","p":"n.","d":"a person who is skilled at writing beautifully","c":"書法家","s":"The famous calligrapher wrote the sign for the new temple, and visitors often stop to admire the strong, flowing characters.","t":"這位著名的書法家為新寺廟題了匾額，遊客常停下來欣賞那些蒼勁流暢的字。"},{"w":"Chinese calligraphy","p":"n.phr.","d":"the traditional art of writing Chinese characters with a brush","c":"中國書法","s":"In our school's culture week, foreign students tried Chinese calligraphy for the first time, and many of them found holding the brush quite difficult.","t":"在我們學校的文化週，外國學生第一次嘗試中國書法，許多人覺得拿毛筆相當困難。"},{"w":"calligraphy brush","p":"n.phr.","d":"a soft brush used for writing characters with ink","c":"毛筆","s":"My art teacher showed us how to hold a calligraphy brush straight up and move it slowly so that every line is thick and even.","t":"美術老師教我們如何把毛筆拿直、慢慢移動，讓每一筆都粗而均勻。"},{"w":"cape","p":"n.","d":"a large piece of land that sticks out into the sea","c":"岬；海角","s":"From the lighthouse on the cape, you can watch the fishing boats return to the harbor every evening at sunset.","t":"從海角上的燈塔，你可以看到漁船每天傍晚在日落時回港。","h":1},{"w":"cape","p":"n.","d":"a loose coat without sleeves that hangs from the shoulders","c":"斗篷；披風","s":"In the school play, the little boy wore a red cape and pretended to fly across the stage like a superhero.","t":"在學校話劇中，小男孩披著紅色披風，假裝像超級英雄一樣飛過舞台。"},{"w":"the Cape of Good Hope","p":"n.phr.","d":"the famous cape at the southern tip of Africa","c":"好望角","s":"Hundreds of years ago, ships from Europe had to sail around the Cape of Good Hope to reach Asia, and the journey took many months.","t":"幾百年前，歐洲的船必須繞過好望角才能到達亞洲，航程要花好幾個月。"},{"w":"capsule","p":"n.","d":"a small round container of medicine that you swallow","c":"膠囊","s":"The doctor told me to take one capsule after breakfast and one after dinner, and to drink a full glass of water with each.","t":"醫生要我早餐後吃一顆膠囊、晚餐後吃一顆，每次都要配一整杯水。","h":1},{"w":"capsule","p":"n.","d":"the part of a spacecraft in which people travel","c":"太空艙","s":"The astronauts returned to Earth in a small capsule that landed in the ocean, where a ship was waiting to pick them up.","t":"太空人乘坐一個小太空艙返回地球，落在海上，那裡有一艘船等著接他們。"},{"w":"time capsule","p":"n.phr.","d":"a container of objects from the present that is buried to be opened in the future","c":"時空膠囊","s":"Our class buried a time capsule under the big tree, and we promised to come back and open it together in twenty years.","t":"我們班在大樹下埋了一個時空膠囊，並約定二十年後一起回來打開它。"},{"w":"capsule hotel","p":"n.phr.","d":"a cheap hotel where each guest sleeps in a very small box-shaped room","c":"膠囊旅館","s":"When I missed the last train in Tokyo, I spent the night in a capsule hotel near the station for only twenty dollars.","t":"我在東京錯過末班電車時，只花二十美元就在車站附近的膠囊旅館過了一夜。"},{"w":"caption","p":"n.","d":"words printed under a picture that explain what it shows","c":"圖片說明；標題","s":"The caption under the photo said it was taken in 1950, but the cars in the picture look much newer than that.","t":"照片下方的圖片說明寫著拍攝於一九五〇年，但照片裡的汽車看起來新得多。","h":1},{"w":"caption","p":"v.","d":"to write words that explain a picture or video","c":"為…加上說明文字","s":"Please caption every photo in the school newspaper with the names of the students, so readers know who is who.","t":"請為校刊中的每張照片加上學生姓名的說明，讓讀者知道誰是誰。"},{"w":"captioned","p":"adj.","d":"having words on the screen that show what is being said","c":"有字幕的","s":"The library shows captioned movies on Friday afternoons so that students who are learning English can read along while they listen.","t":"圖書館星期五下午播放有字幕的電影，讓學英文的學生可以邊聽邊讀。"},{"w":"closed captions","p":"n.phr.","d":"written text on a screen that shows the words being spoken, which can be turned on or off","c":"隱藏式字幕","s":"If you cannot hear the video clearly, turn on the closed captions and the words will appear at the bottom of the screen.","t":"如果你聽不清楚影片，打開隱藏式字幕，文字就會出現在螢幕底部。"},{"w":"captive","p":"n.","d":"a person or animal that is kept somewhere and not allowed to leave","c":"俘虜；囚徒","s":"The pirates kept their captive in the ship's dark cellar for weeks, until the navy finally found the ship and freed him.","t":"海盜把俘虜關在船上黑暗的地窖好幾週，直到海軍終於找到那艘船並救出他。","h":1},{"w":"captivity","p":"n.","d":"the state of being kept in a place and not allowed to leave","c":"囚禁；圈養","s":"Pandas born in captivity often cannot survive in the wild because they have never learned to find food on their own.","t":"在圈養中出生的熊貓常常無法在野外生存，因為牠們從未學會自己找食物。","h":1},{"w":"captive","p":"adj.","d":"kept in a place and unable to leave or escape","c":"被囚禁的；被俘的","s":"The captive birds in the market looked sad and tired, so the animal group bought them all and set them free in the forest.","t":"市場裡那些被關住的鳥看起來又悲傷又疲倦，所以動保團體把牠們全買下來，放回森林。"},{"w":"in captivity","p":"phr.","d":"kept in a zoo, cage, or prison rather than being free","c":"在圈養中；被囚禁","s":"The old elephant has lived in captivity for forty years, and the zoo is now building a much larger space for her to walk in.","t":"這頭老象已經在圈養中生活了四十年，動物園現在正為牠建造一個大得多的活動空間。"},{"w":"hold sb captive","p":"v.phr.","d":"to keep someone as a prisoner","c":"囚禁某人","s":"The robbers held the manager captive for six hours inside the bank until the police agreed to let them leave in a car.","t":"搶匪在銀行裡把經理囚禁了六小時，直到警方同意讓他們開車離開。","a":"held the manager captive"},{"w":"captor","p":"n.","d":"a person who keeps someone as a prisoner","c":"捕獲者；綁匪","s":"The kidnapped boy later told the police that his captor had given him food and water but never let him see daylight.","t":"被綁架的男孩後來告訴警方，他的綁匪給他食物和水，但從不讓他看到日光。"},{"w":"cardboard","p":"n.","d":"thick, stiff paper used for making boxes","c":"紙板；硬紙板","s":"The children made a castle out of old cardboard and painted it grey, and it stood in the corner of the classroom for a month.","t":"孩子們用舊紙板做了一座城堡並塗成灰色，它在教室角落放了一個月。","h":1},{"w":"cardboard box","p":"n.phr.","d":"a box made of thick, stiff paper","c":"紙箱","s":"When we moved to the new apartment, we packed all our books into a dozen large cardboard boxes and labeled each one with a marker.","t":"我們搬到新公寓時，把所有的書裝進十幾個大紙箱，並用麥克筆在每個箱子上做標記。","a":"cardboard boxes"},{"w":"cardboard cutout","p":"n.phr.","d":"a life-size picture of a person printed on stiff paper and cut out","c":"人形立牌","s":"Fans lined up to take photos with a cardboard cutout of the singer outside the concert hall because the real star was busy backstage.","t":"歌迷在音樂廳外排隊和歌手的人形立牌合照，因為真正的明星正在後台忙碌。"},{"w":"cardinal","p":"n.","d":"a very high-ranking priest in the Roman Catholic Church","c":"樞機主教","s":"The cardinal traveled from Rome to visit the small church in the mountains, and hundreds of people waited outside to see him.","t":"樞機主教從羅馬前來拜訪山區的小教堂，數百人在外面等著想見他一面。","h":1},{"w":"cardinal","p":"adj.","d":"most important or basic","c":"主要的；基本的","s":"Honesty is a cardinal rule in our family, so my parents are never angry about a mistake, only about a lie.","t":"誠實是我們家的基本規則，所以我父母從不因為犯錯而生氣，只會因為說謊而生氣。"},{"w":"cardinal","p":"n.","d":"a small North American bird with bright red feathers","c":"北美紅雀","s":"A bright red cardinal landed on the snowy branch outside my window, and its color looked amazing against the white snow.","t":"一隻鮮紅的紅雀落在我窗外積雪的樹枝上，牠的顏色在白雪中顯得非常驚豔。"},{"w":"cardinal number","p":"n.phr.","d":"a number such as one, two, or three that shows how many","c":"基數","s":"In today's English class we learned that cardinal numbers like one and two tell you how many, while first and second tell you the order.","t":"今天英文課我們學到，像 one 和 two 這樣的基數告訴你數量，而 first 和 second 則表示順序。","a":"cardinal numbers"},{"w":"cardinal rule","p":"n.phr.","d":"the most important rule that must always be followed","c":"基本原則；金科玉律","s":"The cardinal rule of swimming is never to swim alone, because even strong swimmers can get into trouble in cold or deep water.","t":"游泳的基本原則是絕對不要獨自游泳，因為即使泳技好的人也可能在冰冷或深水中遇到麻煩。"},{"w":"carefree","p":"adj.","d":"having no worries or problems","c":"無憂無慮的","s":"I miss the carefree days of elementary school, when my biggest problem was deciding which game to play after lunch.","t":"我懷念小學那些無憂無慮的日子，那時我最大的問題是決定午餐後要玩哪種遊戲。","h":1},{"w":"careless","p":"adj.","d":"not paying enough attention, so that mistakes happen","c":"粗心的","s":"He lost ten points on the math test because of careless mistakes, such as writing a plus sign instead of a minus sign.","t":"他數學考試因為粗心的錯誤丟了十分，例如把減號寫成加號。"},{"w":"careful","p":"adj.","d":"paying close attention so that you avoid mistakes or danger","c":"小心的；仔細的","s":"Be careful when you cross this street, because the cars come around the corner very fast and the drivers cannot see you.","t":"過這條街時要小心，因為汽車轉彎過來的速度很快，駕駛看不到你。"},{"w":"care","p":"n.","d":"attention given to avoid mistakes; the act of looking after someone","c":"小心；照顧","s":"The nurse lifted the baby with great care and placed him gently in his mother's arms for the first time.","t":"護士非常小心地抱起嬰兒，第一次輕輕地把他放進母親的懷裡。"},{"w":"carefree childhood","p":"n.phr.","d":"a time of growing up with no worries","c":"無憂無慮的童年","s":"My grandmother says she had a carefree childhood in the countryside, climbing trees and swimming in the river all summer long.","t":"我奶奶說她在鄉下度過了無憂無慮的童年，整個夏天都在爬樹和在河裡游泳。"},{"w":"caretaker","p":"n.","d":"a person whose job is to look after a building or a person","c":"管理員；看護者","s":"The school caretaker arrives at six every morning to unlock the gates, turn on the lights, and check that the classrooms are clean.","t":"學校管理員每天早上六點到校開門、開燈，並檢查教室是否乾淨。","h":1},{"w":"take care of","p":"v.phr.","d":"to look after someone or something","c":"照顧","s":"While my parents are away on business this week, I have to take care of my little brother and cook dinner for both of us.","t":"這週我父母出差時，我必須照顧弟弟，並為我們兩個做晚餐。"},{"w":"care for","p":"v.phr.","d":"to look after someone who is old, young, or sick","c":"照料；照護","s":"Nurses in the hospital care for patients day and night, so it is a job that needs both patience and a kind heart.","t":"醫院的護士日夜照護病人，所以這是一份需要耐心和善心的工作。"},{"w":"caretaker government","p":"n.phr.","d":"a government that stays in power only until a new one is chosen","c":"看守政府","s":"After the election results were questioned, a caretaker government ran the country for three months until a new leader was finally chosen.","t":"選舉結果受到質疑後，一個看守政府管理國家三個月，直到新領導人終於被選出。"},{"w":"carton","p":"n.","d":"a box made of thick paper or plastic used for holding food or drink","c":"紙盒；紙箱","s":"There is only one egg left in the carton, so could you buy a new one on your way home from school today?","t":"紙盒裡只剩一顆蛋了，你今天放學回家的路上可以買一盒新的嗎？","h":1},{"w":"milk carton","p":"n.phr.","d":"a paper box that holds milk","c":"牛奶盒","s":"Please rinse the empty milk carton and flatten it before you put it in the recycling bin outside the kitchen door.","t":"請把空的牛奶盒沖洗乾淨並壓扁，再放進廚房門外的回收桶。"},{"w":"a carton of","p":"n.phr.","d":"a box containing a certain number of things, such as eggs or cigarettes","c":"一盒…","s":"My mother asked me to pick up a carton of eggs and some bread from the store, but I forgot the bread completely.","t":"媽媽要我去商店買一盒蛋和一些麵包，但我把麵包完全忘了。"},{"w":"cashier","p":"n.","d":"a person whose job is to take money from customers in a shop or bank","c":"收銀員；出納員","s":"The cashier at the supermarket smiled and asked if I needed a bag, and then she counted out my change carefully.","t":"超市的收銀員微笑著問我需不需要袋子，然後仔細地數出零錢給我。","h":1},{"w":"cash","p":"n.","d":"money in the form of coins and paper notes","c":"現金","s":"The small noodle shop does not accept credit cards, so make sure you bring enough cash to pay for your lunch.","t":"這家小麵店不接受信用卡，所以要確定你帶了足夠的現金付午餐。"},{"w":"cash","p":"v.","d":"to exchange a check for money","c":"兌現（支票）","s":"My aunt went to the bank this morning to cash the check her company gave her, and she was back home within an hour.","t":"我阿姨今天早上去銀行兌現公司給她的支票，一小時內就回到家了。"},{"w":"cash register","p":"n.phr.","d":"a machine in a shop that records sales and holds the money","c":"收銀機","s":"The new worker was nervous on her first day because she had never used a cash register before, but she learned quickly.","t":"新員工第一天很緊張，因為她從沒用過收銀機，但她學得很快。"},{"w":"cashier's desk","p":"n.phr.","d":"the place in a shop or bank where you pay","c":"收銀台；出納櫃台","s":"Take your books to the cashier's desk near the exit, and the clerk there will put them in a bag after you pay.","t":"把書拿到出口附近的收銀台，付錢後那裡的店員會幫你裝袋。"}]},{"unit":6,"theme":"casualty – civilize","cards":[{"w":"casualty","p":"n.","d":"a person who is hurt or killed in an accident, war, or disaster","c":"傷亡者；受害者","s":"The bus hit a tree on the mountain road last night, but luckily there was only one casualty, and he is already out of the hospital.","t":"昨晚公車在山路上撞到樹，但幸運的是只有一名傷亡者，而且他已經出院了。","h":1},{"w":"heavy casualties","p":"n.phr.","d":"a large number of people hurt or killed","c":"重大傷亡","s":"The news reported heavy casualties after the earthquake, so hospitals in the city asked people to come and give blood.","t":"新聞報導地震後有重大傷亡，所以市內的醫院請民眾前來捐血。"},{"w":"casual","p":"adj.","d":"relaxed and not formal; not planned","c":"輕鬆的；非正式的；隨意的","s":"You can wear casual clothes to the picnic on Saturday because nobody is going to dress up for a day in the park.","t":"星期六的野餐你可以穿輕鬆的衣服，因為沒有人會為了在公園玩一天而盛裝打扮。"},{"w":"casually","p":"adv.","d":"in a relaxed way, without much thought or care","c":"隨意地；漫不經心地","s":"He casually mentioned that he had won the speech contest, as if it were nothing special, and we all cheered loudly.","t":"他隨意地提到他贏了演講比賽，好像那沒什麼特別，我們全都大聲歡呼。"},{"w":"catastrophe","p":"n.","d":"a sudden event that causes great damage or suffering","c":"大災難；浩劫","s":"When the old dam broke after a week of rain, it was the worst catastrophe the valley had seen in a hundred years.","t":"老水壩在連下一週雨後崩塌，那是這個山谷一百年來最嚴重的大災難。","h":1},{"w":"catastrophic","p":"adj.","d":"causing great damage or suffering","c":"災難性的","s":"Scientists warn that the melting of the ice could have catastrophic effects on small islands, which may disappear under the sea.","t":"科學家警告冰層融化可能對小島造成災難性的影響，這些小島可能會消失在海裡。"},{"w":"catastrophically","p":"adv.","d":"in a way that causes great damage","c":"災難性地","s":"The company's new phone failed catastrophically in its first month, and thousands of customers asked for their money back.","t":"這家公司的新手機在第一個月就災難性地失敗了，數千名顧客要求退款。"},{"w":"cater","p":"v.","d":"to provide food and drinks for a party or event","c":"承辦（宴會）飲食","s":"My aunt's small restaurant will cater our school's graduation party, so we will have plenty of sandwiches and fruit for everyone.","t":"我阿姨的小餐廳將承辦我們學校畢業派對的飲食，所以我們會有足夠的三明治和水果給大家。","h":1},{"w":"cater to","p":"v.phr.","d":"to provide the things that a particular group of people want","c":"迎合；滿足…的需求","s":"The new bookstore tries to cater to young readers, and it even has a corner with comics and soft chairs for them.","t":"這家新書店努力迎合年輕讀者，甚至有一個擺著漫畫和軟椅子的角落給他們。"},{"w":"cater for","p":"v.phr.","d":"to provide what is needed for a number of people","c":"為…提供所需；滿足","s":"This hotel can cater for up to three hundred guests at a time, which makes it popular for weddings and company dinners.","t":"這家飯店一次可為多達三百位客人提供餐飲服務，因此很受婚宴和公司晚宴的歡迎。"},{"w":"caterer","p":"n.","d":"a person or company that provides food for events","c":"宴會餐飲業者；外燴業者","s":"The caterer arrived two hours before the party and set up long tables of hot food in the garden.","t":"外燴業者在派對前兩小時抵達，並在花園裡擺好一長排熱食的桌子。"},{"w":"catering","p":"n.","d":"the business of providing food for events","c":"餐飲服務（業）","s":"After she finished cooking school, Lisa started her own catering business, and now she cooks for weddings every weekend.","t":"麗莎從烹飪學校畢業後，開了自己的餐飲服務公司，現在她每個週末都為婚禮做菜。"},{"w":"caterpillar","p":"n.","d":"a small long creature with many legs that later becomes a butterfly or moth","c":"毛毛蟲","s":"A fat green caterpillar was eating the leaves of my cabbage plant, so I gently moved it to the grass outside the garden.","t":"一隻肥肥的綠色毛毛蟲正在吃我高麗菜的葉子，所以我輕輕把它移到花園外的草地上。","h":1},{"w":"cocoon","p":"n.","d":"the soft case a caterpillar makes around itself before it becomes a butterfly or moth","c":"蛹；繭","s":"The students watched the cocoon on the branch every day, and one morning a beautiful butterfly came out of it.","t":"學生們每天觀察樹枝上的繭，有一天早上一隻美麗的蝴蝶從裡面飛了出來。"},{"w":"caterpillar tracks","p":"n.phr.","d":"the metal belts on a heavy vehicle such as a tank that let it move over rough ground","c":"履帶","s":"The big digger moves on caterpillar tracks instead of wheels, so it can climb over mud and rocks without getting stuck.","t":"這台大型挖土機用履帶而不是輪子移動，所以它能越過泥巴和石頭而不會卡住。"},{"w":"cavity","p":"n.","d":"a hole in a tooth caused by decay","c":"蛀牙；齲洞","s":"The dentist found a small cavity in my back tooth and told me to eat less candy and brush more carefully.","t":"牙醫在我的後牙發現一個小蛀牙，並要我少吃糖果、更仔細刷牙。","h":1},{"w":"cavity","p":"n.","d":"a hollow space inside something solid","c":"洞；腔；凹處","s":"The birds built their nest inside a cavity in the old tree, where the eggs were safe from wind and rain.","t":"鳥兒在老樹的一個樹洞裡築巢，蛋在那裡不受風雨侵襲。"},{"w":"fill a cavity","p":"v.phr.","d":"to put material into a hole in a tooth to repair it","c":"補牙","s":"It took the dentist only twenty minutes to fill the cavity, and she said I would not feel any pain after an hour.","t":"牙醫只花了二十分鐘補好蛀牙，她說一小時後我就不會感到任何疼痛了。","a":"fill the cavity"},{"w":"cave","p":"n.","d":"a large natural hole in the side of a hill or under the ground","c":"洞穴","s":"We explored a cool, dark cave near the beach, and our guide showed us old drawings on the stone walls.","t":"我們探索了海灘附近一個涼爽黑暗的洞穴，導遊讓我們看石牆上的古老圖畫。"},{"w":"celery","p":"n.","d":"a vegetable with long, pale green stems that is often eaten raw","c":"芹菜；西洋芹","s":"Mom asked me to wash the celery and cut it into thin sticks, because she wanted to serve it with a cheese dip.","t":"媽媽要我把西洋芹洗好並切成細條，因為她想配著起司醬一起端上桌。","h":1},{"w":"a stick of celery","p":"n.phr.","d":"one long stem of celery","c":"一根芹菜","s":"Instead of eating chips after school, my sister always takes a stick of celery from the fridge and eats it with peanut butter.","t":"放學後我妹妹不吃洋芋片，總是從冰箱拿一根芹菜配花生醬吃。"},{"w":"chopped celery","p":"n.phr.","d":"celery cut into small pieces","c":"切碎的芹菜","s":"The recipe says to add two cups of chopped celery to the soup, and then let everything cook slowly for an hour.","t":"食譜說要在湯裡加兩杯切碎的芹菜，然後讓所有食材慢慢煮一小時。"},{"w":"cellular","p":"adj.","d":"relating to the cells of living things","c":"細胞的","s":"Our biology teacher explained that all living things have a cellular structure, and she showed us onion skin under a microscope.","t":"我們的生物老師解釋所有生物都有細胞的結構，並讓我們在顯微鏡下觀察洋蔥皮。","h":1},{"w":"cell","p":"n.","d":"the smallest living part of a plant or animal","c":"細胞","s":"Every human body is made of billions of tiny cells, and each one is far too small to see with your eyes.","t":"每個人體都是由數十億個微小的細胞組成，每一個都小到無法用肉眼看見。","a":"cells"},{"w":"cell","p":"n.","d":"a small room where a prisoner is kept","c":"牢房","s":"The prisoner spent ten years in a tiny cell with one small window, and he read hundreds of books to pass the time.","t":"那名囚犯在一間只有一扇小窗的狹小牢房裡度過十年，他讀了數百本書來打發時間。"},{"w":"cell phone","p":"n.phr.","d":"a telephone you can carry with you","c":"手機","s":"Please turn off your cell phone before the movie starts, or at least put it on silent mode so it does not ring.","t":"請在電影開始前關掉你的手機，或至少調成靜音模式，以免它響起來。"},{"w":"cellular phone","p":"n.phr.","d":"a mobile phone (formal name)","c":"行動電話","s":"The first cellular phone was as big as a brick and cost thousands of dollars, so very few people owned one in the 1980s.","t":"第一支行動電話像磚頭一樣大，而且要價數千美元，所以在一九八〇年代很少人擁有。"},{"w":"Celsius","p":"n.","d":"a scale for measuring temperature in which water freezes at 0 and boils at 100","c":"攝氏","s":"The weather report says it will be thirty-five degrees Celsius this afternoon, so remember to drink a lot of water.","t":"氣象報告說今天下午會是攝氏三十五度，所以記得要多喝水。","h":1},{"w":"degrees Celsius","p":"n.phr.","d":"units of temperature on the Celsius scale","c":"攝氏…度","s":"Water boils at one hundred degrees Celsius, which is why you can see steam rising from the kettle when it is ready.","t":"水在攝氏一百度沸騰，這就是為什麼水壺燒好時你會看到蒸氣升起。"},{"w":"Fahrenheit","p":"n.","d":"a scale for measuring temperature used mainly in the United States","c":"華氏","s":"My American cousin said it was ninety degrees Fahrenheit in Texas, and I had to change it to Celsius to understand how hot that was.","t":"我的美國表哥說德州是華氏九十度，我必須換算成攝氏才懂那有多熱。"},{"w":"cement","p":"n.","d":"a gray powder mixed with water and sand that becomes hard and holds bricks together","c":"水泥","s":"The workers mixed sand, water, and cement in a large bucket, and then they used the gray paste to lay the bricks.","t":"工人們在大桶裡混合沙子、水和水泥，然後用那灰色的漿來砌磚。","h":1},{"w":"cement","p":"v.","d":"to make a relationship, idea, or position stronger and more certain","c":"鞏固；加強","s":"Working together on the science project helped cement the friendship between the two girls, who are now best friends.","t":"一起做科學專題有助於鞏固那兩個女孩之間的友誼，她們現在是最好的朋友。"},{"w":"cement a relationship","p":"v.phr.","d":"to make a relationship stronger","c":"鞏固關係","s":"The two countries signed a trade agreement last week, and the leaders hope it will cement the relationship between their peoples.","t":"兩國上週簽署了貿易協定，領導人希望這能鞏固兩國人民之間的關係。","a":"cement the relationship"},{"w":"concrete","p":"n.","d":"a hard building material made from cement, sand, small stones, and water","c":"混凝土","s":"Most tall buildings in the city are made of steel and concrete, so they can stand strong even in a big earthquake.","t":"市內大多數高樓是用鋼筋和混凝土建造的，所以即使遇到大地震也能屹立不搖。"},{"w":"census","p":"n.","d":"an official count of all the people living in a country or area","c":"人口普查","s":"The government holds a census every ten years to find out how many people live in each town and how old they are.","t":"政府每十年舉行一次人口普查，以了解每個城鎮有多少人居住以及他們的年齡。","h":1},{"w":"conduct a census","p":"v.phr.","d":"to carry out an official count of the population","c":"進行人口普查","s":"Thousands of workers were hired to conduct a census last year, and they visited every home in the country with long forms.","t":"去年雇用了數千名工作人員來進行人口普查，他們帶著長長的表格拜訪全國每一戶人家。"},{"w":"census data","p":"n.phr.","d":"the information collected in a census","c":"人口普查資料","s":"According to the latest census data, more young people are leaving small towns and moving to big cities to find jobs.","t":"根據最新的人口普查資料，越來越多年輕人離開小鎮，搬到大城市找工作。"},{"w":"ceramic","p":"adj.","d":"made of clay that has been baked until it is hard","c":"陶瓷的","s":"My grandmother keeps her flowers in a beautiful blue ceramic pot that she bought from a small shop in the mountains.","t":"我奶奶把花放在一個漂亮的藍色陶瓷花盆裡，那是她在山上一家小店買的。","h":1},{"w":"ceramic","p":"n.","d":"an object made of baked clay","c":"陶瓷製品","s":"This cup is a hand-made ceramic from Japan, so please wash it gently and never put it in the dishwasher.","t":"這個杯子是來自日本的手工陶瓷製品，所以請輕輕清洗，絕不要放進洗碗機。"},{"w":"ceramics","p":"n.","d":"the art of making objects from baked clay","c":"陶藝","s":"In our art class this term we are learning ceramics, and each student will make a bowl and paint it with colorful glaze.","t":"這學期的美術課我們在學陶藝，每個學生都會做一個碗並塗上彩色釉料。"},{"w":"pottery","p":"n.","d":"pots, dishes, and other objects made from clay; the activity of making them","c":"陶器；製陶","s":"The old town is famous for its pottery, and tourists love to watch the workers shape wet clay into bowls and vases.","t":"這座古鎮以陶器聞名，觀光客喜歡看工匠把濕黏土塑成碗和花瓶。"},{"w":"certify","p":"v.","d":"to state officially that something is true or that someone has passed a test","c":"證明；認證","s":"A doctor must certify that you are healthy before you can join the swimming team, so bring the form to your checkup.","t":"醫生必須證明你身體健康，你才能加入游泳隊，所以健檢時把表格帶去。","h":1},{"w":"certificate","p":"n.","d":"an official paper that proves something is true or that you have finished a course","c":"證書；證明書","s":"After finishing the three-month computer course, every student received a certificate that they could show to future employers.","t":"完成三個月的電腦課程後，每位學生都拿到一張可以給未來雇主看的證書。"},{"w":"certified","p":"adj.","d":"officially recognized as having the skills or qualities needed","c":"經認證的；合格的","s":"Only a certified teacher is allowed to give lessons at this driving school, so you know the lessons will be safe.","t":"只有合格的教練才能在這家駕訓班授課，所以你知道課程一定安全。"},{"w":"certification","p":"n.","d":"the act of officially proving something; the paper that proves it","c":"認證；證明","s":"To work as a lifeguard, you need to get certification in first aid, which takes about two weekends of training.","t":"要當救生員，你需要取得急救認證，這大約需要兩個週末的訓練。"},{"w":"birth certificate","p":"n.phr.","d":"an official paper that records when and where a person was born","c":"出生證明","s":"When you apply for a passport, you must bring your birth certificate and two photos to the office with your parents.","t":"申請護照時，你必須帶著出生證明和兩張照片，和父母一起到辦事處。"},{"w":"chairperson","p":"n.","d":"the person in charge of a meeting, committee, or organization","c":"主席","s":"Ms. Lin was chosen as the chairperson of the parents' meeting, and she made sure that everyone had a chance to speak.","t":"林女士被選為家長會的主席，她確保每個人都有發言的機會。","h":1},{"w":"chairman","p":"n.","d":"a man who is in charge of a meeting or company","c":"主席；董事長（男）","s":"The chairman of the company stood up at the end of the meeting and thanked all the workers for their hard year.","t":"公司的董事長在會議結束時站起來，感謝所有員工辛苦的一年。"},{"w":"chairwoman","p":"n.","d":"a woman who is in charge of a meeting or company","c":"主席；董事長（女）","s":"As the new chairwoman of the school board, Mrs. Wang promised to listen to students as well as to teachers and parents.","t":"身為學校董事會的新任主席，王太太承諾會傾聽學生以及老師和家長的意見。"},{"w":"chair","p":"n.","d":"the person leading a meeting; the position of leader","c":"主席（職位）","s":"The chair asked everyone to turn off their phones so that the meeting could begin on time without any interruptions.","t":"主席請大家關掉手機，讓會議能準時開始而不受干擾。"},{"w":"chair","p":"v.","d":"to be in charge of a meeting","c":"主持（會議）","s":"Our teacher asked Kevin to chair the class meeting this week because he is calm and lets everyone share ideas.","t":"老師這週請凱文主持班會，因為他很冷靜，而且會讓每個人分享想法。"},{"w":"champagne","p":"n.","d":"a French white wine with bubbles, often drunk at celebrations","c":"香檳","s":"When the clock struck twelve on New Year's Eve, my father opened a bottle of champagne and everyone raised a glass.","t":"跨年夜時鐘敲十二點時，我爸爸開了一瓶香檳，大家舉杯慶祝。","h":1},{"w":"pop open the champagne","p":"v.phr.","d":"to open a bottle of champagne to celebrate something","c":"開香檳慶祝","s":"As soon as the team heard that they had won the contest, they popped open the champagne and sprayed it all over the locker room.","t":"球隊一聽到他們贏得比賽，就開香檳慶祝，把它噴得整個休息室都是。","a":"popped open the champagne"},{"w":"sparkling","p":"adj.","d":"(of a drink) having bubbles; shining brightly","c":"有氣泡的；閃亮的","s":"I do not drink alcohol, so I ordered a glass of sparkling water with lemon while my friends had wine with dinner.","t":"我不喝酒，所以我朋友晚餐喝葡萄酒時，我點了一杯加檸檬的氣泡水。"},{"w":"chant","p":"n.","d":"words or a phrase that a group of people shout or sing again and again","c":"反覆喊的口號；吟唱","s":"The chant of the fans grew louder and louder in the last minute of the game, and the players felt their energy.","t":"比賽最後一分鐘，球迷的口號聲越來越大，球員們感受到了他們的能量。","h":1},{"w":"chant","p":"v.","d":"to sing or shout the same words again and again","c":"反覆喊；吟誦","s":"Hundreds of students began to chant the name of their school as the runners came around the final corner.","t":"當跑者繞過最後一個彎道時，數百名學生開始反覆喊著他們學校的名字。"},{"w":"chant a slogan","p":"v.phr.","d":"to repeat a short phrase loudly as a group","c":"高喊口號","s":"The workers marched through the city and chanted a slogan about fair pay, and many people on the street clapped for them.","t":"工人們遊行穿過城市，高喊關於合理薪資的口號，街上許多人為他們鼓掌。","a":"chanted a slogan"},{"w":"charitable","p":"adj.","d":"giving money or help to people who need it","c":"慈善的；樂善好施的","s":"Mr. Chen is a charitable man who gives part of his salary to poor children every month without telling anyone.","t":"陳先生是個樂善好施的人，他每個月把部分薪水捐給貧困的孩子，而且不告訴任何人。","h":1},{"w":"charitable","p":"adj.","d":"kind and not judging other people too hard","c":"寬厚的；仁慈的","s":"Try to be charitable when your little brother makes a mistake, because he is only six and is still learning the rules.","t":"你弟弟犯錯時試著寬厚一點，因為他才六歲，還在學規則。"},{"w":"charity","p":"n.","d":"an organization that helps people in need; the act of giving to such people","c":"慈善機構；慈善","s":"Every winter our class collects warm coats for a local charity that gives them to families who cannot afford new clothes.","t":"每年冬天我們班都會為當地一家慈善機構收集保暖外套，他們會把外套送給買不起新衣的家庭。"},{"w":"charity event","p":"n.phr.","d":"an activity held to raise money for people in need","c":"慈善活動","s":"The school will hold a charity event next Saturday, and all the money from the food stands will go to the children's hospital.","t":"學校下週六將舉辦一場慈善活動，所有小吃攤的收入都會捐給兒童醫院。"},{"w":"uncharitable","p":"adj.","d":"unkind and judging other people too hard","c":"苛刻的；不寬厚的","s":"It was uncharitable of you to laugh at her accent, because she has only been learning English for one year.","t":"你笑她的口音實在太苛刻了，因為她才學英文一年。"},{"w":"checkup","p":"n.","d":"a general examination by a doctor or dentist to see if you are healthy","c":"健康檢查；體檢","s":"Even if you feel fine, you should visit the dentist for a checkup twice a year so that small problems are found early.","t":"即使你覺得沒事，也應該每年去看牙醫做兩次檢查，這樣小問題才能及早發現。","h":1},{"w":"have a checkup","p":"v.phr.","d":"to go to a doctor for a general health examination","c":"做健康檢查","s":"My grandfather has a checkup every spring, and the doctor always tells him to walk more and eat less salt.","t":"我爺爺每年春天都做健康檢查，醫生總是叫他多走路、少吃鹽。","a":"has a checkup"},{"w":"check","p":"v.","d":"to look at something carefully to make sure it is correct or safe","c":"檢查；核對","s":"Please check your answers one more time before you hand in the test, because careless mistakes are easy to miss.","t":"交考卷前請再檢查一次你的答案，因為粗心的錯誤很容易被忽略。"},{"w":"check up on","p":"v.phr.","d":"to find out how someone is or whether they are doing what they should","c":"查看；關心（某人的情況）","s":"My mother calls my grandmother every evening to check up on her, since she lives alone in the countryside.","t":"我媽媽每天晚上打電話給奶奶關心她的狀況，因為她一個人住在鄉下。"},{"w":"chemist","p":"n.","d":"a scientist who studies chemistry","c":"化學家","s":"My uncle works as a chemist in a large laboratory, where he tries to create cleaning products that are safer for children.","t":"我叔叔在一間大型實驗室當化學家，他在那裡試著研發對兒童更安全的清潔產品。","h":1},{"w":"chemist","p":"n.","d":"(British) a person or shop that sells medicine","c":"藥師；藥局（英式）","s":"In London, I went to the chemist on the corner to buy some medicine for my cold, and the pharmacist was very helpful.","t":"在倫敦，我去街角的藥局買治感冒的藥，藥師非常熱心幫忙。"},{"w":"chemistry","p":"n.","d":"the science that studies what things are made of and how they change","c":"化學","s":"In today's chemistry class, we mixed two clear liquids and watched them slowly turn bright blue in the glass.","t":"今天的化學課上，我們混合了兩種透明液體，看著它們在玻璃杯中慢慢變成亮藍色。"},{"w":"chemical","p":"n.","d":"a substance made by or used in chemistry","c":"化學物質","s":"Farmers should be careful with this chemical, because it kills insects but can also harm the bees that help the plants grow.","t":"農民使用這種化學物質時應該小心，因為它能殺死害蟲，但也可能傷害幫助植物生長的蜜蜂。"},{"w":"chestnut","p":"n.","d":"a large shiny brown nut that can be roasted and eaten","c":"栗子","s":"In winter, you can smell sweet roasted chestnuts at the night market, and people eat them warm straight from the paper bag.","t":"冬天時，你可以在夜市聞到香甜的烤栗子味，人們直接從紙袋裡拿出來趁熱吃。","a":"chestnuts","h":1},{"w":"chestnut","p":"adj.","d":"of a deep reddish-brown color","c":"栗色的；紅棕色的","s":"The girl with long chestnut hair in the front row is my cousin, and she just moved here from Kaohsiung last month.","t":"前排那個有一頭栗色長髮的女孩是我表妹，她上個月剛從高雄搬來。"},{"w":"roasted chestnuts","p":"n.phr.","d":"chestnuts cooked over heat until they are soft and sweet","c":"糖炒栗子；烤栗子","s":"Grandpa always buys a warm bag of roasted chestnuts on cold evenings, and he peels them for me while we walk home.","t":"爺爺總是在寒冷的夜晚買一袋熱呼呼的烤栗子，走回家的路上他會剝給我吃。"},{"w":"chestnut tree","p":"n.phr.","d":"the tall tree that produces chestnuts","c":"栗子樹","s":"There is a huge chestnut tree in the middle of the park, and in autumn children run under it to pick up the fallen nuts.","t":"公園中央有一棵巨大的栗子樹，秋天時孩子們在樹下跑來跑去撿掉落的栗子。"},{"w":"chili","p":"n.","d":"a small red or green pepper with a very hot taste","c":"辣椒","s":"Be careful with that red chili in your noodles, because it looks small but it will make your mouth burn for minutes.","t":"小心你麵裡那根紅辣椒，因為它看起來很小，但會讓你的嘴巴辣好幾分鐘。","h":1},{"w":"chili sauce","p":"n.phr.","d":"a hot, spicy sauce made from chilies","c":"辣椒醬","s":"My brother puts chili sauce on almost everything he eats, even on his eggs at breakfast, which the rest of us find strange.","t":"我哥哥幾乎在所有食物上都加辣椒醬，連早餐的蛋也不例外，我們其他人都覺得很奇怪。"},{"w":"chili pepper","p":"n.phr.","d":"the plant or fruit of the chili","c":"辣椒（植物／果實）","s":"We grow a chili pepper plant on our balcony, and by the end of summer it is covered with dozens of bright red fruits.","t":"我們在陽台上種了一株辣椒，到夏末時它結滿了幾十個鮮紅色的果實。"},{"w":"chili powder","p":"n.phr.","d":"dried chilies ground into a fine powder used in cooking","c":"辣椒粉","s":"The recipe calls for one teaspoon of chili powder, but you can add more if your family likes very spicy food.","t":"食譜要求一茶匙的辣椒粉，但如果你的家人喜歡很辣的食物，可以多加一些。"},{"w":"chimpanzee","p":"n.","d":"an African ape with black hair that is very intelligent and closely related to humans","c":"黑猩猩","s":"At the zoo we watched a chimpanzee use a stick to get honey out of a hole, and the guide said it is one of our closest relatives.","t":"在動物園我們看到一隻黑猩猩用棍子從洞裡取蜂蜜，導覽員說它是我們最近的親戚之一。","h":1},{"w":"chimp","p":"n.","d":"a short, informal word for chimpanzee","c":"黑猩猩（口語）","s":"The baby chimp held on to its mother's back as she climbed the tree, and all the children laughed at its funny face.","t":"小黑猩猩緊抱著媽媽的背，媽媽爬上樹時，所有的小孩都被它滑稽的表情逗笑了。"},{"w":"ape","p":"n.","d":"a large animal like a monkey without a tail, such as a chimpanzee or gorilla","c":"猿；類人猿","s":"Unlike a monkey, an ape has no tail, and scientists say these animals can learn to use simple tools and even some signs.","t":"和猴子不同，猿沒有尾巴，科學家說這些動物能學會使用簡單的工具，甚至一些手語。"},{"w":"chirp","p":"v.","d":"(of birds or insects) to make short, high sounds","c":"（鳥、蟲）啁啾；唧唧叫","s":"Every morning at five, the little birds outside my window begin to chirp loudly and wake me up before my alarm rings.","t":"每天早上五點，我窗外的小鳥開始大聲啁啾叫，在鬧鐘響之前就把我叫醒。","h":1},{"w":"chirp","p":"n.","d":"a short, high sound made by a bird or insect","c":"啁啾聲；唧唧聲","s":"In the quiet countryside at night, you can hear the soft chirp of crickets coming from every corner of the garden.","t":"在寧靜的鄉間夜裡，你可以聽到花園每個角落傳來蟋蟀輕柔的唧唧聲。"},{"w":"chirping","p":"adj.","d":"making short, high sounds","c":"啁啾鳴叫的","s":"The chirping birds in the tall trees made the park feel alive, and we sat on the grass listening to them for an hour.","t":"高樹上啁啾鳴叫的鳥兒讓公園充滿生氣，我們坐在草地上聽了它們一個小時。"},{"w":"cholesterol","p":"n.","d":"a fatty substance in the blood; too much of it can cause heart disease","c":"膽固醇","s":"The doctor told my father that his cholesterol was too high, so he must eat less fried food and walk every day.","t":"醫生告訴我爸爸他的膽固醇太高了，所以他必須少吃油炸食物並且每天走路。","h":1},{"w":"high cholesterol","p":"n.phr.","d":"a condition in which there is too much cholesterol in the blood","c":"高膽固醇","s":"People with high cholesterol should avoid butter and fatty meat, and they should have their blood checked at least once a year.","t":"高膽固醇的人應該避免奶油和肥肉，而且至少一年要檢查一次血液。"},{"w":"lower one's cholesterol","p":"v.phr.","d":"to reduce the amount of cholesterol in the blood","c":"降低膽固醇","s":"Eating oats for breakfast and exercising three times a week helped my uncle lower his cholesterol in only six months.","t":"早餐吃燕麥並且每週運動三次，讓我叔叔在短短六個月內降低了膽固醇。","a":"lower his cholesterol"},{"w":"cholesterol level","p":"n.phr.","d":"the amount of cholesterol in a person's blood","c":"膽固醇指數","s":"Your cholesterol level looks much better than last year, the nurse said with a smile, so keep up the healthy eating.","t":"護士微笑著說，你的膽固醇指數比去年好多了，所以請繼續保持健康的飲食。"},{"w":"cigar","p":"n.","d":"a thick roll of dried tobacco leaves that people smoke","c":"雪茄","s":"Grandpa likes to sit on the porch after dinner and smoke a thick brown cigar, although Grandma hates the smell.","t":"爺爺喜歡晚餐後坐在門廊抽一根粗粗的棕色雪茄，雖然奶奶很討厭那個味道。","h":1},{"w":"cigarette","p":"n.","d":"a thin roll of tobacco in paper that people smoke","c":"香菸","s":"The sign at the station says that anyone who smokes a cigarette on the platform will have to pay a fine of ten thousand dollars.","t":"車站的告示寫著，任何在月台上抽香菸的人都要繳一萬元的罰款。"},{"w":"light a cigar","p":"v.phr.","d":"to make a cigar start burning","c":"點雪茄","s":"The old man took out a match to light a cigar, but his daughter reminded him that smoking is not allowed inside the restaurant.","t":"老先生拿出火柴要點雪茄，但他女兒提醒他餐廳裡禁止吸菸。"},{"w":"civilize","p":"v.","d":"to teach people to behave in a more organized and polite way; to bring a society to a more developed stage","c":"使文明；教化","s":"Long ago, some kings believed they could civilize faraway peoples by forcing new laws and religion on them, an idea most people now reject.","t":"很久以前，有些國王認為可以藉由強迫遠方民族接受新法律和宗教來教化他們，如今大多數人都反對這種想法。","h":1},{"w":"civilized","p":"adj.","d":"polite and reasonable; having a well-developed society","c":"文明的；有教養的","s":"Even though the two teams disagreed strongly, they held a civilized discussion and shook hands at the end of the debate.","t":"儘管兩隊意見強烈分歧，他們仍進行了一場文明的討論，並在辯論結束時握手。"},{"w":"uncivilized","p":"adj.","d":"rude or wild; not having a developed society","c":"不文明的；野蠻的","s":"Shouting at the waiter and throwing food on the floor is uncivilized behavior, and the manager asked the man to leave.","t":"對服務生大吼並把食物丟在地上是不文明的行為，經理請那個男人離開。"},{"w":"civilization","p":"n.","d":"a society with its own culture, laws, and way of life, especially an advanced one","c":"文明","s":"The ancient Egyptian civilization built huge pyramids and wrote with pictures thousands of years before modern cities existed.","t":"古埃及文明在現代城市出現前數千年就建造了巨大的金字塔，並用圖畫文字書寫。"},{"w":"civilian","p":"n.","d":"a person who is not a member of the army or police","c":"平民","s":"During the war, many brave doctors stayed in the city to help every injured civilian who came to the hospital.","t":"戰爭期間，許多勇敢的醫生留在城裡，幫助每一位來到醫院受傷的平民。"}]},{"unit":7,"theme":"clam – concession","cards":[{"w":"clam","p":"n.","d":"a sea animal with a shell in two parts that you can eat","c":"蛤蜊","s":"At the seafood restaurant by the harbor, we ordered a plate of clams cooked with garlic and basil, and it was gone in minutes.","t":"在港口旁的海鮮餐廳，我們點了一盤用大蒜和九層塔炒的蛤蜊，幾分鐘就吃光了。","a":"clams","h":1},{"w":"clam chowder","p":"n.phr.","d":"a thick creamy soup made with clams and potatoes","c":"蛤蜊巧達濃湯","s":"On a cold evening in Boston, nothing warms you up better than a bowl of hot clam chowder with a piece of fresh bread.","t":"在波士頓寒冷的夜晚，沒有什麼比一碗熱蛤蜊巧達濃湯配一塊新鮮麵包更暖身的了。"},{"w":"clam up","p":"v.phr.","d":"to suddenly stop talking, usually because you are shy or afraid","c":"閉口不談；突然沉默","s":"My little brother talks all the time at home, but he tends to clam up whenever a stranger asks him a question.","t":"我弟弟在家話很多，但每當陌生人問他問題時，他就會閉口不談。"},{"w":"clasp","p":"v.","d":"to hold someone or something tightly in your hands or arms","c":"緊握；緊抱","s":"The frightened child continued to clasp her mother's hand tightly until the doctor finished giving her the shot.","t":"受驚的孩子一直緊握著媽媽的手，直到醫生打完針。","h":1},{"w":"clasp","p":"n.","d":"a small metal object that fastens a bag, belt, or piece of jewelry","c":"扣環；釦子","s":"The clasp on my grandmother's old necklace is broken, so I am taking it to the jewelry shop to have it fixed before her birthday.","t":"我奶奶舊項鍊上的扣環壞了，所以我要在她生日前拿去珠寶店修理。"},{"w":"clasp hands","p":"v.phr.","d":"to hold hands tightly, often as a sign of friendship or agreement","c":"緊握雙手","s":"After the long peace talks ended, the two leaders stood up to clasp hands in front of the cameras and smiled at each other.","t":"漫長的和平談判結束後，兩位領導人站起來在鏡頭前緊握雙手，相視而笑。"},{"w":"clearance","p":"n.","d":"official permission to do something or enter a place","c":"許可；批准","s":"The pilot waited on the runway for ten minutes because the plane could not take off without clearance from the control tower.","t":"飛行員在跑道上等了十分鐘，因為沒有塔台的許可飛機無法起飛。","h":1},{"w":"clearance sale","p":"n.phr.","d":"a sale in which a shop sells old stock cheaply to make room for new goods","c":"清倉大拍賣","s":"The sports shop is having a clearance sale this weekend, and I bought a pair of running shoes for less than half the usual price.","t":"那家運動用品店這個週末清倉大拍賣，我用不到平常一半的價錢買了一雙跑鞋。"},{"w":"security clearance","p":"n.phr.","d":"official permission to see secret information or enter protected places","c":"安全許可","s":"Only workers with the highest level of security clearance are allowed into the room where the government keeps its most secret files.","t":"只有擁有最高等級安全許可的員工才能進入政府存放最機密檔案的房間。"},{"w":"clear","p":"v.","d":"to remove things from a place; to give official permission","c":"清除；清理；批准","s":"After the typhoon passed, it took the workers three days to clear the fallen trees and mud from the mountain road.","t":"颱風過後，工人花了三天才清除山路上倒下的樹木和泥土。"},{"w":"climax","p":"n.","d":"the most exciting or important point of a story or event","c":"高潮；頂點","s":"The movie reaches its climax when the hero finally discovers who stole the painting, and the whole theater gasped at that moment.","t":"當主角終於發現是誰偷了那幅畫時，電影到達高潮，那一刻整個戲院的人都倒抽一口氣。","h":1},{"w":"climax","p":"v.","d":"to reach the most exciting or important point","c":"達到高潮","s":"The three-day music festival will climax on Sunday night with a fireworks show over the river that everyone is waiting for.","t":"為期三天的音樂節將在星期日晚上以河上的煙火秀達到高潮，大家都在期待。"},{"w":"anticlimax","p":"n.","d":"a disappointing end to something exciting","c":"虎頭蛇尾；令人失望的結局","s":"After months of waiting, the final episode of the series was an anticlimax, and many fans complained online that nothing really happened.","t":"等了好幾個月後，這部影集的最後一集虎頭蛇尾，許多粉絲在網路上抱怨根本沒發生什麼事。"},{"w":"reach a climax","p":"v.phr.","d":"to arrive at the most intense or exciting point","c":"達到高潮","s":"The argument between the two neighbors began to reach a climax when one of them called the police about the noise.","t":"當其中一位鄰居因為噪音報警時，兩人之間的爭吵開始達到高潮。"},{"w":"clockwise","p":"adv.","d":"in the same direction as the hands of a clock move","c":"順時針地","s":"To open the jar, turn the lid clockwise first to loosen it, and then turn it the other way until it comes off.","t":"要打開罐子，先把蓋子順時針轉一下鬆開，然後往另一個方向轉直到它脫落。","h":1},{"w":"clockwise","p":"adj.","d":"moving in the same direction as the hands of a clock","c":"順時針的","s":"The teacher asked the students to pass their papers in a clockwise direction so that every sheet would end up on her desk.","t":"老師要學生以順時針方向傳考卷，這樣每張考卷最後都會到她桌上。"},{"w":"counterclockwise","p":"adv.","d":"in the opposite direction to the hands of a clock","c":"逆時針地","s":"If you want to turn off the water completely, you have to turn the handle counterclockwise until it stops moving.","t":"如果你想把水完全關掉，必須把把手逆時針轉到轉不動為止。"},{"w":"clock","p":"n.","d":"a device that shows the time, usually on a wall or table","c":"時鐘","s":"The old clock in the hallway strikes every hour, and when I was small the sound used to wake me up at night.","t":"走廊上的舊時鐘每小時報時一次，我小時候那聲音常在晚上把我吵醒。"},{"w":"clone","p":"n.","d":"an exact copy of a plant, animal, or thing","c":"複製品；複製動物","s":"Dolly the sheep was the first clone of an adult animal, and her birth in 1996 made scientists around the world very excited.","t":"桃莉羊是第一隻由成年動物複製出來的動物，牠一九九六年的誕生讓全世界的科學家非常興奮。","h":1},{"w":"clone","p":"v.","d":"to make an exact copy of a plant, animal, or thing","c":"複製","s":"Some scientists hope to clone animals that have died out, but many people believe that such experiments should not be allowed.","t":"有些科學家希望複製已經滅絕的動物，但許多人認為不該允許這樣的實驗。"},{"w":"cloning","p":"n.","d":"the process of making an exact copy of a living thing","c":"複製（技術）","s":"The debate about human cloning has gone on for years, and most countries have laws that do not allow it.","t":"關於人類複製的爭論已持續多年，大多數國家都有法律禁止這麼做。"},{"w":"cloned","p":"adj.","d":"made as an exact copy of another living thing","c":"複製的","s":"The cloned cat looked exactly like the original one, but its owner said that the two animals had completely different personalities.","t":"那隻複製的貓看起來和原來那隻一模一樣，但主人說兩隻動物的個性完全不同。"},{"w":"closure","p":"n.","d":"the act of closing a business, school, or road for good or for a time","c":"關閉；停業","s":"The closure of the old factory left two hundred people without jobs, and many families had to move away to find work.","t":"舊工廠的關閉讓兩百人失去工作，許多家庭不得不搬走找工作。","h":1},{"w":"closure","p":"n.","d":"the feeling that a sad experience is finished and you can move on","c":"（情感上的）了結；釋懷","s":"Visiting her grandfather's grave finally gave her a sense of closure, and she stopped dreaming about him every night.","t":"去探望爺爺的墓終於讓她感到釋懷，她不再每晚夢到他。"},{"w":"close","p":"v.","d":"to shut something; to stop a business or activity","c":"關閉；結束","s":"The bakery on the corner will close next month because the owner is eighty years old and wants to rest at last.","t":"轉角的麵包店下個月將結束營業，因為老闆已經八十歲，想終於休息一下。"},{"w":"road closure","p":"n.phr.","d":"the act of stopping traffic from using a road","c":"道路封閉","s":"Because of the road closure for the marathon, the buses took a different route this morning, and I was late for school.","t":"因為馬拉松的道路封閉，今天早上公車改道，所以我上學遲到了。"},{"w":"coalition","p":"n.","d":"a group of political parties or countries that join together for a purpose","c":"聯盟；聯合政府","s":"No single party won enough seats in the election, so three parties formed a coalition to run the country together.","t":"選舉中沒有單一政黨贏得足夠席次，所以三個政黨組成聯盟共同治理國家。","h":1},{"w":"coalition government","p":"n.phr.","d":"a government formed by two or more parties working together","c":"聯合政府","s":"A coalition government is often slow to make decisions because the different parties must agree with each other before any law can pass.","t":"聯合政府做決定常常很慢，因為不同政黨必須先彼此同意，法案才能通過。"},{"w":"form a coalition","p":"v.phr.","d":"to join together with other groups for a common purpose","c":"組成聯盟","s":"Several small environmental groups decided to form a coalition so that their voice would be louder when they talked to the city government.","t":"幾個小型環保團體決定組成聯盟，這樣他們和市政府對話時聲音會更大。"},{"w":"coastline","p":"n.","d":"the land along the edge of the sea, as seen from above or on a map","c":"海岸線","s":"Taiwan's eastern coastline is famous for its high cliffs and clear blue water, and many cyclists ride along it every spring.","t":"台灣東部的海岸線以高聳的懸崖和清澈的藍色海水聞名，每年春天許多單車騎士沿著它騎行。","h":1},{"w":"coast","p":"n.","d":"the area of land next to the sea","c":"海岸","s":"My family drove down the west coast last summer, stopping at small fishing towns to try the local seafood.","t":"去年夏天我們全家沿著西海岸開車南下，在小漁村停留品嚐當地海鮮。"},{"w":"coastal","p":"adj.","d":"near or relating to the coast","c":"沿海的；海岸的","s":"Many coastal towns depend on tourism, so a dirty beach can hurt their shops and hotels for the whole season.","t":"許多沿海小鎮依靠觀光業，所以一片骯髒的海灘可能會讓它們的商店和飯店整季生意受損。"},{"w":"rocky coastline","p":"n.phr.","d":"a coast with many rocks and cliffs instead of sandy beaches","c":"多岩石的海岸線","s":"Ships must sail carefully near the rocky coastline of the northern island, where several boats have crashed in heavy fog.","t":"船隻在北方小島的岩石海岸線附近必須小心航行，好幾艘船曾在濃霧中撞上那裡。"},{"w":"collision","p":"n.","d":"an accident in which two moving things hit each other","c":"碰撞；相撞","s":"A collision between a bus and a truck on the highway this morning injured six people and blocked traffic for three hours.","t":"今天早上高速公路上一輛公車和一輛卡車的相撞造成六人受傷，交通堵塞三小時。","h":1},{"w":"collide","p":"v.","d":"to hit something or someone while moving","c":"相撞；碰撞","s":"Two cyclists tried to pass each other on the narrow bridge and began to collide, but luckily neither of them fell into the river.","t":"兩位騎士在狹窄的橋上試圖互相超越而相撞，但幸運的是沒有人掉進河裡。"},{"w":"collide with","p":"v.phr.","d":"to crash into something or someone","c":"與…相撞","s":"The small fishing boat collided with a rock in the dark, and the fishermen had to swim to the shore to save their lives.","t":"那艘小漁船在黑暗中撞上岩石，漁民們必須游到岸邊逃生。","a":"collided with"},{"w":"head-on collision","p":"n.phr.","d":"a crash in which the fronts of two vehicles hit each other","c":"迎面相撞","s":"The driver fell asleep and crossed into the other lane, causing a head-on collision that sent both cars to the repair shop for weeks.","t":"駕駛睡著後開進對向車道，造成迎面相撞，兩輛車都進修車廠修了好幾週。"},{"w":"colloquial","p":"adj.","d":"used in everyday conversation, not in formal writing","c":"口語的；非正式的","s":"Words like \"gonna\" and \"wanna\" are colloquial, so you should avoid them when you write an essay for the university exam.","t":"像 gonna 和 wanna 這樣的字是口語的，所以寫大學考試的作文時應該避免使用。","h":1},{"w":"colloquially","p":"adv.","d":"in the informal language of everyday conversation","c":"口語地；以非正式說法","s":"The disease is known colloquially as \"the flu,\" although doctors use a much longer medical name for it in their reports.","t":"這種疾病口語上稱為「流感」，雖然醫生在報告中使用更長的醫學名稱。"},{"w":"colloquialism","p":"n.","d":"a word or phrase used in informal conversation","c":"口語用語；俗語","s":"My English teacher explained that \"hang out\" is a colloquialism, which means to spend relaxed time with friends.","t":"我的英文老師解釋說 hang out 是一個口語用語，意思是和朋友一起悠閒地度過時光。"},{"w":"colloquial English","p":"n.phr.","d":"the everyday spoken form of English","c":"口語英文","s":"Watching American TV shows is a good way to learn colloquial English, since textbooks usually teach only formal sentences.","t":"看美國電視節目是學習口語英文的好方法，因為課本通常只教正式的句子。"},{"w":"comet","p":"n.","d":"a bright object with a long tail that moves around the sun","c":"彗星","s":"Last night we climbed to the top of the hill to see the comet, which will not pass near Earth again for seventy years.","t":"昨晚我們爬到山頂去看那顆彗星，它要七十年後才會再次靠近地球。","h":1},{"w":"Halley's Comet","p":"n.phr.","d":"a famous comet that can be seen from Earth about every 76 years","c":"哈雷彗星","s":"My grandfather saw Halley's Comet in 1986, and he hopes I will be able to watch it with my own children when it returns in 2061.","t":"我爺爺在一九八六年看過哈雷彗星，他希望二〇六一年它回來時，我能和我的孩子一起觀看。"},{"w":"the tail of a comet","p":"n.phr.","d":"the long bright stream of gas and dust behind a comet","c":"彗星的尾巴","s":"Through the telescope, the tail of the comet looked like a soft white brush stroke painted across the dark night sky.","t":"透過望遠鏡，彗星的尾巴看起來像一道柔和的白色筆觸，畫在漆黑的夜空中。","a":"the tail of the comet"},{"w":"commonplace","p":"adj.","d":"happening often and therefore not special or surprising","c":"平常的；司空見慣的","s":"Twenty years ago a video call was something amazing, but today it is commonplace for students to see their teacher on a screen.","t":"二十年前視訊通話是件很神奇的事，但今天學生在螢幕上看到老師已經很平常了。","h":1},{"w":"commonplace","p":"n.","d":"something that happens often and is not unusual","c":"常事；平凡的事","s":"Heavy traffic has become a commonplace in this city, so most people leave home an hour early to get to work on time.","t":"交通壅塞在這座城市已成為常事，所以大多數人提早一小時出門才能準時上班。"},{"w":"common","p":"adj.","d":"happening often; shared by many people","c":"常見的；共同的","s":"Colds are very common in winter, so remember to wash your hands often and get enough sleep to stay healthy.","t":"冬天感冒很常見，所以記得常洗手、睡眠充足以保持健康。"},{"w":"commonly","p":"adv.","d":"usually; by most people","c":"通常；普遍地","s":"Rice is commonly eaten at every meal in Taiwan, while people in Europe are more likely to eat bread or potatoes.","t":"在台灣每餐通常都吃米飯，而歐洲人比較可能吃麵包或馬鈴薯。"},{"w":"commonwealth","p":"n.","d":"a group of countries or states joined together for a shared purpose; a nation","c":"聯邦；國協","s":"Australia is officially called a commonwealth because its six states agreed in 1901 to join together under one national government.","t":"澳洲正式名稱為聯邦，因為它的六個州在一九〇一年同意在一個全國政府之下合併。","h":1},{"w":"the Commonwealth","p":"n.phr.","d":"the group of countries that were once part of the British Empire","c":"大英國協","s":"Every four years, athletes from the Commonwealth meet for their own games, which are a bit like a smaller Olympics.","t":"每四年，來自大英國協的運動員會聚在一起舉辦他們自己的運動會，有點像小型的奧運。"},{"w":"wealth","p":"n.","d":"a large amount of money and possessions","c":"財富","s":"The old man gave most of his wealth to the children's hospital, saying that he could not take it with him when he died.","t":"那位老先生把大部分財富捐給兒童醫院，他說人死了什麼也帶不走。"},{"w":"communicative","p":"adj.","d":"willing to talk and share information with people","c":"善於溝通的；健談的","s":"The new student was very quiet at first, but after a few weeks she became much more communicative and now talks to everyone.","t":"新來的學生一開始很安靜，但幾週後她變得健談多了，現在會和每個人聊天。","h":1},{"w":"communicate","p":"v.","d":"to share information or feelings with others by speaking, writing, or signs","c":"溝通；傳達","s":"Even though they do not speak the same language, the two children communicate with each other easily through drawings and gestures.","t":"雖然這兩個孩子說的語言不同，他們透過畫圖和手勢就能輕鬆地溝通。"},{"w":"communication","p":"n.","d":"the process of sharing information or ideas","c":"溝通；通訊","s":"Good communication between parents and teachers helps children do better at school, so our school holds a meeting every two months.","t":"家長和老師之間良好的溝通有助於孩子在學校表現更好，所以我們學校每兩個月開一次會。"},{"w":"communicative skills","p":"n.phr.","d":"the ability to express ideas clearly and understand others","c":"溝通技巧","s":"Employers today want workers with strong communicative skills, not just people who can get high scores on written tests.","t":"今天的雇主想要具備良好溝通技巧的員工，而不只是能在筆試中拿高分的人。"},{"w":"comparative","p":"adj.","d":"judged by comparing with something else; relating to comparison","c":"比較的；相對的","s":"After years of war, the country finally enjoyed a period of comparative peace, although small problems still appeared from time to time.","t":"經過多年戰爭，這個國家終於享有一段相對和平的時期，雖然小問題仍不時出現。","h":1},{"w":"comparatively","p":"adv.","d":"when compared with something else; relatively","c":"比較地；相對地","s":"Our town is comparatively small, with only ten thousand people, so almost everyone knows each other by name.","t":"我們鎮相對較小，只有一萬人，所以幾乎每個人都互相認識。"},{"w":"compare","p":"v.","d":"to look at two or more things to see how they are similar or different","c":"比較","s":"Before you buy a new phone, you should compare prices at several stores, because the same model can cost very different amounts.","t":"買新手機之前，你應該在幾家店比較價格，因為同一款手機的價格可能差很多。"},{"w":"comparison","p":"n.","d":"the act of looking at how things are similar or different","c":"比較","s":"In comparison with last year, the air in the city is much cleaner now, thanks to the new electric buses.","t":"和去年相比，現在城市的空氣乾淨多了，這要歸功於新的電動公車。"},{"w":"comparable","p":"adj.","d":"similar enough to be compared","c":"可比較的；相當的","s":"The two laptops are comparable in price and speed, so I chose the one with the longer battery life.","t":"這兩台筆電的價格和速度相當，所以我選了電池續航力較長的那台。"},{"w":"compass","p":"n.","d":"a tool with a needle that always points north, used to find directions","c":"羅盤；指南針","s":"When the hikers lost the trail in the fog, they used a compass and a map to find their way back to the camp.","t":"登山客在霧中迷失步道時，他們用指南針和地圖找到回營地的路。","h":1},{"w":"a pair of compasses","p":"n.phr.","d":"a tool with two legs used for drawing circles","c":"圓規","s":"In geometry class, each student needs a pair of compasses and a ruler to draw the perfect circles and lines the teacher asks for.","t":"在幾何課上，每位學生都需要一副圓規和一把尺，才能畫出老師要求的完美圓形和線條。"},{"w":"moral compass","p":"n.phr.","d":"a person's inner sense of what is right and wrong","c":"道德羅盤；是非觀念","s":"My grandmother always says that a strong moral compass is more important than money, because it guides you when life gets difficult.","t":"我奶奶總說，堅定的是非觀念比金錢更重要，因為它在人生艱難時會指引你。"},{"w":"compile","p":"v.","d":"to collect information from different places and put it together in a list or book","c":"彙編；編纂","s":"The students worked together to compile a list of every bird they had seen in the park during the whole school year.","t":"學生們一起彙編了一份清單，列出整個學年在公園裡看到的每一種鳥。","h":1},{"w":"compile","p":"v.","d":"to change a computer program into a form that a machine can run","c":"編譯（程式）","s":"After you finish writing the code, you must compile it, and the program will tell you if there are any mistakes to fix.","t":"寫完程式碼後，你必須編譯它，程式會告訴你是否有錯誤需要修正。"},{"w":"compilation","p":"n.","d":"a collection of things such as songs or writings put together","c":"彙編；合輯","s":"My uncle gave me a compilation of the best rock songs from the 1980s, and now I play it every time I clean my room.","t":"我叔叔送我一張一九八〇年代最佳搖滾歌曲的合輯，現在我每次打掃房間都會播放。"},{"w":"compiler","p":"n.","d":"a computer program that changes code into a form the machine can run; a person who compiles","c":"編譯器；編纂者","s":"The compiler found three errors in my program, so I had to go back and check every line again before class ended.","t":"編譯器在我的程式裡找到三個錯誤，所以我必須在下課前回頭再檢查每一行。"},{"w":"complement","p":"v.","d":"to go well with something and make it better or complete","c":"補足；與…相配","s":"The light yellow walls complement the dark wooden furniture perfectly, so the living room feels both warm and bright.","t":"淺黃色的牆壁和深色木質家具搭配得很完美，所以客廳感覺既溫暖又明亮。","h":1},{"w":"complement","p":"n.","d":"something that goes well with another thing and makes it complete","c":"補充物；互補的東西","s":"A glass of cold milk is the perfect complement to a plate of warm chocolate cookies on a rainy afternoon.","t":"在下雨的午後，一杯冰牛奶是一盤溫熱巧克力餅乾的完美搭配。"},{"w":"complementary","p":"adj.","d":"going well together; each supplying what the other lacks","c":"互補的；相配的","s":"The two sisters have complementary skills: one is great at planning, and the other is wonderful at talking to customers.","t":"這對姊妹的技能互補：一個擅長規劃，另一個很會和顧客交談。"},{"w":"complement each other","p":"v.phr.","d":"to combine well because each one adds what the other does not have","c":"互補；相得益彰","s":"The quiet drummer and the lively singer complement each other so well that their band has become the most popular one in school.","t":"安靜的鼓手和活潑的主唱互補得非常好，他們的樂團已經成為學校最受歡迎的樂團。"},{"w":"complexion","p":"n.","d":"the natural color and condition of the skin on a person's face","c":"膚色；氣色","s":"After a week at the beach, her complexion turned golden brown, and her friends said she looked healthier than ever.","t":"在海邊待了一週後，她的膚色變成金棕色，朋友說她看起來比以往更健康。","h":1},{"w":"complexion","p":"n.","d":"the general character or nature of a situation","c":"性質；面貌","s":"The surprising goal in the last minute changed the whole complexion of the game, and the losing team suddenly looked full of hope.","t":"最後一分鐘的意外進球改變了整場比賽的面貌，落後的球隊突然看起來充滿希望。"},{"w":"fair complexion","p":"n.phr.","d":"pale or light-colored skin","c":"白皙的膚色","s":"People with a fair complexion burn easily in the sun, so they should wear a hat and put on sunscreen before going outside.","t":"膚色白皙的人在太陽下容易曬傷，所以出門前應該戴帽子並擦防曬乳。"},{"w":"comprehensive","p":"adj.","d":"including everything or nearly everything that is needed","c":"全面的；綜合的","s":"The doctor gave my grandfather a comprehensive check-up that included blood tests, an eye exam, and a heart scan.","t":"醫生為我爺爺做了一次全面的健康檢查，包括驗血、視力檢查和心臟掃描。","h":1},{"w":"comprehensively","p":"adv.","d":"completely and including everything","c":"全面地；徹底地","s":"Our team lost comprehensively in the final, five to nothing, but the coach said we had learned a lot from playing such a strong side.","t":"我們隊在決賽中以零比五徹底落敗，但教練說和這麼強的對手比賽讓我們學到很多。"},{"w":"comprehend","p":"v.","d":"to understand something fully","c":"理解；領會","s":"The little boy was too young to comprehend why his family had to leave their home, so his mother simply told him it was an adventure.","t":"小男孩年紀太小，無法理解為什麼全家必須離開家園，所以媽媽只告訴他這是一場冒險。"},{"w":"comprehension","p":"n.","d":"the ability to understand something","c":"理解力；理解","s":"The reading comprehension test asks students to read a short story and then answer five questions about its meaning.","t":"閱讀理解測驗要求學生讀一篇短篇故事，然後回答五個關於內容意義的問題。"},{"w":"comprehensive exam","p":"n.phr.","d":"a test that covers everything a student has learned in a course","c":"綜合考試；總考","s":"At the end of the year, every student must pass a comprehensive exam that covers all twelve units of the English textbook.","t":"學年結束時，每位學生都必須通過涵蓋英文課本全部十二個單元的綜合考試。"},{"w":"compute","p":"v.","d":"to calculate an answer, usually with a machine","c":"計算","s":"Scientists used a powerful machine to compute how far the comet was from Earth, and the answer surprised everyone.","t":"科學家用一台強大的機器計算彗星離地球有多遠，答案讓所有人都很驚訝。","h":1},{"w":"computer","p":"n.","d":"an electronic machine that stores information and does calculations","c":"電腦","s":"My first computer was so slow that it took five minutes to open a single photo, but I still loved playing games on it.","t":"我的第一台電腦慢到打開一張照片要五分鐘，但我還是很愛在上面玩遊戲。"},{"w":"computation","p":"n.","d":"the process of calculating something","c":"計算；運算","s":"The computation of the exact date of the eclipse took astronomers many weeks before the age of modern computers.","t":"在現代電腦出現之前，天文學家要花好幾週才能完成日食確切日期的計算。"},{"w":"computing","p":"n.","d":"the study or use of computers","c":"計算機科學；電腦運用","s":"She is studying computing at university because she dreams of designing video games for children one day.","t":"她在大學讀電腦科學，因為她夢想有一天能為孩子設計電動遊戲。"},{"w":"computerize","p":"v.","d":"to use computers to do a job that was done by hand before","c":"電腦化","s":"The library decided to computerize its records last year, so now you can find any book in seconds instead of searching through cards.","t":"圖書館去年決定將紀錄電腦化，所以現在你幾秒鐘就能找到任何一本書，而不用翻找卡片。","h":1},{"w":"computerized","p":"adj.","d":"done or controlled by computer","c":"電腦化的","s":"The new computerized system at the hospital tells the nurses exactly when each patient needs to take medicine.","t":"醫院新的電腦化系統會準確告訴護士每位病人何時需要服藥。"},{"w":"computerization","p":"n.","d":"the process of changing to a system that uses computers","c":"電腦化（過程）","s":"The computerization of the post office made sending packages faster, but some older workers found the new machines hard to learn.","t":"郵局的電腦化讓寄包裹變快了，但有些年長員工覺得新機器很難學。"},{"w":"comrade","p":"n.","d":"a friend who works or fights with you, especially a fellow soldier","c":"同志；戰友；夥伴","s":"Every year on the same day, the old soldier visits the graves of the comrades who died beside him in the war.","t":"每年的同一天，老兵都會去探望在戰爭中死在他身旁的戰友的墳墓。","a":"comrades","h":1},{"w":"comradeship","p":"n.","d":"the friendship and trust between people who share work or danger","c":"同志情誼；友誼","s":"The long climb up the mountain built a strong comradeship among the students, who helped one another at every difficult step.","t":"漫長的登山路程在學生之間建立了深厚的同伴情誼，他們在每個艱難的步伐中互相幫助。"},{"w":"comrade-in-arms","p":"n.phr.","d":"a person who has fought beside you in a war or struggle","c":"戰友","s":"The two old men were comrades-in-arms fifty years ago, and they still meet every month to share stories over a cup of tea.","t":"這兩位老先生五十年前是戰友，他們現在仍每個月見面，邊喝茶邊分享故事。","a":"comrades-in-arms"},{"w":"concession","p":"n.","d":"something you agree to give up in order to end an argument","c":"讓步","s":"After hours of talking, the workers made a concession: they would accept a smaller pay rise if the company gave them one more day off.","t":"經過數小時的談判，工人們做出讓步：如果公司多給一天假，他們願意接受較小的加薪幅度。","h":1},{"w":"concession","p":"n.","d":"a lower price for certain groups such as students or old people","c":"優惠（價格）；減價","s":"The museum offers a concession to students, so bring your student card and you will pay only half the normal ticket price.","t":"博物館提供學生優惠，所以帶著學生證，你只需付正常票價的一半。"},{"w":"concede","p":"v.","d":"to admit that something is true, or to give up something after an argument","c":"承認；讓步","s":"The coach had to concede that the other team played better, even though he was unhappy with the referee's decisions.","t":"教練不得不承認對方球隊打得更好，即使他對裁判的判決不滿。"},{"w":"make concessions","p":"v.phr.","d":"to give up some things in order to reach an agreement","c":"做出讓步","s":"Both sides must make concessions if they want to end the strike, because neither the workers nor the company can win everything.","t":"如果雙方想結束罷工，就必須做出讓步，因為工人和公司都不可能全贏。"}]},{"unit":8,"theme":"concise – cowardly","cards":[{"w":"concise","p":"adj.","d":"short and clear, using few words","c":"簡潔的；簡明的","s":"The manager likes reports that are concise and easy to read, so please keep yours to one page and use simple headings.","t":"經理喜歡簡潔易讀的報告，所以請把你的報告控制在一頁內，並使用簡單的標題。","h":1},{"w":"concisely","p":"adv.","d":"in a short and clear way","c":"簡潔地","s":"She explained the whole plan concisely in less than two minutes, and everyone in the room understood exactly what to do.","t":"她在不到兩分鐘內簡潔地說明了整個計畫，房間裡每個人都清楚知道該做什麼。"},{"w":"conciseness","p":"n.","d":"the quality of being short and clear","c":"簡潔","s":"The judges praised the conciseness of his speech, because he made three strong points without repeating himself once.","t":"評審稱讚他演講的簡潔，因為他提出了三個有力的論點，而且一次都沒有重複。"},{"w":"condense","p":"v.","d":"to make something shorter; to change from gas into liquid","c":"濃縮；精簡；凝結","s":"The editor asked me to condense my five-page story into two pages, which meant cutting out several of my favorite scenes.","t":"編輯要我把五頁的故事精簡成兩頁，這表示要刪掉幾個我最喜歡的場景。","h":1},{"w":"condensation","p":"n.","d":"small drops of water that form on a cold surface","c":"凝結的水珠；凝結","s":"On cold mornings there is always condensation on the inside of the windows, and my little brother likes to draw faces in it.","t":"寒冷的早晨窗戶內側總是有凝結的水珠，我弟弟喜歡在上面畫鬼臉。"},{"w":"condensed","p":"adj.","d":"made shorter or thicker","c":"精簡的；濃縮的","s":"The library has a condensed version of the famous novel for young readers, which tells the same story in only eighty pages.","t":"圖書館有這本名著給年輕讀者的精簡版，只用八十頁就講完同樣的故事。"},{"w":"condensed milk","p":"n.phr.","d":"thick, sweet milk sold in cans","c":"煉乳","s":"Taiwanese shaved ice tastes best with fresh mango on top and a little condensed milk poured over everything at the end.","t":"台灣的剉冰最好吃的方式是上面放新鮮芒果，最後再淋上一點煉乳。"},{"w":"confederation","p":"n.","d":"a group of states, organizations, or people joined together for a common purpose","c":"邦聯；聯盟","s":"Long ago, several small kingdoms formed a confederation to protect themselves, but each one still kept its own laws and king.","t":"很久以前，幾個小王國組成了一個邦聯來保護自己，但每個王國仍然保有自己的法律和國王。","h":1},{"w":"confederate","p":"adj.","d":"belonging to a confederation; joined together","c":"同盟的；聯合的","s":"The confederate states agreed to share one army, and they promised to help each other whenever an enemy attacked.","t":"那些同盟的州同意共享一支軍隊，並承諾在敵人來襲時互相幫助。"},{"w":"federation","p":"n.","d":"a group of states or organizations with one central government","c":"聯邦；聯合會","s":"The international football federation decides the rules of the game and chooses which country will hold the World Cup.","t":"國際足球聯合會決定比賽規則，並選出哪個國家舉辦世界盃。"},{"w":"federal","p":"adj.","d":"relating to the central government of a country made up of states","c":"聯邦的","s":"In the United States, federal laws apply to every state, while each state also has its own rules about things like driving.","t":"在美國，聯邦法律適用於每一州，而各州對開車之類的事也有自己的規定。"},{"w":"congressman","p":"n.","d":"a man who is a member of the US Congress","c":"（美國）國會議員（男）","s":"The congressman visited our school to talk about how laws are made, and he answered questions from students for an hour.","t":"那位國會議員來我們學校談法律是怎麼制定的，他回答學生的問題長達一小時。","h":1},{"w":"congresswoman","p":"n.","d":"a woman who is a member of the US Congress","c":"（美國）國會議員（女）","s":"The young congresswoman promised to fight for cleaner air in the city, and many voters supported her because of this promise.","t":"這位年輕的女國會議員承諾為城市爭取更乾淨的空氣，許多選民因為這個承諾而支持她。"},{"w":"Congress","p":"n.","d":"the group of people elected to make laws in the United States","c":"（美國）國會","s":"Congress passed a new law last month that gives more money to schools in poor areas across the country.","t":"國會上個月通過了一項新法律，給全國貧困地區的學校更多經費。"},{"w":"congressional","p":"adj.","d":"relating to Congress","c":"國會的","s":"A congressional committee is looking into the problem, and its members will interview the company's leaders next week.","t":"一個國會委員會正在調查這個問題，委員們下週將約談該公司的負責人。"},{"w":"conquest","p":"n.","d":"the act of taking control of a country or people by force","c":"征服","s":"The museum has a large map that shows the Roman conquest of Europe, with the dates when each area fell under Roman rule.","t":"博物館有一張大地圖，顯示羅馬征服歐洲的過程，以及各地區落入羅馬統治的年代。","h":1},{"w":"conquer","p":"v.","d":"to take control of a place by force; to succeed in dealing with a problem","c":"征服；克服","s":"Maria decided to conquer her fear of water, so she signed up for swimming lessons at the community pool last summer.","t":"瑪麗亞決定克服她對水的恐懼，所以去年夏天她報名了社區游泳池的游泳課。"},{"w":"conqueror","p":"n.","d":"a person who takes control of a place by force","c":"征服者","s":"The conqueror rode into the city with his army, and the people watched silently from their windows as he passed.","t":"征服者率領軍隊騎進城裡，人們從窗戶靜靜地看著他經過。"},{"w":"conscientious","p":"adj.","d":"careful and taking great care to do things correctly","c":"認真負責的；盡責的","s":"Amy is a conscientious student who checks every answer twice before she hands in her homework, so she rarely makes mistakes.","t":"艾咪是個認真負責的學生，交作業前會把每個答案檢查兩次，所以她很少犯錯。","h":1},{"w":"conscientiously","p":"adv.","d":"in a careful and responsible way","c":"認真負責地","s":"The new nurse conscientiously wrote down every patient's temperature each hour, even when the ward was extremely busy.","t":"新來的護士即使在病房非常忙碌時，仍認真負責地每小時記錄每位病人的體溫。"},{"w":"conscience","p":"n.","d":"the feeling inside you that tells you whether something is right or wrong","c":"良心","s":"After he found the wallet, his conscience would not let him keep the money, so he took it to the police station.","t":"他撿到皮夾後，良心不允許他留下那些錢，所以他把皮夾送到警察局。"},{"w":"conserve","p":"v.","d":"to use something carefully so that it is not wasted; to protect something from harm","c":"節約；保護","s":"Because the river is so low this year, the mayor asked everyone to conserve water by taking shorter showers.","t":"因為今年河水水位很低，市長要求大家縮短淋浴時間來節約用水。","h":1},{"w":"conserve energy","p":"v.phr.","d":"to use less electricity, gas, or fuel","c":"節約能源","s":"Our school tries to conserve energy by turning off the lights and air conditioners in every empty classroom during lunch.","t":"我們學校午餐時間會關掉每間空教室的電燈和冷氣，努力節約能源。"},{"w":"conservation","p":"n.","d":"the protection of nature, animals, and natural resources","c":"保育；保護","s":"Scientists say the conservation of this forest is important because several rare birds live nowhere else in the world.","t":"科學家說這片森林的保育很重要，因為有幾種稀有鳥類只住在這裡。"},{"w":"conservative","p":"adj.","d":"not liking change; careful and traditional","c":"保守的","s":"My grandfather is quite conservative about food, so he always orders the same noodle soup instead of trying new dishes.","t":"我爺爺對食物相當保守，所以他總是點同樣的湯麵，而不嘗試新菜色。"},{"w":"consolation","p":"n.","d":"something that makes you feel better when you are sad or disappointed","c":"安慰","s":"Our team lost the final by one point, and the only consolation was that we had played better than ever before.","t":"我們的隊伍在決賽中以一分之差落敗，唯一的安慰是我們打得比以往任何時候都好。","h":1},{"w":"console","p":"v.","d":"to make someone feel better when they are sad","c":"安慰","s":"Lily's best friend came over to console her after her cat died, and they looked at old photos of the cat together.","t":"莉莉的貓死後，她最好的朋友來安慰她，兩人一起看那隻貓的舊照片。","h":1},{"w":"consolation prize","p":"n.phr.","d":"a small prize given to someone who did not win","c":"安慰獎","s":"I did not win the drawing contest, but I received a consolation prize, a box of colored pencils, which I still use every day.","t":"我沒有贏得繪畫比賽，但得到一份安慰獎——一盒彩色鉛筆，我到現在還每天用。"},{"w":"console","p":"n.","d":"a machine for playing video games; a panel with controls","c":"遊戲主機；控制台","s":"My cousin saved his pocket money for a year to buy a new game console, and now he plays with his friends every weekend.","t":"我表哥存了一年的零用錢買了一台新的遊戲主機，現在他每個週末都和朋友一起玩。"},{"w":"consonant","p":"n.","d":"a speech sound or letter that is not a vowel, such as b, k, or t","c":"子音；子音字母","s":"The word \"strength\" is hard for many learners to say because it begins with three consonant sounds in a row before the vowel.","t":"strength 這個字對許多學習者來說很難唸，因為它在母音前連續有三個子音。","h":1},{"w":"vowel","p":"n.","d":"one of the speech sounds or letters a, e, i, o, u","c":"母音；母音字母","s":"In English, every word must have at least one vowel, and that is why words like \"sky\" use the letter y to make the sound.","t":"在英文中，每個字至少要有一個母音，這就是為什麼像 sky 這樣的字用字母 y 來發音。"},{"w":"syllable","p":"n.","d":"a part of a word that has one vowel sound","c":"音節","s":"The word \"banana\" has three syllables, and the stress falls on the second one, so you should say it a little louder.","t":"banana 這個字有三個音節，重音落在第二個，所以你應該把它唸得大聲一點。","a":"syllables"},{"w":"conspiracy","p":"n.","d":"a secret plan by a group of people to do something bad or illegal","c":"陰謀；共謀","s":"The police discovered a conspiracy to steal money from the bank, and the three workers involved were sent to prison.","t":"警方發現了一起從銀行偷錢的陰謀，涉案的三名員工被送進監獄。","h":1},{"w":"conspire","p":"v.","d":"to secretly plan with other people to do something bad","c":"密謀；共謀","s":"Two of the guards had conspired with the thieves to leave the back door open, which is how the paintings disappeared.","t":"兩名警衛曾與竊賊密謀讓後門敞開，那些畫就是這樣消失的。","a":"conspired"},{"w":"conspirator","p":"n.","d":"a person who takes part in a secret plan to do something bad","c":"共謀者","s":"The main conspirator ran away to another country before the police arrived, but his partners were caught the same night.","t":"主要共謀者在警察到達前逃到了另一個國家，但他的同夥當晚就被抓了。"},{"w":"conspiracy theory","p":"n.phr.","d":"a belief that a secret group is behind an event, usually without proof","c":"陰謀論","s":"My uncle believes a conspiracy theory that the moon landing was filmed in a studio, even though all the evidence says it was real.","t":"我叔叔相信登月是在攝影棚裡拍的陰謀論，儘管所有證據都說那是真的。"},{"w":"contention","p":"n.","d":"angry disagreement between people; a strong opinion in an argument","c":"爭論；爭執；論點","s":"The old family house has been a source of contention between the two brothers for years, and their mother is tired of it.","t":"那棟老家的房子多年來一直是兩兄弟爭執的來源，他們的母親已經厭倦了。","h":1},{"w":"contend","p":"v.","d":"to compete against someone; to claim that something is true","c":"競爭；主張","s":"Three strong teams will contend for the championship this year, so every game in the final week is going to matter.","t":"今年有三支強隊將競爭冠軍，所以最後一週的每場比賽都很重要。"},{"w":"contentious","p":"adj.","d":"likely to cause an argument","c":"有爭議的","s":"Whether students should wear uniforms is a contentious issue at our school, and the meeting about it lasted three hours.","t":"學生是否該穿制服在我們學校是個有爭議的議題，相關會議開了三個小時。"},{"w":"a bone of contention","p":"n.phr.","d":"something that people argue about for a long time","c":"爭論的焦點","s":"Who should wash the dishes after dinner has become a bone of contention between my brother and me, so Mom made a weekly schedule.","t":"晚餐後誰該洗碗已經成為我和哥哥之間爭論的焦點，所以媽媽做了一張每週輪值表。"},{"w":"contestant","p":"n.","d":"a person who takes part in a competition","c":"參賽者","s":"Each contestant in the singing competition gets three minutes on stage, and the judges will choose the best five for the final.","t":"歌唱比賽的每位參賽者有三分鐘的舞台時間，評審將選出最好的五位進入決賽。","h":1},{"w":"contest","p":"n.","d":"a competition in which people try to win a prize","c":"比賽；競賽","s":"Our class won first prize in the school's English speech contest, and the whole class went out for ice cream to celebrate.","t":"我們班在學校的英語演講比賽中獲得第一名，全班一起去吃冰淇淋慶祝。"},{"w":"contest","p":"v.","d":"to formally say that a decision or result is wrong","c":"對…提出異議；爭辯","s":"The coach decided to contest the referee's decision, because the video clearly showed that the ball had crossed the line.","t":"教練決定對裁判的判決提出異議，因為影片清楚顯示球已經越過了線。"},{"w":"continuity","p":"n.","d":"the state of continuing without change or interruption","c":"連續性；延續","s":"The school has had five principals in six years, and teachers hope the new one will stay to give students some continuity.","t":"這所學校六年換了五位校長，老師們希望新校長能留下來，讓學生有一些延續性。","h":1},{"w":"continue","p":"v.","d":"to keep doing something without stopping","c":"繼續","s":"If you continue to practice the piano for half an hour every day, you will be able to play that song by Christmas.","t":"如果你繼續每天練半小時鋼琴，到聖誕節你就能彈那首歌了。"},{"w":"continuous","p":"adj.","d":"happening without stopping","c":"連續的；不斷的","s":"The continuous rain for three days caused the river to rise, and some roads near the bridge were closed on Sunday.","t":"連續三天的降雨使河水上漲，橋附近的一些道路在星期日封閉。"},{"w":"continual","p":"adj.","d":"happening again and again, often in an annoying way","c":"頻繁的；不斷的","s":"The continual noise from the construction site next door made it very hard for me to study for my exams last week.","t":"隔壁工地不斷的噪音讓我上週很難準備考試。"},{"w":"contradict","p":"v.","d":"to say the opposite of what someone else has said; to be different from","c":"反駁；與…矛盾","s":"The manager said the shop closes at eight, but the sign on the door seemed to contradict him because it said nine.","t":"經理說店八點關門，但門上的告示似乎與他的說法矛盾，因為上面寫著九點。","h":1},{"w":"contradiction","p":"n.","d":"a situation in which two things cannot both be true","c":"矛盾","s":"There is a contradiction between what he says and what he does, because he tells us to save money but buys new shoes every week.","t":"他的言行之間存在矛盾，因為他叫我們省錢，自己卻每週買新鞋。"},{"w":"contradictory","p":"adj.","d":"(of two things) so different that they cannot both be true","c":"矛盾的；對立的","s":"The two doctors gave my aunt contradictory advice: one told her to rest in bed and the other told her to exercise daily.","t":"兩位醫生給我阿姨矛盾的建議：一位叫她臥床休息，另一位叫她每天運動。"},{"w":"contradict oneself","p":"v.phr.","d":"to say something that is the opposite of what you said before","c":"自相矛盾","s":"The witness kept contradicting himself during the trial, so the lawyer asked the judge not to believe anything he said.","t":"證人在審判中不斷自相矛盾，所以律師請法官不要相信他說的任何話。","a":"contradicting himself"},{"w":"convene","p":"v.","d":"to call people together for a meeting; to come together for a meeting","c":"召集；召開；集會","s":"After the storm, the mayor decided to convene a special meeting of city leaders to plan help for families who lost their homes.","t":"暴風雨過後，市長決定召開一場市政領導人的特別會議，為失去家園的家庭規劃援助。","h":1},{"w":"convention","p":"n.","d":"a large formal meeting; a traditional way of doing something","c":"大會；慣例","s":"Thousands of doctors attended the medical convention in Taipei last week to learn about new ways of treating heart disease.","t":"上週有數千名醫生參加在台北舉行的醫學大會，學習治療心臟病的新方法。"},{"w":"conventional","p":"adj.","d":"traditional and usual","c":"傳統的；慣常的","s":"Instead of a conventional wedding in a hotel, my cousin and her husband got married on a beach with only twenty guests.","t":"我表姐和她先生沒有在飯店舉行傳統的婚禮，而是在海灘上結婚，只邀請了二十位賓客。"},{"w":"convention center","p":"n.phr.","d":"a large building where big meetings and exhibitions are held","c":"會議中心","s":"The book fair will be held at the convention center near the river, and more than two hundred publishers will have stands there.","t":"書展將在河邊的會議中心舉行，有超過兩百家出版社會在那裡設攤。"},{"w":"coral","p":"n.","d":"a hard, colorful substance made by tiny sea animals, found in warm seas","c":"珊瑚","s":"When we went diving near Green Island, we saw bright pink and orange coral with colorful fish swimming around it.","t":"我們在綠島附近潛水時，看到鮮豔的粉紅色和橘色珊瑚，五彩繽紛的魚在周圍游動。","h":1},{"w":"coral","p":"adj.","d":"pinkish-orange in color","c":"珊瑚色的；橘紅色的","s":"She wore a coral dress to the party, and the warm color looked beautiful against the dark blue of the evening sky.","t":"她穿了一件珊瑚色的洋裝去派對，那溫暖的顏色在深藍色的夜空下顯得很美。"},{"w":"coral reef","p":"n.phr.","d":"a long line of coral under the sea where many fish live","c":"珊瑚礁","s":"The coral reef near the island is home to hundreds of kinds of fish, but warmer sea water is slowly killing the coral.","t":"島附近的珊瑚礁是數百種魚類的家，但變暖的海水正慢慢使珊瑚死亡。"},{"w":"corpse","p":"n.","d":"the dead body of a person","c":"屍體","s":"The police found a corpse in the river early this morning, and they are now trying to find out who the man was.","t":"警方今天清晨在河裡發現一具屍體，現在正試圖查明那名男子的身分。","h":1},{"w":"dead body","p":"n.phr.","d":"the body of a person or animal that has died","c":"屍體；遺體","s":"The hikers were shocked to find the dead body of a deer beside the trail, and they reported it to the park office.","t":"登山客震驚地在步道旁發現一具鹿的屍體，他們向公園管理處通報了。"},{"w":"lifeless","p":"adj.","d":"dead or seeming to be dead; without energy","c":"無生命的；死氣沉沉的","s":"The old fish lay lifeless at the bottom of the tank, so my sister cried and we buried it under the tree in the yard.","t":"那條老魚毫無生氣地躺在魚缸底部，所以我妹妹哭了，我們把牠埋在院子的樹下。"},{"w":"correspondence","p":"n.","d":"letters or emails sent and received","c":"通信；信件","s":"My grandmother keeps all her correspondence with Grandpa from the years before they married, tied together with a red ribbon.","t":"我奶奶保存著她和爺爺婚前那些年的所有通信，用一條紅緞帶綁在一起。","h":1},{"w":"correspondence","p":"n.","d":"a close connection or similarity between two things","c":"一致；對應","s":"There is a clear correspondence between the hours students sleep and their test scores, according to a study of our school.","t":"根據一項針對我們學校的研究，學生的睡眠時數和考試成績之間有明顯的對應關係。"},{"w":"correspond","p":"v.","d":"to match or be the same as something; to write letters to someone","c":"相符；對應；通信","s":"The numbers on your ticket should correspond with the numbers on the seat, so please check before you sit down.","t":"你票上的號碼應該和座位上的號碼相符，所以請在坐下前先確認。"},{"w":"correspondent","p":"n.","d":"a reporter who sends news from a foreign country or a particular place","c":"特派記者；通訊記者","s":"The TV station's correspondent in London reported live from outside the palace on the morning of the royal wedding.","t":"電視台駐倫敦的特派記者在皇室婚禮當天早上從皇宮外進行現場報導。"},{"w":"corresponding","p":"adj.","d":"matching or connected with something you have just mentioned","c":"相應的；對應的","s":"House prices rose by ten percent last year, but there was no corresponding rise in people's salaries, so many families struggled.","t":"去年房價上漲了百分之十，但人們的薪水並沒有相應的上漲，所以許多家庭過得很辛苦。"},{"w":"cosmetic","p":"adj.","d":"improving only the appearance of something, not its real quality","c":"表面的；裝飾性的；美容的","s":"The scratches on the car door are only cosmetic problems, because the engine still runs perfectly after ten years.","t":"車門上的刮痕只是表面的問題，因為引擎在十年後仍運轉得很好。","h":1},{"w":"cosmetics","p":"n.","d":"substances such as lipstick and face cream that people put on their face and body","c":"化妝品","s":"My sister never wears any cosmetics because she likes her natural look, but she spends a lot of money on hair products.","t":"我姐姐從不用任何化妝品，因為她喜歡自然的樣子，但她在護髮產品上花很多錢。","h":1},{"w":"cosmetic surgery","p":"n.phr.","d":"medical operations done to improve a person's appearance","c":"整形手術；美容手術","s":"The actress admitted that she had cosmetic surgery on her nose when she was young, and she said she regrets it now.","t":"那位女演員承認她年輕時做過鼻子的整形手術，她說她現在很後悔。"},{"w":"makeup","p":"n.","d":"colored substances put on the face to make it look more attractive","c":"化妝；化妝品","s":"She puts on a little makeup before work every morning, but on weekends she prefers to let her skin rest.","t":"她每天早上上班前會化一點妝，但週末她比較喜歡讓皮膚休息。"},{"w":"counterpart","p":"n.","d":"a person who has the same job or position as you in another place or organization","c":"（職位相當的）對應者；對方","s":"Our principal flew to Osaka to meet her Japanese counterpart, and the two of them talked about how students learn English.","t":"我們的校長飛到大阪會見她的日本同職位對口人員，兩人談論學生如何學英文。","h":1},{"w":"counterpart","p":"n.","d":"a thing that has the same purpose as another thing in a different place or system","c":"對應物","s":"The Taiwanese night market has no real counterpart in Europe, where most shops and streets become quiet after dark.","t":"台灣的夜市在歐洲沒有真正的對應物，那裡大多數商店和街道在天黑後都很安靜。"},{"w":"run counter to","p":"v.phr.","d":"to be the opposite of something","c":"與…背道而馳","s":"The new rule about homework seems to run counter to what the principal said last month about giving students more free time.","t":"關於作業的新規定似乎與校長上個月說要給學生更多自由時間的說法背道而馳。"},{"w":"counterattack","p":"n.","d":"an attack made in reply to an attack by the enemy or another team","c":"反擊；反攻","s":"After defending for most of the game, our team launched a quick counterattack in the last minute and scored the winning goal.","t":"在比賽大部分時間防守之後，我們的隊伍在最後一分鐘發動快速反擊，踢進了致勝的一球。"},{"w":"coupon","p":"n.","d":"a small piece of paper that gives you a discount or something free","c":"優惠券；折價券","s":"The pizza shop gave us a coupon with our order, so if we go back before Sunday we can get a second pizza for half price.","t":"披薩店隨訂單給了我們一張優惠券，所以如果我們在星期日前回去，可以用半價買第二個披薩。","h":1},{"w":"discount coupon","p":"n.phr.","d":"a coupon that lets you pay less for something","c":"折扣券","s":"My mother cuts out every discount coupon from the newspaper, and last month she saved almost a thousand dollars on groceries.","t":"我媽媽把報紙上每張折扣券都剪下來，上個月她在買菜上省了將近一千元。"},{"w":"coupon code","p":"n.phr.","d":"a set of letters or numbers you type in to get a discount when shopping online","c":"優惠代碼","s":"Enter the coupon code at the end of your order, and the website will take twenty percent off the price of your shoes.","t":"在訂單最後輸入優惠代碼，網站就會為你的鞋子打八折。"},{"w":"clip coupons","p":"v.phr.","d":"to cut discount coupons out of newspapers or magazines","c":"剪優惠券","s":"Every Sunday afternoon, Grandma sits at the kitchen table to clip coupons for the supermarket while she watches her favorite show.","t":"每個星期日下午，奶奶坐在廚房餐桌前一邊看她最愛的節目，一邊為超市購物剪優惠券。"},{"w":"courtyard","p":"n.","d":"an open space surrounded by walls or buildings","c":"庭院；中庭","s":"The old house is built around a small courtyard with a stone fountain, where the family drinks tea on summer evenings.","t":"這棟老房子圍繞著一個有石頭噴泉的小庭院而建，一家人夏天傍晚會在那裡喝茶。","h":1},{"w":"yard","p":"n.","d":"an area of ground next to a house, often with grass","c":"院子","s":"My father spent the whole afternoon cutting the grass in the back yard, and afterwards we had a barbecue there.","t":"我爸爸花了一整個下午在後院割草，之後我們在那裡烤肉。"},{"w":"court","p":"n.","d":"an area marked out for playing a sport such as tennis or basketball","c":"球場","s":"The basketball court behind our school is always full after four o'clock, so we usually have to wait for a game.","t":"我們學校後面的籃球場四點以後總是滿的，所以我們通常得等著才能打一場。"},{"w":"cowardly","p":"adj.","d":"not brave; afraid to do what is right or dangerous","c":"膽小的；懦弱的","s":"Tom felt it was cowardly of him not to help the little kid who was being hit, and he promised himself to be braver next time.","t":"湯姆覺得自己沒有幫助那個被打的小孩是懦弱的，他對自己承諾下次要更勇敢。","h":1},{"w":"coward","p":"n.","d":"a person who is not brave","c":"膽小鬼；懦夫","s":"Jack ran away as soon as the small dog barked, and his friends laughed and called him a coward, which made him angry.","t":"小狗一叫傑克就跑掉了，他的朋友笑他是膽小鬼，這讓他很生氣。"},{"w":"cowardice","p":"n.","d":"the quality of not being brave","c":"膽小；懦弱","s":"The soldier was punished for cowardice because he hid in a house while the rest of his group fought bravely outside.","t":"那名士兵因為膽小而受罰，因為他躲在一間房子裡，而他的同袍在外面英勇作戰。"}]},{"unit":9,"theme":"cozy – deem","cards":[{"w":"cozy","p":"adj.","d":"warm, comfortable, and pleasant","c":"舒適溫暖的；愜意的","s":"It was snowing hard outside, but the little cabin felt cozy because a fire was burning and we had warm blankets.","t":"外面下著大雪，但小木屋裡感覺很舒適溫暖，因為爐火燒著，我們還有溫暖的毯子。","h":1},{"w":"coziness","p":"n.","d":"the quality of being warm and comfortable","c":"舒適；溫馨","s":"Guests love the coziness of this small café, where soft lights and old wooden chairs make everyone want to stay longer.","t":"客人喜愛這家小咖啡館的溫馨氛圍，柔和的燈光和老木椅讓每個人都想多待一會兒。"},{"w":"cozy up to","p":"v.phr.","d":"to try to become friendly with someone in order to get something","c":"討好；巴結","s":"Everyone noticed that Jack began to cozy up to the new manager as soon as he heard that a better job would be open soon.","t":"大家都注意到傑克一聽說很快會有更好的職位空出來，就開始巴結新經理。"},{"w":"crackdown","p":"n.","d":"strong action taken by the police or government to stop something bad","c":"取締；嚴厲打擊","s":"After the crackdown on drivers who use phones, more than three hundred people were fined in only two days.","t":"在對使用手機的駕駛人進行取締後，僅兩天就有超過三百人被罰款。","h":1},{"w":"crack down on","p":"v.phr.","d":"to start dealing with bad behavior in a stricter way","c":"嚴厲打擊；取締","s":"The school has decided to crack down on students who arrive late, so anyone who comes after eight will have to stay after class.","t":"學校決定嚴格取締遲到的學生，所以八點以後到的人都必須留下來。"},{"w":"crack","p":"v.","d":"to break so that lines appear on the surface; to make a sudden sharp sound","c":"使破裂；裂開","s":"Be careful not to crack the eggs when you put them in the basket, because the road home is bumpy.","t":"把蛋放進籃子時小心別弄破，因為回家的路很顛簸。"},{"w":"crack","p":"n.","d":"a thin line on the surface of something where it has broken","c":"裂縫","s":"There is a long crack in the classroom wall after the earthquake, so the principal asked an engineer to check the building.","t":"地震後教室牆上出現了一道長長的裂縫，所以校長請了工程師來檢查這棟建築。"},{"w":"cracker","p":"n.","d":"a thin, dry, hard biscuit, often eaten with cheese","c":"薄脆餅乾","s":"I was hungry after school, so I ate a salty cracker with a piece of cheese on top while I waited for dinner.","t":"我放學後很餓，所以在等晚餐時吃了一片上面放著起司的鹹薄脆餅乾。","h":1},{"w":"firecracker","p":"n.","d":"a small paper tube that explodes with a loud bang when lit","c":"鞭炮","s":"At Chinese New Year, my cousin lit a firecracker in the yard, and the loud bang made all the dogs in the street bark.","t":"農曆新年時，我表哥在院子裡點了一個鞭炮，巨大的響聲讓街上所有的狗都叫了起來。"},{"w":"crackers and cheese","p":"n.phr.","d":"a simple snack of crackers eaten with cheese","c":"餅乾配起司","s":"We served crackers and cheese before dinner, and the guests stood around the kitchen talking while the chicken finished cooking.","t":"我們在晚餐前端出餅乾配起司，客人們站在廚房邊聊天邊等雞肉煮好。"},{"w":"cram","p":"v.","d":"to study a lot in a short time just before an exam","c":"臨時抱佛腳；死記硬背","s":"Jenny did not open her history book all month, so now she has to cram all the dates and names the night before the exam.","t":"珍妮整個月都沒打開歷史課本，所以現在她必須在考試前一晚臨時抱佛腳記住所有日期和人名。","h":1},{"w":"cram","p":"v.","d":"to push a lot of things into a small space","c":"塞滿；擠進","s":"Mom tried to cram one more sweater into the suitcase, but the zipper would not close no matter how hard she pushed.","t":"媽媽試著再把一件毛衣塞進行李箱，但無論她怎麼壓，拉鍊都拉不上。"},{"w":"cram school","p":"n.phr.","d":"a private school where students study extra hours to prepare for exams","c":"補習班","s":"Many high school students in Taiwan go to a cram school after regular classes and do not get home until ten at night.","t":"台灣許多高中生在正課後去補習班，晚上十點才回到家。"},{"w":"crammed","p":"adj.","d":"completely full of people or things","c":"擠滿的；塞滿的","s":"The MRT train was so crammed at eight in the morning that I could not even reach my phone in my pocket.","t":"早上八點的捷運列車擠滿了人，我甚至無法伸手拿口袋裡的手機。"},{"w":"cramp","p":"n.","d":"a sudden, painful tightening of a muscle","c":"抽筋；痙攣","s":"Ken had to stop running in the last part of the race because of a sharp cramp in his leg, and he sat down until it relaxed.","t":"肯在比賽最後一段因為腿部劇烈抽筋不得不停下來，他坐下休息直到肌肉放鬆。","h":1},{"w":"cramp","p":"v.","d":"to limit someone's freedom or development","c":"限制；束縛","s":"My little sister follows me everywhere, which tends to cramp my style when I want to hang out with my friends.","t":"我妹妹到哪裡都跟著我，當我想和朋友出去玩時，這往往會束縛我的行動。"},{"w":"cramped","p":"adj.","d":"(of a room or space) small and crowded","c":"狹窄的；擁擠的","s":"Six of us shared one cramped hotel room on the school trip, so we had to climb over bags just to reach the bathroom.","t":"校外教學時我們六個人共用一間狹窄的飯店房間，所以我們得跨過行李才能到浴室。"},{"w":"get a cramp","p":"v.phr.","d":"to suddenly feel a painful tightening in a muscle","c":"抽筋","s":"If you jump into the cold pool right after eating a big lunch, you may get a cramp and find it hard to swim.","t":"如果你吃完大餐後馬上跳進冰冷的泳池，可能會抽筋而難以游泳。"},{"w":"crater","p":"n.","d":"a large round hole in the ground made by an explosion or by a rock from space; the mouth of a volcano","c":"坑；火山口","s":"A rock from space hit the desert thousands of years ago, and the huge round crater it left is almost a kilometer wide.","t":"數千年前一塊來自太空的岩石撞擊了沙漠，它留下的巨大圓形坑洞將近一公里寬。","h":1},{"w":"crater","p":"v.","d":"to form a large hole; (informal) to fail or fall suddenly","c":"形成坑洞；（口語）暴跌、崩盤","s":"The company's share price began to crater after the news report, falling by half in a single afternoon.","t":"新聞報導後，該公司的股價開始暴跌，一個下午就跌了一半。"},{"w":"volcanic crater","p":"n.phr.","d":"the round opening at the top of a volcano","c":"火山口","s":"From the top of the mountain, we looked down into the volcanic crater, where white smoke was still rising from the rocks.","t":"從山頂，我們往下望進火山口，白煙仍從岩石間升起。"},{"w":"credible","p":"adj.","d":"able to be believed or trusted","c":"可信的；可靠的","s":"The boy's story about a monkey taking his homework was not credible, because there are no monkeys anywhere near our school.","t":"那個男孩說猴子拿走他作業的故事並不可信，因為我們學校附近根本沒有猴子。","h":1},{"w":"credibility","p":"n.","d":"the quality of being believed or trusted","c":"可信度；信譽","s":"The newspaper lost its credibility after it printed a false story, and many readers no longer trust anything it says.","t":"這家報紙刊登了一則假新聞後失去了可信度，許多讀者不再相信它說的任何事。"},{"w":"incredible","p":"adj.","d":"impossible or very hard to believe; extremely good","c":"難以置信的；極好的","s":"It is incredible that a ten-year-old girl swam across the whole lake, but her coach says she trained for two years.","t":"一個十歲女孩游過整個湖泊真是難以置信，但她的教練說她訓練了兩年。"},{"w":"credit","p":"n.","d":"praise or approval for something you have done; an arrangement to buy now and pay later","c":"讚揚；功勞；信用（賒帳）","s":"The whole team deserves credit for the win, not just the player who scored the final goal in the last minute.","t":"整個團隊都應該得到這場勝利的讚揚，而不只是那位在最後一分鐘踢進致勝球的球員。"},{"w":"crocodile","p":"n.","d":"a large reptile with a long body, strong jaws, and sharp teeth that lives in rivers in hot countries","c":"鱷魚","s":"Do not swim in this river, because a large crocodile lives near the bridge and attacked a cow that was drinking there.","t":"不要在這條河裡游泳，因為橋附近住著一隻大鱷魚，牠攻擊過一頭在那裡喝水的牛。","h":1},{"w":"crocodile tears","p":"n.phr.","d":"tears or sadness that are not sincere","c":"鱷魚的眼淚；假哭","s":"She cried when her sister's cake fell, but we all knew they were crocodile tears, because she had wanted the cake to fail.","t":"她姊姊的蛋糕塌了她就哭了，但我們都知道那是鱷魚的眼淚，因為她本來就希望蛋糕失敗。"},{"w":"alligator","p":"n.","d":"a large reptile like a crocodile, found mainly in the US and China","c":"短吻鱷","s":"An alligator has a wider, rounder nose than a crocodile, and you usually cannot see its lower teeth when its mouth is closed.","t":"短吻鱷的鼻子比鱷魚更寬更圓，而且牠嘴巴閉上時通常看不到下排牙齒。"},{"w":"crossing","p":"n.","d":"a place where people can safely cross a road or railway","c":"行人穿越道；平交道","s":"Students should always use the crossing in front of the school, where the white lines tell cars to stop for them.","t":"學生應該永遠使用學校前面的行人穿越道，那裡的白線會提醒車輛停下來讓他們過。","h":1},{"w":"crossing","p":"n.","d":"a journey across a sea or a wide river","c":"橫渡；渡海","s":"The crossing from the mainland to the island took three hours, and many passengers felt sick because of the big waves.","t":"從本島到那座島的渡海航程花了三小時，許多乘客因為大浪而暈船。"},{"w":"cross","p":"v.","d":"to go from one side of something to the other","c":"穿越；橫過","s":"Hold my hand when we cross the street, and remember to look both ways even when the light is green.","t":"我們過馬路時牽著我的手，記得即使是綠燈也要左右看。"},{"w":"pedestrian crossing","p":"n.phr.","d":"a marked place on a road where people on foot can cross","c":"行人穿越道；斑馬線","s":"A new pedestrian crossing with bright lights was built near the hospital so that elderly people can cross the busy road safely.","t":"醫院附近新建了一條有明亮燈光的行人穿越道，讓老年人能安全穿越這條繁忙的道路。"},{"w":"crossroads","p":"n.","d":"a place where two roads meet and cross; a point where an important decision must be made","c":"十字路口；（人生的）關鍵時刻","s":"After graduating from university, Amy felt she was at a crossroads and had to choose between a safe job and her dream of painting.","t":"大學畢業後，艾咪覺得自己正處於人生的十字路口，必須在穩定的工作和繪畫的夢想之間做選擇。"},{"w":"crutch","p":"n.","d":"a long stick that you put under your arm to help you walk when your leg is hurt","c":"拐杖","s":"After Peter broke his ankle, he walked with a crutch under each arm for six weeks and could not play basketball.","t":"彼得腳踝骨折後，他用拐杖撐在兩邊腋下走了六週，不能打籃球。","h":1},{"w":"on crutches","p":"phr.","d":"walking with the help of crutches","c":"拄著拐杖","s":"My grandmother is on crutches after her operation, so we moved her bed downstairs so that she does not need to climb the stairs.","t":"我奶奶手術後拄著拐杖，所以我們把她的床搬到樓下，讓她不用爬樓梯。"},{"w":"crutch","p":"n.","d":"something that you depend on too much for help or support","c":"依靠；精神支柱","s":"Some students use their phone as a crutch during every quiet moment, and they feel nervous when they cannot check it.","t":"有些學生在每個安靜的時刻都把手機當作依靠，當他們無法查看手機時會感到緊張。"},{"w":"cub","p":"n.","d":"a young bear, lion, tiger, wolf, or fox","c":"幼獸","s":"At the zoo, the mother lion lay in the sun while her little cub played in the grass and tried to catch its own tail.","t":"在動物園，母獅躺在陽光下，而她的小幼獅在草地上玩耍，試著抓自己的尾巴。","h":1},{"w":"bear cub","p":"n.phr.","d":"a young bear","c":"小熊","s":"Never go near a bear cub in the forest, because its mother is usually close by and will attack to protect it.","t":"在森林裡絕不要靠近小熊，因為牠的媽媽通常就在附近，會為了保護牠而攻擊。"},{"w":"cub scout","p":"n.phr.","d":"a young member of a scouting group, usually aged seven to ten","c":"幼童軍","s":"My little brother became a cub scout this year, and he loves learning to tie knots and build a fire on weekend camping trips.","t":"我弟弟今年成了幼童軍，他喜歡在週末露營時學習打結和生火。"},{"w":"cucumber","p":"n.","d":"a long green vegetable with a cool, fresh taste, often eaten raw in salads","c":"黃瓜；小黃瓜","s":"Mom cut a long green cucumber into thin slices for the salad, and it tasted cool and fresh on the hot summer evening.","t":"媽媽把一條長長的綠色小黃瓜切成薄片放進沙拉，在炎熱的夏夜吃起來清涼爽口。","h":1},{"w":"as cool as a cucumber","p":"phr.","d":"very calm, even in a difficult situation","c":"非常冷靜；泰然自若","s":"While everyone else was running around in panic before the show, the lead actor stayed as cool as a cucumber and quietly read his lines.","t":"演出前所有人都慌張地跑來跑去，男主角卻泰然自若，安靜地讀著台詞。"},{"w":"sea cucumber","p":"n.phr.","d":"a soft sea animal with a long body that lives on the sea floor and is eaten in some countries","c":"海參","s":"My grandfather ordered sea cucumber at the Chinese New Year dinner, but most of the children refused to try the strange, soft dish.","t":"我爺爺在年夜飯上點了海參，但大多數小孩都不肯嘗試這道奇怪又軟軟的菜。"},{"w":"cultivate","p":"v.","d":"to prepare land and grow crops on it","c":"耕種；栽培","s":"The farmers worked hard for years on the wild land by the river, and now they cultivate rice and vegetables there every season.","t":"農民們在河邊的荒地上辛苦工作了多年，現在他們每季都在那裡耕種稻米和蔬菜。","h":1},{"w":"cultivate","p":"v.","d":"to develop a skill, quality, or relationship by working at it","c":"培養（技能、關係）","s":"Reading a little every day is the best way to cultivate a love of books in young children, according to our librarian.","t":"根據我們的圖書館員所說，每天讀一點是在幼童身上培養對書本熱愛的最好方法。"},{"w":"cultivation","p":"n.","d":"the activity of growing crops; the development of a skill or quality","c":"耕作；栽培；培養","s":"The cultivation of tea on these hills began two hundred years ago, and the farmers still pick the leaves by hand today.","t":"這些山丘上的茶葉栽培始於兩百年前，農民至今仍以手工採摘茶葉。"},{"w":"cultivated","p":"adj.","d":"well-educated and polite; (of land) used for growing crops","c":"有教養的；已耕種的","s":"Our new neighbor is a cultivated woman who speaks four languages and plays the cello in the city orchestra every weekend.","t":"我們的新鄰居是位有教養的女士，她會說四種語言，每個週末在市立管弦樂團拉大提琴。"},{"w":"cumulative","p":"adj.","d":"increasing by one addition after another","c":"累積的；漸增的","s":"Eating cake every day may seem harmless, but the cumulative effect of all that sugar over many years can hurt your health.","t":"每天吃蛋糕似乎無害，但多年來所有那些糖的累積效應可能會損害你的健康。","h":1},{"w":"cumulatively","p":"adv.","d":"in a way that increases by one addition after another","c":"累積地","s":"Each small donation seems tiny on its own, but cumulatively the students raised enough money to build a new library.","t":"每筆小額捐款單獨看都很微小，但累積起來學生們籌到了足夠的錢蓋一座新圖書館。"},{"w":"accumulate","p":"v.","d":"to gradually collect or increase over time","c":"累積；積聚","s":"Grandpa never throws anything away, so over fifty years he has managed to accumulate enough old tools to fill a small museum.","t":"爺爺從不丟東西，所以五十年來他累積了足以填滿一座小博物館的舊工具。"},{"w":"accumulation","p":"n.","d":"a gradual increase or collection of something over time","c":"累積；積聚","s":"The accumulation of dust on the old books showed that nobody had opened the library cupboard for many years.","t":"舊書上積聚的灰塵顯示多年來沒有人打開過圖書館的櫃子。"},{"w":"curb","p":"v.","d":"to control or limit something that is not wanted","c":"抑制；控制","s":"Dad says we must curb our habit of ordering food from restaurants and cook at home at least five nights a week.","t":"爸爸說我們必須控制叫外送的習慣，每週至少在家煮五個晚上。","h":1},{"w":"curb","p":"n.","d":"the raised edge of a sidewalk next to the road","c":"路緣；人行道邊石","s":"The taxi stopped by the curb, and the driver got out to help the old lady with her heavy shopping bags.","t":"計程車停在路緣旁，司機下車幫老太太提沉重的購物袋。"},{"w":"curb spending","p":"v.phr.","d":"to reduce the amount of money that is spent","c":"削減開支","s":"The city government promised to curb spending on new buildings so that more money could go to schools and hospitals.","t":"市政府承諾削減新建築的開支，讓更多的錢能用於學校和醫院。"},{"w":"curfew","p":"n.","d":"a rule that people must be home or indoors by a certain time","c":"宵禁；門禁","s":"My parents have a curfew of ten o'clock, and if I come home after that, I am not allowed to go out the next weekend.","t":"我父母規定十點門禁，如果我超過那個時間回家，下個週末就不准出門。","h":1},{"w":"impose a curfew","p":"v.phr.","d":"to officially order people to stay indoors after a certain time","c":"實施宵禁","s":"After the riots, the city decided to impose a curfew from nine at night until six in the morning for one week.","t":"暴動之後，市政府決定實施宵禁一週，從晚上九點到早上六點。"},{"w":"break curfew","p":"v.phr.","d":"to stay out later than the time you are allowed","c":"違反門禁","s":"Tom's parents took away his phone for a week because he broke curfew on Saturday and came home at midnight.","t":"湯姆的父母沒收了他的手機一週，因為他星期六違反門禁，半夜才回家。","a":"broke curfew"},{"w":"curry","p":"n.","d":"a dish of meat or vegetables cooked in a thick, spicy sauce","c":"咖哩","s":"For dinner we had rice with a thick yellow curry made with chicken and potatoes, and it was so hot that I drank three glasses of water.","t":"晚餐我們吃了配著雞肉馬鈴薯濃郁黃咖哩的飯，它辣到我喝了三杯水。","h":1},{"w":"curry powder","p":"n.phr.","d":"a mixture of spices used to make curry","c":"咖哩粉","s":"Add two spoons of curry powder to the pot after the onions turn soft, and then pour in the coconut milk and let it cook slowly.","t":"洋蔥變軟後在鍋裡加兩匙咖哩粉，然後倒入椰奶慢慢煮。"},{"w":"chicken curry","p":"n.phr.","d":"curry made with chicken","c":"咖哩雞","s":"The chicken curry at the Indian restaurant near our school is famous, and there is always a long line outside at lunchtime.","t":"我們學校附近那家印度餐廳的咖哩雞很有名，午餐時間外面總是排著長隊。"},{"w":"curry favor with","p":"v.phr.","d":"to try to make someone like you by praising or helping them","c":"討好；拍馬屁","s":"Nobody respects a worker who tries to curry favor with the boss by laughing at all his jokes and bringing him coffee every morning.","t":"沒有人尊重那種靠笑老闆所有笑話、每天早上幫他買咖啡來討好老闆的員工。"},{"w":"customary","p":"adj.","d":"usual; done according to custom or tradition","c":"習慣的；慣常的","s":"In Taiwan it is customary to give children red envelopes with money at Chinese New Year, and almost every family follows the tradition.","t":"在台灣，農曆新年給孩子裝錢的紅包是慣常的做法，幾乎每個家庭都遵循這個傳統。","h":1},{"w":"custom","p":"n.","d":"a traditional way of behaving that a group of people has followed for a long time","c":"習俗；風俗","s":"It is an old custom in my hometown to eat long noodles on your birthday, because long noodles mean a long life.","t":"在我的家鄉，生日吃長壽麵是一個古老的習俗，因為長麵條代表長壽。"},{"w":"customs","p":"n.","d":"the place at an airport or border where your bags are checked; the taxes paid on goods brought into a country","c":"海關；關稅","s":"When we arrived at the airport in Japan, we had to wait in line at customs while officers checked our suitcases.","t":"我們抵達日本的機場時，必須在海關排隊等候，官員檢查我們的行李箱。"},{"w":"customarily","p":"adv.","d":"usually; according to custom","c":"習慣上；按照慣例","s":"Shops in this town customarily close for two hours after lunch, so tourists are often surprised to find the doors locked at two.","t":"這個鎮上的商店按照慣例午餐後關門兩小時，所以觀光客常常驚訝地發現兩點時門是鎖著的。"},{"w":"cynical","p":"adj.","d":"believing that people only care about themselves and are not sincere","c":"憤世嫉俗的；懷疑的","s":"Uncle Joe is so cynical that he believes every politician only cares about money, and nothing can change his mind.","t":"喬叔叔非常憤世嫉俗，他認為每個政治人物只在乎錢，沒有什麼能改變他的想法。","h":1},{"w":"cynic","p":"n.","d":"a person who believes that people only do things for selfish reasons","c":"憤世嫉俗者","s":"A cynic might say the company gave money to the school only for good publicity, but the students were still grateful.","t":"憤世嫉俗者可能會說公司捐錢給學校只是為了好名聲，但學生們仍然很感激。"},{"w":"cynicism","p":"n.","d":"the belief that people are only interested in themselves","c":"憤世嫉俗；懷疑主義","s":"Years of broken promises from leaders have created deep cynicism among young voters, and many of them no longer bother to vote.","t":"領導人多年來不斷違背承諾，在年輕選民中造成了深深的憤世嫉俗，許多人不再願意投票。"},{"w":"cynically","p":"adv.","d":"in a way that shows you believe people are selfish or not sincere","c":"憤世嫉俗地；懷疑地","s":"He laughed cynically when the salesman promised that the phone would last ten years, because his last one broke in six months.","t":"當銷售員保證這支手機能用十年時，他嘲諷地笑了，因為他上一支六個月就壞了。"},{"w":"dazzle","p":"v.","d":"(of a bright light) to make someone unable to see clearly for a short time","c":"使目眩；使眼花","s":"The lights of the truck coming toward us seemed to dazzle my father, so he slowed down until he could see the road again.","t":"迎面而來的卡車車燈使我爸爸眼花，所以他減速直到能再看清路為止。","h":1},{"w":"dazzle","p":"v.","d":"to impress someone greatly with skill, beauty, or ability","c":"使讚嘆；使傾倒","s":"The young singer walked onto the stage without fear, and her powerful voice was enough to dazzle all three judges.","t":"這位年輕歌手毫無懼色地走上舞台，她有力的歌聲足以令三位評審驚豔。"},{"w":"dazzling","p":"adj.","d":"extremely bright; extremely impressive","c":"耀眼的；令人讚嘆的","s":"The snow on the mountain was dazzling in the morning sun, so we all had to wear sunglasses to protect our eyes.","t":"山上的雪在晨光下耀眼奪目，所以我們都得戴太陽眼鏡保護眼睛。"},{"w":"dazzle","p":"n.","d":"a brightness that makes it hard to see; impressive beauty or skill","c":"炫目的光；令人目眩的美","s":"Behind all the dazzle of the movie star's life, she said, there were many lonely nights in hotel rooms far from home.","t":"她說，在電影明星生活所有的光鮮亮麗背後，是許多遠離家鄉、在飯店房間裡的孤單夜晚。"},{"w":"deafen","p":"v.","d":"to make someone unable to hear because of a very loud noise","c":"使聽不見；震聾","s":"The band turned the speakers up so high that the noise seemed to deafen us, and my ears were ringing for hours afterward.","t":"樂團把音響開得太大聲，噪音幾乎把我們震聾，之後我的耳朵嗡嗡響了好幾個小時。","h":1},{"w":"deafening","p":"adj.","d":"extremely loud","c":"震耳欲聾的","s":"When the home team scored in the last second, the noise in the stadium was deafening, and I could not hear my friend beside me.","t":"當主隊在最後一秒得分時，體育場裡的聲音震耳欲聾，我聽不到旁邊朋友說的話。"},{"w":"deaf","p":"adj.","d":"unable to hear, or unable to hear well","c":"聾的；失聰的","s":"My grandfather has become a little deaf with age, so you need to speak slowly and clearly when you talk to him.","t":"我爺爺隨著年紀增長有點重聽，所以你跟他說話時要說得慢而且清楚。"},{"w":"deafness","p":"n.","d":"the condition of being unable to hear","c":"耳聾；失聰","s":"Working in the noisy factory for thirty years without ear protection caused his deafness, the doctor explained.","t":"醫生解釋說，在吵雜的工廠裡工作三十年沒有戴耳罩，造成了他的失聰。"},{"w":"decisive","p":"adj.","d":"able to make decisions quickly and with confidence","c":"果斷的","s":"When the fire started, our teacher was decisive and led us all out of the building through the back door within one minute.","t":"火災發生時，我們的老師非常果斷，一分鐘內就帶著我們全部從後門離開了大樓。","h":1},{"w":"decisive","p":"adj.","d":"having a very important effect on the result of something","c":"決定性的","s":"The goal in the last minute was decisive, because it gave our school its first championship in twenty years.","t":"最後一分鐘的那一球是決定性的，因為它讓我們學校贏得了二十年來的第一座冠軍。"},{"w":"indecisive","p":"adj.","d":"unable to make decisions quickly","c":"優柔寡斷的","s":"Mark is so indecisive that it took him twenty minutes to choose between two ice cream flavors at the night market.","t":"馬克非常優柔寡斷，他在夜市花了二十分鐘才在兩種冰淇淋口味之間做出選擇。"},{"w":"decisively","p":"adv.","d":"in a quick, confident way that leaves no doubt","c":"果斷地；決定性地","s":"The captain acted decisively when the storm hit, turning the boat toward the harbor before anyone else noticed the danger.","t":"暴風雨來襲時船長果斷地行動，在其他人注意到危險之前就把船轉向港口。"},{"w":"decision","p":"n.","d":"a choice that you make after thinking about something","c":"決定","s":"Choosing a university is a big decision, so talk to your parents and teachers before you fill in the application form.","t":"選擇大學是一個重大的決定，所以在填申請表之前先和你的父母和老師談談。"},{"w":"dedication","p":"n.","d":"hard work and effort that you give to something you care about","c":"奉獻；投入；敬業","s":"The whole village admires Ms. Huang's dedication to the children, because she has taught at the mountain school for thirty years.","t":"全村都欽佩黃老師對孩子們的奉獻，因為她在山區學校教了三十年書。","h":1},{"w":"dedicate","p":"v.","d":"to give a lot of time and energy to something because you think it is important","c":"奉獻；致力於","s":"After her brother got sick, Dr. Lin decided to dedicate her career to finding better treatments for children with the same disease.","t":"林醫生的弟弟生病後，她決定把自己的職業生涯奉獻給為患有同樣疾病的兒童尋找更好的治療方法。"},{"w":"dedicated","p":"adj.","d":"working very hard at something because you care about it","c":"盡心盡力的；專注的","s":"Dr. Wu works twelve hours a day and visits sick children at home on weekends, so everyone agrees she is a truly dedicated doctor.","t":"吳醫生每天工作十二小時，週末還到家裡探視生病的孩子，所以大家都認為她是一位真正盡心盡力的醫生。"},{"w":"dedicate oneself to","p":"v.phr.","d":"to give all your time and effort to one activity or purpose","c":"獻身於；全心投入","s":"After he retired from teaching, my grandfather dedicated himself to growing roses, and his garden now wins prizes every year.","t":"我爺爺從教職退休後全心投入種植玫瑰，他的花園現在每年都得獎。","a":"dedicated himself to"},{"w":"deduct","p":"v.","d":"to take an amount of money or points away from a total","c":"扣除；減去","s":"The company will deduct two hundred dollars from your pay for each day you are late, so please try to arrive on time.","t":"你每遲到一天，公司就會從你的薪水中扣除兩百元，所以請儘量準時到。","h":1},{"w":"deduction","p":"n.","d":"an amount taken away from a total; a conclusion you reach by thinking","c":"扣除額；推論","s":"After the deduction for taxes and insurance, my first salary was much smaller than the number written in the job advertisement.","t":"扣除稅金和保險後，我的第一份薪水比徵人廣告上寫的數字少了很多。"},{"w":"deductible","p":"adj.","d":"able to be taken away from the total amount of tax you must pay","c":"可扣除的；可抵稅的","s":"Money given to a registered charity is deductible, so keep the receipt and show it when you report your taxes in May.","t":"捐給合法慈善機構的錢是可抵稅的，所以請保留收據，並在五月報稅時出示。"},{"w":"deduct from","p":"v.phr.","d":"to take an amount away from a particular total","c":"從…扣除","s":"The teacher said she would deduct from our final grade five points for every day our project was handed in late.","t":"老師說專題每晚交一天，她就會從我們的期末成績扣五分。"},{"w":"deem","p":"v.","d":"to consider or judge something in a particular way (formal)","c":"認為；視為","s":"Engineers now deem the old bridge too dangerous to use, so all cars must take the long road around the lake until it is repaired.","t":"工程師現在認為這座老橋太危險不能使用，所以在修好之前所有車輛都必須繞湖走遠路。","h":1},{"w":"be deemed","p":"v.phr.","d":"to be considered or judged to be something","c":"被視為；被認為","s":"Any student who misses more than ten classes will be deemed to have failed the course, according to the school's new rules.","t":"根據學校的新規定，任何缺課超過十次的學生將被視為該課程不及格。"},{"w":"deem it necessary","p":"v.phr.","d":"to decide that something must be done","c":"認為有必要","s":"If the doctors deem it necessary, they will keep my grandmother in the hospital for a few more days to watch her heart.","t":"如果醫生認為有必要，他們會讓我奶奶在醫院多住幾天以觀察她的心臟。"}]},{"unit":10,"theme":"default – directive","cards":[{"w":"default","p":"n.","d":"the setting or choice that a machine or program uses when you do not change anything","c":"預設值；預設選項","s":"The default language on this new laptop is English, so my grandmother asked me to change it to Chinese for her.","t":"這台新筆電的預設語言是英文，所以我奶奶請我幫她改成中文。","h":1},{"w":"by default","p":"phr.","d":"automatically, because nothing else was chosen","c":"預設地；自動地","s":"Most apps collect your location by default, so it is a good idea to check the privacy settings when you install them.","t":"大多數 App 都會預設收集你的位置，所以安裝時最好檢查一下隱私設定。"},{"w":"default","p":"v.","d":"to fail to pay money that you owe","c":"拖欠；未履行（債務）","s":"If a company cannot pay back its loans on time, it may default on them, and the bank will lose a lot of money.","t":"如果一家公司無法準時償還貸款，它可能會拖欠債務，銀行就會損失很多錢。"},{"w":"default setting","p":"n.phr.","d":"the original setting of a machine or program before anyone changes it","c":"預設設定","s":"If the game runs too slowly, go back to the default setting and turn off the extra effects that you added last week.","t":"如果遊戲跑得太慢，就回到預設設定，把你上週加的額外特效關掉。"},{"w":"defect","p":"n.","d":"a fault or problem in something that makes it not perfect","c":"缺陷；瑕疵","s":"The company recalled thousands of cars because a defect in the brakes could cause serious accidents on the highway.","t":"這家公司召回了數千輛汽車，因為煞車的一個缺陷可能在高速公路上造成嚴重事故。","h":1},{"w":"defective","p":"adj.","d":"having a fault; not working correctly","c":"有缺陷的；有瑕疵的","s":"My new headphones were defective, so I took them back to the store and the clerk gave me a new pair.","t":"我的新耳機有瑕疵，所以我把它拿回店裡，店員給了我一副新的。"},{"w":"defect","p":"v.","d":"to leave your country or group and join the other side","c":"叛逃；變節","s":"During the war, several soldiers decided to defect to the other side because they no longer believed in the fight.","t":"戰爭期間，幾名士兵決定叛逃到敵方，因為他們不再相信這場戰鬥的意義。"},{"w":"birth defect","p":"n.phr.","d":"a physical problem that a baby is born with","c":"先天缺陷","s":"Doctors say that taking certain medicines during pregnancy may increase the risk of a birth defect in the baby.","t":"醫生說懷孕期間服用某些藥物可能會增加寶寶先天缺陷的風險。"},{"w":"defiance","p":"n.","d":"open refusal to obey someone or something","c":"反抗；違抗","s":"In an act of defiance, the students refused to leave the hall until the principal agreed to listen to their complaints.","t":"學生們以反抗的行動拒絕離開禮堂，直到校長同意聽他們的抱怨。","h":1},{"w":"defy","p":"v.","d":"to refuse to obey a person, rule, or order","c":"違抗；反抗","s":"The little boy chose to defy his parents and stayed out playing until the streetlights came on.","t":"那個小男孩選擇違抗父母，在外面玩到路燈亮了才回家。"},{"w":"in defiance of","p":"phr.","d":"without caring about a rule or warning; against","c":"無視；不顧","s":"The driver kept going at high speed in defiance of the warning signs, and the police stopped him two minutes later.","t":"那位駕駛無視警告標誌繼續高速行駛，兩分鐘後就被警察攔了下來。"},{"w":"defiant","p":"adj.","d":"showing that you refuse to obey","c":"挑釁的；反抗的","s":"The defiant teenager crossed his arms and refused to apologize, even though everyone in the room was waiting.","t":"那個反抗的青少年雙手交叉，拒絕道歉，儘管房間裡每個人都在等。"},{"w":"definitive","p":"adj.","d":"final and certain; the best and most complete","c":"最終的；確定的；權威的","s":"The doctor said she could not give a definitive answer about the illness until all the test results came back next week.","t":"醫生說在下週所有檢驗結果出來之前，她無法對這個病給出確定的答案。","h":1},{"w":"define","p":"v.","d":"to explain exactly what a word or idea means","c":"定義；解釋","s":"Before we start the debate, let us define the word \"success,\" because each of us may understand it differently.","t":"在開始辯論之前，我們先定義「成功」這個詞，因為我們每個人的理解可能不同。"},{"w":"definition","p":"n.","d":"an explanation of what a word means","c":"定義","s":"If you do not know a word, look up its definition in the dictionary instead of guessing what it means.","t":"如果你不認識一個字，就去字典裡查它的定義，而不是猜它的意思。"},{"w":"definite","p":"adj.","d":"clear and certain; not likely to change","c":"明確的；確定的","s":"We need a definite answer from you by Friday, or we will have to give the ticket to another student.","t":"我們需要你在星期五前給出明確的答覆，否則我們只好把票給別的學生。"},{"w":"definitely","p":"adv.","d":"certainly; without any doubt","c":"肯定地；絕對地","s":"I will definitely come to your birthday party on Saturday, even if I have to finish my homework late at night.","t":"我星期六一定會去你的生日派對，即使我得熬夜把作業做完。"},{"w":"dental","p":"adj.","d":"connected with teeth","c":"牙齒的；牙科的","s":"Children should have a dental checkup every six months so that small problems with their teeth are found early.","t":"孩子每六個月應該做一次牙科檢查，這樣牙齒的小問題才能早點被發現。","h":1},{"w":"dentist","p":"n.","d":"a doctor who takes care of people's teeth","c":"牙醫","s":"I was afraid of going to the dentist when I was little, but now I know that a quick visit saves a lot of pain.","t":"我小時候很怕去看牙醫，但現在我知道快速看一下可以省掉很多痛苦。"},{"w":"dental floss","p":"n.phr.","d":"a thin thread used to clean between your teeth","c":"牙線","s":"Brushing is not enough, so my dentist told me to use dental floss every night to clean between my teeth.","t":"只刷牙是不夠的，所以牙醫告訴我每天晚上要用牙線清潔牙縫。"},{"w":"dentistry","p":"n.","d":"the medical study and treatment of teeth","c":"牙醫學","s":"My cousin is studying dentistry at a university in Taipei because she wants to open her own clinic in the future.","t":"我表姊在台北的一所大學讀牙醫學，因為她將來想開自己的診所。"},{"w":"deplete","p":"v.","d":"to use up most of something so that little is left","c":"耗盡；用盡","s":"If we continue to deplete the fish in the ocean at this speed, our grandchildren may never taste fresh seafood.","t":"如果我們繼續以這種速度耗盡海洋裡的魚，我們的孫子可能永遠吃不到新鮮海鮮。","h":1},{"w":"depleted","p":"adj.","d":"used up; almost gone","c":"耗盡的；枯竭的","s":"After the long marathon, the runner's energy was completely depleted, and he needed to rest for a whole week.","t":"跑完漫長的馬拉松後，那位跑者的體力完全耗盡，他需要休息整整一週。"},{"w":"depletion","p":"n.","d":"the act of using up something so that little is left","c":"耗盡；枯竭","s":"Scientists are worried about the depletion of the ozone layer, which protects us from the harmful rays of the sun.","t":"科學家擔心臭氧層的耗損，臭氧層保護我們不受太陽有害射線的傷害。"},{"w":"deplete one's savings","p":"v.phr.","d":"to use up almost all the money you have saved","c":"耗盡存款","s":"The medical bills began to deplete their savings quickly, so the family had to ask relatives for help with the costs.","t":"醫療費用開始迅速耗盡他們的存款，所以這家人只好向親戚求助分擔費用。","a":"deplete their savings"},{"w":"deprive","p":"v.","d":"to take something important away from someone","c":"剝奪；使喪失","s":"Staying up late to play games will deprive you of the sleep your brain needs to remember what you learned today.","t":"熬夜打遊戲會剝奪你大腦記住今天所學內容所需要的睡眠。","h":1},{"w":"deprive sb of sth","p":"v.phr.","d":"to stop someone from having something they need","c":"剝奪某人的…","s":"The long power cut deprived the village of light and heat for two whole days during the coldest week of winter.","t":"在冬天最冷的那一週，長時間的停電剝奪了村子的光和熱整整兩天。","a":"deprived the village of"},{"w":"deprived","p":"adj.","d":"not having enough of the things people need, such as money or food","c":"貧困的；匱乏的","s":"Many children from deprived areas do not have a quiet place to study, so the library stays open late for them.","t":"許多來自貧困地區的孩子沒有安靜的地方讀書，所以圖書館為他們開放到很晚。"},{"w":"deprivation","p":"n.","d":"the state of not having something you need","c":"剝奪；匱乏","s":"Sleep deprivation can make people angry and forgetful, which is why doctors say teenagers need at least eight hours a night.","t":"睡眠不足會讓人易怒又健忘，這就是為什麼醫生說青少年每晚至少需要八小時睡眠。"},{"w":"descent","p":"n.","d":"the act of going down","c":"下降；下落","s":"The plane began its descent into Taoyuan Airport, and the pilot asked everyone to return to their seats and fasten their belts.","t":"飛機開始下降準備降落桃園機場，機長請大家回到座位並繫好安全帶。","h":1},{"w":"descent","p":"n.","d":"your family origin; the people you come from","c":"血統；祖籍","s":"Many people in this town are of Japanese descent, and their grandparents still speak the language at home.","t":"這個鎮上許多人有日本血統，他們的祖父母在家裡仍然說日語。"},{"w":"descend","p":"v.","d":"to go or come down","c":"下降；下來","s":"Be careful when you descend the stairs in the old temple, because the stone steps are narrow and often wet.","t":"走下古廟的樓梯時要小心，因為石階很窄而且常常是濕的。"},{"w":"descendant","p":"n.","d":"a person who is related to someone who lived long ago","c":"後代；子孫","s":"The old man is a descendant of a famous general, and his family still keeps the general's sword in their living room.","t":"那位老先生是一位名將的後代，他的家族至今仍把將軍的劍保存在客廳裡。"},{"w":"despise","p":"v.","d":"to dislike someone or something very strongly and have no respect for them","c":"鄙視；看不起","s":"I despise people who throw trash out of their car windows, because they make the streets dirty for everyone else.","t":"我鄙視那些把垃圾丟出車窗的人，因為他們把街道弄髒，害到其他所有人。","h":1},{"w":"despicable","p":"adj.","d":"very bad and deserving no respect","c":"卑鄙的；可鄙的","s":"Stealing money from an old lady who trusted you is a truly despicable thing to do, and the judge said so in court.","t":"偷一位信任你的老太太的錢是真正卑鄙的行為，法官在法庭上也這麼說。"},{"w":"despise sb for sth","p":"v.phr.","d":"to have no respect for someone because of something they did","c":"因…而鄙視某人","s":"She despised him for lying to the whole team about the missing money, and she never spoke to him again.","t":"她因為他對整個團隊謊報失蹤款項的事而鄙視他，從此再也沒跟他說過話。","a":"despised him for"},{"w":"destined","p":"adj.","d":"certain to happen or to become something in the future","c":"注定的；命中注定的","s":"Everyone said the talented young singer was destined for great things, and ten years later she won an international award.","t":"大家都說這位有才華的年輕歌手注定會有大成就，十年後她果然贏得了國際大獎。","h":1},{"w":"be destined to","p":"v.phr.","d":"to be certain to do or become something","c":"注定會…","s":"With such hard-working players and a smart coach, the team was destined to win the championship this year.","t":"有這麼努力的球員和聰明的教練，這支球隊注定會贏得今年的冠軍。","a":"was destined to"},{"w":"destiny","p":"n.","d":"the things that will happen to someone in the future; fate","c":"命運；天命","s":"Some people believe that destiny decides who we marry, but my grandmother says you have to make good choices yourself.","t":"有些人相信命運決定我們和誰結婚，但我奶奶說你必須自己做出好的選擇。"},{"w":"destination","p":"n.","d":"the place you are traveling to","c":"目的地","s":"After a twelve-hour flight, we finally reached our destination, a small island with white beaches and clear blue water.","t":"經過十二小時的飛行，我們終於到達目的地，一座有白色沙灘和清澈藍海的小島。"},{"w":"detach","p":"v.","d":"to separate one thing from another","c":"分開；拆下","s":"You can detach the keyboard from this tablet when you want to watch a movie, and attach it again for typing.","t":"當你想看電影時，可以把鍵盤從這台平板拆下來，要打字時再裝回去。","h":1},{"w":"detached","p":"adj.","d":"not showing feelings; not involved","c":"超然的；冷漠的","s":"The nurse stayed calm and detached during the emergency, which helped the frightened family feel that everything was under control.","t":"那位護理師在緊急狀況中保持冷靜超然，讓受驚的家人覺得一切都在掌控之中。"},{"w":"detachment","p":"n.","d":"the state of not being affected by feelings; a small group of soldiers sent to do a job","c":"超然；冷靜；分遣隊","s":"A good judge must look at every case with detachment, without letting personal feelings change the final decision.","t":"好的法官必須以超然的態度看待每一個案件，不讓個人感情改變最終判決。"},{"w":"attach","p":"v.","d":"to fasten or join one thing to another","c":"附上；貼上；連接","s":"Please attach a recent photo to your application form before you hand it in to the office next Monday.","t":"請在下週一把申請表交到辦公室之前，附上一張近照。"},{"w":"detain","p":"v.","d":"to keep someone in a place and not let them leave, especially by the police","c":"拘留；扣留","s":"The police can detain a suspect for up to twenty-four hours before they must either charge him or let him go.","t":"警方可以拘留嫌疑人最多二十四小時，然後必須起訴他或放他走。","h":1},{"w":"detention","p":"n.","d":"the state of being kept in a place; a punishment of staying at school after classes","c":"拘留；留校察看","s":"Tom got detention after school for a week because he kept throwing paper balls at his classmates during the math class.","t":"湯姆被罰放學後留校察看一週，因為他在數學課上一直朝同學丟紙球。","h":1},{"w":"be detained","p":"v.phr.","d":"to be kept somewhere and not allowed to leave","c":"被拘留；被耽擱","s":"Several reporters were detained at the airport for hours because their papers were not in order when they arrived.","t":"幾位記者在機場被扣留了好幾個小時，因為他們抵達時證件不齊全。","a":"were detained"},{"w":"detention center","p":"n.phr.","d":"a place where people are kept while officials decide what to do with them","c":"收容所；拘留中心","s":"The young men were kept at a detention center near the border while officials checked where they had come from.","t":"那些年輕人被關在邊境附近的拘留中心，等待官員查明他們來自哪裡。"},{"w":"detainee","p":"n.","d":"a person who is kept in a place by the police or army","c":"被拘留者","s":"Lawyers visited the detainee every week to make sure he was treated fairly while he waited for his trial.","t":"律師每週探視這名被拘留者，確保他在等待審判期間受到公平對待。"},{"w":"deter","p":"v.","d":"to make someone decide not to do something, often by making them afraid","c":"阻止；威懾；使打消念頭","s":"The school hopes that the new cameras in the hallways will deter students from fighting or stealing things from lockers.","t":"學校希望走廊上新裝的攝影機能阻止學生打架或偷置物櫃裡的東西。","h":1},{"w":"deterrent","p":"n.","d":"something that stops people from doing something bad","c":"威懾物；遏制物","s":"A big dog in the yard is a good deterrent against thieves, even if the dog is actually very friendly.","t":"院子裡的大狗是對小偷很好的威懾，即使那隻狗其實非常友善。"},{"w":"deter sb from","p":"v.phr.","d":"to stop someone from doing something","c":"阻止某人做…","s":"Heavy rain did not deter the fans from going to the concert, and they stood outside in wet clothes for three hours.","t":"大雨沒有阻止粉絲們去聽演唱會，他們穿著濕衣服在外面站了三個小時。","a":"deter the fans from"},{"w":"undeterred","p":"adj.","d":"continuing to do something even though there are problems","c":"未被嚇阻的；不氣餒的","s":"Undeterred by two failed attempts, the climber tried a third time and finally reached the top of the mountain in June.","t":"兩次失敗都沒有讓那位登山者退縮，他第三次嘗試，終於在六月登上山頂。","a":"Undeterred"},{"w":"detergent","p":"n.","d":"a liquid or powder used for washing clothes or dishes","c":"清潔劑；洗衣粉","s":"Add one cup of detergent to the washing machine, but do not use more than that or the clothes will feel sticky.","t":"在洗衣機裡加一杯洗衣粉，但不要加太多，否則衣服會有黏黏的感覉。","h":1},{"w":"laundry detergent","p":"n.phr.","d":"soap used for washing clothes","c":"洗衣精；洗衣粉","s":"We are out of laundry detergent, so please pick up a bottle at the supermarket on your way home from school.","t":"我們的洗衣精用完了，所以請你放學回家路上到超市買一瓶。"},{"w":"liquid detergent","p":"n.phr.","d":"a cleaning product in liquid form","c":"液態清潔劑；洗衣精","s":"Many families now prefer liquid detergent because it dissolves faster in cold water and leaves no white marks on dark clothes.","t":"現在許多家庭比較喜歡液態洗衣精，因為它在冷水中溶解得更快，也不會在深色衣服上留下白色痕跡。"},{"w":"devour","p":"v.","d":"to eat something quickly because you are very hungry","c":"吞食；狼吞虎嚥","s":"After the long hike, the hungry boys began to devour the pizza as soon as it was placed on the table.","t":"長途健行之後，飢餓的男孩們在披薩一放上桌就開始狼吞虎嚥。","h":1},{"w":"devour","p":"v.","d":"to read or watch something quickly and eagerly","c":"如飢似渴地閱讀（或觀看）","s":"My little sister can devour a three-hundred-page novel in a single weekend if the story is exciting enough.","t":"如果故事夠精彩，我妹妹可以在一個週末內一口氣讀完一本三百頁的小說。"},{"w":"be devoured by","p":"v.phr.","d":"to be destroyed or completely taken over by something","c":"被…吞噬","s":"The small wooden houses were devoured by the forest fire within minutes, and the families lost everything they owned.","t":"那些小木屋在幾分鐘內就被森林大火吞噬，這些家庭失去了所有的財產。","a":"were devoured by"},{"w":"diabetes","p":"n.","d":"a serious illness in which the body cannot control the amount of sugar in the blood","c":"糖尿病","s":"People with diabetes have to watch how much sugar they eat, and some of them need to check their blood every day.","t":"患有糖尿病的人必須注意吃多少糖，有些人還需要每天檢查血糖。","h":1},{"w":"diabetic","p":"adj.","d":"connected with diabetes; suitable for people with diabetes","c":"糖尿病的；供糖尿病患者的","s":"The bakery now sells diabetic cakes made with less sugar, so my grandfather can finally enjoy dessert again.","t":"這家麵包店現在賣少糖的糖尿病蛋糕，所以我爺爺終於可以再享用甜點了。"},{"w":"diabetic","p":"n.","d":"a person who has diabetes","c":"糖尿病患者","s":"As a diabetic, my uncle always carries a small snack in his bag in case his blood sugar suddenly drops.","t":"身為糖尿病患者，我叔叔總是在包包裡帶一小份點心，以防血糖突然下降。"},{"w":"dictate","p":"v.","d":"to say words for someone to write down","c":"口述；聽寫","s":"The teacher will dictate ten sentences, and you have to write down exactly what you hear without looking at your book.","t":"老師會口述十個句子，你們必須不看書，把聽到的內容一字不差地寫下來。","h":1},{"w":"dictation","p":"n.","d":"the activity of writing down what someone says","c":"聽寫","s":"We have an English dictation test every Monday, so I practice spelling the new words with my mother on Sunday night.","t":"我們每個星期一都有英文聽寫測驗，所以我星期天晚上會和媽媽一起練習拼新單字。","h":1},{"w":"dictator","p":"n.","d":"a ruler who has total power and often uses it cruelly","c":"獨裁者","s":"The dictator ruled the country for thirty years and put anyone who disagreed with him in prison without a trial.","t":"這位獨裁者統治國家三十年，把任何不同意他的人未經審判就關進監獄。","h":1},{"w":"dictatorship","p":"n.","d":"a country or government ruled by a dictator","c":"獨裁統治；獨裁國家","s":"After decades of dictatorship, the people finally held free elections and chose their own leaders for the first time.","t":"經過數十年的獨裁統治，人民終於舉行了自由選舉，第一次選出自己的領導人。","h":1},{"w":"dictate","p":"v.","d":"to tell someone exactly what to do, in a way they must obey","c":"命令；支配","s":"Parents should guide their children, but they should not dictate every decision about which friends they can have.","t":"父母應該引導孩子，但不應該支配孩子交哪些朋友的每一個決定。"},{"w":"dictatorial","p":"adj.","d":"using power in an unfair way and not listening to others","c":"獨裁的；專橫的","s":"The new manager has a dictatorial style, and he never asks for anyone's opinion before changing the rules of the office.","t":"新經理的作風很專橫，他在更改辦公室規定之前從不徵詢任何人的意見。"},{"w":"diesel","p":"n.","d":"a heavy oil used as fuel in trucks, buses, and some cars","c":"柴油","s":"Most big trucks and buses run on diesel, which is cheaper than gasoline but produces more black smoke.","t":"大多數大卡車和公車都使用柴油，它比汽油便宜，但會產生更多黑煙。","h":1},{"w":"diesel engine","p":"n.phr.","d":"an engine that burns diesel oil","c":"柴油引擎","s":"The old fishing boat has a diesel engine that is loud and smelly, but it has never broken down in twenty years.","t":"這艘老漁船有一台又吵又臭的柴油引擎，但它二十年來從未壞過。"},{"w":"diesel","p":"adj.","d":"using diesel oil as fuel","c":"柴油的","s":"My father bought a diesel car because he drives long distances every week and wants to save money on fuel.","t":"我爸爸買了一輛柴油車，因為他每週都開長途，想節省油錢。"},{"w":"differentiate","p":"v.","d":"to see or show how two things are different","c":"區別；辨別","s":"It is hard for many English learners to differentiate between the sounds of \"l\" and \"r\" when they listen to fast speech.","t":"許多英語學習者在聽快速講話時，很難分辨l 和 r 的發音。","h":1},{"w":"differ","p":"v.","d":"to be different from something","c":"不同；相異","s":"My brother and I differ in many ways; he loves sports and noise, while I prefer quiet afternoons with a good book.","t":"我和我哥哥在很多方面都不同；他喜歡運動和熱鬧，而我比較喜歡安靜的下午配一本好書。"},{"w":"difference","p":"n.","d":"the way in which two things are not the same","c":"差異；不同","s":"The main difference between the two phones is the camera, so choose the better one if you like taking pictures.","t":"這兩支手機主要的差別在於相機，所以如果你喜歡拍照，就選相機比較好的那支。"},{"w":"different","p":"adj.","d":"not the same","c":"不同的","s":"Although the twins look exactly the same, their personalities are completely different, and they rarely enjoy the same movies.","t":"雖然這對雙胞胎長得一模一樣，但他們的個性完全不同，很少喜歡同一部電影。"},{"w":"differentiation","p":"n.","d":"the act of showing or seeing how things are different","c":"區別；分化","s":"Clear differentiation between fact and opinion is an important skill when you read news on the Internet.","t":"在網路上閱讀新聞時，清楚區分事實和意見是一項重要的能力。"},{"w":"diplomacy","p":"n.","d":"the work of managing relations between countries; skill in dealing with people","c":"外交；交際手腕","s":"The two countries solved the problem through diplomacy instead of war, and their leaders met to sign a peace agreement.","t":"兩國透過外交而非戰爭解決了問題，兩國領導人會面簽署了和平協議。","h":1},{"w":"diplomat","p":"n.","d":"a person whose job is to represent their country in another country","c":"外交官","s":"As a diplomat, my aunt has lived in five different countries and can greet people in at least seven languages.","t":"身為外交官，我阿姨住過五個不同的國家，能用至少七種語言跟人打招呼。"},{"w":"diplomatic","p":"adj.","d":"connected with diplomacy; good at dealing with people without upsetting them","c":"外交的；有手腕的","s":"When two friends argue, Lisa always finds a diplomatic way to calm them down without taking either side.","t":"當兩個朋友吵架時，麗莎總能找到圓融的方式讓他們冷靜下來，而不偏袒任何一方。"},{"w":"diplomatic relations","p":"n.phr.","d":"the official relationship between two countries","c":"外交關係","s":"The two nations restored diplomatic relations last year, and tourists can now travel between them without a special visa.","t":"這兩個國家去年恢復了外交關係，現在觀光客不需要特別簽證就能在兩國之間旅行。"},{"w":"directive","p":"n.","d":"an official order or instruction","c":"指令；指示","s":"The government issued a new directive that requires all restaurants to stop giving out plastic straws by the end of the year.","t":"政府發布了一項新指令，要求所有餐廳在年底前停止提供塑膠吸管。","h":1},{"w":"direct","p":"v.","d":"to control or manage something; to tell someone the way","c":"指導；指揮；指路","s":"A police officer stood in the middle of the road to direct traffic after the traffic lights stopped working.","t":"紅綠燈壞掉後，一名警察站在馬路中央指揮交通。"},{"w":"direction","p":"n.","d":"the way that someone or something is going or facing","c":"方向","s":"We walked in the wrong direction for twenty minutes before we realized the station was behind us all the time.","t":"我們朝錯誤的方向走了二十分鐘，才發現車站一直在我們後面。"},{"w":"director","p":"n.","d":"a person who is in charge of a film, play, or company","c":"導演；主管","s":"The film director asked the actors to repeat the scene five times until everyone was happy with it.","t":"電影導演要求演員把那一幕重拍五次，直到大家都滿意為止。"},{"w":"directly","p":"adv.","d":"without anything or anyone in between; straight","c":"直接地","s":"Instead of sending an email, she went directly to the manager's office to explain the problem face to face.","t":"她沒有寄電子郵件，而是直接去經理辦公室當面解釋問題。"}]},{"unit":11,"theme":"disable – dividend","cards":[{"w":"disable","p":"v.","d":"to stop something from working; to injure someone so they cannot use part of their body","c":"使失去功能；停用；使殘廢","s":"You should disable the pop-up messages on your phone during the exam so that nothing distracts you from the questions.","t":"考試期間你應該關閉手機上的彈出訊息，這樣才不會有東西讓你分心。","h":1},{"w":"disabled","p":"adj.","d":"not able to use part of your body or mind fully","c":"身心障礙的","s":"The new library has wide doors and ramps so that disabled visitors in wheelchairs can enter every room easily.","t":"新圖書館有寬門和斜坡，讓坐輪椅的身心障礙訪客能輕鬆進入每個房間。"},{"w":"disability","p":"n.","d":"a physical or mental condition that makes it hard to do some things","c":"殘疾；身心障礙","s":"Having a disability did not stop my cousin from finishing university and finding a job she really loves.","t":"有身心障礙並沒有阻止我表姊完成大學學業，並找到一份她真正熱愛的工作。"},{"w":"the disabled","p":"n.","d":"people who have a disability","c":"身心障礙者","s":"These parking spaces near the entrance are only for the disabled, so please leave your car somewhere else.","t":"入口附近的這些停車位只提供給身心障礙者，所以請把車停在別的地方。"},{"w":"disastrous","p":"adj.","d":"very bad; causing a lot of damage or trouble","c":"災難性的；極糟的","s":"The school trip was disastrous: the bus broke down, it rained all day, and two students lost their bags.","t":"這次校外教學糟透了：巴士拋錨、整天下雨，還有兩個學生弄丟了包包。","h":1},{"w":"disaster","p":"n.","d":"a terrible event that causes great damage or suffering","c":"災難","s":"After the earthquake, people from all over the island sent food and blankets to help the victims of the disaster.","t":"地震過後，全島各地的人們寄來食物和毛毯，幫助這場災難的受害者。"},{"w":"natural disaster","p":"n.phr.","d":"a terrible event caused by nature, such as a flood or earthquake","c":"天災；自然災害","s":"Typhoons are the most common natural disaster in Taiwan, so every family should keep a flashlight and some water ready.","t":"颱風是台灣最常見的天災，所以每個家庭都應該準備好手電筒和一些水。"},{"w":"disastrously","p":"adv.","d":"in a way that is very bad or harmful","c":"災難性地；慘重地","s":"The plan went disastrously wrong when the main speaker missed his flight and nobody else was ready to give the talk.","t":"當主講人錯過班機、又沒有人準備好代講時，這個計畫就徹底出了大錯。"},{"w":"disbelief","p":"n.","d":"the feeling of not being able to believe something","c":"不相信；懷疑","s":"The students stared at the teacher in disbelief when she said the final exam had been canceled for the whole grade.","t":"當老師說整個年級的期末考取消時，學生們不敢相信地盯著她看。","h":1},{"w":"disbelieve","p":"v.","d":"to not believe someone or something","c":"不相信","s":"There is no reason to disbelieve her story, because three other people saw the same strange light in the sky.","t":"沒有理由不相信她說的事，因為另外三個人也看到了天空中同樣奇怪的光。"},{"w":"in disbelief","p":"phr.","d":"in a way that shows you cannot believe something","c":"不敢相信地","s":"He shook his head in disbelief when the doctor told him that the little cut on his finger needed five stitches.","t":"當醫生告訴他手指上的小傷口需要縫五針時，他不敢相信地搖了搖頭。"},{"w":"believe","p":"v.","d":"to think that something is true","c":"相信","s":"I believe that hard work matters more than talent, because I have seen lazy geniuses fail many times.","t":"我相信努力比天分更重要，因為我看過很多懶惰的天才失敗。"},{"w":"discard","p":"v.","d":"to throw something away because you do not want it","c":"丟棄；拋棄","s":"Please do not discard the old textbooks, because the younger students can still use them for extra practice.","t":"請不要丟掉舊課本，因為低年級的學生還可以拿來做額外練習。","h":1},{"w":"discarded","p":"adj.","d":"thrown away","c":"被丟棄的","s":"Volunteers collected hundreds of discarded bottles and cans from the beach in just two hours on Sunday morning.","t":"志工們在星期天早上短短兩小時內，就從海灘上撿了數百個被丟棄的瓶子和罐子。"},{"w":"discard","p":"n.","d":"a card or thing that has been thrown away","c":"棄牌；丟棄物","s":"In this card game, each player picks up one card and then puts one discard face up in the middle of the table.","t":"在這個紙牌遊戲中，每位玩家抽一張牌，然後把一張棄牌正面朝上放在桌子中間。"},{"w":"discharge","p":"v.","d":"to allow someone to leave a hospital or the army; to send out gas or liquid","c":"允許離開（醫院／軍隊）；排放","s":"The hospital will discharge my grandmother tomorrow morning if her temperature stays normal during the night.","t":"如果我奶奶的體溫在夜裡保持正常，醫院明天早上就會讓她出院。","h":1},{"w":"discharge","p":"n.","d":"the act of sending out gas or liquid; the act of letting someone leave","c":"排放；出院；退伍","s":"The factory was fined for the discharge of dirty water into the river, which killed many fish downstream.","t":"這家工廠因為把髒水排放到河裡而被罰款，這造成下游許多魚死亡。"},{"w":"be discharged from","p":"v.phr.","d":"to be officially allowed to leave a hospital, the army, etc.","c":"從…出院／退伍","s":"My brother was discharged from the army last month, and now he is looking for a job in the city.","t":"我哥哥上個月從軍隊退伍，現在他正在城裡找工作。","a":"was discharged from"},{"w":"disciple","p":"n.","d":"a person who follows and learns from a teacher or leader","c":"門徒；信徒；弟子","s":"The old master taught kung fu to only one disciple, who later opened schools all over the country.","t":"老師父只把功夫教給一位弟子，這位弟子後來在全國各地開了武館。","h":1},{"w":"discipline","p":"n.","d":"the practice of making people obey rules; control over your own behavior","c":"紀律","s":"Good discipline in class helps everyone learn, so the teacher explains the rules clearly on the first day.","t":"課堂上良好的紀律有助於每個人學習，所以老師在第一天就把規則說清楚。"},{"w":"discipline","p":"v.","d":"to punish someone or train them to obey rules","c":"懲戒；管教；訓練","s":"Parents should discipline their children with patience, because shouting usually teaches them to shout back.","t":"父母應該有耐心地管教孩子，因為大吼通常只會教孩子吼回來。"},{"w":"self-discipline","p":"n.","d":"the ability to make yourself do what you should do","c":"自律","s":"Studying at home takes a lot of self-discipline, because nobody is there to stop you from watching videos all afternoon.","t":"在家讀書需要很強的自律，因為沒有人會阻止你看一整個下午的影片。"},{"w":"disciplinary","p":"adj.","d":"connected with punishing people who break rules","c":"紀律的；懲戒的","s":"The school took disciplinary action against the two boys who painted on the walls of the gym last weekend.","t":"學校對上週末在體育館牆上塗鴉的兩個男生採取了懲戒行動。","h":1},{"w":"disciplined","p":"adj.","d":"able to control your behavior and follow rules","c":"守紀律的；自律的","s":"The disciplined athlete gets up at five every morning to train, even when it is cold and dark outside.","t":"這位自律的運動員每天早上五點起床訓練，即使外面又冷又暗。"},{"w":"disciplinary committee","p":"n.phr.","d":"a group of people who decide how to punish rule-breakers","c":"紀律委員會","s":"The case was sent to the disciplinary committee, which will decide whether the player should be banned from the next three games.","t":"這個案件被送交紀律委員會，委員會將決定該球員是否應被禁賽接下來的三場比賽。"},{"w":"disclosure","p":"n.","d":"the act of making secret information known","c":"揭露；公開","s":"The disclosure of the company's secret report shocked customers, who learned that their personal data had been sold.","t":"公司秘密報告的揭露讓顧客震驚，他們得知自己的個人資料已被出售。","h":1},{"w":"disclose","p":"v.","d":"to tell people something that was secret","c":"揭露；透露","s":"The company refused to disclose how many users were affected by the attack until the police finished their investigation.","t":"在警方完成調查之前，這家公司拒絕透露有多少用戶受到這次攻擊的影響。"},{"w":"undisclosed","p":"adj.","d":"not made known to the public","c":"未公開的","s":"The singer was paid an undisclosed amount of money to perform at the private party on the island.","t":"這位歌手收了一筆未公開的金額，到島上的私人派對演出。"},{"w":"full disclosure","p":"n.phr.","d":"giving all the facts, hiding nothing","c":"完全公開；充分揭露","s":"The new law requires full disclosure of all the ingredients in food products, including the chemicals used to keep them fresh.","t":"新法律要求完全公開食品中的所有成分，包括用來保鮮的化學物質。"},{"w":"discomfort","p":"n.","d":"a feeling of slight pain or of being uneasy","c":"不適；不安","s":"You may feel some discomfort in your arm for a day after the injection, but it should go away by itself.","t":"打針後一天內你的手臂可能會有些不適，但它應該會自己消失。","h":1},{"w":"comfort","p":"n.","d":"a pleasant feeling of being relaxed and free from pain or worry","c":"舒適；安慰","s":"After a hard day at work, my mother finds comfort in a hot bath and a cup of tea by the window.","t":"辛苦工作一天後，我媽媽在熱水澡和窗邊的一杯茶中找到慰藉。"},{"w":"comfortable","p":"adj.","d":"making you feel relaxed and free from pain","c":"舒適的；舒服的","s":"These new shoes are so comfortable that I walked around the city for six hours without any pain.","t":"這雙新鞋非常舒服，我在城裡走了六個小時都不會痛。"},{"w":"uncomfortable","p":"adj.","d":"not pleasant to wear, sit in, or be in; feeling uneasy","c":"不舒服的；不自在的","s":"I felt uncomfortable at the party because I did not know anyone and everybody was talking about people I had never met.","t":"我在派對上覺得很不自在，因為我誰都不認識，而大家都在談論我從沒見過的人。"},{"w":"discreet","p":"adj.","d":"careful not to say or do things that might embarrass someone or give away a secret","c":"謹慎的；慎重的；不張揚的","s":"Please be discreet about my birthday plans, because I want the party to be a surprise for my sister.","t":"關於我的生日計畫請保密謹慎一點，因為我希望這個派對能給我妹妹一個驚喜。","h":1},{"w":"discreetly","p":"adv.","d":"in a careful and quiet way, without attracting attention","c":"謹慎地；不張揚地","s":"The waiter discreetly told the man that his credit card had been refused, so that nobody else at the table could hear.","t":"服務生低調地告訴那位先生他的信用卡被拒刷了，這樣桌上其他人都聽不到。"},{"w":"discretion","p":"n.","d":"the freedom to decide what to do; care in what you say and do","c":"自行決定權；謹慎","s":"Teachers may use their own discretion when deciding whether a late homework can still receive full marks.","t":"老師在決定遲交的作業是否還能拿滿分時，可以自行斟酌。"},{"w":"indiscreet","p":"adj.","d":"saying or doing things you should keep private","c":"不謹慎的；輕率的","s":"It was indiscreet of him to talk about his friend's family problems in front of the whole class.","t":"他在全班面前談論朋友的家庭問題，實在是太輕率了。"},{"w":"disgrace","p":"n.","d":"something that is so bad that it makes people ashamed; loss of respect","c":"恥辱；丟臉的事","s":"It is a disgrace that the beautiful old park is now full of trash, and the city has done nothing about it.","t":"那座美麗的老公園現在滿是垃圾真是一種恥辱，而市政府卻什麼也沒做。","h":1},{"w":"disgrace","p":"v.","d":"to make people lose respect for you or your group","c":"使丟臉；使蒙羞","s":"The player was sent home for cheating, and he knew he had disgraced himself and his whole team.","t":"那位球員因作弊被遣送回家，他知道自己讓自己和整支球隊蒙羞了。","a":"disgraced"},{"w":"disgraceful","p":"adj.","d":"very bad and making people feel ashamed","c":"可恥的；丟臉的","s":"The fans' disgraceful behavior after the game, throwing bottles onto the field, was shown on the news all week.","t":"球迷賽後把瓶子丟進場內的可恥行為，整個星期都在新聞上播出。"},{"w":"in disgrace","p":"phr.","d":"having lost people's respect because of something bad you did","c":"丟臉地；失寵地","s":"The minister left office in disgrace after reporters proved that he had lied about his spending.","t":"在記者證明他謊報開支之後，這位部長狼狽地下台了。"},{"w":"dismay","p":"n.","d":"a feeling of shock and sadness when something bad happens","c":"沮喪；驚愕","s":"To the dismay of the fans, the concert was canceled only an hour before it was supposed to begin.","t":"令粉絲沮喪的是，演唱會在原定開始前一小時才宣布取消。","h":1},{"w":"dismay","p":"v.","d":"to make someone feel shocked and sad","c":"使沮喪；使驚愕","s":"The poor test results dismayed the teacher, who had spent weeks preparing the class for the exam.","t":"糟糕的考試成績讓老師很沮喪，她花了好幾週為全班準備這次考試。","a":"dismayed"},{"w":"dismayed","p":"adj.","d":"feeling shocked and sad","c":"沮喪的；驚愕的","s":"We were dismayed to find that the museum was closed on Mondays, since we had traveled two hours to see it.","t":"我們發現博物館星期一休館時非常沮喪，因為我們花了兩個小時的車程來參觀。"},{"w":"to one's dismay","p":"phr.","d":"used to say that something made you feel upset","c":"令某人沮喪的是","s":"To my dismay, the only cake left at the bakery was the one with raisins, which I really cannot stand.","t":"令我沮喪的是，麵包店裡只剩下葡萄乾蛋糕，而那是我最受不了的。","a":"To my dismay"},{"w":"dispensable","p":"adj.","d":"not necessary; able to be done without","c":"可有可無的；非必要的","s":"In a small company, no worker is dispensable; when one person is sick, everyone else has to do extra work.","t":"在小公司裡，沒有一個員工是可有可無的；當有人生病時，其他人都得多做額外的工作。","h":1},{"w":"dispense","p":"v.","d":"to give out something to people; to prepare and give medicine","c":"分配；發放；配藥","s":"The machine in the hallway can dispense hot drinks, snacks, and even umbrellas to students on rainy days.","t":"走廊上的那台機器可以在下雨天提供熱飲、點心，甚至雨傘給學生。","h":1},{"w":"indispensable","p":"adj.","d":"so important that you cannot do without it","c":"不可或缺的","s":"A smartphone has become indispensable for many people, who use it to pay, to travel, and to talk to friends.","t":"智慧型手機對許多人來說已經變得不可或缺，他們用它付款、旅行和跟朋友聊天。"},{"w":"dispense with","p":"v.phr.","d":"to stop using or doing something because it is not needed","c":"省去；免除","s":"Let us dispense with the long introductions and start the meeting, because everyone here already knows each other.","t":"我們省去冗長的自我介紹，直接開會吧，因為在場的每個人都已經互相認識了。"},{"w":"dispenser","p":"n.","d":"a machine or container that gives out a product","c":"自動給料機；給皂機；販賣機","s":"There is a soap dispenser next to every sink in the school bathrooms, so there is no excuse for dirty hands.","t":"學校廁所每個洗手台旁邊都有一個給皂機，所以沒有藉口不洗手。"},{"w":"disposable","p":"adj.","d":"made to be used once or a few times and then thrown away","c":"用完即丟的；一次性的","s":"Many coffee shops now charge extra for disposable cups, so bring your own bottle if you want to save money.","t":"現在很多咖啡店對一次性杯子額外收費，所以如果你想省錢就自己帶瓶子。","h":1},{"w":"disposal","p":"n.","d":"the act of getting rid of something","c":"處理；丟棄","s":"Proper disposal of old batteries is important because the chemicals inside them can poison the soil and water.","t":"妥善處理舊電池很重要，因為裡面的化學物質會污染土壤和水。","h":1},{"w":"dispose","p":"v.","d":"to get rid of something you do not want (used with of)","c":"處理；丟掉","s":"Please dispose of your lunch boxes in the correct bin, because paper and plastic are collected separately.","t":"請把你的便當盒丟進正確的垃圾桶，因為紙類和塑膠是分開回收的。","h":1},{"w":"dispose of","p":"v.phr.","d":"to throw away or get rid of something","c":"處理掉；丟棄","s":"The hotel had to dispose of hundreds of old mattresses when it replaced all the beds last summer.","t":"去年夏天飯店更換所有床鋪時，必須處理掉數百張舊床墊。"},{"w":"at one's disposal","p":"phr.","d":"available for someone to use whenever they want","c":"可供某人隨意使用","s":"During the project, the students had the computer lab at their disposal every afternoon after four o'clock.","t":"在這個專題期間，學生們每天下午四點以後都可以隨意使用電腦教室。","a":"at their disposal"},{"w":"dissent","p":"n.","d":"strong disagreement with an official opinion or decision","c":"異議；反對","s":"The new rule passed without any dissent, because every member of the club agreed that the change was necessary.","t":"新規定在沒有任何異議的情況下通過了，因為社團每位成員都同意這項改變是必要的。","h":1},{"w":"dissent","p":"v.","d":"to say that you disagree with an official opinion","c":"持異議；不同意","s":"Two judges chose to dissent from the decision, saying that the evidence against the man was too weak.","t":"兩位法官選擇對這項判決提出異議，說對那名男子不利的證據太薄弱。"},{"w":"dissenting","p":"adj.","d":"disagreeing with the official or majority view","c":"持異議的；反對的","s":"The only dissenting voice at the meeting came from Mr. Lin, who thought the new uniform was too expensive.","t":"會議上唯一反對的聲音來自林先生，他認為新制服太貴了。"},{"w":"distraction","p":"n.","d":"something that takes your attention away from what you are doing","c":"使人分心的事物","s":"Social media is a big distraction for students, so I turn off my phone when I need to finish an essay.","t":"社群媒體對學生來說是很大的干擾，所以當我需要完成作文時我會把手機關掉。","h":1},{"w":"distract","p":"v.","d":"to take someone's attention away from what they are doing","c":"使分心","s":"Please do not distract the driver by talking to him while he is turning onto the busy highway.","t":"請不要在司機轉上繁忙的高速公路時跟他說話，以免讓他分心。"},{"w":"distracted","p":"adj.","d":"not able to pay attention because you are thinking about something else","c":"分心的；心不在焉的","s":"The distracted student kept looking out of the window and did not hear the teacher call his name twice.","t":"那個心不在焉的學生一直望著窗外，沒聽到老師叫了他兩次名字。"},{"w":"distracting","p":"adj.","d":"taking your attention away from what you are doing","c":"令人分心的","s":"The music from the next apartment is so distracting that I cannot concentrate on my homework at all.","t":"隔壁公寓傳來的音樂太令人分心了，我完全無法專心寫作業。"},{"w":"distress","p":"n.","d":"great pain, sadness, or worry; a situation of danger","c":"痛苦；悲痛；困境","s":"The lost child was in great distress until a kind police officer helped her find her parents at the station.","t":"那個走失的孩子非常痛苦不安，直到一位好心的警察幫她在車站找到父母。","h":1},{"w":"distress","p":"v.","d":"to make someone feel very upset","c":"使痛苦；使悲痛","s":"The news of the accident distressed the whole village, and people gathered at the temple to pray for the families.","t":"這起意外的消息讓整個村子都很悲痛，人們聚集在廟裡為那些家庭祈禱。","a":"distressed"},{"w":"distressed","p":"adj.","d":"very upset or worried","c":"痛苦的；憂慮的","s":"The distressed owner put up posters all over the neighborhood, hoping someone had seen her lost cat.","t":"那位焦急的主人在整個社區貼滿海報，希望有人看到她走失的貓。"},{"w":"distressing","p":"adj.","d":"making you feel very upset","c":"令人痛苦的；令人難過的","s":"It was distressing to see so many animals without homes, so my sister decided to volunteer at the shelter.","t":"看到這麼多無家可歸的動物令人難過，所以我姊姊決定去收容所當志工。"},{"w":"in distress","p":"phr.","d":"in great danger or trouble and needing help","c":"處於危難中；處於困境","s":"The coast guard received a call from a fishing boat in distress and sent a helicopter to rescue the crew.","t":"海巡隊接到一艘遇難漁船的求救電話，派出直升機去救援船員。"},{"w":"disturbance","p":"n.","d":"something that interrupts or upsets people; noisy or violent behavior","c":"騷擾；干擾；騷動","s":"The neighbors called the police about the disturbance because the party upstairs was still going at three in the morning.","t":"鄰居打電話報警投訴這場騷擾，因為樓上的派對凌晨三點還在進行。","h":1},{"w":"disturb","p":"v.","d":"to interrupt someone or stop them from continuing what they are doing","c":"打擾；妨礙","s":"Please do not disturb your father while he is on the phone with his boss about the important contract.","t":"你爸爸正在和老闆講那份重要合約的電話，請不要打擾他。"},{"w":"disturbing","p":"adj.","d":"making you feel worried or upset","c":"令人不安的","s":"The movie had several disturbing scenes, so the theater warned that it was not suitable for young children.","t":"這部電影有幾個令人不安的場景，所以電影院警告它不適合幼童觀看。"},{"w":"disturbed","p":"adj.","d":"worried or upset; interrupted","c":"不安的；受干擾的","s":"She was deeply disturbed by the strange phone calls, so she changed her number the next day.","t":"她被那些奇怪的電話弄得非常不安，所以隔天就換了電話號碼。"},{"w":"diversify","p":"v.","d":"to start doing or producing a wider range of things","c":"使多樣化；多角化經營","s":"The farmer decided to diversify his crops, growing fruit and vegetables instead of only rice, to protect himself from bad prices.","t":"這位農夫決定讓作物多樣化，除了稻米也種水果和蔬菜，以免受到價格不好的影響。","h":1},{"w":"diverse","p":"adj.","d":"very different from each other; of many different kinds","c":"多樣的；各式各樣的","s":"Taipei is a diverse city where you can hear many languages and taste food from all over the world in one street.","t":"台北是一座多元的城市，在同一條街上你可以聽到多種語言，也能嚐到來自世界各地的食物。"},{"w":"diversity","p":"n.","d":"the fact of including many different kinds of people or things","c":"多樣性；多元","s":"The school celebrates cultural diversity every spring with a fair where students share food and music from their families' home countries.","t":"學校每年春天舉辦園遊會慶祝文化多元，學生們分享來自家族母國的食物和音樂。"},{"w":"diversification","p":"n.","d":"the process of starting to do or produce a wider range of things","c":"多樣化；多角化","s":"The company's diversification into electric bikes helped it survive when fewer people were buying cars.","t":"這家公司多角化經營跨入電動腳踏車，幫助它在買車的人變少時存活下來。"},{"w":"diversion","p":"n.","d":"a change in the direction that traffic or something else usually takes","c":"改道；轉移；分流","s":"The police set up a diversion around the accident, so we had to drive through the small streets to reach the school.","t":"警方在事故現場周圍設了改道路線，所以我們得開過小巷才能到學校。","h":1},{"w":"divert","p":"v.","d":"to make something go in a different direction; to turn attention away","c":"使轉向；使改道；轉移","s":"The city plans to divert traffic away from the night market on weekends so that visitors can walk safely.","t":"市政府計畫在週末把車流引導離開夜市，讓遊客可以安全地步行。","h":1},{"w":"divert sb's attention from","p":"v.phr.","d":"to make someone stop looking at or thinking about something","c":"轉移某人對…的注意力","s":"The clever thief dropped a bag of coins to divert the guards' attention from the door of the vault.","t":"聰明的小偷丟下一袋硬幣，好轉移警衛對金庫門的注意力。","a":"divert the guards' attention from"},{"w":"diversion","p":"n.","d":"an activity you do for pleasure","c":"消遣；娛樂","s":"Playing the guitar is a pleasant diversion after a long day of studying, and it helps me forget my worries.","t":"讀了一整天書之後，彈吉他是很愉快的消遣，它幫我忘掉煩惱。"},{"w":"dividend","p":"n.","d":"money that a company pays to the people who own its shares","c":"股利；紅利","s":"The company paid a dividend of five dollars per share this year, so my grandfather received a nice check in June.","t":"這家公司今年每股發放五美元的股利，所以我爺爺六月收到了一張不錯的支票。","h":1},{"w":"divide","p":"v.","d":"to separate into parts; to share something between people","c":"分開；分配；除","s":"Let us divide the class into four teams so that everyone gets a chance to speak during the game.","t":"我們把全班分成四隊，這樣每個人在遊戲中都有機會發言。"},{"w":"division","p":"n.","d":"the act of separating into parts; a part of an organization; dividing numbers","c":"分割；部門；除法","s":"My little brother is learning division in math class this week, and he keeps asking me to check his answers.","t":"我弟弟這週在數學課上學除法，他一直要我幫他檢查答案。"},{"w":"pay dividends","p":"v.phr.","d":"to bring good results later","c":"帶來好處；產生回報","s":"Learning to type fast in junior high paid dividends later, when I had to write long reports at university.","t":"國中時學會快速打字，後來在大學必須寫長篇報告時帶來了回報。","a":"paid dividends"}]},{"unit":12,"theme":"doom – emigration","cards":[{"w":"doom","p":"n.","d":"death, destruction, or a terrible end that cannot be avoided","c":"厄運；毀滅；劫數","s":"In the old story, a dark cloud hung over the castle as a sign of the doom that was coming to the king.","t":"在那個古老的故事裡，一朵烏雲籠罩著城堡，預示著國王即將面臨的厄運。","h":1},{"w":"doom","p":"v.","d":"to make something certain to fail or be destroyed","c":"注定（失敗）；使在劫難逃","s":"The decision to cut the team's budget in half seemed to doom the project from the very start.","t":"把團隊預算砍半的決定，似乎從一開始就注定了這個專案的失敗。"},{"w":"be doomed to","p":"v.phr.","d":"to be certain to fail or suffer","c":"注定會…","s":"Without enough rain this spring, the farmers' crops are doomed to fail, no matter how hard everyone works.","t":"今年春天雨水不足，不管大家多努力，農民的作物都注定會歉收。","a":"are doomed to"},{"w":"doomed","p":"adj.","d":"certain to fail or be destroyed","c":"注定失敗的；在劫難逃的","s":"Everyone could see that the doomed plan would never work, but the manager refused to listen to any advice.","t":"每個人都看得出這個注定失敗的計畫行不通，但經理拒絕聽任何建議。"},{"w":"doomsday","p":"n.","d":"the end of the world","c":"世界末日","s":"Some people believed the year 2000 would bring doomsday, so they stored food and water in their basements.","t":"有些人相信 2000 年會帶來世界末日，所以他們在地下室儲存了食物和水。"},{"w":"dormitory","p":"n.","d":"a building where students live at a school or university","c":"宿舍","s":"First-year students must live in the dormitory on campus, where two people share a small room and a bathroom.","t":"一年級學生必須住在校內的宿舍，兩個人共用一間小房間和一間浴室。","h":1},{"w":"dorm","p":"n.","d":"a short, informal word for dormitory","c":"宿舍（口語）","s":"My roommate in the dorm snores so loudly that I have started wearing earplugs to get some sleep.","t":"我宿舍的室友打呼聲太大，我已經開始戴耳塞才能睡著。"},{"w":"dorm room","p":"n.phr.","d":"a bedroom in a dormitory","c":"宿舍房間","s":"Our dorm room is tiny, but we decorated it with posters and plants to make it feel like home.","t":"我們的宿舍房間很小，但我們用海報和植物裝飾它，讓它有家的感覺。"},{"w":"dormant","p":"adj.","d":"not active now but able to become active later","c":"休眠的；蟄伏的","s":"The volcano has been dormant for three hundred years, but scientists still check it carefully every month.","t":"這座火山已經休眠三百年了，但科學家仍然每個月仔細檢查它。"},{"w":"downward","p":"adj.","d":"moving or pointing toward a lower place or level","c":"向下的；下降的","s":"The company's sales have been on a downward trend for two years, so the owners are worried about the future.","t":"這家公司的銷售量兩年來一直呈下降趨勢，所以老闆們很擔心未來。","h":1},{"w":"downward","p":"adv.","d":"toward a lower place or level","c":"向下地","s":"Water always flows downward, which is why the farmers built their fields in steps on the side of the hill.","t":"水總是往下流，這就是為什麼農民把田地建成階梯狀在山坡上。"},{"w":"downwards","p":"adv.","d":"toward a lower place (another spelling of downward)","c":"向下地","s":"The path leads downwards through the forest to a quiet beach that very few tourists know about.","t":"這條小路穿過森林向下通往一處很少遊客知道的安靜海灘。"},{"w":"upward","p":"adj.","d":"moving or pointing toward a higher place or level","c":"向上的；上升的","s":"Prices for apartments in the city have been moving in an upward direction, making it hard for young people to buy a home.","t":"城裡的公寓價格一直朝上升的方向走，讓年輕人很難買房子。"},{"w":"upwards","p":"adv.","d":"toward a higher place or level","c":"向上地","s":"The red balloon floated upwards until it was only a tiny dot high above the park.","t":"紅色氣球向上飄，直到變成公園上空高處的一個小點。"},{"w":"doze","p":"v.","d":"to sleep lightly for a short time","c":"打瞌睡；小睡","s":"Grandpa likes to doze in his chair after lunch, and he gets angry if anyone says he was sleeping.","t":"爺爺喜歡午餐後在椅子上打瞌睡，如果有人說他睡著了他會生氣。","h":1},{"w":"doze off","p":"v.phr.","d":"to fall asleep without meaning to","c":"打起盹來；不知不覺睡著","s":"I started to doze off during the long movie, and my friend had to poke me when the best part came.","t":"看那部長電影時我開始打起盹來，最精彩的部分來的時候朋友還得戳我一下。"},{"w":"doze","p":"n.","d":"a short, light sleep","c":"小睡；瞌睡","s":"A short doze on the train after work left me feeling fresh enough to cook dinner for the family.","t":"下班後在火車上小睡一下，讓我有精神回家幫全家煮晚餐。"},{"w":"drowsy","p":"adj.","d":"tired and almost asleep","c":"昏昏欲睡的","s":"This cold medicine can make you drowsy, so you should not drive or ride a scooter after taking it.","t":"這種感冒藥會讓你昏昏欲睡，所以吃了之後不應該開車或騎機車。"},{"w":"drastic","p":"adj.","d":"extreme and sudden; having a very big effect","c":"激烈的；嚴厲的；大幅的","s":"The doctor told him to make drastic changes to his diet, or his heart problems would only get worse.","t":"醫生告訴他必須對飲食做大幅的改變，否則他的心臟問題只會更糟。","h":1},{"w":"drastically","p":"adv.","d":"in an extreme or sudden way","c":"大幅地；激烈地","s":"The price of eggs rose drastically last month, so my mother started buying them at a farm outside town.","t":"上個月蛋價大幅上漲，所以我媽媽開始到鎮外的農場買蛋。"},{"w":"drastic measures","p":"n.phr.","d":"extreme actions taken to solve a serious problem","c":"激烈的手段；斷然措施","s":"The school took drastic measures to stop cheating, including cameras in every classroom and new seating plans.","t":"學校採取了激烈的手段來杜絕作弊，包括每間教室裝攝影機和新的座位安排。"},{"w":"draught","p":"n.","d":"a current of cold air blowing through a room (British spelling of draft)","c":"穿堂風；氣流（英式拼法）","s":"Close the window, please; there is a cold draught blowing across the room, and Grandma is starting to shiver.","t":"請把窗戶關上；有一股冷風吹過房間，奶奶開始發抖了。","h":1},{"w":"draft","p":"n.","d":"an early version of a piece of writing; a current of cold air (American spelling)","c":"草稿；氣流（美式拼法）","s":"I finished the first draft of my essay last night, but I still need to fix the ending before Friday.","t":"我昨晚完成了作文的初稿，但星期五之前還得修改結尾。"},{"w":"draft","p":"v.","d":"to write the first version of something","c":"起草；擬定","s":"The committee will draft a new set of rules for the library and show them to the students next week.","t":"委員會將為圖書館起草一套新規定，並在下週向學生說明。"},{"w":"draughty","p":"adj.","d":"having cold air blowing through it","c":"有穿堂風的；通風漏風的","s":"The old classroom is so draughty in winter that students wear their coats and scarves during lessons.","t":"這間舊教室冬天漏風得很厲害，學生上課時都穿著外套和圍巾。"},{"w":"dresser","p":"n.","d":"a piece of furniture with drawers for clothes, often with a mirror","c":"梳妝台；五斗櫃","s":"I keep my socks in the top drawer of the dresser, and my sweaters go in the two drawers below it.","t":"我把襪子放在五斗櫃最上面的抽屜，毛衣放在下面兩個抽屜裡。","h":1},{"w":"dressing","p":"n.","d":"a sauce for salad","c":"沙拉醬","s":"Put a little oil and vinegar on the salad, because the bottled dressing from the store has too much sugar.","t":"在沙拉上加一點油和醋就好，因為商店賣的瓶裝沙拉醬糖太多了。","h":1},{"w":"dressing","p":"n.","d":"a covering put on a wound to protect it","c":"敷料；包紮","s":"The nurse changed the dressing on my cut every morning until the wound was completely closed.","t":"護理師每天早上幫我換傷口上的敷料，直到傷口完全癒合。"},{"w":"dress","p":"v.","d":"to put clothes on yourself or someone else","c":"穿衣；給…穿衣","s":"It takes my little sister twenty minutes to dress herself in the morning because she changes her mind about every shirt.","t":"我妹妹早上要花二十分鐘穿衣服，因為她每件上衣都會改變主意。"},{"w":"dress up","p":"v.phr.","d":"to wear special or formal clothes; to wear a costume","c":"盛裝打扮；裝扮成","s":"The children love to dress up as superheroes on Halloween and knock on every door in the neighborhood.","t":"孩子們喜歡在萬聖節裝扮成超級英雄，去敲社區裡的每一扇門。"},{"w":"dressing room","p":"n.phr.","d":"a room where actors or players change their clothes","c":"更衣室；化妝室","s":"The actors waited in the dressing room behind the stage, fixing their makeup and practicing their lines.","t":"演員們在舞台後方的更衣室等候，整理妝容並練習台詞。"},{"w":"dual","p":"adj.","d":"having two parts or two purposes","c":"雙重的；雙的","s":"The new building has a dual purpose: it is a library during the day and a community center at night.","t":"這棟新建築有雙重用途：白天是圖書館，晚上是社區活動中心。","h":1},{"w":"dual citizenship","p":"n.phr.","d":"being a citizen of two countries at the same time","c":"雙重國籍","s":"My cousin holds dual citizenship, so she can live and work in both Taiwan and Canada without a visa.","t":"我表姊擁有雙重國籍，所以她不需要簽證就能在台灣和加拿大兩地生活和工作。"},{"w":"duo","p":"n.","d":"two people who perform or work together","c":"二人組；雙人組合","s":"The comedy duo became famous on the Internet, and now they perform in theaters all over Asia.","t":"這個喜劇二人組在網路上成名，現在他們在全亞洲的劇院演出。"},{"w":"duet","p":"n.","d":"a piece of music sung or played by two people","c":"二重唱；二重奏","s":"The two singers performed a beautiful duet at the end of the concert, and the audience asked for more.","t":"兩位歌手在演唱會最後表演了一首美妙的二重唱，觀眾還要求安可。"},{"w":"dubious","p":"adj.","d":"probably not honest or true; not sure about something","c":"可疑的；半信半疑的","s":"The salesman made some dubious claims about the medicine, saying it could cure almost every illness in a week.","t":"那位推銷員對這種藥做了一些可疑的宣稱，說它一週內幾乎能治好所有的病。","h":1},{"w":"be dubious about","p":"v.phr.","d":"to have doubts about something","c":"對…懷疑；對…不太有把握","s":"I was dubious about the plan to climb the mountain in one day, because none of us had done any training.","t":"我對一天內爬完那座山的計畫很懷疑，因為我們沒有人做過任何訓練。","a":"was dubious about"},{"w":"doubt","p":"n.","d":"a feeling of not being sure about something","c":"懷疑；疑問","s":"There is no doubt that she is the best player on the team; she scored in every game this season.","t":"毫無疑問她是隊上最好的球員；她這一季每場比賽都有得分。"},{"w":"doubtful","p":"adj.","d":"not likely; not sure","c":"懷疑的；不太可能的","s":"It is doubtful that the package will arrive before the weekend, because the post office is very busy in December.","t":"包裹不太可能在週末前送達，因為郵局十二月非常忙碌。"},{"w":"duration","p":"n.","d":"the length of time that something lasts","c":"持續時間；期間","s":"Please keep your phones off for the duration of the concert, which should be about two hours including the break.","t":"演唱會期間請保持手機關機，整場包含中場休息大約兩小時。","h":1},{"w":"during","p":"prep.","d":"through the whole of a period of time; at some point in a period","c":"在…期間","s":"Nobody is allowed to leave the room during the test, so go to the bathroom before it starts.","t":"考試期間任何人都不准離開教室，所以開始前先去上廁所。"},{"w":"durable","p":"adj.","d":"staying in good condition for a long time","c":"耐用的；持久的","s":"These hiking boots are expensive, but they are so durable that my father has worn his pair for ten years.","t":"這種登山鞋很貴，但非常耐穿，我爸爸那雙已經穿了十年。"},{"w":"for the duration","p":"phr.","d":"for the whole time that something lasts","c":"在整段期間","s":"The hotel pool is closed for repairs, and sadly it will stay closed for the duration of our stay.","t":"飯店泳池因維修關閉，可惜在我們住宿的整段期間它都會關著。"},{"w":"dusk","p":"n.","d":"the time in the evening when it starts to get dark","c":"黃昏；薄暮","s":"The park closes at dusk, so we should start walking back to the gate as soon as the sun gets low.","t":"公園在黃昏時關閉，所以太陽一低下來我們就該開始走回大門。","h":1},{"w":"at dusk","p":"phr.","d":"when the sun has just gone down","c":"在黃昏時","s":"The bats come out of the cave at dusk every evening, and hundreds of tourists wait outside to watch them.","t":"蝙蝠每天傍晚黃昏時飛出洞穴，數百名遊客在外面等著看牠們。"},{"w":"dawn","p":"n.","d":"the time in the morning when light first appears","c":"黎明；破曉","s":"We got up before dawn to climb the hill and watch the sun rise slowly over the sea.","t":"我們在黎明前起床爬上山丘，看太陽從海面上慢慢升起。"},{"w":"from dawn to dusk","p":"phr.","d":"from early morning until evening; all day long","c":"從早到晚","s":"During the harvest, the farmers work from dawn to dusk, stopping only for a quick lunch under the trees.","t":"收割期間，農民們從早工作到晚，只在樹下快速吃個午餐就繼續。"},{"w":"dwarf","p":"n.","d":"a very small person in stories; a person or thing that is much smaller than usual","c":"矮人；侏儒","s":"In the fairy tale, a friendly dwarf helps the lost princess find her way out of the dark forest.","t":"在童話裡，一個友善的矮人幫助迷路的公主找到走出黑暗森林的路。","h":1},{"w":"dwarf","p":"v.","d":"to make something seem small by comparison","c":"使相形見絀；使顯得矮小","s":"The new tower will dwarf every other building in the city, standing almost twice as tall as the old station.","t":"新的高塔將讓城裡其他所有建築相形見絀，它幾乎是舊車站的兩倍高。"},{"w":"dwarf","p":"adj.","d":"of a type that is much smaller than usual","c":"矮小品種的","s":"My grandmother grows dwarf fruit trees on her balcony because they stay small and still give sweet oranges.","t":"我奶奶在陽台上種矮種果樹，因為它們長不高卻還是能結出甜橘子。"},{"w":"be dwarfed by","p":"v.phr.","d":"to look very small next to something much bigger","c":"被…比得相形見絀","s":"The little fishing boats were dwarfed by the huge cruise ship that entered the harbor this morning.","t":"小漁船被今天早上進港的巨大郵輪比得非常渺小。","a":"were dwarfed by"},{"w":"dwell, dwelt, dwelt","p":"v.","d":"to live in a place (formal or literary)","c":"居住","s":"Long ago, people used to dwell in caves, where they were safe from wild animals and the cold wind.","t":"很久以前，人們住在洞穴裡，在那裡可以躲避野獸和寒風。","a":"dwell","h":1},{"w":"dwelling","p":"n.","d":"a house or place where someone lives (formal)","c":"住所；住處","s":"The old stone dwelling on the hill has no electricity, but a family of four still lives there happily.","t":"山丘上那間古老的石造住所沒有電，但一家四口仍然快樂地住在那裡。","h":1},{"w":"dwell on","p":"v.phr.","d":"to keep thinking or talking about something, especially something bad","c":"老是想著；一直談論","s":"Try not to dwell on your mistakes in the last game; think about what you can do better next time.","t":"試著不要一直想著上一場比賽的失誤；想想下次可以怎麼做得更好。"},{"w":"dweller","p":"n.","d":"a person or animal that lives in a particular kind of place","c":"居住者；居民","s":"City dwellers often dream of a quiet life in the countryside, until they try living without convenience stores.","t":"都市居民常常夢想鄉下的寧靜生活，直到他們試著過沒有便利商店的日子。","a":"dwellers"},{"w":"eccentric","p":"adj.","d":"behaving in a strange or unusual way","c":"古怪的；異於常人的","s":"Our eccentric neighbor wears a winter coat in July and talks to his plants every morning, but he is very kind.","t":"我們古怪的鄰居七月穿冬天的大衣，每天早上還跟他的植物說話，但他人很好。","h":1},{"w":"eccentric","p":"n.","d":"a person who behaves in a strange way","c":"古怪的人；怪人","s":"The old painter was known as an eccentric who lived alone with twenty cats and never answered the door.","t":"這位老畫家是出了名的怪人，他和二十隻貓獨居，而且從不應門。"},{"w":"eccentricity","p":"n.","d":"strange or unusual behavior; a strange habit","c":"古怪；怪癖","s":"Wearing two different socks to work every day is just one of my uncle's many little eccentricities.","t":"每天穿兩隻不一樣的襪子上班，只是我叔叔許多小怪癖中的一個。","a":"eccentricities"},{"w":"eclipse","p":"n.","d":"a time when the sun or moon is hidden by the moon or the Earth","c":"日蝕；月蝕","s":"Thousands of people gathered on the beach to watch the solar eclipse safely through special dark glasses.","t":"數千人聚集在海灘上，透過特殊的深色眼鏡安全地觀看日蝕。","h":1},{"w":"lunar eclipse","p":"n.phr.","d":"a time when the Earth's shadow hides the moon","c":"月蝕","s":"During a lunar eclipse, the moon slowly turns a deep red color, which some people in the past thought was a bad sign.","t":"月蝕時，月亮會慢慢變成深紅色，過去有些人認為這是不祥之兆。"},{"w":"eclipse","p":"v.","d":"to become more important or successful than someone else","c":"使黯然失色；超越","s":"The young singer's success soon began to eclipse that of her famous older brother, who had taught her everything.","t":"這位年輕歌手的成功很快就蓋過了教她一切的知名哥哥。"},{"w":"total eclipse","p":"n.phr.","d":"a time when the sun or moon is completely hidden","c":"全蝕","s":"A total eclipse of the sun will be seen in Taiwan next year, and schools are already planning special lessons about it.","t":"明年台灣將可看到日全蝕，學校已經在規劃相關的特別課程。"},{"w":"edible","p":"adj.","d":"safe to eat","c":"可食用的","s":"Not every mushroom in the forest is edible, so never eat one unless an expert tells you it is safe.","t":"森林裡不是每一種蘑菇都可以吃，所以除非專家告訴你安全，否則絕對不要吃。","h":1},{"w":"inedible","p":"adj.","d":"not safe or not good enough to eat","c":"不能吃的","s":"The cake was so burnt that it was completely inedible, and we had to order pizza for the party instead.","t":"蛋糕烤焦到完全不能吃，我們只好改訂披薩來開派對。"},{"w":"edible flowers","p":"n.phr.","d":"flowers that can be safely eaten","c":"可食用花卉","s":"The restaurant decorates its salads with edible flowers that are grown without chemicals in its own garden.","t":"這家餐廳用自家花園裡不用化學藥劑栽種的可食用花卉來裝飾沙拉。"},{"w":"editorial","p":"n.","d":"an article in a newspaper that gives the editor's opinion","c":"社論","s":"The newspaper's editorial this morning argued that the city should build more bike lanes instead of parking lots.","t":"今天早上報紙的社論主張市政府應該多建自行車道，而不是停車場。","h":1},{"w":"editorial","p":"adj.","d":"connected with editing or editors","c":"編輯的","s":"She works for a publisher and makes editorial decisions about which new novels the company should print.","t":"她在出版社工作，負責做編輯決策，決定公司該出版哪些新小說。"},{"w":"edit","p":"v.","d":"to correct and improve a piece of writing or a film","c":"編輯；修改","s":"Please edit your essay carefully before you hand it in, because small spelling mistakes can lose you points.","t":"交作文之前請仔細修改，因為小小的拼字錯誤可能會讓你失分。"},{"w":"editor","p":"n.","d":"a person who corrects and prepares writing for a newspaper, book, or magazine","c":"編輯","s":"The editor of the school magazine asked me to write an article about the basketball team's trip to Japan.","t":"校刊的編輯請我寫一篇關於籃球隊日本之旅的文章。"},{"w":"edition","p":"n.","d":"a particular version of a book or newspaper","c":"版本；版次","s":"The second edition of the textbook has new pictures and exercises, so the old copies can no longer be used in class.","t":"課本的第二版有新的圖片和練習題，所以舊版本不能再在課堂上使用了。"},{"w":"electrician","p":"n.","d":"a person whose job is to fix or put in electrical wires and equipment","c":"電工；電氣技師","s":"We called an electrician to fix the broken light switch, because it is dangerous to touch wires if you are not trained.","t":"我們請了電工來修壞掉的電燈開關，因為沒受過訓練去碰電線很危險。","h":1},{"w":"electric","p":"adj.","d":"worked by electricity; producing electricity","c":"電的；電動的","s":"My father bought an electric scooter last month because it is quiet and much cheaper to run than a gasoline one.","t":"我爸爸上個月買了一輛電動機車，因為它很安靜，而且比汽油機車便宜很多。"},{"w":"electricity","p":"n.","d":"the form of energy that powers lights and machines","c":"電；電力","s":"The storm cut off the electricity for six hours, so we ate dinner by candlelight and told stories.","t":"暴風雨讓電力中斷了六個小時，所以我們在燭光下吃晚餐、講故事。"},{"w":"electrical","p":"adj.","d":"connected with electricity","c":"電的；與電有關的","s":"Never use electrical appliances with wet hands, because water and electricity together can kill you.","t":"絕對不要用濕手使用電器用品，因為水和電加在一起可能會要你的命。"},{"w":"electronic","p":"adj.","d":"using tiny electrical parts such as chips, like computers and phones","c":"電子的","s":"All electronic devices, including phones and watches, must be turned off during the listening test.","t":"聽力測驗期間，所有電子裝置，包括手機和手錶，都必須關機。"},{"w":"elevate","p":"v.","d":"to lift something up; to make something higher or better","c":"抬高；提升","s":"If you hurt your ankle, elevate your leg on a pillow and put some ice on it to reduce the swelling.","t":"如果你扭傷腳踝，把腿抬高放在枕頭上並冰敷，以減輕腫脹。","h":1},{"w":"elevator","p":"n.","d":"a machine that carries people up and down in a building","c":"電梯","s":"The elevator in our building is being repaired, so we have to climb nine floors of stairs every day this week.","t":"我們大樓的電梯正在維修，所以這週我們每天都得爬九層樓的樓梯。"},{"w":"elevation","p":"n.","d":"the height of a place above the sea","c":"海拔；高度","s":"The mountain village sits at an elevation of two thousand meters, so even in summer the nights are cold.","t":"這座山村位於海拔兩千公尺，所以即使在夏天夜晚也很冷。"},{"w":"elevated","p":"adj.","d":"raised above the ground; higher than usual","c":"高架的；升高的","s":"The elevated train line runs above the busy streets, so passengers get a great view of the city on their way to work.","t":"高架鐵路線在繁忙的街道上方行駛，所以乘客上班途中可以看到很棒的城市景觀。"},{"w":"emigrant","p":"n.","d":"a person who leaves their own country to live in another","c":"移民（移出者）；僑民","s":"My great-grandfather was an emigrant who left his village in China and sailed to Taiwan with nothing but a small bag.","t":"我的曾祖父是一位移民，他離開中國的村莊，只帶著一個小包袱就坐船來到台灣。","h":1},{"w":"emigrate","p":"v.","d":"to leave your own country to live in another","c":"移居國外","s":"Many young people from the island decided to emigrate to Australia in the 1990s, hoping to find better-paid jobs.","t":"1990 年代，島上許多年輕人決定移居澳洲，希望找到薪水更好的工作。","h":1},{"w":"emigration","p":"n.","d":"the act of leaving your own country to live in another","c":"移居國外；移出","s":"After the war, emigration from the country increased sharply, and whole villages became empty within a few years.","t":"戰後，從這個國家移出的人口急遽增加，幾年內整個村莊都空了。","h":1},{"w":"immigrant","p":"n.","d":"a person who comes to live in a country from another country","c":"移民（移入者）","s":"The new immigrant from Vietnam opened a small restaurant near our school, and her spring rolls are now famous.","t":"那位來自越南的新移民在我們學校附近開了一家小餐館，她的春捲現在很有名。"},{"w":"immigrate","p":"v.","d":"to come to live in a country from another country","c":"移入；移民到","s":"My aunt decided to immigrate to the United States after she married an American she met at university.","t":"我阿姨和大學認識的美國人結婚後，決定移民到美國。"},{"w":"migrate","p":"v.","d":"to move from one place to another, especially animals at certain times of the year","c":"遷徙；遷移","s":"Every autumn, thousands of birds migrate south across Taiwan, and bird lovers wait at the coast to photograph them.","t":"每年秋天，成千上萬的鳥類經過台灣向南遷徙，賞鳥人士在海岸邊等著拍攝牠們。"}]},{"unit":13,"theme":"encyclopedia – expenditure","cards":[{"w":"encyclopedia","p":"n.","d":"a big book or website with facts about many subjects","c":"百科全書","s":"Before the Internet became popular, students had to look things up in a heavy encyclopedia at the library when they wrote reports.","t":"在網路普及之前，學生寫報告時必須在圖書館翻厚重的百科全書查資料。","h":1},{"w":"online encyclopedia","p":"n.phr.","d":"a website, like Wikipedia, that gives facts on many topics","c":"線上百科","s":"Many teachers warn that an online encyclopedia can contain mistakes, so you should check important facts in a second source too.","t":"許多老師警告線上百科可能有錯誤，所以重要的事實也應該用第二個來源查證。"},{"w":"a walking encyclopedia","p":"n.phr.","d":"a person who knows a lot about many things","c":"活字典","s":"My grandfather is a walking encyclopedia; whatever question we ask about history or science, he always knows the answer.","t":"我爺爺是一本活字典；不論我們問什麼歷史或科學的問題，他總是知道答案。"},{"w":"endeavor","p":"n.","d":"a serious attempt to do something difficult","c":"努力；嘗試","s":"Climbing Mount Everest without extra oxygen is a dangerous endeavor, and only a few climbers have ever managed to do it.","t":"不帶額外氧氣攀登聖母峰是一項危險的嘗試，只有少數登山者成功過。","h":1},{"w":"endeavor","p":"v.","d":"to try very hard to do something","c":"努力；盡力","s":"The new mayor promised to endeavor to improve public transportation so that fewer people would need to drive to work.","t":"新市長承諾努力改善大眾運輸，讓更少的人需要開車上班。"},{"w":"make every endeavor","p":"v.phr.","d":"to try as hard as possible","c":"竭盡所能","s":"The hospital staff made every endeavor to save the injured driver, and after six hours of surgery he finally woke up.","t":"醫院人員竭盡所能搶救受傷的駕駛，經過六小時手術後他終於醒來了。","a":"made every endeavor"},{"w":"endowment","p":"n.","d":"money given to a school or organization to support it for a long time","c":"捐款；捐贈基金","s":"Thanks to a large endowment from a former student, the university can now offer free tuition to twenty poor students every year.","t":"多虧一位校友的大筆捐贈基金，這所大學現在每年能提供二十名貧困學生免學費。","h":1},{"w":"endowment","p":"n.","d":"a natural ability or quality that a person is born with","c":"天賦","s":"A beautiful singing voice is a natural endowment, but even talented singers must practice for hours every day to become professionals.","t":"美妙的歌喉是一種天生的天賦，但即使有才華的歌手也必須每天練習數小時才能成為專業歌手。"},{"w":"endow","p":"v.","d":"to give money to a school or organization; to give a quality","c":"捐贈；賦予","s":"The rich businessman decided to endow a new science building so that students could do experiments in modern labs.","t":"這位富商決定捐資興建一棟新的科學大樓，讓學生能在現代實驗室做實驗。"},{"w":"be endowed with","p":"v.phr.","d":"to naturally have a good quality or ability","c":"天生具有","s":"Taiwan is endowed with beautiful mountains and warm hot springs, which attract millions of visitors from all over Asia every year.","t":"台灣天生擁有美麗的山脈和溫暖的溫泉，每年吸引數百萬來自亞洲各地的遊客。","a":"is endowed with"},{"w":"endurance","p":"n.","d":"the ability to keep doing something difficult for a long time","c":"耐力；忍耐力","s":"Running a marathon tests your endurance more than your speed, because you must keep going for over four hours.","t":"跑馬拉松考驗的是你的耐力而不是速度，因為你必須持續跑四個多小時。","h":1},{"w":"endure","p":"v.","d":"to suffer something painful or difficult for a long time","c":"忍受；持續","s":"The villagers had to endure three weeks without electricity after the typhoon knocked down all the power lines in the mountains.","t":"颱風吹倒山區所有電線後，村民不得不忍受三個星期沒有電的日子。"},{"w":"enduring","p":"adj.","d":"lasting for a very long time","c":"持久的","s":"The two friends have an enduring friendship that began in kindergarten and is still strong after more than forty years.","t":"這兩位朋友有著持久的友誼，從幼兒園開始，四十多年後依然深厚。"},{"w":"endurance test","p":"n.phr.","d":"a test of how long someone can keep going","c":"耐力測驗","s":"The three-day hike through the jungle was a real endurance test for the students, but every one of them finished it.","t":"穿越叢林的三天健行對學生來說是真正的耐力測驗，但每個人都走完了。"},{"w":"enhance","p":"v.","d":"to improve the quality or value of something","c":"提高；增強","s":"Adding a little lemon juice can enhance the flavor of the fish, so many chefs squeeze some on just before serving.","t":"加一點檸檬汁可以提升魚的風味，所以許多廚師在上菜前會擠一些。","h":1},{"w":"enhancement","p":"n.","d":"an improvement that makes something better","c":"增強；提升","s":"The new camera is a big enhancement over the old model, because it takes clear pictures even in very dark rooms.","t":"新相機比舊款有很大的提升，因為即使在很暗的房間也能拍出清晰的照片。"},{"w":"enhanced","p":"adj.","d":"better or stronger than before","c":"增強的；加強的","s":"This drink contains enhanced vitamins, so the company says one bottle gives you everything you need for the whole day.","t":"這款飲料含有強化的維生素，所以公司說一瓶就能提供你一整天所需。"},{"w":"enhance one's image","p":"v.phr.","d":"to make people think better of you","c":"提升形象","s":"The company donated computers to rural schools partly to enhance its image after the news reported its factory had polluted a river.","t":"這家公司捐電腦給偏鄉學校，部分是為了在新聞報導其工廠污染河流後提升形象。","a":"enhance its image"},{"w":"enlighten","p":"v.","d":"to give someone knowledge or understanding","c":"啟發；開導","s":"I have no idea how this new app works, so could you please enlighten me before the meeting starts at ten?","t":"我完全不知道這個新 App 怎麼用，所以在十點會議開始前你能指點我一下嗎？","h":1},{"w":"enlightenment","p":"n.","d":"the state of understanding something clearly; deep wisdom","c":"啟發；開悟","s":"Many people travel to quiet temples in the mountains hoping to find enlightenment away from the noise of city life.","t":"許多人前往山中安靜的寺廟，希望遠離城市的喧囂找到開悟。"},{"w":"enlightening","p":"adj.","d":"giving you new understanding","c":"有啟發性的","s":"The documentary about ocean plastic was so enlightening that our whole class decided to stop using plastic straws afterward.","t":"那部關於海洋塑膠的紀錄片非常有啟發性，看完後我們全班決定不再使用塑膠吸管。"},{"w":"enrich","p":"v.","d":"to improve the quality of something by adding to it","c":"使豐富；充實","s":"Reading novels from different countries can enrich your understanding of the world and make you a more open-minded person.","t":"閱讀來自不同國家的小說能豐富你對世界的理解，讓你成為更開明的人。","h":1},{"w":"enrichment","p":"n.","d":"the process of making something better or richer","c":"豐富；充實","s":"Our school offers after-school enrichment classes in art, coding, and music for students who want to learn more than the regular lessons.","t":"我們學校為想學得比正課更多的學生開設美術、程式設計和音樂的課後充實課程。"},{"w":"enriched","p":"adj.","d":"made better by adding something, especially nutrients","c":"強化的；添加營養的","s":"This bread is enriched with iron and vitamins, which is why doctors recommend it for children who do not eat enough vegetables.","t":"這種麵包添加了鐵質和維生素，這就是為什麼醫生推薦給蔬菜吃得不夠的孩子。"},{"w":"enroll","p":"v.","d":"to officially join a school, class, or course","c":"註冊；報名","s":"If you want to enroll in the summer swimming course, you must hand in the form before the end of May.","t":"如果你想報名暑期游泳課程，必須在五月底前交表格。","h":1},{"w":"enrollment","p":"n.","d":"the number of students in a school; the act of joining","c":"註冊人數；入學","s":"Because of the falling birth rate, enrollment at many elementary schools in Taiwan has dropped sharply over the past ten years.","t":"由於出生率下降，台灣許多小學的註冊人數在過去十年急遽減少。"},{"w":"enroll in","p":"v.phr.","d":"to join a course or school officially","c":"報名參加","s":"My mother decided to enroll in a night class to learn Japanese, because she wants to travel to Kyoto next spring.","t":"我媽媽決定報名參加夜間課程學日文，因為她想明年春天去京都旅行。"},{"w":"equalize","p":"v.","d":"to make things equal or the same","c":"使相等；均衡","s":"The new law aims to equalize pay between men and women, so workers doing the same job will finally receive the same salary.","t":"新法律旨在均衡男女薪資，讓做同樣工作的員工終於能領到相同的薪水。","h":1},{"w":"equal","p":"adj.","d":"the same in size, number, or value","c":"相等的；平等的","s":"Cut the cake into eight equal pieces so that every child at the party gets exactly the same amount.","t":"把蛋糕切成八等份，讓派對上的每個孩子都拿到完全一樣的量。"},{"w":"equality","p":"n.","d":"the state of being equal in rights and chances","c":"平等","s":"Martin Luther King Jr. spent his whole life fighting for racial equality, and his famous speech is still read in schools today.","t":"馬丁·路德·金恩一生為種族平等奮鬥，他著名的演說至今仍在學校裡被閱讀。"},{"w":"equally","p":"adv.","d":"in the same way or to the same degree","c":"同樣地；平等地","s":"The teacher treats all her students equally, whether they get high scores or struggle with every test.","t":"這位老師平等地對待所有學生，不論他們考高分還是每次考試都很吃力。"},{"w":"equate","p":"v.","d":"to think that two things are the same or equal","c":"把…等同於","s":"Many people equate money with happiness, but studies show that close friendships matter much more once basic needs are met.","t":"許多人把金錢等同於快樂，但研究顯示一旦基本需求滿足後，親密的友誼重要得多。","h":1},{"w":"be equated with","p":"v.phr.","d":"to be considered the same as something else","c":"被等同於","s":"In many cultures, a big house is equated with success, so people work extra hours just to buy a larger apartment.","t":"在許多文化中，大房子被等同於成功，所以人們加班只為買更大的公寓。","a":"is equated with"},{"w":"equation","p":"n.","d":"a math statement showing that two things are equal","c":"方程式；等式","s":"The math teacher wrote a long equation on the board and asked us to find the value of x before the bell rang.","t":"數學老師在黑板上寫了一條長長的方程式，要我們在鐘響前算出 x 的值。"},{"w":"equivalent","p":"adj.","d":"equal in value, amount, or meaning","c":"相等的；等值的","s":"One U.S. dollar is roughly equivalent to thirty Taiwan dollars, so a ten-dollar lunch in New York costs about three hundred here.","t":"一美元大約相當於三十元台幣，所以在紐約十美元的午餐在這裡約三百元。"},{"w":"escort","p":"v.","d":"to go with someone to protect or guide them","c":"護送；陪同","s":"Two police officers will escort the famous singer from the airport to her hotel to keep the crowd of fans away.","t":"兩名警察將護送這位知名歌手從機場到飯店，讓粉絲群不會靠近。","h":1},{"w":"escort","p":"n.","d":"a person or group that goes with someone to protect them","c":"護衛；護送者","s":"The president never travels without an escort of at least ten guards, even when he visits a small town.","t":"總統出行從不缺少至少十名警衛的護衛，即使拜訪小鎮也一樣。"},{"w":"under escort","p":"phr.","d":"being guarded by police or soldiers while moving","c":"在押解／護送下","s":"The prisoner was moved to the new jail under escort early in the morning so that nobody would try to help him escape.","t":"犯人在清晨在押解下被移送到新監獄，這樣就沒人會試圖幫他逃跑。"},{"w":"esteem","p":"n.","d":"respect and admiration for someone","c":"尊重；敬重","s":"The old doctor is held in high esteem by everyone in the village because he has treated the poor for free for forty years.","t":"這位老醫生受到村裡每個人的高度敬重，因為他四十年來免費為窮人看病。","h":1},{"w":"esteem","p":"v.","d":"to respect and admire someone greatly","c":"尊敬；敬重","s":"Students esteem Mr. Lin not only for his knowledge of history but also for the patient way he answers every question.","t":"學生敬重林老師，不只因為他的歷史知識，也因為他耐心回答每個問題。"},{"w":"self-esteem","p":"n.","d":"the feeling that you are a valuable person","c":"自尊；自信","s":"Praising children for their effort rather than their grades helps build their self-esteem and makes them willing to try harder tasks.","t":"稱讚孩子的努力而不是成績，有助於建立他們的自尊，並讓他們願意嘗試更難的任務。"},{"w":"esteemed","p":"adj.","d":"greatly respected","c":"受敬重的","s":"Our esteemed guest tonight is a scientist who has spent thirty years studying coral reefs around Taiwan.","t":"今晚我們尊敬的貴賓是一位花了三十年研究台灣周邊珊瑚礁的科學家。"},{"w":"eternity","p":"n.","d":"time that never ends; a very long time","c":"永恆；永遠","s":"Waiting for the test results felt like an eternity, although the teacher actually handed them back after only two days.","t":"等待考試結果感覺像是永恆那麼久，雖然老師其實只過了兩天就發回來了。","h":1},{"w":"eternal","p":"adj.","d":"lasting forever; never ending","c":"永恆的；永久的","s":"In the fairy tale, the prince and princess promise each other eternal love and live happily in the castle until the end of their days.","t":"在童話故事裡，王子和公主互許永恆的愛，在城堡裡幸福地生活到老。"},{"w":"eternally","p":"adv.","d":"forever; always","c":"永遠地","s":"I will be eternally grateful to the stranger who found my lost wallet and mailed it back with all the money inside.","t":"我會永遠感激那位撿到我皮夾並連同所有現金寄回來的陌生人。"},{"w":"evacuate","p":"v.","d":"to move people away from a dangerous place","c":"撤離；疏散","s":"When the fire alarm rings, teachers must evacuate all students to the playground within three minutes and count them carefully.","t":"火警警報響起時，老師必須在三分鐘內把所有學生疏散到操場並仔細點名。","h":1},{"w":"evacuation","p":"n.","d":"the act of moving people out of a dangerous area","c":"撤離；疏散","s":"The government ordered the evacuation of two coastal villages the day before the super typhoon hit the east coast.","t":"超級颱風襲擊東海岸的前一天，政府下令兩個沿海村莊撤離。"},{"w":"evacuee","p":"n.","d":"a person who has been moved from a dangerous place","c":"被疏散者","s":"Hundreds of evacuees slept in the school gym for a week after the flood destroyed their homes along the river.","t":"洪水沖毀河邊家園後，數百名被疏散者在學校體育館睡了一個星期。","a":"evacuees"},{"w":"evergreen","p":"adj.","d":"having green leaves all year round","c":"常綠的","s":"Pine trees are evergreen, so the mountain stays green even in January when the maple trees have lost all their leaves.","t":"松樹是常綠的，所以即使在一月楓樹葉子全部掉光時，山上依然是綠色的。","h":1},{"w":"evergreen","p":"n.","d":"a tree or plant that keeps its leaves all year","c":"常綠樹","s":"My grandmother planted a row of evergreens along the fence so that the garden would not look empty during the winter months.","t":"我奶奶沿著圍籬種了一排常綠樹，這樣花園在冬季幾個月裡就不會看起來空蕩蕩的。","a":"evergreens"},{"w":"evergreen","p":"adj.","d":"always popular and never going out of fashion","c":"永不過時的；長青的","s":"That love song from the 1980s is an evergreen hit, and people of every age still sing it at karaoke today.","t":"那首八〇年代的情歌是長青的金曲，各個年齡的人今天在卡拉OK仍在唱它。"},{"w":"evoke","p":"v.","d":"to bring a feeling or memory into someone's mind","c":"喚起；引起","s":"The smell of fresh bread always seems to evoke happy memories of the Sunday mornings I spent at my grandmother's house.","t":"新鮮麵包的香味似乎總能喚起我在奶奶家度過的星期日早晨的快樂回憶。","h":1},{"w":"evocative","p":"adj.","d":"making you remember or imagine something strongly","c":"引起回憶的；令人聯想的","s":"The old black-and-white photos are highly evocative of Taipei in the 1960s, when there were still rice fields near the train station.","t":"這些老黑白照片強烈令人聯想到一九六〇年代的台北，那時火車站附近還有稻田。"},{"w":"evoke memories","p":"v.phr.","d":"to make someone remember things from the past","c":"喚起回憶","s":"Hearing the school bell again after twenty years evoked memories of my classmates, my teachers, and the noisy lunch breaks.","t":"二十年後再次聽到學校鐘聲，喚起了我對同學、老師和熱鬧午休時光的回憶。","a":"evoked memories"},{"w":"examinee","p":"n.","d":"a person who is taking a test","c":"考生；應試者","s":"Every examinee must show a photo ID at the door and leave all phones in the box before entering the test room.","t":"每位考生進入試場前必須在門口出示有照片的證件，並把所有手機放進箱子裡。","h":1},{"w":"examiner","p":"n.","d":"a person who gives a test or checks the answers","c":"考官；主考人","s":"The speaking test lasted ten minutes, and the examiner asked me questions about my hobbies, my family, and my future plans.","t":"口試持續十分鐘，考官問了我關於嗜好、家人和未來計畫的問題。","h":1},{"w":"examine","p":"v.","d":"to look at something carefully; to test someone","c":"檢查；審查；考試","s":"The doctor will examine your eyes first, and then she will decide whether you need to wear glasses for reading.","t":"醫生會先檢查你的眼睛，然後決定你是否需要戴眼鏡閱讀。"},{"w":"examination","p":"n.","d":"a test; a careful check","c":"考試；檢查","s":"The final examination covers everything we learned this semester, so you should start reviewing your notes at least two weeks early.","t":"期末考試涵蓋這學期學的所有內容，所以你至少應該提前兩週開始複習筆記。"},{"w":"take an exam","p":"v.phr.","d":"to sit a test","c":"參加考試","s":"Senior high school students in Taiwan take an exam in January that decides which universities they can apply to.","t":"台灣的高中生在一月參加一場考試，這場考試決定他們能申請哪些大學。"},{"w":"excel","p":"v.","d":"to be extremely good at something","c":"擅長；表現優異","s":"Although Jenny is quiet in class, she excels at drawing, and her pictures have won prizes in three national contests.","t":"雖然珍妮在課堂上很安靜，但她擅長畫畫，她的作品已在三個全國比賽中獲獎。","a":"excels","h":1},{"w":"excel at","p":"v.phr.","d":"to be very good at a particular activity","c":"擅長於","s":"My brother does not excel at math, but he is the best basketball player our school has had in many years.","t":"我哥哥並不擅長數學，但他是我們學校多年來最棒的籃球選手。"},{"w":"excellent","p":"adj.","d":"extremely good","c":"優秀的；極好的","s":"The service at that small restaurant was excellent; the waiter remembered our names and refilled our tea before we even asked.","t":"那家小餐廳的服務非常優秀；服務生記得我們的名字，還在我們開口前就幫我們續茶。"},{"w":"excellence","p":"n.","d":"the quality of being extremely good","c":"卓越；優秀","s":"The school gives an award for excellence in science every year to the student with the most creative project.","t":"學校每年頒發科學卓越獎給專題最有創意的學生。"},{"w":"excerpt","p":"n.","d":"a short part taken from a book, film, or speech","c":"摘錄；節選","s":"The teacher read an excerpt from the novel aloud, and it was so exciting that half the class borrowed the book that week.","t":"老師大聲朗讀小說的一段摘錄，內容如此精彩，那週全班有一半的人去借了那本書。","h":1},{"w":"excerpt","p":"v.","d":"to take a short part from a longer work","c":"摘錄；節選","s":"The magazine plans to excerpt two chapters from the famous writer's new book before it goes on sale in December.","t":"這本雜誌計畫在這位名作家的新書十二月上市前節選其中兩章。"},{"w":"excerpt from","p":"n.phr.","d":"a passage taken out of a longer text","c":"摘錄自…的段落","s":"The reading test included an excerpt from a newspaper article about electric cars, followed by five comprehension questions.","t":"閱讀測驗包含一篇摘錄自有關電動車報紙文章的段落，接著是五個理解問題。"},{"w":"excess","p":"n.","d":"an amount that is more than needed","c":"過量；過度","s":"Doctors warn that an excess of sugar in the diet can lead to serious health problems such as diabetes and heart disease.","t":"醫生警告飲食中過量的糖可能導致糖尿病和心臟病等嚴重健康問題。","h":1},{"w":"excess","p":"adj.","d":"more than is needed or allowed","c":"多餘的；超額的","s":"Passengers must pay extra for excess baggage, so weigh your suitcase at home before you leave for the airport.","t":"旅客必須為超重行李多付費，所以出發去機場前先在家秤一下行李箱。"},{"w":"in excess of","p":"phr.","d":"more than a particular amount","c":"超過","s":"The charity concert raised money in excess of two million dollars, far more than the organizers had hoped for.","t":"慈善音樂會募得超過兩百萬元，遠超出主辦單位的期望。"},{"w":"excessive","p":"adj.","d":"too much; more than is reasonable","c":"過度的；過多的","s":"Playing video games for eight hours a day is clearly excessive, and it will hurt both your eyes and your grades.","t":"每天打八小時電動顯然是過度的，會傷害你的眼睛和成績。"},{"w":"exceed","p":"v.","d":"to be greater than a number or limit","c":"超過；超出","s":"The driver was fined because his speed exceeded the limit by thirty kilometers an hour on the highway.","t":"這位駕駛被罰款，因為他在高速公路上的車速超過限速三十公里。","a":"exceeded"},{"w":"exclusion","p":"n.","d":"the act of keeping someone or something out","c":"排除；排斥","s":"The exclusion of girls from the science club made many parents angry, so the school changed the rule the next semester.","t":"科學社排除女生讓許多家長生氣，所以學校下學期就改了規定。","h":1},{"w":"exclude","p":"v.","d":"to keep someone or something out; to not include","c":"排除；不包括","s":"If you exclude the two students who were absent, the average score of the class rises to eighty-five.","t":"如果你排除那兩位缺席的學生，全班平均分數就上升到八十五分。"},{"w":"exclusive","p":"adj.","d":"only for a particular group; not shared","c":"獨有的；專屬的","s":"The hotel has an exclusive beach that only guests can use, so it is never crowded even in the summer holidays.","t":"這間飯店有一片只有住客能使用的專屬海灘，所以即使在暑假也從不擁擠。"},{"w":"to the exclusion of","p":"phr.","d":"so much that other things are left out","c":"排除…；而不顧","s":"He practiced the piano to the exclusion of everything else, and he even forgot to eat dinner twice last week.","t":"他練鋼琴到了排除其他一切的程度，上週甚至兩次忘了吃晚餐。"},{"w":"exempt","p":"adj.","d":"not having to do something that others must do","c":"免除的；豁免的","s":"Students who passed the English test last year are exempt from taking it again, so they can go home early on Friday.","t":"去年通過英文測驗的學生免再考一次，所以他們星期五可以提早回家。","h":1},{"w":"exempt","p":"v.","d":"to officially free someone from a duty","c":"免除；豁免","s":"The government decided to exempt small farmers from the new tax because many of them earn very little money each year.","t":"政府決定免除小農的新稅，因為許多小農每年收入很少。"},{"w":"be exempt from","p":"v.phr.","d":"to not have to do or pay something","c":"免於；不受…約束","s":"Books and medicine are exempt from the sales tax in this country, which makes them a little cheaper for ordinary families.","t":"在這個國家書籍和藥品免徵營業稅，這讓它們對一般家庭來說便宜一點。","a":"are exempt from"},{"w":"exemption","p":"n.","d":"official permission not to do or pay something","c":"免除；豁免","s":"Families with three or more children can apply for a tax exemption, which saves them several thousand dollars a year.","t":"有三個以上孩子的家庭可以申請稅務減免，每年能為他們省下數千元。"},{"w":"exert","p":"v.","d":"to use power, strength, or influence","c":"施加；運用","s":"Parents often exert a lot of pressure on their children to study, but too much pressure can make kids hate school.","t":"父母常對孩子施加很大的讀書壓力，但壓力太大可能讓孩子討厭上學。","h":1},{"w":"exert oneself","p":"v.phr.","d":"to make a great physical or mental effort","c":"盡力；費力","s":"The doctor told my grandfather not to exert himself too much after the operation, so he only walks slowly around the garden.","t":"醫生告訴我爺爺手術後不要太勞累，所以他只在花園裡慢慢走。","a":"exert himself"},{"w":"exertion","p":"n.","d":"physical or mental effort","c":"努力；費力","s":"After the long climb, the hikers were red-faced from exertion, and they sat down to drink water before taking photos.","t":"長途攀登後，登山客因費力而滿臉通紅，他們坐下來喝水才開始拍照。"},{"w":"exert influence on","p":"v.phr.","d":"to affect how someone thinks or acts","c":"對…施加影響","s":"Famous YouTubers exert influence on teenagers' choices, which is why companies pay them to show new products in their videos.","t":"知名 YouTuber對青少年的選擇施加影響，這就是為什麼公司付錢讓他們在影片中展示新產品。"},{"w":"expenditure","p":"n.","d":"the total amount of money spent","c":"支出；花費","s":"The city's expenditure on new roads rose sharply last year, so there was less money left for parks and libraries.","t":"這座城市去年在新道路上的支出大幅增加，所以剩下給公園和圖書館的錢變少了。","h":1},{"w":"expend","p":"v.","d":"to use time, energy, or money on something","c":"花費；消耗","s":"Do not expend all your energy in the first kilometer of the race, or you will have nothing left for the final sprint.","t":"不要在比賽的第一公里就耗盡所有體力，否則最後衝刺時你會沒力氣。"},{"w":"expense","p":"n.","d":"money spent on something; cost","c":"費用；開銷","s":"Rent is the biggest expense for most young people in Taipei, often taking up more than a third of their monthly salary.","t":"房租是台北大多數年輕人最大的開銷，常常占每月薪水的三分之一以上。"},{"w":"expensive","p":"adj.","d":"costing a lot of money","c":"昂貴的","s":"The new phone is too expensive for a student, so I will wait until the price drops after the holidays.","t":"這款新手機對學生來說太貴了，所以我會等到節日後降價再買。"},{"w":"at the expense of","p":"phr.","d":"causing harm or loss to something else","c":"以…為代價","s":"He finished the project early but at the expense of his health, since he slept only four hours a night for a month.","t":"他提早完成專案，但以健康為代價，因為他一個月來每晚只睡四小時。"}]},{"unit":14,"theme":"expiration – flake","cards":[{"w":"expiration","p":"n.","d":"the end of the time when something can be used","c":"到期；期滿","s":"Check the expiration date on the milk before you buy it, because the store sometimes leaves old bottles on the shelf.","t":"買牛奶前先看一下到期日，因為店裡有時會把舊的瓶子留在架上。","h":1},{"w":"expire","p":"v.","d":"to come to the end of the time it can be used","c":"到期；過期","s":"My passport will expire next month, so I have to apply for a new one before our family trip to Japan.","t":"我的護照下個月就要到期了，所以我必須在全家去日本旅行前申請新的。","h":1},{"w":"expiration date","p":"n.phr.","d":"the last day something can safely be used","c":"有效期限","s":"Medicine that has passed its expiration date may not work well anymore, so throw it away instead of taking it.","t":"過了有效期限的藥可能已經沒什麼效果，所以把它丟掉而不要吃。"},{"w":"expired","p":"adj.","d":"no longer valid or safe to use","c":"過期的","s":"The guard would not let him into the building because his ID card was expired and had not been renewed.","t":"警衛不讓他進大樓，因為他的識別證過期了而且沒有換新。"},{"w":"extract","p":"v.","d":"to take something out, often with effort","c":"提取；拔出；萃取","s":"The dentist had to extract my back tooth because it was too badly broken to be repaired.","t":"牙醫必須拔掉我的後牙，因為它壞得太嚴重無法修補。","h":1},{"w":"extract","p":"n.","d":"a strong substance taken from a plant; a short piece from a book","c":"萃取物；摘錄","s":"This shampoo contains green tea extract, which the company says makes your hair softer and smell fresh all day.","t":"這款洗髮精含有綠茶萃取物，公司說它能讓你的頭髮更柔軟，整天都有清新的香味。"},{"w":"extract information from","p":"v.phr.","d":"to get information from someone or something","c":"從…取得資訊","s":"The police spent hours trying to extract information from the quiet man, but he refused to say where he had been that night.","t":"警方花了好幾個小時試圖從那個沉默的男人身上套出資訊，但他拒絕說出那晚他去了哪裡。"},{"w":"extraction","p":"n.","d":"the act of taking something out","c":"提取；拔除；開採","s":"Oil extraction in the desert has made the small country very rich, but it has also damaged the land.","t":"沙漠裡的石油開採讓這個小國變得非常富有，但也破壞了土地。"},{"w":"extracurricular","p":"adj.","d":"outside the normal school lessons","c":"課外的","s":"Joining extracurricular activities like the drama club helps students make friends and discover talents they never knew they had.","t":"參加戲劇社等課外活動能幫助學生交朋友，並發現自己從不知道的才能。","h":1},{"w":"extracurricular activity","p":"n.phr.","d":"a club or sport done outside class","c":"課外活動","s":"Many universities look at more than grades, so a good extracurricular activity like volunteering can make your application stronger.","t":"許多大學看的不只是成績，所以像志工服務這樣好的課外活動能讓你的申請更有力。"},{"w":"curriculum","p":"n.","d":"the subjects taught in a school or course","c":"課程","s":"The new curriculum includes computer coding for all first-year students, so every class now has two hours in the lab.","t":"新課程包含所有一年級學生的電腦程式設計，所以現在每班每週有兩小時在電腦教室。"},{"w":"extra","p":"adj.","d":"more than usual or needed","c":"額外的","s":"The teacher gave us an extra day to finish the report because the library was closed over the long weekend.","t":"老師多給我們額外一天完成報告，因為圖書館在連假期間關閉。"},{"w":"eyelash","p":"n.","d":"one of the small hairs on the edge of the eyelid","c":"睫毛","s":"An eyelash got into my eye while I was riding my bike, and I had to stop to rub it out.","t":"我騎腳踏車時一根睫毛跑進眼睛，我不得不停下來把它揉出來。","h":1},{"w":"lash","p":"n.","d":"a short word for eyelash; a hit with a whip","c":"睫毛；鞭打","s":"My sister spends ten minutes every morning putting makeup on each lash to make her eyes look bigger.","t":"我姊姊每天早上花十分鐘在每根睫毛上化妝，讓眼睛看起來更大。"},{"w":"false eyelashes","p":"n.phr.","d":"fake eyelashes worn to make eyes look prettier","c":"假睫毛","s":"The actress wore long false eyelashes for the show, but she took them off as soon as she left the stage.","t":"那位女演員為了演出戴了長長的假睫毛，但一下舞台就把它們拿掉了。"},{"w":"eyelid","p":"n.","d":"the piece of skin that covers your eye when you close it","c":"眼皮；眼瞼","s":"After studying until two in the morning, I could hardly keep my eyelids open during the first class.","t":"讀書讀到凌晨兩點後，第一堂課我幾乎無法讓眼皮保持張開。","a":"eyelids","h":1},{"w":"eye","p":"n.","d":"the part of the body you see with","c":"眼睛","s":"A small piece of dust got into my left eye, and it hurt until I washed it out with clean water.","t":"一小粒灰塵跑進我的左眼，一直很痛，直到我用乾淨的水把它沖出來。"},{"w":"not bat an eyelid","p":"v.phr.","d":"to show no surprise or worry","c":"面不改色；眉頭都不皺","s":"When the teacher announced a surprise test, Amy did not bat an eyelid because she had reviewed her notes the night before.","t":"老師宣布臨時小考時，艾美眉頭都沒皺一下，因為她前一晚已經複習過筆記。","a":"did not bat an eyelid"},{"w":"eyesight","p":"n.","d":"the ability to see","c":"視力","s":"Reading in dim light for hours every night can slowly weaken your eyesight, so always turn on a good lamp.","t":"每晚在昏暗的光線下讀書好幾個小時會慢慢削弱你的視力，所以一定要開一盞好的檯燈。","h":1},{"w":"have poor eyesight","p":"v.phr.","d":"to not be able to see well","c":"視力不好","s":"My grandmother has poor eyesight now, so she asks me to read the small print on medicine bottles for her.","t":"我奶奶現在視力不好，所以她請我幫她讀藥瓶上的小字。","a":"has poor eyesight"},{"w":"sight","p":"n.","d":"the ability to see; something that you see","c":"視力；景象","s":"The sunrise from the top of Alishan is a beautiful sight that thousands of tourists get up at four o'clock to see.","t":"從阿里山頂看日出是美麗的景象，成千上萬的遊客四點就起床去看。"},{"w":"at first sight","p":"phr.","d":"when you see someone or something for the first time","c":"第一眼；乍看之下","s":"At first sight, the math problem looked impossible, but after reading it twice I found a simple way to solve it.","t":"乍看之下這道數學題似乎不可能解，但讀了兩遍後我找到一個簡單的解法。","a":"At first sight"},{"w":"fable","p":"n.","d":"a short story, often with animals, that teaches a lesson","c":"寓言","s":"In the famous fable about the tortoise and the hare, the slow but steady tortoise wins the race in the end.","t":"在著名的龜兔賽跑寓言裡，慢但穩的烏龜最後贏了比賽。","h":1},{"w":"Aesop's Fables","p":"n.phr.","d":"a famous collection of old Greek animal stories","c":"伊索寓言","s":"Many children in Taiwan first learn English through Aesop's Fables, because the stories are short and the lessons are easy to understand.","t":"台灣許多孩子最早透過伊索寓言學英文，因為故事很短，道理也容易懂。"},{"w":"fabulous","p":"adj.","d":"extremely good; wonderful","c":"極好的；絕妙的","s":"We had a fabulous time at the beach last weekend; the weather was perfect and the water was warm and clear.","t":"上週末我們在海邊玩得非常愉快；天氣完美，海水溫暖又清澈。"},{"w":"faction","p":"n.","d":"a small group inside a larger group that has different ideas","c":"派系；小集團","s":"The club broke into a small faction that wanted more games and a larger group that preferred quiet reading.","t":"社團分裂成一個想要更多遊戲的小派系和一個偏好安靜閱讀的較大群體。","h":1},{"w":"rival factions","p":"n.phr.","d":"groups inside one organization that fight each other","c":"敵對派系","s":"Fighting between rival factions inside the company grew so bad that the new manager had to call a meeting with everyone.","t":"公司內部敵對派系之間的爭鬥變得太嚴重，新經理不得不召集所有人開會。"},{"w":"factional","p":"adj.","d":"connected with fighting between groups inside an organization","c":"派系的","s":"The factional fighting inside the government made it impossible to pass any new laws for almost a whole year.","t":"政府內部的派系鬥爭使得將近一整年都無法通過任何新法律。"},{"w":"Fahrenheit","p":"n.","d":"a scale for measuring temperature used in the U.S.","c":"華氏","s":"In the United States, people say it is ninety degrees Fahrenheit on a hot day, which is about thirty-two degrees Celsius.","t":"在美國，人們說炎熱的日子有九十度華氏，大約是攝氏三十二度。","h":1},{"w":"degrees Fahrenheit","p":"n.phr.","d":"units of temperature on the Fahrenheit scale","c":"華氏度","s":"Water freezes at thirty-two degrees Fahrenheit, so American weather reports sound very strange to visitors from Taiwan at first.","t":"水在三十二華氏度結冰，所以美國的氣象報告一開始對來自台灣的訪客來說聽起來很奇怪。"},{"w":"Celsius","p":"n.","d":"the temperature scale used in most countries, where water boils at 100","c":"攝氏","s":"The weather report said it would reach thirty-six degrees Celsius this afternoon, so remember to drink plenty of water.","t":"氣象報告說今天下午會達到攝氏三十六度，所以記得多喝水。"},{"w":"thermometer","p":"n.","d":"a tool for measuring temperature","c":"溫度計","s":"The nurse put a thermometer under my arm and said I had a fever of thirty-eight point five degrees.","t":"護士把溫度計放在我腋下，說我發燒到三十八點五度。"},{"w":"falter","p":"v.","d":"to become weaker; to lose confidence and stop","c":"動搖；猶豫；衰退","s":"Her voice began to falter in the middle of the speech, but she took a deep breath and finished it strongly.","t":"她的聲音在演講中途開始顫抖動搖，但她深吸一口氣，堅定地說完了。","h":1},{"w":"faltering","p":"adj.","d":"weak and unsteady","c":"蹣跚的；不穩的","s":"The old man took a few faltering steps toward the door, and his grandson quickly ran over to hold his arm.","t":"老人朝門口走了幾步蹣跚的步伐，他的孫子立刻跑過去扶住他的手臂。"},{"w":"without faltering","p":"phr.","d":"steadily; without stopping or losing courage","c":"毫不動搖地","s":"She recited the whole poem without faltering, even though two hundred parents were watching her from the audience.","t":"她毫不動搖地背完整首詩，即使有兩百位家長從觀眾席看著她。"},{"w":"familiarity","p":"n.","d":"good knowledge of something because you have seen or used it often","c":"熟悉","s":"Her familiarity with the city helped us find a cheap, delicious restaurant that was not in any travel guide.","t":"她對這座城市的熟悉幫助我們找到一家任何旅遊指南都沒有的便宜又好吃的餐廳。","h":1},{"w":"familiar","p":"adj.","d":"well known to you; easy to recognize","c":"熟悉的","s":"The song on the radio sounded familiar, and then I remembered that we had sung it at our graduation ceremony.","t":"收音機裡的歌聽起來很熟悉，然後我想起我們在畢業典禮上唱過它。"},{"w":"be familiar with","p":"v.phr.","d":"to know something well","c":"熟悉…","s":"You should be familiar with the bus routes before you move to Taipei, or you may waste a lot of time getting lost.","t":"搬到台北之前你應該先熟悉公車路線，否則你可能會因迷路浪費很多時間。"},{"w":"unfamiliar","p":"adj.","d":"not known to you; strange","c":"不熟悉的；陌生的","s":"The menu was full of unfamiliar dishes, so we asked the waiter to recommend something that most local people like.","t":"菜單上全是不熟悉的菜，所以我們請服務生推薦大多數當地人喜歡的東西。"},{"w":"familiarize","p":"v.","d":"to learn about something so you know it well","c":"使熟悉","s":"New workers spend their first week trying to familiarize themselves with the company's computer system and safety rules.","t":"新員工第一週都在努力熟悉公司的電腦系統和安全規定。"},{"w":"fascination","p":"n.","d":"a very strong interest in something","c":"著迷；魅力","s":"Ever since he visited the science museum, my little brother has had a fascination with dinosaurs and reads about them every day.","t":"自從參觀科學博物館後，我弟弟就對恐龍非常著迷，每天都在讀相關的書。","h":1},{"w":"fascinate","p":"v.","d":"to interest someone very strongly","c":"使著迷","s":"Stories about space travel fascinate my cousin so much that she has decided to study physics at university.","t":"太空旅行的故事讓我表妹非常著迷，她已決定在大學讀物理。"},{"w":"fascinating","p":"adj.","d":"extremely interesting","c":"迷人的；極有趣的","s":"The documentary about octopuses was so fascinating that nobody in the class looked at their phone for the whole hour.","t":"那部關於章魚的紀錄片太引人入勝了，整整一小時全班沒有人看手機。"},{"w":"be fascinated by","p":"v.phr.","d":"to be very interested in something","c":"對…著迷","s":"Tourists are fascinated by the night markets in Taiwan, where they can try dozens of snacks for less than ten dollars.","t":"觀光客對台灣的夜市著迷，在那裡他們花不到十美元就能嘗試幾十種小吃。","a":"are fascinated by"},{"w":"feasible","p":"adj.","d":"possible to do; practical","c":"可行的","s":"Building a bridge to the small island is not feasible right now because the water is too deep and the cost is too high.","t":"現在建一座橋通往那座小島並不可行，因為水太深而且費用太高。","h":1},{"w":"feasibility","p":"n.","d":"how possible or practical a plan is","c":"可行性","s":"The city hired experts to study the feasibility of a new MRT line before spending billions of dollars on it.","t":"市政府聘請專家研究新捷運線的可行性，然後才花數十億元興建。"},{"w":"a feasible plan","p":"n.phr.","d":"a plan that can really be carried out","c":"可行的計畫","s":"Finishing the whole textbook in one week is not a feasible plan, so let's review two chapters each day instead.","t":"一週內讀完整本課本不是一個可行的計畫，所以我們改成每天複習兩章吧。"},{"w":"feeble","p":"adj.","d":"very weak","c":"虛弱的；微弱的","s":"After two weeks in the hospital, Grandpa was too feeble to walk to the bathroom without someone holding his arm.","t":"住院兩週後，爺爺太虛弱了，沒有人扶著手臂就無法走到浴室。","h":1},{"w":"feeble excuse","p":"n.phr.","d":"a weak reason that nobody believes","c":"站不住腳的藉口","s":"Saying that his dog ate the homework was a feeble excuse, and the teacher just shook her head and sighed.","t":"說狗吃了作業是個站不住腳的藉口，老師只是搖搖頭嘆了口氣。"},{"w":"feebly","p":"adv.","d":"in a weak way","c":"虛弱地；無力地","s":"The injured bird moved its wings feebly when we picked it up, so we took it to the animal hospital at once.","t":"我們把受傷的小鳥撿起來時牠無力地動了動翅膀，所以我們立刻帶牠去動物醫院。"},{"w":"feminine","p":"adj.","d":"having qualities that are thought to be typical of women","c":"女性的；陰柔的","s":"The designer used soft pink colors and flowers to give the room a feminine feeling that the young girl loved.","t":"設計師用柔和的粉紅色和花朵讓房間有一種女性化的感覺，小女孩非常喜歡。","h":1},{"w":"feminine","p":"n.","d":"the form of a word used for females in some languages","c":"陰性","s":"In Spanish class we learned that 'la casa' is in the feminine, while 'el libro' uses the masculine form.","t":"在西班牙文課上我們學到 la casa 是陰性，而 el libro 用的是陽性形式。"},{"w":"masculine","p":"adj.","d":"having qualities thought to be typical of men","c":"男性的；陽剛的","s":"Deep voices and strong muscles are often seen as masculine, but many women athletes have both and are proud of them.","t":"低沉的聲音和強壯的肌肉常被視為陽剛的，但許多女運動員兩者兼具並以此為榮。"},{"w":"femininity","p":"n.","d":"the qualities that are thought to be typical of women","c":"女性特質","s":"Some fashion writers say long hair is a sign of femininity, but plenty of confident women prefer very short styles.","t":"有些時尚作家說長髮是女性特質的象徵，但許多自信的女性偏好非常短的髮型。"},{"w":"female","p":"adj.","d":"belonging to the sex that can have babies","c":"女性的；雌性的","s":"The female lion does most of the hunting for the family, while the male mainly guards the group.","t":"母獅負責家族大部分的狩獵，而公獅主要是守護族群。"},{"w":"fertility","p":"n.","d":"the ability of land to grow good crops; the ability to have babies","c":"肥沃；生育力","s":"Farmers in the valley are worried because years of heavy chemical use have reduced the fertility of their soil.","t":"山谷裡的農民很擔心，因為多年大量使用化學藥劑已降低了他們土壤的肥沃度。","h":1},{"w":"fertilizer","p":"n.","d":"a substance put on soil to help plants grow","c":"肥料","s":"My grandfather adds natural fertilizer made from fruit peels to his garden, and his tomatoes grow bigger every year.","t":"我爺爺在花園裡加入用果皮做的天然肥料，他的番茄每年都長得更大。","h":1},{"w":"fertile","p":"adj.","d":"able to produce good crops; able to have babies","c":"肥沃的；多產的","s":"The land near the river is very fertile, so farmers there can grow rice, vegetables, and fruit all year round.","t":"河邊的土地非常肥沃，所以那裡的農民一年四季都能種稻米、蔬菜和水果。"},{"w":"fertilize","p":"v.","d":"to add substances to soil to help plants grow","c":"施肥","s":"You should fertilize the plants once a month in spring and summer, but they need much less food during the winter.","t":"春夏期間你應該每月給植物施肥一次，但冬天它們需要的養分少得多。"},{"w":"chemical fertilizer","p":"n.phr.","d":"fertilizer made in a factory","c":"化學肥料","s":"Too much chemical fertilizer can wash into rivers when it rains and kill the fish, so organic farmers avoid using it.","t":"下雨時過多的化學肥料會沖進河裡毒死魚類，所以有機農夫避免使用它。"},{"w":"fiancé","p":"n.","d":"the man a woman is going to marry","c":"未婚夫","s":"Linda introduced her fiancé to her parents last Sunday, and they will get married next spring after he finishes his studies.","t":"琳達上週日把未婚夫介紹給父母，他們將在他完成學業後的明年春天結婚。","h":1},{"w":"fiancée","p":"n.","d":"the woman a man is going to marry","c":"未婚妻","s":"Jack bought a ring for his fiancée with the money he had saved from two years of part-time work.","t":"傑克用兩年打工存下的錢為未婚妻買了一枚戒指。"},{"w":"engaged","p":"adj.","d":"having agreed to marry someone","c":"訂婚的","s":"My cousin got engaged last month, and the whole family is already busy planning a big wedding party for December.","t":"我表姊上個月訂婚了，全家人已經忙著籌劃十二月的盛大婚宴。"},{"w":"engagement","p":"n.","d":"an agreement to marry; the time before the wedding","c":"訂婚；婚約","s":"They announced their engagement at the family dinner, and Grandma cried with happiness when she saw the ring.","t":"他們在家庭聚餐上宣布訂婚，奶奶看到戒指時高興得哭了。"},{"w":"fin","p":"n.","d":"a thin flat part on a fish's body used for swimming","c":"鰭","s":"A shark uses its tail and the large fin on its back to move quickly through the water toward its food.","t":"鯊魚用尾巴和背上的大鰭在水中快速游向食物。","h":1},{"w":"fins","p":"n.","d":"rubber shoes shaped like fish fins that help you swim","c":"蛙鞋","s":"Put on your fins before you go into the sea, because they will help you swim faster and save your energy.","t":"下海前先穿上蛙鞋，因為它們能幫你游得更快並節省體力。"},{"w":"shark fin soup","p":"n.phr.","d":"an expensive soup made from shark fins","c":"魚翅湯","s":"Many restaurants in Taiwan no longer serve shark fin soup because killing sharks just for their fins is cruel and harms the ocean.","t":"台灣許多餐廳不再供應魚翅湯，因為只為了魚鰭而殺鯊魚既殘忍又傷害海洋。"},{"w":"dorsal fin","p":"n.phr.","d":"the fin on the back of a fish or dolphin","c":"背鰭","s":"You can tell a dolphin from a shark by its dorsal fin, which is curved instead of straight and pointed.","t":"你可以從背鰭分辨海豚和鯊魚，海豚的背鰭是彎曲的而不是直而尖的。"},{"w":"finite","p":"adj.","d":"having a limit or an end","c":"有限的","s":"Oil and coal are finite resources, so the world must find cleaner energy before they run out completely.","t":"石油和煤是有限的資源，所以世界必須在它們完全用完前找到更乾淨的能源。","h":1},{"w":"infinite","p":"adj.","d":"without any limit or end","c":"無限的","s":"Looking up at the stars on a clear night, you feel that the universe is infinite and our problems are very small.","t":"在晴朗的夜晚仰望星空，你會覺得宇宙是無限的，而我們的問題非常渺小。"},{"w":"infinity","p":"n.","d":"a space, amount, or time without end","c":"無限；無窮","s":"The hotel's swimming pool seems to stretch to infinity, because its far edge disappears into the blue sea behind it.","t":"這間飯店的游泳池彷彿延伸到無限遠，因為它的遠端消失在身後的藍色大海裡。"},{"w":"finish","p":"v.","d":"to complete something; to end","c":"完成；結束","s":"If you finish your homework before dinner, we can watch a movie together after we clean up the kitchen.","t":"如果你在晚餐前完成功課，我們整理完廚房後就可以一起看電影。"},{"w":"firecracker","p":"n.","d":"a small paper tube that explodes with a loud bang","c":"鞭炮","s":"On Chinese New Year's Eve, my uncle lights a long string of firecrackers outside the door to scare away bad luck.","t":"除夕夜，我叔叔在門外點燃一長串鞭炮來趕走壞運氣。","a":"firecrackers","h":1},{"w":"fireworks","p":"n.","d":"colorful explosions in the sky for celebrations","c":"煙火","s":"Thousands of people gather near Taipei 101 every New Year's Eve to watch the fireworks light up the sky at midnight.","t":"每年除夕夜成千上萬的人聚集在台北101附近，觀賞午夜點亮天空的煙火。"},{"w":"set off firecrackers","p":"v.phr.","d":"to light firecrackers so they explode","c":"放鞭炮","s":"Shop owners set off firecrackers on the first day they open after the holiday, hoping for good business in the new year.","t":"店家在假期後開工的第一天放鞭炮，希望新的一年生意興隆。"},{"w":"cracker","p":"n.","d":"a thin dry biscuit","c":"薄脆餅乾；蘇打餅","s":"When I have a stomachache, my mother gives me plain crackers and warm water instead of a big meal.","t":"當我胃痛時，媽媽會給我原味蘇打餅乾和溫水，而不是一頓大餐。","a":"crackers"},{"w":"fireproof","p":"adj.","d":"unable to burn or be damaged by fire","c":"防火的；耐火的","s":"Important documents should be kept in a fireproof box so that they will survive even if the house catches fire.","t":"重要文件應該放在防火箱裡，這樣即使房子失火它們也能保存下來。","h":1},{"w":"waterproof","p":"adj.","d":"not letting water pass through","c":"防水的","s":"My new watch is waterproof, so I do not have to take it off when I wash my hands or go swimming.","t":"我的新手錶是防水的，所以洗手或游泳時不必拿下來。"},{"w":"fire extinguisher","p":"n.phr.","d":"a metal container used to put out small fires","c":"滅火器","s":"Every classroom has a fire extinguisher by the door, and the teacher showed us how to pull the pin and use it.","t":"每間教室門邊都有滅火器，老師示範如何拔掉插銷並使用它。"},{"w":"fire drill","p":"n.phr.","d":"a practice of leaving a building safely in case of fire","c":"消防演習","s":"During the fire drill this morning, the whole school walked to the playground in less than four minutes without pushing.","t":"今早的消防演習中，全校在四分鐘內走到操場，沒有人推擠。"},{"w":"fishery","p":"n.","d":"a place or business where fish are caught or raised","c":"漁業；漁場","s":"The small town depends on its fishery for jobs, so people worry when fewer fish are caught each year.","t":"這個小鎮靠漁業提供工作，所以每年捕到的魚變少時人們就很擔心。","h":1},{"w":"fisherman","p":"n.","d":"a person who catches fish for a living or for fun","c":"漁夫","s":"The old fisherman goes out to sea at four every morning and sells his catch at the harbor market by nine.","t":"這位老漁夫每天早上四點出海，九點前就在漁港市場賣掉他的漁獲。"},{"w":"fishing","p":"n.","d":"the sport or job of catching fish","c":"釣魚；捕魚","s":"My father and I go fishing at the lake every Sunday, although we usually come home with nothing but sunburn.","t":"我和爸爸每個星期天都去湖邊釣魚，雖然我們通常只帶著曬傷回家。"},{"w":"fishing boat","p":"n.phr.","d":"a boat used for catching fish","c":"漁船","s":"Dozens of fishing boats return to the harbor at dawn, and the smell of fresh fish fills the whole market.","t":"數十艘漁船在黎明時返回漁港，新鮮魚的味道充滿整個市場。","a":"fishing boats"},{"w":"flake","p":"n.","d":"a small thin piece of something","c":"薄片；小片","s":"A few flakes of old paint fell from the ceiling onto the table, so we decided it was time to repaint the room.","t":"幾片舊油漆從天花板掉到桌上，所以我們決定是時候重新粉刷房間了。","a":"flakes","h":1},{"w":"flake","p":"v.","d":"to come off in small thin pieces","c":"剝落；脫皮","s":"The skin on my nose started to flake after I got a bad sunburn at the beach last weekend.","t":"上週末在海邊曬傷後，我鼻子上的皮膚開始脫皮。"},{"w":"snowflake","p":"n.","d":"a single small piece of falling snow","c":"雪花","s":"Every snowflake has a different shape, which is why children in cold countries love to catch them on their gloves.","t":"每片雪花的形狀都不同，這就是為什麼寒冷國家的孩子喜歡用手套接住它們。"},{"w":"cornflakes","p":"n.","d":"a breakfast food made of small dry pieces of corn","c":"玉米片","s":"I usually have a bowl of cornflakes with cold milk for breakfast because it is quick and I am always late for school.","t":"我早餐通常吃一碗玉米片加冰牛奶，因為很快，而且我上學總是遲到。"}]},{"unit":15,"theme":"flaw – garment","cards":[{"w":"flaw","p":"n.","d":"a mistake or weak point that makes something not perfect","c":"缺陷；瑕疵","s":"The plan sounded perfect at first, but it had one serious flaw: nobody had checked whether the hall was free that day.","t":"這個計畫起初聽起來很完美，但它有一個嚴重的缺陷：沒有人確認那天禮堂是否有空。","h":1},{"w":"flawless","p":"adj.","d":"perfect; without any mistakes","c":"完美的；無瑕的","s":"The young skater gave a flawless performance and received full marks from every judge at the competition.","t":"這位年輕的滑冰選手表現完美無瑕，在比賽中獲得每位評審的滿分。"},{"w":"flawed","p":"adj.","d":"having mistakes or weak points","c":"有缺陷的","s":"The study was flawed because the scientists only asked twenty people, so nobody trusted its results.","t":"這項研究有缺陷，因為科學家只問了二十個人，所以沒人相信它的結果。"},{"w":"a fatal flaw","p":"n.phr.","d":"a weakness that causes complete failure","c":"致命的缺點","s":"Pride was a fatal flaw in the king's character, and it finally led to the loss of his whole kingdom.","t":"驕傲是這位國王性格中致命的缺點，最終導致他失去整個王國。"},{"w":"flourish","p":"v.","d":"to grow or develop well; to be successful","c":"繁榮；茁壯","s":"Small coffee shops began to flourish in the old street after the city turned it into a walking area for tourists.","t":"市政府把那條老街變成觀光徒步區後，小咖啡店開始在那裡蓬勃發展。","h":1},{"w":"flourish","p":"n.","d":"a confident, showy movement","c":"誇張的動作；炫耀的姿態","s":"The magician pulled the rabbit out of the hat with a flourish, and the children clapped and shouted for more.","t":"魔術師以一個誇張的動作把兔子從帽子裡拉出來，孩子們鼓掌大喊再來一個。"},{"w":"flourishing","p":"adj.","d":"growing and successful","c":"興旺的；繁榮的","s":"Thanks to the new high-speed rail station, Taichung now has a flourishing tourist business with many new hotels and restaurants.","t":"多虧新的高鐵站，台中現在有興旺的觀光業，開了許多新飯店和餐廳。"},{"w":"flunk","p":"v.","d":"to fail a test or course","c":"不及格；當掉","s":"If you flunk the math test again, you will have to take extra classes during the summer vacation.","t":"如果你數學考試又不及格，暑假就得上額外的課。","h":1},{"w":"flunk out","p":"v.phr.","d":"to be forced to leave school because of bad grades","c":"因成績差而退學","s":"My cousin played games all night instead of studying, and he flunked out of university after only one year.","t":"我表哥整晚打電動不讀書，才一年就被大學退學了。","a":"flunked out"},{"w":"flunk a test","p":"v.phr.","d":"to fail a test","c":"考試不及格","s":"Half the class flunked the test last week because the questions were much harder than anything in the textbook.","t":"上週全班有一半的人考試不及格，因為題目比課本裡的任何東西都難得多。","a":"flunked the test"},{"w":"foe","p":"n.","d":"an enemy","c":"敵人；仇敵","s":"In the final battle of the movie, the hero finally faces his old foe, who destroyed his village twenty years earlier.","t":"在電影的最後一戰裡，英雄終於面對二十年前摧毀他村莊的老仇敵。","h":1},{"w":"friend or foe","p":"phr.","d":"someone on your side or against you","c":"是敵是友","s":"In the dark forest it was hard to tell friend or foe, so the soldiers waited silently until morning came.","t":"在黑暗的森林裡很難分辨是敵是友，所以士兵們靜靜地等到天亮。"},{"w":"enemy","p":"n.","d":"a person or country that hates or fights you (= foe)","c":"敵人","s":"The two countries were bitter enemies for fifty years, but today their young people study and travel in each other's cities.","t":"這兩個國家曾是五十年的死敵，但今天他們的年輕人在彼此的城市讀書和旅行。","a":"enemies"},{"w":"folklore","p":"n.","d":"the traditional stories and customs of a group of people","c":"民間傳說；民俗","s":"According to local folklore, a dragon sleeps under the lake and wakes up whenever the village is in danger.","t":"根據當地的民間傳說，有一條龍睡在湖底，每當村莊有危險時就會醒來。","h":1},{"w":"folk","p":"n.","d":"people in general, especially ordinary people","c":"人們；民眾","s":"Country folk usually know their neighbors well, while people in big cities may never learn the names of those next door.","t":"鄉下人通常很了解鄰居，而大城市的人可能永遠不知道隔壁住的人叫什麼名字。"},{"w":"folk song","p":"n.phr.","d":"a traditional song of a people or region","c":"民謠","s":"My grandmother taught me a Taiwanese folk song that her own mother used to sing while working in the rice fields.","t":"我奶奶教我一首台灣民謠，那是她媽媽以前在稻田工作時常唱的。"},{"w":"folk tale","p":"n.phr.","d":"a traditional story passed down by ordinary people","c":"民間故事","s":"The famous folk tale about the cowherd and the weaver girl explains why Chinese people celebrate a festival on July seventh.","t":"著名的牛郎織女民間故事解釋了為什麼華人在七月七日慶祝節日。"},{"w":"formidable","p":"adj.","d":"very powerful or difficult, making you feel afraid or respectful","c":"強大的；令人敬畏的","s":"The champion team from Japan is a formidable opponent, but our players have trained hard and are not afraid of them.","t":"來自日本的冠軍隊是個強大的對手，但我們的球員努力訓練過，並不怕他們。","h":1},{"w":"a formidable task","p":"n.phr.","d":"a very difficult job","c":"艱鉅的任務","s":"Cleaning up the beach after the typhoon was a formidable task, but two hundred volunteers finished it in a single weekend.","t":"颱風後清理海灘是一項艱鉅的任務，但兩百名志工在一個週末內就完成了。"},{"w":"formidably","p":"adv.","d":"in a way that is very powerful or impressive","c":"強大地；令人敬畏地","s":"The new student is formidably smart; she solved in five minutes a problem that took the rest of us a whole class.","t":"這位新同學聰明得令人敬畏；我們其他人花了一整堂課的題目，她五分鐘就解出來了。"},{"w":"formulate","p":"v.","d":"to create a plan or idea carefully; to express something clearly","c":"制定；構想；表達","s":"Before the meeting, the team spent two days trying to formulate a plan that would cut costs without cutting jobs.","t":"會議前，團隊花了兩天試圖制定一個既能降低成本又不裁員的計畫。","h":1},{"w":"formula","p":"n.","d":"a set of letters or numbers that shows a rule; a method for doing something","c":"公式；化學式；配方","s":"Our chemistry teacher wrote the formula for water on the board and asked us why it has two hydrogen atoms.","t":"我們的化學老師在黑板上寫下水的化學式，問我們為什麼它有兩個氫原子。"},{"w":"formulation","p":"n.","d":"the act of creating a plan or idea; the way something is expressed","c":"制定；表述","s":"The formulation of the new school rules took three months because teachers, parents, and students all wanted a say.","t":"新校規的制定花了三個月，因為老師、家長和學生都想表達意見。"},{"w":"formulate a theory","p":"v.phr.","d":"to develop a scientific explanation","c":"提出理論","s":"Darwin spent more than twenty years collecting evidence before he was ready to formulate a theory about how species change.","t":"達爾文花了二十多年收集證據，才準備好提出關於物種如何改變的理論。"},{"w":"forsake, forsook, forsaken","p":"v.","d":"to leave someone or something forever; to give up","c":"拋棄；離棄；放棄","s":"The old fisherman refused to forsake the village where he was born, even after all his children moved to the city.","t":"這位老漁夫拒絕離棄他出生的村莊，即使他所有的孩子都搬去了城市。","a":"forsake","h":1},{"w":"forsaken","p":"adj.","d":"left alone and not cared for","c":"被遺棄的；孤獨的","s":"The forsaken puppy sat shivering by the road in the rain until a kind student picked it up and took it home.","t":"那隻被遺棄的小狗在雨中坐在路邊發抖，直到一位善良的學生把牠抱起來帶回家。"},{"w":"forsake one's principles","p":"v.phr.","d":"to stop following your own rules about right and wrong","c":"放棄原則","s":"The lawyer lost the big case because he would not forsake his principles and lie to the judge for his rich client.","t":"這位律師輸了大案子，因為他不願放棄原則，為富有的委託人對法官說謊。","a":"forsake his principles"},{"w":"forthcoming","p":"adj.","d":"happening or coming soon","c":"即將到來的","s":"Tickets for the band's forthcoming concert in Kaohsiung sold out in only ten minutes after they went on sale online.","t":"這個樂團即將舉行的高雄演唱會門票在網路開賣後十分鐘內就賣光了。","h":1},{"w":"forthcoming","p":"adj.","d":"willing to give information; friendly and helpful","c":"樂於提供資訊的；坦率的","s":"The manager was not very forthcoming about why the store was closing, so the workers learned the truth from the news.","t":"經理對店為什麼要關門不太願意透露，所以員工是從新聞上得知真相的。"},{"w":"come forth","p":"v.phr.","d":"to appear or offer information","c":"出現；站出來","s":"After the accident, several people came forth to tell the police exactly what they had seen on the street.","t":"事故發生後，有幾個人站出來告訴警方他們在街上看到的確切情況。","a":"came forth"},{"w":"upcoming","p":"adj.","d":"happening soon","c":"即將來臨的","s":"Students are already nervous about the upcoming exams, which begin in two weeks and cover the whole semester.","t":"學生們已經對即將到來的考試感到緊張，考試兩週後開始，範圍涵蓋整個學期。"},{"w":"fortify","p":"v.","d":"to make something stronger, especially against attack","c":"加強；設防","s":"The soldiers worked all night to fortify the castle walls because the enemy army was expected to arrive at dawn.","t":"士兵們整夜工作加固城牆，因為敵軍預計黎明時抵達。","h":1},{"w":"fortified","p":"adj.","d":"made stronger; with extra vitamins added","c":"強化的；設防的","s":"This breakfast cereal is fortified with iron and calcium, which is why many parents choose it for their growing children.","t":"這款早餐穀片添加了鐵和鈣，這就是為什麼許多家長為成長中的孩子選擇它。"},{"w":"fortress","p":"n.","d":"a large strong building built to defend a place","c":"堡壘；要塞","s":"The old stone fortress on the hill protected the harbor for three hundred years and is now a popular museum.","t":"山丘上的古老石造堡壘守護了港口三百年，現在是熱門的博物館。"},{"w":"fort","p":"n.","d":"a strong building used by soldiers","c":"堡壘；碉堡","s":"The children built a fort out of sofa cushions in the living room and refused to let their parents come in.","t":"孩子們在客廳用沙發墊搭了一座堡壘，不讓父母進去。"},{"w":"fowl","p":"n.","d":"a bird such as a chicken or duck that is kept for its meat or eggs","c":"家禽","s":"The farmer keeps chickens, ducks, and other fowl in a large yard behind his house and sells their eggs at the market.","t":"這位農夫在屋後的大院子裡養雞、鴨和其他家禽，並在市場賣牠們的蛋。","h":1},{"w":"poultry","p":"n.","d":"chickens, ducks, and other birds raised for food; their meat","c":"家禽；禽肉","s":"Doctors say poultry such as chicken is healthier than red meat, especially when it is baked instead of fried.","t":"醫生說雞肉等禽肉比紅肉健康，尤其是用烤的而不是炸的。"},{"w":"waterfowl","p":"n.","d":"birds such as ducks and geese that live on water","c":"水禽","s":"Every winter, thousands of waterfowl fly from the cold north to the wetlands in southern Taiwan to find food.","t":"每年冬天，成千上萬的水禽從寒冷的北方飛到台灣南部的濕地覓食。"},{"w":"fracture","p":"n.","d":"a break or crack in a bone or hard material","c":"骨折；裂縫","s":"The X-ray showed a small fracture in her wrist, so the doctor put her arm in a cast for six weeks.","t":"X光顯示她的手腕有一處小骨折，所以醫生幫她的手臂打了六週石膏。","h":1},{"w":"fracture","p":"v.","d":"to break or crack something hard","c":"使斷裂；使骨折","s":"He fell off his skateboard and managed to fracture two bones in his left leg, so he will miss the whole season.","t":"他從滑板上摔下來，左腿斷了兩根骨頭，所以整個賽季他都無法上場。"},{"w":"fractured","p":"adj.","d":"broken or cracked","c":"骨折的；破裂的","s":"The player left the field with a fractured finger, but he still came back to cheer for his teammates from the bench.","t":"這位球員帶著骨折的手指離場，但他仍回到板凳區為隊友加油。"},{"w":"fragile","p":"adj.","d":"easily broken or damaged","c":"易碎的；脆弱的","s":"Please handle the box with care because the glass cups inside are very fragile and were a gift from my grandmother.","t":"請小心搬這個箱子，因為裡面的玻璃杯非常易碎，而且是我奶奶送的禮物。"},{"w":"fragrance","p":"n.","d":"a pleasant smell","c":"香味；芳香","s":"The fragrance of jasmine filled the whole garden in the evening, and my grandmother loved to sit outside and enjoy it.","t":"傍晚時茉莉花的香味充滿整個花園，我奶奶喜歡坐在外面享受它。","h":1},{"w":"fragrant","p":"adj.","d":"having a pleasant smell","c":"芳香的","s":"My mother's kitchen was fragrant with the smell of fresh bread, so we all hurried downstairs before she even called us.","t":"媽媽的廚房裡飄著新鮮麵包的香味，所以她還沒叫我們，我們就全都趕快下樓了。","h":1},{"w":"fragrance","p":"n.","d":"a liquid with a pleasant smell; perfume","c":"香水","s":"She wears a light fragrance to work every day, but she avoids strong perfume because a coworker is allergic to it.","t":"她每天上班都擦淡淡的香水，但避免濃烈的香水，因為一位同事對它過敏。"},{"w":"perfume","p":"n.","d":"a liquid with a sweet smell that people put on their skin","c":"香水","s":"My father bought my mother a bottle of French perfume for their anniversary, and she wears it on special occasions.","t":"我爸爸為結婚紀念日買了一瓶法國香水給媽媽，她在特別場合會擦。"},{"w":"frantic","p":"adj.","d":"extremely worried or excited, so that you cannot think calmly","c":"瘋狂的；發狂似的","s":"The mother became frantic when she could not find her little son in the crowded night market and started calling his name.","t":"這位媽媽在擁擠的夜市找不到小兒子時變得發狂似的，開始大叫他的名字。","h":1},{"w":"frantically","p":"adv.","d":"in a very worried, hurried, and uncontrolled way","c":"瘋狂地；慌亂地","s":"With only ten minutes before the deadline, Tom typed frantically to finish the last page of his report.","t":"距離截止時間只剩十分鐘，湯姆瘋狂地打字，想完成報告的最後一頁。"},{"w":"a frantic search","p":"n.phr.","d":"a very hurried and worried attempt to find something","c":"慌亂的搜尋","s":"After a frantic search through every pocket and bag, I finally found my keys sitting on the kitchen table.","t":"慌亂地搜遍每個口袋和包包後，我終於發現鑰匙就放在廚房桌上。"},{"w":"freak","p":"n.","d":"a person who is extremely interested in something; a very strange person or thing","c":"狂熱者；怪人；怪事","s":"My brother is a fitness freak who goes to the gym at five every morning and counts every calorie he eats.","t":"我哥哥是個健身狂，每天早上五點就去健身房，而且計算吃下的每一卡路里。","h":1},{"w":"freak out","p":"v.phr.","d":"to become very angry, scared, or upset","c":"嚇壞；抓狂","s":"My mother will freak out if she sees the broken vase, so let's clean up the pieces and tell her the truth calmly.","t":"如果媽媽看到打破的花瓶會抓狂，所以我們先把碎片清乾淨，再冷靜地告訴她實話。"},{"w":"freak","p":"adj.","d":"very unusual and unexpected","c":"反常的；離奇的","s":"A freak snowstorm hit the city in April, and schools closed for two days because nobody had winter tires on their cars.","t":"四月一場反常的暴風雪襲擊這座城市，學校關閉兩天，因為沒有人的車裝了雪胎。"},{"w":"freaky","p":"adj.","d":"strange and a little frightening","c":"怪異的；嚇人的","s":"The old house made freaky noises at night, so my little sister refused to sleep there without the lights on.","t":"那棟老房子晚上會發出怪異的聲音，所以我妹妹不開燈就不肯睡在那裡。"},{"w":"freeway","p":"n.","d":"a wide road for fast traffic with no traffic lights","c":"高速公路","s":"Traffic on the freeway was so heavy before the holiday that the two-hour drive to Taichung took us almost five hours.","t":"假期前高速公路的車流量太大，原本兩小時到台中的車程花了我們將近五小時。","h":1},{"w":"highway","p":"n.","d":"a main road between towns or cities","c":"公路；幹道","s":"The new highway along the east coast offers beautiful views of the Pacific Ocean, so many people drive slowly to enjoy them.","t":"東海岸的新公路可以看到太平洋的美景，所以許多人開得很慢來欣賞。"},{"w":"expressway","p":"n.","d":"a wide road for fast traffic, like a freeway","c":"快速道路","s":"Taking the expressway saves about twenty minutes, but you have to pay a toll each time you use it.","t":"走快速道路可以省大約二十分鐘，但每次使用都得付過路費。"},{"w":"free","p":"adj.","d":"costing nothing; not controlled or limited","c":"免費的；自由的","s":"Admission to the park is free on weekdays, but on weekends visitors have to buy a ticket at the gate.","t":"平日公園免費入場，但週末遊客必須在門口買票。"},{"w":"friction","p":"n.","d":"the force that makes it hard for one surface to slide over another","c":"摩擦力","s":"Rubbing your hands together creates friction, which is why they start to feel warm after a few seconds.","t":"雙手互搓會產生摩擦力，這就是為什麼幾秒鐘後它們會開始感覺溫暖。","h":1},{"w":"friction","p":"n.","d":"disagreement or anger between people","c":"摩擦；不和","s":"There has been some friction between the two roommates ever since one of them started bringing friends home late at night.","t":"自從其中一人開始深夜帶朋友回家後，這兩位室友之間就有了一些摩擦。"},{"w":"cause friction","p":"v.phr.","d":"to make people argue or feel angry with each other","c":"引起摩擦","s":"Sharing one bathroom among five people causes friction every morning, especially when someone takes a long shower.","t":"五個人共用一間浴室每天早上都會引起摩擦，尤其當有人洗澡洗很久的時候。","a":"causes friction"},{"w":"fume","p":"v.","d":"to be very angry, often without saying much","c":"生悶氣；發怒","s":"My father sat in the car and fumed silently for twenty minutes after another driver took the parking space he had been waiting for.","t":"另一位駕駛搶走了爸爸等很久的停車位後，他坐在車裡默默生悶氣二十分鐘。","a":"fumed","h":1},{"w":"fumes","p":"n.","d":"strong, unpleasant, or dangerous gas or smoke","c":"煙霧；廢氣","s":"The fumes from the old bus were so thick and black that people on the sidewalk covered their noses as it passed.","t":"那輛老舊公車排出的廢氣又濃又黑，經過時人行道上的人都摀住鼻子。"},{"w":"exhaust fumes","p":"n.phr.","d":"the waste gas that comes out of a car engine","c":"汽車廢氣","s":"Never run a car engine inside a closed garage, because the exhaust fumes can make you sick or even kill you.","t":"絕對不要在密閉的車庫裡發動汽車引擎，因為廢氣會讓你生病甚至喪命。"},{"w":"fury","p":"n.","d":"very strong anger","c":"狂怒；暴怒","s":"The coach could not hide his fury when the player ignored the plan and lost the ball in the final minute.","t":"當球員無視戰術並在最後一分鐘丟球時，教練無法掩飾他的狂怒。","h":1},{"w":"furious","p":"adj.","d":"extremely angry","c":"狂怒的","s":"My mother was furious when she found out that I had lied to her about where I went last Saturday night.","t":"當媽媽發現我對上週六晚上去哪裡說了謊時，她非常生氣。"},{"w":"furiously","p":"adv.","d":"in a very angry way; very fast and with a lot of energy","c":"狂怒地；猛烈地","s":"The dog barked furiously at the mailman every morning, but it never actually tried to bite anyone.","t":"這隻狗每天早上對郵差狂吠，但牠從來沒有真的想咬人。"},{"w":"fly into a fury","p":"v.phr.","d":"to suddenly become extremely angry","c":"勃然大怒","s":"The customer flew into a fury when the waiter spilled soup on his new suit, and the manager had to come and calm him down.","t":"服務生把湯灑在顧客的新西裝上時，顧客勃然大怒，經理不得不過來安撫他。","a":"flew into a fury"},{"w":"fuse","p":"n.","d":"a small safety part that breaks the electric current when there is too much electricity","c":"保險絲","s":"When all the lights suddenly went out, Dad checked the box by the door and found that a fuse had blown.","t":"所有燈突然熄滅時，爸爸檢查門邊的電箱，發現一根保險絲燒斷了。","h":1},{"w":"fuse","p":"v.","d":"to join two things together, often by heating them","c":"熔合；融合","s":"The artist used heat to fuse pieces of colored glass together, creating a beautiful window for the church.","t":"這位藝術家用高溫把彩色玻璃片熔合在一起，為教堂創作了一扇美麗的窗戶。"},{"w":"blow a fuse","p":"v.phr.","d":"to suddenly become very angry; to make a fuse break","c":"大發雷霆；燒斷保險絲","s":"Dad blew a fuse when he saw the phone bill, because my sister had spent hours calling her friend in Canada.","t":"爸爸看到電話帳單時大發雷霆，因為我妹妹花了好幾個小時打電話給她在加拿大的朋友。","a":"blew a fuse"},{"w":"fusion","p":"n.","d":"the joining of two different things into one","c":"融合；熔合","s":"The restaurant is famous for its fusion food, which mixes Taiwanese flavors with Italian cooking in surprising ways.","t":"這家餐廳以融合料理聞名，以令人驚喜的方式把台灣風味和義大利烹調結合在一起。"},{"w":"fuss","p":"n.","d":"too much worry or excitement about something unimportant","c":"大驚小怪；小題大作","s":"My grandmother makes a big fuss every time I visit, cooking ten dishes even though I always tell her not to.","t":"每次我去看奶奶她都會大費周章，即使我總是告訴她不用，她還是煮十道菜。","h":1},{"w":"fuss","p":"v.","d":"to worry or pay too much attention to small things","c":"大驚小怪；忙亂","s":"Stop fussing over my hair, Mom; it is only a school picture, and nobody will notice if it is a little messy.","t":"媽，別再為我的頭髮忙東忙西了；只是學校照片而已，有點亂也沒人會注意。","a":"fussing"},{"w":"make a fuss about","p":"v.phr.","d":"to complain or worry loudly about something small","c":"對…小題大作","s":"There is no need to make a fuss about a few drops of rain; we can still walk to the restaurant in five minutes.","t":"不需要為幾滴雨小題大作；我們還是可以五分鐘走到餐廳。"},{"w":"fussy","p":"adj.","d":"hard to please; caring too much about small details","c":"挑剔的；難以取悅的","s":"My little brother is a fussy eater who refuses to touch any vegetable that is green or has a strange shape.","t":"我弟弟吃東西很挑剔，拒絕碰任何綠色或形狀奇怪的蔬菜。"},{"w":"gallop","p":"v.","d":"to run very fast, as a horse does","c":"飛奔；疾馳","s":"The horses began to gallop across the open field as soon as the riders gave them a gentle kick.","t":"騎士輕輕一踢，馬兒就開始在開闊的田野上飛奔。","h":1},{"w":"gallop","p":"n.","d":"the fastest way a horse runs","c":"疾馳；飛奔","s":"The cowboy rode off at a gallop to warn the town that the river was rising and would soon flood the bridge.","t":"牛仔飛奔而去，警告鎮上的人河水正在上漲，很快就會淹沒橋梁。"},{"w":"at a gallop","p":"phr.","d":"very quickly","c":"飛快地","s":"The waiter cleared the tables at a gallop because fifty hungry tourists were waiting outside the small restaurant.","t":"服務生飛快地收拾桌子，因為五十名飢餓的觀光客正在小餐館外面等著。"},{"w":"gangster","p":"n.","d":"a member of a group of violent criminals","c":"歹徒；黑幫分子","s":"In the movie, a young gangster decides to leave his violent life behind after his best friend is killed in a street fight.","t":"電影裡，一位年輕的黑幫分子在摯友死於街頭鬥毆後，決定離開暴力的生活。","h":1},{"w":"gang","p":"n.","d":"a group of young people who cause trouble; a group of criminals","c":"幫派；一幫人","s":"The police arrested five members of a gang that had stolen more than thirty motorcycles in the area this year.","t":"警方逮捕了一個幫派的五名成員，他們今年在這個地區偷了三十多輛機車。"},{"w":"gang up on","p":"v.phr.","d":"to join together against one person","c":"聯合起來對付","s":"It is unfair when several students gang up on one classmate just because he is new and speaks with a different accent.","t":"幾個學生只因為一位同學是新來的、口音不同就聯合起來欺負他，這是不公平的。"},{"w":"garment","p":"n.","d":"a piece of clothing","c":"衣服；服裝","s":"Wash this garment in cold water only, because hot water will make the colors run and the wool shrink.","t":"這件衣服只能用冷水洗，因為熱水會讓顏色暈開、羊毛縮水。","h":1},{"w":"garment factory","p":"n.phr.","d":"a factory where clothes are made","c":"成衣工廠","s":"My grandmother worked in a garment factory for thirty years, sewing shirts that were sold in department stores in America.","t":"我奶奶在成衣工廠工作了三十年，縫製在美國百貨公司販售的襯衫。"},{"w":"the garment industry","p":"n.phr.","d":"the business of making and selling clothes","c":"服裝業","s":"Many people in the small town used to work in the garment industry, but most factories moved overseas twenty years ago.","t":"這個小鎮許多人過去在服裝業工作，但大多數工廠二十年前都搬到國外去了。"},{"w":"clothing","p":"n.","d":"clothes in general","c":"衣物；服裝","s":"The charity collects warm clothing every November and gives it to homeless people before the cold weather arrives.","t":"這個慈善機構每年十一月收集保暖衣物，在寒冷天氣來臨前送給無家可歸的人。"}]},{"unit":16,"theme":"gauge – handicap","cards":[{"w":"gauge","p":"n.","d":"a tool that measures the amount or size of something","c":"測量儀器；量表","s":"The fuel gauge on the dashboard showed that the tank was almost empty, so we stopped at the next gas station.","t":"儀表板上的油量計顯示油箱幾乎空了，所以我們在下一個加油站停了下來。","h":1},{"w":"gauge","p":"v.","d":"to judge or measure something carefully","c":"評估；測量","s":"It is hard to gauge how the students feel about the new schedule until we ask them directly in class.","t":"在我們在課堂上直接問學生之前，很難評估他們對新時間表的感受。"},{"w":"gauge sb's reaction","p":"v.phr.","d":"to watch someone to find out how they feel about something","c":"評估某人的反應","s":"Before announcing the price increase, the manager tried to gauge their reaction by showing the plan to a few loyal customers first.","t":"在宣布漲價之前，經理先把計畫給幾位忠實顧客看，試著評估他們的反應。","a":"gauge their reaction"},{"w":"pressure gauge","p":"n.phr.","d":"a tool that shows how much pressure there is in a tire or a machine","c":"壓力計","s":"The mechanic checked the tires with a pressure gauge and told us the back wheels needed more air before the long trip.","t":"技工用壓力計檢查輪胎，並告訴我們長途旅行前後輪需要再打一些氣。"},{"w":"gay","p":"adj.","d":"attracted to people of the same sex","c":"同性戀的","s":"My cousin is gay, and his family welcomed his partner warmly when they came home for the New Year dinner.","t":"我表哥是同性戀，他和伴侶回家吃年夜飯時，家人熱情地歡迎了他的伴侶。","h":1},{"w":"gay","p":"adj.","d":"(old use) happy, bright, and full of fun","c":"（舊式用法）快樂的；鮮豔的","s":"In the old folk song, the children dance with gay hearts around the tree, and everyone sings happily under the bright moon.","t":"在那首古老的民謠裡，孩子們懷著快樂的心圍著樹跳舞，大家在明亮的月光下開心地唱歌。"},{"w":"gay rights","p":"n.phr.","d":"equal rights for gay people","c":"同志權益","s":"Many young people joined the march to support gay rights, and they carried colorful flags through the center of the city.","t":"許多年輕人加入遊行以支持同志權益，他們舉著彩色旗幟穿過市中心。"},{"w":"gay marriage","p":"n.phr.","d":"marriage between two people of the same sex","c":"同性婚姻","s":"Taiwan became the first place in Asia to make gay marriage legal in 2019, and many couples got married that very week.","t":"台灣在 2019 年成為亞洲第一個讓同性婚姻合法的地方，許多情侶就在那一週結婚了。"},{"w":"geographical","p":"adj.","d":"connected with geography or the position of places","c":"地理的","s":"Taiwan's geographical position between Japan and the Philippines makes it an important stop for ships and planes crossing the Pacific.","t":"台灣位於日本和菲律賓之間的地理位置，使它成為橫越太平洋的船隻和飛機的重要停靠點。","h":1},{"w":"geography","p":"n.","d":"the study of the earth's land, seas, weather, and people","c":"地理；地理學","s":"In geography class this week, we learned the names of all the rivers in Taiwan and where they begin in the mountains.","t":"這週的地理課，我們學了台灣所有河流的名稱，以及它們在山裡的源頭。"},{"w":"geographic","p":"adj.","d":"connected with geography (same as geographical)","c":"地理的","s":"The map shows the geographic features of the island, such as its high mountains in the center and its flat plains in the west.","t":"這張地圖顯示了這座島的地理特徵，例如中央的高山和西部的平原。"},{"w":"geographically","p":"adv.","d":"in a way that is connected with where places are","c":"在地理上","s":"Geographically, Kaohsiung is closer to the Philippines than to Japan, which is one reason the port has so many ships from Southeast Asia.","t":"在地理上，高雄離菲律賓比離日本近，這是這個港口有這麼多東南亞船隻的原因之一。","a":"Geographically"},{"w":"geometry","p":"n.","d":"the part of math that studies shapes, lines, and angles","c":"幾何學","s":"In geometry class, we learned how to find the area of a triangle and why its angles always add up to 180 degrees.","t":"在幾何課上，我們學到如何算三角形的面積，以及為什麼它的內角和總是 180 度。","h":1},{"w":"geometric","p":"adj.","d":"made of regular shapes like circles, squares, and triangles","c":"幾何的","s":"The floor of the old temple is covered with geometric patterns, and the circles and squares were made from tiny colored stones.","t":"這座古老寺廟的地板佈滿幾何圖案，那些圓形和方形是用細小的彩色石頭拼成的。"},{"w":"geometrical","p":"adj.","d":"connected with geometry; made of simple shapes","c":"幾何（學）的","s":"The artist used simple geometrical shapes like cubes and triangles to build a city of paper that filled the whole gallery.","t":"這位藝術家用立方體和三角形等簡單的幾何形狀，做出一座佈滿整個展廳的紙城市。"},{"w":"glacier","p":"n.","d":"a very large mass of ice that moves slowly down a mountain","c":"冰河；冰川","s":"Scientists say the glacier in the mountains has become much smaller over the past fifty years because the summers are getting warmer.","t":"科學家說，由於夏天越來越暖，山上的冰河在過去五十年縮小了很多。","h":1},{"w":"glacial","p":"adj.","d":"connected with glaciers; extremely cold","c":"冰河的；冰冷的","s":"The glacial lake was so cold that nobody dared to swim in it, even on the hottest day of August.","t":"這座冰河湖冷到沒有人敢下去游泳，即使在八月最熱的那一天也一樣。"},{"w":"melting glaciers","p":"n.phr.","d":"glaciers that are turning into water because of warmer weather","c":"融化的冰河","s":"Melting glaciers are causing sea levels to rise, so low islands in the Pacific may disappear within this century if nothing changes.","t":"融化的冰河正使海平面上升，所以如果情況不改變，太平洋上的低矮島嶼可能在本世紀內消失。","a":"Melting glaciers"},{"w":"glamorous","p":"adj.","d":"attractive and exciting in a rich, beautiful way","c":"迷人的；富有魅力的","s":"Being a movie star looks glamorous on TV, but the actors often work sixteen hours a day and travel far away from their families.","t":"當電影明星在電視上看起來很迷人，但演員們常常一天工作十六小時，還要遠離家人到各地去。","h":1},{"w":"glamour","p":"n.","d":"the attractive and exciting quality that some people, places, or jobs have","c":"魅力；光彩","s":"Many teenagers are attracted by the glamour of the fashion world, but few of them know how hard the models really work.","t":"許多青少年被時尚界的魅力吸引，但很少人知道模特兒工作其實有多辛苦。","h":1},{"w":"glamorize","p":"v.","d":"to make something seem more attractive or exciting than it really is","c":"美化；使更有吸引力","s":"Some movies glamorize smoking by showing cool heroes with cigarettes, so health groups ask directors to stop doing this.","t":"有些電影讓帥氣的英雄抽著菸來美化吸菸，所以健康團體要求導演不要再這麼做。"},{"w":"glamorously","p":"adv.","d":"in an attractive and exciting way","c":"迷人地；華麗地","s":"The singer was glamorously dressed in a long silver gown, and every camera in the room turned toward her at once.","t":"這位歌手華麗地穿著銀色長禮服，房間裡每台相機立刻都轉向了她。"},{"w":"gleam","p":"n.","d":"a small, soft light that shines for a short time","c":"微光；閃光","s":"Through the fog, the sailors saw the faint gleam of the lighthouse, and they knew the harbor was finally near.","t":"穿過霧氣，水手們看見燈塔微弱的光芒，他們知道港口終於近了。","h":1},{"w":"gleam","p":"v.","d":"to shine softly; to reflect light","c":"閃爍；發微光","s":"The kitchen floor gleamed after Mom spent the whole afternoon cleaning it, so we took off our shoes before going in.","t":"媽媽花了整個下午清掃後，廚房地板閃閃發亮，所以我們進去前先脫了鞋。","a":"gleamed"},{"w":"gleaming","p":"adj.","d":"shining brightly, usually because it is clean or new","c":"閃閃發亮的","s":"He parked his gleaming new motorcycle in front of the school, and all his classmates ran out to take a look.","t":"他把他閃閃發亮的新機車停在學校前面，所有同學都跑出來看。"},{"w":"a gleam in sb's eye","p":"n.phr.","d":"a look of excitement or a secret idea in someone's eyes","c":"眼中的光芒（興奮或有想法）","s":"When Grandpa talks about his first trip to Japan, there is always a gleam in his eye, and his stories seem to go on forever.","t":"每當爺爺談起他第一次去日本的旅行，他眼中總是有一道光芒，他的故事似乎永遠講不完。","a":"a gleam in his eye"},{"w":"glide","p":"v.","d":"to move smoothly and quietly, often through the air or over water","c":"滑行；滑翔","s":"The swans glided across the quiet lake without making a sound, and the tourists on the bank took photo after photo.","t":"天鵝無聲地滑過平靜的湖面，岸上的遊客一張接一張地拍照。","a":"glided","h":1},{"w":"glide","p":"n.","d":"a smooth, quiet movement","c":"滑行；滑翔","s":"The eagle's long glide over the valley lasted almost a minute, and it never once moved its wide wings.","t":"老鷹在山谷上空的長距離滑翔持續了近一分鐘，牠寬大的翅膀一次也沒有動。"},{"w":"glider","p":"n.","d":"a light aircraft with no engine","c":"滑翔機","s":"A glider has no engine, so the pilot must use the rising warm air to stay in the sky for a long time.","t":"滑翔機沒有引擎，所以駕駛員必須利用上升的暖空氣才能長時間留在空中。"},{"w":"gliding","p":"n.","d":"the sport of flying in a glider","c":"滑翔運動","s":"My uncle took up gliding after he retired, and now he flies over the hills every sunny weekend with his club.","t":"我叔叔退休後開始玩滑翔，現在每個晴朗的週末他都和俱樂部一起飛越山丘。"},{"w":"glitter","p":"v.","d":"to shine with many small flashes of light","c":"閃閃發光","s":"The sea glittered in the morning sun as our boat left the harbor, and everyone on deck felt excited about the trip.","t":"我們的船離開港口時，大海在晨光中閃閃發光，甲板上每個人都對這趟旅行感到興奮。","a":"glittered","h":1},{"w":"glitter","p":"n.","d":"very small shiny pieces used for decoration","c":"亮片；閃光","s":"The children covered their holiday cards with gold glitter, and tiny shiny pieces were still on the floor a week later.","t":"孩子們在節日卡片上灑滿了金色亮片，一週後地板上仍然有細小閃亮的碎片。"},{"w":"glittering","p":"adj.","d":"shining brightly with many small lights; very successful","c":"閃閃發亮的；輝煌的","s":"The actress walked down the red carpet in a glittering dress covered with thousands of small crystals.","t":"這位女演員穿著一件綴滿數千顆小水晶的閃亮禮服走上紅地毯。"},{"w":"glittery","p":"adj.","d":"covered with glitter; shiny","c":"閃亮的","s":"My little sister chose a glittery pink backpack for school because she loves anything that shines in the light.","t":"我妹妹選了一個閃亮的粉紅色書包上學，因為她喜歡任何在光線下會發亮的東西。"},{"w":"gloom","p":"n.","d":"a feeling of sadness and no hope; darkness","c":"憂鬱；幽暗","s":"After the team lost the final match, a heavy gloom hung over the whole school for the rest of the week.","t":"球隊輸掉決賽後，那一週剩下的日子整個學校都籠罩在沉重的憂鬱之中。","h":1},{"w":"gloomy","p":"adj.","d":"dark and sad; without hope","c":"陰暗的；憂鬱的","s":"The weather has been gloomy and rainy for ten days, so everybody in the office is dreaming of a sunny holiday.","t":"天氣已經陰沉多雨十天了，所以辦公室裡每個人都夢想著一個陽光普照的假期。"},{"w":"gloomily","p":"adv.","d":"in a sad way without hope","c":"憂鬱地；沮喪地","s":"He stared gloomily at his test paper, because he had studied for weeks and still failed by only two points.","t":"他沮喪地盯著考卷，因為他讀了好幾週的書，卻還是以兩分之差不及格。"},{"w":"doom and gloom","p":"n.phr.","d":"a feeling that everything is bad and will get worse","c":"悲觀的氣氛；前景黯淡","s":"The news is full of doom and gloom these days, so my grandmother prefers to watch cooking shows instead.","t":"這些日子新聞充滿悲觀黯淡的消息，所以我奶奶寧願改看烹飪節目。"},{"w":"goalkeeper","p":"n.","d":"the player who stands in the goal and stops the ball","c":"守門員","s":"The goalkeeper jumped to the left and stopped the ball with one hand, and the whole stadium cheered loudly.","t":"守門員向左撲出，單手擋下了球，整個體育場大聲歡呼。","h":1},{"w":"goal","p":"n.","d":"something you want to do in the future; a point in a game","c":"目標；進球","s":"She set herself the goal of reading twenty English books this year, and she has already finished twelve of them.","t":"她為自己訂下今年讀二十本英文書的目標，而且已經讀完十二本了。"},{"w":"score a goal","p":"v.phr.","d":"to get a point by putting the ball into the goal","c":"進球；得分","s":"Our captain scored a goal in the last minute of the game, so we won the city championship for the first time.","t":"我們的隊長在比賽最後一分鐘進了一球，所以我們第一次贏得市冠軍。","a":"scored a goal"},{"w":"goalpost","p":"n.","d":"one of the two posts that form the sides of a goal","c":"球門柱","s":"The ball hit the goalpost and bounced back onto the field, so the striker missed his chance to win the game.","t":"球打到球門柱彈回場內，所以前鋒錯過了贏得比賽的機會。"},{"w":"keeper","p":"n.","d":"a goalkeeper; a person who takes care of animals or a place","c":"守門員；看守者","s":"The zoo keeper feeds the penguins twice a day, and visitors love watching the birds rush toward the fish.","t":"動物園的飼育員每天餵企鵝兩次，遊客喜歡看這些鳥兒衝向魚的樣子。"},{"w":"goodwill","p":"n.","d":"friendly and helpful feelings toward other people","c":"善意；友好","s":"The two countries exchanged gifts as a sign of goodwill, and both leaders promised to work together on trade.","t":"兩國交換禮物作為善意的表示，兩位領導人都承諾在貿易上合作。","h":1},{"w":"a gesture of goodwill","p":"n.phr.","d":"something you do to show you want to be friendly","c":"善意的表示","s":"The company sent free tickets to the unhappy customers as a gesture of goodwill, hoping they would come back to the theater again.","t":"公司寄免費票給不滿的顧客作為善意的表示，希望他們會再回到這家戲院。"},{"w":"ill will","p":"n.phr.","d":"unfriendly feelings; the wish to hurt someone","c":"惡意；敵意","s":"Although the two neighbors argued about the fence last year, they say there is no ill will between them now.","t":"雖然這兩位鄰居去年為了圍籬吵過架，但他們說現在彼此之間已經沒有敵意了。"},{"w":"goodwill ambassador","p":"n.phr.","d":"a famous person who helps a charity or an organization","c":"親善大使","s":"The famous singer was named a goodwill ambassador for the children's charity and visited schools in several poor countries.","t":"這位知名歌手被任命為兒童慈善機構的親善大使，並到幾個貧窮國家的學校訪問。"},{"w":"gorilla","p":"n.","d":"the largest kind of ape, with black hair, living in Africa","c":"大猩猩","s":"The gorilla is the largest of all the apes, and an adult male can weigh more than two hundred kilograms.","t":"大猩猩是所有猿類中最大的，成年雄性體重可以超過兩百公斤。","h":1},{"w":"ape","p":"n.","d":"a large animal like a monkey but with no tail","c":"猿","s":"Unlike monkeys, an ape such as a chimpanzee has no tail, and it can walk on two legs for a short distance.","t":"和猴子不同，像黑猩猩這樣的猿沒有尾巴，而且可以用兩條腿走一小段路。"},{"w":"primate","p":"n.","d":"any animal of the group that includes humans, apes, and monkeys","c":"靈長類動物","s":"Humans, monkeys, and gorillas all belong to the group of animals called primates, which have large brains and hands that can grab things.","t":"人類、猴子和大猩猩都屬於叫做靈長類的動物群，它們有大腦袋和能抓握東西的手。","a":"primates"},{"w":"gospel","p":"n.","d":"the teachings of Jesus; one of the four books about his life in the Bible","c":"福音；福音書","s":"The priest read a story from the gospel about a man who helped a stranger lying hurt on the road.","t":"神父從福音書中讀了一個故事，講一個人幫助了躺在路上受傷的陌生人。","h":1},{"w":"gospel music","p":"n.phr.","d":"a kind of strong, joyful religious music","c":"福音音樂","s":"The choir sang gospel music with such energy that even people walking past the church stopped to listen and clap.","t":"合唱團充滿活力地唱著福音音樂，連經過教堂的路人都停下來聆聽並鼓掌。"},{"w":"take sth as gospel","p":"v.phr.","d":"to believe something is completely true without checking","c":"把…當作真理","s":"Many people take as gospel whatever the famous doctor says on TV, but even experts can make mistakes sometimes.","t":"許多人把那位名醫在電視上說的任何話都當作真理，但即使是專家有時也會犯錯。","a":"take as gospel"},{"w":"the gospel truth","p":"n.phr.","d":"something that is completely true","c":"絕對的真話","s":"I promise this is the gospel truth: I saw the teacher dancing in the empty classroom when she thought nobody was watching.","t":"我保證這是千真萬確的事：我看到老師以為沒人在看時，在空教室裡跳舞。"},{"w":"grapefruit","p":"n.","d":"a large round yellow fruit with a sour taste","c":"葡萄柚","s":"My mother eats half a grapefruit every morning because she believes its sour juice helps her stay slim and healthy.","t":"我媽媽每天早上吃半顆葡萄柚，因為她相信它酸酸的果汁能幫助她保持苗條健康。","h":1},{"w":"grape","p":"n.","d":"a small green or purple fruit that grows in bunches","c":"葡萄","s":"We picked bunches of purple grapes at the farm in Miaoli, and the farmer taught us how to make juice from them.","t":"我們在苗栗的農場摘了一串串紫色葡萄，農夫還教我們怎麼用它們做果汁。","a":"grapes"},{"w":"citrus","p":"adj.","d":"belonging to the group of fruits like oranges and lemons","c":"柑橘類的","s":"Oranges, lemons, and grapefruits are all citrus fruits, and they are rich in vitamin C, which helps fight colds.","t":"橘子、檸檬和葡萄柚都是柑橘類水果，它們富含維生素 C，有助於對抗感冒。"},{"w":"grapevine","p":"n.","d":"the plant that grapes grow on; (hear sth on the grapevine) news passed from person to person","c":"葡萄藤；小道消息","s":"I heard on the grapevine that our English teacher is getting married next month, but she has not told the class yet.","t":"我聽到小道消息說我們的英文老師下個月要結婚了，但她還沒告訴班上。"},{"w":"graze","p":"v.","d":"(of animals) to eat grass in a field","c":"吃草","s":"Dozens of cows graze on the green hills behind the farmhouse, and the farmer checks on them twice a day.","t":"幾十頭牛在農舍後面的綠色山坡上吃草，農夫每天去看牠們兩次。","h":1},{"w":"graze","p":"v.","d":"to touch or rub something lightly while passing; to scrape the skin","c":"擦過；擦傷","s":"The bullet only grazed the soldier's arm, so he was able to walk back to the camp without any help.","t":"子彈只擦過那名士兵的手臂，所以他能夠不靠任何幫助走回營地。","a":"grazed"},{"w":"graze","p":"n.","d":"a small injury where the skin has been rubbed off","c":"擦傷","s":"She fell off her bike on the gravel road and got a painful graze on her knee, but luckily nothing was broken.","t":"她在碎石路上從腳踏車摔下來，膝蓋上有一道疼痛的擦傷，但幸好沒有骨折。"},{"w":"grazing land","p":"n.phr.","d":"land where farm animals eat grass","c":"牧草地","s":"The government bought the valley to protect it as grazing land for the local sheep farmers, who had used it for centuries.","t":"政府買下這個山谷，把它保護為當地牧羊人的牧草地，他們已經使用這裡好幾個世紀了。"},{"w":"grease","p":"n.","d":"a thick oily substance, used on machines or left by cooking","c":"油脂；潤滑油","s":"After fixing the bicycle chain, his hands were covered in black grease that took ten minutes of scrubbing to wash off.","t":"修好腳踏車鏈條後，他的手上滿是黑色油污，花了十分鐘用力刷才洗掉。","h":1},{"w":"grease","p":"v.","d":"to put oil or fat on something","c":"塗油；上潤滑油","s":"Remember to grease the baking pan with butter before you pour in the batter, or the cake will stick to the bottom.","t":"記得在倒入麵糊前先用奶油塗抹烤盤，否則蛋糕會黏在底部。"},{"w":"greasy","p":"adj.","d":"covered with grease or oil; containing too much oil","c":"油膩的","s":"The fries at that stand were so greasy that the paper bag was almost transparent by the time we got home.","t":"那個攤子的薯條太油膩了，等我們到家時紙袋幾乎變成透明的了。"},{"w":"elbow grease","p":"n.phr.","d":"hard physical work, especially cleaning or polishing","c":"費力的擦洗工作","s":"The old pot was black with burnt rice, but with some soap and a lot of elbow grease, Dad made it shine like new.","t":"那個舊鍋子被燒焦的米飯染黑了，但靠著肥皂和大量費力的擦洗，爸爸把它刷得像新的一樣亮。"},{"w":"groan","p":"v.","d":"to make a long, low sound because of pain or unhappiness","c":"呻吟；哀嘆","s":"The students groaned loudly when the teacher announced a surprise test, but they quickly took out their pencils.","t":"老師宣布臨時考試時，學生們大聲哀嘆，但他們很快就拿出了鉛筆。","a":"groaned","h":1},{"w":"groan","p":"n.","d":"a long, low sound of pain or unhappiness","c":"呻吟聲；哀嘆聲","s":"We heard a low groan from under the fallen tree, and the firefighters rushed over to pull the man out.","t":"我們聽到倒下的樹底下傳來低低的呻吟聲，消防員衝過去把那個人拉了出來。"},{"w":"groan with pain","p":"v.phr.","d":"to make a low sound because something hurts","c":"痛得呻吟","s":"The player groaned with pain as the doctor touched his swollen ankle, and the coach knew he could not finish the game.","t":"醫生碰到他腫脹的腳踝時，那名球員痛得呻吟，教練知道他無法打完這場比賽了。","a":"groaned with pain"},{"w":"growl","p":"v.","d":"(of a dog or other animal) to make a low, angry sound","c":"低吼；咆哮","s":"The dog began to growl when the stranger came too close to the gate, so the man quickly stepped back.","t":"當陌生人太靠近大門時，那隻狗開始低吼，所以那個人很快就退後了。","h":1},{"w":"growl","p":"n.","d":"a low, angry sound","c":"低吼聲","s":"A deep growl came from the dark cave, and the hikers decided it was time to head back down the mountain.","t":"黑暗的洞穴裡傳來一聲低沉的吼聲，登山客們決定該下山了。"},{"w":"growl at","p":"v.phr.","d":"to speak to someone in a low, angry voice","c":"對…咆哮","s":"The angry boss growled at anyone who knocked on his door that morning, so we waited until after lunch to ask our question.","t":"那天早上生氣的老闆對任何敲他門的人咆哮，所以我們等到午餐後才去問問題。","a":"growled at"},{"w":"grumble","p":"v.","d":"to complain in a quiet, unhappy way","c":"發牢騷；抱怨","s":"My grandfather likes to grumble about the price of vegetables, but he still buys fresh ones at the market every day.","t":"我爺爺喜歡抱怨菜價，但他還是每天到市場買新鮮的蔬菜。","h":1},{"w":"grumble","p":"n.","d":"a quiet complaint","c":"牢騷；抱怨","s":"There was a general grumble among the staff when the company moved the holiday party to a Monday night.","t":"公司把節日派對改到星期一晚上時，員工之間普遍發出牢騷。"},{"w":"grumble about","p":"v.phr.","d":"to complain about something","c":"抱怨…","s":"Instead of grumbling about the homework, why don't we start now and finish it before dinner?","t":"與其抱怨作業，我們何不現在就開始，在晚餐前把它做完？","a":"grumbling about"},{"w":"grumpy","p":"adj.","d":"in a bad mood and easily annoyed","c":"脾氣壞的；易怒的","s":"Dad is always grumpy before his first cup of coffee, so we wait until he has finished it to ask for anything.","t":"爸爸在喝第一杯咖啡前總是脾氣很壞，所以我們都等他喝完才開口要東西。"},{"w":"hacker","p":"n.","d":"a person who secretly gets into other people's computer systems","c":"駭客","s":"A hacker broke into the company's computer system last night and stole the personal information of thousands of customers.","t":"一名駭客昨晚入侵了公司的電腦系統，竊取了數千名顧客的個人資料。","h":1},{"w":"hack","p":"v.","d":"to secretly get into a computer system without permission","c":"非法入侵（電腦）","s":"Someone tried to hack into my email account yesterday, so I changed my password and turned on two-step login.","t":"昨天有人試圖入侵我的電子郵件帳戶，所以我更改了密碼並開啟了兩步驗證登入。"},{"w":"hack","p":"v.","d":"to cut something roughly with a big knife or an axe","c":"砍；劈","s":"The farmers had to hack their way through the thick jungle with long knives before they could reach the river.","t":"農夫們必須用長刀在茂密的叢林中砍出一條路，才能到達河邊。"},{"w":"hacking","p":"n.","d":"the activity of secretly getting into computer systems","c":"駭客行為","s":"The bank spends millions of dollars every year to protect its customers from hacking and other online crimes.","t":"這家銀行每年花數百萬元保護顧客免受駭客攻擊和其他網路犯罪的侵害。"},{"w":"life hack","p":"n.phr.","d":"a simple trick that makes everyday life easier","c":"生活小技巧","s":"Here is a useful life hack: put a wooden spoon across the pot, and the boiling water will not spill over the edge.","t":"這裡有個實用的生活小技巧：把木湯匙橫放在鍋子上，沸水就不會溢出來。"},{"w":"hail","p":"n.","d":"small hard balls of ice that fall from the sky like rain","c":"冰雹","s":"The sudden storm brought hail the size of marbles, and it broke several car windows in the parking lot.","t":"突然的暴風雨帶來彈珠大小的冰雹，打破了停車場裡好幾輛車的車窗。","h":1},{"w":"hail","p":"v.","d":"(of hail) to fall from the sky","c":"下冰雹","s":"It hailed for ten minutes this afternoon, and the white balls covered the playground like a thin layer of snow.","t":"今天下午下了十分鐘的冰雹，白色的小球像一層薄雪一樣覆蓋了操場。","a":"hailed"},{"w":"hail","p":"v.","d":"to call or wave to a taxi to stop; to praise someone publicly","c":"招呼（計程車）；歡呼讚揚","s":"It was raining hard, so we tried to hail a taxi outside the station, but every one that passed was already full.","t":"雨下得很大，所以我們試著在車站外招計程車，但每輛經過的車都已經載了客人。"},{"w":"hail sb as","p":"v.phr.","d":"to publicly say that someone is very good or important","c":"讚揚某人為…","s":"After the young pitcher won his tenth game, newspapers hailed him as the future star of Taiwanese baseball.","t":"這位年輕投手贏得第十場比賽後，報紙讚揚他為台灣棒球未來的明星。","a":"hailed him as"},{"w":"hailstorm","p":"n.","d":"a storm with a lot of hail","c":"冰雹暴","s":"A hailstorm destroyed most of the farmer's melons in a single hour, just one week before they were ready to pick.","t":"一場冰雹暴在一小時內毀掉了農夫大部分的西瓜，而那時距離採收只剩一週。"},{"w":"hamper","p":"v.","d":"to make it difficult for something to happen or for someone to do something","c":"阻礙；妨礙","s":"Heavy rain and thick fog hampered the rescue work in the mountains, and the helicopter could not take off until morning.","t":"大雨和濃霧阻礙了山區的救援工作，直升機直到早上才能起飛。","a":"hampered","h":1},{"w":"hamper","p":"n.","d":"a large basket with a lid, used for food or dirty clothes","c":"有蓋大籃子","s":"We packed sandwiches, fruit, and cold drinks into a picnic hamper and carried it to the beach for the afternoon.","t":"我們把三明治、水果和冷飲裝進野餐籃，帶到海邊度過下午。"},{"w":"be hampered by","p":"v.phr.","d":"to be held back or slowed down by something","c":"受…阻礙","s":"The small school's sports program is hampered by a lack of money, so the children have to share one old ball.","t":"這所小學校的體育課程受到經費不足的阻礙，所以孩子們必須共用一顆舊球。","a":"hampered by"},{"w":"handicap","p":"n.","d":"something that makes it harder for you to do something; a disadvantage","c":"障礙；不利條件","s":"Not speaking the local language was a real handicap when I first moved to Japan, especially at the bank and the hospital.","t":"我剛搬到日本時，不會說當地語言是個真正的障礙，尤其是在銀行和醫院。","h":1},{"w":"handicap","p":"v.","d":"to make it harder for someone to do something","c":"妨礙；使不利","s":"The team was handicapped by the loss of its two best players, so it finished last in the tournament this year.","t":"這支球隊因失去兩名最佳球員而處於不利，所以今年在錦標賽中排名最後。","a":"handicapped"},{"w":"handicapped","p":"adj.","d":"(older word) not able to use part of the body or mind fully","c":"身心障礙的（較舊的用法）","s":"The parking spaces near the door are reserved for handicapped drivers, so please do not leave your car there even for a minute.","t":"門口附近的停車位是保留給身心障礙駕駛的，所以請不要把車停在那裡，一分鐘也不行。"},{"w":"disability","p":"n.","d":"a condition that makes it hard for someone to use part of the body or mind (the polite word today)","c":"殘障；身心障礙（現今較禮貌的說法）","s":"Today people prefer to say that someone has a disability rather than calling them handicapped, because the newer word sounds more respectful.","t":"現在人們比較喜歡說某人有身心障礙，而不是叫他們 handicapped，因為新的用語聽起來更尊重人。"}]},{"unit":17,"theme":"handicraft – hover","cards":[{"w":"handicraft","p":"n.","d":"a skill of making things by hand; things made this way","c":"手工藝；手工藝品","s":"The night market sells all kinds of local handicrafts, such as bamboo baskets and hand-painted fans made by village artists.","t":"夜市販售各式各樣的當地手工藝品，像是村裡藝術家製作的竹籃和手繪扇子。","a":"handicrafts","h":1},{"w":"craft","p":"n.","d":"a job or activity that needs skill with your hands","c":"工藝；手藝","s":"Pottery is a craft that takes years to learn, so the old master still practices every morning before his students arrive.","t":"陶藝是一門需要多年學習的手藝，所以老師傅每天早上在學生到達前仍然持續練習。"},{"w":"craftsman","p":"n.","d":"a person who is very skilled at making things by hand","c":"工匠","s":"The craftsman spent three months carving the wooden door, and every flower on it looks real enough to touch.","t":"這位工匠花了三個月雕刻這扇木門，門上的每一朵花都真實得像可以摸到一樣。"},{"w":"handmade","p":"adj.","d":"made by hand, not by a machine","c":"手工製的","s":"My grandmother gave me a handmade scarf for my birthday, and she said it took her two weeks to knit it.","t":"我奶奶送我一條手工織的圍巾當生日禮物，她說她花了兩週才織好。"},{"w":"harass","p":"v.","d":"to keep annoying or frightening someone again and again","c":"騷擾","s":"The company fired the manager because he continued to harass a young worker even after she asked him to stop.","t":"公司開除了那位經理，因為即使在一位年輕員工要求他停止之後，他仍繼續騷擾她。","h":1},{"w":"harassment","p":"n.","d":"the act of annoying or frightening someone again and again","c":"騷擾","s":"Schools now teach students that sending unwanted messages again and again is a form of harassment and can be reported.","t":"學校現在教導學生，一再傳送別人不想要的訊息是一種騷擾，而且可以舉報。"},{"w":"sexual harassment","p":"n.phr.","d":"unwanted sexual words or actions that make someone feel uncomfortable","c":"性騷擾","s":"The new law protects workers from sexual harassment and allows them to report any problem without losing their jobs.","t":"新法律保護員工免於性騷擾，並允許他們在不失去工作的情況下舉報任何問題。"},{"w":"harassed","p":"adj.","d":"tired and worried because you have too much to do","c":"疲於應付的","s":"The harassed waiter was trying to serve ten tables at once, so he forgot to bring our drinks for twenty minutes.","t":"那位疲於應付的服務生想同時招呼十桌客人，所以忘了送我們的飲料長達二十分鐘。"},{"w":"harden","p":"v.","d":"to become hard or make something hard","c":"變硬；使變硬","s":"Leave the clay in the sun for a few hours, and it will harden enough for the children to paint their little animals.","t":"把黏土放在太陽下幾個小時，它就會變硬到足以讓孩子們為他們的小動物上色。","h":1},{"w":"harden","p":"v.","d":"to make someone less kind or less easily hurt","c":"使冷酷；使堅強","s":"Years of living on the street had hardened the boy's heart, and he found it hard to trust anyone who offered help.","t":"多年的街頭生活使這個男孩的心變得冷硬，他發現很難信任任何伸出援手的人。","a":"hardened"},{"w":"hardened","p":"adj.","d":"having done something bad for so long that you will not change","c":"積習已深的；冷酷的","s":"The police said the man was a hardened criminal who had been in prison four times and showed no sign of changing.","t":"警方說這名男子是一個積習已深的罪犯，曾入獄四次，而且毫無改變的跡象。"},{"w":"hardness","p":"n.","d":"the quality of being hard","c":"硬度","s":"Diamond has the greatest hardness of any natural material, which is why it is used to cut glass and stone.","t":"鑽石是所有天然材料中硬度最高的，這就是為什麼它被用來切割玻璃和石頭。"},{"w":"harmonica","p":"n.","d":"a small musical instrument that you play by blowing and sucking air through it","c":"口琴","s":"My grandfather carries a small harmonica in his pocket and plays old folk songs for the children at every family party.","t":"我爺爺口袋裡總是帶著一把小口琴，在每次家庭聚會上為孩子們演奏老民謠。","h":1},{"w":"harmony","p":"n.","d":"a pleasant combination of musical notes; peace and agreement","c":"和聲；和諧","s":"The two singers' voices blended in perfect harmony, and the audience asked them to sing the song one more time.","t":"兩位歌手的聲音融合成完美的和聲，觀眾要求他們再唱一次那首歌。"},{"w":"harmonious","p":"adj.","d":"peaceful and friendly; pleasant to hear or see together","c":"和諧的","s":"The neighbors have lived in harmonious peace for decades, sharing fruit from their gardens and watching each other's children.","t":"這些鄰居幾十年來和諧相處，分享花園裡的水果，也互相照看彼此的孩子。"},{"w":"harmonize","p":"v.","d":"to sing or play notes that go well together; to make things fit together","c":"合唱和聲；使和諧","s":"The school choir practices every day to harmonize their voices, so that no single singer sounds louder than the others.","t":"學校合唱團每天練習讓他們的聲音和諧融合，這樣就沒有任何一位歌手的聲音會比其他人大。"},{"w":"harness","p":"n.","d":"a set of straps that holds a person or an animal safely","c":"馬具；安全吊帶","s":"Before climbing the wall, each student must put on a safety harness and have the teacher check that every strap is tight.","t":"攀岩之前，每位學生都必須穿上安全吊帶，並請老師檢查每條帶子是否繫緊。","h":1},{"w":"harness","p":"v.","d":"to control and use the power of something, such as wind or the sun","c":"利用（能源等）","s":"Engineers are building huge wind farms off the west coast to harness the strong winds that blow across the Taiwan Strait.","t":"工程師正在西海岸外興建大型風力發電場，以利用吹過台灣海峽的強風。"},{"w":"harness","p":"v.","d":"to put a harness on a horse and fix it to a cart","c":"給（馬）套上馬具","s":"The farmer harnessed the two horses to the cart and drove slowly into town to sell his vegetables.","t":"農夫把兩匹馬套上馬具拴在車上，慢慢地駕車進城去賣他的蔬菜。","a":"harnessed"},{"w":"harness solar energy","p":"v.phr.","d":"to collect and use the power of the sun","c":"利用太陽能","s":"Many schools in Taiwan now have panels on their roofs to harness solar energy, which cuts their electricity bills in summer.","t":"台灣許多學校現在屋頂上都有太陽能板來利用太陽能，這降低了他們夏天的電費。"},{"w":"haunt","p":"v.","d":"(of a ghost) to appear in a place again and again","c":"（鬼魂）出沒","s":"People in the village say that a ghost haunts the old house on the hill, so nobody wants to buy it.","t":"村裡的人說有鬼出沒在山丘上的老房子裡，所以沒有人想買它。","a":"haunts","h":1},{"w":"haunt","p":"v.","d":"(of a bad memory) to keep coming back and troubling someone","c":"縈繞心頭；困擾","s":"The memory of the accident still haunts the driver, and he has not driven a car since that terrible night.","t":"那場意外的記憶仍然縈繞著那位駕駛，自從那個可怕的夜晚之後他就沒有再開過車。","a":"haunts"},{"w":"haunt","p":"n.","d":"a place that someone visits often","c":"常去的地方","s":"This little coffee shop near the university was our favorite haunt when we were students twenty years ago.","t":"二十年前我們還是學生時，大學附近這家小咖啡店是我們最喜歡常去的地方。"},{"w":"haunted","p":"adj.","d":"visited by ghosts","c":"鬧鬼的","s":"The haunted house at the amusement park was so scary that my little brother cried and asked to leave halfway through.","t":"遊樂園的鬼屋太可怕了，我弟弟走到一半就哭著要求離開。"},{"w":"haunting","p":"adj.","d":"beautiful or sad in a way that stays in your mind","c":"縈繞心頭的；難忘的","s":"The movie's haunting music stayed in my head for days, and I finally bought the soundtrack so I could listen to it properly.","t":"這部電影縈繞心頭的音樂在我腦中停留了好幾天，我最後買了原聲帶好好地聽。"},{"w":"headphones","p":"n.","d":"a pair of small speakers worn over the ears for listening","c":"頭戴式耳機","s":"Please use your headphones when you watch videos on the train, because other passengers do not want to hear your show.","t":"在火車上看影片時請戴耳機，因為其他乘客不想聽到你的節目。","h":1},{"w":"earphones","p":"n.","d":"very small speakers that you put inside your ears","c":"耳塞式耳機","s":"I lost my earphones on the bus yesterday, so I had to listen to the English practice test through the phone's speaker.","t":"我昨天在公車上弄丟了耳機，所以只好用手機的喇叭聽英文模擬測驗。"},{"w":"headset","p":"n.","d":"headphones with a small microphone attached","c":"耳機麥克風","s":"The customer service workers wear a headset all day so that they can type on the computer while talking to callers.","t":"客服人員整天戴著耳機麥克風，這樣他們就能一邊和來電者說話一邊在電腦上打字。"},{"w":"noise-cancelling headphones","p":"n.phr.","d":"headphones that block out the sounds around you","c":"降噪耳機","s":"My brother bought noise-cancelling headphones for the long flight, and he said he could not hear the engines or the crying baby at all.","t":"我哥哥為了長途飛行買了降噪耳機，他說他完全聽不到引擎聲或嬰兒的哭聲。"},{"w":"healthful","p":"adj.","d":"good for your health","c":"有益健康的","s":"The school cafeteria now offers more healthful choices, such as brown rice, fresh vegetables, and fruit instead of fried snacks.","t":"學校餐廳現在提供更多有益健康的選擇，例如糙米、新鮮蔬菜和水果，而不是油炸點心。","h":1},{"w":"health","p":"n.","d":"the condition of your body and mind","c":"健康","s":"Regular exercise and enough sleep are the two most important things you can do for your health, according to my doctor.","t":"根據我的醫生所說，規律運動和充足的睡眠是你能為自己的健康做的兩件最重要的事。"},{"w":"healthy","p":"adj.","d":"strong and not ill; good for your health","c":"健康的；有益健康的","s":"My grandmother is still healthy at ninety because she walks to the market every morning and never eats too much.","t":"我奶奶九十歲了仍然很健康，因為她每天早上走路去市場，而且從不吃太多。"},{"w":"unhealthy","p":"adj.","d":"not good for your health; not well","c":"不健康的","s":"Eating instant noodles every night is unhealthy, so my roommate decided to learn how to cook simple dishes.","t":"每天晚上吃泡麵是不健康的，所以我的室友決定學做簡單的菜。"},{"w":"hearty","p":"adj.","d":"(of a meal) large and filling","c":"豐盛的","s":"After the long hike, we enjoyed a hearty meal of beef stew and fresh bread at the little mountain restaurant.","t":"長途健行之後，我們在山上的小餐館享用了一頓有燉牛肉和新鮮麵包的豐盛餐點。","h":1},{"w":"hearty","p":"adj.","d":"warm, loud, and friendly","c":"爽朗的；熱情的","s":"The coach gave each player a hearty handshake and a loud laugh, and the nervous team suddenly felt much more relaxed.","t":"教練和每位球員熱情地握手並大聲地笑，緊張的球隊突然覺得放鬆多了。"},{"w":"heartily","p":"adv.","d":"in a warm and energetic way; very much","c":"盡情地；熱誠地","s":"The guests laughed heartily at the groom's funny speech, and even the shy bride could not stop giggling.","t":"賓客們聽到新郎有趣的致詞開懷大笑，連害羞的新娘也忍不住一直咯咯笑。"},{"w":"heartfelt","p":"adj.","d":"showing strong and sincere feeling","c":"衷心的","s":"She wrote a heartfelt letter to thank the nurses who had taken care of her father during his last month in the hospital.","t":"她寫了一封衷心的信，感謝在她父親住院的最後一個月照顧他的護士們。"},{"w":"hedge","p":"n.","d":"a row of bushes or small trees growing close together like a wall","c":"樹籬","s":"A tall green hedge grows along the front of the garden, so people on the street cannot see into our living room.","t":"一道高高的綠色樹籬沿著花園前方生長，所以街上的人看不到我們的客廳。","h":1},{"w":"hedge","p":"v.","d":"to avoid giving a clear answer","c":"避免正面回答；含糊其辭","s":"When reporters asked the mayor about the new tax, he hedged and said he would need to study the numbers first.","t":"記者問市長關於新稅的問題時，他含糊其辭，說他需要先研究一下數字。","a":"hedged"},{"w":"hedge against","p":"v.phr.","d":"to protect yourself against possible loss","c":"防備；對沖（風險）","s":"Some families buy gold to hedge against rising prices, because they believe it keeps its value when money loses it.","t":"有些家庭買黃金來防備物價上漲，因為他們相信當金錢貶值時黃金能保值。"},{"w":"hedgehog","p":"n.","d":"a small animal with sharp spines on its back","c":"刺蝟","s":"We found a small hedgehog rolled into a ball under the bushes, and we left some water for it before going inside.","t":"我們在灌木叢下發現一隻縮成一團的小刺蝟，進屋前我們留了一些水給牠。"},{"w":"heighten","p":"v.","d":"to make a feeling or an effect stronger","c":"提高；增強","s":"The dark music and the empty street heightened the fear of the audience before the monster finally appeared on the screen.","t":"在怪物終於出現在銀幕上之前，陰暗的音樂和空蕩的街道增強了觀眾的恐懼。","a":"heightened","h":1},{"w":"height","p":"n.","d":"how tall someone or something is","c":"高度；身高","s":"The nurse measured my height and weight during the school check-up and said I had grown four centimeters this year.","t":"學校健康檢查時，護士量了我的身高和體重，說我今年長高了四公分。"},{"w":"heightened","p":"adj.","d":"stronger or greater than usual","c":"增強的；提高的","s":"There was heightened security at the airport after the warning, and every passenger's bag was opened and checked by hand.","t":"警告發布後，機場的安檢加強了，每位乘客的包包都被打開並以人工檢查。"},{"w":"heights","p":"n.","d":"high places","c":"高處","s":"My father is afraid of heights, so he waited at the bottom while we rode the glass elevator to the top of Taipei 101.","t":"我爸爸怕高，所以當我們搭玻璃電梯到台北 101 頂樓時，他在樓下等。"},{"w":"hemisphere","p":"n.","d":"one half of the earth; one half of the brain","c":"半球；（大腦）半球","s":"Australia is in the southern hemisphere, so when it is winter in Taiwan, Australians are enjoying their summer holidays at the beach.","t":"澳洲位於南半球，所以當台灣是冬天時，澳洲人正在海灘上享受暑假。","h":1},{"w":"sphere","p":"n.","d":"a round solid shape like a ball; an area of activity","c":"球體；領域","s":"The earth is not a perfect sphere; it is slightly flatter at the top and bottom and wider around the middle.","t":"地球不是一個完美的球體；它的頂部和底部稍微扁平，中間較寬。"},{"w":"the Northern Hemisphere","p":"n.phr.","d":"the half of the earth north of the equator","c":"北半球","s":"Most of the world's land and people are in the Northern Hemisphere, which is why its summer is the busiest travel season of the year.","t":"世界上大部分的陸地和人口都在北半球，這就是為什麼北半球的夏天是一年中最忙的旅遊季節。"},{"w":"the left hemisphere","p":"n.phr.","d":"the left half of the brain","c":"左腦半球","s":"Scientists say the left hemisphere of the brain controls language in most people, which is why some patients lose speech after a stroke.","t":"科學家說大多數人的語言是由大腦的左半球控制的，這就是為什麼有些病人中風後會失去說話能力。"},{"w":"heroic","p":"adj.","d":"very brave; like a hero","c":"英勇的","s":"The firefighter's heroic rescue of the two children from the burning apartment was shown on the news all over the country.","t":"這位消防員從燃燒的公寓中英勇救出兩名孩童的事蹟，在全國的新聞上播出。","h":1},{"w":"hero","p":"n.","d":"a person who is admired for doing something very brave or good","c":"英雄","s":"To the whole town, the quiet old doctor was a hero because he had treated poor patients for free for forty years.","t":"對整個鎮上的人來說，這位安靜的老醫生是個英雄，因為他四十年來免費為貧窮的病人看病。"},{"w":"heroine","p":"n.","d":"a woman who is admired for being brave; the main female character in a story","c":"女英雄；女主角","s":"The heroine of the novel is a brave young girl who crosses the mountains alone to find her missing father.","t":"這本小說的女主角是一個勇敢的年輕女孩，她獨自翻山越嶺去尋找失蹤的父親。"},{"w":"heroism","p":"n.","d":"very brave behavior","c":"英勇行為","s":"The soldier received a medal for his heroism after he carried three wounded friends to safety under heavy fire.","t":"這名士兵在猛烈的炮火下把三位受傷的同袍背到安全處，因其英勇行為而獲頒獎章。"},{"w":"heroically","p":"adv.","d":"in a very brave way","c":"英勇地","s":"The small team fought heroically until the last minute of the game, even though they were losing by twenty points.","t":"這支小球隊英勇地奮戰到比賽的最後一分鐘，即使他們落後了二十分。"},{"w":"heroin","p":"n.","d":"a very strong illegal drug that people become addicted to","c":"海洛因","s":"The police found a large amount of heroin hidden inside the truck's tires, and the driver was arrested at the border.","t":"警方在卡車輪胎裡發現藏有大量海洛因，司機在邊境被逮捕。","h":1},{"w":"drug","p":"n.","d":"an illegal substance that people take for pleasure; a medicine","c":"毒品；藥物","s":"The school invited a former police officer to talk about how one bad decision about drugs can destroy a young person's future.","t":"學校邀請一位退休警官來談談關於毒品的一個錯誤決定如何能毀掉年輕人的未來。","a":"drugs"},{"w":"drug addict","p":"n.phr.","d":"a person who cannot stop taking illegal drugs","c":"吸毒者","s":"The center helps each drug addict find a job and a safe place to live after they finish the treatment program.","t":"這個中心幫助每位吸毒者在完成治療計畫後找到工作和安全的住所。"},{"w":"addiction","p":"n.","d":"the state of not being able to stop taking a drug or doing something","c":"上癮；癮","s":"Heroin addiction is extremely hard to break, so doctors say the best protection is never to try the drug even once.","t":"海洛因癮極難戒除，所以醫生說最好的保護就是連一次都不要嘗試這種毒品。"},{"w":"heterosexual","p":"adj.","d":"attracted to people of the opposite sex","c":"異性戀的","s":"Most of the couples in the survey were heterosexual, but the study also included many same-sex couples from across the country.","t":"調查中大多數的伴侶是異性戀，但這項研究也包括了全國各地許多同性伴侶。","h":1},{"w":"heterosexual","p":"n.","d":"a person who is attracted to people of the opposite sex","c":"異性戀者","s":"The new law gives same-sex couples the same rights as heterosexuals have always had, including the right to adopt children.","t":"新法律給予同性伴侶與異性戀者一直以來享有的同樣權利，包括收養孩子的權利。","a":"heterosexuals"},{"w":"sexual orientation","p":"n.phr.","d":"whether a person is attracted to men, women, or both","c":"性傾向","s":"The company's rules say that nobody can be treated unfairly because of their race, religion, or sexual orientation.","t":"公司的規定說，任何人都不能因為種族、宗教或性傾向而受到不公平的對待。"},{"w":"hierarchy","p":"n.","d":"a system in which people or things are arranged in levels of importance","c":"階級制度；等級體系","s":"In a traditional company, there is a strict hierarchy, and a new worker must get permission from several bosses before making any decision.","t":"在傳統公司裡有嚴格的階級制度，新員工在做任何決定前都必須獲得好幾位主管的許可。","h":1},{"w":"hierarchical","p":"adj.","d":"arranged in levels from the most important to the least important","c":"階級的；分層的","s":"The school's hierarchical system means the principal decides, the teachers carry out the plan, and students are seldom asked for opinions.","t":"學校的階級體系意味著校長做決定，老師執行計畫，而學生很少被問到意見。"},{"w":"rank","p":"n.","d":"a person's position or level in an organization","c":"等級；階級；軍階","s":"A captain holds a higher rank than a lieutenant, so the younger officer must follow the captain's orders during the training.","t":"上尉的軍階比中尉高，所以訓練期間較年輕的軍官必須服從上尉的命令。"},{"w":"hijack","p":"v.","d":"to take control of a plane, bus, or ship by force","c":"劫持（飛機、車輛等）","s":"Two armed men tried to hijack the plane, but the passengers and crew managed to stop them before it reached the coast.","t":"兩名持械男子試圖劫持飛機，但乘客和機組人員在飛機抵達海岸前成功制止了他們。","h":1},{"w":"hijack","p":"n.","d":"the act of taking control of a plane or vehicle by force","c":"劫持事件","s":"After the hijack in 2001, airports around the world introduced much stricter checks on every passenger and every bag.","t":"2001 年的劫機事件之後，世界各地的機場對每位乘客和每件行李都引進了更嚴格的檢查。"},{"w":"hijacker","p":"n.","d":"a person who hijacks a plane or vehicle","c":"劫持者；劫機者","s":"The hijacker demanded a million dollars and a plane to another country, but the police talked with him for six hours until he gave up.","t":"劫機者要求一百萬美元和一架飛往其他國家的飛機，但警方和他談了六個小時，直到他放棄。"},{"w":"hijacking","p":"n.","d":"the crime of hijacking","c":"劫持（罪行）","s":"Thanks to better airport security, hijacking has become very rare, and most passengers no longer worry about it.","t":"由於機場安檢改善，劫機已經變得非常罕見，大多數乘客不再為此擔心。"},{"w":"hoarse","p":"adj.","d":"(of a voice) rough and low, often because of a sore throat or shouting","c":"沙啞的","s":"After cheering for three hours at the baseball game, my voice was so hoarse that I could hardly speak the next morning.","t":"在棒球賽上加油三個小時後，我的聲音沙啞到隔天早上幾乎說不出話來。","h":1},{"w":"hoarsely","p":"adv.","d":"in a rough, low voice","c":"沙啞地","s":"\"Water, please,\" the sick man whispered hoarsely, and the nurse quickly brought a cup to his bed.","t":"「請給我水。」生病的男子沙啞地低聲說，護士很快就端了一杯水到他床邊。"},{"w":"hoarseness","p":"n.","d":"the condition of having a rough, low voice","c":"沙啞","s":"The doctor said the singer's hoarseness was caused by too many concerts, and she needed to rest her voice for at least two weeks.","t":"醫生說這位歌手的聲音沙啞是因為演唱會太多造成的，她需要讓嗓子休息至少兩週。"},{"w":"homosexual","p":"adj.","d":"attracted to people of the same sex","c":"同性戀的","s":"The film tells the true story of a homosexual couple who fought for years for the right to marry and raise a family together.","t":"這部電影講述一對同性戀伴侶的真實故事，他們為了結婚和共同組成家庭的權利奮鬥了多年。","h":1},{"w":"homosexual","p":"n.","d":"a person who is attracted to people of the same sex","c":"同性戀者","s":"In the past, homosexuals often had to hide who they were, but today many of them live openly with their partners.","t":"過去，同性戀者常常必須隱藏自己的身分，但如今許多人公開地和伴侶一起生活。","a":"homosexuals"},{"w":"homosexuality","p":"n.","d":"the state of being attracted to people of the same sex","c":"同性戀","s":"Attitudes toward homosexuality have changed greatly in Taiwan over the past thirty years, especially among younger people.","t":"過去三十年來，台灣對同性戀的態度有了很大的改變，尤其是在年輕人之間。"},{"w":"same-sex","p":"adj.","d":"of or between people of the same sex","c":"同性的","s":"Since 2019, same-sex couples in Taiwan have been able to register their marriage at any household office.","t":"自 2019 年起，台灣的同性伴侶就可以在任何戶政事務所登記結婚。"},{"w":"honorary","p":"adj.","d":"given as an honor, without the usual work or requirements","c":"名譽的","s":"The university gave the famous writer an honorary degree to thank her for the many books she had written about the island.","t":"這所大學授予這位知名作家名譽學位，感謝她寫了許多關於這座島嶼的書。","h":1},{"w":"honor","p":"n.","d":"something that makes you feel proud; great respect","c":"榮譽；尊敬","s":"It is a great honor to be chosen to carry the flag at the opening ceremony, so Amy practiced walking for a whole week.","t":"被選中在開幕典禮上舉旗是極大的榮譽，所以艾咪練習走路練了整整一週。"},{"w":"honorable","p":"adj.","d":"deserving respect; morally good","c":"光榮的；可敬的","s":"Losing the final is not shameful; playing fairly and giving your best effort is always an honorable way to finish.","t":"輸掉決賽並不可恥；公平比賽並盡全力，永遠是一種光榮的結束方式。"},{"w":"in honor of","p":"phr.","d":"in order to show respect for someone","c":"為了向…致敬；為紀念","s":"The town built a small park in honor of the teacher who had taught three generations of children to read.","t":"小鎮建了一座小公園以紀念那位教過三代孩子識字的老師。"},{"w":"hospitable","p":"adj.","d":"friendly and generous to visitors","c":"好客的","s":"The people in the mountain village were so hospitable that they invited us, complete strangers, to stay the night and share their dinner.","t":"山村裡的人非常好客，他們邀請我們這些完全陌生的人過夜並一起吃晚餐。","h":1},{"w":"hospitality","p":"n.","d":"friendly and generous behavior toward visitors","c":"款待；好客","s":"Thank you for your warm hospitality during our stay; the home-cooked meals and the comfortable room made us feel like family.","t":"感謝你們在我們停留期間的熱情款待；家常菜和舒適的房間讓我們覺得像家人一樣。","h":1},{"w":"the hospitality industry","p":"n.phr.","d":"the business of hotels, restaurants, and travel","c":"餐旅業","s":"My sister studies tourism because she wants to work in the hospitality industry, perhaps managing a hotel in Kenting one day.","t":"我姐姐讀觀光，因為她想在餐旅業工作，也許有一天能在墾丁管理一家飯店。"},{"w":"inhospitable","p":"adj.","d":"(of a place) difficult to live in; (of people) unfriendly to visitors","c":"不宜居住的；不好客的","s":"The desert is an inhospitable place, with burning days, freezing nights, and almost no water for hundreds of kilometers.","t":"沙漠是一個不宜居住的地方，白天酷熱、夜晚冰冷，而且方圓數百公里幾乎沒有水。"},{"w":"hospitalize","p":"v.","d":"to send someone to a hospital for treatment","c":"使住院","s":"The doctor decided to hospitalize the old man for a few days because his fever would not go down with the usual medicine.","t":"醫生決定讓這位老先生住院幾天，因為他的燒用一般的藥退不下來。","h":1},{"w":"hospital","p":"n.","d":"a place where sick or injured people are treated","c":"醫院","s":"My aunt works as a nurse at the city hospital, and she often has to work through the night during busy weeks.","t":"我阿姨在市立醫院當護士，在忙碌的週間她常常必須通宵工作。"},{"w":"be hospitalized","p":"v.phr.","d":"to be taken into a hospital for treatment","c":"住院","s":"Three students were hospitalized after the school lunch made them sick, but luckily all of them went home the next day.","t":"三名學生在吃了營養午餐生病後住院，但幸運的是他們隔天都回家了。","a":"were hospitalized"},{"w":"hospitalization","p":"n.","d":"the state of being in a hospital for treatment","c":"住院（治療）","s":"Our insurance covers the cost of hospitalization, so the family did not have to pay for the two weeks Grandpa spent in the ward.","t":"我們的保險涵蓋住院費用，所以爺爺在病房待的那兩週家裡不必付錢。"},{"w":"hostel","p":"n.","d":"a cheap place to stay, often with shared rooms, for travelers or students","c":"青年旅舍；宿舍","s":"We stayed at a cheap hostel near the station, sharing a room with four other travelers from Japan and Germany.","t":"我們住在車站附近一家便宜的青年旅舍，和另外四位來自日本和德國的旅客同住一間房。","h":1},{"w":"youth hostel","p":"n.phr.","d":"a cheap hostel for young travelers","c":"青年旅舍","s":"A bed in a youth hostel costs only a few hundred dollars a night, so it is popular with students traveling on a small budget.","t":"青年旅舍的一個床位一晚只要幾百元，所以很受預算有限的學生旅客歡迎。"},{"w":"host","p":"n.","d":"a person who invites guests and takes care of them","c":"主人；東道主","s":"Our host prepared a huge dinner for us on our first night in France, and she even made a cake with our names on it.","t":"我們在法國的第一個晚上，女主人為我們準備了豐盛的晚餐，她甚至做了一個寫著我們名字的蛋糕。"},{"w":"hostess","p":"n.","d":"a woman who invites guests and takes care of them","c":"女主人","s":"The hostess greeted every guest at the door and made sure that nobody was left standing alone at the party.","t":"女主人在門口迎接每一位客人，並確保派對上沒有人被孤單地晾在一旁。"},{"w":"hover","p":"v.","d":"to stay in the air in one place","c":"盤旋；懸停","s":"A hummingbird can hover in the air in front of a flower while it drinks, moving its tiny wings fifty times a second.","t":"蜂鳥喝花蜜時可以在花前懸停在空中，牠細小的翅膀每秒拍動五十次。","h":1},{"w":"hover","p":"v.","d":"(of a number or level) to stay close to a certain amount","c":"徘徊（於某數值）","s":"The temperature has hovered around ten degrees all week, so my mother keeps telling me to wear a thicker jacket.","t":"這整週氣溫一直徘徊在十度左右，所以我媽媽一直叫我穿厚一點的外套。","a":"hovered"},{"w":"hover over","p":"v.phr.","d":"to stay close to someone and watch them in an annoying way","c":"在…旁邊徘徊；盯著","s":"The nervous mother kept hovering over her son as he did his homework, until he finally asked her to let him work alone.","t":"那位緊張的母親在兒子寫功課時一直在他身旁盯著，直到他終於要求她讓他自己做。","a":"hovering over"},{"w":"hovercraft","p":"n.","d":"a vehicle that travels over water or land on a cushion of air","c":"氣墊船","s":"A hovercraft can travel over both water and flat land because it floats on a cushion of air pushed out by its engines.","t":"氣墊船可以在水面和平地上行駛，因為它浮在引擎推出的氣墊上。"}]},{"unit":18,"theme":"humiliate – inhabit","cards":[{"w":"humiliate","p":"v.","d":"to make someone feel ashamed or stupid in front of others","c":"羞辱；使丟臉","s":"The coach should not humiliate players in front of their teammates when they make a mistake, because it only makes them more nervous.","t":"教練不應該在隊友面前羞辱犯錯的球員，因為那只會讓他們更緊張。","h":1},{"w":"humiliation","p":"n.","d":"a feeling of great shame; something that makes you feel this","c":"羞辱；恥辱","s":"Forgetting all his lines in the school play was a deep humiliation for Jack, and he refused to go on stage again for a year.","t":"在學校戲劇中忘光所有台詞對傑克來說是極大的恥辱，他有一年都拒絕再上台。"},{"w":"humiliating","p":"adj.","d":"making you feel ashamed or stupid","c":"丟臉的；羞辱性的","s":"Losing 10-0 to the youngest team in the league was a humiliating experience, and the players left the field without saying a word.","t":"以 0 比 10 輸給聯盟中最年輕的球隊是一次丟臉的經驗，球員們一句話也沒說就離開了球場。"},{"w":"humble","p":"adj.","d":"not thinking you are better than other people","c":"謙虛的","s":"Although she has won many prizes, the scientist remains humble and always thanks her students for their help in every speech.","t":"雖然她贏得了許多獎項，這位科學家仍然很謙虛，每次演講總是感謝學生的幫助。"},{"w":"hunch","p":"n.","d":"a feeling that something is true, even without proof","c":"直覺；預感","s":"I had a hunch that the store would be closed on the holiday, so I called first instead of taking the bus all the way there.","t":"我有一種預感那家店在假日會關門，所以我先打了電話，而不是搭公車大老遠跑過去。","h":1},{"w":"hunch","p":"v.","d":"to bend your back and shoulders forward","c":"弓背；駝背","s":"Do not hunch over your desk when you study, because sitting like that for hours will hurt your back and neck.","t":"讀書時不要弓著背趴在書桌上，因為那樣坐好幾個小時會傷害你的背和脖子。"},{"w":"have a hunch","p":"v.phr.","d":"to feel that something is true without being sure","c":"有預感","s":"The detective had a hunch that the quiet neighbor knew more than he was saying, so she decided to visit him again.","t":"這位偵探有預感那位安靜的鄰居知道的比他說的還多，所以她決定再去拜訪他一次。","a":"had a hunch"},{"w":"hunchback","p":"n.","d":"a person whose back has a large round lump","c":"駝背的人","s":"In the famous French novel, the kind hunchback who rings the church bells is laughed at by the people of Paris because of his looks.","t":"在那本著名的法國小說裡，負責敲教堂鐘的善良駝子因為外貌而被巴黎人嘲笑。"},{"w":"hurdle","p":"n.","d":"a problem that you must solve before you can succeed; a barrier to jump over in a race","c":"障礙；跨欄","s":"Finding enough money was the biggest hurdle for the young couple who wanted to open a small bakery near the school.","t":"對這對想在學校附近開一家小麵包店的年輕夫妻來說，籌到足夠的錢是最大的障礙。","h":1},{"w":"hurdle","p":"v.","d":"to jump over something while running","c":"跨越","s":"The runner hurdled the last barrier and sprinted to the finish line, winning the race by less than half a second.","t":"那名跑者跨過最後一道欄架，衝向終點線，以不到半秒的差距贏得比賽。","a":"hurdled"},{"w":"hurdles","p":"n.","d":"a race in which runners jump over barriers","c":"跨欄賽跑","s":"My sister trains for the 100-meter hurdles every morning, jumping over ten barriers as fast as she can.","t":"我姐姐每天早上為一百公尺跨欄練習，盡可能快速地跳過十道欄架。"},{"w":"clear a hurdle","p":"v.phr.","d":"to get past a difficulty","c":"跨過一道障礙","s":"The new medicine has cleared a hurdle by passing its first safety test, but it still needs two more years of study.","t":"這種新藥通過了第一次安全測試，跨過了一道障礙，但它還需要再研究兩年。","a":"cleared a hurdle"},{"w":"hybrid","p":"n.","d":"something made by mixing two different things; a car that uses both gas and electricity","c":"混合物；雜交種；油電混合車","s":"My father bought a hybrid last year because it uses both gasoline and electricity and saves a lot of money on fuel.","t":"我爸爸去年買了一輛油電混合車，因為它同時使用汽油和電力，能省下很多油錢。","h":1},{"w":"hybrid","p":"adj.","d":"mixing two different things or ways","c":"混合的；雜交的","s":"Many companies now offer hybrid work, so employees spend three days at the office and two days working from home.","t":"許多公司現在提供混合工作模式，所以員工三天在辦公室、兩天在家工作。"},{"w":"hybrid car","p":"n.phr.","d":"a car with both a gas engine and an electric motor","c":"油電混合車","s":"A hybrid car switches to its electric motor in slow city traffic, which makes it quieter and much cleaner than a normal car.","t":"油電混合車在緩慢的市區車流中會切換成電動馬達，這讓它比一般汽車更安靜也乾淨得多。"},{"w":"hybrid rice","p":"n.phr.","d":"rice made by mixing two kinds of rice plants","c":"雜交稻","s":"Scientists in Asia developed hybrid rice that grows faster and gives more food per field, helping to feed millions of people.","t":"亞洲的科學家培育出生長更快、每塊田產量更多的雜交稻，幫助養活了數百萬人。"},{"w":"hygiene","p":"n.","d":"keeping yourself and your surroundings clean to stay healthy","c":"衛生","s":"Good hygiene in the kitchen, such as washing your hands and keeping raw meat separate, prevents most cases of food poisoning.","t":"廚房良好的衛生習慣，例如洗手和把生肉分開放，可以預防大多數的食物中毒。","h":1},{"w":"hygienic","p":"adj.","d":"clean and not likely to cause illness","c":"衛生的","s":"The street food stand looked clean and hygienic, with the cook wearing gloves and all the dishes covered from flies.","t":"這個街頭小吃攤看起來乾淨又衛生，廚師戴著手套，所有的菜都蓋著以防蒼蠅。"},{"w":"personal hygiene","p":"n.phr.","d":"keeping your own body clean","c":"個人衛生","s":"The school nurse gave a talk about personal hygiene, reminding students to shower after sports and brush their teeth twice a day.","t":"學校護士做了一場關於個人衛生的演講，提醒學生運動後要洗澡，而且每天刷牙兩次。"},{"w":"unhygienic","p":"adj.","d":"dirty and likely to cause illness","c":"不衛生的","s":"The restaurant was closed by the city because its unhygienic kitchen had old food on the floor and insects in the rice.","t":"這家餐廳被市政府勒令停業，因為它不衛生的廚房地板上有腐壞的食物，米裡還有蟲。"},{"w":"hypocrite","p":"n.","d":"a person who says one thing but does the opposite","c":"偽君子","s":"He tells his children never to lie, yet he lies to his boss every week; such a hypocrite cannot expect his kids to respect him.","t":"他告訴孩子絕不能說謊，自己卻每週都對老闆說謊；這樣的偽君子不能指望孩子尊敬他。","h":1},{"w":"hypocrisy","p":"n.","d":"behavior in which someone pretends to have beliefs they do not really have","c":"偽善","s":"It is pure hypocrisy for the politician to talk about saving energy while he flies around the country in a private jet.","t":"那位政治人物一邊談節約能源，一邊坐私人飛機全國飛來飛去，這純粹是偽善。"},{"w":"hypocritical","p":"adj.","d":"saying one thing but doing the opposite","c":"偽善的","s":"It would be hypocritical of me to complain about people using their phones at dinner when I check mine every five minutes.","t":"我自己每五分鐘就看一次手機，卻抱怨別人吃晚餐時用手機，這會是很偽善的。"},{"w":"iceberg","p":"n.","d":"a very large piece of ice floating in the sea","c":"冰山","s":"The ship hit an iceberg in the dark and sank within three hours, and more than a thousand passengers lost their lives.","t":"那艘船在黑暗中撞上一座冰山，三小時內就沉沒了，一千多名乘客喪生。","h":1},{"w":"the tip of the iceberg","p":"n.phr.","d":"a small part of a much bigger problem","c":"冰山一角","s":"The ten cases reported this week are only the tip of the iceberg; the doctor believes hundreds more people are sick but have not seen a doctor.","t":"這週通報的十個病例只是冰山一角；醫生相信還有數百人生病了但沒有去看醫生。"},{"w":"iceberg lettuce","p":"n.phr.","d":"a round, pale green lettuce with crisp leaves","c":"結球萵苣；美生菜","s":"The sandwich comes with tomatoes and crisp iceberg lettuce, which stays fresh longer than the soft green leaves.","t":"這份三明治配有番茄和爽脆的美生菜，它比柔軟的綠葉菜更能保持新鮮。"},{"w":"icy","p":"adj.","d":"covered with ice; extremely cold","c":"結冰的；冰冷的","s":"Be careful on the icy steps this morning, because two people have already slipped and fallen in front of the building.","t":"今天早上走結冰的台階要小心，因為已經有兩個人在大樓前滑倒了。"},{"w":"illuminate","p":"v.","d":"to shine light on something","c":"照亮","s":"At night, hundreds of small lamps illuminate the old bridge, and couples like to walk across it to enjoy the view of the river.","t":"夜晚，數百盞小燈照亮了這座老橋，情侶們喜歡走過橋上欣賞河景。","h":1},{"w":"illuminate","p":"v.","d":"to make something clear and easy to understand","c":"闡明；說明","s":"The teacher used a simple story about two farmers to illuminate the difficult idea of supply and demand for the class.","t":"老師用一個關於兩個農夫的簡單故事，向全班闡明供給與需求這個困難的概念。"},{"w":"illumination","p":"n.","d":"light; the act of lighting something","c":"照明；燈飾","s":"The illumination in the museum is kept low to protect the old paintings, so visitors sometimes need a minute for their eyes to adjust.","t":"博物館的照明保持微弱以保護古畫，所以參觀者有時需要一分鐘讓眼睛適應。"},{"w":"illuminating","p":"adj.","d":"helping you understand something better","c":"有啟發性的","s":"The documentary about plastic in the ocean was so illuminating that our whole class decided to stop using plastic straws.","t":"那部關於海洋塑膠的紀錄片非常有啟發性，我們全班決定不再使用塑膠吸管。"},{"w":"imminent","p":"adj.","d":"going to happen very soon","c":"迫在眉睫的；即將發生的","s":"The dark clouds and the sudden cold wind warned the fishermen that a storm was imminent, so they hurried back to the harbor.","t":"烏雲和突然的冷風警告漁民暴風雨即將來臨，所以他們趕緊回到港口。","h":1},{"w":"imminently","p":"adv.","d":"very soon","c":"即刻地；很快地","s":"The company announced that the new phone would be released imminently, and fans lined up outside the stores the same evening.","t":"公司宣布新手機很快就會上市，粉絲們當天晚上就在店外排隊了。"},{"w":"in imminent danger","p":"n.phr.","d":"about to be hurt or killed","c":"處於迫切的危險中","s":"The rescue team said the climbers were in imminent danger because the temperature was dropping fast and they had no tent.","t":"救援隊說那些登山客處於迫切的危險中，因為氣溫正在快速下降，而他們沒有帳篷。"},{"w":"imperative","p":"adj.","d":"extremely important and urgent","c":"必要的；緊急的","s":"It is imperative that everyone leaves the building immediately when the fire alarm rings, even if they think it is only a practice.","t":"火警鈴響時每個人立刻離開大樓是絕對必要的，即使他們認為那只是演習。","h":1},{"w":"imperative","p":"n.","d":"something that must be done","c":"必要的事；當務之急","s":"Protecting clean water has become an imperative for the city, because its population has doubled in only twenty years.","t":"保護乾淨的水源已成為這座城市的當務之急，因為它的人口在短短二十年內增加了一倍。"},{"w":"the imperative","p":"n.phr.","d":"the form of a verb used for orders, such as \"Sit down\"","c":"祈使語氣","s":"In English, we use the imperative to give orders or instructions, such as \"Close the door\" or \"Please sit down.\"","t":"在英文裡，我們用祈使語氣來下命令或給指示，例如「關門」或「請坐下」。"},{"w":"imperial","p":"adj.","d":"connected with an empire or an emperor","c":"帝國的；皇帝的","s":"Visitors to Beijing love to walk through the imperial palace, where Chinese emperors lived for almost five hundred years.","t":"到北京的遊客喜歡走進皇宮，中國皇帝在那裡住了將近五百年。","h":1},{"w":"empire","p":"n.","d":"a group of countries ruled by one person or government","c":"帝國","s":"The Roman Empire once ruled lands from Britain to Egypt, and its roads and buildings can still be seen today.","t":"羅馬帝國曾經統治從英國到埃及的土地，它的道路和建築至今仍然可見。","a":"Empire"},{"w":"emperor","p":"n.","d":"the ruler of an empire","c":"皇帝","s":"The young emperor took the throne at the age of six, so his mother and uncles made most of the decisions for him.","t":"這位年輕的皇帝六歲就登上王位，所以大部分的決定都由他的母親和叔叔們代他做。"},{"w":"imperialism","p":"n.","d":"a system in which one country controls other countries","c":"帝國主義","s":"In the nineteenth century, imperialism led European countries to take control of large parts of Africa and Asia.","t":"十九世紀時，帝國主義導致歐洲國家控制了非洲和亞洲的大片土地。"},{"w":"implicit","p":"adj.","d":"suggested but not said directly","c":"隱含的；不言明的","s":"There was an implicit promise in the manager's words that anyone who worked hard this year would get a pay raise in January.","t":"經理的話裡有一個隱含的承諾：今年努力工作的人一月都會加薪。","h":1},{"w":"implicitly","p":"adv.","d":"in a way that is suggested but not said directly","c":"含蓄地；暗中","s":"By saying nothing when the boys laughed at the new student, the teacher implicitly allowed the bullying to continue.","t":"男孩們嘲笑新同學時老師什麼都沒說，這等於暗中允許霸凌繼續下去。"},{"w":"explicit","p":"adj.","d":"said clearly and directly","c":"明確的","s":"The instructions on the box are very explicit: add two cups of water, stir for one minute, and wait five minutes before eating.","t":"盒子上的說明非常明確：加兩杯水，攪拌一分鐘，等五分鐘再吃。"},{"w":"imply","p":"v.","d":"to suggest something without saying it directly","c":"暗示","s":"I did not mean to imply that you were lazy; I only wanted to say that you could finish the report faster with some help.","t":"我不是要暗示你懶惰；我只是想說有人幫忙的話你可以更快完成報告。"},{"w":"imposing","p":"adj.","d":"large and impressive","c":"雄偉的；令人印象深刻的","s":"The new library is an imposing building with tall stone columns, and it can be seen from almost every part of the town.","t":"新圖書館是一棟有高大石柱的雄偉建築，從鎮上幾乎每個地方都看得到。","h":1},{"w":"impose","p":"v.","d":"to force people to accept a rule, tax, or idea","c":"強加；徵收","s":"The government decided to impose a new tax on sugary drinks to encourage people to choose water or tea instead.","t":"政府決定對含糖飲料徵收新稅，以鼓勵人們改選擇水或茶。"},{"w":"impose on","p":"v.phr.","d":"to cause trouble for someone by asking them to do something for you","c":"打擾；麻煩","s":"I do not want to impose on your family, so I will stay at a hotel instead of sleeping in your spare room.","t":"我不想麻煩你的家人，所以我會住旅館，而不是睡在你們的客房。"},{"w":"imposition","p":"n.","d":"something that causes trouble or extra work for someone","c":"強加的負擔；麻煩","s":"Asking the neighbors to feed our cat for a whole month felt like an imposition, so we hired a pet sitter instead.","t":"請鄰居幫忙餵我們的貓整整一個月感覺像是一種負擔，所以我們改請了寵物保姆。"},{"w":"imprison","p":"v.","d":"to put someone in prison","c":"監禁","s":"The judge decided to imprison the thief for three years because it was the fourth time he had stolen from the same store.","t":"法官決定監禁這名小偷三年，因為這已經是他第四次在同一家店偷東西。","h":1},{"w":"imprisonment","p":"n.","d":"the state of being kept in prison","c":"監禁","s":"He was sentenced to ten years' imprisonment for selling drugs, and his family cried quietly as he was led out of the court.","t":"他因販毒被判十年監禁，當他被帶出法庭時，他的家人默默地哭泣。"},{"w":"prison","p":"n.","d":"a building where criminals are kept as punishment","c":"監獄","s":"After leaving prison, the man found it hard to get a job because few employers wanted to hire someone with a criminal record.","t":"離開監獄後，這名男子發現很難找到工作，因為很少雇主願意雇用有犯罪紀錄的人。"},{"w":"prisoner","p":"n.","d":"a person who is kept in prison","c":"囚犯","s":"The prisoner spent his days in the small cell reading books and writing letters to his daughter, whom he had not seen for years.","t":"這名囚犯在小牢房裡讀書、寫信給多年未見的女兒，度過一天又一天。"},{"w":"life imprisonment","p":"n.phr.","d":"the punishment of staying in prison for the rest of your life","c":"無期徒刑","s":"The killer received life imprisonment instead of the death penalty because he was only eighteen when the crime happened.","t":"這名兇手被判無期徒刑而非死刑，因為犯案時他只有十八歲。"},{"w":"incline","p":"v.","d":"to feel that you want to do or believe something","c":"傾向於","s":"I incline to believe her story, because she has never lied to me in the ten years we have been friends.","t":"我傾向於相信她的說法，因為在我們當朋友的十年裡她從未對我說謊。","h":1},{"w":"incline","p":"n.","d":"a slope","c":"斜坡","s":"The old train slowed down on the steep incline outside the town, and passengers could see the tea fields on both sides.","t":"老火車在鎮外陡峭的斜坡上放慢了速度，乘客可以看到兩旁的茶園。"},{"w":"be inclined to","p":"v.phr.","d":"to tend to do something; to want to do something","c":"傾向於；有…的傾向","s":"My grandmother is inclined to trust anyone with a kind face, so we have to protect her from telephone scams.","t":"我奶奶傾向於相信任何面相和善的人，所以我們必須保護她不受電話詐騙。","a":"is inclined to"},{"w":"inclination","p":"n.","d":"a feeling that makes you want to do something","c":"傾向；意願","s":"After working twelve hours, I had no inclination to cook, so I ordered a bowl of noodles from the shop downstairs.","t":"工作了十二個小時後，我完全沒有做飯的意願，所以就向樓下的店叫了一碗麵。"},{"w":"inclusive","p":"adj.","d":"including everyone, especially people who are often left out","c":"包容的；包含所有人的","s":"The school is proud of its inclusive sports day, where students with disabilities compete side by side with their classmates.","t":"學校以其包容的運動會為榮，身心障礙的學生和同學們並肩競賽。","h":1},{"w":"inclusive","p":"adj.","d":"(of a price) including everything","c":"包含在內的（價格）","s":"The price of the tour is inclusive of meals and hotel rooms, so you only need to bring money for souvenirs.","t":"這趟旅遊的價格包含餐點和飯店房間，所以你只需要帶買紀念品的錢。"},{"w":"include","p":"v.","d":"to have something as a part","c":"包括","s":"The ticket price does not include the boat ride, so you will need to pay another two hundred dollars at the pier.","t":"票價不包括搭船，所以你需要在碼頭另外付兩百元。"},{"w":"inclusion","p":"n.","d":"the act of including something or someone","c":"包含；納入","s":"The inclusion of a Taiwanese dish on the airline's menu made many passengers from Taiwan feel proud and happy.","t":"航空公司菜單上納入了一道台灣菜，讓許多來自台灣的乘客感到驕傲又開心。"},{"w":"incur","p":"v.","d":"to have to pay a cost or suffer something bad because of what you did","c":"招致；遭受（損失、費用）","s":"If you pay the bill late, you will incur an extra fee of two hundred dollars, so please pay before the end of the month.","t":"如果你延遲付帳單，就會招致兩百元的額外費用，所以請在月底前付款。","h":1},{"w":"incur sb's anger","p":"v.phr.","d":"to make someone angry because of what you did","c":"招致某人的憤怒","s":"The young clerk incurred the manager's anger by losing the important contract, and nobody in the office dared to speak to the boss all day.","t":"這位年輕職員因為弄丟了重要合約而招致經理的憤怒，辦公室裡一整天沒有人敢和老闆說話。","a":"incurred the manager's anger"},{"w":"incur a loss","p":"v.phr.","d":"to lose money","c":"蒙受損失","s":"The company incurred a loss of millions of dollars when the typhoon destroyed its factory in southern Taiwan last September.","t":"去年九月颱風摧毀了公司在南台灣的工廠時，公司蒙受了數百萬元的損失。","a":"incurred a loss"},{"w":"indifference","p":"n.","d":"a lack of interest or care","c":"漠不關心","s":"The students' indifference to the school election worried the teachers, because fewer than half of them bothered to vote.","t":"學生對學校選舉的漠不關心讓老師們擔憂，因為不到一半的人願意去投票。","h":1},{"w":"indifferent","p":"adj.","d":"not interested in or caring about something","c":"冷漠的；不感興趣的","s":"My brother is completely indifferent to fashion and wears the same gray T-shirt and jeans almost every day of the year.","t":"我哥哥對時尚完全不感興趣，一年裡幾乎每天都穿同一件灰色 T 恤和牛仔褲。"},{"w":"be indifferent to","p":"v.phr.","d":"to not care about something","c":"對…漠不關心","s":"We cannot be indifferent to the plastic in the ocean, because it ends up in the fish that we eat.","t":"我們不能對海洋中的塑膠漠不關心，因為它最後會進入我們吃的魚裡。"},{"w":"indignant","p":"adj.","d":"angry because something is unfair","c":"憤慨的","s":"The customers were indignant when the restaurant charged them for water, and several of them left without ordering any food.","t":"餐廳向顧客收水費時，顧客們很憤慨，有幾位沒點任何食物就離開了。","h":1},{"w":"indignation","p":"n.","d":"anger caused by something unfair","c":"憤慨","s":"There was public indignation when the news showed the factory pouring dirty water into the river that supplies the town.","t":"新聞播出工廠把髒水倒進供應鎮上用水的河裡時，引起了大眾的憤慨。"},{"w":"indignantly","p":"adv.","d":"in an angry way because of something unfair","c":"憤慨地","s":"\"I have never cheated in my life!\" the student said indignantly when the teacher asked where the answers had come from.","t":"當老師問答案是從哪裡來的時，那位學生憤慨地說：「我這輩子從沒作弊過！」"},{"w":"induce","p":"v.","d":"to cause something to happen; to persuade someone to do something","c":"誘發；引起；勸誘","s":"Loud music and bright lights can induce headaches in some people, so the shop decided to turn the volume down.","t":"大聲的音樂和強光會引起某些人頭痛，所以商店決定把音量調低。","h":1},{"w":"induce sb to do","p":"v.phr.","d":"to persuade someone to do something","c":"勸誘某人做…","s":"Nothing could induce my grandfather to sell the old farmhouse, even when a company offered him a very high price.","t":"沒有任何事能勸誘我爺爺賣掉老農舍，即使有公司開出非常高的價錢。","a":"induce my grandfather to"},{"w":"inducement","p":"n.","d":"something that persuades you to do something","c":"誘因；獎勵","s":"The company offered a free laptop as an inducement for new customers to sign a two-year contract for its internet service.","t":"這家公司提供免費筆電作為誘因，吸引新顧客簽兩年的網路服務合約。"},{"w":"industrialize","p":"v.","d":"to develop many factories and industries in a country or area","c":"工業化","s":"Taiwan began to industrialize quickly in the 1960s, and within thirty years it changed from a farming island into a center of high technology.","t":"台灣在 1960 年代開始快速工業化，三十年內從一個農業島嶼變成高科技中心。","h":1},{"w":"industrial","p":"adj.","d":"connected with factories and the making of goods","c":"工業的","s":"The air in the industrial area near the port is often gray, because the factories there run their machines day and night.","t":"港口附近工業區的空氣常常是灰色的，因為那裡的工廠日夜不停地運轉機器。"},{"w":"industry","p":"n.","d":"the making of goods in factories; a particular kind of business","c":"工業；產業","s":"The tourism industry in Kenting depends on the summer months, when thousands of visitors come to swim and surf.","t":"墾丁的觀光產業依賴夏季月份，那時有數千名遊客前來游泳和衝浪。"},{"w":"industrialization","p":"n.","d":"the process of developing industries in a country","c":"工業化","s":"Rapid industrialization brought jobs and money to the city, but it also filled the rivers with waste and the air with smoke.","t":"快速的工業化為這座城市帶來工作和金錢，但也讓河流充滿廢棄物、空氣充滿煙霧。"},{"w":"infectious","p":"adj.","d":"(of a disease) able to spread from one person to another","c":"傳染性的","s":"Chickenpox is highly infectious, so children who catch it must stay home from school until all the spots have dried.","t":"水痘具有高度傳染性，所以得病的孩子必須待在家裡不上學，直到所有的疹子都乾了。","h":1},{"w":"infectious","p":"adj.","d":"(of a feeling) spreading quickly to other people","c":"有感染力的","s":"Her laugh is so infectious that even the grumpiest customers in the shop end up smiling by the time they leave.","t":"她的笑聲非常有感染力，連店裡脾氣最壞的顧客離開時也都笑了。"},{"w":"infect","p":"v.","d":"to give a disease to someone; to make something dirty with germs","c":"感染","s":"Wash the cut carefully with clean water, or dirt from the playground may infect the wound and make it swell.","t":"用乾淨的水仔細清洗傷口，否則操場上的髒東西可能會感染傷口並使它腫起來。"},{"w":"infection","p":"n.","d":"an illness caused by germs entering the body","c":"感染","s":"The doctor gave me medicine for an ear infection, and she said the pain should go away in two or three days.","t":"醫生給我治療耳朵感染的藥，她說疼痛應該會在兩三天內消失。"},{"w":"infer","p":"v.","d":"to decide that something is true from the information you have","c":"推論；推斷","s":"From the muddy boots by the door, we could infer that Dad had been working in the garden all morning.","t":"從門邊沾滿泥的靴子，我們可以推斷爸爸整個早上都在花園裡工作。","h":1},{"w":"inference","p":"n.","d":"a conclusion you reach from the information you have","c":"推論","s":"Reading tests often ask you to make an inference about how a character feels from what he says and does.","t":"閱讀測驗常要求你從角色的言行推論出他的感受。"},{"w":"infer from","p":"v.phr.","d":"to reach a conclusion from certain facts","c":"從…推斷","s":"What can you infer from the empty plates and happy faces? The dinner must have been a great success.","t":"你能從空盤子和開心的表情推斷出什麼？這頓晚餐一定非常成功。"},{"w":"inflict","p":"v.","d":"to make someone suffer something bad","c":"造成（傷害）；施加","s":"The typhoon inflicted serious damage on the small fishing villages along the east coast, and many boats were destroyed.","t":"颱風對東海岸的小漁村造成嚴重的損害，許多船隻都被摧毀了。","a":"inflicted","h":1},{"w":"inflict pain on","p":"v.phr.","d":"to cause someone to feel pain","c":"使…痛苦","s":"A good doctor tries never to inflict pain on a patient unnecessarily, so she explains every step before the treatment begins.","t":"好醫生盡量不會不必要地使病人痛苦，所以她在治療開始前會解釋每一個步驟。"},{"w":"infliction","p":"n.","d":"the act of making someone suffer something","c":"施加（痛苦）","s":"The infliction of cruel punishments on prisoners is against the law in most countries of the world today.","t":"如今在世界上大多數國家，對囚犯施加殘酷的懲罰是違法的。"},{"w":"inhabit","p":"v.","d":"to live in a place","c":"居住於；棲息於","s":"Only a few hundred people inhabit the tiny island, and most of them make their living by fishing or growing vegetables.","t":"只有幾百人居住在這座小島上，他們大多以捕魚或種菜為生。","h":1},{"w":"inhabitant","p":"n.","d":"a person or animal that lives in a place","c":"居民","s":"The oldest inhabitant of the village is a woman of 102, and she still remembers the first car that ever drove into town.","t":"村裡最年長的居民是一位 102 歲的女士，她還記得第一輛開進鎮上的汽車。"},{"w":"habitat","p":"n.","d":"the natural place where an animal or plant lives","c":"棲息地","s":"Cutting down the forest destroys the habitat of many birds and animals, which then have nowhere to live or find food.","t":"砍伐森林會破壞許多鳥類和動物的棲息地，牠們之後就無處可住，也找不到食物。"},{"w":"uninhabited","p":"adj.","d":"with no people living there","c":"無人居住的","s":"The sailors landed on an uninhabited island, where there were no houses, no roads, and no sign that any person had ever lived there.","t":"水手們登上一座無人居住的島，那裡沒有房子、沒有道路，也沒有任何人曾經住過的跡象。"}]},{"unit":19,"theme":"inhabitant – isle","cards":[{"w":"inhabitant","p":"n.","d":"a person or animal that lives in a place","c":"居民","s":"The small island has only about two hundred inhabitants, and most of them make a living by fishing in the nearby waters.","t":"這座小島只有大約兩百名居民，而且大多數人靠在附近海域捕魚維生。","a":"inhabitants","h":1},{"w":"inhabit","p":"v.","d":"to live in a place","c":"居住於；棲息於","s":"Many rare birds inhabit this wetland, so visitors are asked to stay on the wooden paths and keep quiet.","t":"許多稀有的鳥類棲息於這片濕地，所以遊客被要求待在木棧道上並保持安靜。"},{"w":"habitat","p":"n.","d":"the natural home of a plant or animal","c":"棲息地","s":"When forests are cut down for farmland, wild animals lose their natural habitat and often come into villages looking for food.","t":"當森林被砍伐成農地時，野生動物失去了天然的棲息地，常常跑進村子裡找食物。"},{"w":"uninhabited","p":"adj.","d":"with no people living there","c":"無人居住的","s":"The ship stopped at an uninhabited island, where the sailors found fresh water but no sign of people anywhere.","t":"船停靠在一座無人居住的島上，水手們在那裡找到了淡水，卻完全看不到人的蹤跡。"},{"w":"injustice","p":"n.","d":"the fact of a situation being unfair","c":"不公正；不公平的事","s":"Martin Luther King Jr. spent his whole life fighting against injustice, and his speeches still inspire people around the world today.","t":"馬丁・路德・金恩博士一生都在對抗不公正，他的演講至今仍激勵著世界各地的人。","h":1},{"w":"justice","p":"n.","d":"fair treatment; the law and courts","c":"正義；公正；司法","s":"The victim's family waited ten years for justice, and they cried when the judge finally sent the criminal to prison.","t":"受害者的家人等了十年才等到正義，當法官終於把罪犯送進監獄時，他們哭了。"},{"w":"unjust","p":"adj.","d":"not fair","c":"不公正的","s":"Many workers felt that the new rule was unjust because only the youngest employees were asked to work on weekends.","t":"許多員工覺得新規定不公平，因為只有最年輕的員工被要求在週末工作。"},{"w":"do sb an injustice","p":"v.phr.","d":"to judge someone unfairly","c":"對某人不公平；冤枉某人","s":"If you say Tom is lazy, you do him an injustice, because he stayed up all night finishing the group report by himself.","t":"如果你說湯姆懶惰，那你就是對他不公平，因為他熬了整夜獨自完成小組報告。","a":"do him an injustice"},{"w":"inland","p":"adj.","d":"far from the sea; in the middle of a country","c":"內陸的","s":"Because our town is an inland city far from the coast, fresh seafood here is much more expensive than in Keelung.","t":"因為我們的城鎮是遠離海岸的內陸城市，這裡的新鮮海產比基隆貴得多。","h":1},{"w":"inland","p":"adv.","d":"toward the middle of a country, away from the sea","c":"向內陸","s":"After the typhoon warning, many fishing families moved inland to stay with relatives until the strong winds passed.","t":"颱風警報發布後，許多漁民家庭往內陸移動，到親戚家暫住直到強風過去。"},{"w":"land","p":"n.","d":"the solid part of the earth, not the sea","c":"陸地；土地","s":"After three weeks at sea, the sailors were overjoyed to see land and shouted with happiness when the ship reached the harbor.","t":"在海上三週後，水手們看到陸地時欣喜若狂，船進港時他們高興地大喊。"},{"w":"mainland","p":"n.","d":"the main part of a country, not its islands","c":"大陸；本土","s":"The ferry from Penghu to the mainland takes about two hours, and many students use it to go to university in Kaohsiung.","t":"從澎湖到本島的渡輪大約要兩小時，許多學生搭它去高雄上大學。"},{"w":"innumerable","p":"adj.","d":"too many to be counted","c":"無數的","s":"On a clear night in the mountains, you can see innumerable stars, far more than you could ever see from the city.","t":"在山上晴朗的夜晚，你可以看到無數的星星，比你在城市裡能看到的多得多。","h":1},{"w":"numerous","p":"adj.","d":"many","c":"許多的；為數眾多的","s":"The school received numerous complaints about the new lunch menu, so the principal promised to bring back the popular fried chicken.","t":"學校收到許多關於新午餐菜單的抱怨，所以校長答應把受歡迎的炸雞加回來。"},{"w":"number","p":"n.","d":"an amount of people or things","c":"數量；數字","s":"The number of tourists visiting Taiwan has grown quickly since the new direct flights from Europe began last year.","t":"自從去年歐洲直飛航班開航以來，來台灣觀光的遊客數量快速成長。"},{"w":"numerical","p":"adj.","d":"shown as numbers or in the order of numbers","c":"數字的；按數字順序的","s":"Please arrange the files in numerical order so that the staff can find any customer's record in just a few seconds.","t":"請把檔案按數字順序排好，這樣員工幾秒鐘內就能找到任何一位客戶的紀錄。"},{"w":"inquire","p":"v.","d":"to ask for information","c":"詢問；查詢","s":"Before booking the hotel, my mother called to inquire whether breakfast was included in the price of the room.","t":"訂飯店之前，我媽媽打電話詢問房價是否包含早餐。","h":1},{"w":"inquire about","p":"v.phr.","d":"to ask for information about something","c":"詢問關於…","s":"A customer phoned this morning to inquire about the red bicycle in the window, but it had already been sold.","t":"今天早上一位顧客打電話來詢問櫥窗裡那輛紅色腳踏車，但它已經賣掉了。"},{"w":"inquiry","p":"n.","d":"a question or request for information","c":"詢問；調查","s":"The company set up a special phone line to answer every inquiry about the new electric scooter before it goes on sale.","t":"公司在新款電動機車上市前設了一條專線，回答關於它的每一個詢問。"},{"w":"make inquiries","p":"v.phr.","d":"to ask people questions to find something out","c":"打聽；查詢","s":"The police are making inquiries in the neighborhood to find out whether anyone saw the missing boy on Friday afternoon.","t":"警方正在這個社區打聽，想找出星期五下午是否有人看到那個失蹤的男孩。","a":"making inquiries"},{"w":"insistence","p":"n.","d":"the act of saying firmly that something must happen or is true","c":"堅持","s":"At my grandmother's insistence, we all stayed for dinner even though we had planned to leave before dark.","t":"在奶奶的堅持下，我們全都留下來吃晚餐，雖然原本打算天黑前離開。","h":1},{"w":"insist","p":"v.","d":"to say firmly that something must happen or is true","c":"堅持；堅決主張","s":"Although I offered to pay for the meal, my uncle would insist on paying because he said I was still a student.","t":"雖然我提議請客，我叔叔還是堅持付錢，因為他說我還是學生。"},{"w":"insist on","p":"v.phr.","d":"to demand something firmly","c":"堅持要…","s":"My father always insists on checking the weather report before any family trip, even if the sky looks perfectly clear.","t":"我爸爸在每次家庭旅行前總是堅持要看天氣預報，即使天空看起來非常晴朗。","a":"insists on"},{"w":"insistent","p":"adj.","d":"demanding something firmly and not giving up","c":"堅持的；執意的","s":"The little girl was so insistent about getting a puppy that her parents finally agreed to visit the animal shelter.","t":"小女孩對養小狗這件事太堅持了，她的父母最後同意去動物收容所看看。"},{"w":"instinctive","p":"adj.","d":"done without thinking, from a natural feeling","c":"本能的；直覺的","s":"When the ball flew toward her face, Amy's instinctive reaction was to close her eyes and raise both hands.","t":"當球朝她的臉飛過來時，艾咪本能的反應是閉上眼睛並舉起雙手。","h":1},{"w":"instinct","p":"n.","d":"a natural ability or feeling that makes you act without thinking","c":"本能；直覺","s":"Baby turtles use instinct to find the sea as soon as they leave their eggs, and nobody has to teach them.","t":"小海龜一離開蛋就憑本能找到大海，沒有人需要教它們。"},{"w":"instinctively","p":"adv.","d":"without thinking, because of a natural feeling","c":"本能地","s":"The mother instinctively grabbed her son's arm when a motorcycle suddenly came around the corner at high speed.","t":"當一輛機車突然高速轉過街角時，那位母親本能地抓住兒子的手臂。"},{"w":"by instinct","p":"phr.","d":"because of a natural feeling, not because of learning","c":"憑本能","s":"Birds know by instinct when to fly south for the winter, even if they have never made the long journey before.","t":"鳥類憑本能知道何時該往南飛過冬，即使它們以前從未進行過這段漫長的旅程。"},{"w":"intake","p":"n.","d":"the amount of food, drink, etc. that you take into your body","c":"攝取量","s":"The doctor told my father to reduce his daily salt intake because his blood pressure has been too high this year.","t":"醫生要我爸爸減少每天的鹽分攝取量，因為他今年的血壓一直太高。","h":1},{"w":"take in","p":"v.phr.","d":"to absorb something into the body","c":"吸收；攝取","s":"Plants take in carbon dioxide from the air during the day and turn it into the oxygen that we need to breathe.","t":"植物在白天從空氣中吸收二氧化碳，並把它轉變成我們呼吸所需要的氧氣。"},{"w":"take, took, taken","p":"v.","d":"to swallow medicine; to get hold of something","c":"服用；拿取","s":"Remember to take this medicine twice a day after meals, and do not drink coffee or tea within an hour.","t":"記得一天兩次飯後服用這個藥，而且一小時內不要喝咖啡或茶。","a":"take"},{"w":"intake","p":"n.","d":"the number of people accepted into a school or organization","c":"錄取人數；吸收的人數","s":"The university's intake of foreign students has doubled since it started offering more classes taught in English.","t":"自從這所大學開始提供更多英語授課的課程後，外籍學生的錄取人數翻了一倍。"},{"w":"intellect","p":"n.","d":"the ability to think, understand, and learn","c":"智力；才智","s":"Albert Einstein was famous not only for his great intellect but also for his kind heart and his sense of humor.","t":"愛因斯坦不只因為他卓越的才智而聞名，也因為他善良的心和幽默感。","h":1},{"w":"intellectual","p":"adj.","d":"connected with thinking and understanding","c":"智力的；知識的","s":"Reading difficult books and solving puzzles are good intellectual exercises that keep your brain active as you get older.","t":"閱讀困難的書和解謎是很好的智力鍛鍊，能讓你的大腦在年紀漸長時保持活躍。"},{"w":"intellectual","p":"n.","d":"a person who thinks deeply and is well educated","c":"知識分子","s":"In the 1920s, many young intellectuals met in Paris cafés to discuss art, politics, and the future of their countries.","t":"一九二〇年代，許多年輕的知識分子在巴黎的咖啡館聚會，討論藝術、政治和他們國家的未來。","a":"intellectuals"},{"w":"intelligence","p":"n.","d":"the ability to learn and understand things","c":"智慧；智力","s":"Dolphins show a high level of intelligence, and scientists have found that they can even call each other by name.","t":"海豚展現出高度的智慧，科學家發現它們甚至能用名字互相呼喚。"},{"w":"intelligent","p":"adj.","d":"clever; able to learn and understand quickly","c":"聰明的","s":"My neighbor's dog is so intelligent that it can open the gate by itself and bring the newspaper to the door.","t":"我鄰居的狗聰明到可以自己開大門，還會把報紙拿到門口。"},{"w":"interpreter","p":"n.","d":"a person who translates spoken words from one language into another","c":"口譯員","s":"Because the visiting doctor spoke only French, the hospital hired an interpreter to help him talk with the patients.","t":"因為來訪的醫生只會說法語，醫院僱了一位口譯員幫助他和病人溝通。","h":1},{"w":"interpret","p":"v.","d":"to translate spoken words; to explain the meaning of something","c":"口譯；解釋","s":"Could you interpret for my grandmother at the bank tomorrow, since she speaks only Taiwanese and the new clerk does not understand it?","t":"明天你能在銀行幫我奶奶口譯嗎？因為她只會說台語，而新來的行員聽不懂。"},{"w":"interpretation","p":"n.","d":"an explanation of the meaning of something","c":"解釋；詮釋","s":"The two critics gave completely different interpretations of the film's ending, so the audience left the theater still arguing.","t":"兩位影評人對電影結局提出了完全不同的詮釋，所以觀眾離開電影院時還在爭論。","a":"interpretations"},{"w":"misinterpret","p":"v.","d":"to understand something wrongly","c":"誤解；曲解","s":"I am afraid you misinterpreted my message; I was not angry at all, I simply forgot to add a smiley face.","t":"我想你誤解了我的訊息；我一點都沒有生氣，只是忘了加笑臉而已。","a":"misinterpreted"},{"w":"intersection","p":"n.","d":"a place where two roads cross","c":"十字路口；交叉口","s":"Turn left at the next intersection, and you will see the post office right across from the 7-Eleven.","t":"在下一個十字路口左轉，你就會看到郵局就在 7-Eleven 的正對面。","h":1},{"w":"intersect","p":"v.","d":"to cross each other","c":"相交；交叉","s":"The two main roads intersect in the center of town, which is why there is always a traffic jam there at five o'clock.","t":"這兩條主要道路在市中心交會，這就是為什麼那裡五點時總是塞車。"},{"w":"section","p":"n.","d":"one of the parts that something is divided into","c":"部分；區域","s":"The library has a special section for children on the second floor, with small chairs and hundreds of picture books.","t":"圖書館二樓有一個專為兒童設的區域，有小椅子和幾百本繪本。"},{"w":"crossroads","p":"n.","d":"a place where roads cross; a time when an important choice must be made","c":"十字路口；人生的轉折點","s":"At the age of eighteen, she stood at a crossroads in her life and had to choose between studying medicine and becoming a dancer.","t":"十八歲時，她站在人生的十字路口，必須在學醫和成為舞者之間做出選擇。"},{"w":"intervene","p":"v.","d":"to become involved in a situation to change what happens","c":"介入；干預","s":"When the two boys started fighting in the hallway, a teacher had to intervene before anyone got seriously hurt.","t":"當兩個男孩開始在走廊打架時，一位老師必須介入，以免有人受重傷。","h":1},{"w":"intervene in","p":"v.phr.","d":"to get involved in a problem or argument","c":"介入…；干預…","s":"Parents should not always intervene in their children's arguments, because kids need to learn how to solve small problems themselves.","t":"父母不應該總是介入孩子們的爭吵，因為孩子需要學習自己解決小問題。"},{"w":"intervention","p":"n.","d":"the act of becoming involved to change a situation","c":"介入；干預","s":"Thanks to the quick intervention of a passing nurse, the old man who fell at the station was saved.","t":"多虧一位路過護理師的迅速介入，在車站跌倒的老先生獲救了。"},{"w":"interfere","p":"v.","d":"to get involved in something that is not your business","c":"干涉；妨礙","s":"Please do not interfere with my work; I know exactly what I am doing, and I will finish it on time.","t":"請不要干涉我的工作；我很清楚自己在做什麼，而且我會準時完成。"},{"w":"intimacy","p":"n.","d":"a close personal relationship","c":"親密；親近","s":"The intimacy between the two sisters was clear to everyone; they shared secrets that nobody else in the family knew.","t":"這兩姊妹之間的親密大家都看得出來；她們分享著家裡其他人都不知道的秘密。","h":1},{"w":"intimate","p":"adj.","d":"very close and friendly; private","c":"親密的；私人的","s":"Only a few intimate friends were invited to the wedding, so the dinner felt warm and relaxed rather than formal.","t":"只有少數幾位親密的朋友受邀參加婚禮，所以晚宴感覺溫馨輕鬆而不是正式。"},{"w":"intimately","p":"adv.","d":"in a close way; in great detail","c":"密切地；親密地；詳盡地","s":"As a tour guide, she knows the old streets of Tainan intimately and can tell a story about almost every temple.","t":"身為導遊，她對台南的老街非常熟悉，幾乎每座廟都能說出一個故事。"},{"w":"be on intimate terms with","p":"v.phr.","d":"to know someone very well and be close to them","c":"與…關係密切","s":"Our manager is on intimate terms with the company's biggest customers, so she often has dinner with them on weekends.","t":"我們的經理與公司最大的客戶關係密切，所以她常常在週末和他們吃晚餐。","a":"is on intimate terms with"},{"w":"intimidate","p":"v.","d":"to frighten someone so that they do what you want","c":"威嚇；恫嚇","s":"The older students tried to intimidate the new boy into giving them his lunch money, but he reported them to the teacher.","t":"那些高年級學生試圖威嚇新來的男孩交出午餐錢，但他向老師舉報了他們。","h":1},{"w":"intimidating","p":"adj.","d":"making you feel frightened or nervous","c":"令人生畏的","s":"The job interview was less intimidating than I had expected, because the manager smiled and chatted with me like an old friend.","t":"這次面試沒有我預期的那麼令人生畏，因為經理微笑著像老朋友一樣和我聊天。"},{"w":"intimidation","p":"n.","d":"the act of frightening someone to make them do something","c":"威嚇；恐嚇","s":"The school has a strict rule against bullying and intimidation, and students who break it may be suspended for a week.","t":"學校有嚴格的規定禁止霸凌和恐嚇，違反的學生可能被停學一週。"},{"w":"timid","p":"adj.","d":"shy and easily frightened","c":"膽小的；羞怯的","s":"The timid kitten hid under the sofa for two whole days before it finally came out to eat from my hand.","t":"那隻膽小的小貓在沙發底下躲了整整兩天，才終於出來吃我手上的食物。"},{"w":"intonation","p":"n.","d":"the rise and fall of the voice when speaking","c":"語調","s":"In English, a rising intonation at the end of a sentence usually shows that the speaker is asking a question.","t":"在英語中，句尾上揚的語調通常表示說話者在問問題。","h":1},{"w":"tone","p":"n.","d":"the quality of a voice that shows feeling","c":"語氣；音調","s":"I could tell from the tone of her voice that she was disappointed, even though she said everything was fine.","t":"我從她說話的語氣聽得出她很失望，雖然她說一切都好。"},{"w":"monotone","p":"n.","d":"a dull voice that stays at the same level","c":"單調的聲音","s":"The speaker read his report in a dull monotone for forty minutes, and half of the audience fell asleep.","t":"演講者用沉悶單調的聲音念了四十分鐘的報告，一半的聽眾都睡著了。"},{"w":"tone of voice","p":"n.phr.","d":"the way your voice sounds when you speak, showing your feelings","c":"說話的語氣","s":"Please watch your tone of voice when you talk to your grandfather; he is old, but he still deserves your respect.","t":"和爺爺說話時請注意你的說話語氣；他雖然老了，但仍然值得你尊重。"},{"w":"intrigue","p":"v.","d":"to make someone very interested and curious","c":"激起…的興趣；使好奇","s":"The strange old map in the attic intrigued the children so much that they spent the whole summer searching for the treasure.","t":"閣樓裡那張奇怪的舊地圖讓孩子們大感興趣，他們整個夏天都在尋找寶藏。","a":"intrigued","h":1},{"w":"intrigue","p":"n.","d":"secret plans to do something bad","c":"陰謀；密謀","s":"The novel is full of political intrigue, with ministers secretly planning to remove the young king from his throne.","t":"這本小說充滿政治陰謀，大臣們秘密計畫把年輕的國王趕下王位。"},{"w":"intriguing","p":"adj.","d":"very interesting because it is strange or mysterious","c":"引人入勝的；耐人尋味的","s":"The documentary raises an intriguing question: why did this ancient city disappear so suddenly about three thousand years ago?","t":"這部紀錄片提出了一個耐人尋味的問題：這座古城為什麼在大約三千年前突然消失？"},{"w":"be intrigued by","p":"v.phr.","d":"to be very interested in and curious about something","c":"對…感到好奇","s":"Most visitors are intrigued by the robot waiter at the restaurant, and many of them take videos of it bringing their food.","t":"大多數客人對餐廳裡的機器人服務生感到好奇，許多人還拍下它送餐的影片。","a":"are intrigued by"},{"w":"intrude","p":"v.","d":"to go into a place or situation where you are not wanted","c":"侵入；闖入；打擾","s":"I am sorry to intrude on your meeting, but there is an urgent phone call for Mr. Lin from the hospital.","t":"很抱歉打擾你們的會議，但醫院有一通給林先生的緊急電話。","h":1},{"w":"intruder","p":"n.","d":"a person who enters a place without permission","c":"入侵者；闖入者","s":"The dog barked loudly in the middle of the night, and the family later found that an intruder had broken the kitchen window.","t":"狗在半夜大聲吠叫，這家人後來發現有個闖入者打破了廚房的窗戶。","h":1},{"w":"intrude upon","p":"v.phr.","d":"to disturb someone's private life or time","c":"侵擾；打擾","s":"Reporters should not intrude upon the privacy of the victim's family during such a sad and difficult time.","t":"在如此悲傷艱難的時刻，記者不應該侵擾受害者家人的隱私。"},{"w":"intrusion","p":"n.","d":"the act of entering or disturbing without permission","c":"侵入；打擾","s":"Please forgive the intrusion, but I need to borrow your phone for a minute because mine has just died.","t":"請原諒我的打擾，但我需要借你的手機一分鐘，因為我的剛沒電了。"},{"w":"intrusive","p":"adj.","d":"disturbing you in an unwelcome way","c":"侵擾的；冒昧的","s":"Many people find pop-up ads on their phones intrusive, so they install programs that block them completely.","t":"許多人覺得手機上的彈出式廣告很擾人，所以他們安裝程式把廣告完全擋掉。"},{"w":"invaluable","p":"adj.","d":"extremely useful; too valuable to be measured","c":"無價的；極寶貴的","s":"Her ten years of experience in the hospital proved invaluable when the new clinic had to deal with its first emergency.","t":"當新診所必須處理第一次緊急狀況時，她在醫院十年的經驗證明是極其寶貴的。","h":1},{"w":"valuable","p":"adj.","d":"worth a lot of money; very useful","c":"有價值的；貴重的","s":"Do not leave valuable items such as laptops or cameras in the car, because thieves often break windows in this parking lot.","t":"不要把筆電或相機等貴重物品留在車上，因為小偷常在這個停車場打破車窗。"},{"w":"value","p":"n.","d":"how much something is worth","c":"價值","s":"The value of this old stamp has risen sharply, and a collector recently offered my grandfather fifty thousand dollars for it.","t":"這張舊郵票的價值大幅上漲，最近有位收藏家出價五萬元向我爺爺購買。"},{"w":"value","p":"v.","d":"to think that something is important","c":"重視；珍視","s":"I value your honest opinion more than anyone else's, so please tell me what you really think of my essay.","t":"我比任何人都更重視你誠實的意見，所以請告訴我你對我這篇文章真正的想法。"},{"w":"valueless","p":"adj.","d":"worth nothing","c":"無價值的；毫無用處的","s":"Without a signature, the famous player's photo is almost valueless, so fans wait for hours to get it signed.","t":"沒有簽名的話，這位知名球員的照片幾乎是毫無價值的，所以粉絲排隊等好幾個小時請他簽名。"},{"w":"invariably","p":"adv.","d":"always, without any change","c":"總是；一律","s":"My grandfather invariably wakes up at five o'clock, even on holidays when the rest of the family sleeps until noon.","t":"我爺爺總是五點起床，即使在假日家裡其他人都睡到中午也一樣。","h":1},{"w":"vary","p":"v.","d":"to be different or to change","c":"變化；不同","s":"Prices at the night market vary from stall to stall, so it is worth walking around before you buy anything.","t":"夜市裡的價格每個攤位都不同，所以買東西之前值得先四處逛逛。"},{"w":"various","p":"adj.","d":"several different","c":"各種的；不同的","s":"The bakery sells various kinds of bread, from soft milk loaves to hard French bread with a crispy crust.","t":"這家麵包店賣各種麵包，從柔軟的牛奶吐司到外皮酥脆的硬法國麵包都有。"},{"w":"variety","p":"n.","d":"many different kinds of things","c":"多樣性；種類","s":"The new supermarket offers a wide variety of imported cheese, which was very hard to find in our town before.","t":"新超市提供種類繁多的進口起司，這在我們鎮上以前很難買到。"},{"w":"invariable","p":"adj.","d":"never changing","c":"不變的","s":"The restaurant's invariable rule is that every customer must be greeted within ten seconds of walking through the door.","t":"這家餐廳不變的規定是，每位客人進門十秒內都必須受到問候。"},{"w":"inventory","p":"n.","d":"a complete list of the goods in a shop or building","c":"存貨；庫存清單","s":"The shop takes inventory every December, counting every item on the shelves to see what needs to be ordered.","t":"這家店每年十二月都會盤點庫存，清點架上每一件商品，看看需要訂購什麼。","h":1},{"w":"take inventory","p":"v.phr.","d":"to count and list all the goods in a place","c":"盤點","s":"All staff must stay late on Friday to take inventory of the warehouse before the new products arrive next week.","t":"所有員工星期五都必須留晚一點盤點倉庫，趕在下週新產品到貨之前。"},{"w":"invent","p":"v.","d":"to make or think of something completely new","c":"發明","s":"Thomas Edison did not invent the light bulb alone; many scientists before him had worked on the same idea.","t":"愛迪生並不是獨自發明電燈泡；在他之前已有許多科學家研究過同樣的構想。"},{"w":"invention","p":"n.","d":"a new thing that someone has made","c":"發明；發明物","s":"The smartphone is probably the most important invention of the past thirty years, and it has changed how we live.","t":"智慧型手機可能是過去三十年最重要的發明，它改變了我們的生活方式。"},{"w":"inventor","p":"n.","d":"a person who invents things","c":"發明家","s":"The young inventor won first prize at the science fair for a machine that turns kitchen waste into fertilizer.","t":"這位年輕的發明家以一台把廚餘變成肥料的機器，在科展中贏得第一名。"},{"w":"ironic","p":"adj.","d":"funny or strange because it is the opposite of what you expect","c":"諷刺的；令人啼笑皆非的","s":"It is ironic that the fire station burned down last night while all the firefighters were out putting out another fire.","t":"諷刺的是，昨晚消防局燒毀了，而當時所有消防員都出去撲滅另一場火。","h":1},{"w":"irony","p":"n.","d":"a situation that is strange or funny because it is the opposite of what you expect","c":"諷刺；反諷","s":"The irony is that the man who invented the alarm clock could never wake up on time himself.","t":"諷刺的是，發明鬧鐘的那個人自己卻從來無法準時起床。"},{"w":"ironically","p":"adv.","d":"in a way that is the opposite of what you expect","c":"諷刺地；具有諷刺意味的是","s":"Ironically, the teacher who always told us to be on time was the only person late for the final exam.","t":"諷刺的是，那位總是叫我們要準時的老師，是期末考唯一遲到的人。","a":"Ironically"},{"w":"irritable","p":"adj.","d":"becoming annoyed easily","c":"易怒的；煩躁的","s":"My brother gets very irritable when he is hungry, so we always keep some snacks in the car on long trips.","t":"我哥哥肚子餓的時候會變得很煩躁，所以長途旅行時我們總是在車上放一些零食。","h":1},{"w":"irritate","p":"v.","d":"to make someone annoyed; to make skin sore","c":"使惱怒；刺激","s":"The constant noise from the construction site next door began to irritate everyone in the office by the second week.","t":"隔壁工地不停的噪音到了第二週開始惹惱辦公室裡的每一個人。","h":1},{"w":"irritating","p":"adj.","d":"making you feel annoyed","c":"令人惱火的","s":"The most irritating thing about my roommate is that he leaves his dirty dishes in the sink for days.","t":"我室友最令人惱火的地方是，他會把髒碗盤放在水槽裡好幾天。"},{"w":"irritation","p":"n.","d":"the feeling of being annoyed","c":"惱怒；煩躁","s":"She could not hide her irritation when the waiter brought the wrong dish for the third time that evening.","t":"當服務生那晚第三次送錯菜時，她無法掩飾自己的惱怒。"},{"w":"be irritated by","p":"v.phr.","d":"to be annoyed by something","c":"被…惹惱","s":"The teacher was irritated by the students who kept whispering during the test, so she moved them to the front row.","t":"老師被考試中一直竊竊私語的學生惹惱了，所以她把他們調到第一排。","a":"was irritated by"},{"w":"isle","p":"n.","d":"a small island (used mostly in names and poems)","c":"小島","s":"The British Isles include Great Britain, Ireland, and thousands of smaller islands and rocks scattered around their long coasts.","t":"不列顛群島包括大不列顛島、愛爾蘭島，以及散布在漫長海岸周圍數千個較小的島嶼和岩礁。","a":"Isles","h":1},{"w":"island","p":"n.","d":"a piece of land with water all around it","c":"島","s":"Taiwan is an island surrounded by the sea, so fresh seafood is easy to find in almost every city and town.","t":"台灣是一座四面環海的島，所以幾乎每個城鎮都很容易找到新鮮的海產。"},{"w":"islander","p":"n.","d":"a person who lives on an island","c":"島民","s":"The friendly islanders welcomed the tourists with fresh coconuts and showed them the best places to swim.","t":"友善的島民用新鮮的椰子歡迎遊客，並帶他們去最適合游泳的地方。","a":"islanders"},{"w":"desert island","p":"n.phr.","d":"a small island with no people living on it","c":"荒島","s":"If you were left alone on a desert island, which three things would you want to have with you?","t":"如果你被獨自留在一座荒島上，你會想帶哪三樣東西？"}]},{"unit":20,"theme":"itch – lessen","cards":[{"w":"itch","p":"n.","d":"an uncomfortable feeling on the skin that makes you want to scratch","c":"癢","s":"After walking through the tall grass, I had a terrible itch on both legs, and I could not stop scratching them all evening.","t":"走過高高的草叢後，我的兩條腿癢得要命，整個晚上都忍不住一直抓。","h":1},{"w":"itch","p":"v.","d":"to have an uncomfortable feeling that makes you want to scratch","c":"發癢","s":"The new wool sweater makes my neck itch so badly that I have to wear a cotton shirt underneath it.","t":"這件新的羊毛毛衣讓我的脖子癢得受不了，所以我得在裡面穿一件棉質襯衫。"},{"w":"itchy","p":"adj.","d":"making you want to scratch","c":"發癢的","s":"Mosquito bites are very itchy, but the doctor says scratching them will only make the skin red and sore.","t":"蚊子叮的包非常癢，但醫生說抓它們只會讓皮膚變紅、變痛。"},{"w":"be itching to","p":"v.phr.","d":"to want to do something very much","c":"渴望做…；迫不及待想…","s":"The children were itching to open their presents, but their mother made them wait until everyone had finished dinner.","t":"孩子們迫不及待想拆禮物，但媽媽要他們等到大家都吃完晚餐。","a":"were itching to"},{"w":"ivy","p":"n.","d":"a climbing plant with dark green leaves","c":"常春藤","s":"The old stone walls of the castle are covered with thick green ivy, which makes the building look even older.","t":"城堡古老的石牆上爬滿了茂密的綠色常春藤，讓這棟建築看起來更加古老。","h":1},{"w":"Ivy League","p":"n.phr.","d":"a group of eight famous old universities in the eastern US","c":"常春藤聯盟（美國八所名校）","s":"Her dream is to study at an Ivy League university such as Harvard or Yale, so she works hard on her English every day.","t":"她的夢想是進入哈佛或耶魯這類常春藤聯盟大學就讀，所以她每天努力學英文。"},{"w":"poison ivy","p":"n.phr.","d":"a plant that makes the skin red and itchy when you touch it","c":"毒藤","s":"Be careful when you hike in the woods in North America, because touching poison ivy can give you a painful red rash.","t":"在北美的樹林裡健行時要小心，因為碰到毒藤會讓你起又痛又紅的疹子。"},{"w":"ivy-covered","p":"adj.","d":"covered with ivy","c":"爬滿常春藤的","s":"The ivy-covered cottage at the end of the lane looks like something out of a fairy tale, especially in the autumn.","t":"巷子盡頭那棟爬滿常春藤的小屋看起來像童話裡的場景，尤其是在秋天。"},{"w":"jade","p":"n.","d":"a hard green stone used for jewelry","c":"玉","s":"My grandmother gave me a small jade necklace on my eighteenth birthday, and she said it would bring me good luck.","t":"我十八歲生日時，奶奶送我一條小小的玉項鍊，她說它會帶給我好運。","h":1},{"w":"jade","p":"adj.","d":"of a bright green color like jade","c":"翠綠色的","s":"The lake in the mountains has a beautiful jade green color because of the minerals in the water that flows into it.","t":"山中的湖泊因為流入湖水中的礦物質而呈現美麗的翠綠色。"},{"w":"jaded","p":"adj.","d":"tired and bored because you have had too much of something","c":"厭倦的；疲憊的","s":"After ten years in the same job, he felt jaded and bored, so he decided to travel around the world for a year.","t":"在同一份工作做了十年之後，他感到厭倦又無聊，所以決定花一年環遊世界。"},{"w":"the Jade Emperor","p":"n.phr.","d":"the ruler of heaven in Chinese folk religion","c":"玉皇大帝","s":"In Chinese folk religion, the Jade Emperor is the ruler of heaven, and many temples in Taiwan hold big celebrations on his birthday.","t":"在中國民間信仰中，玉皇大帝是天庭的統治者，台灣許多廟宇都在他的誕辰舉行盛大的慶典。"},{"w":"janitor","p":"n.","d":"a person whose job is to clean and look after a building","c":"工友；大樓管理員","s":"The school janitor arrives at six every morning to unlock the gates and sweep the leaves from the playground.","t":"學校工友每天早上六點到校，打開大門並把操場上的落葉掃乾淨。","h":1},{"w":"janitorial","p":"adj.","d":"connected with cleaning and looking after a building","c":"清潔工作的","s":"The company hired a janitorial service to clean the offices every night after the last employee goes home.","t":"公司僱了一家清潔服務公司，每晚在最後一位員工回家後打掃辦公室。"},{"w":"caretaker","p":"n.","d":"a person who looks after a building or land","c":"看管人；管理員","s":"During the winter, a caretaker lives in the empty hotel to make sure the pipes do not freeze and nobody breaks in.","t":"冬天期間，有一位看管人住在空蕩的飯店裡，確保水管不會結冰，也沒有人闖入。"},{"w":"cleaner","p":"n.","d":"a person whose job is to clean buildings","c":"清潔工","s":"The cleaner found a wallet under the seat of the bus and handed it to the driver right away.","t":"清潔工在公車座位底下發現一個皮夾，馬上把它交給了司機。"},{"w":"jasmine","p":"n.","d":"a plant with small white flowers that smell sweet","c":"茉莉花","s":"In the evening, the sweet smell of jasmine fills our garden, and my mother likes to sit outside with a cup of tea.","t":"傍晚時，茉莉花的甜香瀰漫整個花園，我媽媽喜歡端著一杯茶坐在外面。","h":1},{"w":"jasmine tea","p":"n.phr.","d":"tea with the smell of jasmine flowers","c":"茉莉花茶","s":"Many people in Taiwan enjoy a pot of jasmine tea after dinner, since its light flavor goes well with sweet desserts.","t":"台灣許多人喜歡晚餐後喝一壺茉莉花茶，因為它清淡的味道和甜點很搭。"},{"w":"jasmine rice","p":"n.phr.","d":"a kind of long rice from Thailand that smells sweet","c":"茉莉香米；泰國香米","s":"The Thai restaurant serves its green curry with a bowl of soft jasmine rice, which has a wonderful smell when it is hot.","t":"這家泰式餐廳的綠咖哩配一碗鬆軟的茉莉香米飯，熱騰騰時香氣非常迷人。"},{"w":"jingle","p":"n.","d":"a short, simple song used in an advertisement; a ringing sound","c":"廣告歌；叮噹聲","s":"That ice cream company's jingle is so catchy that my little sister sings it every time she hears the truck coming.","t":"那家冰淇淋公司的廣告歌太好記了，我妹妹每次聽到冰淇淋車來就會唱起來。","h":1},{"w":"jingle","p":"v.","d":"to make a light ringing sound like small bells","c":"發出叮噹聲","s":"The keys in his pocket jingled with every step, so we always knew when the manager was walking toward our office.","t":"他口袋裡的鑰匙每走一步就叮噹作響，所以我們總是知道經理什麼時候走向我們的辦公室。","a":"jingled"},{"w":"jingle bells","p":"n.phr.","d":"small round bells that ring when shaken","c":"叮噹作響的鈴鐺","s":"At Christmas time, the horses pulling the carriage wore jingle bells that rang happily as they trotted through the snow.","t":"聖誕節時，拉馬車的馬戴著叮噹鈴鐺，在雪中小跑時發出歡快的響聲。"},{"w":"jockey","p":"n.","d":"a person who rides horses in races","c":"騎師","s":"The jockey was only about 160 centimeters tall and very light, which is important for anyone who wants to race horses professionally.","t":"這位騎師只有大約一百六十公分高，體重很輕，這對任何想成為職業賽馬騎手的人都很重要。","h":1},{"w":"jockey for position","p":"v.phr.","d":"to try to get into a better position than other people","c":"爭奪有利位置","s":"Before the race began, the runners jockeyed for position near the front of the line, each hoping to get a quick start.","t":"比賽開始前，跑者們在起跑線前方爭搶有利位置，每個人都希望能搶得先機。","a":"jockeyed for position"},{"w":"disc jockey","p":"n.phr.","d":"a person who plays music on the radio or at a party (a DJ)","c":"唱片騎師；DJ","s":"My cousin works as a disc jockey at a radio station, where he plays music and chats with listeners late at night.","t":"我表哥在電台當DJ，他在深夜播放音樂並和聽眾聊天。"},{"w":"jolly","p":"adj.","d":"happy and cheerful","c":"快樂的；愉快的","s":"Our jolly bus driver sings along with the radio and tells jokes, so even the long ride to school feels short.","t":"我們快樂的公車司機會跟著廣播唱歌、講笑話，所以連漫長的上學車程都感覺很短。","h":1},{"w":"jolly","p":"adv.","d":"very (British, informal)","c":"非常（英式口語）","s":"It was jolly cold on the mountain this morning, so I was glad that I had packed an extra jacket in my bag.","t":"今天早上山上非常冷，所以我很慶幸自己在包包裡多放了一件外套。"},{"w":"jolly good","p":"phr.","d":"very good; well done (British)","c":"很好；太棒了（英式）","s":"\"Jolly good, you finished all the work before lunch,\" said the British manager with a big smile on his face.","t":"「太棒了，你在午餐前就把工作全部做完了，」英國經理笑容滿面地說。","a":"Jolly good"},{"w":"joyous","p":"adj.","d":"full of joy; very happy","c":"歡樂的；喜悅的","s":"The wedding was a joyous occasion, with music, dancing, and laughter that went on late into the warm summer night.","t":"這場婚禮是個歡樂的場合，音樂、舞蹈和笑聲一直持續到溫暖的夏夜深處。","h":1},{"w":"joy","p":"n.","d":"a feeling of great happiness","c":"喜悅；快樂","s":"Nothing can compare with the joy of seeing your own name on the list of students who passed the exam.","t":"沒有什麼能比得上在及格名單上看到自己名字的那種喜悅。"},{"w":"joyful","p":"adj.","d":"very happy","c":"快樂的；充滿喜悅的","s":"The children's joyful laughter could be heard all over the park as they ran through the water fountains.","t":"孩子們穿過噴水池奔跑時，他們歡樂的笑聲整個公園都聽得到。"},{"w":"enjoy","p":"v.","d":"to get pleasure from something","c":"享受；喜歡","s":"We really enjoyed the trip to Hualien last weekend, especially the boat ride along the coast to watch the dolphins.","t":"我們上週末真的很享受花蓮之旅，尤其是沿著海岸賞海豚的那趟船程。","a":"enjoyed"},{"w":"overjoyed","p":"adj.","d":"extremely happy","c":"欣喜若狂的","s":"My parents were overjoyed when they heard that my sister had won a scholarship to study music in Vienna.","t":"當我父母聽到姊姊獲得獎學金要去維也納學音樂時，他們欣喜若狂。"},{"w":"junction","p":"n.","d":"a place where roads or railway lines meet","c":"交叉路口；交會點","s":"Get off the highway at the next junction and follow the signs toward the airport for about ten more kilometers.","t":"在下一個交流道下高速公路，然後跟著往機場的指標再開大約十公里。","h":1},{"w":"join","p":"v.","d":"to become a member of a group; to connect things","c":"加入；連接","s":"Would you like to join our hiking club? We meet every Saturday morning and walk a different trail each week.","t":"你想加入我們的登山社嗎？我們每週六早上集合，每週走一條不同的步道。"},{"w":"joint","p":"adj.","d":"shared by two or more people or groups","c":"共同的；聯合的","s":"The two schools organized a joint concert, and students from both choirs sang together on the same stage.","t":"這兩所學校舉辦了一場聯合音樂會，兩校合唱團的學生在同一個舞台上一起演唱。"},{"w":"joint","p":"n.","d":"a place where two bones meet","c":"關節","s":"My grandfather's knee joints hurt when it rains, so he can usually tell when bad weather is coming.","t":"我爺爺的膝關節下雨時會痛，所以他通常能知道壞天氣什麼時候要來。","a":"joints"},{"w":"kin","p":"n.","d":"your family and relatives","c":"親屬；家人","s":"In many villages, people still live close to their kin, and three generations often share the same house.","t":"在許多村莊裡，人們仍然和親屬住得很近，三代人常常住在同一棟房子裡。","h":1},{"w":"next of kin","p":"n.phr.","d":"your closest living relative","c":"最近的親屬","s":"The hospital asked the patient for the name and phone number of his next of kin before the operation began.","t":"手術開始前，醫院向病人詢問他最近親屬的姓名和電話號碼。"},{"w":"kinship","p":"n.","d":"family relationship; a feeling of being close to someone","c":"親屬關係；親近感","s":"Although they were not related by blood, the two old soldiers felt a deep sense of kinship after years of fighting side by side.","t":"雖然沒有血緣關係，這兩位老兵在多年並肩作戰後，感受到一種深厚的親情。"},{"w":"kindred","p":"adj.","d":"similar; having the same interests","c":"同類的；志趣相投的","s":"At the book club, I finally met some kindred spirits who love old mystery novels as much as I do.","t":"在讀書會上，我終於遇到了一些和我一樣熱愛老推理小說的志趣相投的人。"},{"w":"kindle","p":"v.","d":"to start a fire","c":"點燃","s":"It took us almost an hour to kindle a fire with the wet wood we had collected after the rain.","t":"我們用雨後撿來的濕木頭花了將近一小時才點燃火。","h":1},{"w":"kindle","p":"v.","d":"to make a feeling or interest start","c":"激起；引發","s":"The teacher's trip to Africa kindled an interest in wildlife among her students, and many of them joined the nature club.","t":"老師的非洲之旅激起了學生們對野生動物的興趣，許多人因此加入了自然社。","a":"kindled"},{"w":"rekindle","p":"v.","d":"to make a feeling or relationship start again","c":"重新點燃；重燃","s":"Meeting her old classmates at the reunion helped to rekindle friendships that had faded over twenty years.","t":"在同學會上見到老同學，讓她得以重燃二十年來逐漸淡去的友誼。"},{"w":"kindling","p":"n.","d":"small dry pieces of wood used to start a fire","c":"引火柴","s":"Before you light the campfire, collect some dry leaves and small sticks to use as kindling, or the big logs will never catch.","t":"生營火之前，先收集一些乾樹葉和小樹枝當引火柴，否則大木頭永遠燒不起來。"},{"w":"knowledgeable","p":"adj.","d":"knowing a lot about something","c":"知識淵博的；博學的","s":"Our guide was very knowledgeable about the history of the temple, and she answered every question the tourists asked.","t":"我們的導遊對這座廟的歷史非常了解，遊客問的每個問題她都答得出來。","h":1},{"w":"knowledge","p":"n.","d":"the facts and information that you know","c":"知識","s":"A good doctor needs not only medical knowledge but also the ability to listen carefully to what patients say.","t":"好醫生不只需要醫學知識，還需要仔細傾聽病人說話的能力。"},{"w":"know, knew, known","p":"v.","d":"to have information in your mind","c":"知道；認識","s":"Did you know that the library stays open until midnight during exam week so that students have a quiet place to study?","t":"你知道考試週圖書館會開到午夜，好讓學生有個安靜的地方讀書嗎？","a":"know"},{"w":"well-known","p":"adj.","d":"famous; known by many people","c":"著名的；眾所皆知的","s":"The night market is well-known for its oyster omelets, and tourists line up for more than thirty minutes to try them.","t":"這個夜市以蚵仔煎聞名，遊客排隊超過三十分鐘就為了嚐一嚐。"},{"w":"acknowledge","p":"v.","d":"to accept or admit that something is true","c":"承認","s":"The company finally had to acknowledge that its new phone had a serious battery problem and offered a free replacement.","t":"這家公司最後不得不承認新手機有嚴重的電池問題，並提供免費更換。"},{"w":"lad","p":"n.","d":"a boy or young man","c":"小伙子；少年","s":"When my grandfather was a young lad of fifteen, he left his village and went to work at a factory in Taipei.","t":"我爺爺還是個十五歲的少年時，就離開村子到台北的工廠工作。","h":1},{"w":"lads","p":"n.","d":"a group of young men who are friends (informal)","c":"一群小伙子；哥兒們","s":"After the football match, the lads went to a small restaurant together to celebrate their first win of the season.","t":"足球賽結束後，小伙子們一起去一家小餐館慶祝他們本季的第一場勝利。"},{"w":"lass","p":"n.","d":"a girl or young woman","c":"少女；姑娘","s":"The old song tells the story of a sailor who falls in love with a lass from a fishing village on the coast.","t":"這首老歌講述一位水手愛上海邊漁村一位姑娘的故事。"},{"w":"landlady","p":"n.","d":"a woman who rents a room or house to people","c":"女房東","s":"Our landlady lives downstairs and is very kind; she sometimes brings us homemade soup when the weather is cold.","t":"我們的女房東住在樓下，人很好；天氣冷的時候她有時會帶自己煮的湯給我們。","h":1},{"w":"landlord","p":"n.","d":"a man who rents a room or house to people","c":"房東","s":"The landlord promised to fix the broken air conditioner before the summer, but it is already July and nothing has happened.","t":"房東答應在夏天前修好壞掉的冷氣，但現在已經七月了，什麼都沒做。"},{"w":"land","p":"v.","d":"to come down onto the ground after flying","c":"著陸；降落","s":"The plane will land in Tokyo at seven in the morning, so we should be at the hotel before lunch.","t":"飛機早上七點會在東京降落，所以我們應該在午餐前就能到飯店。"},{"w":"landowner","p":"n.","d":"a person who owns land","c":"地主","s":"The landowner agreed to let the village use part of his field for a weekend farmers' market.","t":"地主同意讓村子用他田地的一部分來辦週末農夫市集。"},{"w":"landslide","p":"n.","d":"a mass of earth and rocks falling down a hill","c":"山崩；土石流","s":"After three days of heavy rain, a landslide blocked the mountain road, and the villagers were cut off for a week.","t":"連續三天大雨之後，一場土石流堵住了山路，村民們與外界隔絕了一週。","h":1},{"w":"landslide","p":"n.","d":"an election victory by a very large number of votes","c":"（選舉）壓倒性勝利","s":"The young mayor won the election by a landslide, taking more than seventy percent of the votes in the city.","t":"這位年輕的市長以壓倒性勝利贏得選舉，拿下全市超過七成的選票。"},{"w":"slide, slid, slid","p":"v.","d":"to move smoothly over a surface","c":"滑動；滑落","s":"The children love to slide down the grassy hill on pieces of cardboard whenever the weather is dry.","t":"只要天氣乾燥，孩子們就喜歡坐在紙板上從草坡上滑下來。","a":"slide"},{"w":"landscape","p":"n.","d":"everything you can see when you look across an area of land","c":"風景；景觀","s":"The landscape changed completely after we crossed the mountains, from green rice fields to dry, rocky hills.","t":"翻過山之後，景觀完全改變了，從綠油油的稻田變成乾燥多石的丘陵。"},{"w":"latitude","p":"n.","d":"the distance of a place north or south of the equator","c":"緯度","s":"Taipei lies at about 25 degrees north latitude, which is why its winters are mild compared with those in Tokyo.","t":"台北位於北緯大約二十五度，這就是為什麼它的冬天比東京溫和。","h":1},{"w":"longitude","p":"n.","d":"the distance of a place east or west of a line through Greenwich","c":"經度","s":"Sailors in the past found it hard to measure longitude at sea until an accurate clock was invented in the 1700s.","t":"過去的水手在海上很難測量經度，直到十八世紀發明了準確的時鐘。"},{"w":"latitude","p":"n.","d":"freedom to choose what you do","c":"自由；餘地","s":"The new manager gives her staff plenty of latitude to make their own decisions, as long as the work is finished on time.","t":"新經理給員工很大的自由自己做決定，只要工作能準時完成。"},{"w":"lateral","p":"adj.","d":"connected with the side of something; sideways","c":"側面的；橫向的","s":"The coach asked the players to practice lateral movements, stepping quickly from side to side across the court.","t":"教練要球員練習橫向移動，在球場上快速地左右跨步。"},{"w":"lavish","p":"adj.","d":"very large in amount and expensive","c":"奢侈的；豪華的","s":"The company threw a lavish party at the hotel to celebrate its fiftieth anniversary, with a live band and endless champagne.","t":"公司在飯店舉辦了一場豪華的派對慶祝五十週年，有現場樂團和喝不完的香檳。","h":1},{"w":"lavish","p":"v.","d":"to give a lot of something to someone","c":"慷慨給予；大量施予","s":"Grandparents often lavish gifts and attention on their first grandchild, sometimes more than the parents think is good.","t":"祖父母常常大量給予第一個孫子禮物和關注，有時多到父母覺得不太好。"},{"w":"lavishly","p":"adv.","d":"in a very expensive or generous way","c":"奢侈地；大量地","s":"The palace was lavishly decorated with gold and silk, which showed how rich the king was in those days.","t":"宮殿用黃金和絲綢奢華地裝飾，顯示出當時國王有多麼富有。"},{"w":"lavish praise on","p":"v.phr.","d":"to praise someone a lot","c":"大加讚揚","s":"The critics lavished praise on the young actress after her first film, calling her the best new talent of the year.","t":"影評人在這位年輕女演員的第一部電影之後對她大加讚揚，稱她為年度最佳新人。","a":"lavished praise on"},{"w":"layman","p":"n.","d":"a person who is not an expert in a subject","c":"外行人；門外漢","s":"The doctor explained the test results in simple words so that a layman like me could understand what was wrong.","t":"醫生用簡單的話解釋檢查結果，好讓我這樣的外行人也能明白哪裡出了問題。","h":1},{"w":"in layman's terms","p":"phr.","d":"in simple words that a non-expert can understand","c":"用外行人聽得懂的話","s":"Could you explain how the vaccine works in layman's terms? I did not study science, and the article was far too technical for me.","t":"你能用外行人聽得懂的方式解釋疫苗怎麼運作嗎？我沒學過科學，那篇文章對我來說太專業了。"},{"w":"layperson","p":"n.","d":"a person who is not an expert (used for men and women)","c":"外行人","s":"The museum's new signs were written for the layperson, not for scientists, so even children can understand them.","t":"博物館的新說明牌是為一般民眾而不是科學家寫的，所以連小孩都能看懂。"},{"w":"lay","p":"adj.","d":"not having expert knowledge","c":"外行的；非專業的","s":"The hospital invited several lay members of the community to join the committee and share the patients' point of view.","t":"醫院邀請了幾位社區的非專業成員加入委員會，分享病人的觀點。"},{"w":"layout","p":"n.","d":"the way things are arranged in a place or on a page","c":"佈局；版面設計","s":"The layout of the new library is easy to follow, with the children's books on the left and study rooms on the right.","t":"新圖書館的格局很容易理解，童書在左邊，自習室在右邊。","h":1},{"w":"lay out","p":"v.phr.","d":"to arrange things so they can be seen or used","c":"擺放；規劃","s":"Before the guests arrived, we laid out the plates and glasses on the long table in the garden.","t":"客人到之前，我們把盤子和杯子擺放在花園的長桌上。","a":"laid out"},{"w":"lay, laid, laid","p":"v.","d":"to put something down carefully; to produce an egg","c":"放置；下蛋","s":"Yesterday the hen laid two eggs, and my little brother ran to the garden to collect them before school.","t":"昨天母雞下了兩顆蛋，我弟弟上學前跑到花園去撿。","a":"laid"},{"w":"layer","p":"n.","d":"a thin sheet of something that covers a surface","c":"層","s":"In winter, it is wise to wear several thin layers of clothing rather than one thick coat, so you can take some off indoors.","t":"冬天穿幾層薄衣服比穿一件厚大衣聰明，這樣在室內可以脫掉一些。","a":"layers"},{"w":"lease","p":"n.","d":"a legal agreement to rent a building or car for a period of time","c":"租約","s":"Our lease on the apartment ends in August, so we need to decide soon whether to stay for another year.","t":"我們公寓的租約八月到期，所以我們得儘快決定要不要再住一年。","h":1},{"w":"lease","p":"v.","d":"to rent something for a period of time by a legal agreement","c":"出租；租用","s":"The company decided to lease ten new delivery trucks instead of buying them, because leasing costs less at the start.","t":"公司決定租用十輛新貨車而不是購買，因為一開始租的成本比較低。"},{"w":"sign a lease","p":"v.phr.","d":"to agree to rent a place by signing a contract","c":"簽租約","s":"Before you sign a lease, read every page carefully and ask the landlord about anything you do not understand.","t":"簽租約之前，請仔細閱讀每一頁，有任何不懂的地方就問房東。"},{"w":"release","p":"v.","d":"to let someone or something go free; to make something available","c":"釋放；發行","s":"The band will release its new album next month, and fans can already order it online from the band's website.","t":"這個樂團下個月將發行新專輯，歌迷已經可以在樂團的網站上線上預購。"},{"w":"legislator","p":"n.","d":"a member of a group that makes laws","c":"立法者；立法委員","s":"Several legislators visited the flooded town to see the damage for themselves before voting on the new budget.","t":"幾位立法委員親自到淹水的城鎮查看災情，然後才對新預算進行表決。","a":"legislators","h":1},{"w":"legislation","p":"n.","d":"a law or set of laws","c":"立法；法規","s":"The government has passed new legislation that bans plastic straws in all restaurants from next January.","t":"政府通過了新的法規，從明年一月起禁止所有餐廳使用塑膠吸管。"},{"w":"legislative","p":"adj.","d":"connected with making laws","c":"立法的","s":"Making laws is the legislative branch's job, while the courts decide whether those laws have been broken.","t":"制定法律是立法部門的工作，而法院則判斷那些法律是否被違反。"},{"w":"legislate","p":"v.","d":"to make laws","c":"立法","s":"Many parents want the government to legislate against junk food advertising that is aimed at young children.","t":"許多家長希望政府立法禁止針對幼童的垃圾食物廣告。"},{"w":"legal","p":"adj.","d":"allowed by law; connected with the law","c":"合法的；法律的","s":"In Taiwan, the legal age for buying alcohol is eighteen, and shops must check a young customer's ID card.","t":"在台灣，購買酒類的法定年齡是十八歲，商店必須檢查年輕顧客的身分證。"},{"w":"lengthy","p":"adj.","d":"very long, often too long","c":"冗長的","s":"After a lengthy discussion that lasted four hours, the committee finally agreed to build the new parking lot.","t":"經過長達四小時的冗長討論，委員會終於同意興建新的停車場。","h":1},{"w":"length","p":"n.","d":"how long something is","c":"長度","s":"The swimming pool is fifty meters in length, so swimming there twenty times equals exactly one kilometer.","t":"這個游泳池長五十公尺，所以在那裡游二十趟正好等於一公里。"},{"w":"lengthen","p":"v.","d":"to make something longer","c":"加長；延長","s":"The tailor can lengthen these trousers by three centimeters, so you will not have to buy a new pair for the ceremony.","t":"裁縫師可以把這條褲子加長三公分，所以你不用為了典禮再買一條新的。"},{"w":"at length","p":"phr.","d":"for a long time and in detail","c":"詳細地；長時間地","s":"The professor spoke at length about the causes of the war, and the lecture ran twenty minutes past the usual time.","t":"教授詳細地講述了戰爭的起因，這堂課比平常多上了二十分鐘。"},{"w":"lesbian","p":"adj.","d":"relating to women who are attracted to other women","c":"女同性戀的","s":"The film tells the story of a lesbian couple who opened a small bookshop together in Taipei in the 1990s.","t":"這部電影講述一對女同性戀伴侶在一九九〇年代一起在台北開了一家小書店的故事。","h":1},{"w":"lesbian","p":"n.","d":"a woman who is attracted to other women","c":"女同性戀者","s":"As a lesbian, she was glad when Taiwan became the first place in Asia to allow same-sex marriage in 2019.","t":"身為女同性戀者，當台灣在二〇一九年成為亞洲第一個允許同性婚姻的地方時，她很高興。"},{"w":"gay","p":"adj.","d":"attracted to people of the same sex","c":"同性戀的","s":"My uncle is gay, and he and his husband have been together for more than twenty years.","t":"我叔叔是同性戀，他和他的丈夫已經在一起超過二十年了。"},{"w":"same-sex marriage","p":"n.phr.","d":"marriage between two people of the same sex","c":"同性婚姻","s":"Taiwan made same-sex marriage legal in 2019, and thousands of couples across the island have registered their marriages since then.","t":"台灣在二〇一九年讓同性婚姻合法化，從那時起全島已有數千對伴侶登記結婚。"},{"w":"lessen","p":"v.","d":"to become or make something smaller or less","c":"減少；減輕","s":"Taking a deep breath before a speech can lessen your fear and help you speak more clearly to the audience.","t":"演講前深呼吸可以減輕你的恐懼，幫助你對聽眾說得更清楚。","h":1},{"w":"less","p":"adj.","d":"a smaller amount of something","c":"較少的","s":"Doctors suggest eating less sugar and more vegetables if you want to stay healthy and keep your weight under control.","t":"如果你想保持健康並控制體重，醫生建議吃較少的糖和更多的蔬菜。"},{"w":"lesser","p":"adj.","d":"smaller or less important","c":"較小的；次要的","s":"He was found guilty of a lesser crime and had to pay a fine instead of going to prison.","t":"他被判犯了較輕的罪，只需繳罰金而不用坐牢。"},{"w":"more or less","p":"phr.","d":"almost; approximately","c":"大致上；差不多","s":"The report is more or less finished; I just need to check the spelling and add a few pictures before sending it.","t":"報告差不多完成了；我只需要檢查拼字，再加幾張圖片就可以寄出。"}]},{"unit":21,"theme":"lethal – lotion","cards":[{"w":"lethal","p":"adj.","d":"able to cause death","c":"致命的","s":"The chemical in this bottle is lethal if swallowed, so keep it locked away where small children cannot reach it.","t":"這個瓶子裡的化學物質吞下去是致命的，所以要把它鎖在小孩拿不到的地方。","h":1},{"w":"lethal weapon","p":"n.phr.","d":"a weapon that can kill","c":"致命武器","s":"The police found that the man was carrying a lethal weapon, so they arrested him before he could enter the station.","t":"警方發現那名男子身上帶著致命武器，所以在他進入車站前就逮捕了他。"},{"w":"lethal dose","p":"n.phr.","d":"an amount of a drug or poison large enough to kill","c":"致死劑量","s":"Even common medicine can be dangerous; taking far more than the normal amount may reach a lethal dose for a small child.","t":"即使是普通的藥也可能很危險；服用遠超過正常的量，對小孩來說可能達到致死劑量。"},{"w":"lethally","p":"adv.","d":"in a way that can cause death","c":"致命地","s":"The snake's bite is lethally poisonous, so hikers in this area are told to wear boots and watch where they step.","t":"這種蛇咬一口有致命的毒性，所以這一帶的登山客被要求穿靴子並注意腳下。"},{"w":"liable","p":"adj.","d":"likely to do or suffer something, usually something bad","c":"容易…的；有…傾向的","s":"The old wooden bridge is liable to collapse in a strong typhoon, so the town has closed it until repairs are finished.","t":"這座老舊的木橋在強烈颱風中很容易倒塌，所以鎮上已將它封閉直到修復完成。","h":1},{"w":"liable","p":"adj.","d":"legally responsible for something","c":"應負法律責任的","s":"If a customer slips on the wet floor, the restaurant owner may be held liable for any injuries that result.","t":"如果顧客在濕地板上滑倒，餐廳老闆可能要對由此造成的任何傷害負責。"},{"w":"be liable for","p":"v.phr.","d":"to be responsible by law for paying for something","c":"對…負有責任","s":"Parents are liable for any damage their children cause at the hotel, so please watch them carefully near the swimming pool.","t":"父母要對孩子在飯店造成的任何損壞負責，所以請在游泳池附近仔細看好他們。","a":"are liable for"},{"w":"liability","p":"n.","d":"legal responsibility; something that causes problems","c":"責任；負擔","s":"The company bought insurance to cover its liability in case a worker was injured while using the new machines.","t":"公司買了保險來承擔它的責任，以防工人在使用新機器時受傷。"},{"w":"liberate","p":"v.","d":"to set someone free","c":"解放；釋放","s":"In 1945, Allied soldiers arrived to liberate the prisoners, many of whom had not seen their families for five years.","t":"一九四五年，盟軍士兵前來解放囚犯，其中許多人已經五年沒見到家人了。","h":1},{"w":"liberation","p":"n.","d":"the act of setting people free","c":"解放","s":"The city celebrates its liberation from foreign rule every October with parades, fireworks, and speeches in the main square.","t":"這座城市每年十月都以遊行、煙火和主廣場上的演講來慶祝從外國統治中解放。","h":1},{"w":"liberty","p":"n.","d":"freedom","c":"自由","s":"The Statue of Liberty in New York was a gift from France and has welcomed millions of people arriving by ship.","t":"紐約的自由女神像是法國送的禮物，曾迎接數百萬乘船抵達的人。","a":"Liberty"},{"w":"liberal","p":"adj.","d":"willing to accept new ideas and different ways of living","c":"開明的；自由的","s":"My grandparents have surprisingly liberal views for their age, and they fully supported my decision to study art instead of medicine.","t":"以我祖父母的年紀來說，他們的觀念出乎意料地開明，他們完全支持我學藝術而不是學醫的決定。"},{"w":"liberated","p":"adj.","d":"free from old rules about how to behave","c":"解放的；不受拘束的","s":"Her grandmother was a liberated woman for her time; she ran her own business in the 1950s when most women stayed at home.","t":"她的祖母在那個年代是位思想解放的女性；一九五〇年代大多數女性待在家裡時，她經營著自己的事業。"},{"w":"lieutenant","p":"n.","d":"an officer of low rank in the army, navy, or police","c":"中尉；少尉；警察副隊長","s":"After four years at the military academy, my cousin became a lieutenant and was put in charge of thirty soldiers.","t":"在軍校四年後，我表哥成為中尉，負責帶領三十名士兵。","h":1},{"w":"lieutenant","p":"n.","d":"a person who helps and acts for someone more important","c":"副手；助手","s":"As the manager's trusted lieutenant, she runs the office whenever he travels abroad to meet customers.","t":"身為經理信任的副手，每當他出國拜訪客戶時，就由她負責管理辦公室。"},{"w":"lieutenant colonel","p":"n.phr.","d":"an army officer above a major and below a colonel","c":"中校","s":"The lieutenant colonel spoke to the new soldiers about discipline and reminded them that their training would be hard but fair.","t":"中校對新兵講述紀律，並提醒他們訓練會很辛苦但很公平。"},{"w":"tenant","p":"n.","d":"a person who pays rent to live in a house or apartment","c":"房客；租戶","s":"The tenant on the third floor always pays the rent on time and keeps the apartment very clean.","t":"三樓的房客總是準時付房租，而且把公寓保持得非常乾淨。"},{"w":"lifelong","p":"adj.","d":"lasting all through your life","c":"終身的；一生的","s":"Reading has been a lifelong habit for my grandmother, who still finishes at least one novel every week at ninety.","t":"閱讀是我奶奶一生的習慣，九十歲的她每週仍至少讀完一本小說。","h":1},{"w":"lifelong learning","p":"n.phr.","d":"continuing to learn new things all through your life","c":"終身學習","s":"The community college offers cheap evening classes to encourage lifelong learning, and many retired people study languages there.","t":"社區大學提供便宜的夜間課程來鼓勵終身學習，許多退休人士在那裡學語言。"},{"w":"lifetime","p":"n.","d":"the length of time that a person lives","c":"一生；終身","s":"In her lifetime, my great-grandmother saw the arrival of the first cars, airplanes, television, and finally the internet.","t":"在我曾祖母的一生中，她見證了第一批汽車、飛機、電視，最後還有網路的出現。"},{"w":"lifestyle","p":"n.","d":"the way a person lives","c":"生活方式","s":"A healthy lifestyle includes regular exercise, enough sleep, and meals with plenty of fresh vegetables and fruit.","t":"健康的生活方式包括規律運動、充足睡眠，以及含有大量新鮮蔬果的餐點。"},{"w":"lifespan","p":"n.","d":"the length of time that a person or animal usually lives","c":"壽命","s":"The average lifespan of a house cat is about fifteen years, though some live well into their twenties.","t":"家貓的平均壽命大約十五年，不過有些能活到二十多歲。"},{"w":"lighten","p":"v.","d":"to make something less heavy or less serious","c":"減輕","s":"To lighten my backpack before the hike, I took out two books and a heavy water bottle.","t":"為了在健行前減輕背包的重量，我拿出了兩本書和一個很重的水壺。","h":1},{"w":"lighten the mood","p":"v.phr.","d":"to make a situation feel less serious or tense","c":"緩和氣氛","s":"The host told a funny story to lighten the mood after the awkward silence that followed the argument at the dinner table.","t":"餐桌上的爭吵之後是一陣尷尬的沉默，主人講了一個好笑的故事來緩和氣氛。"},{"w":"lighten up","p":"v.phr.","d":"to become more relaxed and less serious","c":"放輕鬆","s":"You need to lighten up a little; it was only a practice test, and nobody expects a perfect score the first time.","t":"你需要放輕鬆一點；那只是模擬考，沒有人期待第一次就拿滿分。"},{"w":"light","p":"adj.","d":"not heavy","c":"輕的","s":"This laptop is so light that I can carry it in one hand all day without my arm getting tired.","t":"這台筆電非常輕，我可以單手拿一整天，手臂也不會累。"},{"w":"enlighten","p":"v.","d":"to give someone knowledge or understanding","c":"啟發；開導","s":"The documentary really enlightened me about how much water is used to make a single pair of jeans.","t":"這部紀錄片真的讓我明白製作一條牛仔褲要用掉多少水。","a":"enlightened"},{"w":"limp","p":"v.","d":"to walk with difficulty because one leg or foot is hurt","c":"跛行；一瘸一拐地走","s":"After twisting his ankle on the stairs, Jack had to limp to the nurse's office with the help of a friend.","t":"在樓梯上扭傷腳踝後，傑克必須在朋友的攙扶下一瘸一拐地走到保健室。","h":1},{"w":"limp","p":"n.","d":"a way of walking with difficulty because of a hurt leg","c":"跛行","s":"My grandfather has walked with a slight limp ever since he fell off his motorcycle thirty years ago.","t":"自從三十年前從機車上摔下來後，我爺爺走路就一直有點跛。"},{"w":"limp","p":"adj.","d":"not stiff or firm; weak","c":"軟弱無力的；癱軟的","s":"The lettuce had gone limp after two days in the hot kitchen, so we threw it away and bought fresh vegetables.","t":"萵苣在悶熱的廚房放了兩天後已經軟掉了，所以我們把它丟掉，買了新鮮的蔬菜。"},{"w":"liner","p":"n.","d":"a large ship that carries passengers; a layer that covers the inside of something","c":"郵輪；襯墊","s":"The luxury liner carried two thousand passengers across the Atlantic, with swimming pools and theaters on board.","t":"這艘豪華郵輪載著兩千名乘客橫渡大西洋，船上有游泳池和劇院。","h":1},{"w":"lining","p":"n.","d":"a layer of material that covers the inside of clothes, boxes, etc.","c":"內襯；內裡","s":"My winter coat has a soft lining made of wool, which keeps me warm even on the coldest mornings.","t":"我的冬季大衣有柔軟的羊毛內襯，即使在最冷的早晨也能讓我保暖。","h":1},{"w":"line","p":"n.","d":"a long thin mark; a row of people waiting","c":"線；隊伍","s":"There was a long line outside the bakery at seven in the morning because everyone wanted the famous pineapple cakes.","t":"早上七點麵包店外就排了一條長長的隊伍，因為大家都想買那有名的鳳梨酥。"},{"w":"line","p":"v.","d":"to form rows along the sides of something","c":"沿…排列","s":"Hundreds of fans lined the street to welcome the baseball team home after their big win in the championship.","t":"數百名球迷沿街排列，歡迎棒球隊在冠軍賽大勝後凱旋歸來。","a":"lined"},{"w":"every cloud has a silver lining","p":"phr.","d":"every bad situation has some good side","c":"禍中有福；黑暗中總有一線光明","s":"I lost my job last year, but every cloud has a silver lining: I finally had time to start the small bakery I had always dreamed of.","t":"去年我失業了，但每朵烏雲都鑲著銀邊（禍中有福）：我終於有時間開一家我一直夢想的小麵包店。"},{"w":"linger","p":"v.","d":"to stay somewhere longer than necessary; to be slow to disappear","c":"逗留；徘徊；縈繞","s":"After the concert ended, many fans lingered outside the hall, hoping to catch a glimpse of the singer leaving.","t":"演唱會結束後，許多歌迷逗留在會場外，希望能看到歌手離開時的身影。","a":"lingered","h":1},{"w":"linger on","p":"v.phr.","d":"to continue to exist for a long time","c":"持續存在；久久不散","s":"The smell of burnt toast lingered on in the kitchen for hours, even though we had opened all the windows.","t":"烤焦吐司的味道在廚房裡久久不散，即使我們已經打開了所有的窗戶。","a":"lingered on"},{"w":"lingering","p":"adj.","d":"lasting for a long time","c":"持久的；揮之不去的","s":"Although the doctor said he had fully recovered, he still had a lingering cough that bothered him at night.","t":"雖然醫生說他已經完全康復，他晚上仍有揮之不去的咳嗽困擾著他。"},{"w":"liter","p":"n.","d":"a unit for measuring liquid","c":"公升","s":"Doctors recommend drinking about two liters of water a day, especially in summer when you sweat a lot.","t":"醫生建議每天喝大約兩公升的水，尤其是在容易流汗的夏天。","a":"liters","h":1},{"w":"milliliter","p":"n.","d":"one thousandth of a liter","c":"毫升","s":"The medicine bottle holds 100 milliliters, and the doctor said to take five of them three times a day.","t":"這個藥瓶裝有一百毫升，醫生說一天三次，每次服用五毫升。","a":"milliliters"},{"w":"per liter","p":"phr.","d":"for each liter","c":"每公升","s":"Gas prices rose to thirty-five dollars per liter this week, so many people are taking the MRT to work instead of driving.","t":"這週油價漲到每公升三十五元，所以許多人改搭捷運上班而不開車。"},{"w":"literacy","p":"n.","d":"the ability to read and write","c":"識字能力；讀寫能力","s":"The country's literacy rate rose from fifty percent to nearly one hundred percent after free schools were opened in every village.","t":"在每個村莊都開設免費學校後，這個國家的識字率從百分之五十上升到接近百分之百。","h":1},{"w":"literal","p":"adj.","d":"following the exact, basic meaning of words","c":"字面的","s":"The literal meaning of \"break a leg\" sounds painful, but actors say it to each other to wish good luck.","t":"break a leg 的字面意思聽起來很痛，但演員們互相這麼說是為了祝好運。","h":1},{"w":"literate","p":"adj.","d":"able to read and write","c":"識字的；有讀寫能力的","s":"Two hundred years ago, only a small number of people in the village were literate, so letters were read aloud in the square.","t":"兩百年前，村子裡只有少數人識字，所以信件都在廣場上被大聲念出來。","h":1},{"w":"literally","p":"adv.","d":"in the exact meaning of the words; really","c":"字面上地；真正地","s":"When I said the test was killing me, I did not mean it literally; I just meant that it was very difficult.","t":"我說考試要我的命時，並不是字面上的意思；我只是說它非常難。"},{"w":"illiterate","p":"adj.","d":"not able to read or write","c":"不識字的","s":"My great-grandfather was illiterate because he never went to school, so he signed his name with a simple mark.","t":"我曾祖父因為從未上過學而不識字，所以他用一個簡單的記號來簽名。"},{"w":"literature","p":"n.","d":"written works such as novels, poems, and plays","c":"文學","s":"She is studying English literature at university and spends most of her time reading novels by Dickens and Austen.","t":"她在大學讀英國文學，大部分時間都在讀狄更斯和奧斯汀的小說。"},{"w":"livestock","p":"n.","d":"farm animals such as cows, sheep, and pigs","c":"家畜；牲畜","s":"Before the typhoon arrived, the farmers moved their livestock into the barns so that the animals would be safe from the wind.","t":"颱風來臨前，農民把牲畜移到穀倉裡，好讓動物不會受到強風傷害。","h":1},{"w":"stock","p":"n.","d":"goods kept in a shop for sale","c":"存貨；庫存","s":"The shop has run out of stock of the popular toy, and the next delivery will not arrive until next week.","t":"這家店那款熱門玩具的存貨已經賣完了，下一批貨要到下週才會到。"},{"w":"in stock","p":"phr.","d":"available to buy in a shop now","c":"有現貨","s":"Do you have this jacket in stock in a medium size? The one on the shelf is too large for me.","t":"這件外套中號的有現貨嗎？架上那件對我來說太大了。"},{"w":"livelihood","p":"n.","d":"the way a person earns money to live","c":"生計","s":"Fishing is the main livelihood of the people in this village, so the new rules about the sea worry them a lot.","t":"捕魚是這個村子居民主要的生計，所以新的海洋規定讓他們非常擔心。"},{"w":"lizard","p":"n.","d":"a small reptile with four legs and a long tail","c":"蜥蜴","s":"A small green lizard ran across the warm wall of the garden and disappeared into a crack before the cat could catch it.","t":"一隻綠色的小蜥蜴跑過花園溫暖的牆面，在貓抓到牠之前鑽進裂縫裡消失了。","h":1},{"w":"reptile","p":"n.","d":"a cold-blooded animal such as a snake, lizard, or crocodile","c":"爬蟲類動物","s":"Snakes, lizards, and crocodiles are all reptiles, which means they are cold-blooded and usually lay eggs.","t":"蛇、蜥蜴和鱷魚都是爬蟲類，也就是說牠們是冷血動物，而且通常會下蛋。","a":"reptiles"},{"w":"gecko","p":"n.","d":"a small lizard that can walk on walls and ceilings","c":"壁虎","s":"In Taiwan, you often hear a gecko making clicking sounds on the ceiling at night, and it helps by eating mosquitoes.","t":"在台灣，晚上常常聽到壁虎在天花板上發出喀喀聲，牠會吃蚊子，對我們有幫助。"},{"w":"locker","p":"n.","d":"a small cupboard with a lock, at school or at a gym","c":"置物櫃","s":"Students keep their textbooks and sports clothes in a locker at school so that their bags are not too heavy.","t":"學生把課本和運動服放在學校的置物櫃裡，這樣書包才不會太重。","h":1},{"w":"lock","p":"v.","d":"to close something with a key","c":"鎖上","s":"Please remember to lock the door and turn off the lights when you are the last person to leave the office.","t":"當你是最後一個離開辦公室的人時，請記得鎖門並關燈。"},{"w":"lock","p":"n.","d":"a device that keeps a door or box closed","c":"鎖","s":"The lock on my bicycle is broken, so I have to carry the bike up to my apartment every night.","t":"我腳踏車的鎖壞了，所以我每晚都得把車搬上公寓。"},{"w":"locker room","p":"n.phr.","d":"a room where people change clothes and keep things in lockers","c":"更衣室","s":"After the game, the coach gathered the players in the locker room and told them how proud he was of their effort.","t":"比賽結束後，教練把球員集合在更衣室，告訴他們自己有多為他們的努力感到驕傲。"},{"w":"unlock","p":"v.","d":"to open something that was locked","c":"開鎖；解鎖","s":"You can unlock this phone with your fingerprint, so you do not need to remember a long password.","t":"你可以用指紋解鎖這支手機，所以不需要記一長串密碼。"},{"w":"lodge","p":"n.","d":"a small house in the countryside, used by hunters, hikers, or skiers","c":"小屋；山莊","s":"We stayed at a mountain lodge near the trail, where the owner cooked hot soup for the tired hikers every evening.","t":"我們住在步道附近的一間山間小屋，屋主每晚都為疲憊的登山客煮熱湯。","h":1},{"w":"lodge","p":"v.","d":"to stay in someone's house and pay rent","c":"投宿；寄宿","s":"During the exchange program, the students will lodge with local families instead of staying in a hotel.","t":"在交換計畫期間，學生們將寄宿在當地家庭，而不是住飯店。"},{"w":"lodge a complaint","p":"v.phr.","d":"to make a formal complaint","c":"提出申訴","s":"Several neighbors decided to lodge a complaint with the city about the loud music coming from the bar every night.","t":"幾位鄰居決定向市政府提出申訴，抗議那家酒吧每晚傳來的吵鬧音樂。"},{"w":"lodging","p":"n.","d":"a place to stay for a short time","c":"住宿；寄宿處","s":"The job offers free lodging and meals, so the young workers can save most of their salary for the future.","t":"這份工作提供免費住宿和餐點，所以年輕員工可以把大部分薪水存起來。"},{"w":"lofty","p":"adj.","d":"very high; (of ideas) noble but hard to achieve","c":"高聳的；崇高的","s":"The young doctor had the lofty goal of building a free hospital for the poor, and she worked toward it for thirty years.","t":"這位年輕醫生有一個崇高的目標——為窮人建一所免費醫院，她為此努力了三十年。","h":1},{"w":"loft","p":"n.","d":"a room or space under the roof of a building","c":"閣樓","s":"We turned the dusty loft under the roof into a cozy reading room with a small window and soft cushions.","t":"我們把屋頂下積滿灰塵的閣樓改造成一間舒適的閱讀室，有小窗戶和柔軟的坐墊。"},{"w":"aloft","p":"adv.","d":"high up in the air","c":"在高處；在空中","s":"The eagle held the fish aloft in its claws as it flew back to its nest high on the cliff.","t":"老鷹用爪子把魚高高地抓在空中，飛回懸崖高處的巢。"},{"w":"logo","p":"n.","d":"a symbol or design that a company uses as its sign","c":"商標；標誌","s":"The sports company's famous logo is a simple curved line, and you can see it on shoes all over the world.","t":"這家運動公司著名的商標是一條簡單的弧線，你可以在世界各地的鞋子上看到它。","h":1},{"w":"logo design","p":"n.phr.","d":"the work of creating a logo","c":"標誌設計","s":"The club held a logo design contest, and the winning picture of a blue bird will be printed on all the new T-shirts.","t":"社團舉辦了標誌設計比賽，獲勝的藍鳥圖案將印在所有的新T恤上。"},{"w":"slogan","p":"n.","d":"a short phrase that is easy to remember, used in advertising","c":"口號；標語","s":"The company's new slogan, \"Think green, live clean,\" appears under the logo on every bus in the city.","t":"這家公司的新標語「思考綠色，生活乾淨」出現在市內每輛公車的商標下方。"},{"w":"lonesome","p":"adj.","d":"sad because you are alone","c":"寂寞的","s":"The old dog looked lonesome sitting by the gate every afternoon, waiting for the children to come home from school.","t":"那隻老狗每天下午坐在門口看起來很寂寞，等著孩子們放學回家。","h":1},{"w":"lonely","p":"adj.","d":"unhappy because you have no friends or people to talk to","c":"孤獨的；寂寞的","s":"Moving to a new city can be lonely at first, but joining a club is a good way to make new friends.","t":"搬到新城市一開始可能會很孤單，但加入社團是交新朋友的好方法。"},{"w":"loneliness","p":"n.","d":"the feeling of being alone and sad","c":"孤獨；寂寞","s":"Many old people suffer from loneliness after their children move away, so weekly visits from volunteers mean a lot to them.","t":"許多老人在孩子搬走後飽受孤獨之苦，所以志工每週的探訪對他們意義重大。"},{"w":"alone","p":"adv.","d":"without other people","c":"獨自地","s":"I prefer to study alone in the library because my roommate always plays music while he does his homework.","t":"我比較喜歡獨自在圖書館讀書，因為我室友做功課時總是放音樂。"},{"w":"all alone","p":"phr.","d":"completely by yourself","c":"獨自一人","s":"The little boy was all alone in the park, so the police officer stayed with him until his mother came.","t":"小男孩獨自一人在公園裡，所以警察陪著他直到他媽媽來。"},{"w":"longevity","p":"n.","d":"long life; lasting a long time","c":"長壽；長久","s":"Scientists believe that the longevity of people in Okinawa comes from their simple diet and active social life.","t":"科學家認為沖繩人的長壽來自他們簡單的飲食和活躍的社交生活。","h":1},{"w":"long-lived","p":"adj.","d":"living or lasting a long time","c":"長壽的","s":"Some turtles are extremely long-lived; one famous giant tortoise reached the age of about one hundred and ninety.","t":"有些烏龜非常長壽；一隻著名的巨型陸龜活到了大約一百九十歲。"},{"w":"prolong","p":"v.","d":"to make something last longer","c":"延長","s":"Regular exercise and a good diet can prolong your life by several years, according to a recent study.","t":"根據最近的一項研究，規律運動和良好的飲食可以延長你好幾年的壽命。"},{"w":"longitude","p":"n.","d":"the distance of a place east or west of an imaginary line through Greenwich","c":"經度","s":"Taiwan lies at about 121 degrees east longitude, which is why its clocks are eight hours ahead of London.","t":"台灣位於東經大約一百二十一度，這就是為什麼它的時鐘比倫敦快八小時。","h":1},{"w":"latitude","p":"n.","d":"the distance of a place north or south of the equator","c":"緯度","s":"Because of its low latitude, Singapore is hot and humid all year round, with almost no difference between seasons.","t":"由於緯度低，新加坡全年又熱又濕，四季幾乎沒有差別。"},{"w":"longitudinal","p":"adj.","d":"(of a study) following the same people over a long period of time","c":"縱向的；長期追蹤的","s":"The researchers carried out a longitudinal study, following the same group of children from kindergarten until they finished university.","t":"研究人員進行了一項長期追蹤研究，從幼兒園一直追蹤同一群孩子到他們大學畢業。"},{"w":"lotion","p":"n.","d":"a liquid that you put on your skin to protect it or make it soft","c":"乳液；護膚液","s":"After a day at the beach, put some cooling lotion on your shoulders, or the sunburn will hurt all night.","t":"在海邊玩了一天之後，在肩膀上擦點清涼的乳液，否則曬傷會痛一整晚。","h":1},{"w":"body lotion","p":"n.phr.","d":"lotion used on the skin of the body","c":"身體乳液","s":"In winter my skin gets very dry, so I use body lotion every night after my shower to keep it soft.","t":"冬天我的皮膚會變得很乾，所以我每晚洗完澡都擦身體乳液來保持柔嫩。"},{"w":"suntan lotion","p":"n.phr.","d":"lotion that protects the skin from the sun","c":"防曬乳","s":"Do not forget to bring suntan lotion to the pool, because the sun is very strong at noon in July.","t":"別忘了帶防曬乳去游泳池，因為七月中午的太陽非常強烈。"}]},{"unit":22,"theme":"lottery – meditation","cards":[{"w":"lottery","p":"n.","d":"a game in which people buy numbered tickets and win money if their numbers are chosen","c":"樂透；彩券；抽籤","s":"My uncle buys a lottery ticket every Friday, but in ten years he has never won more than a few hundred dollars.","t":"我叔叔每個星期五都買一張樂透彩券，但十年來他從沒贏過超過幾百元。","h":1},{"w":"win the lottery","p":"v.phr.","d":"to get the prize money in a lottery","c":"中樂透","s":"If I win the lottery someday, I will pay off my parents' house first and then travel around the world for a year.","t":"如果有一天我中了樂透，我會先付清父母房子的貸款，然後環遊世界一年。"},{"w":"draw lots","p":"v.phr.","d":"to decide something by picking pieces of paper or sticks by chance","c":"抽籤","s":"Since everyone wanted the window seat, the teacher asked us to draw lots so that the choice would be fair.","t":"因為每個人都想要靠窗的座位，老師要我們抽籤，這樣選擇才公平。"},{"w":"parking lot","p":"n.phr.","d":"an area where cars are parked","c":"停車場","s":"The shopping mall's parking lot was so full on Saturday afternoon that we drove around for twenty minutes looking for a space.","t":"星期六下午購物中心的停車場太滿了，我們繞了二十分鐘找車位。"},{"w":"lotus","p":"n.","d":"a plant with large pink or white flowers that grows in water","c":"蓮花；荷花","s":"In July the pond behind the temple is covered with pink lotus flowers, and many photographers come early in the morning to take pictures.","t":"七月時廟後面的池塘開滿了粉紅色的蓮花，許多攝影師一大早就來拍照。","h":1},{"w":"lotus root","p":"n.phr.","d":"the root of the lotus plant, eaten as a vegetable","c":"蓮藕","s":"My grandmother makes a sweet soup with lotus root and red dates, which she says is good for the lungs in dry weather.","t":"我奶奶用蓮藕和紅棗煮甜湯，她說這在乾燥的天氣對肺很好。"},{"w":"lotus seed","p":"n.phr.","d":"the seed of the lotus plant, used in sweets and soups","c":"蓮子","s":"Moon cakes filled with lotus seed paste are my father's favorite, so we always buy a box for him before the Moon Festival.","t":"包蓮子餡的月餅是我爸爸最喜歡的，所以中秋節前我們總會買一盒給他。"},{"w":"lotus position","p":"n.phr.","d":"a way of sitting with legs crossed, used in yoga and meditation","c":"蓮花坐；盤腿坐","s":"At the start of every yoga class, the teacher asks us to sit in the lotus position and breathe slowly for two minutes.","t":"每堂瑜珈課開始時，老師都要我們以蓮花坐坐好，慢慢呼吸兩分鐘。"},{"w":"loudspeaker","p":"n.","d":"a piece of equipment that makes sound louder so many people can hear it","c":"擴音器；喇叭","s":"A voice came through the loudspeaker telling all passengers that the train to Kaohsiung would leave from platform two.","t":"擴音器傳來一個聲音，告訴所有旅客前往高雄的火車將從第二月台出發。","h":1},{"w":"loud","p":"adj.","d":"making a lot of noise","c":"大聲的","s":"The music at the party was so loud that the neighbors called the police to complain at eleven o'clock.","t":"派對的音樂太大聲了，鄰居在十一點打電話向警察抱怨。"},{"w":"loudly","p":"adv.","d":"in a way that makes a lot of noise","c":"大聲地","s":"The baby cried so loudly on the airplane that the people sitting nearby could not sleep at all during the flight.","t":"那個嬰兒在飛機上哭得非常大聲，坐在附近的人整趟飛行都完全無法入睡。"},{"w":"speaker","p":"n.","d":"a person who gives a talk; a piece of equipment that produces sound","c":"演講者；揚聲器","s":"The guest speaker at the graduation ceremony told the students to follow their dreams and never stop learning new things.","t":"畢業典禮上的特邀演講者告訴學生要追隨夢想，永遠不要停止學習新事物。"},{"w":"aloud","p":"adv.","d":"in a voice that other people can hear","c":"出聲地；大聲地","s":"The teacher asked each student to read one paragraph aloud so that the whole class could practice their pronunciation together.","t":"老師要每位學生出聲朗讀一段，好讓全班一起練習發音。"},{"w":"lucrative","p":"adj.","d":"making a lot of money","c":"賺錢的；有利可圖的","s":"Selling bubble tea near the university has turned out to be a lucrative business, and the owner opened a second shop last month.","t":"在大學附近賣珍珠奶茶結果成了一門賺錢的生意，老闆上個月開了第二家店。","h":1},{"w":"lucrative contract","p":"n.phr.","d":"an agreement that pays a lot of money","c":"高報酬的合約","s":"The young baseball star signed a lucrative contract with a team in Japan, which will pay him more than he could earn at home.","t":"這位年輕的棒球明星和一支日本球隊簽了一份高報酬的合約，薪水比他在國內能賺的還多。"},{"w":"profitable","p":"adj.","d":"making a profit","c":"有利潤的；賺錢的","s":"The small restaurant became profitable only after the owner started selling lunch boxes to the office workers nearby.","t":"這家小餐廳在老闆開始賣便當給附近的上班族之後才開始賺錢。"},{"w":"profit","p":"n.","d":"the money you make after paying your costs","c":"利潤","s":"The students sold cookies at the school fair and gave all the profit to a home for stray dogs in the city.","t":"學生們在校園園遊會賣餅乾，並把全部利潤捐給市內的一間流浪狗之家。"},{"w":"lullaby","p":"n.","d":"a quiet song that you sing to a child to make it sleep","c":"搖籃曲；催眠曲","s":"Every night my mother sang the same soft lullaby to my little brother until his eyes closed and he fell asleep.","t":"每天晚上我媽媽都對弟弟唱同一首輕柔的搖籃曲，直到他閉上眼睛睡著。","h":1},{"w":"lull","p":"v.","d":"to make someone feel calm or sleepy","c":"使平靜；使入睡","s":"The gentle sound of the rain on the roof lulled me to sleep within a few minutes after I lay down.","t":"屋頂上輕柔的雨聲在我躺下後幾分鐘內就哄我入睡了。","a":"lulled"},{"w":"lull","p":"n.","d":"a short quiet period in a noisy or busy situation","c":"暫時的平靜","s":"There was a short lull in the storm around noon, so we ran to the store to buy food before the wind returned.","t":"中午左右暴風雨有一段短暫的平靜，所以我們趁風再起之前跑去商店買食物。"},{"w":"cradle","p":"n.","d":"a small bed for a baby that can be moved from side to side","c":"搖籃","s":"The baby slept peacefully in a wooden cradle that her grandfather had made by hand many years before she was born.","t":"寶寶安穩地睡在一個木製搖籃裡，那是她爺爺在她出生前許多年親手做的。"},{"w":"lunar","p":"adj.","d":"connected with the moon","c":"月亮的；農曆的","s":"Chinese New Year follows the lunar calendar, so its date on the regular calendar changes a little every year.","t":"農曆新年依照陰曆（農曆），所以它在一般日曆上的日期每年都會稍有變動。","h":1},{"w":"lunar eclipse","p":"n.phr.","d":"a time when the earth passes between the sun and the moon and the moon goes dark","c":"月蝕","s":"We stayed up until two in the morning to watch the lunar eclipse, and the moon slowly turned a deep red color.","t":"我們熬夜到凌晨兩點看月蝕，月亮慢慢變成深紅色。"},{"w":"Lunar New Year","p":"n.phr.","d":"the first days of the year in the lunar calendar","c":"農曆新年","s":"During the Lunar New Year, most shops in Taiwan close for several days, and families gather for a big dinner together.","t":"農曆新年期間，台灣大多數商店會關門好幾天，家人聚在一起吃一頓豐盛的晚餐。"},{"w":"solar","p":"adj.","d":"connected with the sun","c":"太陽的","s":"The new solar panels on the school roof produce enough electricity to power all the classroom lights during the day.","t":"學校屋頂上新裝的太陽能板產生的電力足以在白天供應所有教室的燈。"},{"w":"lure","p":"v.","d":"to make someone go somewhere or do something by offering them something nice","c":"引誘；吸引","s":"The shop uses free samples of cake to lure customers inside, and most of them end up buying a whole box.","t":"這家店用免費試吃的蛋糕引誘顧客進店，而且大多數人最後都買了一整盒。","h":1},{"w":"lure","p":"n.","d":"the power to attract people; something used to attract fish or animals","c":"誘惑力；誘餌","s":"The lure of a high salary made many young engineers leave their hometown and move to the big city for work.","t":"高薪的誘惑讓許多年輕工程師離開家鄉，搬到大城市工作。"},{"w":"lure away","p":"v.phr.","d":"to attract someone so that they leave a place or job","c":"引走；拉走","s":"A bigger company tried to lure away our best designer with a huge salary, but she decided to stay with us.","t":"一家更大的公司試圖用高薪拉走我們最好的設計師，但她決定留下來。"},{"w":"allure","p":"n.","d":"the quality of being attractive and exciting","c":"魅力；吸引力","s":"Part of the allure of Tainan is its old streets, where you can find temples and small snack shops on every corner.","t":"台南的部分魅力在於它的老街，每個轉角都能找到廟宇和小吃店。"},{"w":"bait","p":"n.","d":"food put on a hook or in a trap to catch fish or animals","c":"魚餌；誘餌","s":"The fisherman put a small piece of fish on the hook as bait and waited quietly for a big one to bite.","t":"漁夫把一小塊魚肉掛在鉤子上當魚餌，靜靜地等著大魚上鉤。"},{"w":"lush","p":"adj.","d":"(of plants) growing thickly and strongly; green and healthy","c":"茂盛的；蒼翠的","s":"After a week of heavy rain, the hills behind our school turned lush and green, and wild flowers appeared everywhere.","t":"下了一週大雨之後，學校後面的山丘變得蒼翠碧綠，野花隨處可見。","h":1},{"w":"lush","p":"adj.","d":"very comfortable and expensive","c":"豪華的","s":"The hotel's lush rooms, with thick carpets and silk curtains, made the guests feel like kings and queens.","t":"飯店豪華的房間鋪著厚地毯、掛著絲綢窗簾，讓客人覺得自己像國王和皇后。"},{"w":"dense","p":"adj.","d":"with many things or people close together","c":"稠密的；濃密的","s":"The forest was so dense that almost no sunlight reached the ground, and we needed a flashlight even at noon.","t":"這片森林太茂密了，幾乎沒有陽光照到地面，即使中午我們也需要手電筒。"},{"w":"greenery","p":"n.","d":"green plants and trees","c":"綠色植物；綠意","s":"The new park in the middle of the city is full of greenery, which gives office workers a cool place to rest at lunchtime.","t":"市中心的新公園充滿綠意，讓上班族午休時有個涼爽的地方休息。"},{"w":"madam","p":"n.","d":"a polite way to speak to a woman whose name you do not know (also ma'am)","c":"女士；夫人（ma'am 為口語形式）","s":"\"Excuse me, Madam, you left your umbrella on the seat,\" the young waiter said politely as the woman walked toward the door.","t":"「不好意思，女士，您把雨傘留在座位上了，」年輕的服務生在那位女士走向門口時禮貌地說。","a":"Madam","h":1},{"w":"sir","p":"n.","d":"a polite way to speak to a man","c":"先生","s":"\"Good morning, sir. May I see your ticket, please?\" the conductor asked the old man sitting by the window.","t":"「早安，先生。可以看一下您的車票嗎？」列車長問坐在窗邊的老先生。"},{"w":"lady","p":"n.","d":"a polite word for a woman","c":"女士；小姐","s":"An old lady with a small dog sat next to me on the bus and told me stories about the city when she was young.","t":"一位帶著小狗的老太太在公車上坐在我旁邊，告訴我她年輕時這座城市的故事。"},{"w":"gentleman","p":"n.","d":"a polite word for a man; a man who is polite and behaves well","c":"先生；紳士","s":"The gentleman held the door open for everyone behind him and waited until the last person had walked through.","t":"那位紳士為後面的每個人撐著門，一直等到最後一個人走過去。"},{"w":"ladies and gentlemen","p":"phr.","d":"the polite way to begin a speech to a group of people","c":"各位先生女士","s":"\"Ladies and gentlemen, please take your seats; the show is about to begin in five minutes,\" the announcer said in a clear voice.","t":"「各位先生女士，請就座；表演將在五分鐘後開始，」主持人用清晰的聲音說。","a":"Ladies and gentlemen"},{"w":"magnify","p":"v.","d":"to make something look bigger than it is","c":"放大","s":"This microscope can magnify a drop of pond water four hundred times, so you can see tiny living things swimming in it.","t":"這台顯微鏡可以把一滴池水放大四百倍，所以你可以看到裡面游動的微小生物。","h":1},{"w":"magnifying glass","p":"n.phr.","d":"a round piece of glass that makes things look bigger","c":"放大鏡","s":"My grandfather uses a magnifying glass to read the small print in the newspaper because his eyes are not as good as before.","t":"我爺爺用放大鏡看報紙上的小字，因為他的眼睛不如以前好了。"},{"w":"magnificent","p":"adj.","d":"very beautiful or impressive","c":"壯麗的；宏偉的","s":"From the top of Taipei 101, we had a magnificent view of the whole city and the mountains behind it at sunset.","t":"從台北101的頂樓，我們在日落時欣賞到整座城市及其後方山脈的壯麗景色。"},{"w":"magnitude","p":"n.","d":"the great size or importance of something; the strength of an earthquake","c":"規模；重要性；（地震）規模","s":"The earthquake had a magnitude of 6.4, and people felt the shaking in every part of the island for almost a minute.","t":"這場地震的規模為6.4，全島各地的人都感受到了將近一分鐘的搖晃。"},{"w":"magnet","p":"n.","d":"a piece of metal that pulls iron toward it","c":"磁鐵","s":"Our refrigerator door is covered with magnets from every country my parents have visited over the past twenty years.","t":"我們的冰箱門上貼滿了我父母過去二十年造訪過的每個國家的磁鐵。","a":"magnets"},{"w":"maiden","p":"n.","d":"(old use) a young woman who is not married","c":"少女；未婚女子","s":"In the old story, a brave knight saves a young maiden from a dragon and then marries her in the castle.","t":"在古老的故事裡，一位勇敢的騎士從惡龍手中救出一位年輕少女，然後在城堡裡娶了她。","h":1},{"w":"maiden voyage","p":"n.phr.","d":"the first journey of a new ship","c":"首航","s":"The Titanic sank on its maiden voyage in 1912, and more than fifteen hundred people lost their lives in the icy water.","t":"鐵達尼號在一九一二年的首航中沉沒，超過一千五百人在冰冷的海水中喪生。"},{"w":"maiden name","p":"n.phr.","d":"a woman's family name before she gets married","c":"娘家姓；婚前姓","s":"In Taiwan most women keep their maiden name after they get married, which is different from the custom in many Western countries.","t":"在台灣，大多數女性結婚後仍保留娘家的姓，這和許多西方國家的習俗不同。"},{"w":"maid","p":"n.","d":"a woman whose job is to clean rooms and do housework","c":"女傭；女服務員","s":"The rich family hired a maid to clean the house, cook the meals, and take care of the children after school.","t":"這個有錢的家庭雇了一名女傭來打掃房子、做飯，並在放學後照顧孩子。"},{"w":"bridesmaid","p":"n.","d":"a woman or girl who helps the bride at a wedding","c":"伴娘","s":"My sister asked me to be a bridesmaid at her wedding, so I had to wear a long pink dress and hold flowers.","t":"我姊姊請我在她的婚禮上當伴娘，所以我得穿粉紅色長裙並捧著花。"},{"w":"mainland","p":"n.","d":"the main part of a country or continent, not its islands","c":"大陸；本土","s":"Ferries carry people from the small island to the mainland twice a day, and the trip takes about forty minutes each way.","t":"渡輪每天兩次載人從小島到本島，單程大約需要四十分鐘。","h":1},{"w":"main","p":"adj.","d":"most important; largest","c":"主要的","s":"The main reason I chose this school is that it is only a ten-minute walk from my grandmother's house.","t":"我選擇這所學校主要的原因是它離我奶奶家只有十分鐘的步行路程。"},{"w":"mainly","p":"adv.","d":"for the most part; mostly","c":"主要地；大部分","s":"Our class trip to Hualien was mainly about nature, so we spent two whole days hiking in Taroko Gorge.","t":"我們班到花蓮的旅行主要是親近大自然，所以我們花了整整兩天在太魯閣健行。"},{"w":"mainstream","p":"n.","d":"the ideas and ways of living that most people accept as normal","c":"主流","s":"Electric cars used to be rare, but now they have entered the mainstream and you can see them on every street in Taipei.","t":"電動車以前很少見，但現在已進入主流，在台北的每條街上都能看到。"},{"w":"main course","p":"n.phr.","d":"the most important dish of a meal","c":"主菜","s":"For the main course I ordered grilled fish with vegetables, and my friend chose the beef noodles that the waiter recommended.","t":"主菜我點了烤魚配蔬菜，我朋友則選了服務生推薦的牛肉麵。"},{"w":"majestic","p":"adj.","d":"very beautiful, large, and impressive","c":"雄偉的；壯麗的","s":"The majestic mountains of Yushan rise above the clouds, and hikers who reach the top at sunrise never forget the view.","t":"雄偉的玉山山脈高聳入雲，在日出時登頂的登山客永遠忘不了那景色。","h":1},{"w":"majesty","p":"n.","d":"the quality of being very beautiful, large, and impressive","c":"威嚴；壯麗","s":"Standing at the bottom of the giant waterfall, we were silent for a moment, amazed by its power and majesty.","t":"站在巨大瀑布的底部，我們一時沉默不語，為它的力量與壯麗感到驚嘆。","h":1},{"w":"Your Majesty","p":"n.phr.","d":"the polite way to speak to a king or queen","c":"陛下","s":"\"Your Majesty, the people are waiting outside the palace to hear your speech,\" the servant said with a deep bow.","t":"「陛下，人民正在宮殿外等著聽您的演講，」僕人深深一鞠躬說。"},{"w":"majestically","p":"adv.","d":"in a way that is grand and impressive","c":"雄偉地；莊嚴地","s":"The eagle flew majestically over the valley, its wide wings hardly moving as it rode the warm wind higher and higher.","t":"老鷹莊嚴地飛過山谷，寬闊的翅膀幾乎不動，乘著暖風越飛越高。"},{"w":"manuscript","p":"n.","d":"the text of a book or article before it is printed; an old handwritten book","c":"手稿；原稿","s":"The writer sent her manuscript to ten publishers, and nine of them said no before the last one finally agreed to print it.","t":"這位作家把她的手稿寄給十家出版社，其中九家拒絕了，最後一家才終於同意出版。","h":1},{"w":"script","p":"n.","d":"the written words of a play, movie, or speech","c":"劇本；腳本","s":"The actors spent the whole weekend reading the script together so that everyone would know their lines before filming began.","t":"演員們整個週末一起讀劇本，好讓每個人在開拍前都記住自己的台詞。"},{"w":"handwriting","p":"n.","d":"the way a person writes with a pen or pencil","c":"字跡；筆跡","s":"The doctor's handwriting was so hard to read that the pharmacist had to call his office to check the name of the medicine.","t":"醫生的字跡太難辨認了，藥師不得不打電話到他的診所確認藥名。"},{"w":"transcript","p":"n.","d":"an official record of a student's grades; a written copy of spoken words","c":"成績單；逐字稿","s":"To apply for the university in Canada, you need to send an official transcript of your grades from all three years of senior high school.","t":"要申請加拿大的大學，你需要寄出高中三年成績的正式成績單。"},{"w":"manual","p":"n.","d":"a book that tells you how to use something","c":"使用手冊；說明書","s":"Before using the new washing machine, read the manual carefully, or you might choose the wrong setting and damage your clothes.","t":"使用新洗衣機之前，請仔細閱讀說明書，否則你可能選錯設定而損壞衣服。"},{"w":"maple","p":"n.","d":"a tree with leaves that have five points and turn red in autumn","c":"楓樹","s":"In late November, the maple trees in the mountains of Taiwan turn red and gold, and thousands of visitors drive up to see them.","t":"十一月下旬，台灣山區的楓樹轉為紅色和金色，數千名遊客開車上山觀賞。","h":1},{"w":"maple syrup","p":"n.phr.","d":"a sweet liquid made from the juice of maple trees","c":"楓糖漿","s":"On Sunday mornings my father makes pancakes, and we pour sweet maple syrup from Canada over them before they get cold.","t":"星期天早上我爸爸做鬆餅，我們趁熱淋上來自加拿大的甜楓糖漿。"},{"w":"maple leaf","p":"n.phr.","d":"the leaf of a maple tree, the symbol of Canada","c":"楓葉","s":"The red maple leaf on Canada's flag is one of the most famous national symbols in the world, and it appears on coins too.","t":"加拿大國旗上的紅色楓葉是世界上最著名的國家象徵之一，也出現在硬幣上。"},{"w":"pine","p":"n.","d":"a tall tree with thin sharp leaves that stay green all year","c":"松樹","s":"The old pine trees in the park stay green all winter, and their needles cover the ground like a soft brown carpet.","t":"公園裡的老松樹整個冬天都是綠的，松針像柔軟的棕色地毯一樣鋪滿地面。"},{"w":"mar","p":"v.","d":"to spoil something good or beautiful","c":"損毀；破壞；玷汙","s":"A single ugly red sign on the hillside was enough to mar the beautiful view that the hotel had promised its guests.","t":"山坡上一個醜陋的紅色招牌就足以破壞飯店向客人承諾的美景。","h":1},{"w":"be marred by","p":"v.phr.","d":"to be spoiled by something","c":"被…破壞","s":"The opening ceremony was marred by a power cut, so the singers performed in the dark for nearly ten minutes.","t":"開幕典禮被停電破壞了，歌手們在黑暗中表演了將近十分鐘。","a":"was marred by"},{"w":"spoil","p":"v.","d":"to make something bad or useless; to give a child everything it wants","c":"破壞；寵壞","s":"Please do not spoil the ending of the movie for me; I am going to watch it with my cousins this weekend.","t":"請不要破壞我看電影結局的樂趣；我這個週末要和表兄弟姊妹一起看。"},{"w":"damage","p":"n.","d":"harm that makes something broken or less useful","c":"損壞；損害","s":"The typhoon did serious damage to the roof of our school, so classes were cancelled for two days while workers repaired it.","t":"颱風對我們學校的屋頂造成嚴重損壞，所以工人修理期間停課了兩天。"},{"w":"ruin","p":"v.","d":"to destroy something completely","c":"毀掉；破壞","s":"Too much salt will ruin the soup, so add a little at a time and taste it after each spoonful.","t":"太多鹽會毀掉這鍋湯，所以一次加一點，每加一匙就嚐一下。"},{"w":"marginal","p":"adj.","d":"small and not important","c":"微小的；邊緣的","s":"The new medicine made only a marginal difference to the patient's pain, so the doctor decided to try a stronger one.","t":"新藥對病人的疼痛只有微小的改善，所以醫生決定試試更強的藥。","h":1},{"w":"margin","p":"n.","d":"the empty space at the side of a page; the difference between two amounts","c":"頁邊空白；差距；利潤","s":"Please leave a wide margin on the left side of the page so that the teacher has room to write comments.","t":"請在頁面左側留下寬一點的空白邊，好讓老師有地方寫評語。"},{"w":"by a narrow margin","p":"phr.","d":"by a very small difference","c":"以微小的差距","s":"Our team won the final game by a narrow margin of just two points, and the whole school cheered when the buzzer sounded.","t":"我們的球隊以僅僅兩分的微小差距贏得決賽，蜂鳴器響起時全校都歡呼起來。"},{"w":"marginally","p":"adv.","d":"very slightly","c":"略微地","s":"This year's test was only marginally harder than last year's, so most students got about the same scores as before.","t":"今年的考試只比去年略微難一點，所以大多數學生的分數和以前差不多。"},{"w":"profit margin","p":"n.phr.","d":"the difference between the cost of something and the price it is sold for","c":"利潤率","s":"The bookstore's profit margin is very small, so the owner also sells coffee and cake to make enough money to pay the rent.","t":"這家書店的利潤率很低，所以老闆也賣咖啡和蛋糕來賺足夠的錢付房租。"},{"w":"martial","p":"adj.","d":"connected with fighting or war","c":"武術的；軍事的","s":"The movie is full of martial scenes in which the hero fights ten enemies at once with nothing but his bare hands.","t":"這部電影充滿武打場面，主角赤手空拳同時對抗十個敵人。","h":1},{"w":"martial arts","p":"n.phr.","d":"fighting sports such as kung fu, karate, and judo","c":"武術","s":"My little brother has been learning martial arts since he was six, and now he can break a wooden board with his foot.","t":"我弟弟從六歲就開始學武術，現在他可以用腳踢斷一塊木板。"},{"w":"martial law","p":"n.phr.","d":"control of a country by the army instead of the usual government","c":"戒嚴","s":"Taiwan lived under martial law for thirty-eight years, from 1949 to 1987, and newspapers could not print whatever they wanted.","t":"台灣從一九四九年到一九八七年經歷了三十八年的戒嚴，報紙不能隨意刊登想刊登的內容。"},{"w":"military","p":"adj.","d":"connected with soldiers or the armed forces","c":"軍事的；軍隊的","s":"All young men in Taiwan must complete a period of military service after they finish school or university.","t":"台灣所有年輕男性在完成學業或大學後都必須服一段時間的兵役。"},{"w":"Mars","p":"n.","d":"the red planet that is fourth from the sun, named after the Roman god of war","c":"火星","s":"Scientists hope to send people to Mars within the next twenty years, but the trip would take at least six months each way.","t":"科學家希望在接下來的二十年內把人送上火星，但單程旅行至少需要六個月。"},{"w":"marvel","p":"n.","d":"a wonderful and surprising thing or person","c":"奇觀；奇蹟；令人驚嘆的人或事","s":"The high-speed rail is a marvel of modern engineering; it takes you from Taipei to Kaohsiung in only ninety minutes.","t":"高鐵是現代工程的奇蹟；它只要九十分鐘就能把你從台北帶到高雄。","h":1},{"w":"marvel at","p":"v.phr.","d":"to be very surprised and impressed by something","c":"對…感到驚嘆","s":"Tourists stand in the square and marvel at the old cathedral, which took more than two hundred years to build.","t":"遊客站在廣場上驚嘆於這座古老的大教堂，它花了超過兩百年才建成。"},{"w":"marvelous","p":"adj.","d":"extremely good; wonderful","c":"極好的；非凡的","s":"We had a marvelous time at the beach: the water was warm, the sky was clear, and the food was delicious.","t":"我們在海邊度過了美妙的時光：海水溫暖、天空晴朗、食物美味。"},{"w":"wonder","p":"n.","d":"a feeling of surprise and admiration; something that causes this feeling","c":"驚奇；奇觀","s":"The Great Wall of China is often called one of the seven wonders of the world because of its great length and age.","t":"中國的萬里長城因為長度驚人且歷史悠久，常被稱為世界七大奇觀之一。","a":"wonders"},{"w":"mastery","p":"n.","d":"great skill or knowledge of something; complete control","c":"精通；掌握","s":"Her mastery of English and Japanese helped her get a job as a tour guide for visitors from all over Asia.","t":"她對英語和日語的精通幫助她得到一份導遊工作，接待來自亞洲各地的遊客。","h":1},{"w":"master","p":"v.","d":"to learn how to do something very well","c":"精通；掌握","s":"It takes years of daily practice to master the piano, so do not give up just because the first month is hard.","t":"要精通鋼琴需要多年的每日練習，所以不要因為第一個月很難就放棄。"},{"w":"master","p":"n.","d":"a person who is very skilled at something; the person in charge","c":"大師；主人","s":"The old master taught his students that a good painting begins with hours of patient looking, not with the brush.","t":"老大師教導他的學生，一幅好畫始於數小時耐心的觀察，而不是畫筆。"},{"w":"master's degree","p":"n.phr.","d":"a university degree that you get after your first degree","c":"碩士學位","s":"After working for two years, my sister went back to school to get a master's degree in computer science.","t":"工作兩年後，我姊姊回到學校攻讀電腦科學的碩士學位。"},{"w":"masterpiece","p":"n.","d":"a work of art that is the best of its kind","c":"傑作；代表作","s":"The Mona Lisa is considered a masterpiece, and millions of people visit the museum in Paris every year just to see it.","t":"《蒙娜麗莎》被視為一件傑作，每年有數百萬人造訪巴黎的博物館，只為了看它一眼。"},{"w":"mediate","p":"v.","d":"to try to end a disagreement between two people or groups","c":"調解；調停","s":"When the two neighbors could not agree about the noisy dog, a community leader offered to mediate and help them find a solution.","t":"當兩位鄰居無法就那隻吵鬧的狗達成一致時，一位社區領袖主動提議調解，幫助他們找到解決辦法。","h":1},{"w":"mediator","p":"n.","d":"a person who tries to end a disagreement between others","c":"調解人；調停者","s":"The two companies could not settle the dispute themselves, so they asked an experienced mediator to help them reach an agreement.","t":"兩家公司無法自己解決爭端，所以他們請了一位有經驗的調解人幫助他們達成協議。"},{"w":"mediation","p":"n.","d":"the process of trying to end a disagreement between two sides","c":"調解；調停","s":"Instead of going to court, the couple chose mediation, which was cheaper and let them talk calmly with a third person present.","t":"這對夫妻沒有上法院，而是選擇調解，這樣比較便宜，也能在第三方在場的情況下冷靜地談。"},{"w":"medium","p":"adj.","d":"in the middle between two sizes, amounts, or levels","c":"中等的","s":"Would you like a small, medium, or large drink with your meal? The medium one is only five dollars more.","t":"您的餐點想搭配小杯、中杯還是大杯飲料？中杯只多五元。"},{"w":"media","p":"n.","d":"television, radio, newspapers, and the internet","c":"媒體","s":"Social media such as Instagram and YouTube have changed the way young people get their news and spend their free time.","t":"Instagram 和 YouTube 等社群媒體改變了年輕人獲取新聞和度過空閒時間的方式。"},{"w":"medieval","p":"adj.","d":"connected with the Middle Ages (about AD 1000 to 1450)","c":"中世紀的","s":"The medieval castle on the hill has stone walls three meters thick, which protected the town from enemies eight hundred years ago.","t":"山丘上的中世紀城堡有三公尺厚的石牆，八百年前保護了這座城鎮免受敵人侵襲。","h":1},{"w":"Middle Ages","p":"n.phr.","d":"the period in European history from about AD 1000 to 1450","c":"中世紀","s":"During the Middle Ages, most people in Europe were farmers who never traveled more than a few miles from their village.","t":"在中世紀，歐洲大多數人都是農民，一生從未離開村子超過幾英里。"},{"w":"middle","p":"n.","d":"the central part of something","c":"中間；中央","s":"My grandmother woke up in the middle of the night because she heard a strange noise coming from the kitchen.","t":"我奶奶在半夜當中醒來，因為她聽到廚房傳來奇怪的聲音。"},{"w":"knight","p":"n.","d":"a soldier of high rank in the Middle Ages who rode a horse and wore armor","c":"騎士","s":"In the story, a brave knight rides out of the castle to fight the dragon that has been burning the farmers' fields.","t":"故事中，一位勇敢的騎士騎馬出城，去對抗一直在燒毀農民田地的惡龍。"},{"w":"meditate","p":"v.","d":"to sit quietly and empty your mind in order to become calm","c":"冥想；打坐","s":"Every morning before breakfast, my aunt sits quietly on a cushion to meditate for twenty minutes, which she says calms her mind.","t":"每天早餐前，我阿姨都安靜地坐在坐墊上冥想二十分鐘，她說這能讓她心情平靜。","h":1},{"w":"meditation","p":"n.","d":"the practice of sitting quietly and emptying your mind","c":"冥想；靜坐","s":"Many doctors now recommend meditation to reduce stress, and some schools even teach students how to breathe slowly and relax.","t":"現在許多醫生建議用冥想來減輕壓力，有些學校甚至教學生如何慢慢呼吸和放鬆。","h":1},{"w":"meditate on","p":"v.phr.","d":"to think carefully and deeply about something","c":"深思；仔細思考","s":"The monk told us to meditate on one simple question each day: what truly makes us happy and what we can let go of.","t":"僧人要我們每天深思一個簡單的問題：什麼真正讓我們快樂，以及我們可以放下什麼。"},{"w":"meditative","p":"adj.","d":"thinking deeply and quietly","c":"沉思的；冥想的","s":"Walking alone along the quiet beach at dawn put me in a meditative mood, and I thought about my future for a long time.","t":"黎明時獨自走在安靜的海灘上，讓我進入一種沉思的心情，我想了很久關於自己的未來。"},{"w":"contemplate","p":"v.","d":"to think carefully about something for a long time","c":"沉思；考慮","s":"She sat by the window for an hour to contemplate whether she should accept the job in Tokyo or stay near her family.","t":"她在窗邊坐了一個小時思考該接受東京的工作，還是留在家人身邊。"}]},{"unit":23,"theme":"melancholy – mound","cards":[{"w":"melancholy","p":"n.","d":"a deep feeling of sadness that lasts a long time","c":"憂鬱；愁思","s":"A feeling of melancholy came over me as I watched the last leaves fall from the old tree outside my bedroom window.","t":"當我看著臥室窗外老樹上最後幾片葉子落下時，一股憂鬱湧上心頭。","h":1},{"w":"melancholy","p":"adj.","d":"very sad, or making you feel sad","c":"憂鬱的；令人傷感的","s":"The melancholy music from the violin made several people in the audience cry, even though no one understood the Italian words.","t":"小提琴憂傷的音樂讓觀眾席上好幾個人流淚，儘管沒有人聽得懂義大利文歌詞。"},{"w":"gloomy","p":"adj.","d":"dark and sad; without hope","c":"陰暗的；憂鬱的","s":"The weather has been gloomy all week, with gray skies and cold rain, so nobody feels like going out after school.","t":"這整個星期天氣都很陰沉，灰色的天空和冰冷的雨，所以放學後沒有人想出門。"},{"w":"sorrow","p":"n.","d":"a feeling of great sadness","c":"悲傷；悲痛","s":"Her sorrow at losing her old dog was so deep that she could not look at its photo for many months.","t":"失去老狗的悲傷如此深切，她好幾個月都無法看牠的照片。"},{"w":"mentality","p":"n.","d":"a particular way of thinking","c":"心態；思維方式","s":"Many players on the team have a winning mentality; they believe they can come back even when they are ten points behind.","t":"隊上許多球員都有必勝的心態；即使落後十分，他們也相信自己能反敗為勝。","h":1},{"w":"mental","p":"adj.","d":"connected with the mind","c":"心理的；精神的","s":"Doing crossword puzzles every day is good mental exercise for older people and may help them remember things better.","t":"每天玩填字遊戲對老年人來說是很好的心智運動，可能有助於他們記得更清楚。"},{"w":"mentally","p":"adv.","d":"in the mind","c":"精神上；心理上","s":"After studying for twelve hours straight, I was so mentally tired that I could not even remember my own phone number.","t":"連續讀了十二小時的書後，我精神上累到連自己的電話號碼都記不起來。"},{"w":"mental health","p":"n.phr.","d":"the condition of a person's mind and feelings","c":"心理健康","s":"The school now has a counselor who helps students with their mental health, especially during the stressful weeks before the big exam.","t":"學校現在有一位輔導老師協助學生的心理健康，尤其是在大考前壓力很大的那幾週。"},{"w":"merchandise","p":"n.","d":"goods that are bought and sold","c":"商品；貨物","s":"The shop sells merchandise from the popular cartoon, such as T-shirts, cups, and key rings, and children love it.","t":"這家店賣那部熱門卡通的商品，像是T恤、杯子和鑰匙圈，小朋友都很喜歡。","h":1},{"w":"merchant","p":"n.","d":"a person who buys and sells goods in large amounts","c":"商人","s":"In the old days, a merchant would travel from town to town with a cart full of cloth, salt, and tea to sell.","t":"從前，商人會帶著裝滿布料、鹽和茶葉的推車，從一個城鎮走到另一個城鎮去賣。"},{"w":"commerce","p":"n.","d":"the buying and selling of goods and services","c":"商業；貿易","s":"The invention of the internet changed commerce forever, because now people can buy almost anything without leaving home.","t":"網路的發明永遠改變了商業，因為現在人們不用出門幾乎什麼都買得到。"},{"w":"commercial","p":"adj.","d":"connected with buying and selling; made to make money","c":"商業的","s":"During the basketball game there were so many commercial breaks that my dad fell asleep before the fourth quarter started.","t":"籃球比賽中有太多廣告時間，我爸爸在第四節開始前就睡著了。"},{"w":"goods","p":"n.","d":"things that are made to be sold","c":"商品；貨物","s":"The store received a truck full of new goods this morning, so the workers were busy putting everything on the shelves.","t":"這家店今天早上收到一整卡車的新貨，所以員工忙著把所有東西上架。"},{"w":"mermaid","p":"n.","d":"an imaginary sea creature with a woman's upper body and a fish's tail","c":"美人魚","s":"In the fairy tale, a mermaid gives up her beautiful voice so that she can have legs and walk on land with the prince.","t":"在童話故事裡，美人魚放棄了她美妙的聲音，好讓自己有雙腿能和王子一起在陸地上行走。","h":1},{"w":"fairy tale","p":"n.phr.","d":"a traditional story for children with magic and imaginary creatures","c":"童話故事","s":"My little sister asks for the same fairy tale every night, and she gets angry if I change even one word of the story.","t":"我妹妹每天晚上都要聽同一個童話故事，如果我改了故事裡的任何一個字，她就會生氣。"},{"w":"legend","p":"n.","d":"an old story about people or events that may not be true","c":"傳說","s":"According to a local legend, a giant turtle sleeps under the lake and causes a flood whenever it turns over.","t":"根據當地的傳說，有一隻巨大的烏龜睡在湖底，每當牠翻身就會引發洪水。"},{"w":"myth","p":"n.","d":"an old story about gods or heroes; something many people believe that is not true","c":"神話；迷思","s":"The story of the dragon is only a myth, but the villagers still leave rice at the cave door every spring.","t":"龍的故事只是個神話，但村民每年春天仍然會在洞口放米。"},{"w":"migrant","p":"n.","d":"a person who moves to another place or country to find work","c":"移居者；移工","s":"Thousands of migrants come to the city every year looking for work in factories, restaurants, and construction sites.","t":"每年有數千名移居者來到這座城市，在工廠、餐廳和建築工地找工作。","a":"migrants","h":1},{"w":"migrant worker","p":"n.phr.","d":"a person who comes from another place or country to work","c":"移工；外籍勞工","s":"Many migrant workers from Vietnam and the Philippines take care of elderly people in Taiwan, and some of them stay for over ten years.","t":"許多來自越南和菲律賓的移工在台灣照顧老人，有些人一待就超過十年。","a":"migrant workers"},{"w":"migrate","p":"v.","d":"(of birds or animals) to move to another place at a certain time of year; to move to another country","c":"遷徙；移居","s":"Every autumn, millions of birds migrate south to warmer countries, and some of them stop in Taiwan to rest and eat.","t":"每年秋天，數百萬隻鳥向南遷徙到較溫暖的國家，其中有些會在台灣停留休息覓食。"},{"w":"migration","p":"n.","d":"the movement of many people or animals from one place to another","c":"遷徙；移居","s":"The great migration of animals across the African grasslands is one of the most amazing sights in the natural world.","t":"動物橫越非洲草原的大遷徙是自然界最令人驚嘆的景象之一。"},{"w":"immigrant","p":"n.","d":"a person who comes to live permanently in another country","c":"（外來）移民","s":"My grandfather came to Taiwan as an immigrant in 1949 with nothing but a small bag and a photograph of his mother.","t":"我爺爺一九四九年以移民身分來到台灣，身上只有一個小包和一張他母親的照片。"},{"w":"mimic","p":"v.","d":"to copy the way someone speaks or moves, often to make people laugh","c":"模仿","s":"My little cousin likes to mimic the way our teacher talks, and his voice sounds so similar that everyone bursts out laughing.","t":"我的小表弟喜歡模仿我們老師說話的樣子，聲音像到大家都笑出來。","h":1},{"w":"mimic","p":"n.","d":"a person who is good at copying how others speak or move","c":"善於模仿的人","s":"The comedian is a brilliant mimic; he can copy the voices of famous singers and politicians so well that you cannot tell the difference.","t":"這位喜劇演員是個出色的模仿者；他模仿知名歌手和政治人物的聲音像到讓你分不出差別。"},{"w":"imitate","p":"v.","d":"to copy someone or something","c":"模仿；仿效","s":"Babies learn to speak by trying to imitate the sounds they hear their parents make every day.","t":"嬰兒透過嘗試模仿每天聽到父母發出的聲音來學說話。"},{"w":"imitation","p":"n.","d":"a copy of something; the act of copying","c":"仿製品；模仿","s":"This handbag is only an imitation of the famous brand, but it looks so real that few people can tell.","t":"這個手提包只是那個名牌的仿製品，但看起來很真，很少有人分得出來。"},{"w":"copy","p":"v.","d":"to do the same thing as someone else; to make something exactly like another","c":"模仿；抄襲；複製","s":"The teacher warned us not to copy answers from the internet, because she can easily find out where the words came from.","t":"老師警告我們不要從網路上抄答案，因為她很容易就能查出那些文字來自哪裡。"},{"w":"mingle","p":"v.","d":"to move around and talk to different people at a social event; to mix","c":"交際；混合","s":"At the party, the host asked everyone to mingle and talk to at least three people they had never met before.","t":"派對上，主人要每個人四處交流，至少和三位從未見過的人聊天。","h":1},{"w":"mingle with","p":"v.phr.","d":"to mix and talk with a group of people","c":"與…交際往來","s":"The famous actor likes to mingle with ordinary fans at the night market, and he never refuses to take a photo with them.","t":"這位知名演員喜歡在夜市和普通粉絲打成一片，而且從不拒絕和他們合照。"},{"w":"mix","p":"v.","d":"to put different things together so they become one","c":"混合；攪拌","s":"First mix the flour and sugar in a large bowl, and then slowly add the milk while stirring with a wooden spoon.","t":"先在大碗裡把麵粉和糖混合，然後一邊用木湯匙攪拌一邊慢慢加入牛奶。"},{"w":"mixture","p":"n.","d":"something made by mixing different things together","c":"混合物","s":"Pour the mixture into the pan and cook it for ten minutes until the top turns golden brown.","t":"把混合物倒進鍋裡煮十分鐘，直到表面變成金黃色。"},{"w":"blend","p":"n.","d":"a mixture of different things that go well together","c":"混合物；調和","s":"This tea is a blend of green tea and jasmine flowers, which gives it a soft, sweet smell that many people love.","t":"這款茶是綠茶和茉莉花的混合，散發出許多人喜愛的柔和甜香。"},{"w":"miraculous","p":"adj.","d":"very surprising and lucky, like a miracle","c":"奇蹟般的","s":"The doctors had little hope, but the girl made a miraculous recovery and walked out of the hospital two weeks later.","t":"醫生原本不抱什麼希望，但女孩奇蹟般地康復了，兩週後走出了醫院。","h":1},{"w":"miracle","p":"n.","d":"a wonderful event that seems impossible to explain","c":"奇蹟","s":"It was a miracle that no one was hurt when the bus rolled off the road and into the river.","t":"公車衝出道路翻進河裡時竟然沒有人受傷，真是個奇蹟。"},{"w":"miraculously","p":"adv.","d":"in a surprising and lucky way","c":"奇蹟般地","s":"The old man was trapped under the broken house for three days, but miraculously rescuers found him alive and only slightly hurt.","t":"老先生被困在倒塌的房子下三天，但奇蹟般地救難人員發現他還活著，而且只受了輕傷。"},{"w":"by a miracle","p":"phr.","d":"in a way that is very lucky and hard to explain","c":"奇蹟似地","s":"By a miracle, the little dog survived the typhoon by hiding under a car for two whole days.","t":"奇蹟似地，小狗躲在一輛車下整整兩天，熬過了颱風。","a":"By a miracle"},{"w":"miscellaneous","p":"adj.","d":"of many different kinds that do not belong to one group","c":"各式各樣的；雜項的","s":"The last drawer in my desk is full of miscellaneous items: old keys, broken pens, rubber bands, coins, and a few photos.","t":"我書桌最後一個抽屜裝滿了各式各樣的東西：舊鑰匙、壞掉的筆、橡皮筋、硬幣和幾張照片。","h":1},{"w":"miscellaneous expenses","p":"n.phr.","d":"small amounts of money spent on many different things","c":"雜費；雜支","s":"Besides rent and food, you should keep some money every month for miscellaneous expenses such as haircuts, gifts, and bus tickets.","t":"除了房租和伙食，你每個月應該留一些錢給雜費，像是理髮、禮物和公車票。"},{"w":"various","p":"adj.","d":"several different","c":"各種的；不同的","s":"The museum shop sells various kinds of postcards, so you will surely find one that your grandmother will like.","t":"博物館的商店賣各種明信片，所以你一定能找到一張奶奶會喜歡的。"},{"w":"assorted","p":"adj.","d":"of different types, mixed together","c":"什錦的；混合的","s":"She brought a box of assorted cookies to the party, with chocolate, butter, and almond flavors for everyone to choose from.","t":"她帶了一盒什錦餅乾到派對，有巧克力、奶油和杏仁口味讓大家選。"},{"w":"mischievous","p":"adj.","d":"liking to play tricks and cause small trouble","c":"調皮的；淘氣的","s":"The mischievous boy hid his sister's shoes before school, and then he laughed when she searched the whole house for them.","t":"那個調皮的男孩上學前把姊姊的鞋子藏起來，然後看她找遍整個家時笑個不停。","h":1},{"w":"mischief","p":"n.","d":"bad behavior that causes trouble but no serious harm","c":"惡作劇；淘氣","s":"The twins are always up to some mischief, such as putting salt in the sugar bowl or hiding the TV remote.","t":"這對雙胞胎總是在搞惡作劇，像是把鹽放進糖罐或藏起電視遙控器。"},{"w":"naughty","p":"adj.","d":"(of a child or pet) behaving badly","c":"頑皮的；不聽話的","s":"The naughty puppy chewed up my new sneakers while I was at school, but I could not stay angry at its sweet face.","t":"那隻頑皮的小狗趁我上學時把我的新球鞋咬爛了，但看到牠可愛的臉我實在氣不起來。"},{"w":"mischievously","p":"adv.","d":"in a playful way that causes a little trouble","c":"調皮地","s":"She smiled mischievously and said she had a surprise for me, but she would not tell me what it was until my birthday.","t":"她調皮地笑著說有個驚喜要給我，但要到我生日那天才肯告訴我是什麼。"},{"w":"mistress","p":"n.","d":"the woman who owns or is in charge of something, such as a pet or a house","c":"女主人","s":"The dog ran to the door as soon as it heard its mistress turn the key, and it jumped up to welcome her home.","t":"狗一聽到女主人轉動鑰匙的聲音就跑到門口，跳起來歡迎她回家。","h":1},{"w":"master","p":"n.","d":"the man who owns or is in charge of something, such as a pet","c":"男主人；主人","s":"The dog waited by the gate every evening for its master to come home from work, and it never missed a single day.","t":"那隻狗每天傍晚都在門口等主人下班回家，一天也沒有錯過。"},{"w":"Mrs.","p":"n.","d":"a title used before the family name of a married woman","c":"太太；夫人","s":"Mrs. Wang, our new math teacher, is strict about homework, but she explains difficult problems so clearly that nobody falls asleep.","t":"我們的新數學老師王太太對功課很嚴格，但她把難題解釋得非常清楚，沒有人會睡著。"},{"w":"Miss","p":"n.","d":"a title used before the family name of a woman who is not married","c":"小姐","s":"Miss Chen, who teaches us art on Fridays, is only twenty-five, and she is the youngest teacher at our school this year.","t":"每週五教我們美術的陳小姐只有二十五歲，是我們學校今年最年輕的老師。"},{"w":"headmistress","p":"n.","d":"a woman who is the head of a school","c":"女校長","s":"The headmistress spoke to the whole school on the first day and reminded us to be kind to the new students.","t":"開學第一天，女校長對全校講話，提醒我們要善待新同學。"},{"w":"mobilize","p":"v.","d":"to bring people together and get them ready to act","c":"動員","s":"After the earthquake, the government moved quickly to mobilize soldiers and volunteers to search for people trapped under fallen buildings.","t":"地震後，政府迅速動員軍人和志工，搜救被困在倒塌建築下的人。","h":1},{"w":"mobile","p":"adj.","d":"able to move or be moved easily","c":"可移動的；行動的","s":"A mobile library visits our village every Wednesday, so people who cannot travel to town can still borrow books.","t":"行動圖書館每週三都會來我們村子，所以無法進城的人也能借書。"},{"w":"mobile phone","p":"n.phr.","d":"a telephone that you can carry with you","c":"手機；行動電話","s":"Students must turn off their mobile phones during the exam and put them in the box at the front of the classroom.","t":"學生在考試期間必須關掉手機，並放進教室前面的箱子裡。","a":"mobile phones"},{"w":"mobility","p":"n.","d":"the ability to move or travel around easily","c":"行動能力；移動性","s":"After the car accident, my uncle lost some of the mobility in his left leg, so he now walks with a stick.","t":"車禍後，我叔叔左腿的行動能力變差了，所以他現在拄著拐杖走路。"},{"w":"automobile","p":"n.","d":"a car","c":"汽車","s":"The first automobile factory in the country opened in 1950, and today it produces more than half a million cars every year.","t":"這個國家的第一座汽車工廠於一九五〇年開幕，如今每年生產超過五十萬輛車。"},{"w":"modernize","p":"v.","d":"to make something more modern by using new ideas or equipment","c":"使現代化","s":"The city plans to modernize its old train stations by adding elevators, free Wi-Fi, and clear signs in several languages.","t":"市政府計畫透過增設電梯、免費Wi-Fi和多語清楚標示，讓老舊的火車站現代化。","h":1},{"w":"modernization","p":"n.","d":"the process of making something modern","c":"現代化","s":"The modernization of farming, with machines replacing hand work, has allowed one farmer to grow food for hundreds of people.","t":"農業的現代化，以機器取代人工，讓一位農夫就能種出供應數百人的糧食。","h":1},{"w":"modern","p":"adj.","d":"of the present time; using the newest ideas or methods","c":"現代的；新式的","s":"The new library is a very modern building with glass walls, a rooftop garden, and computers on every floor.","t":"新圖書館是一棟非常現代化的建築，有玻璃牆、屋頂花園，每層樓都有電腦。"},{"w":"up-to-date","p":"adj.","d":"including the newest information; modern","c":"最新的；現代的","s":"Make sure the information on your résumé is up-to-date before you send it to the company next week.","t":"下週把履歷寄給公司之前，請確認上面的資訊是最新的。"},{"w":"old-fashioned","p":"adj.","d":"not modern; from the past","c":"老式的；過時的","s":"My grandmother still uses an old-fashioned telephone with a round dial, and she refuses to buy a smartphone.","t":"我奶奶還在用老式的轉盤電話，而且她拒絕買智慧型手機。"},{"w":"momentum","p":"n.","d":"the force that keeps something moving or growing stronger","c":"動力；氣勢；動量","s":"The campaign to clean up the river gained momentum after a famous singer posted photos of the dirty water online.","t":"在一位知名歌手把髒河水的照片貼上網之後，清理河川的活動獲得了動力。","h":1},{"w":"gain momentum","p":"v.phr.","d":"to become stronger or faster","c":"獲得動力；勢頭增強","s":"The small bookshop's weekend reading club gained momentum quickly, and now more than fifty people come every Saturday morning.","t":"這家小書店的週末讀書會很快聲勢大增，現在每週六早上有超過五十人參加。","a":"gained momentum"},{"w":"moment","p":"n.","d":"a very short period of time","c":"片刻；時刻","s":"Wait a moment, please; I just need to find my keys before we leave for the station.","t":"請等一下；我們去車站前，我得先找到我的鑰匙。"},{"w":"momentary","p":"adj.","d":"lasting for a very short time","c":"短暫的；瞬間的","s":"There was a momentary silence in the room after the loud crash, and then everyone started talking at once.","t":"巨響之後房間裡出現短暫的沉默，然後大家同時開始說話。"},{"w":"at the moment","p":"phr.","d":"now; at the present time","c":"此刻；目前","s":"I'm sorry, the manager is in a meeting at the moment, but I can ask her to call you back within an hour.","t":"很抱歉，經理目前在開會，但我可以請她在一小時內回電給您。"},{"w":"monarch","p":"n.","d":"a king or queen","c":"君主","s":"Queen Elizabeth II was the monarch of the United Kingdom for seventy years, longer than any other king or queen in its history.","t":"伊莉莎白二世女王擔任英國君主長達七十年，比歷史上任何一位國王或女王都久。","h":1},{"w":"monarchy","p":"n.","d":"a system of government with a king or queen as head","c":"君主制；君主國","s":"Japan, Thailand, and Britain are among the countries that still have a monarchy, although the kings and queens have little real power.","t":"日本、泰國和英國都是仍保有君主制的國家，不過國王和女王幾乎沒有實權。"},{"w":"royal","p":"adj.","d":"connected with a king or queen","c":"皇家的；王室的","s":"Thousands of people lined the streets to watch the royal wedding, and the whole ceremony was shown live on television.","t":"數千人沿街觀看王室婚禮，整個典禮在電視上現場轉播。"},{"w":"throne","p":"n.","d":"the special chair of a king or queen; the position of being king or queen","c":"王座；王位","s":"The young prince was only nine years old when he came to the throne, so his uncle ruled the country for him.","t":"年輕的王子登上王位時只有九歲，所以由他的叔叔代他治理國家。"},{"w":"reign","p":"n.","d":"the period when a king or queen rules","c":"在位期間；統治","s":"During her long reign, the queen saw fifteen different prime ministers come and go, and the world changed in ways she never expected.","t":"在她漫長的在位期間，女王見證了十五位首相的更迭，世界也以她從未預料到的方式改變了。"},{"w":"monetary","p":"adj.","d":"connected with money, especially a country's money","c":"貨幣的；金錢的","s":"The central bank changed its monetary policy and raised interest rates to slow down the rising prices of food and housing.","t":"中央銀行調整了貨幣政策並提高利率，以減緩食物和房價的上漲。","h":1},{"w":"money","p":"n.","d":"coins and paper notes used to buy things","c":"錢；金錢","s":"I have been saving money from my part-time job for a year so that I can buy a laptop before university starts.","t":"我已經把打工賺的錢存了一年，好在上大學前買一台筆電。"},{"w":"currency","p":"n.","d":"the money used in a particular country","c":"貨幣","s":"Before our trip to Japan, we went to the bank to change some New Taiwan dollars into Japanese currency.","t":"去日本旅行前，我們到銀行把一些新台幣換成日本貨幣。"},{"w":"financial","p":"adj.","d":"connected with money and how it is managed","c":"財務的；金融的","s":"After losing his job, my uncle had serious financial problems and had to borrow money from his brother to pay the rent.","t":"失業後，我叔叔遇到嚴重的財務問題，不得不向他哥哥借錢付房租。"},{"w":"monotony","p":"n.","d":"boring sameness, with no change or variety","c":"單調；乏味","s":"To break the monotony of the long bus ride, the tour guide told jokes and taught us a few songs in Hakka.","t":"為了打破長途巴士旅程的單調，導遊講笑話，還教我們幾首客家歌。","h":1},{"w":"monotonous","p":"adj.","d":"boring because it never changes","c":"單調的；乏味的","s":"The speaker's monotonous voice never went up or down, and half the audience was asleep before he reached his second point.","t":"演講者單調的聲音從不高低起伏，他講到第二點之前就有一半的聽眾睡著了。"},{"w":"monotone","p":"n.","d":"a way of speaking in which the voice stays at the same level","c":"單調的聲音","s":"The robot read the instructions in a flat monotone, with no feeling at all, which made the safety video rather boring.","t":"機器人用毫無起伏的單調聲音念出說明，完全沒有感情，讓安全影片相當無聊。"},{"w":"boredom","p":"n.","d":"the feeling of being bored","c":"無聊；厭倦","s":"Out of pure boredom on the rainy afternoon, the children started counting the cars that passed the window.","t":"在下雨的午後，孩子們純粹因為無聊，開始數經過窗外的車子。"},{"w":"monstrous","p":"adj.","d":"extremely large and frightening","c":"巨大的；駭人的","s":"The monstrous wave, as tall as a five-story building, swept away the boats in the harbor in less than a minute.","t":"那道巨大駭人的海浪有五層樓高，不到一分鐘就把港口裡的船沖走了。","h":1},{"w":"monstrous","p":"adj.","d":"very cruel and shocking","c":"滔天的；極惡的","s":"Stealing money from poor old people is a monstrous crime, and the judge sent the man to prison for ten years.","t":"偷窮苦老人的錢是令人髮指的罪行，法官判那名男子入獄十年。"},{"w":"monster","p":"n.","d":"a large, ugly, frightening creature in stories","c":"怪物","s":"In the movie, a huge monster rises out of the sea and attacks the city, and only a little girl knows how to stop it.","t":"電影中，一隻巨大的怪物從海裡升起攻擊城市，只有一個小女孩知道如何阻止牠。"},{"w":"gigantic","p":"adj.","d":"extremely large","c":"巨大的","s":"A gigantic balloon in the shape of a dinosaur floated above the parade, and children screamed with excitement when they saw it.","t":"一個恐龍形狀的巨大氣球飄在遊行隊伍上方，孩子們看到時興奮地尖叫。"},{"w":"moody","p":"adj.","d":"having moods that change quickly; often unhappy or angry","c":"喜怒無常的；情緒化的","s":"My teenage brother has been very moody lately; one minute he is laughing and the next minute he slams his door and will not talk.","t":"我十幾歲的弟弟最近非常情緒化；前一分鐘還在笑，下一分鐘就甩門不說話。","h":1},{"w":"mood","p":"n.","d":"the way you feel at a particular time","c":"心情；情緒","s":"The boss is in a good mood today because the company just won a big contract, so it is a good time to ask for a day off.","t":"老闆今天心情很好，因為公司剛拿到一份大合約，所以現在是請假的好時機。"},{"w":"in the mood for","p":"phr.","d":"wanting to have or do something","c":"想要…；有…的興致","s":"I'm not in the mood for pizza tonight; let's have something lighter, like a bowl of noodles or a salad.","t":"我今晚不想吃披薩；我們吃點清淡的吧，像是一碗麵或沙拉。"},{"w":"moodiness","p":"n.","d":"the state of having quickly changing moods","c":"喜怒無常；情緒化","s":"Her moodiness made it hard for her friends to know whether she would be happy or angry when they called.","t":"她的情緒化讓朋友們很難知道打電話給她時，她會是開心還是生氣。"},{"w":"morale","p":"n.","d":"the level of confidence and good feeling in a group of people","c":"士氣","s":"After three losses in a row, the team's morale was low, so the coach took everyone out for pizza and a movie.","t":"連輸三場後，球隊的士氣很低落，所以教練帶大家去吃披薩、看電影。","h":1},{"w":"boost morale","p":"v.phr.","d":"to make a group of people feel more confident and positive","c":"提振士氣","s":"The manager gave everyone a Friday afternoon off to boost morale after the long and tiring project.","t":"在漫長又累人的專案結束後，經理讓大家星期五下午放假，以提振士氣。"},{"w":"moral","p":"adj.","d":"connected with what is right and wrong","c":"道德的","s":"The story teaches a moral lesson: if you tell one lie, you will soon have to tell many more to cover it.","t":"這個故事教了一個道德教訓：如果你說了一個謊，很快就得說更多謊來掩蓋它。"},{"w":"moral","p":"n.","d":"the lesson that a story teaches","c":"寓意；教訓","s":"The moral of the story is that slow and steady work wins in the end, just like the tortoise beat the rabbit.","t":"這個故事的寓意是穩紮穩打最終會獲勝，就像烏龜打敗了兔子。"},{"w":"morality","p":"n.","d":"ideas about what is right and wrong","c":"道德；道德觀","s":"Some people say that morality comes from religion, but others believe that we are born knowing right from wrong.","t":"有些人說道德來自宗教，但其他人相信我們天生就知道是非對錯。"},{"w":"mortal","p":"adj.","d":"that must die one day; that cannot live forever","c":"終有一死的","s":"All living things are mortal; even the giant trees in the forest will one day grow old and die.","t":"所有生物都是終有一死的；就連森林裡的巨樹有一天也會衰老死去。","h":1},{"w":"mortal","p":"n.","d":"a human being, who must die one day","c":"凡人","s":"In Greek stories, the gods on the mountain often come down to earth and fall in love with ordinary mortals.","t":"在希臘故事中，山上的眾神常常下到人間，愛上平凡的凡人。","a":"mortals"},{"w":"mortality","p":"n.","d":"the number of deaths in a certain period; the fact that people must die","c":"死亡率；必死性","s":"Thanks to clean water and vaccines, child mortality in the country has dropped sharply over the past fifty years.","t":"多虧了乾淨的水和疫苗，這個國家的兒童死亡率在過去五十年大幅下降。"},{"w":"immortal","p":"adj.","d":"living or lasting forever","c":"不朽的；永生的","s":"Shakespeare's plays are immortal; four hundred years after his death, they are still performed in theaters around the world.","t":"莎士比亞的戲劇是不朽的；在他去世四百年後，世界各地的劇院仍在上演。"},{"w":"motherhood","p":"n.","d":"the state of being a mother","c":"母親身分；母職","s":"Motherhood changed my sister's life completely; now she gets up at five every morning and has not slept a full night in a year.","t":"當媽媽完全改變了我姊姊的生活；現在她每天早上五點起床，一年來沒有睡過一個完整的夜晚。","a":"Motherhood","h":1},{"w":"Mother's Day","p":"n.phr.","d":"a special day for honoring mothers, in May","c":"母親節","s":"On Mother's Day, my brother and I cooked breakfast for Mom and gave her a card we had made ourselves.","t":"母親節那天，我和哥哥為媽媽做早餐，還送她一張我們自己做的卡片。"},{"w":"motherly","p":"adj.","d":"kind and caring, like a good mother","c":"慈母般的","s":"Our neighbor is a motherly woman who always brings hot soup when anyone on the street is sick.","t":"我們的鄰居是位慈母般的女士，街上有人生病時，她總會送來熱湯。"},{"w":"childhood","p":"n.","d":"the time when a person is a child","c":"童年","s":"My grandfather spent his childhood in a small fishing village, where he learned to swim before he could read.","t":"我爺爺在一個小漁村度過童年，在那裡他還不識字就先學會了游泳。"},{"w":"fatherhood","p":"n.","d":"the state of being a father","c":"父親身分；父職","s":"Fatherhood made my brother more patient; he used to get angry easily, but now he can calmly handle a crying baby at three in the morning.","t":"當爸爸讓我哥哥變得更有耐心；他以前很容易生氣，但現在凌晨三點也能冷靜地照顧哭鬧的嬰兒。","a":"Fatherhood"},{"w":"motto","p":"n.","d":"a short sentence that expresses what someone believes or aims for","c":"座右銘；格言","s":"My grandmother's motto was \"Never waste a single grain of rice,\" and she lived by it until the day she died.","t":"我奶奶的座右銘是「一粒米都不要浪費」，她一直奉行到離世那天。","h":1},{"w":"slogan","p":"n.","d":"a short phrase used in advertising or by a group","c":"口號；標語","s":"The company's new slogan, \"Just one more step,\" appears on every bus and billboard in the city.","t":"這家公司的新標語「再多走一步」出現在市內每輛公車和看板上。"},{"w":"saying","p":"n.","d":"a well-known short sentence that gives advice","c":"諺語；格言","s":"There is an old saying that the early bird catches the worm, which means people who start early get the best chances.","t":"有句古老的諺語說早起的鳥兒有蟲吃，意思是早開始的人能得到最好的機會。"},{"w":"proverb","p":"n.","d":"a short well-known sentence that gives advice or says something true","c":"諺語；格言","s":"My English teacher writes a different proverb on the board every Monday and asks us to explain what it means.","t":"我的英文老師每週一都在黑板上寫一句不同的諺語，並要我們解釋它的意思。"},{"w":"mound","p":"n.","d":"a pile of earth, sand, or other things shaped like a small hill","c":"土堆；小丘；一堆","s":"The children built a mound of sand on the beach and stuck a small flag on top to make it look like a castle.","t":"孩子們在海灘上堆了一個沙堆，並在頂端插上一面小旗子，讓它看起來像城堡。","h":1},{"w":"pitcher's mound","p":"n.phr.","d":"the small hill in a baseball field where the pitcher stands","c":"投手丘","s":"The pitcher stood on the pitcher's mound and took a deep breath before throwing the final ball of the championship game.","t":"投手站在投手丘上深吸一口氣，然後投出冠軍賽的最後一球。"},{"w":"pile","p":"n.","d":"a number of things lying on top of one another","c":"一堆","s":"There was a pile of dirty dishes in the sink, so I washed them all before my mother came home from work.","t":"水槽裡有一堆髒盤子，所以我在媽媽下班回家前把它們全洗了。"},{"w":"heap","p":"n.","d":"an untidy pile of things","c":"一堆（雜亂的）","s":"The old clothes lay in a heap on the floor of the closet until my mom made me fold them and put them away.","t":"舊衣服一堆躺在衣櫃地板上，直到媽媽要我把它們摺好收起來。"}]},{"unit":24,"theme":"mourn – oatmeal","cards":[{"w":"mourn","p":"v.","d":"to feel and show great sadness because someone has died","c":"哀悼；悼念","s":"The whole town came to the funeral to mourn the old doctor, who had cared for three generations of families there.","t":"全鎮的人都來參加葬禮哀悼這位老醫生，他曾照顧過當地三代家庭。","h":1},{"w":"mournful","p":"adj.","d":"very sad","c":"悲傷的；哀傷的","s":"The mournful sound of the temple bell at dusk made the empty street feel even lonelier than usual.","t":"黃昏時寺廟鐘聲哀傷的聲音，讓空蕩的街道顯得比平常更寂寞。","h":1},{"w":"mourn the loss of","p":"v.phr.","d":"to feel great sadness because someone or something is gone","c":"哀悼…的逝去","s":"Fans around the world mourned the loss of the singer, who died suddenly at the age of only thirty-two.","t":"全世界的歌迷都哀悼這位歌手的逝去，他在年僅三十二歲時突然過世。","a":"mourned the loss of"},{"w":"mourning","p":"n.","d":"the period of great sadness after someone has died","c":"哀悼；服喪","s":"The family stayed home in mourning for a week after Grandfather died, and neighbors brought them food every evening.","t":"爺爺過世後，全家在家服喪一週，鄰居每天晚上都送食物來。"},{"w":"mourner","p":"n.","d":"a person at a funeral who is sad because someone has died","c":"哀悼者；送葬者","s":"Hundreds of mourners dressed in black walked slowly behind the car that carried the coffin through the quiet streets.","t":"數百名身穿黑衣的送葬者緩緩走在載著棺木的車後面，穿過安靜的街道。","a":"mourners"},{"w":"grieve","p":"v.","d":"to feel very sad, especially because someone has died","c":"悲傷；哀悼","s":"It is natural to grieve for a long time after losing a pet, so do not let anyone tell you to just get over it.","t":"失去寵物後長時間悲傷是很自然的，所以別讓任何人叫你「看開一點就好」。"},{"w":"mow, mowed, mown/mowed","p":"v.","d":"to cut grass with a machine","c":"割（草）","s":"Every Saturday morning my father has to mow the lawn, and the smell of fresh-cut grass fills the whole street.","t":"每個星期六早上我爸爸都得割草坪，剛割過的青草味瀰漫整條街。","a":"mow","h":1},{"w":"lawn mower","p":"n.phr.","d":"a machine for cutting grass","c":"割草機","s":"Our neighbor's noisy lawn mower woke me up at seven on Sunday, so I could not sleep late as I had planned.","t":"鄰居吵鬧的割草機在星期天早上七點把我吵醒，所以我沒辦法像計畫的那樣睡晚一點。"},{"w":"lawn","p":"n.","d":"an area of short grass in a garden or park","c":"草坪","s":"The children played on the soft green lawn in front of the house while their parents drank tea on the porch.","t":"孩子們在屋前柔軟的綠色草坪上玩耍，父母則在門廊上喝茶。"},{"w":"trim","p":"v.","d":"to cut a small amount off something to make it neat","c":"修剪","s":"The gardener comes once a month to trim the bushes and cut the dead branches off the trees.","t":"園丁每個月來一次修剪灌木，並剪掉樹上的枯枝。"},{"w":"muse","p":"n.","d":"a person or thing that gives an artist ideas","c":"靈感來源；繆思","s":"The painter said that his wife was his muse; almost every picture he made in forty years showed her face.","t":"這位畫家說他的妻子是他的繆思；四十年來他畫的幾乎每一幅畫都有她的臉。","h":1},{"w":"muse","p":"v.","d":"to think about something carefully and for a long time; to say something thoughtfully","c":"沉思；若有所思地說","s":"\"I wonder what life was like a thousand years ago,\" she mused as we walked past the ruins of the old temple.","t":"「不知道一千年前的生活是什麼樣子，」當我們走過古廟遺址時，她若有所思地說。","a":"mused"},{"w":"museum","p":"n.","d":"a building where interesting objects are kept and shown to the public","c":"博物館","s":"The new science museum lets children touch everything, build their own robots, and even sleep next to the dinosaur bones.","t":"新的科學博物館讓孩子們可以觸摸所有展品、組裝自己的機器人，甚至睡在恐龍骨頭旁邊。"},{"w":"amuse","p":"v.","d":"to make someone laugh or smile","c":"逗樂；使發笑","s":"My grandfather likes to amuse the children with card tricks, and they never figure out how he does them.","t":"我爺爺喜歡用撲克牌魔術逗孩子們開心，而他們永遠猜不出他是怎麼做到的。"},{"w":"inspiration","p":"n.","d":"something that gives you new ideas","c":"靈感","s":"Many writers find inspiration in nature, so they take long walks in the mountains whenever they cannot think of anything to write.","t":"許多作家在大自然中找到靈感，所以每當寫不出東西時，他們就到山裡長途散步。"},{"w":"mustache","p":"n.","d":"hair that grows above a man's upper lip","c":"小鬍子；八字鬍","s":"My uncle grew a thick black mustache over the summer, and now my little cousin does not recognize him in old photos.","t":"我叔叔在夏天留了濃密的黑鬍子，現在我的小表弟認不出舊照片裡的他了。","h":1},{"w":"beard","p":"n.","d":"hair that grows on a man's chin and cheeks","c":"鬍鬚（下巴的）","s":"The old fisherman's white beard reached down to his chest, and he said he had not shaved since his wedding day.","t":"老漁夫的白鬍子垂到胸前，他說自從結婚那天起就沒刮過鬍子。"},{"w":"shave","p":"v.","d":"to cut hair off the face or body with a razor","c":"刮（鬍子）","s":"My father has to shave every morning before work, or his boss will say that he looks untidy.","t":"我爸爸每天早上上班前都得刮鬍子，否則老闆會說他看起來不整潔。"},{"w":"whiskers","p":"n.","d":"the long stiff hairs that grow near the mouth of a cat or other animal","c":"（貓等的）鬚","s":"A cat uses its long whiskers to feel whether a space is wide enough for its body to pass through.","t":"貓用牠長長的鬍鬚來感覺一個空間是否寬到足以讓身體通過。"},{"w":"mute","p":"adj.","d":"not speaking; silent","c":"沉默的；啞的","s":"The boy stood mute in front of the class, too nervous to say a single word of the speech he had practiced.","t":"男孩一言不發地站在全班面前，緊張到連練習過的演講一個字也說不出來。","h":1},{"w":"mute","p":"v.","d":"to turn off the sound of a device","c":"將…靜音","s":"Please mute your microphone during the online class unless the teacher asks you a question.","t":"線上課程期間請把麥克風靜音，除非老師問你問題。"},{"w":"on mute","p":"phr.","d":"with the sound turned off","c":"靜音狀態","s":"You have been talking for a minute, but we cannot hear you because your phone is still on mute.","t":"你已經講了一分鐘了，但我們聽不到你，因為你的手機還在靜音。"},{"w":"muted","p":"adj.","d":"(of colors or sounds) soft and not bright or loud","c":"柔和的；低沉的","s":"The designer chose muted colors like soft gray and light brown for the bedroom, which made the room feel calm.","t":"設計師為臥室選了淺灰和淺棕這類柔和的顏色，讓房間感覺很平靜。"},{"w":"silent","p":"adj.","d":"making no sound; not speaking","c":"寂靜的；沉默的","s":"The library was completely silent except for the sound of pages turning and the clock ticking on the wall.","t":"圖書館裡完全寂靜，只有翻頁聲和牆上時鐘的滴答聲。"},{"w":"nag","p":"v.","d":"to keep complaining to someone or asking them to do something","c":"嘮叨；不斷催促","s":"My mother will nag me about cleaning my room until I finally do it, and she asks about it at least five times a day.","t":"我媽媽會一直嘮叨要我打掃房間直到我真的去做，她一天至少問五次。","h":1},{"w":"nag at","p":"v.phr.","d":"to keep criticizing or complaining to someone","c":"對…嘮叨不停","s":"Don't nag at your brother about his grades; he already feels bad enough, and shouting will not help him study.","t":"別為了成績對你弟弟嘮叨個不停；他已經夠難過了，大吼大叫也不會幫助他讀書。"},{"w":"nag","p":"n.","d":"a person who keeps complaining or asking for things","c":"愛嘮叨的人","s":"My roommate is such a nag about the dishes that I now wash my cup the second I finish my coffee.","t":"我室友對洗碗這件事嘮叨得要命，所以現在我一喝完咖啡就馬上洗杯子。"},{"w":"nagging","p":"adj.","d":"(of a feeling or pain) that does not go away","c":"揮之不去的；持續的","s":"I had a nagging feeling that I had forgotten something, and halfway to school I realized my homework was still on the kitchen table.","t":"我有一種揮之不去的感覺，好像忘了什麼，走到半路才想起功課還放在廚房桌上。"},{"w":"narrate","p":"v.","d":"to tell a story; to describe what is happening in a film","c":"敘述；旁白","s":"The famous actor was asked to narrate the documentary about whales, and his deep voice fit the ocean scenes perfectly.","t":"這位知名演員受邀為鯨魚紀錄片旁白，他低沉的聲音和海洋畫面十分契合。","h":1},{"w":"narrator","p":"n.","d":"the person who tells a story in a book or film","c":"敘述者；旁白者","s":"In the novel, the narrator is a ten-year-old girl, so we see the war through the eyes of a child.","t":"在這本小說中，敘述者是個十歲的女孩，所以我們透過孩子的眼睛看這場戰爭。","h":1},{"w":"narrative","p":"n.","d":"a story, or the way a story is told","c":"敘事；故事","s":"The movie's narrative jumps back and forth between 1950 and today, which can be confusing the first time you watch it.","t":"這部電影的敘事在一九五〇年和現今之間來回跳躍，第一次看可能會讓人困惑。"},{"w":"narration","p":"n.","d":"the act of telling a story; the spoken words in a film that explain what is happening","c":"敘述；旁白","s":"The museum's audio guide provides clear narration in six languages, so visitors from abroad can understand every painting.","t":"博物館的語音導覽提供六種語言的清楚解說，讓外國遊客能看懂每一幅畫。"},{"w":"nationalism","p":"n.","d":"the belief that your own country is better than others; a strong love of your country","c":"民族主義；國家主義","s":"In the 1930s, extreme nationalism in several European countries led to hatred of foreigners and finally to a terrible war.","t":"一九三〇年代，歐洲幾個國家極端的民族主義導致對外國人的仇恨，最終引發一場可怕的戰爭。","h":1},{"w":"nation","p":"n.","d":"a country with its own people and government","c":"國家；民族","s":"The whole nation stopped to watch the baseball final on television, and the streets were empty for three hours.","t":"全國的人都停下來看電視轉播的棒球決賽，街上空了三個小時。"},{"w":"national","p":"adj.","d":"connected with a whole country","c":"國家的；全國的","s":"Before the game began, both teams stood quietly while the national anthem of each country was played.","t":"比賽開始前，兩隊都安靜地站著，等兩國的國歌播放完畢。"},{"w":"nationality","p":"n.","d":"the legal fact of belonging to a particular country","c":"國籍","s":"The form asks for your name, date of birth, and nationality, and you must sign at the bottom.","t":"表格要填你的姓名、出生日期和國籍，而且你必須在底部簽名。"},{"w":"nationalist","p":"n.","d":"a person who believes their country is better than others or should be independent","c":"民族主義者","s":"The speaker was a strong nationalist who believed that his country should make all its own products and buy nothing from abroad.","t":"這位演講者是個強烈的民族主義者，他認為自己的國家應該自製所有產品，不向國外購買任何東西。"},{"w":"international","p":"adj.","d":"involving two or more countries","c":"國際的","s":"Our school holds an international food fair every spring, where students cook dishes from their parents' home countries.","t":"我們學校每年春天舉辦國際美食園遊會，學生們烹煮來自父母家鄉的菜餚。"},{"w":"navigate","p":"v.","d":"to find the way to a place, especially by ship or plane","c":"導航；航行","s":"Before GPS, sailors had to navigate by the stars, and a cloudy night could leave a ship lost at sea.","t":"在有GPS之前，水手必須靠星星導航，一個多雲的夜晚就可能讓船在海上迷失方向。","h":1},{"w":"navigation","p":"n.","d":"the skill or process of finding the way from one place to another","c":"導航；航行","s":"The ship's navigation system failed in the storm, so the captain had to use an old paper map to find the harbor.","t":"船的導航系統在暴風雨中故障了，所以船長必須用一張舊的紙本地圖找到港口。","h":1},{"w":"navigator","p":"n.","d":"a person who plans the route of a ship, plane, or car","c":"領航員","s":"On our road trip, my sister was the navigator; she held the map and told Dad where to turn at every corner.","t":"公路旅行時，我姊姊是領航員；她拿著地圖，在每個路口告訴爸爸該往哪轉。"},{"w":"navy","p":"n.","d":"the part of a country's armed forces that fights at sea","c":"海軍","s":"My cousin joined the navy after high school and spent two years on a ship that sailed around the Pacific.","t":"我表哥高中畢業後加入海軍，在一艘環繞太平洋航行的船上待了兩年。"},{"w":"naval","p":"adj.","d":"connected with the navy","c":"海軍的","s":"The old naval base near the harbor has been turned into a museum where visitors can walk through a real submarine.","t":"港口附近的舊海軍基地已改建為博物館，遊客可以走進一艘真正的潛艇參觀。"},{"w":"nearsighted","p":"adj.","d":"able to see things clearly only when they are close","c":"近視的","s":"Because I am nearsighted, I cannot read the words on the board unless I sit in the first row or wear my glasses.","t":"因為我近視，除非坐在第一排或戴眼鏡，否則我看不清黑板上的字。","h":1},{"w":"farsighted","p":"adj.","d":"able to see things clearly only when they are far away","c":"遠視的","s":"My grandmother is farsighted, so she can see the mountains clearly but needs glasses to read the newspaper.","t":"我奶奶遠視，所以她能清楚看到山，卻需要眼鏡才能看報紙。"},{"w":"eyesight","p":"n.","d":"the ability to see","c":"視力","s":"Playing on your phone in the dark for hours every night is bad for your eyesight, so turn on a lamp at least.","t":"每天晚上在黑暗中玩好幾個小時的手機對你的視力不好，所以至少開盞燈吧。"},{"w":"sight","p":"n.","d":"the ability to see; something that you see","c":"視力；景象","s":"The doctor said my grandfather might lose his sight in one eye if he did not have the operation soon.","t":"醫生說如果我爺爺不盡快動手術，可能會失去一隻眼睛的視力。"},{"w":"short-sighted","p":"adj.","d":"not thinking about what will happen in the future","c":"短視的；目光短淺的","s":"Cutting the school's sports budget to save money is short-sighted; healthy students learn better and cost less in the long run.","t":"為了省錢而刪減學校的體育預算是短視的；健康的學生學得更好，長期來看花費也更少。"},{"w":"nickel","p":"n.","d":"a US coin worth five cents","c":"五分鎳幣","s":"In the United States, a nickel is worth five cents, and it is slightly bigger than the one-cent coin.","t":"在美國，一枚五分鎳幣值五美分，比一美分硬幣稍微大一點。","h":1},{"w":"nickel","p":"n.","d":"a hard silver-white metal","c":"鎳","s":"The coin looks like silver, but it is actually made of nickel and copper, which are much cheaper metals.","t":"這枚硬幣看起來像銀，但其實是由鎳和銅製成的，這兩種金屬便宜得多。"},{"w":"coin","p":"n.","d":"a small flat piece of metal used as money","c":"硬幣","s":"I found an old coin from 1920 in my grandfather's drawer, and the shop said it might be worth a lot of money.","t":"我在爺爺的抽屜裡發現一枚一九二〇年的舊硬幣，店家說它可能值很多錢。"},{"w":"dime","p":"n.","d":"a US coin worth ten cents","c":"一角硬幣","s":"A dime is worth ten cents, yet it is smaller than a nickel, which confuses many visitors to the United States.","t":"一枚一角硬幣值十美分，卻比五分鎳幣還小，這讓許多到美國的遊客感到困惑。"},{"w":"penny","p":"n.","d":"a coin worth one cent","c":"一分硬幣","s":"My grandmother keeps every penny she finds on the street in a big glass jar, and once a year she gives the money to charity.","t":"我奶奶把在街上撿到的每一枚一分硬幣都放進一個大玻璃罐，每年把錢捐給慈善機構一次。"},{"w":"nostril","p":"n.","d":"one of the two openings at the end of the nose","c":"鼻孔","s":"The horse breathed hard after the race, and steam came out of each nostril in the cold morning air.","t":"賽後馬喘得很厲害，在寒冷的晨風中，每個鼻孔都冒出白煙。","h":1},{"w":"nosy","p":"adj.","d":"too interested in other people's private lives","c":"愛管閒事的；好打聽的","s":"Our nosy neighbor asks about everything: where we go, what we buy, and why the lights were on so late last night.","t":"我們愛打聽的鄰居什麼都問：我們去哪裡、買了什麼、昨晚燈為什麼那麼晚還亮著。"},{"w":"sniff","p":"v.","d":"to breathe in through the nose in order to smell something","c":"嗅；聞","s":"The dog stopped to sniff every tree and lamp post on the walk, so it took us an hour to go around the block.","t":"散步時狗停下來嗅每一棵樹和路燈柱，所以我們花了一個小時才繞完街區。"},{"w":"runny nose","p":"n.phr.","d":"a nose that keeps producing liquid, as when you have a cold","c":"流鼻水","s":"I have a runny nose and a sore throat today, so the teacher told me to wear a mask and go home early.","t":"我今天流鼻水又喉嚨痛，所以老師叫我戴口罩早點回家。"},{"w":"notable","p":"adj.","d":"important or interesting enough to be noticed","c":"顯著的；值得注意的","s":"One notable change in the new school rules is that students may now use phones during lunch break.","t":"新校規中一項顯著的改變是學生現在午休時可以使用手機。","h":1},{"w":"notable","p":"n.","d":"an important or famous person","c":"名人；顯要人物","s":"The dinner was attended by local notables, including the mayor, two judges, and the owner of the biggest factory in town.","t":"出席這場晚宴的有當地的名流，包括市長、兩位法官和鎮上最大工廠的老闆。","a":"notables"},{"w":"notably","p":"adv.","d":"especially; in a way that is easy to notice","c":"尤其；顯著地","s":"Several countries, most notably Japan and Korea, have invested heavily in high-speed trains over the past thirty years.","t":"好幾個國家，尤其是日本和韓國，在過去三十年裡大量投資高速鐵路。"},{"w":"note","p":"v.","d":"to notice or pay attention to something","c":"注意；留意","s":"Please note that the museum closes at five on weekdays, so plan to arrive before three if you want to see everything.","t":"請注意博物館平日五點關門，所以如果想看完所有展品，請計畫在三點前到達。"},{"w":"noteworthy","p":"adj.","d":"interesting or important enough to be noticed","c":"值得注意的","s":"It is noteworthy that the youngest player on the team scored the most points in the whole tournament.","t":"值得注意的是，隊上最年輕的球員在整個錦標賽中得分最多。"},{"w":"notorious","p":"adj.","d":"well known for something bad","c":"惡名昭彰的；聲名狼藉的","s":"The old bridge is notorious for traffic jams, so most drivers leave home thirty minutes early during the morning rush.","t":"這座老橋以塞車惡名昭彰，所以大多數駕駛在早上尖峰時段都提早三十分鐘出門。","h":1},{"w":"notoriously","p":"adv.","d":"in a way that is well known for being bad","c":"惡名昭彰地；出了名地","s":"The math teacher is notoriously strict about homework; if you hand it in one minute late, she will not accept it.","t":"這位數學老師對功課出了名地嚴格；如果你晚一分鐘交，她就不收。"},{"w":"infamous","p":"adj.","d":"famous for being bad","c":"聲名狼藉的；臭名遠播的","s":"The pirate was infamous for attacking ships along the coast, and parents used his name to frighten their children.","t":"這名海盜因襲擊沿岸船隻而惡名遠播，父母們用他的名字來嚇唬孩子。"},{"w":"famous","p":"adj.","d":"known by many people","c":"著名的","s":"Tainan is famous for its street food, and people travel from all over the island just to eat there.","t":"台南以街頭小吃聞名，全島各地的人專程前往只為了吃一頓。"},{"w":"fame","p":"n.","d":"the state of being known by many people","c":"名聲；名氣","s":"The young singer's fame grew so quickly that she could not walk through a night market without being stopped for photos.","t":"這位年輕歌手的名氣漲得太快，走過夜市時總會被攔下來合照。"},{"w":"nourish","p":"v.","d":"to give a person, animal, or plant the food they need to live and grow","c":"滋養；養育","s":"A bowl of warm rice soup can nourish a sick child who is too weak to eat anything heavier.","t":"一碗溫熱的米粥可以滋養虛弱到吃不下其他食物的生病孩子。","h":1},{"w":"nourishment","p":"n.","d":"food that is needed to live and grow","c":"營養；養分","s":"Babies get all the nourishment they need from milk during the first six months of their lives.","t":"嬰兒在出生後的前六個月，從奶水中獲得所需的全部營養。"},{"w":"nourishing","p":"adj.","d":"(of food) healthy and good for you","c":"有營養的；滋補的","s":"My grandmother cooks a nourishing chicken soup with ginger and dates whenever anyone in the family catches a cold.","t":"每當家裡有人感冒，我奶奶就會煮一鍋加了薑和紅棗的滋補雞湯。"},{"w":"nutrition","p":"n.","d":"the process of eating the right kind of food to be healthy","c":"營養","s":"Good nutrition is especially important for teenagers because their bodies and brains are still growing fast.","t":"良好的營養對青少年特別重要，因為他們的身體和大腦仍在快速成長。"},{"w":"nutritious","p":"adj.","d":"(of food) full of the things your body needs to be healthy","c":"營養豐富的","s":"A nutritious breakfast with eggs, fruit, and whole-grain bread will keep you full and focused until lunchtime.","t":"一頓有蛋、水果和全麥麵包的營養早餐，能讓你飽足且專注到午餐時間。"},{"w":"undernourished","p":"adj.","d":"not healthy because of not having enough good food","c":"營養不良的","s":"Many children in the poorest villages are undernourished, so the charity sends milk and eggs to the schools every week.","t":"最貧窮村莊裡的許多孩子營養不良，所以慈善機構每週都送牛奶和雞蛋到學校。"},{"w":"novice","p":"n.","d":"a person who is new to a job or activity","c":"新手；初學者","s":"As a novice at skiing, I spent most of the first day falling down, while my little sister raced past me.","t":"身為滑雪新手，第一天我大部分時間都在跌倒，而我妹妹則從我身旁飛馳而過。","h":1},{"w":"beginner","p":"n.","d":"a person who has just started to learn something","c":"初學者","s":"This yoga class is for beginners, so the teacher explains every pose slowly and nobody feels embarrassed.","t":"這堂瑜珈課是給初學者上的，所以老師慢慢解釋每個動作，沒有人會覺得不好意思。","a":"beginners"},{"w":"novel","p":"adj.","d":"new and different from anything before","c":"新穎的；新奇的","s":"The restaurant has a novel idea: customers pick their own vegetables from the garden before the chef cooks them.","t":"這家餐廳有個新穎的點子：顧客先到菜園自己摘蔬菜，再由主廚烹調。"},{"w":"novelty","p":"n.","d":"the quality of being new and unusual; a new and unusual thing","c":"新奇；新奇的事物","s":"At first the robot waiter was a novelty that drew big crowds, but after a few months nobody paid attention to it.","t":"起初機器人服務生是個吸引大批人潮的新奇事物，但幾個月後就沒有人注意它了。"},{"w":"amateur","p":"n.","d":"a person who does something for pleasure, not as a job","c":"業餘者；業餘愛好者","s":"The photo contest is open to amateurs only, so professional photographers who earn money from their pictures cannot enter.","t":"這場攝影比賽只開放給業餘愛好者，所以靠照片賺錢的專業攝影師不能參加。","a":"amateurs"},{"w":"nucleus","p":"n.","d":"the central part of an atom or cell","c":"原子核；細胞核","s":"The nucleus of an atom is tiny, but it contains almost all of the atom's weight.","t":"原子的原子核非常小，但它幾乎包含了原子的全部重量。","h":1},{"w":"nucleus","p":"n.","d":"the central and most important part of a group","c":"核心","s":"These three experienced players form the nucleus of the team, and the coach builds every game plan around them.","t":"這三位經驗豐富的球員構成球隊的核心，教練的每個比賽計畫都圍繞著他們。"},{"w":"nuclear","p":"adj.","d":"connected with the nucleus of an atom; using nuclear energy","c":"核子的；核能的","s":"After the accident in Japan, many countries began to ask whether nuclear power was really safe enough to keep using.","t":"日本的事故之後，許多國家開始質疑核能是否真的安全到可以繼續使用。"},{"w":"nuclear power plant","p":"n.phr.","d":"a place where electricity is produced using nuclear energy","c":"核能發電廠","s":"The old nuclear power plant on the coast will be closed next year, and the government plans to replace it with wind farms.","t":"海岸邊的舊核能發電廠明年將關閉，政府計畫用風力發電廠來取代它。"},{"w":"core","p":"n.","d":"the central or most important part of something","c":"核心；中心","s":"The core of the problem is that students are expected to memorize too much and understand too little.","t":"問題的核心在於學生被要求背太多，而理解得太少。"},{"w":"nude","p":"adj.","d":"not wearing any clothes","c":"裸體的","s":"The art museum has several famous paintings of nude figures from ancient Greek stories, which some visitors find surprising.","t":"這座美術館有幾幅著名的古希臘故事裸體人物畫，有些參觀者覺得很驚訝。","h":1},{"w":"nude","p":"n.","d":"a painting or statue of a person without clothes","c":"裸體畫；裸體像","s":"The sculptor's most famous work is a marble nude of a young man, which stands in the main hall of the gallery.","t":"這位雕塑家最有名的作品是一座年輕男子的大理石裸體像，立在畫廊的主廳裡。"},{"w":"naked","p":"adj.","d":"not wearing any clothes","c":"赤裸的","s":"The little boy ran naked out of the bathroom and across the living room, laughing while his mother chased him with a towel.","t":"小男孩光著身子從浴室跑出來穿過客廳，媽媽拿著毛巾追著他，他笑個不停。"},{"w":"bare","p":"adj.","d":"not covered by clothes; empty","c":"赤裸的；光禿的","s":"The children walked on the hot sand with bare feet and then ran screaming into the cool sea.","t":"孩子們光著腳走在滾燙的沙上，然後尖叫著跑進涼爽的海裡。"},{"w":"nurture","p":"v.","d":"to care for and help something grow or develop","c":"培育；養育；栽培","s":"Good teachers nurture their students' interests, giving them time and tools to explore whatever they are curious about.","t":"好老師會培養學生的興趣，給他們時間和工具去探索任何感到好奇的事物。","h":1},{"w":"nurture","p":"n.","d":"the care and support given to someone while they grow","c":"養育；後天培養","s":"Scientists still argue about nature versus nurture: are we shaped more by our genes or by the way we are raised?","t":"科學家仍在爭論先天與後天：我們更多是由基因還是由成長方式所塑造的？"},{"w":"nurse","p":"v.","d":"to take care of a person or animal that is sick","c":"照顧；看護","s":"She stayed up all night to nurse her sick cat, giving it water with a spoon every hour.","t":"她整夜沒睡照顧生病的貓，每小時用湯匙餵牠喝水。"},{"w":"nursery","p":"n.","d":"a place where young plants are grown and sold; a place where small children are cared for","c":"苗圃；托兒所","s":"We bought the young orange tree at a nursery outside town, where they grow thousands of plants in long glass houses.","t":"我們在鎮外的一家苗圃買了這棵小橘子樹，那裡在長長的玻璃溫室裡種了數千株植物。"},{"w":"foster","p":"v.","d":"to help something grow or develop","c":"促進；培養","s":"The exchange program aims to foster friendship between students in Taiwan and Japan through home stays and sports.","t":"這個交換計畫旨在透過寄宿家庭和運動促進台灣和日本學生之間的友誼。"},{"w":"oasis","p":"n.","d":"a place in a desert where there is water and plants can grow","c":"綠洲","s":"After three days of crossing the desert, the travelers finally saw an oasis with palm trees and a small pool of clear water.","t":"穿越沙漠三天後，旅人們終於看到一片有棕櫚樹和一小池清水的綠洲。","h":1},{"w":"oasis","p":"n.","d":"a pleasant place that is different from everything around it","c":"樂土；安樂窩","s":"The small park is an oasis of calm in the middle of the noisy city, where office workers eat lunch under the trees.","t":"這座小公園是喧鬧城市中的一片寧靜綠洲，上班族在樹下吃午餐。"},{"w":"desert","p":"n.","d":"a large area of dry land with very few plants","c":"沙漠","s":"Almost no rain falls in the Sahara desert, and daytime temperatures can reach fifty degrees Celsius.","t":"撒哈拉沙漠幾乎不下雨，白天氣溫可達攝氏五十度。"},{"w":"palm tree","p":"n.phr.","d":"a tall tree with large leaves at the top that grows in hot countries","c":"棕櫚樹","s":"Tall palm trees line the beach in Kenting, and their wide leaves offer the only shade on a hot afternoon.","t":"高大的棕櫚樹沿著墾丁的海灘排列，寬大的葉子是炎熱午後唯一的遮蔭。","a":"palm trees"},{"w":"oath","p":"n.","d":"a formal promise to do something or to tell the truth","c":"誓言；誓約","s":"The new president placed her hand on the book and took an oath to serve the country faithfully.","t":"新總統把手放在書上，立下誓言要忠實地為國家服務。","h":1},{"w":"take an oath","p":"v.phr.","d":"to make a formal promise","c":"宣誓","s":"Before giving evidence in court, every witness must take an oath to tell the truth and nothing but the truth.","t":"在法庭上作證之前，每位證人都必須宣誓只說實話。"},{"w":"under oath","p":"phr.","d":"having made a formal promise to tell the truth in court","c":"宣誓之下","s":"The witness was under oath, so lying to the judge about where he was that night would have been a serious crime.","t":"證人是在宣誓之下作證，所以對法官謊報他那晚的行蹤會是重罪。"},{"w":"swear, swore, sworn","p":"v.","d":"to promise strongly that something is true","c":"發誓","s":"I swear I did not touch your phone; it was on the table when I left the room this morning.","t":"我發誓我沒碰你的手機；今天早上我離開房間時它還在桌上。","a":"swear"},{"w":"vow","p":"n.","d":"a serious promise","c":"誓言；誓約","s":"On their wedding day, the couple made a vow to stay together in good times and in bad, in sickness and in health.","t":"在婚禮當天，這對新人立下誓言，無論順境逆境、健康疾病都要在一起。"},{"w":"promise","p":"n.","d":"a statement that you will definitely do something","c":"承諾；諾言","s":"My father made a promise to take us camping this summer, and he always keeps his word.","t":"我爸爸承諾今年夏天帶我們去露營，而他總是說話算話。"},{"w":"oatmeal","p":"n.","d":"a soft hot food made from oats and milk or water, eaten for breakfast","c":"燕麥粥；燕麥片","s":"A warm bowl of oatmeal with banana and honey is my favorite breakfast on cold winter mornings.","t":"在寒冷的冬天早晨，一碗加了香蕉和蜂蜜的溫熱燕麥粥是我最愛的早餐。","h":1},{"w":"oats","p":"n.","d":"a grain used as food for people and animals","c":"燕麥","s":"Farmers in Scotland have grown oats for hundreds of years because the plant can survive the cold, wet weather there.","t":"蘇格蘭的農民種植燕麥已有數百年歷史，因為這種植物能在當地寒冷潮濕的天氣中存活。"},{"w":"cereal","p":"n.","d":"a breakfast food made from grain, usually eaten with milk","c":"穀片；麥片","s":"Most children in Taiwan eat rice or bread for breakfast, but my brother prefers a bowl of cereal with cold milk.","t":"台灣大多數孩子早餐吃飯或麵包，但我弟弟比較喜歡一碗配冰牛奶的穀片。"},{"w":"porridge","p":"n.","d":"a soft hot food made by boiling oats or rice in water or milk","c":"粥；麥片粥","s":"In Scotland, porridge is traditionally made with oats, water, and a little salt, and eaten hot every morning.","t":"在蘇格蘭，傳統的麥片粥是用燕麥、水和一點鹽煮成的，每天早上趁熱吃。"},{"w":"grain","p":"n.","d":"the seeds of plants such as rice, wheat, and oats, used as food","c":"穀物","s":"Rice, wheat, and corn are the three most important grain crops in the world, feeding billions of people every day.","t":"稻米、小麥和玉米是世界上最重要的三種穀物作物，每天養活數十億人。"}]},{"unit":25,"theme":"oblige – outlaw","cards":[{"w":"oblige","p":"v.","d":"to make someone do something because it is a duty or the law","c":"使不得不；迫使","s":"The new rule will oblige every student to wear a helmet when riding a scooter to school, even for a very short trip.","t":"新規定將迫使每位學生騎機車上學時都要戴安全帽，即使是很短的路程也一樣。","h":1},{"w":"be obliged to","p":"v.phr.","d":"to have to do something","c":"不得不；有義務","s":"Because the last bus had already left, we were obliged to take a taxi home, which cost us almost five hundred dollars.","t":"因為最後一班公車已經開走，我們不得不搭計程車回家，花了我們將近五百元。","a":"were obliged to"},{"w":"obliged","p":"adj.","d":"grateful; thankful","c":"感激的","s":"I would be much obliged if you could send me the meeting notes before Friday, since I was absent that day.","t":"如果你能在星期五前把會議紀錄寄給我，我會非常感激，因為那天我沒出席。"},{"w":"obligation","p":"n.","d":"something you must do because of duty or law","c":"義務；責任","s":"Parents have an obligation to send their children to school, and the government checks that every child attends classes.","t":"父母有送孩子上學的義務，政府會檢查每個孩子是否都有去上課。"},{"w":"obligatory","p":"adj.","d":"that must be done; required","c":"必須的；強制性的","s":"Attendance at the morning meeting is obligatory for all new workers, so please arrive at the office before eight thirty.","t":"所有新員工都必須出席早會，所以請在八點半前到辦公室。"},{"w":"obsess","p":"v.","d":"to fill someone's mind so that they cannot think of anything else","c":"使著迷；使心神不寧","s":"Thoughts about the final exam began to obsess him, and he could not sleep well for a whole week before the test.","t":"關於期末考的念頭開始纏住他，考前整整一週他都睡不好。","h":1},{"w":"be obsessed with","p":"v.phr.","d":"to think about something all the time","c":"對…著迷；沉迷於","s":"My little brother is obsessed with dinosaurs, so he can tell you the name of every single one in the museum.","t":"我弟弟對恐龍著迷，所以他能告訴你博物館裡每一隻恐龍的名字。","a":"is obsessed with"},{"w":"obsession","p":"n.","d":"something you cannot stop thinking about","c":"著迷；執念","s":"Collecting old coins started as a hobby for my uncle, but over the years it has become an obsession that takes all his free time.","t":"收集舊硬幣對我叔叔來說一開始只是嗜好，但多年來已變成佔據他所有空閒時間的執念。"},{"w":"obsessive","p":"adj.","d":"thinking about something too much","c":"過分著迷的；強迫性的","s":"She is obsessive about cleaning, and she wipes the kitchen table at least ten times a day even when it looks perfectly clean.","t":"她對打掃過分執著，即使廚房桌子看起來很乾淨，她一天也至少擦十次。"},{"w":"obstinate","p":"adj.","d":"refusing to change your mind or your plan","c":"頑固的；固執的","s":"My grandfather is so obstinate that he refuses to see a doctor even when his back has hurt for two whole weeks.","t":"我爺爺非常固執，即使背已經痛了整整兩個星期，他還是拒絕看醫生。","h":1},{"w":"obstinately","p":"adv.","d":"in a way that refuses to change","c":"頑固地","s":"Although everyone told him the shortcut was flooded, he obstinately drove down that road and got stuck in the water.","t":"雖然大家都告訴他那條捷徑淹水了，他還是固執地開進那條路，結果車子卡在水裡。"},{"w":"obstinacy","p":"n.","d":"the quality of refusing to change your mind","c":"頑固；固執","s":"Her obstinacy cost the team the game, because she would not pass the ball even when three players were open.","t":"她的固執讓球隊輸了比賽，因為即使有三名隊友無人防守，她也不肯傳球。"},{"w":"stubborn","p":"adj.","d":"not willing to change your mind; hard to deal with","c":"固執的；頑固的","s":"The stubborn child sat on the floor of the toy store and refused to leave until his mother bought him the robot.","t":"那個固執的孩子坐在玩具店地板上，直到媽媽買機器人給他才肯離開。"},{"w":"occurrence","p":"n.","d":"something that happens; how often something happens","c":"發生；事件","s":"Heavy rain in the afternoon is a common occurrence in Taipei during summer, so most people carry an umbrella every day.","t":"台北夏天午後下大雨是常見的現象，所以大多數人每天都帶著傘。","h":1},{"w":"occur","p":"v.","d":"to happen","c":"發生","s":"Most traffic accidents occur when drivers are tired or looking at their phones, according to the police report.","t":"根據警方的報告，大多數交通事故發生在駕駛疲勞或看手機的時候。"},{"w":"occur to sb","p":"v.phr.","d":"to come into someone's mind suddenly","c":"突然想到","s":"It did not occur to me that the shop might be closed on Monday, so we drove all the way there for nothing.","t":"我沒想到那家店星期一可能休息，所以我們白白開車跑了一趟。","a":"occur to me"},{"w":"recur","p":"v.","d":"to happen again, especially many times","c":"再發生；復發","s":"If the same problem continues to recur after you restart the computer, you should take it to the repair shop.","t":"如果重新開機後同樣的問題仍不斷再發生，你應該把電腦拿去維修店。"},{"w":"recurring","p":"adj.","d":"happening again and again","c":"一再發生的","s":"Being late for the first class is a recurring problem for him, so the teacher finally called his parents last week.","t":"第一堂課遲到是他一再發生的問題，所以老師上週終於打電話給他父母。"},{"w":"octopus","p":"n.","d":"a sea animal with a soft body and eight arms","c":"章魚","s":"An octopus can change the color of its skin in less than a second to hide from fish that want to eat it.","t":"章魚能在不到一秒內改變皮膚的顏色，以躲避想吃它的魚。","h":1},{"w":"grilled octopus","p":"n.phr.","d":"octopus cooked over fire","c":"烤章魚","s":"The small restaurant near the harbor is famous for its grilled octopus, which the cook prepares fresh every single morning.","t":"港口附近那家小餐廳以烤章魚聞名，廚師每天早上都用新鮮的章魚來做。"},{"w":"tentacle","p":"n.","d":"one of the long thin arms of an octopus or squid","c":"觸手；觸腕","s":"Each tentacle of the octopus is covered with small round suckers that help it hold on to rocks and catch food.","t":"章魚的每隻觸腕都布滿小小的圓形吸盤，幫助它抓住岩石和捕食。"},{"w":"squid","p":"n.","d":"a sea animal like an octopus with ten arms","c":"魷魚","s":"Fried squid is one of the most popular snacks at Taiwanese night markets, and it is usually served with pepper and salt.","t":"炸魷魚是台灣夜市最受歡迎的小吃之一，通常會撒上胡椒鹽。"},{"w":"odor","p":"n.","d":"a smell, often an unpleasant one","c":"氣味；臭味","s":"A strange odor came from the back of the refrigerator, and we finally found a piece of fish that had gone bad.","t":"冰箱後面傳來一股奇怪的氣味，我們最後找到一塊壞掉的魚。","h":1},{"w":"body odor","p":"n.phr.","d":"the unpleasant smell of a person's body","c":"體味；體臭","s":"After playing basketball for two hours in the heat, the boys had strong body odor, so the coach sent them straight to the showers.","t":"在高溫下打了兩小時籃球後，男孩們有濃重的體味，所以教練直接叫他們去沖澡。"},{"w":"odorless","p":"adj.","d":"having no smell","c":"無味的","s":"Natural gas is odorless, so gas companies add a special smell to it so that people can notice a leak quickly.","t":"天然氣是無味的，所以瓦斯公司會加入特殊氣味，讓人們能迅速察覺漏氣。"},{"w":"deodorant","p":"n.","d":"something you put on your body to stop bad smells","c":"除臭劑；體香劑","s":"Most teenagers start using deodorant in junior high school, especially after PE class on hot summer days.","t":"大多數青少年在國中開始使用體香劑，尤其是在炎熱夏日的體育課後。"},{"w":"offshore","p":"adj.","d":"in the sea, not far from the land","c":"離岸的；近海的","s":"The government plans to build several offshore wind farms along the west coast to produce clean electricity for millions of homes.","t":"政府計畫在西海岸興建幾座離岸風電場，為數百萬戶家庭提供清潔的電力。","h":1},{"w":"offshore","p":"adv.","d":"away from the land, in the sea","c":"在海上；向海面","s":"The fishing boats go far offshore every night and come back to the harbor with their catch before the sun rises.","t":"漁船每晚駛到離岸很遠的地方，在日出前帶著漁獲回到港口。"},{"w":"shore","p":"n.","d":"the land along the edge of the sea or a lake","c":"岸；海岸","s":"We walked along the shore for an hour, picking up shells and watching the waves roll in one after another.","t":"我們沿著海岸走了一小時，撿貝殼並看著海浪一波波滾滾而來。"},{"w":"onshore","p":"adj.","d":"on the land, or coming toward the land from the sea","c":"陸上的；向岸的","s":"Strong onshore winds pushed the small boat back toward the beach before the two boys could reach the island.","t":"強勁的向岸風把小船推回海灘，兩個男孩還沒能抵達那座島。"},{"w":"offspring","p":"n.","d":"the children or young of a person or animal","c":"子孫；後代；幼獸","s":"A female sea turtle lays over a hundred eggs, but only a few of her offspring will live long enough to become adults.","t":"一隻母海龜會下一百多顆蛋，但她的後代只有少數能活到成年。","h":1},{"w":"spring from","p":"v.phr.","d":"to come from; to be caused by","c":"源自；起因於","s":"Many of his health problems spring from his habit of eating fast food late at night and sleeping only five hours.","t":"他的許多健康問題源自他深夜吃速食、只睡五小時的習慣。"},{"w":"descendant","p":"n.","d":"a person related to someone who lived long ago","c":"後裔；子孫","s":"Many people living in Tainan today are descendants of farmers who came to Taiwan from Fujian more than three hundred years ago.","t":"今日住在台南的許多人是三百多年前從福建來到台灣的農民的後裔。","a":"descendants"},{"w":"ancestor","p":"n.","d":"a person in your family who lived long before you","c":"祖先","s":"Every year during Tomb Sweeping Day, our family visits the graves of our ancestors and cleans the stones together.","t":"每年清明節，我們全家會去掃祖先的墓，一起清理墓碑。","a":"ancestors"},{"w":"operative","p":"adj.","d":"working and able to be used; in effect","c":"運作中的；有效的","s":"The new ticket machines at the MRT station will not be fully operative until next month, so please buy tickets at the counter.","t":"捷運站的新售票機要到下個月才會完全投入運作，所以請在櫃檯購票。","h":1},{"w":"operate","p":"v.","d":"to work; to make a machine work; to do surgery","c":"運作；操作；動手術","s":"Only trained staff are allowed to operate this heavy machine, because one small mistake could cause a serious injury.","t":"只有受過訓練的員工才被允許操作這台重機具，因為一個小錯誤就可能造成嚴重傷害。"},{"w":"operation","p":"n.","d":"surgery; the way something works","c":"手術；運作","s":"The doctor said the operation on her knee went well, and she should be able to walk without pain in about six weeks.","t":"醫生說她膝蓋的手術很順利，大約六週後她應該就能走路不痛了。"},{"w":"operator","p":"n.","d":"a person who works a machine or answers phone calls","c":"操作員；接線生","s":"If you dial zero on the hotel phone, an operator will answer and connect you to any room or service you need.","t":"如果你在飯店電話上撥零，接線生會接聽並幫你轉接到任何房間或服務。"},{"w":"cooperative","p":"adj.","d":"willing to work together and help","c":"合作的；配合的","s":"The patient was very cooperative during the check-up, so the nurse finished all the tests in less than twenty minutes.","t":"病人在檢查時非常配合，所以護理師不到二十分鐘就完成所有檢測。"},{"w":"oppress","p":"v.","d":"to treat people in a cruel and unfair way, especially by using power","c":"壓迫","s":"For many years the king used his army to oppress the farmers, taking most of their rice and leaving them hungry.","t":"多年來國王利用軍隊壓迫農民，拿走他們大部分的稻米，讓他們飢餓。","h":1},{"w":"oppression","p":"n.","d":"cruel and unfair treatment by people in power","c":"壓迫","s":"Thousands of people left the country to escape oppression, hoping to find freedom and a better life across the sea.","t":"成千上萬的人離開那個國家以逃離壓迫，希望在海的另一邊找到自由和更好的生活。","h":1},{"w":"oppressive","p":"adj.","d":"cruel and unfair; (of weather) hot and uncomfortable","c":"壓迫的；（天氣）悶熱的","s":"The heat in the classroom was so oppressive that the teacher let the students take the test in the air-conditioned library instead.","t":"教室裡的熱氣悶熱得令人難受，所以老師讓學生改到有冷氣的圖書館考試。"},{"w":"the oppressed","p":"n.","d":"people who are treated cruelly and unfairly","c":"受壓迫的人","s":"The young lawyer spent her whole life fighting for the oppressed, and she never charged poor families for her help.","t":"這位年輕律師一生都在為受壓迫的人奮鬥，而且從不向貧窮家庭收取費用。"},{"w":"oppressor","p":"n.","d":"a person or group that treats others cruelly and unfairly","c":"壓迫者","s":"In the movie, the villagers finally stand together and drive away the cruel oppressor who had taxed them for twenty years.","t":"電影中，村民最終團結起來，趕走了向他們課稅二十年的殘暴壓迫者。"},{"w":"ordeal","p":"n.","d":"a very difficult or painful experience","c":"苦難；折磨；考驗","s":"Being lost in the mountains for three cold nights was a terrible ordeal, but the two hikers were finally found alive.","t":"在山裡迷路、度過三個寒冷的夜晚是一場可怕的磨難，但兩名登山客最後被活著找到。","h":1},{"w":"go through an ordeal","p":"v.phr.","d":"to experience something very hard","c":"經歷苦難","s":"The family went through an ordeal when their house burned down, but neighbors brought them food and clothes every day for a month.","t":"房子燒毀時這家人經歷了一場苦難，但鄰居們一個月來每天都送食物和衣服給他們。","a":"went through an ordeal"},{"w":"hardship","p":"n.","d":"something that makes life difficult, such as having little money","c":"艱苦；困境","s":"During the war, people faced great hardship; many families had only one meal a day and no electricity at night.","t":"戰爭期間人們面臨極大的艱苦，許多家庭一天只有一餐，晚上也沒有電。"},{"w":"orderly","p":"adj.","d":"well arranged; calm and well behaved","c":"整齊的；有秩序的","s":"The teacher asked the students to leave the hall in an orderly way, one row at a time, after the fire alarm rang.","t":"火警警報響起後，老師要求學生以有秩序的方式一次一排離開禮堂。","h":1},{"w":"orderly","p":"n.","d":"a hospital worker who helps move patients and does other simple jobs","c":"醫院護理員；勤務員","s":"An orderly pushed my grandfather's wheelchair from the X-ray room back to his ward on the fifth floor.","t":"一名護理員把我爺爺的輪椅從X光室推回五樓的病房。"},{"w":"order","p":"n.","d":"the way things are arranged; a command; a request for goods","c":"順序；命令；訂單","s":"Please put these books back on the shelf in alphabetical order so that other students can find them easily.","t":"請把這些書按字母順序放回書架，以便其他學生容易找到。"},{"w":"in order to","p":"phr.","d":"so that you can do something","c":"為了","s":"She gets up at five every morning in order to practice the piano for an hour before she leaves for school.","t":"她每天早上五點起床，為了在上學前練一小時鋼琴。"},{"w":"disorder","p":"n.","d":"a messy state; an illness of the mind or body","c":"混亂；失調；疾病","s":"After the party, the living room was in complete disorder, with cups, plates, and paper everywhere on the floor.","t":"派對之後客廳一片混亂，杯子、盤子和紙張散落在地板各處。"},{"w":"organizer","p":"n.","d":"a person who plans and arranges an event","c":"組織者；主辦者","s":"The organizer of the charity run thanked all three hundred volunteers who had worked at the water stations along the route.","t":"慈善路跑的主辦人感謝沿路在補水站工作的全部三百位志工。","h":1},{"w":"organize","p":"v.","d":"to plan and arrange something; to put things in order","c":"組織；籌辦；整理","s":"Our class decided to organize a farewell party for Mr. Lin, who is leaving the school at the end of this semester.","t":"我們班決定為這學期結束後要離開學校的林老師籌辦一場送別會。"},{"w":"organization","p":"n.","d":"a group of people who work together for a purpose","c":"組織；機構","s":"This organization collects used books from schools and sends them to children in poor villages around the island.","t":"這個組織向學校收集二手書，送給全島貧窮村莊的孩子。"},{"w":"organized","p":"adj.","d":"well planned; good at arranging things","c":"有條理的；井然有序的","s":"My sister is so organized that she writes down every homework task in her planner and never misses a deadline.","t":"我姐姐非常有條理，她把每項作業都寫在行事曆上，從不錯過期限。"},{"w":"organic","p":"adj.","d":"grown without chemicals; from living things","c":"有機的","s":"Many families now buy organic vegetables at the weekend market because they are grown without any chemical sprays.","t":"許多家庭現在會在週末市集購買有機蔬菜，因為它們是在不噴灑任何化學藥劑的情況下種植的。"},{"w":"orient","p":"v.","d":"to find your position; to make something suitable for a purpose","c":"定位；使適應；使朝向","s":"When you come out of the MRT station, use the tall tower to orient yourself, and then walk toward the river.","t":"走出捷運站後，利用那座高塔確定自己的方位，然後朝河邊走。","h":1},{"w":"oriental","p":"adj.","d":"connected with the countries of East Asia","c":"東方的","s":"The museum's new hall shows oriental art, including Chinese paintings, Japanese fans, and Korean pottery from several centuries ago.","t":"博物館的新展廳展出東方藝術，包括幾世紀前的中國畫、日本扇子和韓國陶器。","h":1},{"w":"the Orient","p":"n.","d":"the countries of East Asia (an old-fashioned word)","c":"東方（亞洲）","s":"Hundreds of years ago, European traders sailed to the Orient to buy silk, tea, and spices that they could sell at home.","t":"數百年前，歐洲商人航行到東方購買絲綢、茶葉和香料，帶回國販售。"},{"w":"orientation","p":"n.","d":"a meeting that introduces new people to a place; direction","c":"新生訓練；方向","s":"All freshmen must attend the orientation on the first day, where teachers explain the school rules and show them around campus.","t":"所有新生必須參加第一天的新生訓練，老師會在那裡說明校規並帶他們參觀校園。"},{"w":"be oriented toward","p":"v.phr.","d":"to be mainly aimed at or interested in","c":"以…為導向","s":"The new course is oriented toward students who want to work in hotels, so it includes a lot of speaking practice.","t":"這門新課程以想在飯店工作的學生為導向，所以包含許多口說練習。","a":"is oriented toward"},{"w":"originate","p":"v.","d":"to start or come from a place or time","c":"起源；發源","s":"Many scholars believe that the custom of giving red envelopes did not originate in Taiwan but was brought here from southern China.","t":"許多學者認為送紅包的習俗並非起源於台灣，而是從中國南方傳來的。","h":1},{"w":"originate from","p":"v.phr.","d":"to come from a place or source","c":"源自於","s":"Several English words that we use every day, such as \"typhoon\" and \"tea,\" actually originate from Chinese languages.","t":"我們每天使用的幾個英文字，例如 typhoon 和 tea，其實源自漢語。"},{"w":"origin","p":"n.","d":"where something comes from; the beginning","c":"起源；出身","s":"Nobody knows the exact origin of this festival, but old people in the village say it began more than two hundred years ago.","t":"沒有人知道這個節慶確切的起源，但村裡的老人說它始於兩百多年前。"},{"w":"original","p":"adj.","d":"first; new and not copied","c":"原來的；原創的","s":"The original plan was to meet at six, but we changed it to seven because half of the group had to work late.","t":"原本的計畫是六點見面，但因為一半的人要加班，我們改成七點。"},{"w":"originally","p":"adv.","d":"at first; in the beginning","c":"原本；起初","s":"The building was originally a train station, but it was turned into a shopping mall after the new high-speed rail line opened.","t":"這棟建築原本是火車站，但在新的高鐵線開通後被改成購物中心。"},{"w":"ornament","p":"n.","d":"a small pretty object used for decoration","c":"裝飾品","s":"Every December my mother takes out a box of glass ornaments and hangs them carefully on the tree in our living room.","t":"每年十二月，媽媽都會拿出一盒玻璃裝飾品，小心地掛在客廳的樹上。","a":"ornaments","h":1},{"w":"ornament","p":"v.","d":"to decorate something","c":"裝飾","s":"The temple roof is ornamented with colorful dragons and birds, which were made by local artists over fifty years ago.","t":"廟的屋頂裝飾著彩色的龍和鳥，是當地藝術家五十多年前製作的。","a":"ornamented"},{"w":"ornamental","p":"adj.","d":"used for decoration rather than for a purpose","c":"裝飾用的","s":"The old fireplace in the hotel lobby is purely ornamental; it has not been used for real fires since the 1970s.","t":"飯店大廳裡的舊壁爐純粹是裝飾用的，自一九七〇年代起就沒再真正生過火。"},{"w":"adorn","p":"v.","d":"to make something more beautiful by adding things","c":"裝飾；點綴","s":"Hundreds of paper lanterns adorn the old street during the festival, and tourists line up to take photos under them.","t":"節慶期間，數百個紙燈籠點綴著老街，遊客排隊在燈籠下拍照。"},{"w":"decoration","p":"n.","d":"something that makes a place look nicer","c":"裝飾","s":"The students spent the whole afternoon making decorations for the Christmas party, including paper snowflakes and colored lights.","t":"學生們花了整個下午製作聖誕派對的裝飾，包括紙雪花和彩色燈。","a":"decorations"},{"w":"orphanage","p":"n.","d":"a home for children whose parents are dead","c":"孤兒院","s":"Every Saturday morning, a group of college students visits the orphanage to read stories and play games with the children there.","t":"每個星期六早上，一群大學生會去孤兒院讀故事給那裡的孩子聽，並和他們玩遊戲。","h":1},{"w":"orphan","p":"n.","d":"a child whose parents are dead","c":"孤兒","s":"The movie tells the story of a young orphan who travels across the country alone to find his only living relative.","t":"這部電影講述一個年幼的孤兒獨自穿越全國，尋找他唯一在世親人的故事。"},{"w":"be orphaned","p":"v.phr.","d":"to lose both parents, usually as a child","c":"成為孤兒","s":"Thousands of children were orphaned by the earthquake, and families around the world offered to adopt them.","t":"成千上萬的孩子因地震而成為孤兒，世界各地的家庭都表示願意收養他們。","a":"were orphaned"},{"w":"adopt","p":"v.","d":"to take someone else's child into your family legally","c":"收養","s":"My aunt and uncle decided to adopt a baby girl from the orphanage after they learned they could not have children.","t":"我阿姨和姨丈得知無法生育後，決定從孤兒院收養一個女嬰。"},{"w":"orthodox","p":"adj.","d":"following the usual or traditional beliefs or methods","c":"正統的；傳統的","s":"The doctor preferred orthodox treatments such as medicine and rest, and he warned patients about strange cures sold online.","t":"這位醫生偏好正統的療法，例如藥物和休息，並警告病人小心網路上販售的奇怪療方。","h":1},{"w":"unorthodox","p":"adj.","d":"different from what is usual or traditional","c":"非正統的；非傳統的","s":"The young coach uses unorthodox methods, like having the players practice yoga, but the team has won every game this season.","t":"這位年輕教練採用非傳統的方法，例如讓球員練瑜珈，但球隊本季每場比賽都贏了。"},{"w":"orthodoxy","p":"n.","d":"traditional and generally accepted beliefs","c":"正統觀念","s":"For centuries, scientific orthodoxy said the sun moved around the earth, and anyone who disagreed was in serious trouble.","t":"數百年來，科學正統觀念認為太陽繞著地球轉，任何不同意的人都會惹上大麻煩。"},{"w":"the Orthodox Church","p":"n.phr.","d":"the main Christian church of Greece, Russia, and eastern Europe","c":"東正教會","s":"Many people in Greece and Russia belong to the Orthodox Church, which celebrates Christmas on a different date from the West.","t":"希臘和俄羅斯的許多人屬於東正教會，它慶祝聖誕節的日期與西方不同。"},{"w":"ounce","p":"n.","d":"a unit of weight equal to about 28 grams","c":"盎司","s":"This recipe needs eight ounces of butter, which is about one and a half of the small blocks sold at the supermarket.","t":"這份食譜需要八盎司奶油，大約是超市賣的小塊奶油一塊半。","a":"ounces","h":1},{"w":"an ounce of","p":"phr.","d":"a very small amount of something (often in negative sentences)","c":"一點點（常用於否定句）","s":"If he had an ounce of common sense, he would not have left his new bicycle unlocked outside the night market.","t":"如果他有一點常識，就不會把新腳踏車沒上鎖地留在夜市外面。"},{"w":"pound","p":"n.","d":"a unit of weight equal to 16 ounces, about 450 grams","c":"磅","s":"The baby weighed just over seven pounds when she was born, and the doctor said she was perfectly healthy.","t":"這個女嬰出生時體重剛超過七磅，醫生說她非常健康。","a":"pounds"},{"w":"gram","p":"n.","d":"a small unit of weight; there are 1,000 grams in a kilogram","c":"公克","s":"One slice of this cake contains about forty grams of sugar, which is more than a child should eat in a whole day.","t":"這種蛋糕一片含有大約四十公克的糖，比小孩一整天該吃的量還多。","a":"grams"},{"w":"outbreak","p":"n.","d":"the sudden start of something bad, such as a disease or war","c":"爆發","s":"After the outbreak of flu in the school, more than a hundred students stayed home, and classes were canceled for three days.","t":"學校流感爆發後，超過一百名學生在家休息，課程停了三天。","h":1},{"w":"break out","p":"v.phr.","d":"to start suddenly (a fire, war, or disease)","c":"突然發生；爆發","s":"A fire broke out in the kitchen of the restaurant last night, but luckily the workers put it out before anyone was hurt.","t":"昨晚餐廳廚房突然起火，但幸好員工在有人受傷前就把火撲滅了。","a":"broke out"},{"w":"break, broke, broken","p":"v.","d":"to separate into pieces; to damage","c":"打破；弄壞","s":"Be careful not to break the glass vase on the table; it was a wedding gift from my grandmother forty years ago.","t":"小心不要打破桌上的玻璃花瓶，那是我奶奶四十年前的結婚禮物。","a":"break"},{"w":"breakdown","p":"n.","d":"a failure of a machine; a failure of a relationship or system","c":"故障；崩潰；破裂","s":"The train was delayed for two hours because of a breakdown in the signal system, and many passengers missed their connecting flights.","t":"火車因為號誌系統故障而延誤兩小時，許多乘客錯過了轉接的航班。"},{"w":"outgoing","p":"adj.","d":"friendly and enjoying meeting people","c":"外向的；開朗的","s":"My outgoing roommate made friends with everyone on our floor during the first week, while I only knew two people.","t":"我外向的室友第一週就和我們這層樓的每個人都成了朋友，而我只認識兩個人。","h":1},{"w":"outgoing","p":"adj.","d":"leaving a position or a place","c":"即將離職的；寄出的","s":"The outgoing principal gave a short speech at the graduation ceremony and thanked the teachers for their ten years of hard work.","t":"即將離職的校長在畢業典禮上發表簡短演說，感謝老師們十年來的辛勞。"},{"w":"go out","p":"v.phr.","d":"to leave your home for fun; to stop burning","c":"外出；熄滅","s":"We usually go out for dinner on Friday nights, and my little sister always chooses the same noodle shop near the park.","t":"我們星期五晚上通常會外出吃晚餐，我妹妹總是選公園附近同一家麵店。"},{"w":"incoming","p":"adj.","d":"arriving; just elected or chosen","c":"進來的；新上任的","s":"The incoming class president promised to add more sports clubs and to fix the broken water fountain near the gym.","t":"新上任的班長承諾增加更多運動社團，並修好體育館附近壞掉的飲水機。"},{"w":"extroverted","p":"adj.","d":"lively and confident; enjoying being with people","c":"外向的","s":"Sales jobs usually suit extroverted people who enjoy talking to strangers and do not mind hearing \"no\" several times a day.","t":"業務工作通常適合外向的人，他們喜歡和陌生人交談，也不介意一天被拒絕好幾次。"},{"w":"outing","p":"n.","d":"a short trip for pleasure","c":"郊遊；短途旅行","s":"The company arranged an outing to a hot spring resort in Beitou, and every employee was allowed to bring one family member.","t":"公司安排了一次到北投溫泉度假村的郊遊，每位員工都可以帶一位家人。","h":1},{"w":"a family outing","p":"n.phr.","d":"a short trip that a family takes together for fun","c":"家庭出遊","s":"Last Sunday we had a family outing to the zoo, and my little cousin cried when it was time to leave the pandas.","t":"上星期天我們全家出遊去動物園，要離開熊貓時我的小表弟哭了。"},{"w":"excursion","p":"n.","d":"a short trip made by a group of people for pleasure or study","c":"遠足；短途旅行","s":"Our geography class is going on an excursion to Yangmingshan next week to study the volcanic rocks and hot springs.","t":"我們地理課下週要去陽明山遠足，研究火山岩和溫泉。"},{"w":"picnic","p":"n.","d":"a meal eaten outdoors","c":"野餐","s":"The weather was perfect for a picnic in the park, so we packed sandwiches, fruit, and a big bottle of lemonade.","t":"天氣非常適合在公園野餐，所以我們打包了三明治、水果和一大瓶檸檬水。"},{"w":"outlaw","p":"n.","d":"a criminal who is hiding from the law, especially in the past","c":"逃犯；亡命之徒","s":"In the old Western movie, the outlaw robbed three banks before the sheriff finally caught him near the border.","t":"在那部老西部電影中，亡命之徒搶了三家銀行，警長才終於在邊境附近抓到他。","h":1},{"w":"outlaw","p":"v.","d":"to make something illegal","c":"宣布…為非法；禁止","s":"The city decided to outlaw the use of plastic straws in restaurants, so most shops now offer paper or metal ones instead.","t":"市政府決定禁止餐廳使用塑膠吸管，所以大多數店家現在改提供紙吸管或金屬吸管。"},{"w":"law","p":"n.","d":"a rule made by the government that everyone must follow","c":"法律","s":"Under the new law, drivers who use their phones while driving will have to pay a fine of three thousand dollars.","t":"根據新法律，開車時使用手機的駕駛將必須繳三千元罰款。"},{"w":"lawful","p":"adj.","d":"allowed by law","c":"合法的","s":"It is lawful to ride a bicycle on this path, but motorcycles are not allowed because it passes through a children's park.","t":"在這條小徑上騎腳踏車是合法的，但機車不行，因為它穿過兒童公園。"},{"w":"lawyer","p":"n.","d":"a person whose job is to help people with the law","c":"律師","s":"My cousin worked as a lawyer for ten years before she became a judge in the district court last spring.","t":"我表姐當了十年律師，去年春天才成為地方法院的法官。"}]},{"unit":26,"theme":"outlook – patriotic","cards":[{"w":"outlook","p":"n.","d":"what is likely to happen in the future; your general attitude to life","c":"前景；展望；看法","s":"The weather outlook for the weekend is good, so we can finally go camping by the lake as we planned last month.","t":"週末的天氣展望良好，所以我們終於可以照上個月的計畫去湖邊露營。","h":1},{"w":"a positive outlook","p":"n.phr.","d":"a hopeful way of thinking about life","c":"樂觀的態度","s":"Even after losing his job, my uncle kept a positive outlook and said that something better would come along very soon.","t":"即使丟了工作，我叔叔仍保持樂觀的態度，說很快就會有更好的機會出現。"},{"w":"look out","p":"v.phr.","d":"to be careful; to watch for danger","c":"小心；留意","s":"Look out for motorcycles when you cross this street, because many riders do not stop at the red light here.","t":"過這條街時要小心機車，因為這裡很多騎士不會在紅燈停下來。","a":"Look out"},{"w":"overlook","p":"v.","d":"to fail to notice something; to have a view over","c":"忽略；俯瞰","s":"The teacher asked us to check our essays twice so that we would not overlook any spelling mistakes before handing them in.","t":"老師要我們把作文檢查兩次，以免交出去前忽略任何拼字錯誤。"},{"w":"lookout","p":"n.","d":"a place to watch from; a person who watches for danger","c":"瞭望台；守望者","s":"From the lookout at the top of the hill, visitors can see the whole harbor and the ships coming in from the sea.","t":"從山頂的瞭望台，遊客可以看到整個港口和從海上駛入的船隻。"},{"w":"outnumber","p":"v.","d":"to be more in number than another group","c":"數量多於","s":"At the small village school, girls outnumber boys by almost two to one, so the soccer team has many female players.","t":"在這所小村校，女生人數多於男生將近二比一，所以足球隊有許多女隊員。","h":1},{"w":"be outnumbered","p":"v.phr.","d":"to be fewer than the other group","c":"寡不敵眾；人數居劣勢","s":"Our team was outnumbered six to four after two players were sent off, but we still managed to win the game.","t":"兩名球員被罰出場後，我們隊以四對六人數居劣勢，但我們仍設法贏得比賽。","a":"was outnumbered"},{"w":"number","p":"n.","d":"a word or sign that shows how many; a telephone number","c":"數字；號碼","s":"Please write your student number at the top of the answer sheet before you start the listening test this morning.","t":"今天早上開始聽力測驗前，請在答案卡最上方寫下你的學號。"},{"w":"a number of","p":"phr.","d":"several; many","c":"一些；許多","s":"A number of students have complained about the noise from the construction site next to the library this week.","t":"這週一些學生抱怨圖書館旁邊工地的噪音。","a":"A number of"},{"w":"numerous","p":"adj.","d":"very many","c":"許多的","s":"The old temple has been repaired numerous times over the past three hundred years, but its wooden doors are still the original ones.","t":"這座古廟在過去三百年來被修復過許多次，但它的木門仍是原來的。"},{"w":"outrage","p":"n.","d":"a strong feeling of anger and shock; a very cruel or shocking act","c":"憤慨；暴行","s":"The news that the company had dumped waste into the river caused public outrage, and hundreds of people protested outside its office.","t":"該公司把廢棄物倒入河中的消息引起公眾憤慨，數百人在其辦公室外抗議。","h":1},{"w":"outrageous","p":"adj.","d":"very shocking and unfair; very unusual","c":"令人髮指的；離譜的","s":"Charging two thousand dollars for a bowl of noodles is outrageous, and the restaurant lost most of its customers within a month.","t":"一碗麵收費兩千元實在離譜，那家餐廳一個月內就失去了大部分顧客。","h":1},{"w":"outrage","p":"v.","d":"to make someone very angry and shocked","c":"激怒","s":"The decision to close the only hospital in the town outraged the local people, who had to travel an hour to see a doctor.","t":"關閉鎮上唯一醫院的決定激怒了當地居民，他們必須花一小時的車程才能看醫生。","a":"outraged"},{"w":"be outraged by","p":"v.phr.","d":"to be very angry and shocked by something","c":"對…感到憤慨","s":"Parents were outraged by the school's plan to cut all art and music classes to save money next year.","t":"家長們對學校明年為省錢而取消所有美術和音樂課的計畫感到憤慨。","a":"were outraged by"},{"w":"rage","p":"n.","d":"very strong anger","c":"狂怒","s":"He hit the wall in a rage after his little brother broke the model ship that had taken him a month to build.","t":"他弟弟弄壞了他花一個月做好的模型船後，他暴怒之下捶了牆壁。"},{"w":"outright","p":"adj.","d":"complete and total; clear","c":"完全的；徹底的；直接的","s":"The election ended in an outright victory for the young mayor, who won more than seventy percent of the votes.","t":"這場選舉以年輕市長的完全勝利告終，他獲得超過百分之七十的選票。","h":1},{"w":"outright","p":"adv.","d":"completely; directly and openly; at once","c":"完全地；直截了當地；當場","s":"Instead of making excuses, she told her boss outright that she had forgotten to send the report on Friday.","t":"她沒有找藉口，而是直截了當地告訴老闆她星期五忘了寄報告。"},{"w":"right","p":"adv.","d":"exactly; immediately; correctly","c":"正好；立刻；正確地","s":"The bus stop is right in front of the school gate, so you will not have to walk far in the rain.","t":"公車站就在校門口前面，所以你不必在雨中走很遠。"},{"w":"rightful","p":"adj.","d":"that you have a legal or moral right to","c":"合法的；正當的","s":"After a long court case, the old house was finally returned to its rightful owner, who had lost it during the war.","t":"經過漫長的訴訟，那棟老房子終於歸還給它合法的主人，他在戰爭期間失去了它。"},{"w":"outset","p":"n.","d":"the beginning of something","c":"開始；開端","s":"From the outset, the coach made it clear that every player had to attend all the practices or leave the team.","t":"從一開始，教練就說清楚每位球員必須參加所有練習，否則就離開球隊。","h":1},{"w":"at the outset","p":"phr.","d":"at the beginning","c":"一開始","s":"At the outset of the trip, nobody expected that we would get lost twice and arrive at the hotel after midnight.","t":"旅程一開始，沒有人料到我們會迷路兩次，半夜過後才到飯店。","a":"At the outset"},{"w":"set out","p":"v.phr.","d":"to start a journey; to start doing something with a clear aim","c":"出發；著手","s":"The hikers set out at five in the morning so that they could reach the top of the mountain before the afternoon rain.","t":"登山客早上五點出發，以便在午後下雨前登上山頂。"},{"w":"set, set, set","p":"v.","d":"to put something somewhere carefully; to decide on a time or price","c":"放置；設定","s":"Please set the alarm for six o'clock, because we need to leave the house by seven to catch the early train.","t":"請把鬧鐘設定在六點，因為我們必須七點前出門才趕得上早班火車。","a":"set"},{"w":"onset","p":"n.","d":"the beginning of something, especially something bad","c":"（不好的事的）開始","s":"Doctors say that getting enough sleep can delay the onset of many health problems that often appear after the age of fifty.","t":"醫生說充足的睡眠可以延緩許多常在五十歲後出現的健康問題的發生。"},{"w":"outskirts","p":"n.","d":"the areas at the edge of a town or city","c":"郊區；市郊","s":"My grandparents live on the outskirts of Taichung, where the houses have gardens and the air is much cleaner than downtown.","t":"我祖父母住在台中市郊，那裡的房子有花園，空氣也比市中心乾淨得多。","h":1},{"w":"on the outskirts of","p":"phr.","d":"at the edge of a town or city","c":"在…的郊區","s":"The new factory was built on the outskirts of the city, so most workers drive about forty minutes to get there every morning.","t":"新工廠建在城市的郊區，所以大多數員工每天早上開車大約四十分鐘才能到。"},{"w":"suburb","p":"n.","d":"an area where people live outside the center of a city","c":"郊區","s":"Many young families move to the suburbs because apartments there are cheaper and the schools have bigger playgrounds.","t":"許多年輕家庭搬到郊區，因為那裡的公寓比較便宜，學校的操場也比較大。","a":"suburbs"},{"w":"skirt","p":"n.","d":"a piece of clothing for women and girls that hangs from the waist","c":"裙子","s":"Our school uniform includes a dark blue skirt for girls and gray pants for boys, and everyone wears a white shirt.","t":"我們的校服包括女生的深藍色裙子和男生的灰色長褲，每個人都穿白襯衫。"},{"w":"outward","p":"adj.","d":"on the outside; going away from a place","c":"外表的；向外的","s":"His outward calm hid the fact that he was extremely nervous before his first speech in front of the whole school.","t":"他外表的平靜掩蓋了他在全校面前第一次演講前極度緊張的事實。","h":1},{"w":"outward","p":"adv.","d":"toward the outside; away from the center","c":"向外","s":"The two doors of the emergency exit open outward, so push them hard if the alarm rings and you need to leave quickly.","t":"緊急出口的兩扇門是向外開的，所以如果警報響了需要快速離開，請用力推。"},{"w":"outwards","p":"adv.","d":"toward the outside (= outward, British spelling)","c":"向外","s":"Stand in a circle, face outwards, and hold hands with the people next to you; this is how the game begins.","t":"站成一個圓圈，面向外，並和旁邊的人牽手，遊戲就是這樣開始的。"},{"w":"inward","p":"adj.","d":"on the inside; toward the inside; of the mind","c":"向內的；內心的","s":"She felt an inward peace after finishing the last exam, even though she did not know her score yet.","t":"考完最後一科後她感到一種內心的平靜，即使她還不知道成績。"},{"w":"outward appearance","p":"n.phr.","d":"the way something looks from the outside","c":"外表","s":"You should not judge a shop by its outward appearance; the old place with the broken sign sells the best dumplings in town.","t":"你不該以外表評斷一家店；那家招牌壞掉的老店賣全鎮最好吃的水餃。"},{"w":"overdo, overdid, overdone","p":"v.","d":"to do something too much","c":"做得過火；過度","s":"It is good to exercise, but do not overdo it in the first week, or your muscles will hurt so much that you give up.","t":"運動是好事，但第一週不要過度，否則你的肌肉會痛到讓你放棄。","a":"overdo","h":1},{"w":"overdo it","p":"v.phr.","d":"to work or exercise too hard","c":"做過頭；累壞自己","s":"The doctor told my mother not to overdo it at work, because she had been staying at the office until ten every night.","t":"醫生告訴我媽媽工作不要做過頭，因為她每晚都待在辦公室到十點。"},{"w":"overdone","p":"adj.","d":"cooked too long; done too much","c":"煮過頭的；過火的","s":"The steak was overdone and tasted like leather, so my father politely asked the waiter to bring another one.","t":"牛排煮過頭，吃起來像皮革，所以我爸爸客氣地請服務生再送一份。"},{"w":"undo, undid, undone","p":"v.","d":"to open or loosen something; to cancel the effect of an action","c":"解開；取消；復原","s":"If you delete the wrong file by mistake, you can undo the action by pressing these two keys at the same time.","t":"如果你不小心刪錯檔案，可以同時按這兩個鍵來復原這個動作。","a":"undo"},{"w":"overeat","p":"v.","d":"to eat too much","c":"吃得過多","s":"People tend to overeat at buffet restaurants because they want to try every dish and get their money's worth.","t":"人們在吃到飽餐廳容易吃過量，因為他們想嘗試每道菜，覺得才值回票價。"},{"w":"overflow","p":"v.","d":"to flow over the edge of something because it is too full","c":"溢出；氾濫","s":"If you leave the tap running, the bathtub will overflow and the water will run under the door into the hallway.","t":"如果你讓水龍頭一直開著，浴缸會溢出，水會從門下流到走廊。","h":1},{"w":"overflow","p":"n.","d":"the liquid or amount that flows over; too many people or things","c":"溢出；滿溢","s":"The overflow of visitors at the night market was so large that the police had to close two nearby streets to cars.","t":"夜市滿溢的人潮太多，警方不得不封閉附近兩條街禁止車輛通行。"},{"w":"overflow with","p":"v.phr.","d":"to be very full of something","c":"充滿；擠滿","s":"On the first day of the sale, the small shop overflowed with customers, and people had to wait outside in a long line.","t":"特賣第一天，那家小店擠滿顧客，人們必須在外面排長隊等候。","a":"overflowed with"},{"w":"flow","p":"v.","d":"to move smoothly and continuously, like water","c":"流動","s":"The river used to flow through the center of the old town before the city built a new channel for it.","t":"在市政府修建新河道之前，這條河原本流經老城的中心。"},{"w":"flood","p":"n.","d":"a large amount of water covering land that is usually dry","c":"洪水","s":"After three days of heavy rain, the flood covered the farms, and families had to leave their homes by boat.","t":"連續三天大雨後，洪水淹沒了農田，許多家庭必須乘船離開家園。"},{"w":"overhear, overheard, overheard","p":"v.","d":"to hear what other people are saying by accident","c":"無意中聽到","s":"I happened to overhear two teachers talking in the hallway, and it seems that the final exam will be easier this year.","t":"我碰巧無意中聽到兩位老師在走廊上交談，看來今年的期末考會比較簡單。","a":"overhear","h":1},{"w":"hear, heard, heard","p":"v.","d":"to receive sounds with your ears","c":"聽到","s":"Could you speak a little louder, please? I cannot hear you clearly because the fans in this room are very noisy.","t":"請你說大聲一點好嗎？我聽不清楚你說的話，因為這個房間的風扇很吵。","a":"hear"},{"w":"hear from","p":"v.phr.","d":"to receive a letter, an email, or a call from someone","c":"收到…的消息","s":"We have not heard from our cousin in Canada since last Christmas, so my mother is going to call her this weekend.","t":"自去年聖誕節以來我們就沒有收到加拿大表姐的消息，所以我媽媽這個週末要打電話給她。","a":"heard from"},{"w":"hearing","p":"n.","d":"the ability to hear; a meeting in court","c":"聽力；聽證會","s":"My grandfather's hearing is not as good as it used to be, so we always sit on his right side and speak slowly.","t":"我爺爺的聽力不如從前，所以我們總是坐在他右邊慢慢說話。"},{"w":"eavesdrop","p":"v.","d":"to listen secretly to a private conversation","c":"偷聽","s":"It is rude to eavesdrop on other people's conversations, even if you are very curious about what they are saying.","t":"偷聽別人的談話是不禮貌的，即使你很好奇他們在說什麼。"},{"w":"overlap","p":"v.","d":"to cover part of the same area; to happen partly at the same time","c":"重疊；部分相同","s":"The two classes overlap by twenty minutes, so I have to leave the chemistry lab early every Tuesday to get to English.","t":"這兩堂課重疊二十分鐘，所以我每週二都得提早離開化學實驗室去上英文課。","h":1},{"w":"overlap","p":"n.","d":"a part that is shared or the same","c":"重疊部分","s":"There is a lot of overlap between the two textbooks, so you do not need to read every chapter in both of them.","t":"這兩本教科書有很多重疊的內容，所以你不必把兩本的每一章都讀完。"},{"w":"overlapping","p":"adj.","d":"covering part of the same area or time","c":"重疊的","s":"The roof is made of overlapping tiles, so rain runs down from one tile to the next without getting inside the house.","t":"屋頂是由重疊的瓦片組成，所以雨水從一片瓦流到下一片，不會滲進屋內。"},{"w":"lap","p":"n.","d":"the top part of your legs when you sit down; one time around a track","c":"大腿上；一圈","s":"The cat jumped onto my lap and fell asleep while I was reading, so I could not get up for an hour.","t":"我看書時貓跳到我大腿上睡著了，所以我一個小時都不能起身。"},{"w":"overwork","p":"v.","d":"to work too hard or make someone work too hard","c":"使過度勞累；工作過度","s":"The manager should not overwork the new staff, because tired workers make more mistakes and often quit within a year.","t":"經理不應該讓新員工過度勞累，因為疲累的員工會犯更多錯誤，而且常在一年內離職。","h":1},{"w":"overwork","p":"n.","d":"the act of working too hard","c":"過度勞累","s":"The doctor said that overwork was the main reason for his headaches, and he advised him to take a two-week vacation.","t":"醫生說過度勞累是他頭痛的主因，建議他休假兩週。"},{"w":"overworked","p":"adj.","d":"having too much work to do","c":"工作過度的","s":"The nurses at the hospital are overworked and underpaid, so many of them are thinking about changing jobs next year.","t":"這家醫院的護理師工作過度且薪水過低，所以許多人正考慮明年換工作。"},{"w":"workload","p":"n.","d":"the amount of work a person has to do","c":"工作量","s":"The workload in the final month of the semester is heavy, with three reports and two exams in just two weeks.","t":"學期最後一個月的工作量很重，兩週內就有三份報告和兩場考試。"},{"w":"workaholic","p":"n.","d":"a person who cannot stop working","c":"工作狂","s":"My father is a workaholic who checks his email at dinner and goes back to the office on Sunday mornings.","t":"我爸爸是個工作狂，晚餐時查電子郵件，星期天早上還回辦公室。"},{"w":"oyster","p":"n.","d":"a flat sea shellfish that can be eaten and sometimes makes pearls","c":"牡蠣；蚵仔","s":"Farmers in Tainan raise millions of oysters in the shallow water along the coast, and they sell them to restaurants all over the island.","t":"台南的養殖戶在沿岸淺水區養殖數百萬顆牡蠣，賣給全島各地的餐廳。","a":"oysters","h":1},{"w":"oyster omelet","p":"n.phr.","d":"a Taiwanese dish made of eggs and oysters","c":"蚵仔煎","s":"The oyster omelet at that stand is famous, so people line up for half an hour just to get one hot plate.","t":"那個攤位的蚵仔煎很有名，所以人們排半小時只為買到一盤熱騰騰的。"},{"w":"the world is your oyster","p":"phr.","d":"you can do anything or go anywhere you want","c":"世界任你遨遊","s":"With a good education and two languages, the world is your oyster, so do not be afraid to apply for jobs overseas.","t":"有了良好的教育和兩種語言，世界任你遨遊，所以別害怕去申請海外的工作。"},{"w":"shellfish","p":"n.","d":"sea animals with shells, such as oysters, clams, and shrimp","c":"貝類；甲殼類海鮮","s":"People who are allergic to shellfish must be careful at seafood restaurants, since even a small piece of shrimp can make them sick.","t":"對貝類海鮮過敏的人在海鮮餐廳必須小心，因為即使一小塊蝦子也可能讓他們生病。"},{"w":"pearl","p":"n.","d":"a small round white jewel that grows inside an oyster","c":"珍珠","s":"My grandmother gave my sister a pearl necklace on her wedding day, and it had belonged to our great-grandmother.","t":"奶奶在我姐姐結婚那天送她一條珍珠項鍊，那原本是我們曾祖母的。"},{"w":"ozone","p":"n.","d":"a form of oxygen gas high in the air that protects the earth from the sun's harmful rays","c":"臭氧","s":"Scientists warned that certain chemicals in old refrigerators destroy ozone and let more harmful sunlight reach the earth.","t":"科學家警告，舊冰箱中的某些化學物質會破壞臭氧，讓更多有害的陽光到達地球。","h":1},{"w":"the ozone layer","p":"n.phr.","d":"the layer of ozone high above the earth","c":"臭氧層","s":"Thanks to a worldwide agreement in 1987, the ozone layer has slowly started to repair itself, which is good news for everyone.","t":"多虧了一九八七年的全球協議，臭氧層已慢慢開始自我修復，這對每個人來說都是好消息。"},{"w":"oxygen","p":"n.","d":"the gas in the air that people and animals need to breathe","c":"氧氣","s":"At the top of the mountain, the air has less oxygen, so climbers walk slowly and stop often to catch their breath.","t":"山頂的空氣氧氣較少，所以登山者走得很慢，常停下來喘口氣。"},{"w":"atmosphere","p":"n.","d":"the mixture of gases around the earth; the feeling in a place","c":"大氣層；氣氛","s":"Factories and cars send huge amounts of carbon dioxide into the atmosphere, which makes the earth warmer every year.","t":"工廠和汽車排放大量二氧化碳到大氣層，使地球每年都變得更暖。"},{"w":"packet","p":"n.","d":"a small paper or plastic container; a small package","c":"小包；小袋","s":"Please add one packet of sugar to my coffee, but not two, because I am trying to eat less sweet food this month.","t":"請在我的咖啡裡加一小包糖，但不要兩包，因為我這個月想少吃甜食。","h":1},{"w":"pack","p":"v.","d":"to put things into bags or boxes for a trip","c":"打包；收拾","s":"Do not forget to pack a warm jacket for the trip, because the mountain gets very cold after the sun goes down.","t":"別忘了為這趟旅行打包一件保暖外套，因為太陽下山後山上會變得很冷。"},{"w":"package","p":"n.","d":"something wrapped in paper or put in a box, especially for sending","c":"包裹","s":"A package arrived for you this morning while you were at school; I think it is the books you ordered online.","t":"今天早上你在學校時有一個包裹寄來給你，我想是你在網路上訂的書。"},{"w":"backpack","p":"n.","d":"a bag that you carry on your back","c":"背包","s":"My backpack is so heavy with textbooks that my shoulders hurt by the time I get to school every morning.","t":"我的背包裝了教科書重得要命，每天早上到學校時我的肩膀都在痛。"},{"w":"a pack of","p":"n.phr.","d":"a group of animals; a set of cards; a packet","c":"一群；一副；一包","s":"A pack of wild dogs lives in the hills behind our school, so the teachers tell us not to go there alone.","t":"一群野狗住在我們學校後面的山丘上，所以老師叫我們不要單獨去那裡。","a":"A pack of"},{"w":"paddle","p":"n.","d":"a short pole with a flat end used to move a small boat","c":"槳","s":"Hold the paddle with both hands and pull it through the water on one side, then the other, to keep the canoe straight.","t":"雙手握住槳，先在一側划水再換另一側，讓獨木舟保持直線。","h":1},{"w":"paddle","p":"v.","d":"to move a small boat with a paddle; to walk in shallow water","c":"划船；涉水","s":"We had to paddle hard against the wind to get the boat back to the shore before the storm arrived.","t":"我們必須頂著風用力划，才能在暴風雨來臨前把船划回岸邊。"},{"w":"paddle board","p":"n.phr.","d":"a long board that you stand on and move with a paddle","c":"立槳板","s":"Standing on a paddle board for the first time is not easy, and most beginners fall into the water a few times.","t":"第一次站在立槳板上並不容易，大多數初學者會落水幾次。"},{"w":"row","p":"v.","d":"to move a boat through water using oars","c":"划船","s":"My grandfather taught me how to row a boat on the lake when I was eight, and now I can go out alone.","t":"我八歲時爺爺教我如何在湖上划船，現在我可以自己出去划了。"},{"w":"canoe","p":"n.","d":"a light narrow boat that you move with a paddle","c":"獨木舟","s":"The tour guide showed us how to get into the canoe without tipping it over, and then we floated slowly down the river.","t":"導遊教我們如何上獨木舟而不讓它翻覆，然後我們沿河慢慢漂流而下。"},{"w":"paperback","p":"n.","d":"a book with a soft paper cover","c":"平裝書","s":"I bought the paperback instead of the hardcover edition because it was half the price and much lighter to carry on the train.","t":"我買了平裝本而不是精裝版，因為它價格只有一半，而且在火車上帶著輕得多。","h":1},{"w":"hardcover","p":"n.","d":"a book with a stiff, hard cover","c":"精裝書","s":"The library keeps the hardcover of this novel on the reference shelf, so you can read it there but cannot take it home.","t":"圖書館把這本小說的精裝本放在參考書架上，你可以在那裡閱讀但不能帶回家。"},{"w":"paper","p":"n.","d":"thin material used for writing; a newspaper; an essay","c":"紙；報紙；論文","s":"We need to buy more paper for the printer before Monday, because every class has to print a report that day.","t":"我們必須在星期一前多買些印表機用紙，因為那天每個班級都要列印報告。"},{"w":"paperwork","p":"n.","d":"the written work, such as forms, that you have to do for a job","c":"文書工作","s":"Opening a small restaurant involves a lot of paperwork, including licenses for food safety, fire safety, and tax.","t":"開一家小餐廳需要許多文書工作，包括食品安全、消防安全和稅務的執照。"},{"w":"paradox","p":"n.","d":"a statement or situation that seems impossible because it has two opposite facts","c":"悖論；矛盾的情況","s":"It is a paradox that the more free time some people have, the less they seem to get done during the day.","t":"有些人空閒時間越多，一天之中似乎完成得越少，這真是個矛盾的現象。","h":1},{"w":"paradoxical","p":"adj.","d":"seeming impossible or strange because of two opposite facts","c":"似是而非的；矛盾的","s":"It may sound paradoxical, but the fastest way to finish the project is to stop for a short rest and clear your mind.","t":"這聽起來可能矛盾，但完成這個專案最快的方法是停下來短暫休息，讓頭腦清醒。"},{"w":"paradoxically","p":"adv.","d":"in a way that seems impossible or strange","c":"矛盾地；反常地","s":"Paradoxically, the cheapest phone in the shop lasted longer than the expensive one that my brother bought last year.","t":"矛盾的是，店裡最便宜的手機比我哥哥去年買的昂貴手機用得更久。","a":"Paradoxically"},{"w":"contradiction","p":"n.","d":"a difference between two statements or facts so that both cannot be true","c":"矛盾","s":"There is a clear contradiction between what the company says about clean energy and the smoke coming from its factory.","t":"該公司關於清潔能源的說法與其工廠冒出的煙之間存在明顯的矛盾。"},{"w":"paralyze","p":"v.","d":"to make a person unable to move; to stop something from working","c":"使癱瘓；使麻痺","s":"The heavy snow could paralyze the whole city, so the mayor asked people to stay home and keep the roads clear for ambulances.","t":"大雪可能使整個城市癱瘓，所以市長要求民眾待在家裡，讓道路保持暢通給救護車使用。","h":1},{"w":"paralyzed","p":"adj.","d":"unable to move part or all of your body","c":"癱瘓的","s":"After the motorcycle accident, he was paralyzed from the waist down, but he learned to play basketball in a wheelchair.","t":"機車事故後他腰部以下癱瘓，但他學會了坐輪椅打籃球。"},{"w":"paralysis","p":"n.","d":"loss of the ability to move; a state in which nothing can work","c":"癱瘓；麻痺","s":"The strike by bus and train drivers caused total paralysis of public transport in the city for two full days.","t":"公車和火車司機的罷工使該市的大眾運輸完全癱瘓了整整兩天。"},{"w":"be paralyzed with fear","p":"v.phr.","d":"to be so frightened that you cannot move","c":"嚇得動彈不得","s":"When the big dog ran toward her, the little girl was paralyzed with fear and could not even scream for help.","t":"當大狗朝她跑來時，小女孩嚇得動彈不得，甚至無法尖叫求救。","a":"was paralyzed with fear"},{"w":"parliament","p":"n.","d":"the group of people who make the laws of a country","c":"議會；國會","s":"The new law must be passed by parliament before it can take effect, and the vote is expected to take place next month.","t":"新法律必須經國會通過才能生效，預計下個月進行投票。","h":1},{"w":"member of parliament","p":"n.phr.","d":"a person elected to parliament","c":"國會議員","s":"Our neighbor was elected as a member of parliament last year, and now she spends most of the week in the capital.","t":"我們的鄰居去年當選國會議員，現在她一週大部分時間都待在首都。"},{"w":"parliamentary","p":"adj.","d":"connected with parliament","c":"議會的；國會的","s":"The parliamentary election will be held in January, and over a thousand candidates are running for the 113 seats.","t":"國會選舉將在一月舉行，一千多名候選人角逐一百一十三個席次。"},{"w":"congress","p":"n.","d":"the group of people elected to make laws in the US and some other countries","c":"國會","s":"Members of Congress debated the new education bill for two weeks before they finally voted on it last Friday.","t":"國會議員就新的教育法案辯論了兩週，上週五終於進行投票。","a":"Congress"},{"w":"legislator","p":"n.","d":"a member of a group that makes laws","c":"立法者；立法委員","s":"Every legislator in Taiwan is elected for four years, and voters can call them to complain about problems in their area.","t":"台灣每位立法委員的任期為四年，選民可以打電話向他們反映地方上的問題。"},{"w":"pastime","p":"n.","d":"something you enjoy doing in your free time","c":"消遣；娛樂","s":"Fishing is a popular pastime among older men in the village, and they sit by the river for hours every afternoon.","t":"釣魚是村裡年長男性常見的消遣，他們每天下午在河邊坐上好幾個小時。","h":1},{"w":"a favorite pastime","p":"n.phr.","d":"the free-time activity that you like best","c":"最喜歡的消遣","s":"Reading comic books is a favorite pastime of mine, and I have collected more than three hundred of them since junior high.","t":"看漫畫是我最喜歡的消遣，從國中開始我已經收集了三百多本。"},{"w":"hobby","p":"n.","d":"an activity that you do for pleasure in your free time","c":"嗜好","s":"My new hobby is baking bread, and my family says the whole house smells wonderful on Sunday mornings.","t":"我的新嗜好是烤麵包，家人說星期天早上整個屋子都香噴噴的。"},{"w":"leisure","p":"n.","d":"time when you are not working and can relax","c":"閒暇","s":"Most people in the city have very little leisure time during the week, so parks are crowded on Saturday and Sunday.","t":"城市裡大多數人平日幾乎沒有閒暇時間，所以公園在週六和週日都很擁擠。"},{"w":"recreation","p":"n.","d":"activities done for enjoyment when you are not working","c":"休閒娛樂","s":"The new community center offers many kinds of recreation, such as swimming, table tennis, and dance classes for seniors.","t":"新的社區中心提供多種休閒活動，例如游泳、桌球和長者舞蹈課。"},{"w":"patriot","p":"n.","d":"a person who loves their country and is ready to defend it","c":"愛國者","s":"The old soldier was honored as a patriot because he had risked his life many times to protect his homeland.","t":"這位老兵被尊為愛國者，因為他曾多次冒著生命危險保衛家園。","h":1},{"w":"patriotic","p":"adj.","d":"having or showing love for your country","c":"愛國的","s":"The crowd sang patriotic songs and waved flags as the national team walked into the stadium for the opening ceremony.","t":"當國家代表隊走進體育場參加開幕典禮時，群眾高唱愛國歌曲並揮舞國旗。","h":1},{"w":"patriotism","p":"n.","d":"love for your country","c":"愛國心；愛國主義","s":"The teacher explained that true patriotism means caring about the people of your country, not just cheering at sports events.","t":"老師解釋說，真正的愛國心意味著關心國家的人民，而不只是在運動賽事上歡呼。"},{"w":"compatriot","p":"n.","d":"a person from the same country as you","c":"同胞","s":"When she won the gold medal, her compatriots back home stayed up until two in the morning to watch the final race.","t":"當她贏得金牌時，她國內的同胞熬夜到凌晨兩點觀看決賽。","a":"compatriots"},{"w":"nationalism","p":"n.","d":"a strong feeling of pride in your country","c":"民族主義；國家主義","s":"Extreme nationalism can be dangerous, because it may lead people to look down on other countries and their cultures.","t":"極端的民族主義可能很危險，因為它可能使人們看不起其他國家及其文化。"}]},{"unit":27,"theme":"peacock – plow","cards":[{"w":"peacock","p":"n.","d":"a large male bird with long blue and green tail feathers that it can open like a fan","c":"孔雀","s":"When the peacock at the zoo opened its beautiful tail, all the children stopped talking and took out their phones to take pictures.","t":"當動物園裡的孔雀展開牠美麗的尾巴時，所有的孩子都停止說話，拿出手機拍照。","h":1},{"w":"peacock feather","p":"n.phr.","d":"one of the long colorful feathers from a peacock's tail","c":"孔雀羽毛","s":"My aunt keeps a peacock feather in a tall glass vase by the window, and it shines blue and green when the sun comes in.","t":"我阿姨在窗邊的高玻璃花瓶裡插了一根孔雀羽毛，陽光照進來時它會閃著藍綠色的光。"},{"w":"peahen","p":"n.","d":"a female peacock, which is brown and has no long tail","c":"雌孔雀","s":"The peahen is much plainer than the male, so visitors often walk past her without noticing that she is the same kind of bird.","t":"雌孔雀比雄孔雀樸素得多，所以遊客常常走過她身邊，沒注意到她是同一種鳥。"},{"w":"as proud as a peacock","p":"phr.","d":"very proud and pleased with yourself","c":"非常得意；趾高氣揚","s":"After winning the speech contest, Kevin walked around the campus as proud as a peacock and told everyone about his gold medal.","t":"贏得演講比賽後，凱文趾高氣揚地在校園裡走來走去，告訴每個人他得了金牌。"},{"w":"pebble","p":"n.","d":"a small smooth round stone, usually found on a beach or in a river","c":"小圓石；卵石","s":"The little boy picked up a smooth gray pebble from the riverbank and threw it as far as he could into the water.","t":"小男孩從河岸撿起一顆光滑的灰色小圓石，用盡全力把它丟進水裡。","h":1},{"w":"pebble beach","p":"n.phr.","d":"a beach covered with small stones instead of sand","c":"卵石灘","s":"Walking on the pebble beach without shoes hurt our feet, so we put our sandals back on and sat down to watch the waves.","t":"不穿鞋走在卵石灘上很傷腳，所以我們又穿上涼鞋，坐下來看海浪。"},{"w":"stone","p":"n.","d":"a hard solid material found in the ground; a small piece of this material","c":"石頭","s":"The old bridge was built of stone more than two hundred years ago, and farmers still cross it with their carts every morning.","t":"這座老橋是兩百多年前用石頭建造的，農民每天早上仍推著推車過橋。"},{"w":"gravel","p":"n.","d":"small stones used to make paths and roads","c":"碎石；礫石","s":"The path to the cabin is covered with gravel, so you can hear the sound of car tires long before the car arrives.","t":"通往小屋的小路鋪著碎石，所以早在車子抵達前，你就能聽到輪胎的聲音。"},{"w":"peek","p":"v.","d":"to look at something quickly, often secretly or through a small opening","c":"偷看；窺視","s":"Please do not peek at your birthday presents before the party; your father spent a long time wrapping them for you.","t":"請不要在派對前偷看你的生日禮物，你爸爸花了很長時間幫你包裝。","h":1},{"w":"peek","p":"n.","d":"a quick look, often secret","c":"一瞥；偷看","s":"The teacher let us have a quick peek at the test questions, but she took the papers back after thirty seconds.","t":"老師讓我們快速看了一眼考題，但三十秒後她就把考卷收回去了。"},{"w":"sneak a peek","p":"v.phr.","d":"to look at something secretly and quickly","c":"偷偷看一眼","s":"While my sister was in the kitchen, I sneaked a peek at her diary, but I felt so guilty that I closed it right away.","t":"我姐姐在廚房時，我偷偷看了一眼她的日記，但我覺得很愧疚，馬上就把它合上了。","a":"sneaked a peek"},{"w":"peep","p":"v.","d":"to look quickly and secretly at something, especially through a small hole","c":"偷看；窺視","s":"The children peeped through the window to see what their mother was cooking for the New Year dinner.","t":"孩子們透過窗戶偷看媽媽正在為年夜飯煮什麼。","a":"peeped"},{"w":"glance","p":"n.","d":"a quick look","c":"一瞥；匆匆一看","s":"With one glance at the dark sky, my mother decided that we should take an umbrella to the night market.","t":"媽媽朝昏暗的天空看了一眼，就決定我們去夜市應該帶把傘。"},{"w":"pending","p":"adj.","d":"waiting to be decided or finished","c":"待決定的；未決的","s":"Your application for the scholarship is still pending, so please check your email every day for the committee's final decision.","t":"你的獎學金申請仍在審核中，所以請每天查看電子郵件，等候委員會的最終決定。","h":1},{"w":"pending","p":"prep.","d":"while waiting for something to happen","c":"在…之前；直到","s":"The new pool will stay closed pending a safety check by the city, which should be finished by the end of the month.","t":"新泳池將持續關閉直到市政府完成安全檢查，預計月底前完成。"},{"w":"depend on","p":"v.phr.","d":"to need someone or something; to be decided by something","c":"依賴；取決於","s":"Whether we go hiking on Sunday will depend on the weather, because the trail becomes dangerous after heavy rain.","t":"星期天是否去健行將取決於天氣，因為大雨過後步道會變得危險。"},{"w":"dependent","p":"adj.","d":"needing someone or something in order to live or succeed","c":"依賴的；依靠的","s":"Many small farms in the valley are completely dependent on the river, so a dry summer can destroy a whole year of work.","t":"山谷裡許多小農場完全依賴這條河，所以一個乾旱的夏天就可能毀掉一整年的辛勞。"},{"w":"independent","p":"adj.","d":"not needing other people; not controlled by others","c":"獨立的","s":"My grandmother is very independent and still cooks, shops, and takes the bus by herself at the age of eighty-five.","t":"我奶奶非常獨立，八十五歲了還自己煮飯、購物和搭公車。"},{"w":"peninsula","p":"n.","d":"a long piece of land that is surrounded by water on three sides","c":"半島","s":"Hengchun is a peninsula at the southern tip of Taiwan, so you can watch the sun rise over one sea and set over another.","t":"恆春是台灣南端的一個半島，所以你可以看太陽從一片海升起，又落入另一片海。","h":1},{"w":"the Korean Peninsula","p":"n.phr.","d":"the piece of land that includes North and South Korea","c":"朝鮮半島","s":"Our history teacher showed us a map of the Korean Peninsula and explained why it was divided into two countries after the war.","t":"歷史老師給我們看朝鮮半島的地圖，並解釋為什麼戰後它被分成兩個國家。"},{"w":"island","p":"n.","d":"a piece of land that is completely surrounded by water","c":"島","s":"Green Island is a small island off the east coast of Taiwan, and it is famous for its clear water and hot springs.","t":"綠島是台灣東海岸外的一個小島，以清澈的海水和溫泉聞名。"},{"w":"mainland","p":"n.","d":"the main part of a country or continent, not the islands near it","c":"大陸；本土","s":"Fishermen on the small island take a boat to the mainland once a week to sell their fish and buy rice and vegetables.","t":"小島上的漁民每週搭船到本島一次，賣魚並購買米和蔬菜。"},{"w":"perch","p":"v.","d":"(of a bird) to sit on a branch or an edge; to sit on something high or narrow","c":"（鳥）棲息；坐在高處","s":"Every evening, dozens of small birds perch on the electric wires outside our window and sing until the sun goes down.","t":"每天傍晚，數十隻小鳥棲息在我們窗外的電線上，一直唱到太陽下山。","h":1},{"w":"perch","p":"n.","d":"a place where a bird sits; a high place where a person sits","c":"棲木；高處","s":"The parrot flew back to its perch near the window as soon as my brother opened the bag of sunflower seeds.","t":"我哥哥一打開葵花籽的袋子，鸚鵡就飛回窗邊的棲木上。"},{"w":"be perched on","p":"v.phr.","d":"to be placed on top of something high or on the edge of something","c":"坐落於…頂上；位於…邊緣","s":"The old temple is perched on a cliff above the sea, and visitors have to climb three hundred steps to reach it.","t":"這座古廟坐落於海邊的懸崖頂上，遊客必須爬三百級階梯才能到達。","a":"is perched on"},{"w":"perch","p":"n.","d":"a kind of freshwater fish that people often catch and eat","c":"鱸魚","s":"We caught two perch in the lake this morning, and my father cooked them with ginger and soy sauce for lunch.","t":"今天早上我們在湖裡釣到兩條鱸魚，我爸爸中午用薑和醬油把牠們煮了。"},{"w":"peril","p":"n.","d":"serious danger","c":"危險；險境","s":"The small fishing boat was in great peril when the typhoon arrived early, but the coast guard reached it just in time.","t":"颱風提早來襲時，那艘小漁船陷入極大的危險，但海巡隊及時趕到。","h":1},{"w":"in peril","p":"phr.","d":"in serious danger","c":"處於危險中","s":"Many sea turtles are in peril because plastic bags in the ocean look like the jellyfish that they usually eat.","t":"許多海龜處於危險中，因為海洋裡的塑膠袋看起來像牠們平常吃的水母。"},{"w":"perilous","p":"adj.","d":"very dangerous","c":"危險的","s":"The road to the mountain village is perilous in winter, with ice on every curve and no fence between the road and the valley.","t":"通往山村的道路在冬天很危險，每個彎道都有冰，而且路和山谷之間沒有護欄。"},{"w":"endanger","p":"v.","d":"to put someone or something in danger","c":"危及；使遭受危險","s":"Drivers who look at their phones endanger not only themselves but also every person walking or riding near them.","t":"看手機的駕駛不僅危及自己，也危及每一個在附近行走或騎車的人。"},{"w":"at your own peril","p":"phr.","d":"(do something) knowing that you alone take the risk","c":"後果自負","s":"The sign at the beach says that people may swim here at their own peril, because there is no lifeguard on duty after five.","t":"海灘的告示牌寫著民眾可以在這裡游泳但後果自負，因為五點後沒有救生員值班。","a":"at their own peril"},{"w":"perish","p":"v.","d":"to die, especially in a sudden or terrible way; to be destroyed","c":"死亡；喪生；消亡","s":"Thousands of trees will perish if the dry weather continues for another month, so the farmers are praying for rain.","t":"如果乾燥的天氣再持續一個月，成千上萬的樹木將會枯死，所以農民正在祈雨。","h":1},{"w":"perishable","p":"adj.","d":"(of food) likely to go bad quickly","c":"易腐壞的","s":"Milk, fish, and fresh meat are perishable, so put them in the refrigerator as soon as you get home from the market.","t":"牛奶、魚和新鮮的肉是易腐壞的，所以從市場回家後請立刻把它們放進冰箱。"},{"w":"perish the thought","p":"phr.","d":"used to say that you hope something will never happen","c":"但願不會如此；千萬別這麼想","s":"If our team loses the final game tomorrow, perish the thought, the coach says we will still celebrate the great season we had.","t":"如果我們隊明天輸了決賽，但願不會如此，教練說我們仍會慶祝這個精彩的球季。"},{"w":"die out","p":"v.phr.","d":"to disappear completely; to become extinct","c":"滅絕；消失","s":"Many old customs began to die out after television arrived in the village, because families stopped gathering to tell stories.","t":"電視來到村裡後，許多古老的習俗開始消失，因為家人不再聚在一起講故事。"},{"w":"permissible","p":"adj.","d":"allowed by the rules or the law","c":"可允許的；容許的","s":"Using a calculator is permissible in the math exam, but phones and smart watches must be left in your bag outside the room.","t":"數學考試中允許使用計算機，但手機和智慧手錶必須留在教室外的包包裡。","h":1},{"w":"permission","p":"n.","d":"the act of allowing someone to do something","c":"允許；許可","s":"You need written permission from your parents before you can join the three-day camping trip in the mountains next month.","t":"你需要父母的書面許可，才能參加下個月山上的三天露營。"},{"w":"permit","p":"v.","d":"to allow someone to do something","c":"允許；准許","s":"The school does not permit students to leave the campus during lunch, so everyone eats in the classroom or the cafeteria.","t":"學校不允許學生在午餐時間離開校園，所以大家都在教室或餐廳吃飯。"},{"w":"permit","p":"n.","d":"an official paper that allows you to do something","c":"許可證","s":"My uncle had to wait three months for a work permit before he could start his new job at the hotel in Japan.","t":"我叔叔等了三個月才拿到工作許可證，之後才能開始在日本飯店的新工作。"},{"w":"permissive","p":"adj.","d":"allowing people a lot of freedom, especially in a way that others think is too much","c":"寬容的；放任的","s":"Some parents are too permissive and let their children play video games until two in the morning on school nights.","t":"有些父母太放任，讓孩子在上學日的晚上玩電動玩到凌晨兩點。"},{"w":"persevere","p":"v.","d":"to keep trying to do something difficult without giving up","c":"堅持不懈；不屈不撓","s":"Learning to play the violin is hard at first, but if you persevere, you will be able to play a simple song within a year.","t":"學小提琴一開始很難，但如果你堅持不懈，一年內就能拉一首簡單的曲子。","h":1},{"w":"persevere with","p":"v.phr.","d":"to continue doing something difficult","c":"堅持做…","s":"My sister decided to persevere with her English lessons even though she failed the first test, and now she is the best in class.","t":"我姐姐決定堅持她的英文課程，即使第一次考試不及格，現在她是班上最好的。"},{"w":"perseverance","p":"n.","d":"the quality of continuing to try even when something is difficult","c":"毅力；堅持不懈","s":"It took great perseverance for him to finish the marathon with an injured knee, but he crossed the line after six hours.","t":"他帶著受傷的膝蓋跑完馬拉松需要極大的毅力，但六小時後他越過了終點線。"},{"w":"endure","p":"v.","d":"to suffer something painful or difficult for a long time without giving up","c":"忍受；忍耐","s":"The climbers had to endure freezing winds and thin air for five days before they finally reached the top of the mountain.","t":"登山者必須忍受刺骨的寒風和稀薄的空氣五天，才終於登上山頂。"},{"w":"persistence","p":"n.","d":"the quality of continuing to do something even when it is difficult or others say no","c":"堅持；執著","s":"Thanks to her persistence, the young scientist finally got the money for her research after her plan had been refused four times.","t":"由於她的堅持，這位年輕科學家的計畫被拒絕四次後，終於拿到了研究經費。","h":1},{"w":"persistent","p":"adj.","d":"continuing to do something although it is difficult; continuing for a long time","c":"堅持不懈的；持續的","s":"The persistent salesman called our office every morning for two weeks until the manager finally agreed to meet him.","t":"那位鍥而不捨的業務員連續兩週每天早上打電話到我們辦公室，直到經理終於同意見他。","h":1},{"w":"persist","p":"v.","d":"to continue to do something although it is difficult; to continue to exist","c":"堅持；持續存在","s":"If the pain in your back persists for more than a week, you should stop playing basketball and see a doctor.","t":"如果你的背痛持續超過一週，你應該停止打籃球並去看醫生。","a":"persists"},{"w":"persist in","p":"v.phr.","d":"to continue doing something, especially something others do not like","c":"堅持做…（常指不好的事）","s":"Although the teacher warned him twice, Jack persisted in talking during the test and was finally sent out of the room.","t":"雖然老師警告了他兩次，傑克仍堅持在考試中說話，最後被趕出教室。","a":"persisted in"},{"w":"persistently","p":"adv.","d":"in a way that continues for a long time or does not give up","c":"持續地；執著地","s":"The little girl persistently asked her father for a puppy every day for a whole year, and he finally said yes at Christmas.","t":"小女孩整整一年每天不斷地向爸爸要一隻小狗，他終於在聖誕節答應了。"},{"w":"petrol","p":"n.","d":"the liquid fuel used in cars (British English; American English: gas, gasoline)","c":"汽油","s":"The price of petrol went up again this week, so my father has started riding his bicycle to work instead of driving.","t":"這週汽油價格又上漲了，所以我爸爸開始騎腳踏車上班而不開車。","h":1},{"w":"petroleum","p":"n.","d":"the thick oil found under the ground that petrol and plastic are made from","c":"石油","s":"Plastic bags, paint, and many kinds of medicine are made from petroleum, so our daily lives depend on it more than we think.","t":"塑膠袋、油漆和許多種藥品都是由石油製成的，所以我們的日常生活比想像中更依賴它。","h":1},{"w":"petrol station","p":"n.phr.","d":"a place where you buy petrol for a car (= gas station)","c":"加油站","s":"We stopped at a petrol station on the highway to fill up the tank and buy some cold drinks before the long drive home.","t":"我們在高速公路上的一個加油站停下來加滿油，並買了一些冷飲，才開始漫長的回家路程。"},{"w":"gasoline","p":"n.","d":"the liquid fuel used in cars (American English; also 'gas')","c":"汽油","s":"Electric cars do not need any gasoline, which is why so many families are thinking about buying one next year.","t":"電動車不需要任何汽油，這就是為什麼這麼多家庭考慮明年買一輛。"},{"w":"fuel","p":"n.","d":"any material that is burned to produce heat or power","c":"燃料","s":"The airplane carries enough fuel to fly for fourteen hours, which is more than enough for the trip from Taipei to London.","t":"這架飛機載有足夠飛行十四小時的燃料，對從台北到倫敦的航程來說綽綽有餘。"},{"w":"pharmacist","p":"n.","d":"a person whose job is to prepare and sell medicines","c":"藥劑師","s":"The pharmacist explained that I should take one pill after each meal and avoid drinking coffee while I am on this medicine.","t":"藥師解釋說我應該每餐飯後吃一顆藥，並且服藥期間避免喝咖啡。","h":1},{"w":"pharmacy","p":"n.","d":"a shop or a part of a hospital where medicines are prepared and sold","c":"藥局；藥房","s":"After seeing the doctor, you can take this paper to the pharmacy on the first floor, and they will give you the medicine.","t":"看完醫生後，你可以拿這張單子到一樓的藥局，他們會把藥給你。","h":1},{"w":"pharmaceutical","p":"adj.","d":"connected with making and selling medicines","c":"製藥的；藥物的","s":"My cousin works for a large pharmaceutical company that is developing a new medicine for people with heart problems.","t":"我表哥在一家大型製藥公司工作，該公司正在為心臟病患者研發新藥。"},{"w":"drugstore","p":"n.","d":"a shop that sells medicines and also things like soap and shampoo","c":"藥妝店；藥房","s":"There is a drugstore right next to the MRT station where you can buy cold medicine, toothpaste, and even snacks.","t":"捷運站旁邊就有一家藥妝店，你可以在那裡買感冒藥、牙膏，甚至零食。"},{"w":"prescription","p":"n.","d":"a paper from a doctor that says which medicine you should take","c":"處方；藥方","s":"You cannot buy this medicine without a prescription, so you will have to see a doctor first and bring the paper here.","t":"沒有處方箋你不能買這種藥，所以你必須先看醫生，再把單子帶來這裡。"},{"w":"pianist","p":"n.","d":"a person who plays the piano, especially as a job","c":"鋼琴家","s":"The famous pianist began learning the piano at the age of four, and she gave her first concert when she was only nine.","t":"這位著名的鋼琴家四歲開始學琴，九歲時就舉行了第一場音樂會。","h":1},{"w":"piano","p":"n.","d":"a large musical instrument with black and white keys that you press","c":"鋼琴","s":"My parents bought a second-hand piano for my little sister, and now she practices for half an hour every evening.","t":"我父母為我妹妹買了一台二手鋼琴，現在她每天晚上練習半小時。"},{"w":"play the piano","p":"v.phr.","d":"to make music on a piano","c":"彈鋼琴","s":"My grandmother can still play the piano beautifully at the age of eighty, and she plays old songs for us every Sunday.","t":"我奶奶八十歲了仍能把鋼琴彈得很美，每個星期天她都為我們彈老歌。"},{"w":"violinist","p":"n.","d":"a person who plays the violin","c":"小提琴家","s":"The young violinist from Taiwan won first prize at the international music contest in Vienna last month.","t":"來自台灣的年輕小提琴家上個月在維也納的國際音樂比賽中贏得第一名。"},{"w":"musician","p":"n.","d":"a person who plays a musical instrument or writes music","c":"音樂家","s":"Several street musicians play guitars and drums near the night market on weekends, and people stop to listen and give them money.","t":"週末有幾位街頭音樂家在夜市附近彈吉他和打鼓，人們會停下來聆聽並給他們錢。","a":"musicians"},{"w":"pickpocket","p":"n.","d":"a person who steals things from people's pockets or bags in crowded places","c":"扒手","s":"A pickpocket took my wallet on the crowded MRT this morning, and I did not notice until I tried to buy lunch.","t":"今天早上在擁擠的捷運上，一名扒手拿走了我的皮夾，直到我想買午餐時才發現。","h":1},{"w":"pick sb's pocket","p":"v.phr.","d":"to steal something from someone's pocket without them noticing","c":"扒竊某人的口袋","s":"Someone picked his pocket while he was watching the street performance, and his phone and keys were gone.","t":"他在看街頭表演時，有人扒了他的口袋，他的手機和鑰匙都不見了。","a":"picked his pocket"},{"w":"pocket","p":"n.","d":"a small bag sewn into clothes for keeping things in","c":"口袋","s":"I always keep my MRT card in the front pocket of my school bag so that I can find it quickly at the gate.","t":"我總是把捷運卡放在書包的前口袋，這樣在閘門口就能很快找到它。"},{"w":"pocket money","p":"n.phr.","d":"a small amount of money that parents give to children","c":"零用錢","s":"My parents give me five hundred dollars of pocket money every week, and I save half of it to buy a new bicycle.","t":"我父母每週給我五百元零用錢，我存一半要買新腳踏車。"},{"w":"thief","p":"n.","d":"a person who steals things","c":"小偷","s":"The police caught the thief two days later because a camera in the shop had recorded his face very clearly.","t":"警方兩天後抓到了那個小偷，因為店裡的攝影機清楚地拍到了他的臉。"},{"w":"pilgrim","p":"n.","d":"a person who travels a long way to a holy place for religious reasons","c":"朝聖者；香客","s":"Every spring, thousands of pilgrims walk for nine days behind the Mazu statue from Taichung to Chiayi and back.","t":"每年春天，成千上萬的香客跟在媽祖神像後面，從台中走到嘉義再走回來，共九天。","a":"pilgrims","h":1},{"w":"pilgrimage","p":"n.","d":"a journey to a holy place","c":"朝聖之旅","s":"My grandmother went on a pilgrimage to a famous temple in the mountains to pray for my grandfather's health.","t":"我奶奶到山上一座著名的寺廟朝聖，為我爺爺的健康祈福。"},{"w":"make a pilgrimage to","p":"v.phr.","d":"to travel to a holy or special place","c":"前往…朝聖","s":"Many baseball fans make a pilgrimage to the old stadium every year because their favorite team won its first championship there.","t":"許多棒球迷每年都前往那座老球場朝聖，因為他們最喜愛的球隊在那裡贏得了第一座冠軍。"},{"w":"shrine","p":"n.","d":"a holy place where people go to pray, often built for a god or a famous person","c":"神殿；聖地；神社","s":"The small shrine by the road is dedicated to the god of the land, and farmers leave fruit there before the harvest.","t":"路邊的小神祠是供奉土地公的，農民在收成前會在那裡留下水果。"},{"w":"pimple","p":"n.","d":"a small red spot on the skin, especially on the face","c":"青春痘；面皰","s":"Tim woke up with a big pimple on his nose on the morning of the school dance, and he almost decided not to go.","t":"提姆在學校舞會當天早上醒來，鼻子上長了一顆大青春痘，他差點決定不去了。","h":1},{"w":"acne","p":"n.","d":"a skin problem that causes many pimples, common among teenagers","c":"粉刺；痤瘡","s":"Many teenagers have acne, and doctors say that washing your face gently twice a day can help keep the skin clean.","t":"許多青少年有粉刺問題，醫生說每天輕柔地洗臉兩次有助於保持皮膚乾淨。"},{"w":"pimply","p":"adj.","d":"having a lot of pimples","c":"長滿青春痘的","s":"In old photos my father was a thin, pimply teenager, but now he has clear skin and laughs about those years.","t":"在舊照片裡我爸爸是個瘦瘦的、長滿青春痘的少年，但現在他皮膚乾淨，還會笑談那些年。"},{"w":"rash","p":"n.","d":"an area of red spots on the skin, caused by illness or something you touched","c":"疹子；皮疹","s":"After eating the shrimp, she got a red rash on her arms and neck, so her mother took her to the doctor right away.","t":"吃了蝦子之後，她的手臂和脖子上長了紅色的疹子，所以媽媽馬上帶她去看醫生。"},{"w":"pinch","p":"v.","d":"to press someone's skin tightly between your finger and thumb","c":"捏；掐","s":"My little cousin likes to pinch my arm when he wants my attention, and it hurts more than he thinks.","t":"我的小表弟想引起我注意時喜歡捏我的手臂，那比他想像的還痛。","h":1},{"w":"pinch","p":"n.","d":"the act of pinching; a very small amount of something","c":"捏；一撮","s":"She gave her brother a quick pinch on the arm to stop him from laughing during the quiet part of the ceremony.","t":"她在典禮安靜的時刻快速捏了弟弟的手臂一下，阻止他笑出來。"},{"w":"a pinch of salt","p":"n.phr.","d":"a very small amount of salt held between your finger and thumb","c":"一撮鹽","s":"Add a pinch of salt to the soup at the end, and then taste it before you decide whether it needs any more.","t":"最後在湯裡加一撮鹽，然後先嚐一嚐，再決定是否需要再加。"},{"w":"feel the pinch","p":"v.phr.","d":"to have less money than before and find life harder","c":"手頭拮据；感到經濟壓力","s":"Many small restaurants began to feel the pinch when the price of vegetables doubled after the typhoon last month.","t":"上個月颱風過後蔬菜價格翻倍，許多小餐廳開始感到經濟壓力。"},{"w":"plague","p":"n.","d":"a disease that spreads quickly and kills many people; a large number of harmful animals","c":"瘟疫；災害","s":"In the fourteenth century, a terrible plague spread across Europe and killed about one third of the people living there.","t":"十四世紀時，一場可怕的瘟疫席捲歐洲，奪走了當地約三分之一人口的性命。","h":1},{"w":"plague","p":"v.","d":"to cause trouble or pain to someone again and again","c":"使困擾；折磨","s":"Knee problems continued to plague the basketball star for years, and he finally had to leave the team at thirty.","t":"膝蓋問題多年來持續困擾這位籃球明星，他最終在三十歲時不得不離開球隊。"},{"w":"be plagued by","p":"v.phr.","d":"to suffer from something again and again","c":"飽受…之苦","s":"The small town was plagued by floods every summer until the government built a new wall along the river in 2015.","t":"這個小鎮每年夏天都飽受洪水之苦，直到政府在二〇一五年沿河修建了新的堤防。","a":"was plagued by"},{"w":"epidemic","p":"n.","d":"a disease that spreads quickly to many people in an area","c":"流行病；傳染病","s":"During the flu epidemic last winter, the hospital asked visitors to wear masks and wash their hands at the door.","t":"去年冬天流感大流行期間，醫院要求訪客戴口罩並在門口洗手。"},{"w":"plantation","p":"n.","d":"a large farm where crops such as tea, coffee, or sugar are grown","c":"大農場；種植園","s":"We visited a tea plantation in Nantou, where workers pick the leaves by hand and dry them in the sun on the same day.","t":"我們參觀了南投的一座茶園，工人手工採茶，並在當天把茶葉曬乾。","h":1},{"w":"plant","p":"v.","d":"to put seeds or young plants into the ground so that they will grow","c":"種植","s":"Our class will plant thirty trees along the school fence this Friday, and each student will take care of one tree.","t":"這個星期五我們班將沿著學校圍牆種植三十棵樹，每位學生照顧一棵。"},{"w":"plant","p":"n.","d":"a factory or a building where power is produced","c":"工廠；發電廠","s":"The new power plant outside the city uses natural gas instead of coal, so the air has become cleaner this year.","t":"城外新的發電廠使用天然氣而不是煤，所以今年空氣變得更乾淨了。"},{"w":"tea plantation","p":"n.phr.","d":"a large farm where tea is grown","c":"茶園","s":"The hills of Alishan are covered with tea plantations, and the view of the green rows in the morning mist is wonderful.","t":"阿里山的山坡上布滿茶園，清晨薄霧中一排排綠色茶樹的景色美極了。","a":"tea plantations"},{"w":"transplant","p":"v.","d":"to move a plant to a new place; to move an organ into another person's body","c":"移植","s":"The gardener told us to transplant the young tomato plants into bigger pots when they are about ten centimeters tall.","t":"園丁告訴我們，當小番茄苗長到大約十公分高時，要把它們移植到更大的盆子裡。"},{"w":"playwright","p":"n.","d":"a person who writes plays for the theater","c":"劇作家","s":"Shakespeare is the most famous playwright in English history, and his plays are still performed all over the world today.","t":"莎士比亞是英國歷史上最著名的劇作家，他的戲劇至今仍在世界各地上演。","h":1},{"w":"play","p":"n.","d":"a story that is written to be performed by actors in a theater","c":"戲劇；劇本","s":"Our drama club will perform a play about a family during the war, and tickets are free for all students and parents.","t":"我們的戲劇社將演出一齣關於戰時一家人的戲劇，所有學生和家長都可以免費索票。"},{"w":"script","p":"n.","d":"the written words of a play, film, or speech","c":"劇本；腳本","s":"The actors have only two weeks to learn the script, so they practice their lines together every day after school.","t":"演員們只有兩週的時間背劇本，所以他們每天放學後一起練習台詞。"},{"w":"drama","p":"n.","d":"a play for the theater or television; an exciting situation","c":"戲劇；戲劇性事件","s":"My sister wants to study drama at university because she has loved acting since her first school play in grade three.","t":"我姐姐想在大學讀戲劇，因為從三年級第一次演學校話劇起她就熱愛表演。"},{"w":"dramatist","p":"n.","d":"a person who writes plays (= playwright)","c":"劇作家","s":"The young dramatist wrote her first play at nineteen, and it was performed at a small theater in Taipei the following year.","t":"這位年輕的劇作家十九歲時寫了她的第一部劇本，隔年就在台北的一家小劇場上演。"},{"w":"plow","p":"n.","d":"a large farm tool used to turn over the soil before planting","c":"犁","s":"In the old days, farmers pulled the plow with a water buffalo, but now most of them use small machines instead.","t":"從前農民用水牛拉犁，但現在大多數人改用小型機器。","h":1},{"w":"plow","p":"v.","d":"to turn over the soil with a plow","c":"犁（田）；耕","s":"The farmers plow their fields in early spring, and a few weeks later they plant the first rice of the year.","t":"農民在早春犁田，幾週後種下當年的第一批稻子。"},{"w":"plow through","p":"v.phr.","d":"to make slow progress through something difficult or boring","c":"艱難地完成；費力地讀完","s":"I had to plow through three hundred pages of history before the exam, so I stayed in the library until it closed.","t":"考試前我必須費力地讀完三百頁的歷史，所以我在圖書館待到關門。"},{"w":"snowplow","p":"n.","d":"a vehicle or machine that pushes snow off roads","c":"掃雪車；除雪機","s":"After the heavy snow, a snowplow cleared the main road before dawn so that the school buses could run on time.","t":"大雪過後，一輛掃雪車在天亮前清理了主要道路，讓校車能準時行駛。"},{"w":"tractor","p":"n.","d":"a strong vehicle with big wheels used on farms to pull machines","c":"曳引機；拖拉機","s":"My grandfather drives his old red tractor slowly across the field every morning, pulling a cart full of vegetables.","t":"我爺爺每天早上開著他那台舊紅色曳引機慢慢穿過田地，拉著一車滿滿的蔬菜。"}]},{"unit":28,"theme":"pneumonia – proficiency","cards":[{"w":"pneumonia","p":"n.","d":"a serious illness of the lungs that makes breathing difficult","c":"肺炎","s":"My grandfather caught a bad cold last winter, and it turned into pneumonia, so he had to stay in the hospital for two weeks.","t":"我爺爺去年冬天得了重感冒，後來轉成肺炎，所以他必須住院兩週。","h":1},{"w":"lung","p":"n.","d":"one of the two organs in your chest that you breathe with","c":"肺","s":"Smoking damages your lungs little by little, and many smokers do not notice the harm until they are much older.","t":"吸菸會一點一點地損害你的肺，許多吸菸者直到年紀大了才注意到傷害。","a":"lungs"},{"w":"infection","p":"n.","d":"an illness caused by germs entering the body","c":"感染","s":"The doctor said the cut on my hand had a small infection, so she cleaned it carefully and gave me some medicine.","t":"醫生說我手上的傷口有輕微感染，所以她仔細清洗並給了我一些藥。"},{"w":"come down with","p":"v.phr.","d":"to become sick with an illness","c":"染上（疾病）","s":"Half of the class came down with the flu after the field trip, so the teacher had to cancel the test on Friday.","t":"校外教學後班上有一半的人染上流感，所以老師不得不取消星期五的考試。","a":"came down with"},{"w":"polar","p":"adj.","d":"relating to the North or South Pole","c":"極地的","s":"The polar regions are getting warmer every year, and scientists warn that the sea level will rise if the ice keeps melting.","t":"極地地區每年都在變暖，科學家警告如果冰持續融化，海平面將會上升。","h":1},{"w":"polar bear","p":"n.phr.","d":"a large white bear that lives in the Arctic","c":"北極熊","s":"At the zoo, the children watched a polar bear swim under the water, and they were surprised by how fast it moved.","t":"在動物園裡，孩子們看著一隻北極熊在水下游泳，牠的速度之快讓他們很驚訝。"},{"w":"pole","p":"n.","d":"the most northern or southern point of the earth","c":"極；（南／北）極","s":"Few people have ever walked to the South Pole, because the journey across the ice takes weeks in freezing wind.","t":"很少有人曾經走到南極，因為穿越冰原的旅程要在刺骨寒風中花上好幾個星期。","a":"Pole"},{"w":"polar opposite","p":"n.phr.","d":"something that is completely different from another thing","c":"截然相反的人／事物","s":"My twin brother and I are polar opposites: he loves noisy parties, while I would rather stay home with a good book.","t":"我和我的雙胞胎哥哥截然相反：他喜愛熱鬧的派對，而我寧願待在家裡看本好書。","a":"polar opposites"},{"w":"ponder","p":"v.","d":"to think about something carefully for a long time","c":"仔細考慮；沉思","s":"Before you accept the job in another city, you should ponder how the move will affect your family and friends.","t":"在你接受另一個城市的工作之前，你應該仔細考慮搬家會如何影響你的家人和朋友。","h":1},{"w":"ponder over","p":"v.phr.","d":"to think deeply about a question or problem","c":"深思；反覆思量","s":"She pondered over the strange message for hours, but she still could not understand who had sent it or why.","t":"她反覆思量那則奇怪的訊息好幾個小時，但她仍然無法理解是誰寄的，或為什麼。","a":"pondered over"},{"w":"reflect on","p":"v.phr.","d":"to think carefully about something that happened","c":"反思；回想","s":"At the end of each school year, our teacher asks us to reflect on what we have learned and what we want to improve.","t":"每個學年結束時，老師都會要我們反思學到了什麼，以及想要改進什麼。"},{"w":"pony","p":"n.","d":"a small horse","c":"小馬","s":"At the farm, the children took turns riding a gentle brown pony while their parents took photos from the fence.","t":"在農場裡，孩子們輪流騎一匹溫馴的棕色小馬，而他們的父母在柵欄邊拍照。","h":1},{"w":"ponytail","p":"n.","d":"hair tied together at the back of the head","c":"馬尾（髮型）","s":"Before the race, she tied her long hair into a ponytail so that it would not get in her eyes while running.","t":"比賽前，她把長髮綁成馬尾，這樣跑步時頭髮才不會跑進眼睛裡。"},{"w":"horse","p":"n.","d":"a large animal that people ride or use to pull things","c":"馬","s":"My uncle keeps three horses on his farm, and every morning he feeds them before the sun comes up.","t":"我叔叔在他的農場養了三匹馬，每天早上太陽升起前他都會先餵牠們。","a":"horses"},{"w":"populate","p":"v.","d":"to live in an area and fill it with people or animals","c":"居住於；填滿","s":"Thousands of birds populate this small island every spring, and bird lovers travel from far away to watch them.","t":"每年春天有數千隻鳥棲居於這座小島，愛鳥人士從遠方前來觀賞。","h":1},{"w":"population","p":"n.","d":"all the people living in a place","c":"人口","s":"The population of Taipei is over two million, so the MRT is always crowded during the morning rush hour.","t":"台北的人口超過兩百萬，所以早上尖峰時段捷運總是很擠。"},{"w":"populated","p":"adj.","d":"having people living there","c":"有人居住的","s":"The valley is thinly populated, and the nearest hospital is more than an hour away by car on a narrow road.","t":"這個山谷居住的人很少，最近的醫院開車走狹窄的道路要一個多小時。"},{"w":"popular","p":"adj.","d":"liked by many people","c":"受歡迎的","s":"Bubble tea is so popular in Taiwan that you can find a tea shop on almost every busy street corner.","t":"珍珠奶茶在台灣非常受歡迎，幾乎每個熱鬧的街角都能找到一家茶飲店。"},{"w":"overpopulated","p":"adj.","d":"having too many people living in one place","c":"人口過多的","s":"Some big cities are overpopulated, so housing is expensive and the roads are full of cars from morning to night.","t":"有些大城市人口過多，所以房價昂貴，道路從早到晚都塞滿了車。"},{"w":"porter","p":"n.","d":"a person whose job is to carry bags at a station or hotel","c":"行李員；搬運工","s":"When we arrived at the hotel, a friendly porter carried our heavy suitcases up to the room on the fifth floor.","t":"我們抵達飯店時，一位友善的行李員幫我們把沉重的行李箱搬到五樓的房間。","h":1},{"w":"port","p":"n.","d":"a town or area where ships load and unload","c":"港口","s":"Kaohsiung is the largest port in Taiwan, and huge ships from all over the world arrive there every day.","t":"高雄是台灣最大的港口，每天都有來自世界各地的巨大船隻抵達那裡。"},{"w":"portable","p":"adj.","d":"easy to carry or move","c":"便於攜帶的","s":"I bought a portable speaker for the picnic, so we can listen to music by the river without any wires.","t":"我買了一個便於攜帶的喇叭去野餐，這樣我們就能在河邊不用任何電線聽音樂。"},{"w":"transport","p":"v.","d":"to carry people or goods from one place to another","c":"運輸；運送","s":"Trucks transport fresh vegetables from the farms to the city markets before dawn, so everything is ready when the shops open.","t":"卡車在天亮前把新鮮蔬菜從農場運送到城市的市場，所以商店開門時一切都準備好了。"},{"w":"posture","p":"n.","d":"the way you hold your body when sitting or standing","c":"姿勢；姿態","s":"Sitting in front of a computer all day can give you bad posture, so stand up and stretch every hour.","t":"整天坐在電腦前會讓你姿勢不良，所以每小時要站起來伸展一下。","h":1},{"w":"good posture","p":"n.phr.","d":"a straight, healthy way of holding your body","c":"良好的姿勢","s":"Dancers must keep good posture at all times, because the way they hold their backs is part of the beauty of the dance.","t":"舞者必須隨時保持良好的姿勢，因為他們挺直背部的方式是舞蹈美感的一部分。"},{"w":"pose","p":"v.","d":"to sit or stand in a position for a photo or painting","c":"擺姿勢","s":"The whole family had to pose for ten minutes while the photographer fixed the lights and changed the camera.","t":"攝影師調整燈光和更換相機時，全家人必須擺姿勢十分鐘。"},{"w":"position","p":"n.","d":"the place where something is; the way a body is placed","c":"位置；姿勢","s":"Please put the chairs back in their original position after the meeting, so the next class can use the room.","t":"會議後請把椅子放回原來的位置，這樣下一堂課才能使用這間教室。"},{"w":"potent","p":"adj.","d":"very strong and powerful in effect","c":"強效的；有力的","s":"This medicine is very potent, so you must take only one small pill a day and never share it with others.","t":"這種藥非常強效，所以你一天只能吃一顆小藥丸，而且絕不能給別人吃。","h":1},{"w":"potential","p":"n.","d":"the possibility of becoming good or successful","c":"潛力","s":"The coach believes the young swimmer has great potential, and she could win a medal if she trains hard for three years.","t":"教練相信這位年輕泳者有很大的潛力，如果她認真訓練三年，可能會贏得獎牌。"},{"w":"potential","p":"adj.","d":"possible in the future","c":"潛在的；可能的","s":"Before you sign the contract, read every page carefully and look for any potential problems that could cost you money.","t":"簽約前要仔細閱讀每一頁，並找出任何可能讓你損失金錢的潛在問題。"},{"w":"power","p":"n.","d":"the ability to control or do something; electricity","c":"力量；權力；電力","s":"The storm was so strong that the whole town lost power for two days, and people had to use candles at night.","t":"暴風雨太強了，整個鎮電力中斷兩天，人們晚上必須點蠟燭。"},{"w":"powerful","p":"adj.","d":"having great power or strength","c":"強大的","s":"The new engine is twice as powerful as the old one, so the car can climb steep mountain roads with no trouble.","t":"新引擎的動力是舊引擎的兩倍強大，所以這輛車能毫無困難地爬上陡峭的山路。"},{"w":"poultry","p":"n.","d":"birds such as chickens and ducks kept for meat and eggs","c":"家禽","s":"The farmer keeps poultry in a large yard behind the house, and he sells fresh eggs at the market every Sunday.","t":"農夫在屋後的大院子裡養家禽，每個星期天在市場賣新鮮雞蛋。","h":1},{"w":"chicken","p":"n.","d":"a bird kept for its eggs and meat; its meat","c":"雞；雞肉","s":"My mother roasted a whole chicken for dinner, and the smell filled the house long before we sat down to eat.","t":"我媽媽烤了一整隻雞當晚餐，我們坐下來吃之前，香味早就充滿了整間屋子。"},{"w":"livestock","p":"n.","d":"farm animals such as cows, pigs, and sheep","c":"家畜","s":"During the flood, the farmers moved their livestock to higher ground, but some fields of rice were completely destroyed.","t":"水災期間，農民把他們的家畜移到高處，但有些稻田完全被毀了。"},{"w":"preach","p":"v.","d":"to give a religious talk; to tell people how they should behave","c":"講道；說教","s":"Every Sunday morning, the pastor would preach to a small group of villagers in the old church by the river.","t":"每個星期天早上，牧師都會在河邊的老教堂裡對一小群村民講道。","h":1},{"w":"preacher","p":"n.","d":"a person who gives religious talks","c":"傳教士；講道者","s":"The preacher spoke so warmly about kindness that even people who were not religious stayed to listen to the end.","t":"那位講道者談到善良時如此溫暖，連不信教的人也留下來聽到最後。"},{"w":"sermon","p":"n.","d":"a religious talk given in a church","c":"講道；佈道","s":"The sermon lasted almost an hour, and the little boy fell asleep on his mother's shoulder halfway through it.","t":"那場講道持續了近一個小時，小男孩在中途就靠在媽媽肩上睡著了。"},{"w":"practice what you preach","p":"v.phr.","d":"to do the things you tell others to do","c":"言行一致；以身作則","s":"Our teacher always practices what she preaches: she tells us to read every day, and we often see her with a book at lunch.","t":"我們老師總是言行一致：她要我們每天閱讀，而我們常看到她午餐時拿著書。","a":"practices what she preaches"},{"w":"precede","p":"v.","d":"to happen or come before something","c":"在…之前發生；先於","s":"A short video will precede the speech, so please arrive early and turn off your phones before the lights go down.","t":"一段短片將先於演講播放，所以請提早到，並在燈光暗下前關掉手機。","h":1},{"w":"precedent","p":"n.","d":"an earlier event that is used as an example for later ones","c":"先例","s":"The school set a precedent last year by letting students vote on the uniform, so now they expect a vote every year.","t":"學校去年讓學生投票決定制服，開了先例，所以現在他們期待每年都能投票。","h":1},{"w":"preceding","p":"adj.","d":"coming just before","c":"先前的；在前的","s":"Sales this month were much higher than in the preceding month, so the manager gave everyone a small bonus.","t":"這個月的銷售額比前一個月高出許多，所以經理給每個人一點小獎金。"},{"w":"unprecedented","p":"adj.","d":"never having happened before","c":"空前的；前所未有的","s":"The city received an unprecedented amount of rain in one day, and many roads were under water by the evening.","t":"這座城市一天內降下前所未有的雨量，到傍晚許多道路都淹在水裡了。"},{"w":"set a precedent","p":"v.phr.","d":"to do something that becomes an example for the future","c":"開先例","s":"If the boss lets one worker leave early without a reason, it will set a precedent that everyone else will want to follow.","t":"如果老闆讓一位員工無故提早離開，就會開先例，其他所有人都會想跟著做。"},{"w":"precision","p":"n.","d":"the quality of being exact and accurate","c":"精確；準確","s":"Watchmakers work with great precision, because even a tiny mistake can stop a watch from keeping the right time.","t":"製錶師以極高的精確度工作，因為即使是微小的錯誤也會讓手錶無法準確計時。","h":1},{"w":"precise","p":"adj.","d":"exact and correct in every detail","c":"精確的","s":"Please give me the precise time of your arrival, so I can be waiting at the station when your train comes in.","t":"請告訴我你確切的到達時間，這樣你的火車進站時我就能在車站等候。"},{"w":"precisely","p":"adv.","d":"exactly","c":"精確地；正是","s":"The meeting will start at nine o'clock precisely, and the door will be closed to anyone who arrives late.","t":"會議將準九點開始，遲到的人將會被關在門外。"},{"w":"imprecise","p":"adj.","d":"not exact","c":"不精確的","s":"The map was imprecise, so we took the wrong turn twice and arrived at the campsite long after dark.","t":"那張地圖不精確，所以我們轉錯了兩次彎，天黑很久後才到營地。"},{"w":"predecessor","p":"n.","d":"the person who had a job before someone else","c":"前任","s":"The new principal thanked her predecessor for his twenty years of hard work and promised to continue his good programs.","t":"新校長感謝她的前任二十年來的辛勤工作，並承諾繼續推行他的好計畫。","h":1},{"w":"successor","p":"n.","d":"the person who takes a job after someone else","c":"繼任者","s":"Before the old manager retired, he spent two months training his successor so the team would not notice any change.","t":"老經理退休前花了兩個月訓練他的繼任者，這樣團隊才不會感覺到任何改變。"},{"w":"former","p":"adj.","d":"of an earlier time; previous","c":"以前的；前任的","s":"My former English teacher now works at a university, but she still sends our class a card every New Year.","t":"我以前的英文老師現在在一所大學工作，但她每年新年仍會寄卡片給我們班。"},{"w":"prehistoric","p":"adj.","d":"from the time before history was written down","c":"史前的","s":"The museum has prehistoric tools made of stone, which people used to cut meat more than ten thousand years ago.","t":"博物館裡有石頭製成的史前工具，一萬多年前人們用它們來切肉。","h":1},{"w":"historic","p":"adj.","d":"important in history","c":"歷史上重要的","s":"The two leaders shook hands in a historic meeting that ended a war which had lasted for almost thirty years.","t":"兩位領袖在一場歷史性的會議上握手，結束了一場持續近三十年的戰爭。"},{"w":"historical","p":"adj.","d":"connected with the past or the study of history","c":"歷史的","s":"She loves reading historical novels because they show how ordinary people lived hundreds of years ago.","t":"她喜愛閱讀歷史小說，因為它們呈現了幾百年前普通人的生活方式。"},{"w":"history","p":"n.","d":"everything that happened in the past; the study of it","c":"歷史","s":"In history class today, we learned how the first railway in Taiwan was built more than a hundred years ago.","t":"今天歷史課上，我們學到台灣第一條鐵路是如何在一百多年前建造的。"},{"w":"premiere","p":"n.","d":"the first public showing of a film or play","c":"首映；首演","s":"Hundreds of fans waited outside the theater for the film's premiere, hoping to see the stars walk down the red carpet.","t":"數百名影迷在劇院外等待這部電影的首映，希望看到明星走紅地毯。","h":1},{"w":"premiere","p":"v.","d":"to be shown or performed for the first time","c":"首映；首演","s":"The new musical will premiere in Taipei next month, and tickets for the first week have already sold out.","t":"這部新音樂劇下個月將在台北首演，第一週的票已經賣完了。"},{"w":"premier","p":"adj.","d":"best or most important","c":"首要的；最佳的","s":"The hotel calls itself the city's premier place to stay, but the rooms are small and the service is slow.","t":"這家飯店自稱是本市最頂級的住宿地點，但房間很小，服務也很慢。"},{"w":"premier","p":"n.","d":"the head of a government in some countries","c":"總理；首相","s":"The premier promised on television that the government would lower the price of electricity before the summer.","t":"總理在電視上承諾政府將在夏天前降低電價。"},{"w":"preside","p":"v.","d":"to be in charge of a meeting or event","c":"主持；主管","s":"The oldest judge will preside at the trial, and she is known for being strict about time and silence in court.","t":"最資深的法官將主持這場審判，她以嚴格要求法庭上的時間和安靜而聞名。","h":1},{"w":"preside over","p":"v.phr.","d":"to be in charge of a meeting, event, or organization","c":"主持；掌管","s":"The class leader presided over the meeting about the school trip and made sure everyone had a chance to speak.","t":"班長主持了關於校外旅行的會議，並確保每個人都有機會發言。","a":"presided over"},{"w":"president","p":"n.","d":"the leader of a country, company, or club","c":"總統；總裁；會長","s":"The president of the company visited our factory yesterday and thanked the workers for finishing the order early.","t":"公司總裁昨天參觀了我們的工廠，並感謝工人提早完成訂單。"},{"w":"presidential","p":"adj.","d":"relating to a president","c":"總統的","s":"The presidential election will be held in January, so the streets are already full of colorful flags and posters.","t":"總統選舉將在一月舉行，所以街上已經滿是彩色的旗子和海報。"},{"w":"prestige","p":"n.","d":"respect and admiration that someone or something has","c":"聲望；名望","s":"Teaching used to carry great prestige in the village, and parents always invited the teacher to family celebrations.","t":"教師這個職業在村裡曾經享有很高的聲望，家長總是邀請老師參加家庭慶典。","h":1},{"w":"prestigious","p":"adj.","d":"respected and admired as very important or of high quality","c":"有聲望的；享有盛名的","s":"She was accepted by a prestigious university in London, and her whole town celebrated the news with a big dinner.","t":"她被倫敦一所享有盛名的大學錄取，全鎮的人以一場盛大的晚宴慶祝這個消息。"},{"w":"reputation","p":"n.","d":"the opinion people have about someone or something","c":"名聲","s":"The restaurant has a reputation for the best beef noodles in town, so there is always a long line at lunchtime.","t":"這家餐廳有全鎮最好吃牛肉麵的名聲，所以午餐時間總是有長長的隊伍。"},{"w":"preventive","p":"adj.","d":"intended to stop something bad before it happens","c":"預防的","s":"Washing your hands often is a simple preventive measure that keeps many germs from getting into your body.","t":"常洗手是一個簡單的預防措施，能讓許多細菌無法進入你的身體。","h":1},{"w":"prevent","p":"v.","d":"to stop something from happening","c":"預防；防止","s":"A good helmet can prevent serious head injuries, so you should always wear one when you ride a scooter.","t":"一頂好的安全帽可以防止嚴重的頭部傷害，所以騎機車時一定要戴。"},{"w":"prevention","p":"n.","d":"the act of stopping something from happening","c":"預防","s":"The city spends a lot of money on fire prevention, including free smoke alarms for every old apartment building.","t":"這座城市花很多錢在火災預防上，包括為每棟老公寓免費提供煙霧警報器。"},{"w":"preventable","p":"adj.","d":"able to be stopped before it happens","c":"可預防的","s":"Many traffic accidents are preventable, and most of them happen because drivers look at their phones instead of the road.","t":"許多交通事故是可預防的，大多數是因為駕駛看手機而不看路才發生的。"},{"w":"preview","p":"n.","d":"a chance to see something before it is shown to the public","c":"預覽；預展；試映","s":"We were invited to a special preview of the new exhibition, two days before it opened to the general public.","t":"我們受邀參加新展覽的特別預展，比對一般大眾開放早了兩天。","h":1},{"w":"preview","p":"v.","d":"to see or show something before it is shown to others","c":"預覽；預先觀看","s":"Teachers can preview the new textbook online this month, and they should send their comments to the publisher by May.","t":"老師們這個月可以在線上預覽新教科書，並應在五月前把意見寄給出版社。"},{"w":"view","p":"v.","d":"to look at something, especially from a distance","c":"觀看；眺望","s":"From the top of the mountain, you can view the whole city, and at night the lights look like a sea of stars.","t":"從山頂你可以眺望整座城市，夜晚的燈光看起來像一片星海。"},{"w":"review","p":"n.","d":"a report that gives an opinion about a book, film, or product","c":"評論","s":"The movie got a bad review in the newspaper, but my friends and I enjoyed it a lot anyway.","t":"這部電影在報紙上得到一篇負面評論，但我和朋友們還是看得很開心。"},{"w":"sneak preview","p":"n.phr.","d":"a chance to see a small part of something before it is released","c":"先睹為快；搶先看","s":"The game company gave fans a sneak preview of the new characters, and the short video was shared millions of times online.","t":"遊戲公司讓粉絲搶先看新角色，那段短片在網路上被分享了數百萬次。"},{"w":"priceless","p":"adj.","d":"so valuable that no price can be given; extremely important","c":"無價的；極珍貴的","s":"The old photo of my grandparents' wedding is priceless to our family, so we keep it in a safe box.","t":"我祖父母婚禮的老照片對我們家來說是無價的，所以我們把它放在保險箱裡。","h":1},{"w":"price","p":"n.","d":"the amount of money you pay for something","c":"價格","s":"The price of eggs went up again this month, and many families are buying fewer of them than before.","t":"這個月雞蛋的價格又上漲了，許多家庭買的比以前少。"},{"w":"pricey","p":"adj.","d":"expensive","c":"昂貴的","s":"The new phone looks great, but it is a bit pricey for a student, so I will wait for a sale.","t":"新手機看起來很棒，但對學生來說有點貴，所以我會等特價。"},{"w":"at any price","p":"phr.","d":"whatever it costs; no matter what","c":"不惜任何代價","s":"The team wanted to win the championship at any price, so the players trained in the heat all summer.","t":"這支球隊想不惜任何代價贏得冠軍，所以球員們整個夏天都在酷熱中訓練。"},{"w":"privatize","p":"v.","d":"to sell a company or service owned by the government to private owners","c":"使私有化；民營化","s":"The government decided to privatize the national airline, and a large company bought it for several billion dollars.","t":"政府決定將國家航空公司民營化，一家大公司以數十億元買下了它。","h":1},{"w":"private","p":"adj.","d":"for one person or group only; not public","c":"私人的；私密的","s":"This is a private beach that belongs to the hotel, so only guests are allowed to swim here.","t":"這是屬於飯店的私人海灘，所以只有住客可以在這裡游泳。"},{"w":"privacy","p":"n.","d":"the state of being alone and not watched by others","c":"隱私","s":"Teenagers need some privacy, so my parents always knock before they come into my room.","t":"青少年需要一些隱私，所以我爸媽進我房間前總是會先敲門。"},{"w":"privatization","p":"n.","d":"the act of selling a public company to private owners","c":"私有化；民營化","s":"Many workers protested against the privatization of the railway because they were afraid of losing their jobs.","t":"許多工人抗議鐵路民營化，因為他們害怕失去工作。"},{"w":"in private","p":"phr.","d":"with no other people present","c":"私下地","s":"The coach asked to speak to the player in private because he did not want to embarrass him in front of the team.","t":"教練要求和那位球員私下談，因為他不想在全隊面前讓他難堪。"},{"w":"probe","p":"n.","d":"a careful investigation; a spacecraft that explores space","c":"調查；探測器","s":"The space probe sent back clear pictures of the planet's surface after traveling for more than seven years.","t":"這台太空探測器在航行超過七年後，傳回了這顆行星表面的清晰照片。","h":1},{"w":"probe","p":"v.","d":"to ask many questions to find out hidden information","c":"探究；追問","s":"The reporter continued to probe into the company's spending, even though the manager refused to answer any questions.","t":"儘管經理拒絕回答任何問題，記者仍繼續探查公司的開支。"},{"w":"probe into","p":"v.phr.","d":"to investigate something carefully","c":"深入調查","s":"The police probed into the fire for weeks before they found out that it had started in the kitchen.","t":"警方深入調查這場火災好幾週，才查出火是從廚房開始的。","a":"probed into"},{"w":"investigate","p":"v.","d":"to try to find out the truth about something","c":"調查","s":"The teacher promised to investigate who had written on the wall, and she asked every student to tell the truth.","t":"老師承諾要調查是誰在牆上寫字，並要求每個學生說實話。"},{"w":"procession","p":"n.","d":"a line of people or vehicles moving slowly as part of a ceremony","c":"隊伍；遊行行列","s":"A long procession of dancers and drummers moved slowly through the streets during the temple festival last night.","t":"昨晚廟會期間，一列長長的舞者和鼓手隊伍緩慢地穿過街道。","h":1},{"w":"proceed","p":"v.","d":"to continue doing something; to move forward","c":"繼續進行；前進","s":"After the fire alarm turned out to be a mistake, the teacher told us to proceed with the test.","t":"火警警報後來證實是誤報，老師要我們繼續進行考試。"},{"w":"proceed to","p":"v.phr.","d":"to go on to do the next thing","c":"接著做…；前往","s":"Once you finish the first part of the form, proceed to the second page and sign your name at the bottom.","t":"一旦你填完表格的第一部分，就接著到第二頁，並在底部簽名。"},{"w":"process","p":"n.","d":"a series of actions done to achieve a result","c":"過程","s":"Learning a language is a slow process, and you should not feel bad when you make mistakes along the way.","t":"學習語言是一個緩慢的過程，你不應該因為一路上犯錯而感到難過。"},{"w":"procedure","p":"n.","d":"the correct or official way of doing something","c":"程序；步驟","s":"Please follow the safety procedure before you use the machine, and ask the teacher if any step is unclear.","t":"使用機器前請遵守安全程序，如果任何步驟不清楚就問老師。"},{"w":"proficiency","p":"n.","d":"a high level of skill in doing something","c":"熟練；精通","s":"Students must show proficiency in English before they can join the exchange program in Canada next year.","t":"學生必須證明自己英文熟練，才能參加明年在加拿大的交換計畫。","h":1},{"w":"proficient","p":"adj.","d":"skilled and able to do something well","c":"熟練的；精通的","s":"After living in Japan for five years, my cousin became proficient in Japanese and now works as a translator.","t":"在日本住了五年後，我表哥的日文變得很熟練，現在是一名翻譯。"},{"w":"be proficient in","p":"v.phr.","d":"to be very skilled at something","c":"精通於…","s":"Our new assistant is proficient in three languages, so she handles all the emails from our customers in Europe.","t":"我們的新助理精通三種語言，所以她處理所有歐洲客戶的電子郵件。","a":"is proficient in"},{"w":"skillful","p":"adj.","d":"good at doing something","c":"熟練的；靈巧的","s":"The skillful driver turned the bus around on the narrow mountain road without touching the wall on either side.","t":"那位技術熟練的駕駛在狹窄的山路上把公車調頭，兩側的牆都沒碰到。"}]},{"unit":29,"theme":"prohibition – rap","cards":[{"w":"prohibition","p":"n.","d":"the act of not allowing something by law or rule","c":"禁止；禁令","s":"The prohibition of smoking in restaurants has made eating out much more pleasant for families with small children.","t":"餐廳禁止吸菸讓有小孩的家庭外出用餐愉快多了。","h":1},{"w":"prohibit","p":"v.","d":"to not allow something, especially by law","c":"禁止","s":"The school rules prohibit students from using their phones during class, but they may use them at lunch.","t":"校規禁止學生上課時使用手機，但午餐時可以用。"},{"w":"prohibited","p":"adj.","d":"not allowed","c":"被禁止的","s":"Fishing is prohibited in this part of the river, because the government wants to protect the young fish in spring.","t":"這段河流禁止釣魚，因為政府想在春天保護幼魚。"},{"w":"forbid, forbade, forbidden","p":"v.","d":"to order someone not to do something","c":"禁止；不准","s":"My parents forbade me to ride my bike on the main road until I had learned the traffic rules well.","t":"我爸媽不准我在大馬路上騎腳踏車，直到我把交通規則學好。","a":"forbade"},{"w":"ban","p":"n.","d":"an official rule that says something is not allowed","c":"禁令","s":"The city put a ban on plastic straws last year, so most drink shops now give customers paper ones.","t":"這座城市去年對塑膠吸管下了禁令，所以現在大多數飲料店給顧客紙吸管。"},{"w":"propel","p":"v.","d":"to push or drive something forward","c":"推進；推動","s":"Strong winds propelled the small boat across the lake so quickly that we reached the other side in ten minutes.","t":"強風推動小船穿過湖面，速度快到我們十分鐘就到了對岸。","a":"propelled","h":1},{"w":"propeller","p":"n.","d":"a set of turning blades that moves a boat or plane","c":"螺旋槳","s":"The old plane still has a propeller on its nose, and it spins so fast that you cannot see the blades.","t":"那架老飛機的機鼻上仍有一個螺旋槳，它轉得快到你看不見葉片。"},{"w":"launch","p":"v.","d":"to send a rocket into the sky; to start selling something new","c":"發射；推出","s":"The company will launch its new phone next month, and thousands of fans have already ordered it online.","t":"這家公司下個月將推出新手機，已經有數千名粉絲在線上訂購了。"},{"w":"prose","p":"n.","d":"ordinary written language, not poetry","c":"散文","s":"The writer is famous for her clear and simple prose, which even young readers can enjoy without a dictionary.","t":"這位作家以清楚簡單的散文聞名，連年輕讀者不用字典也能享受。","h":1},{"w":"poetry","p":"n.","d":"poems in general","c":"詩（總稱）","s":"Our English teacher reads a little poetry to us every Friday, and some students have started writing their own poems.","t":"我們的英文老師每個星期五讀一點詩給我們聽，有些學生已經開始寫自己的詩了。"},{"w":"essay","p":"n.","d":"a short piece of writing about one subject","c":"文章；論說文","s":"For homework, we have to write a two-page essay about a person who has changed our lives in some way.","t":"回家作業是寫一篇兩頁的文章，談一位以某種方式改變我們人生的人。"},{"w":"literature","p":"n.","d":"books, poems, and plays that are considered to be art","c":"文學","s":"She decided to study English literature at university because she has loved reading novels since she was a child.","t":"她決定在大學讀英國文學，因為她從小就熱愛閱讀小說。"},{"w":"prosecute","p":"v.","d":"to officially accuse someone of a crime in a court","c":"起訴；檢控","s":"The police have enough evidence to prosecute the man who stole money from three old people in our neighborhood.","t":"警方有足夠的證據起訴那個從我們社區三位老人那裡偷錢的男子。","h":1},{"w":"prosecution","p":"n.","d":"the act of taking someone to court; the lawyers who do this","c":"起訴；檢方","s":"The prosecution showed the video from the store camera, and everyone in the court could see the man take the bag.","t":"檢方播放了商店監視器的影片，法庭上每個人都能看到那名男子拿走包包。"},{"w":"prosecutor","p":"n.","d":"a lawyer who tries to prove that someone is guilty","c":"檢察官","s":"The prosecutor asked the driver why he had not stopped after the accident, but the driver refused to answer.","t":"檢察官問那位駕駛為什麼事故後沒有停車，但駕駛拒絕回答。"},{"w":"sue","p":"v.","d":"to take legal action against someone to get money","c":"控告；提告","s":"The customer decided to sue the restaurant after she became seriously ill from eating its undercooked chicken.","t":"那位顧客吃了餐廳沒煮熟的雞肉後病得很重，決定控告這家餐廳。"},{"w":"prospective","p":"adj.","d":"likely to become or do something in the future","c":"預期的；未來的；可能的","s":"The university invites prospective students to visit the campus in March so they can see the classrooms and talk to teachers.","t":"大學邀請未來可能入學的學生三月參觀校園，讓他們看看教室並和老師交談。","h":1},{"w":"prospect","p":"n.","d":"the possibility that something good will happen","c":"前景；可能性","s":"The prospect of a long holiday at the beach kept me working hard through the last busy week of the term.","t":"到海邊長假的前景讓我在學期最後忙碌的一週努力工作。"},{"w":"prospects","p":"n.","d":"chances of being successful in the future","c":"前途；發展機會","s":"Learning a second language can improve your job prospects, because many companies now do business with other countries.","t":"學第二種語言可以改善你的工作前途，因為現在許多公司都與其他國家做生意。"},{"w":"prospective buyer","p":"n.phr.","d":"a person who may buy something","c":"潛在買家","s":"Several prospective buyers came to look at the house on Sunday, and two of them said they would make an offer.","t":"星期天有幾位潛在買家來看房子，其中兩位說他們會出價。","a":"prospective buyers"},{"w":"prototype","p":"n.","d":"the first model of something new, used for testing","c":"原型；樣機","s":"The engineers built a prototype of the electric bicycle and tested it on the hills for a month before selling it.","t":"工程師製作了電動腳踏車的原型，並在山路上測試一個月後才販售。","h":1},{"w":"type","p":"n.","d":"a kind or group of things with the same features","c":"種類；類型","s":"What type of music do you like best, and do you ever listen to songs in languages you do not understand?","t":"你最喜歡哪一類音樂？你會聽自己聽不懂的語言的歌嗎？"},{"w":"typical","p":"adj.","d":"having the usual features of a kind of thing","c":"典型的","s":"A typical Taiwanese breakfast includes soy milk and a warm egg pancake, which you can buy at almost any corner shop.","t":"典型的台灣早餐包括豆漿和溫熱的蛋餅，幾乎在任何街角的店都能買到。"},{"w":"model","p":"n.","d":"a small copy of something; a particular design of a product","c":"模型；型號","s":"My little brother spent the whole weekend building a model of a ship, and he painted every tiny window by hand.","t":"我弟弟整個週末都在組一艘船的模型，每一扇小窗戶都是他親手上色的。"},{"w":"proverb","p":"n.","d":"a short well-known saying that gives advice","c":"諺語；格言","s":"My grandmother loves the proverb \"Practice makes perfect,\" and she repeats it whenever I complain about piano lessons.","t":"我奶奶最愛「熟能生巧」這句諺語，每當我抱怨鋼琴課時她就會重複這句話。","h":1},{"w":"saying","p":"n.","d":"a well-known phrase that gives advice or shows what is true","c":"俗話；格言","s":"There is an old saying that the early bird catches the worm, which means people who start early get the best chances.","t":"有句古老的俗話說早起的鳥兒有蟲吃，意思是早開始的人能得到最好的機會。"},{"w":"motto","p":"n.","d":"a short sentence that expresses a belief or goal","c":"座右銘；校訓","s":"Our school motto is \"Never give up,\" and it is painted in big letters above the front door.","t":"我們學校的校訓是「永不放棄」，它以大字漆在正門上方。"},{"w":"wisdom","p":"n.","d":"the ability to make good decisions because of knowledge and experience","c":"智慧","s":"Old proverbs carry the wisdom of many generations, and that is why people still repeat them hundreds of years later.","t":"古老的諺語承載著許多世代的智慧，這就是為什麼幾百年後人們仍在傳誦它們。"},{"w":"provincial","p":"adj.","d":"connected with a province; of the countryside rather than the capital","c":"省的；地方的","s":"The provincial government has promised to build a new hospital in the small town, since the nearest one is two hours away.","t":"省政府承諾在那個小鎮建一座新醫院，因為最近的醫院距離兩小時。","h":1},{"w":"province","p":"n.","d":"one of the large areas that some countries are divided into","c":"省","s":"Canada is divided into ten provinces, and each one has its own government that decides about schools and hospitals.","t":"加拿大分成十個省，每個省都有自己的政府，決定學校和醫院的事務。","a":"provinces"},{"w":"provincial","p":"adj.","d":"narrow-minded; not interested in new ideas","c":"眼光狹隘的；偏狹的","s":"Some people in the village have rather provincial views, and they are not interested in anything that happens outside their town.","t":"村裡有些人的觀念相當狹隘，對鎮外發生的任何事都不感興趣。"},{"w":"local","p":"adj.","d":"relating to a particular area where you live","c":"當地的","s":"We bought fresh fruit from a local farmer at the market, and it tasted much better than the fruit from the supermarket.","t":"我們在市場向一位當地的農民買了新鮮水果，味道比超市的水果好多了。"},{"w":"provisional","p":"adj.","d":"arranged for the present time only and likely to change","c":"臨時的；暫時的","s":"The new teacher has a provisional contract for one year, and the school will decide in June whether to keep her.","t":"新老師有一份為期一年的臨時合約，學校會在六月決定是否留任她。","h":1},{"w":"provision","p":"n.","d":"the act of providing something; a condition in an agreement","c":"提供；條款","s":"The provision of free lunches has helped many poor children in the mountain schools pay more attention in class.","t":"提供免費午餐幫助了山區學校許多貧困的孩子更專心上課。"},{"w":"provide","p":"v.","d":"to give someone something they need","c":"提供","s":"The hotel will provide free breakfast for all guests, and you can also borrow a bicycle to ride around the lake.","t":"飯店將為所有住客提供免費早餐，你也可以借腳踏車環湖騎。"},{"w":"temporary","p":"adj.","d":"lasting only a short time","c":"暫時的；臨時的","s":"After the earthquake, the families lived in temporary houses made of wood until their own homes were rebuilt.","t":"地震後，這些家庭住在木造的臨時房屋裡，直到他們自己的家重建完成。"},{"w":"psychiatry","p":"n.","d":"the branch of medicine that treats mental illness","c":"精神病學；精神醫學","s":"After six years of medical school, she chose to study psychiatry because she wanted to help people with mental illness.","t":"醫學院六年後，她選擇研讀精神醫學，因為她想幫助有心理疾病的人。","h":1},{"w":"psychiatrist","p":"n.","d":"a doctor who treats mental illness","c":"精神科醫師","s":"The psychiatrist talked with the patient for an hour and then decided which medicine would help him sleep better.","t":"精神科醫師和病人談了一個小時，然後決定哪種藥能幫助他睡得更好。"},{"w":"psychology","p":"n.","d":"the study of the mind and how people behave","c":"心理學","s":"Many students take psychology classes because they want to understand why people act the way they do.","t":"許多學生修心理學課程，因為他們想了解人們為什麼會那樣行動。"},{"w":"psychologist","p":"n.","d":"a person who studies the mind and behavior","c":"心理學家；心理師","s":"The school psychologist helps students who feel too worried about exams, and she teaches them simple ways to relax.","t":"學校心理師幫助對考試過度焦慮的學生，並教他們簡單的放鬆方法。"},{"w":"psychic","p":"adj.","d":"connected with strange powers of the mind, such as knowing the future","c":"通靈的；有超能力的","s":"The woman claimed to have psychic powers and said she could tell people what would happen to them next year.","t":"那位女士聲稱擁有通靈能力，並說她能告訴人們明年會發生什麼事。","h":1},{"w":"psychic","p":"n.","d":"a person who claims to have special mental powers","c":"通靈者；靈媒","s":"My aunt paid a psychic to tell her future, but nothing the woman said has come true so far.","t":"我阿姨付錢請一位靈媒預測她的未來，但那位女士說的到目前為止都沒有成真。"},{"w":"psychological","p":"adj.","d":"connected with the mind and how it works","c":"心理的","s":"Losing the final game had a strong psychological effect on the team, and several players felt sad for weeks.","t":"輸掉決賽對球隊造成強烈的心理影響，有幾位球員難過了好幾個星期。"},{"w":"mental","p":"adj.","d":"relating to the mind","c":"心智的；精神的","s":"Doing puzzles and reading every day can keep your mental skills sharp, even when you grow old.","t":"每天做益智遊戲和閱讀可以讓你的心智能力保持敏銳，即使年紀大了也一樣。"},{"w":"psychotherapy","p":"n.","d":"the treatment of mental problems by talking with a trained person","c":"心理治療","s":"After the accident, he went for psychotherapy once a week, and talking about his fear slowly helped him drive again.","t":"事故後他每週接受一次心理治療，談論自己的恐懼慢慢幫助他重新開車。","h":1},{"w":"therapy","p":"n.","d":"treatment for an illness or problem, often without medicine","c":"治療；療法","s":"The doctor suggested physical therapy for my knee, so I do special exercises with a trainer twice a week.","t":"醫生建議我的膝蓋做物理治療，所以我每週兩次和訓練員做特別的運動。"},{"w":"therapist","p":"n.","d":"a person trained to give therapy","c":"治療師","s":"The speech therapist worked with the little boy for a year, and now he can say every sound clearly.","t":"語言治療師和小男孩一起練習了一年，現在他每個音都能說得很清楚。"},{"w":"counseling","p":"n.","d":"professional advice given to help someone with problems","c":"諮商；輔導","s":"The school offers free counseling to students who feel stressed, and they can book a time online.","t":"學校為感到壓力的學生提供免費諮商，他們可以在線上預約時間。"},{"w":"publicize","p":"v.","d":"to make something known to the public","c":"宣傳；公布","s":"The club used posters and social media to publicize the charity concert, and all the tickets were sold within a week.","t":"社團用海報和社群媒體宣傳慈善音樂會，所有的票在一週內賣完。","h":1},{"w":"public","p":"adj.","d":"for everyone to use; known to all people","c":"公共的；公立的；公開的","s":"The new public library opens at eight in the morning, and anyone with an ID card can borrow up to ten books.","t":"新的公立圖書館早上八點開門，任何有身分證的人最多可以借十本書。"},{"w":"publicity","p":"n.","d":"attention given to something by newspapers, TV, and the internet","c":"宣傳；關注","s":"The small bakery got a lot of free publicity after a famous singer posted a photo of its bread online.","t":"一位知名歌手在網路上張貼了這家小麵包店麵包的照片後，它得到許多免費宣傳。"},{"w":"publish","p":"v.","d":"to print a book or article and make it available to people","c":"出版；發表","s":"The company plans to publish her first novel in September, and the author is already working on the second one.","t":"這家公司計畫在九月出版她的第一本小說，而作者已經在寫第二本了。"},{"w":"in public","p":"phr.","d":"where other people can see or hear","c":"公開地；當眾","s":"My brother hates singing in public, but at home he sings loudly in the shower every single morning.","t":"我哥哥討厭當眾唱歌，但在家裡他每天早上都在淋浴時大聲唱。"},{"w":"puff","p":"n.","d":"a small amount of air, smoke, or wind that is blown","c":"一陣（風、煙）；一股","s":"A puff of smoke came out of the old car's engine, and the driver quickly pulled over to the side of the road.","t":"老車的引擎冒出一股煙，駕駛迅速把車靠邊停。","h":1},{"w":"puff","p":"v.","d":"to breathe fast and loudly after running or hard work","c":"喘氣","s":"After climbing ten floors of stairs, my uncle had to stop and puff for a few minutes before he could speak.","t":"爬了十層樓梯後，我叔叔必須停下來喘氣幾分鐘才能說話。"},{"w":"puff out","p":"v.phr.","d":"to make something bigger by filling it with air","c":"鼓起；吹脹","s":"The little boy puffed out his cheeks and blew as hard as he could, but the balloon did not get any bigger.","t":"小男孩鼓起臉頰用盡全力吹，但氣球一點也沒變大。","a":"puffed out"},{"w":"puffy","p":"adj.","d":"swollen and larger than usual","c":"腫起的；浮腫的","s":"Her eyes were red and puffy the next morning because she had cried for hours after watching the sad movie.","t":"她第二天早上眼睛又紅又腫，因為看完那部悲傷的電影後她哭了好幾個小時。"},{"w":"punctual","p":"adj.","d":"arriving or doing something at the right time; not late","c":"準時的","s":"Our bus driver is always punctual, so if you arrive at the stop one minute late, you will miss the bus.","t":"我們的公車司機總是很準時，所以如果你晚一分鐘到站牌，就會錯過公車。","h":1},{"w":"punctuality","p":"n.","d":"the habit of being on time","c":"守時","s":"The boss praised her punctuality, because in three years she had never once come to work late.","t":"老闆稱讚她的守時，因為三年來她從未遲到過一次。"},{"w":"punctually","p":"adv.","d":"at the exact time","c":"準時地","s":"The train left punctually at seven, and two students who were still buying breakfast had to wait for the next one.","t":"火車準時七點出發，兩個還在買早餐的學生必須等下一班。"},{"w":"on time","p":"phr.","d":"not late; at the planned time","c":"準時","s":"If you want to finish the project on time, you should start working on it today instead of next week.","t":"如果你想準時完成這個專案，就應該今天開始做，而不是下週。"},{"w":"purify","p":"v.","d":"to remove dirty or harmful things from something","c":"淨化；使純淨","s":"This machine can purify river water in a few minutes, so people in the village can drink it safely.","t":"這台機器幾分鐘就能淨化河水，所以村民可以安全地飲用。","h":1},{"w":"purity","p":"n.","d":"the state of being clean, pure, or not mixed with anything else","c":"純淨；純度","s":"The purity of the mountain air surprised us, and every breath felt cool and clean after weeks in the city.","t":"山上空氣的純淨讓我們驚訝，在城市待了幾週後，每一口呼吸都感覺清涼乾淨。","h":1},{"w":"pure","p":"adj.","d":"not mixed with anything else; clean","c":"純的；純淨的","s":"The ring is made of pure gold, so it was far more expensive than the ones with silver mixed in.","t":"這枚戒指是純金製成的，所以比那些混了銀的戒指貴得多。"},{"w":"purely","p":"adv.","d":"only; completely","c":"純粹地；僅僅","s":"We met at the airport purely by chance, and now we have been best friends for more than ten years.","t":"我們純粹是偶然在機場相遇的，現在我們已經是十多年的好朋友了。"},{"w":"purification","p":"n.","d":"the process of making something clean and pure","c":"淨化","s":"Water purification is the first step at the factory, because even a little dirt can spoil the whole batch of juice.","t":"水的淨化是工廠的第一步，因為即使一點點髒東西也會毀掉整批果汁。"},{"w":"impure","p":"adj.","d":"not pure; mixed with something dirty or bad","c":"不純的；有雜質的","s":"The water from the old well was impure, so the villagers boiled it for ten minutes before drinking it.","t":"老井的水不純淨，所以村民喝之前把它煮沸十分鐘。"},{"w":"quake","p":"v.","d":"to shake because of fear or cold","c":"顫抖；發抖","s":"The little dog began to quake with fear when the thunder started, so I held him until the storm passed.","t":"打雷開始時小狗嚇得發抖，所以我抱著牠直到暴風雨過去。","h":1},{"w":"quake","p":"n.","d":"an earthquake","c":"地震","s":"A strong quake shook the city at three in the morning, and many people ran out of their homes in their pajamas.","t":"凌晨三點一場強烈的地震搖撼了這座城市，許多人穿著睡衣跑出家門。"},{"w":"earthquake","p":"n.","d":"a sudden shaking of the ground","c":"地震","s":"Taiwan has many earthquakes every year, so all new buildings must be strong enough to stand through heavy shaking.","t":"台灣每年有許多地震，所以所有新建築都必須堅固到足以承受劇烈搖晃。","a":"earthquakes"},{"w":"shake, shook, shaken","p":"v.","d":"to move quickly up and down or from side to side","c":"搖動；震動","s":"The whole house began to shake when the big truck drove past, and a picture fell off the wall.","t":"大卡車經過時整棟房子開始搖晃，一幅畫從牆上掉了下來。","a":"shake"},{"w":"qualification","p":"n.","d":"an exam you have passed or a skill you have that makes you suitable for a job","c":"資格；資歷","s":"You need a teaching qualification before you can work at a public school, even if you speak English perfectly.","t":"你需要教師資格才能在公立學校工作，即使你的英文說得很完美。","h":1},{"w":"qualify","p":"v.","d":"to have the right skills or pass the exam needed for something","c":"取得資格；有資格","s":"Our team must win two more games to qualify for the national finals, which will be held in Kaohsiung in May.","t":"我們的球隊必須再贏兩場才能取得五月在高雄舉行的全國決賽資格。"},{"w":"qualified","p":"adj.","d":"having the skills or training needed","c":"合格的；有資格的","s":"Only a qualified electrician should fix the wiring in your house, because a small mistake could start a fire.","t":"只有合格的電工才應該修理你家的電線，因為一個小錯誤可能引發火災。"},{"w":"be qualified for","p":"v.phr.","d":"to have the right skills or experience for a job","c":"有資格做…","s":"She is qualified for the manager's job because she has worked in the store for ten years and knows every customer.","t":"她有資格擔任經理這份工作，因為她在店裡工作了十年，認識每一位顧客。","a":"is qualified for"},{"w":"disqualify","p":"v.","d":"to stop someone from taking part because they broke a rule","c":"取消…的資格","s":"The judges had to disqualify the runner because he started before the signal and pushed another athlete.","t":"裁判必須取消那位跑者的資格，因為他在信號前起跑，還推了另一位選手。"},{"w":"radiant","p":"adj.","d":"showing great happiness; shining brightly","c":"容光煥發的；光芒四射的","s":"The bride looked radiant as she walked into the garden, and her smile made everyone at the wedding smile too.","t":"新娘走進花園時看起來容光煥發，她的笑容讓婚禮上的每個人也跟著微笑。","h":1},{"w":"radiate","p":"v.","d":"to send out light or heat; to show a strong feeling","c":"散發；發出（光、熱）","s":"The old stone walls radiate heat long after sunset, so the cats like to sleep against them on cool nights.","t":"日落很久後老石牆仍散發熱氣，所以貓咪喜歡在涼爽的夜晚靠著牆睡覺。","h":1},{"w":"radiation","p":"n.","d":"energy sent out in rays; dangerous energy from nuclear material","c":"輻射","s":"Workers at the nuclear plant wear special suits to protect themselves from radiation, and they check their health every month.","t":"核電廠的工人穿特殊防護衣保護自己免受輻射，並且每個月檢查健康。"},{"w":"radiator","p":"n.","d":"a metal object that heats a room; part of a car that cools the engine","c":"暖氣機；散熱器","s":"It was so cold in the apartment that we sat right next to the radiator with our hands around cups of hot tea.","t":"公寓裡太冷了，我們緊挨著暖氣機坐著，手捧著熱茶。"},{"w":"radiate confidence","p":"v.phr.","d":"to clearly show that you feel sure of yourself","c":"散發自信","s":"The young speaker seemed to radiate confidence as she walked onto the stage, even though it was her first big speech.","t":"這位年輕講者走上舞台時似乎散發出自信，雖然這是她第一次重要的演講。"},{"w":"radioactive","p":"adj.","d":"containing or producing dangerous energy from atoms","c":"放射性的；有輻射的","s":"The radioactive waste from the power plant must be stored deep underground, where it cannot harm people for thousands of years.","t":"發電廠的放射性廢料必須存放在地底深處，數千年內都不會傷害人類。","h":1},{"w":"radioactivity","p":"n.","d":"the dangerous energy produced by some materials","c":"放射性；放射能","s":"Scientists measured the radioactivity in the soil near the old factory and found that it was still too high for farming.","t":"科學家測量了舊工廠附近土壤的放射性，發現它仍然高到無法耕作。"},{"w":"nuclear","p":"adj.","d":"relating to the energy produced by splitting atoms","c":"核能的；核子的","s":"Some countries are closing their nuclear power plants and building more wind farms along the coast instead.","t":"有些國家正在關閉核能發電廠，改在沿海建造更多風力發電場。"},{"w":"radio","p":"n.","d":"a device that receives sound broadcasts; the broadcasts themselves","c":"收音機；廣播","s":"My grandfather still listens to the news on the radio every morning while he eats his breakfast in the kitchen.","t":"我爺爺每天早上在廚房吃早餐時，仍然用收音機聽新聞。"},{"w":"radish","p":"n.","d":"a small round or long vegetable with a sharp taste, eaten raw or cooked","c":"蘿蔔","s":"My grandmother makes a delicious soup with white radish and pork ribs, and she always cooks it on cold winter nights.","t":"我奶奶用白蘿蔔和排骨煮一道美味的湯，她總是在寒冷的冬夜煮這道湯。","h":1},{"w":"carrot","p":"n.","d":"a long orange vegetable that grows under the ground","c":"胡蘿蔔","s":"Rabbits are not the only animals that love carrots; my dog begs for one every time I open the fridge.","t":"兔子不是唯一愛吃胡蘿蔔的動物；每次我打開冰箱，我的狗都會討一根。","a":"carrots"},{"w":"vegetable","p":"n.","d":"a plant or part of a plant that is eaten as food","c":"蔬菜","s":"Doctors say we should eat at least three kinds of vegetables every day, but many students only eat rice and meat.","t":"醫生說我們每天應該吃至少三種蔬菜，但許多學生只吃飯和肉。","a":"vegetables"},{"w":"radius","p":"n.","d":"the distance from the center of a circle to its edge","c":"半徑","s":"The radius of the circle is five centimeters, so the line across the middle must be ten centimeters long.","t":"這個圓的半徑是五公分，所以穿過中心的那條線一定是十公分長。","h":1},{"w":"within a radius of","p":"phr.","d":"inside an area that is a certain distance from a point","c":"在…半徑範圍內；方圓…內","s":"There are six convenience stores within a radius of two hundred meters from our school, so students never go hungry.","t":"我們學校方圓兩百公尺內有六家便利商店，所以學生從不挨餓。"},{"w":"diameter","p":"n.","d":"a straight line through the center of a circle; its length","c":"直徑","s":"The diameter of the old tree's trunk is almost two meters, so three children cannot put their arms around it.","t":"老樹樹幹的直徑將近兩公尺，所以三個孩子也抱不住它。"},{"w":"circle","p":"n.","d":"a round flat shape","c":"圓；圓圈","s":"The children sat in a circle on the grass while the teacher read them a story about a brave little fox.","t":"孩子們在草地上圍成一圈坐著，老師讀一個關於勇敢小狐狸的故事給他們聽。"},{"w":"rap","p":"n.","d":"a type of music in which words are spoken quickly to a strong beat","c":"饒舌（音樂）","s":"My cousin writes his own rap songs about life in Taipei, and he performs them at a small cafe every Saturday.","t":"我表哥寫自己的饒舌歌曲描述台北的生活，每個星期六在一家小咖啡館表演。","h":1},{"w":"rap","p":"v.","d":"to perform rap music; to hit something quickly","c":"說唱；敲擊","s":"He can rap so fast that most listeners cannot catch every word, but they still love the strong beat.","t":"他饒舌的速度快到大多數聽眾無法聽清每個字，但他們仍然喜愛那強烈的節拍。"},{"w":"rapper","p":"n.","d":"a person who performs rap music","c":"饒舌歌手","s":"The famous rapper grew up in a poor neighborhood, and many of his songs tell stories about his childhood.","t":"這位知名饒舌歌手在貧困的社區長大，他的許多歌都在講述童年的故事。"},{"w":"rap on","p":"v.phr.","d":"to knock on something quickly","c":"敲打","s":"I heard someone rap on the window at midnight, and it was my brother, who had forgotten his key again.","t":"午夜我聽到有人敲窗戶，原來是我哥哥，他又忘了帶鑰匙。"},{"w":"hip-hop","p":"n.","d":"a style of music and culture that includes rap music","c":"嘻哈（音樂）","s":"Hip-hop dance classes are very popular at our school, and the students will perform at the festival in December.","t":"嘻哈舞蹈課在我們學校很受歡迎，學生們將在十二月的慶典上表演。","a":"Hip-hop"}]},{"unit":30,"theme":"rash – reliant","cards":[{"w":"rash","p":"n.","d":"an area of red spots on the skin","c":"疹子；皮疹","s":"After eating the strawberries, my little sister got a red rash on her arms, so Mom took her to the doctor.","t":"吃了草莓後，我妹妹手臂上長了紅色的疹子，所以媽媽帶她去看醫生。","h":1},{"w":"rash","p":"adj.","d":"done too quickly without thinking carefully","c":"輕率的；魯莽的","s":"Quitting your job before finding a new one was a rash decision, and now you are worried about paying the rent.","t":"還沒找到新工作就辭職是個輕率的決定，現在你正擔心付不出房租。"},{"w":"break out in a rash","p":"v.phr.","d":"to suddenly get red spots on the skin","c":"突然起疹子","s":"If you break out in a rash after taking the medicine, stop taking it at once and call the clinic for advice.","t":"如果你吃了藥後突然起疹子，立刻停藥並打電話給診所尋求建議。"},{"w":"hasty","p":"adj.","d":"done in a hurry without enough thought","c":"匆忙的；草率的","s":"Do not make a hasty choice about which university to attend; visit a few campuses first and talk to students.","t":"不要草率決定要讀哪所大學；先參觀幾個校園，和學生聊聊。"},{"w":"ratify","p":"v.","d":"to make an agreement official by signing or voting for it","c":"批准；正式通過","s":"The two countries signed the trade agreement in May, but their parliaments must ratify it before it becomes law.","t":"兩國在五月簽署了貿易協定，但他們的國會必須批准它才能成為法律。","h":1},{"w":"ratification","p":"n.","d":"the act of making an agreement official","c":"批准；核准","s":"The ratification of the treaty took almost two years because several members of the parliament were against it.","t":"條約的批准花了將近兩年，因為國會有幾位議員反對它。"},{"w":"approve","p":"v.","d":"to officially agree to something","c":"核准；贊成","s":"The city council will approve the plan for the new park next week if enough residents support it.","t":"如果有足夠的居民支持，市議會下週將核准新公園的計畫。"},{"w":"treaty","p":"n.","d":"a formal written agreement between countries","c":"條約","s":"The peace treaty was signed in Paris, and soldiers on both sides were finally able to go home to their families.","t":"和平條約在巴黎簽署，雙方的士兵終於能回家與家人團聚。"},{"w":"realization","p":"n.","d":"the moment when you understand something; the act of achieving something","c":"領悟；意識到；實現","s":"The realization that she had left her passport at home hit her just as the taxi reached the airport.","t":"計程車剛到機場，她突然意識到自己把護照忘在家裡了。","h":1},{"w":"realize","p":"v.","d":"to understand or become aware of something; to achieve","c":"意識到；了解；實現","s":"I did not realize how late it was until I looked out the window and saw that the sky was dark.","t":"直到我往窗外看，看到天色已暗，才意識到時間已經很晚了。"},{"w":"realize a dream","p":"v.phr.","d":"to make a dream come true","c":"實現夢想","s":"After years of saving money, my aunt finally realized her dream of opening her own small bookstore by the sea.","t":"存了好幾年的錢之後，我阿姨終於實現了在海邊開一家小書店的夢想。","a":"realized her dream"},{"w":"real","p":"adj.","d":"actually existing; true","c":"真實的；真正的","s":"The movie is based on a real story about a doctor who saved hundreds of children during the war.","t":"這部電影根據一個真實的故事改編，講述一位醫生在戰爭期間救了數百名兒童。"},{"w":"reality","p":"n.","d":"the way things actually are","c":"現實","s":"In his dreams he was a famous singer, but in reality he worked at a small shop and sang only on weekends.","t":"在夢裡他是知名歌手，但現實中他在一家小店工作，只有週末才唱歌。"},{"w":"reap","p":"v.","d":"to cut and collect crops; to get something good as a result of your work","c":"收割；獲得","s":"The farmers will reap the rice in late June, and the whole village helps because the work must be finished quickly.","t":"農民將在六月下旬收割稻米，全村的人都來幫忙，因為工作必須迅速完成。","h":1},{"w":"reap the benefits","p":"v.phr.","d":"to enjoy the good results of something","c":"獲得好處；享受成果","s":"If you practice English a little every day, you will reap the benefits when you travel abroad next summer.","t":"如果你每天練習一點英文，明年夏天出國旅行時就會享受到成果。"},{"w":"harvest","p":"n.","d":"the time when crops are collected; the crops collected","c":"收成；收穫","s":"This year's apple harvest was the best in ten years, so the farmers sold fruit at lower prices than usual.","t":"今年的蘋果收成是十年來最好的，所以農民以比平常更低的價格賣水果。"},{"w":"crop","p":"n.","d":"a plant grown in large amounts for food","c":"農作物","s":"Rice is the main crop in this area, and you can see green fields stretching all the way to the mountains.","t":"稻米是這個地區的主要農作物，你可以看到綠色的田野一直延伸到山邊。"},{"w":"reckless","p":"adj.","d":"not caring about danger or the results of your actions","c":"魯莽的；不顧後果的","s":"The reckless driver passed three cars on the narrow mountain road, and he nearly hit a bus coming the other way.","t":"那位魯莽的駕駛在狹窄的山路上超了三輛車，差點撞上對向來的公車。","h":1},{"w":"recklessly","p":"adv.","d":"in a way that shows no care about danger","c":"魯莽地","s":"The boys rode their scooters recklessly through the night market, and an old woman dropped her bag of fruit in fear.","t":"男孩們魯莽地騎著機車穿過夜市，一位老太太嚇得把水果袋掉在地上。"},{"w":"recklessness","p":"n.","d":"behavior that shows no care about danger","c":"魯莽；輕率","s":"The judge said the young man's recklessness had caused the accident, and he lost his license for a year.","t":"法官說這位年輕人的魯莽造成了這場事故，他的駕照被吊銷一年。"},{"w":"careless","p":"adj.","d":"not giving enough attention to what you are doing","c":"粗心的","s":"She lost ten points on the test because of careless mistakes, such as writing the wrong date and missing a question.","t":"她因為粗心的錯誤在考試中丟了十分，例如寫錯日期和漏掉一題。"},{"w":"reckon","p":"v.","d":"to think or believe something; to calculate","c":"認為；估計","s":"I reckon the trip will take about three hours if the traffic is light, so we should leave before seven.","t":"我估計如果交通順暢，這趟路程大約要三小時，所以我們應該七點前出發。","h":1},{"w":"reckon on","p":"v.phr.","d":"to expect something to happen and plan for it","c":"指望；預期","s":"We did not reckon on rain during the picnic, so nobody brought an umbrella and we all got wet.","t":"我們沒預期野餐時會下雨，所以沒有人帶傘，大家都淋濕了。"},{"w":"calculate","p":"v.","d":"to find a number or amount by using math","c":"計算","s":"Please calculate how much money we need for the trip, including the train tickets and two nights at the hotel.","t":"請計算我們這趟旅行需要多少錢，包括火車票和兩晚飯店住宿。"},{"w":"estimate","p":"v.","d":"to guess the size, amount, or cost of something","c":"估計","s":"The mechanic could not tell us the exact price, but he could estimate that fixing the car would cost about ten thousand dollars.","t":"技師無法告訴我們確切的價格，但他估計修車大約要花一萬元。"},{"w":"reconcile","p":"v.","d":"to become friendly again after a disagreement; to make two ideas agree","c":"和解；調和","s":"The two brothers finally decided to reconcile after not speaking to each other for almost five years.","t":"兩兄弟近五年沒有說過話之後，終於決定和解。","h":1},{"w":"reconcile with","p":"v.phr.","d":"to become friends again with someone","c":"與…和解","s":"She wants to reconcile with her old friend, so she sent a long letter saying sorry for the things she had said.","t":"她想與老朋友和解，所以寄了一封長信，為自己說過的話道歉。"},{"w":"reconciliation","p":"n.","d":"the act of becoming friendly again after a fight","c":"和解；調和","s":"The reconciliation between the two families took place at a big dinner, and the children played together for the first time.","t":"兩家人的和解在一場盛大的晚餐上達成，孩子們第一次一起玩耍。"},{"w":"make peace with","p":"v.phr.","d":"to end a fight or argument with someone","c":"與…講和","s":"After the long argument, my sister made peace with me by bringing my favorite bubble tea to my room.","t":"長時間的爭吵後，我姐姐把我最愛的珍珠奶茶送到我房間，與我講和。","a":"made peace with"},{"w":"recreational","p":"adj.","d":"done for enjoyment when you are not working","c":"休閒的；娛樂的","s":"The park has many recreational areas, including a swimming pool, a skating rink, and several basketball courts.","t":"這座公園有許多休閒區域，包括游泳池、溜冰場和幾個籃球場。","h":1},{"w":"recreation","p":"n.","d":"activities you do for enjoyment","c":"休閒活動；娛樂","s":"Reading and hiking are my favorite forms of recreation, and I try to do both every weekend if the weather is good.","t":"閱讀和健行是我最喜歡的休閒活動，天氣好的話我每個週末都盡量兩者都做。"},{"w":"recreate","p":"v.","d":"to make something exist again; to make a copy of something from the past","c":"重現；重建","s":"The museum tried to recreate a street from one hundred years ago, with old shops, lamps, and even a horse cart.","t":"博物館試圖重現一百年前的街道，有舊商店、路燈，甚至還有馬車。"},{"w":"leisure","p":"n.","d":"time when you are not working or studying","c":"閒暇；休閒","s":"My father has very little leisure time during the week, so he spends every Sunday fishing by the lake.","t":"我爸爸平日幾乎沒有閒暇時間，所以他每個星期天都在湖邊釣魚。"},{"w":"redundancy","p":"n.","d":"the state of being more than is needed; losing a job because it is no longer needed","c":"多餘；裁員","s":"The company announced the redundancy of two hundred workers after the new machines took over most of the work.","t":"新機器接手大部分工作後，公司宣布裁員兩百名員工。","h":1},{"w":"redundant","p":"adj.","d":"not needed any more; more than is necessary","c":"多餘的；被裁員的","s":"When the factory closed, three hundred workers were made redundant, and many of them could not find new jobs.","t":"工廠關閉時，三百名工人被裁員，其中許多人找不到新工作。"},{"w":"unnecessary","p":"adj.","d":"not needed","c":"不必要的","s":"Taking a taxi to the station is unnecessary, because the bus stops right outside our door every ten minutes.","t":"搭計程車去車站是不必要的，因為公車每十分鐘就在我們門口停一次。"},{"w":"lay off","p":"v.phr.","d":"to stop employing someone because there is not enough work","c":"解僱；資遣","s":"The restaurant had to lay off two cooks during the slow winter months, but it hired them back in spring.","t":"餐廳在冬季淡月不得不資遣兩位廚師，但春天又把他們聘回來了。"},{"w":"reef","p":"n.","d":"a line of rocks or coral near the surface of the sea","c":"礁；暗礁","s":"The boat hit a reef hidden under the water, and the captain had to call for help before it began to sink.","t":"船撞上藏在水下的暗礁，船長在船開始下沉前不得不呼救。","h":1},{"w":"coral reef","p":"n.phr.","d":"a reef made of coral where many sea animals live","c":"珊瑚礁","s":"Kenting has a beautiful coral reef, and every year thousands of visitors swim there to look at the colorful fish.","t":"墾丁有美麗的珊瑚礁，每年有數千名遊客到那裡游泳觀賞色彩繽紛的魚。"},{"w":"coral","p":"n.","d":"a hard colorful material made by tiny sea animals","c":"珊瑚","s":"Warmer seas are killing the coral in many parts of the world, and the fish that live there are disappearing too.","t":"海水變暖正在殺死世界許多地方的珊瑚，住在那裡的魚也正在消失。"},{"w":"shore","p":"n.","d":"the land along the edge of a sea or lake","c":"岸；海岸","s":"We walked along the shore at sunset, picking up shells and watching the small crabs run into the sand.","t":"我們在日落時沿著海岸散步，撿貝殼，看小螃蟹跑進沙裡。"},{"w":"referee","p":"n.","d":"a person who makes sure players follow the rules in a game","c":"裁判","s":"The referee blew his whistle and stopped the game because two players had started pushing each other.","t":"裁判吹哨暫停比賽，因為兩名球員開始互相推擠。","h":1},{"w":"referee","p":"v.","d":"to act as the referee in a game","c":"擔任裁判","s":"My PE teacher will referee the final basketball game on Friday, so everyone expects it to be fair.","t":"我的體育老師星期五將為籃球決賽擔任裁判，所以大家都期待比賽會很公平。"},{"w":"refer to","p":"v.phr.","d":"to mention or talk about something; to look at something for information","c":"提到；參考","s":"If you forget a word during the speech, you may refer to your notes, but try not to read the whole thing.","t":"如果你演講時忘了某個字，可以參考筆記，但盡量不要整篇照念。"},{"w":"judge","p":"n.","d":"a person who decides the winner in a competition; a person in charge of a court","c":"評審；法官","s":"Each judge in the singing contest gave the girl ten points, and the audience cheered for almost a minute.","t":"歌唱比賽的每位評審都給這個女孩十分，觀眾歡呼了將近一分鐘。"},{"w":"umpire","p":"n.","d":"a person who makes sure players follow the rules in baseball or tennis","c":"（棒球、網球）裁判","s":"The umpire called the runner out at home plate, and the coach ran onto the field to argue with him.","t":"裁判判跑者在本壘出局，教練衝進場內和他爭論。"},{"w":"referendum","p":"n.","d":"a vote in which all the people of a country decide an important question","c":"公民投票；公投","s":"The government will hold a referendum in November, and citizens will vote on whether to lower the voting age to eighteen.","t":"政府將在十一月舉行公投，公民將投票決定是否把投票年齡降到十八歲。","h":1},{"w":"vote","p":"v.","d":"to show your choice in an election by marking a paper or raising your hand","c":"投票","s":"Citizens over twenty can vote for the president, and many young people lined up early at the polling stations.","t":"二十歲以上的公民可以投票選總統，許多年輕人一早就在投票所排隊。"},{"w":"election","p":"n.","d":"a time when people vote to choose a leader","c":"選舉","s":"The city will hold an election for a new mayor next spring, and three candidates have already started their campaigns.","t":"這座城市明年春天將舉行市長選舉，三位候選人已經開始競選活動。"},{"w":"ballot","p":"n.","d":"a piece of paper on which you mark your vote; the act of voting","c":"選票；投票","s":"Each voter writes an X on the ballot and folds it before putting it into the box at the front of the room.","t":"每位選民在選票上畫X並摺好，然後投入房間前方的箱子裡。"},{"w":"refine","p":"v.","d":"to make something pure; to improve something by making small changes","c":"精煉；改進","s":"The factory will refine the oil before it is sold, removing the dirt and the parts that cannot be used in cars.","t":"工廠會在販售前精煉石油，去除雜質和汽車無法使用的部分。","h":1},{"w":"refinement","p":"n.","d":"a small change that improves something; good manners and taste","c":"改進；精緻；優雅","s":"The design needs a few more refinements before we show it to the customer, especially the color of the buttons.","t":"這個設計在給客戶看之前還需要一些改進，尤其是按鈕的顏色。","a":"refinements"},{"w":"refined","p":"adj.","d":"made pure; polite and well educated","c":"精煉的；精製的；有教養的","s":"Doctors say that eating too much refined sugar is bad for your teeth and can make you gain weight quickly.","t":"醫生說吃太多精製糖對牙齒不好，而且會讓你很快變胖。"},{"w":"refinery","p":"n.","d":"a factory where oil or sugar is made pure","c":"煉油廠；精煉廠","s":"The oil refinery near the harbor works day and night, and you can see its lights from the top of the hill.","t":"港口附近的煉油廠日夜運作，從山頂可以看到它的燈光。"},{"w":"reflective","p":"adj.","d":"able to send back light; thinking deeply","c":"反光的；深思的","s":"Cyclists should wear reflective clothing at night, so that drivers can see them clearly from far away.","t":"騎自行車的人晚上應該穿反光衣物，這樣駕駛才能從遠處清楚看見他們。","h":1},{"w":"reflect","p":"v.","d":"to send back light, heat, or sound; to think carefully","c":"反射；反映；深思","s":"The calm lake was so still that it seemed to reflect every tree and cloud like a giant mirror.","t":"平靜的湖面如此靜止，彷彿像一面巨大的鏡子映照出每一棵樹和雲朵。"},{"w":"reflection","p":"n.","d":"an image seen in a mirror or water; careful thought","c":"倒影；反射；反思","s":"She looked at her reflection in the shop window and fixed her hair before going in for the interview.","t":"她看著商店櫥窗裡自己的倒影，整理好頭髮才進去面試。"},{"w":"on reflection","p":"phr.","d":"after thinking carefully about something","c":"經過深思後","s":"On reflection, I think we should take the train instead of driving, because parking in the city is expensive and hard to find.","t":"經過深思後，我認為我們應該搭火車而不是開車，因為市區停車又貴又難找。","a":"On reflection"},{"w":"refresh","p":"v.","d":"to make someone feel less tired or hot; to update information","c":"使恢復精神；重新整理","s":"A cold shower will refresh you after the long hike, and then we can go out for a big dinner.","t":"長途健行後沖個冷水澡會讓你恢復精神，然後我們可以出去吃頓大餐。","h":1},{"w":"refreshments","p":"n.","d":"small amounts of food and drink served at a meeting or event","c":"茶點；點心","s":"Refreshments will be served after the meeting, so please stay for some coffee, tea, and cake in the next room.","t":"會議結束後將供應茶點，請留下來到隔壁房間享用咖啡、茶和蛋糕。","a":"Refreshments","h":1},{"w":"refreshment","p":"n.","d":"the feeling of having new energy after rest, food, or drink","c":"恢復精神；提神","s":"The hikers stopped by the stream for refreshment, washing their faces in the cool water and eating some fruit.","t":"登山者在溪邊停下來恢復精神，用清涼的溪水洗臉並吃點水果。"},{"w":"refreshing","p":"adj.","d":"making you feel less tired or hot; pleasantly new","c":"提神的；清爽的；令人耳目一新的","s":"There is nothing more refreshing than a glass of cold lemon water after playing basketball in the summer heat.","t":"在夏天的酷熱中打完籃球後，沒有什麼比一杯冰檸檬水更清爽提神的了。"},{"w":"refresh your memory","p":"v.phr.","d":"to help yourself remember something","c":"喚起記憶","s":"Before the exam, I read my notes once more to refresh my memory, and it really helped me with the hardest questions.","t":"考試前我把筆記再讀一遍來喚起記憶，這對最難的題目真的很有幫助。","a":"refresh my memory"},{"w":"refute","p":"v.","d":"to prove that something is wrong or not true","c":"反駁；駁斥","s":"The scientist was able to refute the claim that the medicine was dangerous by showing the results of ten years of tests.","t":"這位科學家展示十年的測試結果，駁斥了這種藥很危險的說法。","h":1},{"w":"refutation","p":"n.","d":"the act of proving something wrong","c":"反駁；駁斥","s":"Her refutation of the rumor was so clear and calm that the reporters stopped asking questions about it.","t":"她對謠言的反駁如此清楚冷靜，記者們不再追問這件事。"},{"w":"deny","p":"v.","d":"to say that something is not true","c":"否認","s":"The boy continued to deny that he had broken the window, even though his ball was lying in the broken glass.","t":"男孩持續否認是他打破窗戶，即使他的球就躺在碎玻璃中。"},{"w":"argue against","p":"v.phr.","d":"to give reasons why something is wrong or should not be done","c":"反對；提出反對理由","s":"Several parents argued against the longer school day, saying that children already have too little time to play.","t":"幾位家長反對延長上課時間，說孩子們已經沒什麼時間玩了。","a":"argued against"},{"w":"rehabilitate","p":"v.","d":"to help someone return to a healthy or normal life after illness, injury, or prison","c":"使康復；使重新適應社會","s":"The hospital has a special program to rehabilitate patients who have lost the use of their legs after an accident.","t":"醫院有一項特別計畫，幫助事故後失去雙腿功能的病人康復。","h":1},{"w":"rehabilitation","p":"n.","d":"the process of returning to a healthy or normal life","c":"康復；復健","s":"After breaking his leg in the game, the player spent three months in rehabilitation before he could run again.","t":"在比賽中摔斷腿後，這位球員花了三個月復健才能再次跑步。"},{"w":"recover","p":"v.","d":"to become healthy again after an illness or injury","c":"康復；恢復","s":"It took my grandmother two weeks to recover from the flu, and the doctor told her to rest and drink plenty of water.","t":"我奶奶花了兩週才從流感中康復，醫生要她多休息、多喝水。"},{"w":"recovery","p":"n.","d":"the process of becoming healthy again","c":"康復；復原","s":"The doctor said his recovery was going well, and he might be able to leave the hospital by the end of the month.","t":"醫生說他的康復情況良好，月底前可能就能出院。"},{"w":"rehearse","p":"v.","d":"to practice a play, speech, or music before performing it","c":"排練；排演","s":"The students will rehearse the play every afternoon this week, because the big performance is on Saturday night.","t":"學生們這週每天下午都要排練這齣戲，因為盛大的演出是在星期六晚上。","h":1},{"w":"rehearsal","p":"n.","d":"a practice of a play or music before the real performance","c":"排練；排演","s":"The final rehearsal went badly because two actors forgot their lines, but the teacher said the real show would be fine.","t":"最後一次排練進行得很糟，因為兩位演員忘了台詞，但老師說正式演出會沒問題的。"},{"w":"dress rehearsal","p":"n.phr.","d":"the last practice of a play with full costumes","c":"彩排","s":"During the dress rehearsal on Friday, everyone wore their costumes and makeup, and the lights and music were tested too.","t":"星期五彩排時，每個人都穿上戲服、化好妝，燈光和音樂也一併測試。"},{"w":"practice","p":"v.","d":"to do something regularly to become better at it","c":"練習","s":"If you want to play the piano well, you have to practice at least thirty minutes every day, even when you feel tired.","t":"如果你想把鋼琴彈好，就必須每天至少練習三十分鐘，即使覺得累也一樣。"},{"w":"reign","p":"n.","d":"the period when a king or queen rules a country","c":"統治時期；在位期間","s":"During the reign of Queen Victoria, Britain built many railways and became the most powerful country in the world.","t":"在維多利亞女王統治期間，英國建造了許多鐵路，成為世界上最強大的國家。","h":1},{"w":"reign","p":"v.","d":"to rule a country as king or queen","c":"統治；在位","s":"The old king reigned for fifty years, and most people in the country had never known another ruler.","t":"老國王在位五十年，國內大多數人從未經歷過其他統治者。","a":"reigned"},{"w":"rule","p":"v.","d":"to have control over a country or a group of people","c":"統治；管理","s":"The small island was ruled by Spain for two hundred years, so many of its old buildings look Spanish.","t":"這座小島被西班牙統治了兩百年，所以許多老建築看起來很有西班牙風格。","a":"ruled"},{"w":"throne","p":"n.","d":"the special chair of a king or queen; the position of being king or queen","c":"王位；王座","s":"The young prince took the throne at the age of eighteen after his father died suddenly in the spring.","t":"年輕的王子在父親春天突然去世後，於十八歲登上王位。"},{"w":"rejoice","p":"v.","d":"to feel or show great happiness","c":"高興；歡欣","s":"The whole town will rejoice when the local team brings home the championship cup for the first time in thirty years.","t":"當地球隊三十年來第一次把冠軍獎盃帶回家時，全鎮的人都會歡欣鼓舞。","h":1},{"w":"rejoice at","p":"v.phr.","d":"to be very happy about something","c":"為…感到高興","s":"The family rejoiced at the news that the lost dog had been found safe at a farm twenty kilometers away.","t":"一家人為走失的狗在二十公里外的農場被安全找到的消息感到高興。","a":"rejoiced at"},{"w":"joy","p":"n.","d":"a feeling of great happiness","c":"喜悅","s":"Tears of joy ran down her face when she saw her son step off the plane after two years abroad.","t":"看到兒子在國外兩年後走下飛機時，喜悅的淚水流下她的臉頰。"},{"w":"joyful","p":"adj.","d":"very happy","c":"歡樂的；高興的","s":"The wedding was a joyful day for both families, with music, dancing, and laughter late into the night.","t":"婚禮對兩家人來說是歡樂的一天，音樂、舞蹈和笑聲持續到深夜。"},{"w":"celebrate","p":"v.","d":"to do something special for a happy event","c":"慶祝","s":"We always celebrate my grandfather's birthday with a big family dinner, and he blows out the candles with the youngest grandchild.","t":"我們總是用一頓盛大的家庭晚餐來慶祝爺爺的生日，他會和最小的孫子一起吹蠟燭。"},{"w":"relay","p":"n.","d":"a race in which each member of a team runs part of the distance","c":"接力賽","s":"Our class won the 400-meter relay on sports day, and the last runner crossed the line just one step ahead.","t":"我們班在運動會上贏了四百公尺接力賽，最後一棒只領先一步衝過終點。","h":1},{"w":"relay","p":"v.","d":"to pass a message or information from one person to another","c":"轉達；傳遞","s":"Please relay this message to your parents: the school trip has been moved to next Thursday because of the typhoon.","t":"請把這個訊息轉達給你的父母：因為颱風，校外旅行改到下週四。"},{"w":"relay race","p":"n.phr.","d":"a race where team members take turns to run","c":"接力賽跑","s":"In the relay race, dropping the stick can cost the whole team the race, so the runners practice passing it every day.","t":"在接力賽跑中，掉棒可能讓整隊輸掉比賽，所以跑者每天都練習交棒。"},{"w":"pass on","p":"v.phr.","d":"to give information or a thing to someone else","c":"傳遞；轉交","s":"Could you pass on these notes to Jenny when you see her? She missed class yesterday because she was sick.","t":"你見到珍妮時可以把這些筆記轉交給她嗎？她昨天生病沒來上課。"},{"w":"relentless","p":"adj.","d":"continuing without ever stopping or becoming less strong","c":"不間斷的；無情的","s":"The relentless rain lasted for five days, and the river rose so high that the old bridge was completely covered.","t":"不停歇的雨持續了五天，河水漲得很高，老橋完全被淹沒。","h":1},{"w":"relentlessly","p":"adv.","d":"without stopping or becoming weaker","c":"不懈地；無情地","s":"The reporter relentlessly asked the mayor the same question until he finally admitted that the money was missing.","t":"記者不懈地向市長追問同一個問題，直到他終於承認那筆錢不見了。"},{"w":"ceaseless","p":"adj.","d":"never stopping","c":"不停的；不斷的","s":"The ceaseless noise from the construction site next door made it impossible for me to study for my exam.","t":"隔壁工地不停的噪音讓我無法準備考試。"},{"w":"persistent","p":"adj.","d":"continuing to do something although it is difficult; lasting a long time","c":"堅持不懈的；持續的","s":"After weeks of persistent practice, the shy boy finally gave his speech in front of the whole school without shaking.","t":"經過數週堅持不懈的練習，害羞的男孩終於在全校面前發表演講而不發抖。"},{"w":"reliance","p":"n.","d":"the state of depending on someone or something","c":"依賴；依靠","s":"Our reliance on smartphones has grown so much that many people feel lost when their battery dies.","t":"我們對智慧型手機的依賴增加了很多，許多人電池沒電時會感到不知所措。","h":1},{"w":"reliant","p":"adj.","d":"depending on someone or something","c":"依賴的","s":"The small island is reliant on tourists for most of its income, so a bad typhoon season can hurt every family.","t":"這座小島大部分收入都依賴遊客，所以糟糕的颱風季會傷害每個家庭。","h":1},{"w":"rely on","p":"v.phr.","d":"to depend on someone or something","c":"依賴；依靠","s":"Many old people in the village rely on their neighbors to buy food for them when the weather is bad.","t":"村裡許多老人在天氣不好時依靠鄰居幫他們買食物。"},{"w":"reliable","p":"adj.","d":"able to be trusted or depended on","c":"可靠的","s":"My old car is not fast, but it is very reliable, and it has never once broken down in ten years.","t":"我的舊車不快，但非常可靠，十年來從未拋錨過一次。"},{"w":"self-reliant","p":"adj.","d":"able to do things by yourself without help from others","c":"自立的；自力更生的","s":"Living alone in Taipei has made my cousin more self-reliant; she now cooks, cleans, and manages her money by herself.","t":"獨自住在台北讓我表姐變得更自立；她現在自己煮飯、打掃並管理自己的錢。"}]},{"unit":31,"theme":"relic – robust","cards":[{"w":"relic","p":"n.","d":"an old object or custom that has survived from the past","c":"遺物；遺跡","s":"The museum's most famous relic is a bronze bowl that was made more than three thousand years ago by early farmers.","t":"這座博物館最有名的遺物是一個三千多年前由早期農民製作的青銅碗。","h":1},{"w":"relics of the past","p":"n.phr.","d":"old things left from earlier times","c":"過去的遺跡","s":"Walking through the old town, we saw many relics of the past, such as stone walls and a temple built four hundred years ago.","t":"走在老城區裡，我們看到許多過去的遺跡，像是石牆和一座四百年前建造的寺廟。"},{"w":"historical relic","p":"n.phr.","d":"an old object that is important in history","c":"歷史文物","s":"Every historical relic in this room must be kept in a glass case because light and wet air can damage it quickly.","t":"這間展室裡的每件歷史文物都必須放在玻璃櫃中，因為光線和潮濕的空氣會很快損壞它。"},{"w":"remainder","p":"n.","d":"the part that is left after the rest has gone or been used","c":"剩餘部分；其餘","s":"We spent the morning at the beach and used the remainder of the day to visit the night market and buy gifts.","t":"我們上午在海邊度過，然後用一天剩下的時間去逛夜市和買禮物。","h":1},{"w":"remain","p":"v.","d":"to stay in the same place or condition","c":"留下；保持","s":"After the party, only a few close friends decided to remain and help us clean up the kitchen before midnight.","t":"派對結束後，只有幾位好朋友決定留下來，在午夜前幫我們把廚房清理乾淨。"},{"w":"remaining","p":"adj.","d":"still left after the others have gone or been used","c":"剩下的","s":"There are only three remaining tickets for tonight's concert, so you should buy them online right now before they are gone.","t":"今晚的演唱會只剩下三張票，所以你應該現在就上網買，以免賣完。"},{"w":"remains","p":"n.","d":"the parts of something that are left after most of it has gone","c":"遺跡；殘餘物","s":"Scientists found the remains of an ancient city under the farm, and they believe people lived there about two thousand years ago.","t":"科學家在農田底下發現一座古城的遺跡，他們認為大約兩千年前有人住在那裡。"},{"w":"reminiscent","p":"adj.","d":"making you remember something similar","c":"使人想起的；懷舊的","s":"The smell of fresh bread from the bakery is reminiscent of my grandmother's kitchen on Sunday mornings when I was a child.","t":"麵包店新鮮麵包的香味讓我想起小時候星期天早上奶奶的廚房。","h":1},{"w":"be reminiscent of","p":"v.phr.","d":"to make someone remember a similar person, place, or thing","c":"讓人想起…","s":"This small town, with its quiet streets and old shops, is reminiscent of the village where my father grew up sixty years ago.","t":"這個小鎮安靜的街道和老店讓人想起我父親六十年前長大的那個村子。","a":"is reminiscent of"},{"w":"reminisce","p":"v.","d":"to talk or think about happy times in the past","c":"回憶往事；懷舊","s":"At the class reunion, my old classmates and I sat together for hours to reminisce about our high school days and our funny teachers.","t":"在同學會上，我和老同學坐在一起好幾個小時，回憶高中時光和那些有趣的老師。"},{"w":"reminiscence","p":"n.","d":"a story or memory about the past","c":"回憶；懷舊談話","s":"Grandpa's reminiscences of his life as a young sailor kept the whole family listening quietly until late at night.","t":"爺爺回憶年輕時當水手的生活，讓全家人安靜地聽到深夜。","a":"reminiscences"},{"w":"renowned","p":"adj.","d":"famous and respected by many people","c":"著名的；有名望的","s":"The renowned chef opened a small restaurant in Tainan, and people now wait in line for two hours just to taste his beef noodles.","t":"這位著名的廚師在台南開了一家小餐廳，現在人們排隊兩小時只為了嚐他的牛肉麵。","h":1},{"w":"be renowned for","p":"v.phr.","d":"to be famous because of something good","c":"以…聞名","s":"Taiwan is renowned for its friendly people and delicious street food, so many tourists come back again and again every year.","t":"台灣以友善的人民和美味的街頭小吃聞名，所以許多觀光客每年一再回來。","a":"is renowned for"},{"w":"renown","p":"n.","d":"the state of being famous and respected","c":"名望；聲譽","s":"The young pianist won international renown after she took first place in a famous competition in Poland at the age of nineteen.","t":"這位年輕鋼琴家十九歲在波蘭一場著名比賽中得到第一名後，贏得了國際聲譽。"},{"w":"world-renowned","p":"adj.","d":"famous all over the world","c":"世界聞名的","s":"A world-renowned scientist will give a talk at our school next Friday, so the hall is expected to be completely full.","t":"一位世界聞名的科學家下星期五將在我們學校演講，所以禮堂預計會坐滿。"},{"w":"reproduce","p":"v.","d":"to make a copy of something","c":"複製；再現","s":"With this new printer, you can reproduce old family photos so well that nobody can tell the copy from the original.","t":"用這台新印表機，你可以把老家庭照片複製得非常好，沒有人能分辨出複本和原件。","h":1},{"w":"reproduce","p":"v.","d":"to have babies or produce young animals or plants","c":"繁殖","s":"Rabbits reproduce very quickly, so a farm that starts with two rabbits may have dozens of them within a single year.","t":"兔子繁殖得非常快，所以一個從兩隻兔子開始的農場，一年內可能就有幾十隻。"},{"w":"reproduction","p":"n.","d":"a copy of something; the process of producing young","c":"複製品；繁殖","s":"The painting on the wall is only a reproduction, but it looks so real that many guests think it is the original work.","t":"牆上的那幅畫只是一件複製品，但它看起來非常真實，許多客人以為那是原作。"},{"w":"reproductive","p":"adj.","d":"connected with producing babies or young","c":"生殖的；繁殖的","s":"In biology class this week, we learned how the reproductive system of a flower helps the plant make seeds and spread them.","t":"這星期的生物課上，我們學到花的生殖系統如何幫助植物產生種子並散播出去。"},{"w":"reptile","p":"n.","d":"a cold-blooded animal with scales, such as a snake or lizard","c":"爬蟲類動物","s":"A snake is a reptile, which means it has dry skin covered with scales and lays eggs instead of giving birth to live babies.","t":"蛇是一種爬蟲類動物，這表示它有覆蓋著鱗片的乾燥皮膚，而且是生蛋而不是直接生下小寶寶。","h":1},{"w":"reptile house","p":"n.phr.","d":"the building in a zoo where snakes and lizards are kept","c":"爬蟲館","s":"At the zoo, the reptile house is my little brother's favorite place because he loves watching the lizards and turtles move slowly.","t":"在動物園裡，爬蟲館是我弟弟最喜歡的地方，因為他喜歡看蜥蜴和烏龜慢慢地移動。"},{"w":"reptilian","p":"adj.","d":"like or belonging to a reptile","c":"爬蟲類的","s":"The dinosaur's reptilian skin, with its hard scales, protected it from the heat and from attacks by smaller animals.","t":"恐龍爬蟲類的皮膚帶著堅硬的鱗片，保護它不受高溫和較小動物的攻擊。"},{"w":"resent","p":"v.","d":"to feel angry about something because it seems unfair","c":"憤恨；對…感到不滿","s":"My sister still resents the fact that our parents let my brother stay out late while she always had to be home by nine.","t":"我姐姐仍然不滿父母讓我哥哥在外面待到很晚，而她卻總是必須九點前回家。","a":"resents","h":1},{"w":"resentment","p":"n.","d":"a feeling of anger about something unfair","c":"不滿；怨恨","s":"There was deep resentment among the workers when the manager gave himself a big bonus but refused to raise anyone else's pay.","t":"當經理給自己發了一大筆獎金卻拒絕幫其他人加薪時，員工之間充滿了深深的不滿。"},{"w":"resentful","p":"adj.","d":"feeling angry because of something unfair","c":"憤恨的；心懷不滿的","s":"He felt resentful when his teammates took all the credit for the project, even though he had done most of the hard work.","t":"當隊友把專案的功勞全拿走時，他感到憤恨不平，因為大部分辛苦的工作都是他做的。"},{"w":"reside","p":"v.","d":"to live in a particular place","c":"居住","s":"My aunt and uncle have resided in Kaohsiung for over thirty years, and they say they will never move anywhere else.","t":"我的阿姨和姨丈在高雄居住了三十多年，他們說永遠不會搬到別的地方。","a":"resided","h":1},{"w":"resident","p":"n.","d":"a person who lives in a place","c":"居民","s":"Only residents of this building can use the swimming pool on the roof, so please bring your key card with you.","t":"只有這棟大樓的住戶可以使用屋頂的游泳池，所以請隨身攜帶你的門禁卡。","a":"residents"},{"w":"residence","p":"n.","d":"the house or place where someone lives","c":"住宅；住所","s":"The president's official residence is open to the public twice a year, and thousands of visitors come to see its beautiful gardens.","t":"總統的官方住所每年對民眾開放兩次，成千上萬的訪客前來欣賞它美麗的花園。"},{"w":"residential","p":"adj.","d":"describing an area where people live, not work","c":"住宅的","s":"This is a quiet residential area with no shops or factories, so most families here have to drive to the supermarket.","t":"這是一個安靜的住宅區，沒有商店或工廠，所以這裡大多數家庭必須開車去超市。"},{"w":"resistant","p":"adj.","d":"not harmed or changed by something","c":"有抵抗力的；耐…的","s":"These new bananas are resistant to the disease that destroyed thousands of banana trees across the island last year.","t":"這些新品種香蕉對去年摧毀全島數千棵香蕉樹的疾病具有抵抗力。","h":1},{"w":"resist","p":"v.","d":"to fight against something or refuse to accept it","c":"抵抗；抗拒","s":"It is hard to resist the smell of fried chicken from the night market when you are walking home hungry after school.","t":"放學後餓著肚子走回家時，很難抗拒夜市傳來的炸雞香味。"},{"w":"resistance","p":"n.","d":"the act of fighting against or refusing something","c":"抵抗；反對","s":"The new school rule about phones met with strong resistance from students, who said they needed their phones to check the bus schedule.","t":"學校關於手機的新規定遭到學生強烈反對，他們說需要手機來查公車時間。"},{"w":"water-resistant","p":"adj.","d":"able to keep water out for a short time","c":"防水的","s":"This watch is water-resistant, so you can wear it while swimming in the pool, but you should not take it diving in the sea.","t":"這支手錶是防水的，所以你可以戴著它在泳池游泳，但不應該戴著它去海裡潛水。"},{"w":"respective","p":"adj.","d":"belonging to each of the people or things mentioned","c":"各自的；分別的","s":"After the meeting ended, the teachers returned to their respective classrooms to tell the students about the new schedule.","t":"會議結束後，老師們回到各自的教室，告訴學生新的課表。","h":1},{"w":"respectively","p":"adv.","d":"in the same order as the people or things already mentioned","c":"分別地；各自地","s":"John and Mary are twelve and fifteen years old respectively, so Mary is already in senior high school while John is still in junior high.","t":"約翰和瑪麗分別是十二歲和十五歲，所以瑪麗已經讀高中了，而約翰還在讀國中。"},{"w":"with respect to","p":"phr.","d":"about; concerning","c":"關於；至於","s":"With respect to your question about the trip, we will send all the details, including the price and the hotel, by email tomorrow.","t":"關於你對這次旅行的問題，我們明天會用電子郵件寄出所有細節，包括價格和飯店。","a":"With respect to"},{"w":"respect","p":"n.","d":"a feeling that someone is important and should be treated well","c":"尊敬；尊重","s":"Students in Taiwan show respect to their teachers by standing up and bowing at the beginning of each class.","t":"台灣的學生在每堂課開始時起立敬禮，以表示對老師的尊敬。"},{"w":"restoration","p":"n.","d":"the work of repairing something old so it looks new again","c":"修復；恢復","s":"The restoration of the old train station took three years, but now it looks exactly as it did a hundred years ago.","t":"這座老火車站的修復花了三年，但現在它看起來和一百年前完全一樣。","h":1},{"w":"restore","p":"v.","d":"to bring something back to its earlier good condition","c":"恢復；修復","s":"Workers are trying to restore electricity to the mountain villages after the typhoon knocked down power lines across the whole area.","t":"颱風吹倒整個地區的電線後，工人們正努力恢復山區村落的供電。"},{"w":"restore order","p":"v.phr.","d":"to make a place calm and peaceful again","c":"恢復秩序","s":"The police arrived quickly to restore order after the two groups of fans started fighting outside the baseball stadium.","t":"兩群球迷在棒球場外開始打架後，警察很快趕到恢復秩序。"},{"w":"restrain","p":"v.","d":"to stop someone or something from doing something","c":"制止；抑制","s":"The owner had to restrain his big dog when it tried to jump on the little girl who was passing by the gate.","t":"當大狗想撲向經過門口的小女孩時，主人必須制止它。","h":1},{"w":"restraint","p":"n.","d":"calm and controlled behavior; a limit on something","c":"克制；約束","s":"The angry customer showed great restraint and spoke politely to the clerk, even though his order had been wrong three times.","t":"那位生氣的顧客表現出極大的克制，禮貌地和店員說話，儘管他的餐點已經錯了三次。","h":1},{"w":"restrain oneself","p":"v.phr.","d":"to stop yourself from doing something","c":"克制自己","s":"I had to restrain myself from laughing when my teacher walked into class with a piece of paper stuck to his shoe.","t":"當老師鞋子上黏著一張紙走進教室時，我必須克制自己不要笑出來。","a":"restrain myself"},{"w":"restrained","p":"adj.","d":"calm and controlled, not showing strong feelings","c":"克制的；含蓄的","s":"Her speech was calm and restrained, but everyone could feel how strongly she cared about protecting the forest.","t":"她的演講平靜而含蓄，但每個人都能感受到她多麼在乎保護森林。"},{"w":"retort","p":"v.","d":"to answer quickly in an angry or clever way","c":"反駁；回嘴","s":"When his sister said he was lazy, he retorted that at least he did not spend all day watching TV.","t":"當姐姐說他懶惰時，他回嘴說至少他沒有整天看電視。","a":"retorted","h":1},{"w":"retort","p":"n.","d":"a quick, angry, or clever answer","c":"反駁；回嘴的話","s":"Her quick retort made the whole class laugh, and even the teacher could not help smiling at how clever it was.","t":"她快速的回嘴讓全班大笑，連老師也忍不住對這麼機智的回答微笑。"},{"w":"a sharp retort","p":"n.phr.","d":"a quick answer that shows anger","c":"尖銳的反駁","s":"The reporter's rude question earned a sharp retort from the mayor, who told him to check his facts before speaking.","t":"記者無禮的問題換來市長尖銳的反駁，市長要他發言前先查清事實。"},{"w":"retrieve","p":"v.","d":"to find something and bring it back","c":"取回；找回","s":"The dog jumped into the lake to retrieve the ball, and it swam back proudly with the ball in its mouth.","t":"那隻狗跳進湖裡取回球，然後嘴裡含著球驕傲地游回來。","h":1},{"w":"retrieval","p":"n.","d":"the act of getting something back","c":"取回；檢索","s":"Data retrieval from a broken phone can cost a lot, so remember to back up your photos to the cloud every week.","t":"從壞掉的手機取回資料可能要花很多錢，所以記得每週把照片備份到雲端。"},{"w":"retrieve data","p":"v.phr.","d":"to get back information from a computer","c":"取回資料","s":"The engineer helped us retrieve data from the damaged computer, including all the reports we had written last month.","t":"工程師幫我們從損壞的電腦取回資料，包括我們上個月寫的所有報告。"},{"w":"golden retriever","p":"n.phr.","d":"a large, gentle dog with long golden hair","c":"黃金獵犬","s":"Our neighbor's golden retriever is so gentle that it lets the children brush its long fur every afternoon in the yard.","t":"鄰居的黃金獵犬非常溫和，每天下午都讓孩子們在院子裡幫它梳長毛。"},{"w":"revelation","p":"n.","d":"a surprising fact that is made known","c":"揭露；意外的發現","s":"It was a revelation to me that my quiet grandfather had been a famous singer when he was young.","t":"得知我安靜的爺爺年輕時曾是著名歌手，對我來說是個意外的發現。","h":1},{"w":"reveal","p":"v.","d":"to make something known or let it be seen","c":"揭露；透露","s":"The teacher refused to reveal the test scores before class, so we all waited nervously until the bell rang.","t":"老師拒絕在上課前公布考試成績，所以我們都緊張地等到鐘聲響起。"},{"w":"revealing","p":"adj.","d":"showing or telling something that was not known","c":"揭露真相的；透露內情的","s":"The documentary was very revealing about how much food restaurants throw away every night, and it changed how I order.","t":"這部紀錄片非常揭露內情地呈現餐廳每晚丟掉多少食物，也改變了我點餐的方式。"},{"w":"reveal a secret","p":"v.phr.","d":"to tell something that was supposed to be hidden","c":"洩漏祕密","s":"She promised never to reveal the secret about the surprise party, but she told her best friend only ten minutes later.","t":"她答應絕不洩漏驚喜派對的祕密，但才過十分鐘她就告訴了最好的朋友。","a":"reveal the secret"},{"w":"revival","p":"n.","d":"the process of becoming popular or active again","c":"復興；復甦","s":"There has been a revival of interest in old Taiwanese songs, and young singers now perform them at concerts and on TV.","t":"人們對老台語歌的興趣出現了復興，年輕歌手現在會在演唱會和電視上演唱這些歌。","h":1},{"w":"revive","p":"v.","d":"to bring someone back to life or health","c":"使復活；使甦醒","s":"The doctors worked for twenty minutes to revive the man who had stopped breathing after he fell into the cold river.","t":"醫生花了二十分鐘才救醒那個掉進冰冷河裡後停止呼吸的男子。","h":1},{"w":"revive","p":"v.","d":"to make someone feel fresh and full of energy again","c":"使恢復活力","s":"A cup of strong coffee and a short walk outside usually revive me when I feel sleepy during the long afternoon.","t":"在漫長的下午感到昏昏欲睡時，一杯濃咖啡和到外面散散步通常能讓我恢復活力。"},{"w":"revive a tradition","p":"v.phr.","d":"to bring back an old custom","c":"復興傳統","s":"The village decided to revive a tradition that had disappeared fifty years ago, and now the dragon boat race is held every June.","t":"這個村子決定復興一項五十年前消失的傳統，現在每年六月都舉辦划龍舟比賽。"},{"w":"revolt","p":"n.","d":"a fight by many people against their government or leader","c":"反叛；起義","s":"The revolt began when farmers refused to pay the new tax, and soon thousands of people marched to the capital.","t":"這場起義始於農民拒絕繳新稅，很快就有數千人遊行到首都。","h":1},{"w":"revolt","p":"v.","d":"to fight against a government or leader","c":"反叛；起來反抗","s":"The soldiers decided to revolt against the cruel general after he ordered them to attack their own villages.","t":"殘暴的將軍命令士兵攻擊自己的村子後，士兵們決定起來反抗他。"},{"w":"revolting","p":"adj.","d":"extremely unpleasant; making you feel sick","c":"令人作嘔的","s":"The milk had been left out in the sun all day, and its revolting smell filled the whole kitchen when I opened the bottle.","t":"那瓶牛奶在太陽下放了一整天，當我打開瓶子時，令人作嘔的氣味充滿了整個廚房。"},{"w":"revolution","p":"n.","d":"a complete change in the way a country is governed","c":"革命","s":"The French Revolution of 1789 changed the country forever, and students around the world still study its causes today.","t":"一七八九年的法國大革命永遠改變了這個國家，世界各地的學生至今仍在研究它的起因。","a":"Revolution"},{"w":"revolve","p":"v.","d":"to move in a circle around a central point","c":"旋轉；繞轉","s":"The Earth takes one year to revolve around the Sun, and this long journey is what gives us the four seasons.","t":"地球繞太陽運行一圈需要一年，這段漫長的旅程就是我們有四季的原因。","h":1},{"w":"revolve around","p":"v.phr.","d":"to have something as the main subject or interest","c":"以…為中心","s":"My little brother's whole life seems to revolve around basketball, so he talks about NBA players at every meal.","t":"我弟弟的整個生活似乎都以籃球為中心，所以他每餐都在談NBA球員。"},{"w":"revolving door","p":"n.phr.","d":"a door that turns around a central post","c":"旋轉門","s":"Be careful when you walk through the revolving door at the hotel entrance, because it moves quickly and can catch your bag.","t":"走過飯店入口的旋轉門時要小心，因為它轉得很快，可能會夾到你的包包。"},{"w":"rigorous","p":"adj.","d":"very careful, strict, and demanding","c":"嚴格的；嚴謹的","s":"The training for firefighters is extremely rigorous, so only the strongest and most careful students finish the whole program.","t":"消防員的訓練極為嚴格，所以只有最強壯、最細心的學員能完成整個課程。","h":1},{"w":"rigorously","p":"adv.","d":"in a very careful and strict way","c":"嚴格地；嚴謹地","s":"Every toy sold in this store is rigorously tested, so parents can be sure that it is safe for babies and small children.","t":"這家店賣的每個玩具都經過嚴格測試，所以家長可以確定它對嬰兒和小孩是安全的。"},{"w":"rigor","p":"n.","d":"great care and strictness","c":"嚴格；嚴謹","s":"Our science teacher asks for rigor in every experiment, so we must write down each step and measure everything twice.","t":"我們的自然老師要求每個實驗都要嚴謹，所以我們必須寫下每個步驟並把所有東西測量兩次。"},{"w":"ripple","p":"n.","d":"a small wave on the surface of water","c":"波紋；漣漪","s":"When the little boy threw a stone into the pond, each ripple spread out slowly until it reached the lotus leaves.","t":"當小男孩把石頭丟進池塘時，每一道漣漪慢慢擴散，直到碰到荷葉。","h":1},{"w":"ripple","p":"v.","d":"to move in small waves","c":"起波紋；泛起漣漪","s":"A soft wind made the surface of the lake ripple, and the lights from the town danced on the moving water.","t":"微風使湖面泛起漣漪，小鎮的燈光在流動的水面上跳舞。"},{"w":"ripple effect","p":"n.phr.","d":"a situation in which one event causes many others","c":"連鎖反應","s":"Closing the only factory in town had a ripple effect: shops lost customers, and many families had to move away to find work.","t":"關閉鎮上唯一的工廠造成了連鎖反應：商店失去顧客，許多家庭不得不搬走去找工作。"},{"w":"rivalry","p":"n.","d":"a situation in which people or teams compete against each other","c":"競爭；對抗","s":"The rivalry between the two high schools is so strong that their yearly basketball game fills the whole gym with cheering fans.","t":"這兩所高中之間的競爭如此激烈，以致於他們每年的籃球賽都讓整個體育館擠滿歡呼的球迷。","h":1},{"w":"rival","p":"n.","d":"a person or team you compete against","c":"競爭對手","s":"Our team's biggest rival is the school across the river, and we have lost to them in the final two years in a row.","t":"我們球隊最大的對手是河對岸的那所學校，我們已經連續兩年在決賽輸給他們。"},{"w":"rival","p":"v.","d":"to be as good as someone or something","c":"與…匹敵；比得上","s":"No other night market in the city can rival this one for the number of food stalls and the size of the crowds.","t":"就小吃攤的數量和人潮的規模來說，這個城市沒有其他夜市能比得上這一個。"},{"w":"sibling rivalry","p":"n.phr.","d":"competition between brothers and sisters","c":"兄弟姊妹間的競爭","s":"Sibling rivalry is common in many families, but my brother and I stopped fighting over toys once we started sharing a room.","t":"兄弟姊妹間的競爭在許多家庭很常見，但我和哥哥開始共用一間房後就不再為玩具吵架了。","a":"Sibling rivalry"},{"w":"roam","p":"v.","d":"to walk or travel around with no clear purpose","c":"漫遊；閒逛","s":"Cows and goats roam freely across the green hills, and farmers only bring them home when the sun goes down.","t":"牛和山羊在綠色的山丘上自由漫遊，農夫只在太陽下山時才把它們帶回家。","h":1},{"w":"roam around","p":"v.phr.","d":"to wander around a place","c":"四處遊蕩；到處走走","s":"On our first day in Kyoto, we had no plan and just decided to roam around the old streets near the river.","t":"在京都的第一天，我們沒有計畫，只是決定在河邊的老街四處走走。"},{"w":"roaming","p":"n.","d":"using your phone on another company's network, especially abroad","c":"（手機）漫遊","s":"Before you travel abroad, turn off data roaming on your phone, or you may get a huge bill when you come home.","t":"出國旅行前，把手機的數據漫遊關掉，否則回家時你可能會收到一大筆帳單。"},{"w":"robust","p":"adj.","d":"strong and healthy","c":"強健的；健壯的","s":"My grandfather is still robust at eighty, and he climbs the stairs to his fifth-floor apartment every day without any help.","t":"我爺爺八十歲了身體仍然強健，他每天不用人幫忙就爬樓梯到五樓的公寓。","h":1},{"w":"robust","p":"adj.","d":"strong and not likely to fail or break","c":"穩健的；堅固的","s":"The company had a robust year, with sales growing in every month despite the rising price of materials.","t":"這家公司度過了穩健的一年，儘管原料價格上漲，每個月的銷售都在成長。"},{"w":"robustly","p":"adv.","d":"in a strong and healthy way","c":"強健地；穩健地","s":"The economy grew robustly last year, and many young people were able to find good jobs soon after graduation.","t":"去年經濟穩健成長，許多年輕人畢業後很快就找到了好工作。"}]},{"unit":32,"theme":"rotate – serving","cards":[{"w":"rotate","p":"v.","d":"to turn around a central point","c":"旋轉；轉動","s":"The Earth takes twenty-four hours to rotate once, and that is why we have day and night in every part of the world.","t":"地球自轉一圈需要二十四小時，這就是為什麼世界各地都有白天和黑夜。","h":1},{"w":"rotation","p":"n.","d":"the act of turning around a central point; a regular turn-taking","c":"旋轉；輪流","s":"One full rotation of the big wheel at the night market takes about fifteen minutes, so you can enjoy the view for a long time.","t":"夜市摩天輪完整旋轉一圈大約需要十五分鐘，所以你可以欣賞風景很久。","h":1},{"w":"rotate","p":"v.","d":"to take turns doing a job","c":"輪流；輪換","s":"The four of us rotate the job of washing the dishes, so each person only has to do it twice a week.","t":"我們四個人輪流洗碗，所以每個人一週只需要洗兩次。"},{"w":"in rotation","p":"phr.","d":"one after another, taking turns","c":"輪流地","s":"The three nurses work the night shift in rotation, so nobody has to stay awake all night more than twice a week.","t":"三位護理師輪流值夜班，所以沒有人一週需要熬夜超過兩次。"},{"w":"rotating","p":"adj.","d":"turning around a central point","c":"旋轉的","s":"The restaurant on the top floor has a slowly rotating floor, so you can see the whole city while you eat your dinner.","t":"頂樓的餐廳有一個緩慢旋轉的地板，所以你可以一邊吃晚餐一邊看到整個城市。"},{"w":"royalty","p":"n.","d":"kings, queens, and members of their families","c":"王室成員；皇族","s":"The hotel has hosted royalty from several countries, and the king of Thailand once stayed in the room next to ours.","t":"這家飯店接待過好幾個國家的王室成員，泰國國王曾經住在我們隔壁的房間。","h":1},{"w":"royalty","p":"n.","d":"money paid to a writer or musician each time their work is sold or used","c":"版稅","s":"The singer still earns royalties every time her old songs are played on the radio or used in a TV commercial.","t":"每當這位歌手的老歌在電台播放或用在電視廣告裡，她仍然可以賺到版稅。","a":"royalties"},{"w":"royal","p":"adj.","d":"belonging to a king or queen","c":"皇家的；王室的","s":"The royal family waved to the crowd from the balcony of the palace, and thousands of people cheered and took photos.","t":"王室家族在宮殿的陽台上向群眾揮手，成千上萬的人歡呼並拍照。"},{"w":"rubbish","p":"n.","d":"things that are thrown away; garbage","c":"垃圾","s":"Please put all the rubbish in the black bag and take it out to the truck when you hear the music at seven o'clock.","t":"請把所有的垃圾放進黑色袋子裡，七點聽到音樂時拿出去給垃圾車。","h":1},{"w":"rubbish","p":"n.","d":"something silly or untrue; nonsense","c":"胡說；廢話","s":"My brother said he could finish the whole pizza by himself, but we all knew that was rubbish because he eats very little.","t":"我哥哥說他可以一個人吃完整個披薩，但我們都知道那是胡說，因為他吃得很少。"},{"w":"rubbish bin","p":"n.phr.","d":"a container for garbage","c":"垃圾桶","s":"There is a rubbish bin at the corner of every street in this park, so there is no excuse for dropping your bottles on the grass.","t":"這個公園每條路的轉角都有一個垃圾桶，所以沒有理由把瓶子丟在草地上。"},{"w":"talk rubbish","p":"v.phr.","d":"to say things that are silly or untrue","c":"胡說八道","s":"Stop talking rubbish and tell me what really happened to the money that was in the kitchen drawer this morning.","t":"別再胡說八道了，告訴我今天早上廚房抽屜裡的錢到底怎麼了。","a":"talking rubbish"},{"w":"rugged","p":"adj.","d":"rough and uneven, with many rocks and hills","c":"崎嶇的；多岩石的","s":"The east coast of Taiwan is famous for its rugged mountains, which rise straight out of the sea and are covered with thick forest.","t":"台灣東海岸以崎嶇的山脈聞名，這些山從海中直直升起，覆蓋著茂密的森林。","h":1},{"w":"rugged","p":"adj.","d":"strong and able to last in hard conditions","c":"堅固耐用的","s":"I bought a rugged phone case for my hiking trips because my old phone broke the last time I dropped it on a rock.","t":"我為登山旅行買了一個堅固耐用的手機殼，因為上次我的舊手機掉在石頭上就摔壞了。"},{"w":"ruggedly","p":"adv.","d":"in a strong, rough way","c":"粗獷地","s":"The actor is ruggedly handsome, with a strong jaw and a beard, so he is often chosen to play soldiers and cowboys.","t":"這位演員長得粗獷帥氣，有結實的下巴和鬍子，所以常被選來演士兵和牛仔。"},{"w":"ruthless","p":"adj.","d":"cruel and not caring about hurting others","c":"無情的；殘忍的","s":"The ruthless businessman closed the factory and fired five hundred workers just one week before Chinese New Year.","t":"那位無情的商人在農曆新年前一週關閉工廠，解僱了五百名工人。","h":1},{"w":"ruthlessly","p":"adv.","d":"in a cruel way without any pity","c":"無情地","s":"The coach ruthlessly cut anyone who arrived late to practice, so every player made sure to be on the field by six.","t":"教練無情地淘汰任何練習遲到的人，所以每位球員都確保六點前到球場。"},{"w":"ruthlessness","p":"n.","d":"the quality of being cruel and showing no pity","c":"冷酷無情","s":"The general was known for his ruthlessness, and he never showed mercy to the soldiers who lost a battle.","t":"這位將軍以冷酷無情聞名，他從不對打敗仗的士兵手下留情。"},{"w":"salute","p":"v.","d":"to raise your hand to your head to show respect, especially in the army","c":"敬禮","s":"The young soldiers must salute every officer they pass on the base, so their right hands go up many times a day.","t":"年輕士兵必須向基地裡經過的每位軍官敬禮，所以他們的右手一天要舉起很多次。","h":1},{"w":"salute","p":"n.","d":"the act of raising your hand to show respect","c":"敬禮；致敬","s":"At the end of the parade, the whole crowd stood up and gave a salute to the firefighters who had saved the town.","t":"遊行結束時，全體群眾起立向拯救小鎮的消防員致敬。"},{"w":"salute","p":"v.","d":"to praise or honor someone publicly","c":"向…致敬；讚揚","s":"Tonight we salute the teachers who have worked at this school for more than thirty years and taught two generations of students.","t":"今晚我們向在這所學校服務超過三十年、教過兩代學生的老師們致敬。"},{"w":"salvage","p":"v.","d":"to save things from a place that has been damaged","c":"搶救；打撈","s":"After the flood, the family tried to salvage their photos and important papers from the mud, but most of them were ruined.","t":"洪水過後，這家人試著從泥巴裡搶救照片和重要文件，但大部分都毀了。","h":1},{"w":"salvage","p":"n.","d":"the act of saving things from a wreck or disaster","c":"打撈；搶救","s":"The salvage of the sunken ship took two years, and divers brought up gold coins that had been underwater for three centuries.","t":"沉船的打撈工作花了兩年，潛水員撈起了在水下三個世紀的金幣。"},{"w":"salvage a situation","p":"v.phr.","d":"to make a bad situation better","c":"挽救局面","s":"Our picnic was ruined by rain, but Dad managed to salvage the situation by moving everything into the car and driving to a covered park.","t":"我們的野餐被雨毀了，但爸爸把所有東西搬進車裡，開到一個有屋頂的公園，成功挽救了局面。","a":"salvage the situation"},{"w":"sanitation","p":"n.","d":"systems that keep places clean and healthy, such as toilets and clean water","c":"衛生設備；公共衛生","s":"Poor sanitation in the crowded camp caused many people to get sick, so doctors asked for clean toilets and running water first.","t":"擁擠營地裡糟糕的衛生設備讓許多人生病，所以醫生首先要求乾淨的廁所和自來水。","h":1},{"w":"sanitary","p":"adj.","d":"clean and not likely to cause illness","c":"衛生的","s":"The kitchen must be kept in a sanitary condition at all times, so workers wash the floor and tables after every meal.","t":"廚房必須隨時保持衛生的狀態，所以員工每餐後都會清洗地板和桌子。"},{"w":"sanitize","p":"v.","d":"to clean something so that it is free of germs","c":"消毒","s":"Please sanitize your hands before entering the hospital ward, because many of the patients there get sick very easily.","t":"進入病房前請先消毒雙手，因為那裡許多病人很容易生病。"},{"w":"sanitizer","p":"n.","d":"a liquid or gel that kills germs","c":"消毒劑","s":"During the pandemic, every store placed a bottle of hand sanitizer by the door so that customers could clean their hands.","t":"疫情期間，每家商店都在門口放一瓶乾洗手消毒液，讓顧客可以清潔雙手。"},{"w":"savage","p":"adj.","d":"very violent and cruel; wild","c":"野蠻的；兇猛的","s":"The hikers were lucky to escape the savage attack of the wild bear, which had been protecting its two cubs nearby.","t":"登山客很幸運地逃過了野熊兇猛的攻擊，那隻熊當時正在保護附近的兩隻小熊。","h":1},{"w":"savage","p":"n.","d":"a person who is wild and not civilized (an old, unfair word)","c":"野蠻人","s":"In old movies, people from faraway lands were often shown as savages, which we now know was unfair and untrue.","t":"在老電影裡，來自遙遠土地的人常被描繪成野蠻人，我們現在知道那是不公平也不真實的。","a":"savages"},{"w":"savage","p":"v.","d":"to attack violently; to criticize very strongly","c":"猛烈攻擊；嚴厲批評","s":"The film critics savaged the new movie, calling it the worst comedy of the year, but teenagers still lined up to see it.","t":"影評人嚴厲批評這部新電影，稱它為年度最糟的喜劇，但青少年仍然排隊去看。","a":"savaged"},{"w":"savagely","p":"adv.","d":"in a violent and cruel way","c":"野蠻地；猛烈地","s":"The storm hit the small island savagely, tearing roofs off houses and throwing fishing boats onto the road.","t":"暴風雨猛烈地襲擊這座小島，掀掉房屋的屋頂，還把漁船拋到馬路上。"},{"w":"scenic","p":"adj.","d":"having beautiful views of nature","c":"風景優美的","s":"We took the scenic route along the coast instead of the highway, and the drive took longer but the views were amazing.","t":"我們選擇沿海岸的風景優美的路線而不是高速公路，開車時間比較長，但景色美極了。","h":1},{"w":"scenery","p":"n.","d":"the natural things you can see in the countryside, such as mountains and rivers","c":"風景；景色","s":"The scenery in Taroko Gorge is so beautiful that visitors often stop every few minutes to take more photos.","t":"太魯閣峽谷的風景美得讓遊客常常每隔幾分鐘就停下來多拍幾張照片。"},{"w":"scene","p":"n.","d":"the place where something happens; a part of a film or play","c":"現場；場景","s":"The police arrived at the scene of the accident within five minutes and quickly moved the cars to the side of the road.","t":"警察在五分鐘內抵達事故現場，很快就把車子移到路邊。"},{"w":"scenic spot","p":"n.phr.","d":"a place that people visit because of its beautiful views","c":"風景區；景點","s":"Sun Moon Lake is the most popular scenic spot in central Taiwan, and the lake is especially lovely in the early morning mist.","t":"日月潭是台灣中部最受歡迎的風景區，清晨薄霧中的湖面特別美。"},{"w":"scorn","p":"n.","d":"a strong feeling that someone or something is worthless or stupid","c":"輕蔑；鄙視","s":"The old farmer looked at the city boy's soft hands with scorn, sure that he would give up after one day in the fields.","t":"老農夫輕蔑地看著城市男孩柔軟的雙手，確信他在田裡待一天就會放棄。","h":1},{"w":"scorn","p":"v.","d":"to show that you think someone or something is worthless","c":"輕視；嘲笑","s":"Some people scorn cheap clothes from the night market, but I think they are perfect for everyday wear and easy to wash.","t":"有些人看不起夜市的便宜衣服，但我覺得它們非常適合日常穿著，而且容易清洗。"},{"w":"scornful","p":"adj.","d":"showing that you think someone or something is worthless","c":"輕蔑的","s":"She gave a scornful laugh when her brother said he would run a marathon, since he had never even run one kilometer.","t":"當哥哥說他要跑馬拉松時，她輕蔑地笑了，因為他連一公里都沒跑過。"},{"w":"scornfully","p":"adv.","d":"in a way that shows scorn","c":"輕蔑地","s":"\"You call that a painting?\" the art teacher said scornfully, and the student quietly rolled up his work and left the room.","t":"「你說那是一幅畫？」美術老師輕蔑地說，學生默默捲起作品離開了教室。"},{"w":"scrape","p":"v.","d":"to remove something by pulling a hard tool across a surface","c":"刮；刮掉","s":"Every winter morning my father has to scrape the ice off the car windows before he can drive to work.","t":"每個冬天的早晨，我爸爸都必須先刮掉車窗上的冰才能開車上班。","h":1},{"w":"scrape","p":"n.","d":"a small injury where skin has been rubbed off","c":"擦傷","s":"Lily fell off her bike on the way to school, but luckily she only got a small scrape on her knee and no broken bones.","t":"莉莉上學途中從腳踏車上摔下來，但幸運的是她膝蓋上只有一點小擦傷，沒有骨折。"},{"w":"scrape by","p":"v.phr.","d":"to manage to live with very little money","c":"勉強過活","s":"When my parents were young, they had to scrape by on very little money, sometimes eating only rice and eggs for a week.","t":"我父母年輕時必須靠很少的錢勉強過活，有時一整個星期只吃白飯和雞蛋。"},{"w":"scrape together","p":"v.phr.","d":"to collect enough money with difficulty","c":"湊足；東拼西湊","s":"The students managed to scrape together enough money to buy a cake for their teacher's birthday by asking everyone for fifty dollars.","t":"學生們向每個人收五十元，終於湊足了錢買蛋糕慶祝老師的生日。"},{"w":"screwdriver","p":"n.","d":"a tool used for turning screws","c":"螺絲起子","s":"Hand me the screwdriver from the toolbox, because this shelf will fall down if I do not tighten the loose screws right now.","t":"把工具箱裡的螺絲起子遞給我，因為如果我現在不把鬆掉的螺絲鎖緊，這個架子會倒下來。","h":1},{"w":"screw","p":"n.","d":"a thin piece of metal with a sharp point that is turned to hold things together","c":"螺絲","s":"One screw is missing from the back of the chair, which is why it makes a strange noise every time someone sits down.","t":"椅背少了一顆螺絲，這就是為什麼每次有人坐下時它都會發出奇怪的聲音。"},{"w":"screw","p":"v.","d":"to fasten or close something by turning it","c":"用螺絲固定；旋緊","s":"Please screw the lid on tightly after you use the jar, or the cookies inside will go soft by tomorrow morning.","t":"用完罐子後請把蓋子旋緊，否則裡面的餅乾到明天早上就會變軟。"},{"w":"screw up","p":"v.phr.","d":"to do something badly; to make a big mistake","c":"搞砸","s":"I really screwed up my speech by forgetting the ending, but my teacher said the first part was very good.","t":"我忘了結尾，真的把演講搞砸了，但老師說前半部分非常好。","a":"screwed up"},{"w":"scroll","p":"v.","d":"to move text or pictures up or down on a screen","c":"捲動（畫面）；滑（手機）","s":"Many people scroll through their phones for hours before bed, which makes it harder for them to fall asleep at night.","t":"許多人睡前滑手機好幾個小時，這讓他們晚上更難入睡。","h":1},{"w":"scroll","p":"n.","d":"a long roll of paper with writing or pictures on it","c":"捲軸","s":"The museum keeps an old Chinese scroll with a beautiful painting of mountains, and it is only shown to the public once a year.","t":"博物館收藏著一幅畫有美麗山景的中國古捲軸，一年只對民眾展出一次。"},{"w":"scroll down","p":"v.phr.","d":"to move down a page on a screen","c":"向下捲動","s":"Scroll down to the bottom of the page and click the green button to send your answers to the teacher.","t":"向下捲動到頁面底部，然後點綠色按鈕把你的答案送給老師。","a":"Scroll down"},{"w":"scrutiny","p":"n.","d":"careful and detailed examination","c":"細查；審查","s":"The new company came under close scrutiny after reporters found that its advertisements made promises that were not true.","t":"記者發現這家新公司的廣告做出不實承諾後，它受到了嚴密的審查。","h":1},{"w":"scrutinize","p":"v.","d":"to examine something very carefully","c":"仔細檢查","s":"The judges will scrutinize every detail of your science project, so make sure all your numbers and labels are correct.","t":"評審會仔細檢查你科學專題的每個細節，所以要確保所有數字和標籤都正確。"},{"w":"under scrutiny","p":"phr.","d":"being examined carefully","c":"受到審查","s":"The mayor's spending has been under scrutiny since the newspaper reported his expensive trips abroad paid for by the city.","t":"自從報紙報導市長由市政府出錢的昂貴出國旅行後，他的開支就一直受到審查。"},{"w":"sculptor","p":"n.","d":"an artist who makes figures from stone, wood, or metal","c":"雕塑家","s":"The sculptor spent two whole years turning a huge block of stone into the lion that now stands outside the city hall.","t":"這位雕塑家花了整整兩年，把一塊巨大的石頭變成現在立在市政府外的那頭獅子。","h":1},{"w":"sculpture","p":"n.","d":"a work of art made from stone, wood, or metal","c":"雕塑；雕像","s":"In the middle of the park there is a bronze sculpture of a mother holding her child, and people often leave flowers beside it.","t":"公園中央有一座母親抱著孩子的青銅雕像，人們常在旁邊放花。"},{"w":"sculpt","p":"v.","d":"to make a figure by shaping stone, wood, or clay","c":"雕刻；雕塑","s":"At the art camp, the children learned to sculpt small animals out of clay and then painted them in bright colors.","t":"在美術營裡，孩子們學會用黏土雕塑小動物，然後把它們塗上鮮豔的顏色。"},{"w":"seagull","p":"n.","d":"a large gray and white bird that lives near the sea","c":"海鷗","s":"A seagull flew down and stole the sandwich right out of my hand while I was sitting on the beach at Kenting.","t":"我坐在墾丁的海灘上時，一隻海鷗飛下來，直接從我手裡偷走了三明治。","h":1},{"w":"gull","p":"n.","d":"a seagull","c":"鷗；海鷗","s":"The fishermen know that a crowd of gulls flying over the water usually means there is a large group of fish below.","t":"漁夫們知道，一群海鷗在水面上飛通常表示下面有一大群魚。","a":"gulls"},{"w":"a flock of seagulls","p":"n.phr.","d":"a large group of seagulls","c":"一群海鷗","s":"As the boat came into the harbor, a flock of seagulls followed it closely, hoping to catch any fish the fishermen threw away.","t":"船駛進港口時，一群海鷗緊緊跟著它，希望能抓到漁夫丟掉的魚。"},{"w":"seduce","p":"v.","d":"to persuade someone to do something by making it seem very attractive","c":"引誘；誘惑","s":"Bright signs and cheap prices seduce many shoppers into buying things that they do not really need or even want.","t":"鮮豔的招牌和便宜的價格誘使許多購物者買下他們其實不需要、甚至不想要的東西。","h":1},{"w":"seductive","p":"adj.","d":"very attractive and hard to say no to","c":"誘人的","s":"The smell of fresh coffee from the shop was so seductive that I walked in even though I had promised to save money.","t":"店裡飄出的新鮮咖啡香氣太誘人了，儘管我答應過要省錢，還是走了進去。"},{"w":"seduction","p":"n.","d":"the power to attract someone into doing something","c":"誘惑","s":"The seduction of easy money leads some young people to join groups that later get them into serious trouble.","t":"輕鬆賺錢的誘惑讓一些年輕人加入某些團體，後來卻讓他們惹上嚴重的麻煩。"},{"w":"selective","p":"adj.","d":"careful about what or who you choose","c":"精挑細選的；選擇性的","s":"The university is very selective and accepts only one in every twenty students who apply to its medical school each year.","t":"這所大學非常挑剔，每年申請醫學院的學生中只錄取二十分之一。","h":1},{"w":"select","p":"v.","d":"to choose carefully","c":"選擇；挑選","s":"Please select three books from the reading list and write a short report on each of them before the end of May.","t":"請從閱讀清單中挑選三本書，並在五月底前為每本書寫一篇短篇報告。"},{"w":"selection","p":"n.","d":"the act of choosing; a range of things to choose from","c":"選擇；精選品","s":"The bakery offers a wide selection of breads and cakes, so it takes me a long time to decide what to buy.","t":"這家麵包店提供多種麵包和蛋糕可供選擇，所以我總要花很長時間才能決定買什麼。"},{"w":"selectively","p":"adv.","d":"in a careful, choosing way","c":"有選擇地","s":"A good reader reads selectively, choosing the parts of a long article that matter most instead of trying to remember everything.","t":"一個好的讀者會有選擇地閱讀，挑出長篇文章中最重要的部分，而不是試圖記住所有內容。"},{"w":"serene","p":"adj.","d":"calm, peaceful, and quiet","c":"平靜的；安詳的","s":"The lake was so serene in the early morning that the mountains were reflected in it like a perfect mirror.","t":"清晨的湖面非常平靜，群山倒映在湖中就像一面完美的鏡子。","h":1},{"w":"serenity","p":"n.","d":"the state of being calm and peaceful","c":"平靜；寧靜","s":"After a busy week in the city, my grandmother finds serenity in her small garden, where she waters the flowers at sunrise.","t":"在城市忙碌了一週後，我奶奶在她的小花園裡找到寧靜，每天日出時在那裡澆花。"},{"w":"serenely","p":"adv.","d":"in a calm and peaceful way","c":"平靜地；安詳地","s":"The old monk smiled serenely at the noisy tourists and went on sweeping the temple steps as if nothing had happened.","t":"老和尚安詳地對吵鬧的遊客微笑，繼續掃著寺廟的台階，彷彿什麼事都沒發生。"},{"w":"sergeant","p":"n.","d":"a soldier or police officer of middle rank","c":"中士；巡佐","s":"The sergeant ordered the new soldiers to clean their boots again, because he found mud on three pairs during the morning check.","t":"中士命令新兵再把靴子清理一遍，因為他在早上檢查時發現三雙靴子上有泥。","h":1},{"w":"police sergeant","p":"n.phr.","d":"a police officer of middle rank","c":"警察巡佐","s":"A police sergeant came to our school to teach us how to stay safe online and what to do if a stranger messages us.","t":"一位警察巡佐來我們學校教我們如何在網路上保持安全，以及陌生人傳訊息給我們時該怎麼辦。"},{"w":"drill sergeant","p":"n.phr.","d":"a soldier who trains new soldiers very strictly","c":"教育班長；訓練士官","s":"Our PE teacher acts like a drill sergeant, shouting at us to run faster and do ten more push-ups every single class.","t":"我們的體育老師像個教育班長，每堂課都對我們大喊要跑快一點、再做十個伏地挺身。"},{"w":"serial","p":"adj.","d":"doing the same bad thing many times; happening in a series","c":"連續的；連續犯案的","s":"The police finally caught the serial thief who had broken into more than twenty homes in the same neighborhood over six months.","t":"警方終於抓到了那個六個月內在同一個社區闖入二十多戶人家的連續竊賊。","h":1},{"w":"serial number","p":"n.phr.","d":"a number printed on a product to identify it","c":"序號","s":"Write down the serial number of your new laptop and keep it somewhere safe, because the police will need it if the computer is stolen.","t":"把你新筆電的序號記下來並放在安全的地方，因為如果電腦被偷，警察會需要它。"},{"w":"series","p":"n.","d":"a number of things or events that come one after another; a TV show with many episodes","c":"系列；連續劇","s":"My sister watched the whole series in one weekend, all twelve episodes, and now she cannot wait for the next season.","t":"我姐姐一個週末就看完了整部影集，全部十二集，現在她等不及要看下一季。"},{"w":"serialize","p":"v.","d":"to publish a story in parts, one after another","c":"連載","s":"The newspaper decided to serialize the famous novel, printing one chapter every Sunday for almost a year.","t":"這家報社決定連載這本著名小說，每個星期天刊登一章，持續了將近一年。"},{"w":"sermon","p":"n.","d":"a talk about religion given by a priest or minister in church","c":"講道；佈道","s":"The priest's sermon on Sunday was about forgiveness, and he asked everyone to call a person they had argued with that week.","t":"牧師星期天的講道主題是寬恕，他請每個人打電話給那週曾與自己爭吵的人。","h":1},{"w":"sermon","p":"n.","d":"a long talk telling someone how they should behave","c":"說教；訓話","s":"Every time I come home late, my father gives me a long sermon about safety, even though I always send him a message first.","t":"每次我晚回家，爸爸都會對我長篇說教談安全問題，儘管我總是先傳訊息給他。"},{"w":"give a sermon","p":"v.phr.","d":"to speak to people in church about religion","c":"講道","s":"The young priest was nervous about having to give a sermon in front of five hundred people on his very first Sunday at the church.","t":"年輕的牧師對於第一個星期天就要在教堂裡對五百人講道感到很緊張。"},{"w":"serving","p":"n.","d":"an amount of food for one person","c":"一份（食物）","s":"One serving of this rice is enough for a child, but my teenage brother usually eats three servings at dinner.","t":"一份這種飯對小孩來說夠了，但我十幾歲的弟弟晚餐通常要吃三份。","h":1},{"w":"serve","p":"v.","d":"to give food or drink to people; to do work for people","c":"供應（餐點）；服務","s":"The restaurant will serve free dessert to anyone who has a birthday today, so remember to bring your ID card.","t":"這家餐廳會為今天生日的人提供免費甜點，所以記得帶身分證。"},{"w":"servant","p":"n.","d":"a person whose job is to work in someone else's house","c":"僕人","s":"In the old days, rich families had a servant to cook, clean, and open the door for guests, but today most people do these things themselves.","t":"以前有錢人家有僕人負責煮飯、打掃和為客人開門，但現在大多數人都自己做這些事。"},{"w":"service","p":"n.","d":"the help that people in a shop, hotel, or restaurant give you","c":"服務","s":"The service at the new hotel was excellent, and the staff even remembered our names after the first day.","t":"新飯店的服務非常好，員工在第一天之後甚至記住了我們的名字。"},{"w":"serve as","p":"v.phr.","d":"to be used as something","c":"作為；充當","s":"The old train station now serves as a museum, where visitors can learn how people traveled a hundred years ago.","t":"這座舊火車站現在作為博物館，遊客可以在這裡了解一百年前人們如何旅行。","a":"serves as"}]},{"unit":33,"theme":"setback – smuggle","cards":[{"w":"setback","p":"n.","d":"a problem that stops you from making progress for a while","c":"挫折；阻礙","s":"Losing the first game was a big setback for our team, but the coach told us to learn from it and keep training hard.","t":"輸掉第一場比賽對我們球隊是個很大的挫折，但教練要我們從中學習並繼續努力訓練。","h":1},{"w":"set back","p":"v.phr.","d":"to delay something; to cost someone a lot of money","c":"使延後；耗費","s":"The heavy rain set back the building work by two weeks, so the new library will not open until the end of March.","t":"大雨讓建築工程延後了兩週，所以新圖書館要到三月底才會開放。"},{"w":"suffer a setback","p":"v.phr.","d":"to have a problem that slows your progress","c":"遭遇挫折","s":"The young singer suffered a setback when she lost her voice a week before the big concert, but she recovered in time.","t":"這位年輕歌手在大型演唱會前一週失聲，遭遇了挫折，但她及時康復了。","a":"suffered a setback"},{"w":"shabby","p":"adj.","d":"old and in bad condition; poorly dressed","c":"破舊的；寒酸的","s":"The old man wore a shabby coat with holes in the sleeves, but he always gave a warm smile to everyone he met.","t":"那位老人穿著一件袖子有破洞的破舊外套，但他總是對遇到的每個人露出溫暖的微笑。","h":1},{"w":"shabbily","p":"adv.","d":"in a poor or unfair way","c":"寒酸地；不公平地","s":"The guests were shabbily treated at the hotel: their room was dirty, and nobody answered when they called the front desk.","t":"客人在飯店受到糟糕的對待：房間很髒，打電話到櫃台也沒人接。"},{"w":"shabbiness","p":"n.","d":"the state of being old and in bad condition","c":"破舊；寒酸","s":"Despite the shabbiness of the little restaurant, with its broken chairs and old walls, the noodles there are the best in town.","t":"儘管這家小餐館很破舊，椅子壞了、牆也老舊，那裡的麵卻是鎮上最好吃的。"},{"w":"sharpen","p":"v.","d":"to make something sharp or sharper","c":"削尖；磨利","s":"Before the cooking class, the chef showed us how to sharpen a knife safely so that it cuts vegetables cleanly.","t":"烹飪課開始前，主廚示範如何安全地磨利刀子，好讓它能乾淨俐落地切蔬菜。","h":1},{"w":"sharp","p":"adj.","d":"having a thin edge or point that can cut","c":"鋒利的；尖的","s":"Be careful with that knife; it is very sharp, and you could cut your finger badly if you hold it the wrong way.","t":"小心那把刀；它非常鋒利，如果拿的方式不對，你可能會把手指割得很深。"},{"w":"sharpener","p":"n.","d":"a tool for making pencils or knives sharp","c":"削鉛筆機；磨刀器","s":"I left my pencil sharpener at home, so I had to borrow one from my classmate before the drawing test started.","t":"我把削鉛筆機忘在家裡，所以繪畫測驗開始前得向同學借一個。"},{"w":"sharpen one's skills","p":"v.phr.","d":"to improve your ability to do something","c":"磨練技能","s":"Many students join the debate club to sharpen their skills in speaking English in front of other people.","t":"許多學生加入辯論社，以磨練在眾人面前說英語的技巧。","a":"sharpen their skills"},{"w":"shaver","p":"n.","d":"an electric tool for removing hair from the face or body","c":"電動刮鬍刀","s":"My father uses an electric shaver every morning because it is faster and safer than a razor with a blade.","t":"我爸爸每天早上都用電動刮鬍刀，因為它比有刀片的剃刀更快也更安全。","h":1},{"w":"shave","p":"v.","d":"to cut hair off your face or body with a razor","c":"刮（鬍子）；剃","s":"My older brother has to shave every day now, and he complains that it takes him ten extra minutes in the morning.","t":"我哥哥現在每天都得刮鬍子，他抱怨這讓他早上多花十分鐘。"},{"w":"shave","p":"n.","d":"the act of shaving","c":"刮鬍子","s":"After a long week of camping without a mirror, Dad was happy to have a hot shower and a clean shave.","t":"在沒有鏡子的露營一週後，爸爸很高興能洗個熱水澡，好好刮個鬍子。"},{"w":"shortcoming","p":"n.","d":"a fault or weakness in someone or something","c":"缺點；短處","s":"The new phone has one big shortcoming: its battery only lasts about five hours if you watch videos on it.","t":"這款新手機有一個很大的缺點：如果用它看影片，電池只能撐大約五個小時。","h":1},{"w":"shortage","p":"n.","d":"a situation in which there is not enough of something","c":"短缺；不足","s":"There was a shortage of eggs across the island last spring, so many breakfast shops raised their prices or stopped selling egg sandwiches.","t":"去年春天全島雞蛋短缺，所以許多早餐店漲價或停賣蛋三明治。"},{"w":"shorten","p":"v.","d":"to make something shorter","c":"縮短","s":"The teacher decided to shorten the test from fifty questions to thirty because the class had lost two days to the typhoon.","t":"因為颱風讓班上少上了兩天課，老師決定把考試從五十題縮短為三十題。"},{"w":"fall short of","p":"v.phr.","d":"to fail to reach a goal or standard","c":"未達到；不足","s":"Our class fell short of the goal of collecting one thousand bottles, but we still recycled more than any other class.","t":"我們班沒有達到收集一千個瓶子的目標，但我們回收的數量仍然比其他任何班級多。","a":"fell short of"},{"w":"shortsighted","p":"adj.","d":"not able to see things clearly when they are far away","c":"近視的","s":"My sister is shortsighted and cannot read the board from the back of the classroom, so she always sits in the front row.","t":"我妹妹近視，從教室後面看不清黑板，所以她總是坐在第一排。","h":1},{"w":"shortsighted","p":"adj.","d":"not thinking about what will happen in the future","c":"短視的；目光短淺的","s":"Cutting down the whole forest to sell the wood is a shortsighted plan, because the village will lose its clean water and tourists.","t":"砍掉整片森林賣木材是個短視的計畫，因為村子會失去乾淨的水源和觀光客。"},{"w":"shortsightedness","p":"n.","d":"the failure to think about the future","c":"短視；目光短淺","s":"The company's shortsightedness cost it dearly: it saved money by not training workers, and then lost its best staff to other firms.","t":"這家公司的短視讓它付出慘痛代價：它省下訓練員工的錢，之後卻把最好的員工輸給了其他公司。"},{"w":"shred","p":"v.","d":"to cut or tear something into very small pieces","c":"撕碎；切碎","s":"Please shred these old bank letters before you throw them away so that nobody can read your account number.","t":"請在丟掉這些舊的銀行信件前先把它們撕碎，這樣就沒有人能看到你的帳號。","h":1},{"w":"shred","p":"n.","d":"a small, thin piece torn or cut from something","c":"碎片；細條","s":"The strong wind tore the kite into shreds, and the children sadly picked up the pieces of paper from the grass.","t":"強風把風箏撕成碎片，孩子們難過地從草地上撿起紙片。","a":"shreds"},{"w":"shredder","p":"n.","d":"a machine that cuts paper into thin strips","c":"碎紙機","s":"Our office bought a paper shredder last month, and now all documents with customer names are destroyed before being recycled.","t":"我們辦公室上個月買了一台碎紙機，現在所有有客戶姓名的文件在回收前都會先銷毀。"},{"w":"not a shred of","p":"phr.","d":"not even a very small amount of something","c":"一點…也沒有","s":"The police found not a shred of evidence against the man, so they had to let him go home the same evening.","t":"警方完全沒有找到對那名男子不利的證據，所以當天晚上就必須放他回家。"},{"w":"shriek","p":"v.","d":"to give a loud, high cry because of fear, excitement, or pain","c":"尖叫","s":"The girls shrieked with excitement when their favorite singer walked onto the stage and waved to the crowd.","t":"當她們最喜歡的歌手走上舞台向群眾揮手時，女孩們興奮地尖叫。","a":"shrieked","h":1},{"w":"shriek","p":"n.","d":"a loud, high cry","c":"尖叫聲","s":"A loud shriek came from the kitchen, and we ran in to find my mother standing on a chair, pointing at a tiny mouse.","t":"廚房傳來一聲響亮的尖叫，我們跑進去，發現媽媽站在椅子上指著一隻小老鼠。"},{"w":"shriek with laughter","p":"v.phr.","d":"to laugh very loudly","c":"尖聲大笑","s":"The children shrieked with laughter as the clown fell over his own giant shoes for the third time during the show.","t":"表演中小丑第三次被自己的大鞋子絆倒時，孩子們尖聲大笑。","a":"shrieked with laughter"},{"w":"shrub","p":"n.","d":"a plant like a small tree with many woody stems","c":"灌木","s":"My grandmother planted a row of small shrubs along the fence, and in spring they are covered with tiny pink flowers.","t":"我奶奶沿著籬笆種了一排小灌木，春天時它們開滿了小小的粉紅色花朵。","a":"shrubs","h":1},{"w":"shrubbery","p":"n.","d":"an area where many shrubs grow close together","c":"灌木叢","s":"The cat hid in the thick shrubbery beside the house and refused to come out until the fireworks had finished.","t":"貓躲在屋子旁邊茂密的灌木叢裡，直到煙火結束才肯出來。"},{"w":"evergreen shrub","p":"n.phr.","d":"a shrub that keeps its green leaves all year","c":"常綠灌木","s":"The garden center sells an evergreen shrub that stays green all year, so your yard will not look empty in winter.","t":"園藝中心賣一種全年常綠的常綠灌木，這樣你的院子在冬天就不會看起來光禿禿的。"},{"w":"shuffle","p":"v.","d":"to walk slowly without lifting your feet off the ground","c":"拖著腳走","s":"The tired old man shuffled slowly across the room in his slippers, holding the wall for support as he went.","t":"疲憊的老人穿著拖鞋慢慢地拖著腳走過房間，一邊扶著牆支撐自己。","a":"shuffled","h":1},{"w":"shuffle","p":"v.","d":"to mix playing cards before a game","c":"洗牌","s":"Let me shuffle the cards properly before we start the game, because you got all the best cards in the last round.","t":"開始遊戲前讓我好好洗牌，因為上一輪最好的牌全都在你手上。"},{"w":"shuffle","p":"v.","d":"to play songs in a random order","c":"隨機播放","s":"I like to shuffle my playlist on long bus rides so that I never know which song is coming next.","t":"坐長途巴士時我喜歡隨機播放我的播放清單，這樣我永遠不知道下一首是什麼歌。"},{"w":"shuffle","p":"n.","d":"a slow walk without lifting the feet; the act of mixing cards","c":"拖著腳走；洗牌","s":"With a tired shuffle of his feet, the boy walked to the front of the class to read his homework aloud.","t":"男孩疲憊地拖著腳步走到教室前面，大聲朗讀他的作業。"},{"w":"shutter","p":"n.","d":"a wooden or metal cover that closes over a window or shop front","c":"百葉窗；鐵捲門","s":"Before the typhoon arrived, the shop owners closed every shutter and tied down the signs outside their doors.","t":"颱風來臨前，店家關上每一扇鐵捲門，並把門外的招牌綁好。","h":1},{"w":"shutter","p":"n.","d":"the part of a camera that opens to let light in","c":"快門","s":"The camera's shutter opened and closed so fast that the photo of the running horse was perfectly clear.","t":"相機的快門開合得非常快，所以奔跑中的馬的照片非常清晰。"},{"w":"shutter","p":"v.","d":"to close a business or building permanently","c":"關閉（商店、工廠）","s":"The company decided to shutter its three oldest stores and move all its business online by next summer.","t":"這家公司決定關閉三家最老的門市，並在明年夏天前把所有生意移到網路上。"},{"w":"shut","p":"v.","d":"to close something","c":"關上；關閉","s":"Please shut the window before you leave the room, because it looks like it is going to rain this afternoon.","t":"離開房間前請把窗戶關上，因為今天下午看起來要下雨了。"},{"w":"simplicity","p":"n.","d":"the quality of being simple and easy","c":"簡單；簡樸","s":"The beauty of this Japanese garden lies in its simplicity: just white stones, a few trees, and a small pool of water.","t":"這座日本庭園的美在於它的簡樸：只有白色石頭、幾棵樹和一個小水池。","h":1},{"w":"simplify","p":"v.","d":"to make something easier to do or understand","c":"簡化","s":"The teacher tried to simplify the difficult grammar rule by drawing a picture on the board, and suddenly everyone understood.","t":"老師試著在黑板上畫圖來簡化這條困難的文法規則，突然間大家都懂了。","h":1},{"w":"simple","p":"adj.","d":"easy to understand or do; not complicated","c":"簡單的","s":"The recipe is very simple, with only four ingredients, so even a child can make these cookies without help.","t":"這個食譜非常簡單，只有四種材料，所以連小孩都能不用幫忙做出這些餅乾。"},{"w":"simply","p":"adv.","d":"just; only; in a simple way","c":"只是；僅僅；簡單地","s":"I simply forgot about the meeting, so I owe my teammates an apology for leaving them waiting for half an hour.","t":"我只是忘了那場會議，所以我該向隊友道歉，讓他們等了半小時。"},{"w":"simplification","p":"n.","d":"the act of making something simpler","c":"簡化","s":"The simplification of the application form was welcomed by everyone, because the old one had taken an hour to fill in.","t":"申請表的簡化受到大家的歡迎，因為舊的表格要花一個小時才能填完。"},{"w":"simultaneous","p":"adj.","d":"happening at exactly the same time","c":"同時的","s":"The two explosions were simultaneous, so people in the city heard only one loud bang and did not know what had happened.","t":"兩次爆炸是同時的，所以城裡的人只聽到一聲巨響，不知道發生了什麼事。","h":1},{"w":"simultaneously","p":"adv.","d":"at exactly the same time","c":"同時地","s":"It is hard to listen to the teacher and text your friends simultaneously, which is why phones are not allowed in class.","t":"很難同時聽老師講課又傳訊息給朋友，這就是為什麼上課不准用手機。"},{"w":"simultaneous interpretation","p":"n.phr.","d":"translating speech into another language while the person is still speaking","c":"同步口譯","s":"At the international meeting, simultaneous interpretation was provided through headphones so that guests from twenty countries could all understand.","t":"在這場國際會議上，透過耳機提供同步口譯，讓來自二十個國家的來賓都能聽懂。"},{"w":"skeptical","p":"adj.","d":"not sure that something is true or will work","c":"懷疑的","s":"I am skeptical about the advertisement that promises you can learn English in just one week without any effort.","t":"我對那則承諾一週內不用努力就能學會英文的廣告感到懷疑。","h":1},{"w":"skeptic","p":"n.","d":"a person who doubts that something is true","c":"懷疑論者","s":"My uncle is a skeptic who does not believe anything he reads online until he has checked it in at least two newspapers.","t":"我叔叔是個懷疑論者，他在網路上讀到的任何東西，都要先在至少兩份報紙上查證才相信。"},{"w":"skepticism","p":"n.","d":"an attitude of doubting that something is true","c":"懷疑態度","s":"The scientist's new idea was met with skepticism at first, but later experiments proved that she had been right all along.","t":"這位科學家的新想法起初受到質疑，但後來的實驗證明她一直都是對的。"},{"w":"skeptically","p":"adv.","d":"in a way that shows doubt","c":"懷疑地","s":"\"Are you sure that is a real diamond?\" she asked skeptically, holding the cheap-looking ring up to the light.","t":"「你確定那是真鑽石嗎？」她懷疑地問，把看起來很廉價的戒指舉到光線下。"},{"w":"skim","p":"v.","d":"to read something quickly to get the main ideas","c":"瀏覽；略讀","s":"Before the test, I only had time to skim the chapter, so I missed some important details in the middle.","t":"考試前我只有時間略讀這一章，所以漏掉了中間一些重要的細節。","h":1},{"w":"skim","p":"v.","d":"to remove something from the surface of a liquid","c":"撇去（表面的東西）","s":"When the soup starts to boil, skim the fat off the top with a spoon so that the broth stays clear.","t":"湯開始滾的時候，用湯匙把表面的油撇掉，這樣湯才會保持清澈。"},{"w":"skim through","p":"v.phr.","d":"to look through something quickly","c":"快速翻閱","s":"I skim through the newspaper every morning on the MRT, reading only the headlines and the sports page.","t":"我每天早上在捷運上快速翻閱報紙，只看標題和體育版。"},{"w":"skim milk","p":"n.phr.","d":"milk that has had the fat removed","c":"脫脂牛奶","s":"My mother switched to skim milk last year because her doctor told her to eat less fat, and now she prefers the taste.","t":"我媽媽去年改喝脫脂牛奶，因為醫生要她少吃油脂，現在她反而更喜歡這個味道。"},{"w":"slang","p":"n.","d":"very informal words used by a particular group of people","c":"俚語","s":"Teenagers use a lot of slang when they talk to each other, so their parents often have no idea what they are saying.","t":"青少年彼此交談時會用很多俚語，所以父母常常完全不知道他們在說什麼。","h":1},{"w":"slang word","p":"n.phr.","d":"an informal word used by a group of people","c":"俚語字","s":"\"Cool\" was once a slang word used only by young people, but now even grandparents say it all the time.","t":"「Cool」曾經是只有年輕人用的俚語字，但現在連爺爺奶奶都常常說。"},{"w":"slangy","p":"adj.","d":"using a lot of slang","c":"俚俗的；充滿俚語的","s":"His essay was too slangy for a school report, so the teacher asked him to rewrite it in more formal English.","t":"他的作文對學校報告來說太俚俗了，所以老師要他用更正式的英文重寫。"},{"w":"slash","p":"v.","d":"to cut something with a quick, strong movement","c":"砍；劃破","s":"Someone slashed the tires of three cars on our street last night, and the police are now checking the cameras.","t":"昨晚有人劃破了我們這條街上三輛車的輪胎，警察正在調閱監視器。","a":"slashed","h":1},{"w":"slash","p":"v.","d":"to reduce something by a large amount","c":"大幅削減","s":"The store decided to slash its prices by half after Christmas to clear out all the winter coats and boots.","t":"這家店決定在聖誕節後把價格大砍一半，以清掉所有的冬季外套和靴子。"},{"w":"slash","p":"n.","d":"the symbol / used in writing","c":"斜線","s":"When you type a web address, remember to put a slash between the name of the website and the name of the page.","t":"輸入網址時，記得在網站名稱和頁面名稱之間加一個斜線。"},{"w":"slash prices","p":"v.phr.","d":"to make prices much lower","c":"大幅降價","s":"Airlines often slash prices in the weeks after Chinese New Year, so that is a good time to plan a short trip to Japan.","t":"航空公司常在農曆新年後的幾週大幅降價，所以那是計畫日本短期旅行的好時機。"},{"w":"slaughter","p":"v.","d":"to kill animals for food; to kill many people cruelly","c":"屠宰；屠殺","s":"Farmers used to slaughter a pig before every big festival, and the whole village would share the meat at a feast.","t":"農夫以前會在每個大節日前宰一頭豬，全村的人會在宴席上分享豬肉。","h":1},{"w":"slaughter","p":"n.","d":"the cruel killing of many people or animals","c":"屠殺","s":"The war brought terrible slaughter to the region, and thousands of families lost their homes and their loved ones.","t":"戰爭給這個地區帶來可怕的屠殺，成千上萬的家庭失去了家園和親人。"},{"w":"slaughterhouse","p":"n.","d":"a building where animals are killed for meat","c":"屠宰場","s":"The truck full of chickens was on its way to the slaughterhouse when it broke down outside the school, and the birds escaped.","t":"那輛載滿雞的卡車在前往屠宰場的路上，在學校外面拋錨了，雞全都跑了出來。"},{"w":"slay, slew, slain","p":"v.","d":"to kill someone or something violently (used in stories)","c":"殺死（文學用語）","s":"In the old story, the brave knight must slay the dragon before he can marry the princess and become king.","t":"在那個古老的故事裡，勇敢的騎士必須先殺死惡龍，才能娶公主並成為國王。","a":"slay","h":1},{"w":"dragon slayer","p":"n.phr.","d":"a hero who kills a dragon in a story","c":"屠龍者","s":"The children loved the movie about the young dragon slayer who protects her village from a fire-breathing monster.","t":"孩子們很喜歡那部電影，講的是一位年輕的屠龍者保護村子不受噴火怪物攻擊。"},{"w":"be slain","p":"v.phr.","d":"to be killed violently","c":"被殺","s":"According to the legend, the king was slain in battle, and his sword was lost in the lake for a thousand years.","t":"根據傳說，國王在戰鬥中被殺，他的劍在湖裡遺失了一千年。","a":"was slain"},{"w":"sloppy","p":"adj.","d":"careless and untidy","c":"馬虎的；邋遢的","s":"Your homework is too sloppy; the handwriting is hard to read, and there are coffee stains on the first page.","t":"你的作業太馬虎了；字跡難以辨認，第一頁還有咖啡漬。","h":1},{"w":"sloppily","p":"adv.","d":"in a careless and untidy way","c":"馬虎地","s":"The boxes were packed so sloppily that half of the plates were broken by the time the truck arrived at our new house.","t":"箱子打包得太馬虎，卡車到我們新家時，有一半的盤子都破了。"},{"w":"sloppiness","p":"n.","d":"careless and untidy behavior","c":"馬虎；草率","s":"The manager said that sloppiness in the kitchen could make customers sick, so every cook must now wear gloves and a hat.","t":"經理說廚房裡的馬虎可能會讓顧客生病，所以現在每位廚師都必須戴手套和帽子。"},{"w":"slum","p":"n.","d":"a very poor and crowded area of a city","c":"貧民窟","s":"Many families in the slum live in houses made of metal sheets, with no clean water and only one toilet shared by fifty people.","t":"貧民窟裡的許多家庭住在鐵皮搭的房子裡，沒有乾淨的水，五十個人共用一間廁所。","h":1},{"w":"slum it","p":"v.phr.","d":"to live in a cheaper or poorer way than usual, often for fun","c":"過窮日子；克難生活","s":"On our backpacking trip we decided to slum it, staying in cheap hostels and eating street food every day.","t":"背包旅行時我們決定克難生活，住便宜的青年旅館，每天吃街頭小吃。"},{"w":"slum dweller","p":"n.phr.","d":"a person who lives in a slum","c":"貧民窟居民","s":"The city built new apartments for the slum dwellers, who had lived beside the dirty river for more than twenty years.","t":"市政府為那些在骯髒河邊住了二十多年的貧民窟居民蓋了新公寓。","a":"slum dwellers"},{"w":"slump","p":"v.","d":"to fall suddenly by a large amount","c":"暴跌；驟降","s":"Sales of umbrellas slumped during the long dry summer, and the small shop nearly had to close.","t":"在漫長乾燥的夏天，雨傘的銷量暴跌，那家小店差點關門。","a":"slumped","h":1},{"w":"slump","p":"v.","d":"to sit or fall down heavily because you are tired or weak","c":"癱坐；倒下","s":"After running the whole marathon, he slumped into a chair and could not move for almost an hour.","t":"跑完整場馬拉松後，他癱坐在椅子上，將近一小時動彈不得。","a":"slumped"},{"w":"slump","p":"n.","d":"a period when something falls or does badly","c":"衰退期；低潮","s":"The baseball team is in a slump; they have lost eight games in a row, and the fans are starting to stay home.","t":"這支棒球隊正處於低潮；他們已經連輸八場，球迷開始不來看球了。"},{"w":"sly","p":"adj.","d":"clever at tricking people in a secret way","c":"狡猾的","s":"The sly fox waited until the farmer went to lunch, and then it quietly carried off the fattest chicken.","t":"狡猾的狐狸等到農夫去吃午餐，然後悄悄地叼走了最肥的那隻雞。","h":1},{"w":"slyly","p":"adv.","d":"in a secret and clever way","c":"狡猾地；偷偷地","s":"The boy slyly slipped the last cookie into his pocket while his mother was busy talking on the phone.","t":"男孩趁媽媽忙著講電話時，偷偷地把最後一塊餅乾塞進口袋。"},{"w":"on the sly","p":"phr.","d":"secretly, so that nobody knows","c":"偷偷地；暗中","s":"My grandfather is not supposed to eat sweets, but he buys ice cream on the sly whenever he walks past the shop.","t":"我爺爺不應該吃甜食，但每次經過那家店他都會偷偷地買冰淇淋。"},{"w":"smuggle","p":"v.","d":"to take things or people into or out of a country illegally","c":"走私；偷運","s":"The man tried to smuggle two rare birds through the airport in his jacket, but the officers heard them singing.","t":"那名男子試圖把兩隻稀有鳥類藏在外套裡偷運過機場，但官員聽到了牠們的叫聲。","h":1},{"w":"smuggler","p":"n.","d":"a person who takes things into or out of a country illegally","c":"走私者","s":"Coast guards caught the smuggler at night, and his boat was full of cigarettes that he planned to sell without paying tax.","t":"海巡人員在夜裡抓到了那名走私者，他的船上裝滿了打算不繳稅就賣掉的香菸。"},{"w":"smuggling","p":"n.","d":"the crime of taking things into or out of a country illegally","c":"走私","s":"Drug smuggling is a very serious crime in Taiwan, and the signs at the airport warn travelers about it in several languages.","t":"毒品走私在台灣是非常嚴重的罪行，機場的標示用好幾種語言警告旅客。"}]},{"unit":34,"theme":"sneakers – sportsmansportswoman","cards":[{"w":"sneakers","p":"n.","d":"soft sports shoes with rubber bottoms","c":"運動鞋；球鞋","s":"My old sneakers are falling apart, so I need to buy a new pair before the school sports day next week.","t":"我的舊運動鞋快要壞掉了，所以我需要在下週學校運動會之前買一雙新的。","h":1},{"w":"a pair of sneakers","p":"n.phr.","d":"two sports shoes that go together","c":"一雙運動鞋","s":"For his birthday, my brother asked for a pair of sneakers because he wants to join the school running club this year.","t":"我弟弟生日時想要一雙運動鞋，因為他今年想加入學校的跑步社。"},{"w":"running shoes","p":"n.phr.","d":"light shoes made for running","c":"跑步鞋","s":"Good running shoes protect your knees, so do not run a marathon in the cheap shoes you wear every day.","t":"好的跑步鞋能保護你的膝蓋，所以不要穿每天穿的便宜鞋子去跑馬拉松。"},{"w":"sneaky","p":"adj.","d":"doing things secretly and in an unfair way","c":"偷偷摸摸的；狡猾的","s":"It was sneaky of him to read his sister's diary while she was out, and she was furious when she found out.","t":"他趁姊姊外出時偷看她的日記真是偷偷摸摸的，她發現後非常生氣。","h":1},{"w":"sneak, sneaked/snuck, sneaked/snuck","p":"v.","d":"to go somewhere quietly so nobody sees you","c":"偷偷地走；潛行","s":"The boys tried to sneak into the movie theater without tickets, but the manager caught them at the back door.","t":"那些男孩試圖沒買票就偷偷溜進電影院，但經理在後門抓到了他們。","a":"sneak"},{"w":"sneak out","p":"v.phr.","d":"to leave a place quietly and secretly","c":"偷偷溜出去","s":"When the lecture became boring, two students decided to sneak out of the hall, but the professor noticed them immediately.","t":"當演講變得無聊時，兩個學生決定偷偷溜出大廳，但教授立刻注意到他們。"},{"w":"sneak a look at","p":"v.phr.","d":"to look at something quickly and secretly","c":"偷看一眼","s":"I could not wait until morning, so I sneaked a look at my birthday presents while everyone else was asleep.","t":"我等不到早上，所以趁大家都睡著時偷看了一眼我的生日禮物。","a":"sneaked a look at"},{"w":"sneakily","p":"adv.","d":"in a secret and unfair way","c":"偷偷地；狡猾地","s":"My cat sneakily pushed the kitchen door open and ate half of the fish before anyone came home.","t":"我的貓偷偷地推開廚房門，在大家回家前吃掉了半條魚。"},{"w":"sneeze","p":"v.","d":"to suddenly push air out through your nose and mouth","c":"打噴嚏","s":"Every spring I sneeze all day long because the pollen from the trees makes my nose itch terribly.","t":"每年春天我整天打噴嚏，因為樹上的花粉讓我的鼻子奇癢無比。","h":1},{"w":"sneeze","p":"n.","d":"the act of pushing air suddenly through your nose","c":"噴嚏","s":"A loud sneeze from the back of the quiet classroom made everyone turn around and laugh during the test.","t":"考試時安靜教室後方傳來一聲響亮的噴嚏，讓大家都轉過頭來笑了。"},{"w":"cover your mouth when you sneeze","p":"v.phr.","d":"to put your hand or arm in front of your mouth while sneezing","c":"打噴嚏時遮住嘴","s":"The nurse told the children to cover their mouths when they sneeze so that they would not spread germs to their classmates.","t":"護士告訴孩子們打噴嚏時要遮住嘴，這樣才不會把細菌傳給同學。","a":"cover their mouths when they sneeze"},{"w":"snore","p":"v.","d":"to breathe noisily through your nose and mouth while sleeping","c":"打呼","s":"My grandfather snores so loudly that we can hear him from the living room, even when his bedroom door is closed.","t":"我爺爺打呼打得非常大聲，即使他的房門關著，我們在客廳都聽得到。","a":"snores","h":1},{"w":"snore","p":"n.","d":"the loud noise someone makes while sleeping","c":"鼾聲","s":"I could not sleep at the camp because the snore of the boy next to me sounded like a motorcycle all night.","t":"我在營隊裡睡不著，因為旁邊男孩的鼾聲整晚聽起來像摩托車。"},{"w":"snoring","p":"n.","d":"the noise of breathing loudly while asleep","c":"打呼；打鼾","s":"Heavy snoring can be a sign of a health problem, so my father finally went to see a doctor about it.","t":"嚴重打呼可能是健康問題的徵兆，所以我爸爸終於為此去看了醫生。"},{"w":"sociable","p":"adj.","d":"friendly and enjoying being with other people","c":"善於交際的；好相處的","s":"My new roommate is very sociable, so she already knows everyone on our floor after only one week.","t":"我的新室友非常善於交際，所以才一個星期她就認識了我們這層樓的每個人。","h":1},{"w":"social","p":"adj.","d":"connected with society or with meeting people","c":"社會的；社交的","s":"Spending too much time on social media can make teenagers feel lonely instead of connected to their friends.","t":"花太多時間在社交媒體上會讓青少年覺得孤單，而不是和朋友更親近。"},{"w":"socially","p":"adv.","d":"in a way that is connected with meeting people","c":"在社交上","s":"He is brilliant at math, but socially he feels nervous and often does not know what to say at parties.","t":"他數學很厲害，但在社交上他會緊張，在派對上常常不知道該說什麼。"},{"w":"society","p":"n.","d":"all the people who live together in a country or area","c":"社會","s":"In a healthy society, people from different backgrounds respect each other and work together to solve common problems.","t":"在一個健康的社會裡，來自不同背景的人彼此尊重，並一起合作解決共同的問題。"},{"w":"socialism","p":"n.","d":"a political system in which the government owns and shares important industries","c":"社會主義","s":"Under socialism, the government controls the main industries so that wealth can be shared more equally among the people.","t":"在社會主義下，政府控制主要產業，以便財富能在人民之間更平均地分配。","h":1},{"w":"socialist","p":"n.","d":"a person who believes in socialism","c":"社會主義者","s":"My history teacher said that a socialist believes the government should provide free health care and education for everyone.","t":"我的歷史老師說，社會主義者相信政府應該為每個人提供免費的醫療和教育。","h":1},{"w":"socialist","p":"adj.","d":"based on or supporting socialism","c":"社會主義的","s":"The socialist party promised to raise taxes on the rich and use the money to help poor families with children.","t":"社會主義政黨承諾對富人加稅，並用這些錢來幫助有小孩的貧窮家庭。","h":1},{"w":"socialize","p":"v.","d":"to spend time with other people in a friendly way","c":"社交；交際","s":"After work, my colleagues like to socialize at a coffee shop, but I usually go home to rest because I am tired.","t":"下班後我的同事喜歡在咖啡店社交，但我通常回家休息，因為我很累。"},{"w":"socialize with","p":"v.phr.","d":"to meet and talk with people in a friendly way","c":"與…交往","s":"The exchange students were encouraged to socialize with local families so that they could practice Chinese in everyday situations.","t":"交換學生被鼓勵與當地家庭交往，這樣他們就能在日常情境中練習中文。"},{"w":"sociology","p":"n.","d":"the study of society and how people live together","c":"社會學","s":"She chose to study sociology at university because she wants to understand why some neighborhoods have more crime than others.","t":"她選擇在大學讀社會學，因為她想了解為什麼有些社區的犯罪比其他地方多。","h":1},{"w":"sociologist","p":"n.","d":"a person who studies society","c":"社會學家","s":"A famous sociologist spent two years living in a small fishing village to learn how its families share work and money.","t":"一位著名的社會學家在一個小漁村住了兩年，以了解那裡的家庭如何分擔工作和金錢。"},{"w":"sociological","p":"adj.","d":"connected with the study of society","c":"社會學的","s":"The report looks at the problem from a sociological point of view, asking how poverty and education affect young people's choices.","t":"這份報告從社會學的角度探討這個問題，探問貧窮和教育如何影響年輕人的選擇。"},{"w":"solemn","p":"adj.","d":"very serious and formal","c":"莊嚴的；嚴肅的","s":"The students stood in solemn silence as the old soldier told them about his friends who died in the war.","t":"當老兵向學生講述他在戰爭中死去的朋友時，學生們莊嚴肅靜地站著。","h":1},{"w":"solemnly","p":"adv.","d":"in a very serious and formal way","c":"莊嚴地；鄭重地","s":"The new president solemnly promised to serve the people honestly, and the crowd listened without making a sound.","t":"新總統鄭重地承諾要誠實地為人民服務，群眾安靜無聲地聆聽著。"},{"w":"make a solemn promise","p":"v.phr.","d":"to promise something in a very serious way","c":"鄭重承諾","s":"Before he left for the army, he made a solemn promise to his mother that he would write to her every single week.","t":"在他去當兵之前，他向母親鄭重承諾他會每個星期都寫信給她。","a":"made a solemn promise"},{"w":"solidarity","p":"n.","d":"support and agreement among people who share a goal","c":"團結；同心協力","s":"The workers showed great solidarity during the strike, and nobody returned to work until everyone received a fair raise.","t":"工人們在罷工期間展現了極大的團結，在每個人都獲得合理加薪之前沒有人回去工作。","h":1},{"w":"in solidarity with","p":"phr.","d":"to show support for a group of people","c":"聲援；與…團結一致","s":"Thousands of students wore black on Monday in solidarity with the families who had lost their homes in the terrible flood.","t":"週一數千名學生穿著黑衣，聲援在可怕洪水中失去家園的家庭。"},{"w":"solid","p":"adj.","d":"hard and firm; not liquid or gas; strong and reliable","c":"固體的；堅固的；可靠的","s":"The old wooden bridge looks weak, but the engineer said it is still solid enough to carry a small truck.","t":"這座老木橋看起來很脆弱，但工程師說它仍然堅固到足以承載一輛小卡車。"},{"w":"solid","p":"n.","d":"a substance that is hard and keeps its shape","c":"固體","s":"When water freezes, it changes from a liquid into a solid, which is why ice floats on the lake in winter.","t":"水結冰時會從液體變成固體，這就是為什麼冬天冰會浮在湖面上。"},{"w":"solitary","p":"adj.","d":"done alone; living or being alone","c":"獨自的；孤獨的","s":"Writing is a solitary activity, so the author rents a quiet cabin in the mountains whenever she starts a new novel.","t":"寫作是一項獨自的活動，所以這位作家每次開始寫新小說時都會租一間山上安靜的小屋。","h":1},{"w":"solitude","p":"n.","d":"the state of being alone, especially when you enjoy it","c":"獨處；孤獨","s":"After a noisy week at the office, my uncle enjoys the solitude of fishing alone by the river early in the morning.","t":"在辦公室忙碌吵雜的一週後，我叔叔喜歡清晨獨自在河邊釣魚的獨處時光。","h":1},{"w":"solitary confinement","p":"n.phr.","d":"a punishment in which a prisoner is kept alone in a room","c":"單獨監禁","s":"The prisoner spent thirty days in solitary confinement, and he said the silence was worse than any other punishment.","t":"那名囚犯被單獨監禁了三十天，他說那種寂靜比任何其他懲罰都更糟。"},{"w":"lead a solitary life","p":"v.phr.","d":"to live alone and see few people","c":"過著孤獨的生活","s":"Since his wife passed away, the old fisherman has led a solitary life in his small house, speaking only to his dog.","t":"自從妻子過世後，這位老漁夫在小屋裡過著孤獨的生活，只跟他的狗說話。","a":"has led a solitary life"},{"w":"soothe","p":"v.","d":"to make someone calmer or make pain less strong","c":"安撫；舒緩","s":"The young mother sang softly to soothe her crying baby, and within a few minutes he fell asleep.","t":"年輕的媽媽輕聲唱歌安撫哭泣的寶寶，幾分鐘內他就睡著了。","h":1},{"w":"soothing","p":"adj.","d":"making you feel calm and relaxed","c":"令人舒緩的；安撫的","s":"The spa plays soothing music and uses soft lights, so most customers feel sleepy after only ten minutes.","t":"這家水療館播放令人舒緩的音樂並使用柔和的燈光，所以大多數顧客才十分鐘就覺得想睡。"},{"w":"soothe sb's nerves","p":"v.phr.","d":"to help someone stop feeling nervous","c":"安撫某人的情緒","s":"Before the big speech, she took a long walk in the park to soothe her nerves, and it really worked.","t":"在重要演講之前，她到公園散了很久的步來安撫自己的情緒，而且真的有效。","a":"soothe her nerves"},{"w":"sorrowful","p":"adj.","d":"feeling or showing great sadness","c":"悲傷的；哀傷的","s":"The dog gave his owner a sorrowful look when she packed her suitcase, because he knew she was leaving again.","t":"當主人收拾行李箱時，狗狗給了她一個悲傷的眼神，因為它知道她又要離開了。","h":1},{"w":"sorrow","p":"n.","d":"a feeling of great sadness","c":"悲傷；哀痛","s":"The whole town shared the family's sorrow when the young firefighter died saving two children from a burning house.","t":"當年輕的消防員為了從燃燒的房子裡救出兩個孩子而喪生時，全鎮的人都分擔了這家人的悲傷。"},{"w":"sorrowfully","p":"adv.","d":"in a very sad way","c":"悲傷地","s":"The old man looked sorrowfully at the empty chair where his wife used to sit and read every evening.","t":"老人悲傷地望著那張空椅子，他的妻子以前每天晚上都坐在那裡看書。"},{"w":"to one's sorrow","p":"phr.","d":"used to say that something made you very sad","c":"令人悲傷的是","s":"To their sorrow, the family had to sell the farm that had belonged to them for more than one hundred years.","t":"令他們悲傷的是，這家人不得不賣掉屬於他們一百多年的農場。","a":"To their sorrow"},{"w":"sovereign","p":"adj.","d":"having complete power to govern itself","c":"有主權的；獨立自主的","s":"A sovereign nation has the right to make its own laws, so other countries should not interfere in its decisions.","t":"主權國家有權制定自己的法律，所以其他國家不應該干涉它的決定。","h":1},{"w":"sovereign","p":"n.","d":"a king or queen","c":"君主；元首","s":"In the old days, the sovereign had the power to decide who would live and who would die with a single word.","t":"在過去，君主只要一句話就有權決定誰生誰死。"},{"w":"sovereignty","p":"n.","d":"the complete power of a country to govern itself","c":"主權","s":"The two countries have argued about the sovereignty of the small islands for decades, and neither side is willing to give up.","t":"兩國為那些小島的主權爭論了數十年，雙方都不願意放棄。"},{"w":"spacecraft","p":"n.","d":"a vehicle that travels in space","c":"太空船","s":"The spacecraft will travel for seven months before it reaches Mars, and scientists will control it from Earth the whole time.","t":"這艘太空船將航行七個月才會抵達火星，科學家會在整個過程中從地球控制它。","h":1},{"w":"spaceship","p":"n.","d":"a vehicle that carries people into space, especially in stories","c":"太空船；宇宙飛船","s":"In the movie, the children build a spaceship out of old car parts and fly to a planet made of candy.","t":"在電影裡，孩子們用舊汽車零件建造了一艘太空船，飛到一個由糖果組成的星球。"},{"w":"space station","p":"n.phr.","d":"a large structure in space where astronauts live and work","c":"太空站","s":"Astronauts on the space station see sixteen sunrises every day because they circle the Earth once every ninety minutes.","t":"太空站上的太空人每天看到十六次日出，因為他們每九十分鐘繞地球一圈。"},{"w":"spacecraft launch","p":"n.phr.","d":"the moment a spacecraft leaves the ground","c":"太空船發射","s":"Thousands of people gathered on the beach to watch the spacecraft launch, and they cheered as the rocket rose into the sky.","t":"數千人聚集在海灘上觀看太空船發射，當火箭升上天空時他們歡呼起來。"},{"w":"span","p":"n.","d":"the length of time something lasts; the distance from one side to the other","c":"期間；跨距","s":"Over a span of only three years, the small start-up grew into a company with offices in five countries.","t":"在短短三年的期間內，這家小型新創公司成長為在五個國家設有辦公室的企業。","h":1},{"w":"span","p":"v.","d":"to last for a period of time; to stretch across something","c":"橫跨；持續","s":"Her acting career spanned more than fifty years, from her first small role at eighteen to her final film at seventy.","t":"她的演藝生涯橫跨超過五十年，從十八歲的第一個小角色到七十歲的最後一部電影。","a":"spanned"},{"w":"life span","p":"n.phr.","d":"the length of time a person, animal, or thing lives or lasts","c":"壽命","s":"The average life span of a pet rabbit is about eight years, so families should think carefully before buying one.","t":"寵物兔的平均壽命大約八年，所以家庭在購買前應該仔細考慮。"},{"w":"attention span","p":"n.phr.","d":"the length of time you can keep paying attention","c":"注意力持續時間","s":"Young children have a short attention span, so the teacher changes activities every ten minutes to keep them interested.","t":"幼童的注意力持續時間很短，所以老師每十分鐘更換活動來維持他們的興趣。"},{"w":"sparrow","p":"n.","d":"a small brown bird that is very common in towns","c":"麻雀","s":"A little sparrow hopped onto our table at the outdoor café and picked up the crumbs from my sandwich.","t":"一隻小麻雀跳到我們戶外咖啡座的桌上，撿起我三明治的碎屑。","h":1},{"w":"a flock of sparrows","p":"n.phr.","d":"a group of sparrows flying or feeding together","c":"一群麻雀","s":"Every evening a flock of sparrows gathers in the big tree outside my window, and their chirping is louder than the traffic.","t":"每天傍晚一群麻雀聚集在我窗外的大樹上，它們的啁啾聲比車流聲還大。"},{"w":"sparrow's nest","p":"n.phr.","d":"the small home a sparrow builds for its eggs","c":"麻雀的巢","s":"We found a sparrow's nest under the roof of the garage, so my father decided not to clean that corner until the babies flew away.","t":"我們在車庫屋頂下發現一個麻雀的巢，所以我爸爸決定等小鳥飛走後再清理那個角落。"},{"w":"spectacle","p":"n.","d":"a very impressive show or sight","c":"奇觀；壯觀的場面","s":"The fireworks over the river were an amazing spectacle, and people watched with their mouths open for twenty minutes.","t":"河面上的煙火是一場驚人的奇觀，人們張著嘴看了二十分鐘。","h":1},{"w":"spectacles","p":"n.","d":"glasses that you wear to see better (old-fashioned word)","c":"眼鏡","s":"My grandmother cannot read the newspaper without her spectacles, so she keeps them on a string around her neck.","t":"我奶奶沒有眼鏡就看不了報紙，所以她用繩子把眼鏡掛在脖子上。"},{"w":"make a spectacle of oneself","p":"v.phr.","d":"to behave in a silly way so that people stare at you","c":"當眾出醜","s":"He drank too much at the wedding and made a spectacle of himself by dancing on the table while everyone stared.","t":"他在婚禮上喝得太多，在桌上跳舞當眾出醜，大家都盯著他看。","a":"made a spectacle of himself"},{"w":"spectacular","p":"adj.","d":"very impressive and exciting to look at","c":"壯觀的；精彩的","s":"From the top of the mountain, we had a spectacular view of the whole valley with its rivers and tiny villages.","t":"從山頂上，我們看到整個山谷壯觀的景色，有河流和小小的村莊。"},{"w":"spectator","p":"n.","d":"a person who watches a game or event","c":"觀眾","s":"More than fifty thousand spectators filled the stadium, and the noise was so loud that the players could not hear the coach.","t":"超過五萬名觀眾擠滿體育場，噪音大到球員聽不到教練的聲音。","a":"spectators"},{"w":"spiral","p":"n.","d":"a shape that winds around and around a center point","c":"螺旋","s":"The shell of a snail grows in a perfect spiral, and scientists say this shape helps the animal save space.","t":"蝸牛的殼以完美的螺旋生長，科學家說這種形狀有助於這種動物節省空間。","h":1},{"w":"spiral","p":"adj.","d":"winding around a center in a curve","c":"螺旋形的","s":"We climbed the narrow spiral staircase inside the lighthouse, and I felt dizzy by the time we reached the top.","t":"我們爬上燈塔裡狹窄的螺旋形樓梯，到達頂端時我已經頭暈了。"},{"w":"spiral","p":"v.","d":"to move in a winding curve; to increase or decrease quickly","c":"盤旋；急速上升或下降","s":"After the factory closed, prices in the town began to spiral upward, and many families could no longer afford rent.","t":"工廠關閉後，鎮上的物價開始急速飆升，許多家庭再也付不起房租。"},{"w":"spiral out of control","p":"v.phr.","d":"to get worse quickly in a way that cannot be stopped","c":"失控惡化","s":"The small argument between the two brothers spiraled out of control, and by dinner time they were not speaking to each other at all.","t":"兩兄弟之間的小爭吵失控惡化，到晚餐時間他們已經完全不跟對方說話了。","a":"spiraled out of control"},{"w":"splendor","p":"n.","d":"great beauty that impresses people","c":"壯麗；輝煌","s":"Visitors to the palace are amazed by the splendor of its golden ceilings and the huge paintings on every wall.","t":"宮殿的參觀者對金色天花板和每面牆上巨幅畫作的壯麗感到驚嘆。","h":1},{"w":"splendid","p":"adj.","d":"excellent; very beautiful and impressive","c":"極好的；壯麗的","s":"We had a splendid time at the beach, and the weather stayed sunny and warm for the whole long weekend.","t":"我們在海邊度過了極美好的時光，整個長週末天氣都晴朗溫暖。"},{"w":"splendidly","p":"adv.","d":"extremely well; in a very impressive way","c":"極好地；壯麗地","s":"The school choir performed splendidly at the national contest, and the judges gave them the highest score of the day.","t":"學校合唱團在全國比賽中表演得極為出色，評審給了他們當天的最高分。"},{"w":"in all its splendor","p":"phr.","d":"showing all of its beauty","c":"盡顯其壯麗","s":"After the rain stopped, the rainbow appeared over the mountains in all its splendor, and everyone took out their phones.","t":"雨停之後，彩虹盡顯壯麗地出現在群山之上，每個人都拿出手機。"},{"w":"spokesperson","p":"n.","d":"a person who speaks for a group or company","c":"發言人","s":"A spokesperson for the airline said that all passengers would receive a full refund because of the three-day delay.","t":"航空公司的發言人表示，由於延誤三天，所有乘客都會獲得全額退款。","h":1},{"w":"spokesman","p":"n.","d":"a man who speaks for a group or company","c":"（男）發言人","s":"The police spokesman told reporters that the missing boy had been found safe at his grandmother's house.","t":"警方發言人告訴記者，失蹤的男孩已在他奶奶家被安全找到。"},{"w":"spokeswoman","p":"n.","d":"a woman who speaks for a group or company","c":"（女）發言人","s":"The company spokeswoman refused to answer questions about the accident until the investigation was finished.","t":"公司女發言人拒絕回答有關事故的問題，直到調查結束。"},{"w":"speak for","p":"v.phr.","d":"to express the opinions of a person or group","c":"代表…發言","s":"I think I speak for the whole class when I say that we need more time to prepare for the final exam.","t":"我想我代表全班發言：我們需要更多時間準備期末考。"},{"w":"spontaneous","p":"adj.","d":"done suddenly without planning","c":"自發的；一時衝動的","s":"Our trip to the night market was completely spontaneous; we were studying one minute and on the bus the next.","t":"我們去夜市的行程完全是一時衝動的；前一分鐘還在讀書，下一分鐘就在公車上了。","h":1},{"w":"spontaneously","p":"adv.","d":"suddenly and without planning","c":"自發地；自然而然地","s":"When the singer walked onto the stage, the whole audience spontaneously stood up and started to clap and cheer.","t":"當歌手走上舞台時，全場觀眾自發地起立，開始鼓掌歡呼。"},{"w":"spontaneity","p":"n.","d":"the quality of doing things suddenly without planning","c":"自發性；隨興","s":"I love my best friend's spontaneity; she once called me at midnight and said we should drive to the beach to see the sunrise.","t":"我喜歡我最好朋友的隨興；她曾經半夜打電話給我，說我們應該開車去海邊看日出。"},{"w":"sportsman","p":"n.","d":"a man who plays sports, especially one who plays fairly","c":"男運動員；運動家","s":"A true sportsman shakes hands with the other team after the game, even when his own team has just lost badly.","t":"真正的運動家在比賽後會和對方球隊握手，即使自己的隊伍剛剛慘敗。","h":1},{"w":"sportswoman","p":"n.","d":"a woman who plays sports","c":"女運動員","s":"The young sportswoman won three gold medals at the Asian Games and became a hero to girls all over the country.","t":"這位年輕的女運動員在亞運會上贏得三面金牌，成為全國女孩的英雄。"},{"w":"sportsmanship","p":"n.","d":"fair and polite behavior when playing sports","c":"運動精神","s":"The coach cares more about sportsmanship than winning, so he praised the boy who helped an injured opponent off the field.","t":"教練重視運動精神多過勝利，所以他讚揚那個幫助受傷對手離場的男孩。"},{"w":"sportsmanlike","p":"adj.","d":"fair and polite in the way you play sports","c":"有運動精神的","s":"It was not very sportsmanlike of the players to argue with the referee for ten minutes after every single call.","t":"球員們在每次判決後都跟裁判爭論十分鐘，這不太有運動精神。"}]},{"unit":35,"theme":"sportsmanship – subjective","cards":[{"w":"sportsmanship","p":"n.","d":"fair and polite behavior when playing sports","c":"運動精神","s":"The coach praised the team for its sportsmanship because the players helped an injured opponent instead of running past him.","t":"教練稱讚球隊的運動精神，因為球員們幫助了受傷的對手，而不是直接跑過去。","h":1},{"w":"good sportsmanship","p":"n.phr.","d":"polite and fair behavior toward other players","c":"良好的運動精神","s":"Shaking hands after a hard game is a sign of good sportsmanship, and our school expects every player to do it.","t":"激烈比賽後握手是良好運動精神的表現，我們學校期望每位球員都這麼做。"},{"w":"sportsman","p":"n.","d":"a man who plays sports, especially one who plays fairly","c":"男運動員；運動家","s":"Although he lost the final, the young sportsman smiled and congratulated the winner in front of the cheering crowd.","t":"雖然輸了決賽，這位年輕的運動員仍微笑著在歡呼的群眾面前向勝利者道賀。"},{"w":"sportswoman","p":"n.","d":"a woman who plays sports","c":"女運動員","s":"The famous sportswoman visited our school and told the girls that practice matters more than natural talent.","t":"這位著名的女運動員來我們學校，告訴女孩們練習比天賦更重要。"},{"w":"spotlight","p":"n.","d":"a strong light that shines on one person or thing; public attention","c":"聚光燈；（公眾的）注目","s":"When the spotlight shone on the young singer, she forgot the words for a moment but then finished the song beautifully.","t":"當聚光燈照在年輕歌手身上時，她一時忘了歌詞，但後來把歌唱得很美。","h":1},{"w":"in the spotlight","p":"phr.","d":"receiving a lot of public attention","c":"成為焦點；受到矚目","s":"After winning the gold medal, the shy swimmer suddenly found herself in the spotlight, with reporters waiting outside her house every day.","t":"贏得金牌後，害羞的游泳選手突然成為焦點，記者每天都在她家外面等候。"},{"w":"spotlight","p":"v.","d":"to draw attention to a problem or situation","c":"聚焦；使引起注意","s":"The documentary was made to spotlight the problem of plastic in the ocean, and millions of people watched it online.","t":"這部紀錄片是為了讓人關注海洋塑膠的問題而製作的，數百萬人在網路上觀看。"},{"w":"steal the spotlight","p":"v.phr.","d":"to take attention away from someone else","c":"搶走風采","s":"The bride's little nephew stole the spotlight at the wedding when he danced in the middle of the floor during her speech.","t":"新娘的小侄子在婚禮上搶走了風采，他在新娘致詞時跑到舞池中央跳舞。","a":"stole the spotlight"},{"w":"spur","p":"v.","d":"to encourage someone to do something or make something happen faster","c":"激勵；刺激","s":"The teacher's kind words spurred the boy to study harder, and within a year he became one of the best students.","t":"老師親切的話語激勵那個男孩更用功讀書，一年之內他就成為最優秀的學生之一。","a":"spurred","h":1},{"w":"spur","p":"n.","d":"something that encourages you to do something; a sharp object on a rider's boot","c":"刺激；激勵；馬刺","s":"Losing the first game was a spur to the team, and they practiced every evening until they won the championship.","t":"輸掉第一場比賽對球隊是一種激勵，他們每天晚上練習，直到贏得冠軍。"},{"w":"spur sb on","p":"v.phr.","d":"to encourage someone to keep going or try harder","c":"鼓舞某人繼續努力","s":"The cheers from the crowd spurred her on, and the tired runner found the strength to finish the last two kilometers.","t":"群眾的歡呼聲鼓舞她繼續努力，疲憊的跑者找到力量跑完最後兩公里。","a":"spurred her on"},{"w":"on the spur of the moment","p":"phr.","d":"suddenly, without planning","c":"一時衝動地；臨時起意","s":"We bought the concert tickets on the spur of the moment, so we had to call our parents and explain why we would be home late.","t":"我們臨時起意買了演唱會門票，所以必須打電話跟父母解釋為什麼會晚回家。"},{"w":"stabilize","p":"v.","d":"to become steady or make something steady","c":"使穩定；穩定下來","s":"The doctors worked for three hours to stabilize the patient, and by morning his heart rate was finally normal again.","t":"醫生們努力了三個小時來穩定病人的狀況，到了早上他的心跳終於又恢復正常。","h":1},{"w":"stable","p":"adj.","d":"not likely to change, fall, or move; steady","c":"穩定的；穩固的","s":"My parents want me to find a stable job with a regular salary, but I would rather start my own small business.","t":"我父母希望我找一份有固定薪水的穩定工作，但我寧願自己開一家小公司。"},{"w":"stability","p":"n.","d":"the state of being steady and not changing","c":"穩定；穩固","s":"After years of war, the people of the country want nothing more than peace and stability for their children.","t":"經歷多年戰爭之後，這個國家的人民最想要的就是為孩子們帶來和平與穩定。"},{"w":"unstable","p":"adj.","d":"likely to change or fall suddenly; not steady","c":"不穩定的","s":"The old ladder is unstable, so please hold it for me while I climb up to clean the top of the window.","t":"那把舊梯子不穩，所以我爬上去清洗窗戶上方時，請幫我扶著它。"},{"w":"stagger","p":"v.","d":"to walk unsteadily, almost falling","c":"蹣跚；搖搖晃晃地走","s":"The exhausted runner began to stagger in the last hundred meters, but the crowd cheered until he crossed the line.","t":"筋疲力盡的跑者在最後一百公尺開始搖搖晃晃，但群眾一直歡呼到他衝過終點線。","h":1},{"w":"stagger","p":"v.","d":"to arrange events so that they do not all happen at the same time","c":"錯開（時間）","s":"To avoid crowds in the cafeteria, the school decided to stagger lunch times so that each grade eats at a different hour.","t":"為了避免餐廳擁擠，學校決定錯開午餐時間，讓每個年級在不同的時段用餐。"},{"w":"staggering","p":"adj.","d":"so large or surprising that it is hard to believe","c":"驚人的；令人震驚的","s":"The company lost a staggering amount of money last year, and now it has to close half of its stores.","t":"這家公司去年虧損了驚人的金額，現在必須關閉一半的店面。"},{"w":"stagger to one's feet","p":"v.phr.","d":"to stand up slowly and unsteadily","c":"搖搖晃晃地站起來","s":"After the boxer was knocked down, he staggered to his feet and tried to keep fighting, but the referee stopped the match.","t":"拳擊手被擊倒後，他搖搖晃晃地站起來想繼續比賽，但裁判中止了比賽。","a":"staggered to his feet"},{"w":"staple","p":"n.","d":"a basic food that people eat most often","c":"主食","s":"Rice is the staple in most Asian countries, while people in many European countries eat bread with almost every meal.","t":"米飯是大多數亞洲國家的主食，而許多歐洲國家的人幾乎每餐都吃麵包。","h":1},{"w":"staple","p":"adj.","d":"basic and used or needed all the time","c":"主要的；基本的","s":"Potatoes became a staple food in Ireland, so when the crop failed in the 1840s, millions of people went hungry.","t":"馬鈴薯成為愛爾蘭的主要食物，所以當一八四零年代作物歉收時，數百萬人挨餓。"},{"w":"staple","p":"n.","d":"a small piece of bent metal used to hold papers together","c":"訂書針","s":"The report is too thick for one staple, so you should use a large clip to keep all the pages together.","t":"這份報告太厚，一根訂書針釘不住，所以你應該用大夾子把所有頁面夾在一起。"},{"w":"staple","p":"v.","d":"to fasten papers together with staples","c":"用訂書機釘","s":"Please staple your essay in the top left corner before you hand it in, or the pages may get lost.","t":"請在繳交之前把你的作文用訂書機釘在左上角，否則頁面可能會遺失。"},{"w":"stapler","p":"n.","d":"a small machine used to fasten papers with staples","c":"訂書機","s":"Could you pass me the stapler? I need to fasten these twenty pages together before the meeting starts in five minutes.","t":"你可以把訂書機遞給我嗎？我需要在五分鐘後會議開始前把這二十頁釘在一起。"},{"w":"starvation","p":"n.","d":"suffering or death caused by not having enough food","c":"飢餓；餓死","s":"During the long drought, thousands of farm animals died of starvation because the grass dried up and the rivers stopped flowing.","t":"在漫長的乾旱期間，數千隻農場動物死於飢餓，因為草都枯死了，河流也停止流動。","h":1},{"w":"starve","p":"v.","d":"to suffer or die because you do not have enough food","c":"挨餓；餓死","s":"Many birds starve in winter if the snow covers the ground for weeks, so my grandmother always puts seeds outside.","t":"如果積雪覆蓋地面好幾週，許多鳥會在冬天餓死，所以我奶奶總是在外面放種子。"},{"w":"starve to death","p":"v.phr.","d":"to die because of a lack of food","c":"餓死","s":"The lost hikers were found after nine days, and the doctor said they would have starved to death without the river water and wild berries.","t":"迷路的登山客在九天後被找到，醫生說要不是有河水和野莓，他們早就餓死了。","a":"starved to death"},{"w":"starving","p":"adj.","d":"very hungry (informal)","c":"非常餓的","s":"We skipped lunch to finish the science project, so by four o'clock everyone in the group was starving and tired.","t":"我們為了完成科學專題沒吃午餐，所以到了四點，小組裡每個人都餓壞了又累。"},{"w":"statesman","p":"n.","d":"a wise and respected political leader","c":"政治家","s":"The old statesman was respected by both parties because he always put the good of the country before his own career.","t":"這位老政治家受到兩黨的尊敬，因為他總是把國家的利益放在自己的事業之前。","h":1},{"w":"statesmanship","p":"n.","d":"the skill of being a wise and fair political leader","c":"政治才能；治國之才","s":"Ending the war without more fighting required real statesmanship, and the leaders of both countries were later given a peace prize.","t":"在不再動武的情況下結束戰爭需要真正的政治才能，兩國領導人後來都獲得了和平獎。"},{"w":"state","p":"n.","d":"a country; one part of a country with its own government","c":"國家；州","s":"California is the largest state in the United States by population, and more than forty million people live there.","t":"加州是美國人口最多的州，有超過四千萬人住在那裡。"},{"w":"statement","p":"n.","d":"something you say or write officially","c":"聲明；陳述","s":"The mayor made a short statement to the reporters, promising that the bridge would be repaired before the summer holidays.","t":"市長對記者發表了簡短的聲明，承諾橋樑會在暑假之前修好。"},{"w":"stationary","p":"adj.","d":"not moving","c":"靜止的；不動的","s":"The train remained stationary for almost an hour because a tree had fallen across the tracks during the storm.","t":"火車靜止了將近一個小時，因為暴風雨中有一棵樹倒在鐵軌上。","h":1},{"w":"remain stationary","p":"v.phr.","d":"to stay in one place without moving","c":"保持不動","s":"The nurse asked me to remain stationary while the machine took a picture of my broken arm, which was harder than it sounds.","t":"護士要我在機器為我骨折的手臂拍照時保持不動，這比聽起來困難多了。"},{"w":"stationary bike","p":"n.phr.","d":"an exercise bicycle that stays in one place","c":"健身腳踏車","s":"On rainy days my mother rides the stationary bike in the living room for thirty minutes while she watches the news.","t":"下雨天我媽媽會在客廳一邊看新聞，一邊騎健身腳踏車三十分鐘。"},{"w":"station","p":"n.","d":"a place where trains or buses stop; a building for a special service","c":"車站；站","s":"The new MRT station is only a five-minute walk from our school, so many students no longer need the school bus.","t":"新的捷運站離我們學校只有五分鐘的步行路程，所以許多學生不再需要校車。"},{"w":"stationery","p":"n.","d":"paper, pens, envelopes, and other things used for writing","c":"文具；信紙","s":"The school gives every new student a bag of stationery, including notebooks, pencils, and a ruler, on the first day.","t":"學校在開學第一天給每位新生一袋文具，包括筆記本、鉛筆和尺。","h":1},{"w":"stationery store","p":"n.phr.","d":"a shop that sells pens, paper, and other writing things","c":"文具店","s":"There is a small stationery store next to the school gate, and students rush there before class whenever they forget a pen.","t":"學校大門旁有一家小文具店，學生每次忘了帶筆就會在上課前衝去那裡。"},{"w":"office supplies","p":"n.phr.","d":"things like paper, pens, and folders used in an office","c":"辦公用品","s":"Our manager orders office supplies once a month, so if you need more folders or printer paper, tell her by Friday.","t":"我們經理每月訂購一次辦公用品，所以如果你需要更多資料夾或印表紙，請在星期五前告訴她。"},{"w":"stature","p":"n.","d":"a person's height","c":"身高；身材","s":"Although the basketball player is small in stature, he is so fast that taller players can never catch him.","t":"雖然這位籃球員身材矮小，但他速度太快，比較高的球員永遠追不上他。","h":1},{"w":"stature","p":"n.","d":"the importance and respect a person has because of their achievements","c":"聲望；地位","s":"The scientist's stature grew after her discovery, and universities around the world invited her to give talks.","t":"這位科學家的聲望在她的發現之後提高了，世界各地的大學都邀請她去演講。"},{"w":"of great stature","p":"phr.","d":"very important and respected","c":"德高望重的；地位崇高的","s":"He is a writer of great stature, so young authors feel honored when he agrees to read their first novels.","t":"他是一位地位崇高的作家，所以當他同意讀年輕作者的第一本小說時，他們都感到榮幸。"},{"w":"status","p":"n.","d":"a person's position or rank in society; the situation at a time","c":"地位；身分；狀態","s":"In the past, owning a horse was a sign of high social status, just as owning an expensive car is today.","t":"在過去，擁有一匹馬是高社會地位的象徵，就像今天擁有一輛昂貴的汽車一樣。"},{"w":"statute","p":"n.","d":"a written law passed by a government","c":"法令；成文法","s":"Under a new statute, every restaurant in the city must show the price of each dish clearly on the menu.","t":"根據一項新法令，市內每家餐廳都必須在菜單上清楚標示每道菜的價格。","h":1},{"w":"statutory","p":"adj.","d":"decided or controlled by law","c":"法定的","s":"Workers in this country have a statutory right to at least ten days of paid holiday every year, no matter where they work.","t":"這個國家的勞工有法定權利，每年至少享有十天有薪假，不論他們在哪裡工作。"},{"w":"by statute","p":"phr.","d":"according to a written law","c":"依法；根據法令","s":"The minimum age for driving is fixed by statute, so the police cannot make exceptions even for very careful teenagers.","t":"最低駕駛年齡是依法規定的，所以即使是非常小心的青少年，警察也不能破例。"},{"w":"stepchild","p":"n.","d":"the child of your husband or wife from an earlier marriage","c":"繼子女","s":"He treats his stepchild exactly like his own children, and nobody at school even knows they are not related by blood.","t":"他對待繼子就像對待自己的孩子一樣，學校裡甚至沒有人知道他們沒有血緣關係。","h":1},{"w":"stepfather","p":"n.","d":"the man who is married to your mother but is not your father","c":"繼父","s":"My stepfather taught me how to ride a bike and fix a flat tire, and I have called him Dad since I was six.","t":"我的繼父教我騎腳踏車和修補爆胎，從六歲起我就叫他爸爸。","h":1},{"w":"stepmother","p":"n.","d":"the woman who is married to your father but is not your mother","c":"繼母","s":"In many old fairy tales the stepmother is cruel, but in real life many of them love their new families deeply.","t":"在許多古老的童話故事裡繼母很殘忍，但在現實生活中，許多繼母深愛著她們的新家庭。","h":1},{"w":"stepson","p":"n.","d":"the son of your husband or wife from an earlier marriage","c":"繼子","s":"She drives her stepson to baseball practice every Saturday morning, even though his father could easily take him.","t":"她每個星期六早上開車送繼子去練棒球，即使他的父親可以輕易帶他去。"},{"w":"stepdaughter","p":"n.","d":"the daughter of your husband or wife from an earlier marriage","c":"繼女","s":"When his stepdaughter graduated from university, he was the one who cried the most at the ceremony.","t":"當他的繼女大學畢業時，他是典禮上哭得最厲害的人。"},{"w":"stepsister","p":"n.","d":"the daughter of your stepfather or stepmother","c":"繼姊妹","s":"My stepsister and I fought a lot when our parents first married, but now she is my closest friend.","t":"我們的父母剛結婚時，我和我的繼姊常常吵架，但現在她是我最親密的朋友。"},{"w":"stimulation","p":"n.","d":"something that makes you more active, interested, or excited","c":"刺激；激勵","s":"Babies need plenty of stimulation, so parents should talk, sing, and play with them instead of leaving them in front of a screen.","t":"嬰兒需要充分的刺激，所以父母應該跟他們說話、唱歌和玩耍，而不是把他們放在螢幕前。","h":1},{"w":"stimulate","p":"v.","d":"to make something more active or make someone interested","c":"刺激；激發","s":"The government hopes the new holiday will stimulate tourism, because hotels and restaurants have been empty since the pandemic.","t":"政府希望新的假期能刺激觀光，因為自疫情以來旅館和餐廳一直空蕩蕩的。"},{"w":"stimulus","p":"n.","d":"something that causes activity, growth, or a reaction","c":"刺激（物）；激勵","s":"Lower interest rates were meant to be a stimulus for the economy, and within months more people started buying houses again.","t":"較低的利率是為了作為經濟的刺激，幾個月內又有更多人開始買房子。"},{"w":"stimulating","p":"adj.","d":"making you feel interested and full of ideas","c":"有啟發性的；令人興奮的","s":"The debate was so stimulating that the students kept arguing about it in the hallway long after the bell rang.","t":"這場辯論非常有啟發性，鐘響很久之後學生們還在走廊上繼續爭論。"},{"w":"strait","p":"n.","d":"a narrow area of sea between two pieces of land","c":"海峽","s":"Ships must move slowly through the narrow strait because the water is shallow and the rocks are hard to see at night.","t":"船隻必須緩慢通過狹窄的海峽，因為水很淺，而且晚上很難看見岩石。","h":1},{"w":"the Taiwan Strait","p":"n.phr.","d":"the sea between Taiwan and mainland China","c":"台灣海峽","s":"Fishing boats from both sides have worked in the Taiwan Strait for hundreds of years, and the fish there feed millions of people.","t":"數百年來兩岸的漁船都在台灣海峽作業，那裡的魚養活了數百萬人。"},{"w":"in dire straits","p":"phr.","d":"in a very difficult or dangerous situation","c":"陷入困境","s":"The family business was in dire straits after the fire, so the whole town held a market to raise money for them.","t":"火災後這家家族企業陷入困境，所以全鎮的人舉辦市集為他們募款。"},{"w":"strangle","p":"v.","d":"to kill someone by pressing their throat","c":"勒死；掐死","s":"In the detective story, the killer tried to strangle his victim with a scarf, but she escaped and called the police.","t":"在偵探故事裡，兇手試圖用圍巾勒死被害人，但她逃脫並報了警。","h":1},{"w":"strangle","p":"v.","d":"to stop something from growing or developing","c":"扼殺；抑制","s":"Too many rules can strangle creativity, so the art teacher lets her students choose their own topics and materials.","t":"太多的規定會扼殺創意，所以美術老師讓學生自己選擇主題和材料。"},{"w":"stranglehold","p":"n.","d":"complete control over something that stops it from developing","c":"壓制；完全控制","s":"The big company has a stranglehold on the local market, and small shops cannot survive because they cannot match its prices.","t":"這家大公司完全控制了當地市場，小店無法生存，因為它們無法與它的價格競爭。"},{"w":"stray","p":"adj.","d":"lost or without a home (for animals); separated from a group","c":"流浪的；走失的；零星的","s":"A stray dog followed us all the way home from the park, so my parents finally agreed to let us keep it.","t":"一隻流浪狗從公園一路跟著我們回家，所以我父母終於同意讓我們養牠。","h":1},{"w":"stray","p":"v.","d":"to move away from the place or group you should be in","c":"走失；偏離","s":"The teacher told the children not to stray from the group in the museum, because the building was large and crowded.","t":"老師告訴孩子們在博物館裡不要脫離隊伍，因為建築物很大又很擁擠。"},{"w":"stray","p":"n.","d":"an animal that has no home","c":"流浪動物","s":"The animal shelter takes in about two hundred strays every year and tries to find a loving family for each one.","t":"動物收容所每年收容大約兩百隻流浪動物，並試著為每一隻找到有愛心的家庭。","a":"strays"},{"w":"stray from the topic","p":"v.phr.","d":"to start talking about something different from the main subject","c":"離題","s":"Our history teacher often strays from the topic and tells us funny stories about his travels, but we learn a lot anyway.","t":"我們的歷史老師常常離題，跟我們講他旅行時的趣事，但我們還是學到很多。","a":"strays from the topic"},{"w":"stride","p":"n.","d":"a long step","c":"大步；跨步","s":"With his long stride, my tall brother crosses the football field in half the time it takes me.","t":"我高個子的哥哥邁著長長的大步，只用我一半的時間就穿過足球場。","h":1},{"w":"stride, strode, stridden","p":"v.","d":"to walk with long steps, usually quickly and with confidence","c":"大步走","s":"The manager strode into the meeting room, dropped the report on the table, and asked who had written the final page.","t":"經理大步走進會議室，把報告丟在桌上，問是誰寫了最後一頁。","a":"strode"},{"w":"make great strides","p":"v.phr.","d":"to improve or make progress quickly","c":"取得長足進步","s":"Scientists have made great strides in treating this disease, and many patients now live normal lives with a daily pill.","t":"科學家在治療這種疾病方面取得了長足進步，許多病人現在每天吃一顆藥就能過正常生活。","a":"made great strides"},{"w":"take sth in stride","p":"v.phr.","d":"to deal with a problem calmly without getting upset","c":"從容應付；泰然處之","s":"When the hotel lost our booking, my father took it in stride and simply found another place for us to stay nearby.","t":"當飯店弄丟我們的訂房時，我爸爸泰然處之，直接在附近找了另一個地方讓我們住。","a":"took it in stride"},{"w":"stroll","p":"n.","d":"a slow, relaxed walk","c":"散步；漫步","s":"After dinner, my grandparents go for a stroll along the river, and they always come back with stories about the neighbors.","t":"晚餐後，我的祖父母會沿著河邊散步，而且總是帶著鄰居的故事回來。","h":1},{"w":"stroll","p":"v.","d":"to walk slowly in a relaxed way","c":"漫步；閒逛","s":"On Sunday afternoons we like to stroll through the old town and look at the little shops without buying anything.","t":"星期天下午我們喜歡在老城區閒逛，看看小店但什麼都不買。"},{"w":"take a stroll","p":"v.phr.","d":"to go for a slow, relaxed walk","c":"去散步","s":"The doctor suggested that my father take a stroll every morning instead of sitting at his desk all day long.","t":"醫生建議我爸爸每天早上去散步，而不是整天坐在辦公桌前。"},{"w":"stroller","p":"n.","d":"a small chair on wheels for pushing a baby","c":"嬰兒推車","s":"The young couple pushed the stroller through the park while their baby slept peacefully under a tiny blanket.","t":"這對年輕夫妻推著嬰兒推車穿過公園，他們的寶寶在小毯子下安靜地睡著。"},{"w":"stun","p":"v.","d":"to surprise or shock someone so much that they cannot speak or react","c":"使震驚；使目瞪口呆","s":"The news of the school's closing seemed to stun the teachers, and nobody said a word for almost a minute.","t":"學校即將關閉的消息似乎震驚了老師們，將近一分鐘沒有人說一句話。","h":1},{"w":"stun","p":"v.","d":"to make a person or animal unconscious for a short time by hitting them","c":"使昏迷；擊昏","s":"The bird flew into the window and the hit seemed to stun it, but after a few minutes it got up and flew away.","t":"那隻鳥撞上窗戶，撞擊似乎讓牠暫時昏迷，但幾分鐘後牠就站起來飛走了。"},{"w":"stunned","p":"adj.","d":"very surprised or shocked","c":"震驚的；目瞪口呆的","s":"The stunned audience sat in silence for a moment when the magician made the whole car disappear from the stage.","t":"當魔術師讓整輛車從舞台上消失時，震驚的觀眾安靜地坐了一會兒。"},{"w":"stunning","p":"adj.","d":"extremely beautiful or surprising","c":"極美的；令人震驚的","s":"The view from the hotel balcony was stunning, with the whole bay and the mountains turning gold at sunset.","t":"從飯店陽台看出去的景色美極了，整個海灣和山脈在日落時變成金色。"},{"w":"stutter","p":"n.","d":"a speech problem in which a person repeats sounds or has trouble starting words","c":"口吃","s":"The famous actor had a bad stutter as a child, but years of practice helped him speak clearly on stage.","t":"這位著名的演員小時候口吃得很嚴重，但多年的練習幫助他在舞台上清楚地說話。","h":1},{"w":"stutter","p":"v.","d":"to speak with difficulty, repeating sounds or pausing before words","c":"口吃；結結巴巴地說","s":"When the teacher suddenly asked him to read aloud, the nervous boy began to stutter and his face turned red.","t":"當老師突然要他大聲朗讀時，緊張的男孩開始結巴，臉也紅了。"},{"w":"stammer","p":"v.","d":"to speak with pauses and repeated sounds because you are nervous or have a speech problem","c":"結巴","s":"I always stammer when I have to speak in front of a large crowd, so I practice my speeches many times at home.","t":"我在一大群人面前講話時總是會結巴，所以我在家裡把演講練習很多次。"},{"w":"have a stutter","p":"v.phr.","d":"to speak with a stutter","c":"有口吃的毛病","s":"My cousin has a stutter, but he never lets it stop him from asking questions in class or talking to new people.","t":"我表弟有口吃的毛病，但他從不讓這件事阻止他在課堂上發問或跟新朋友聊天。","a":"has a stutter"},{"w":"stylish","p":"adj.","d":"attractive and fashionable","c":"時髦的；有型的","s":"My aunt always looks stylish, even when she is just going to the supermarket in jeans and a simple white shirt.","t":"我阿姨看起來總是很時髦，即使她只是穿著牛仔褲和簡單的白襯衫去超市。","h":1},{"w":"style","p":"n.","d":"a particular way of doing something; fashion","c":"風格；款式；時尚","s":"The new café is decorated in a Japanese style, with wooden tables, paper lamps, and plants in every corner.","t":"這家新咖啡店以日式風格裝潢，有木桌、紙燈，每個角落都有植物。"},{"w":"stylishly","p":"adv.","d":"in an attractive and fashionable way","c":"時髦地","s":"The hotel rooms are stylishly designed, so many guests take photos of the furniture and post them online.","t":"飯店房間設計得很時髦，所以許多客人會拍家具的照片並發到網路上。"},{"w":"in style","p":"phr.","d":"fashionable; in an impressive way","c":"流行的；風光地","s":"Long skirts are back in style this year, and every shop in the mall seems to be selling them in bright colors.","t":"今年長裙又流行起來，購物中心的每家店似乎都在賣亮色的長裙。"},{"w":"stylist","p":"n.","d":"a person whose job is to cut hair or choose clothes for people","c":"髮型師；造型師","s":"The stylist suggested a shorter haircut for the hot summer, and my sister loved the result so much that she took twenty selfies.","t":"髮型師建議為炎熱的夏天剪短一點的髮型，我姊姊非常喜歡結果，自拍了二十張。"},{"w":"subjective","p":"adj.","d":"based on personal feelings and opinions rather than facts","c":"主觀的","s":"Judging art is always subjective, so the painting you love might be the one your best friend finds boring.","t":"評判藝術總是主觀的，所以你喜愛的那幅畫可能正是你最好的朋友覺得無聊的那幅。","h":1},{"w":"subjectively","p":"adv.","d":"in a way that is based on personal feelings rather than facts","c":"主觀地","s":"Teachers try not to grade essays subjectively, so our school uses a clear list of points to score every paper.","t":"老師們盡量不主觀地評分作文，所以我們學校使用清楚的評分項目來給每篇文章打分。"},{"w":"objective","p":"adj.","d":"based on facts, not on personal feelings","c":"客觀的","s":"A good reporter must stay objective and report what actually happened, even when she dislikes the people involved.","t":"一位好記者必須保持客觀，報導真正發生的事，即使她不喜歡其中涉及的人。"},{"w":"subject","p":"n.","d":"the thing being talked about or studied; a school course","c":"主題；科目","s":"English is my favorite subject at school because the teacher lets us watch movies and discuss them in class.","t":"英文是我在學校最喜歡的科目，因為老師讓我們看電影並在課堂上討論。"}]},{"unit":36,"theme":"subordinate – symmetry","cards":[{"w":"subordinate","p":"adj.","d":"having a lower position or less importance","c":"下級的；次要的","s":"In the army, a subordinate officer must follow the orders of the general, even when he does not agree with them.","t":"在軍隊裡，下級軍官必須服從將軍的命令，即使他不同意。","h":1},{"w":"subordinate","p":"n.","d":"a person who has a lower position than you at work","c":"部屬；下屬","s":"A good manager listens to her subordinates and gives them credit when their ideas help the company grow.","t":"好的經理會傾聽她的部屬，並在他們的想法幫助公司成長時給予肯定。","a":"subordinates"},{"w":"subordinate","p":"v.","d":"to treat something as less important than something else","c":"使居次要地位","s":"During the exam month, my brother decided to subordinate his love of basketball to his studies and stopped playing every evening.","t":"在考試月期間，我哥哥決定把他對籃球的熱愛放在學業之後，不再每天晚上打球。"},{"w":"be subordinate to","p":"v.phr.","d":"to be less important than or under the control of","c":"從屬於；次於","s":"In this company every department is subordinate to the main office in Taipei, so no branch can change prices on its own.","t":"在這家公司，每個部門都隸屬於台北總公司，所以沒有分店能自行改變價格。","a":"is subordinate to"},{"w":"subscribe","p":"v.","d":"to pay money regularly to receive a magazine, service, or channel","c":"訂閱","s":"My father used to subscribe to three newspapers, but now he reads all the news on his phone for free.","t":"我爸爸以前訂閱三份報紙，但現在他都在手機上免費看新聞。","h":1},{"w":"subscribe to","p":"v.phr.","d":"to pay for a service regularly; to agree with an idea","c":"訂閱；贊同","s":"If you subscribe to our channel, you will get a message every time we upload a new English lesson.","t":"如果你訂閱我們的頻道，每次我們上傳新的英文課程時你都會收到通知。","h":1},{"w":"subscription","p":"n.","d":"an amount of money you pay regularly to receive a service","c":"訂閱（費）","s":"The music app offers a student subscription for half price, so I can listen to any song without advertisements.","t":"這個音樂應用程式提供半價的學生訂閱方案，所以我可以聽任何歌曲而沒有廣告。"},{"w":"subscriber","p":"n.","d":"a person who pays to receive a service or magazine","c":"訂閱者；訂戶","s":"The young cook's cooking channel reached one million subscribers last week, and she celebrated by making a giant cake.","t":"這位年輕廚師的烹飪頻道上週達到一百萬訂閱者，她做了一個巨大的蛋糕來慶祝。","a":"subscribers"},{"w":"subsidize","p":"v.","d":"to pay part of the cost of something so that it is cheaper for people","c":"補助；資助","s":"The city decided to subsidize bus tickets for students, so a ride to school now costs only eight dollars.","t":"市政府決定補助學生的公車票，所以現在搭車上學只要八元。","h":1},{"w":"subsidy","p":"n.","d":"money given by the government to make something cheaper","c":"補助金；津貼","s":"Farmers receive a subsidy from the government when the price of rice falls too low to cover their costs.","t":"當米價跌到無法支付成本時，農民會從政府獲得補助金。"},{"w":"subsidized","p":"adj.","d":"made cheaper because part of the cost is paid by the government","c":"有補助的","s":"The university offers subsidized housing for students from poor families, and the rent is less than half the normal price.","t":"這所大學為貧困家庭的學生提供有補助的住宿，租金不到正常價格的一半。"},{"w":"government subsidy","p":"n.phr.","d":"money the government pays to support something","c":"政府補助","s":"Thanks to a government subsidy, the old bus company could buy ten electric buses and keep the mountain route open.","t":"多虧了政府補助，這家老公車公司才能購買十輛電動公車，並維持山區路線營運。"},{"w":"succession","p":"n.","d":"a number of things happening one after another; taking a position after someone","c":"一連串；繼承","s":"The team suffered a succession of injuries this season, and at one point only nine healthy players were left.","t":"球隊本季遭遇一連串的傷病，有一段時間只剩九名健康的球員。","h":1},{"w":"in succession","p":"phr.","d":"one after another without a break","c":"接連地；連續地","s":"Our school has won the city basketball championship three years in succession, and the coach wants a fourth title this spring.","t":"我們學校已經連續三年贏得市籃球冠軍，教練希望今年春天拿下第四座。","h":1},{"w":"successive","p":"adj.","d":"following one after another","c":"連續的；接連的","s":"It rained for five successive days during our trip, so we spent most of the holiday playing cards in the hotel.","t":"我們旅行期間連續下了五天雨，所以我們大部分的假期都在飯店裡玩牌。"},{"w":"successor","p":"n.","d":"a person who takes a position after someone else","c":"繼任者；接班人","s":"The principal will retire in June, and the school board is still looking for a successor who can lead the new building project.","t":"校長將在六月退休，校董會仍在尋找能領導新大樓計畫的繼任者。"},{"w":"succeed","p":"v.","d":"to take a position after someone; to achieve what you want","c":"繼任；成功","s":"When the old king died, his daughter was the first woman to succeed to the throne in the country's long history.","t":"老國王去世後，他的女兒成為該國漫長歷史上第一位繼承王位的女性。"},{"w":"suffocate","p":"v.","d":"to die or make someone die because they cannot breathe","c":"使窒息；窒息而死","s":"Firefighters warn that people in a burning building often suffocate from the smoke before the flames ever reach them.","t":"消防員警告，火災大樓裡的人往往在火焰到達之前就因濃煙而窒息。","h":1},{"w":"suffocate","p":"v.","d":"to feel unable to breathe because of heat or lack of air","c":"感到窒息；喘不過氣","s":"The bus was so crowded and hot that I thought I would suffocate before we reached the next stop.","t":"公車又擠又熱，我覺得在到達下一站之前我就要喘不過氣了。"},{"w":"suffocating","p":"adj.","d":"making it hard to breathe; making you feel you cannot be free","c":"令人窒息的","s":"The suffocating heat in the classroom made it impossible to concentrate, so the teacher moved the lesson to the library.","t":"教室裡令人窒息的熱氣讓人無法專心，所以老師把課移到圖書館上。"},{"w":"suffocation","p":"n.","d":"death or difficulty caused by being unable to breathe","c":"窒息","s":"Plastic bags should be kept away from small children because of the danger of suffocation, as the warning on the bag says.","t":"塑膠袋應該放在幼童拿不到的地方，因為有窒息的危險，就像袋子上的警語所說的。"},{"w":"suitcase","p":"n.","d":"a large flat bag with a handle that you carry clothes in when you travel","c":"行李箱","s":"My suitcase was too heavy at the airport, so I had to take out three books and carry them in my backpack.","t":"我的行李箱在機場超重了，所以我必須拿出三本書放在背包裡。","h":1},{"w":"pack a suitcase","p":"v.phr.","d":"to put clothes and other things into a suitcase before a trip","c":"收拾行李","s":"The night before the trip, my mother helped me pack my suitcase and reminded me not to forget my passport.","t":"出發前一晚，我媽媽幫我收拾行李，並提醒我別忘了護照。","a":"pack my suitcase"},{"w":"luggage","p":"n.","d":"all the bags and suitcases you take when you travel","c":"行李","s":"Passengers must keep their luggage with them at all times, because bags left alone in the airport will be removed.","t":"乘客必須隨時把行李帶在身邊，因為留在機場無人看管的袋子會被移走。"},{"w":"baggage","p":"n.","d":"the bags you carry when traveling (same as luggage)","c":"行李","s":"Each passenger can check in one piece of baggage for free, but a second bag costs an extra fifty dollars.","t":"每位乘客可以免費託運一件行李，但第二件要多付五十元。"},{"w":"summon","p":"v.","d":"to officially order someone to come to a place","c":"召喚；傳喚","s":"The principal decided to summon the three boys to his office after he heard about the fight in the playground.","t":"校長聽說操場上的打架事件後，決定召那三個男孩到他的辦公室。","h":1},{"w":"summon up courage","p":"v.phr.","d":"to make yourself brave enough to do something","c":"鼓起勇氣","s":"It took him a whole week to summon up the courage to ask the new girl in class if she wanted to study together.","t":"他花了整整一個星期才鼓起勇氣問班上的新女生要不要一起讀書。","a":"summon up the courage"},{"w":"summons","p":"n.","d":"an official order to appear in court","c":"傳票","s":"The driver received a summons in the mail, and it said he had to appear in court next Tuesday about the accident.","t":"那位駕駛收到一張郵寄來的傳票，上面說他必須在下週二就這起事故出庭。"},{"w":"summon help","p":"v.phr.","d":"to call for people to come and help","c":"呼救；求援","s":"When the old man fell on the stairs, a neighbor quickly used her phone to summon help, and an ambulance arrived in ten minutes.","t":"當老人在樓梯上跌倒時，一位鄰居迅速用手機求援，救護車十分鐘內就到了。"},{"w":"superficial","p":"adj.","d":"only on the surface; not deep or serious","c":"表面的；膚淺的","s":"The doctor said the cut on my knee was only superficial, so I did not need stitches, just a clean bandage.","t":"醫生說我膝蓋上的傷口只是表面的，所以不需要縫合，只要乾淨的繃帶就好。","h":1},{"w":"superficial","p":"adj.","d":"caring only about appearance, not about deeper things","c":"膚淺的（人）","s":"Some people think she is superficial because she talks about clothes all day, but she actually reads more books than anyone I know.","t":"有些人認為她很膚淺，因為她整天談論衣服，但她其實比我認識的任何人都讀更多書。"},{"w":"superficially","p":"adv.","d":"in a way that is only on the surface","c":"表面上；膚淺地","s":"The two phones look superficially similar, but the newer one has a much better camera and a battery that lasts two days.","t":"這兩支手機表面上看起來相似，但較新的那支有好得多的相機和能用兩天的電池。"},{"w":"surface","p":"n.","d":"the outside or top layer of something","c":"表面","s":"The surface of the lake was so still in the early morning that it looked like a giant mirror reflecting the mountains.","t":"清晨湖的表面非常平靜，看起來像一面映照群山的巨大鏡子。"},{"w":"superintendent","p":"n.","d":"a person who is in charge of a building, organization, or school district","c":"主管；總監；（教育局）局長","s":"The superintendent of the apartment building fixed our broken heater within an hour of my phone call last winter.","t":"去年冬天我打電話後不到一小時，公寓大樓的管理主管就修好了我們壞掉的暖氣。","h":1},{"w":"school superintendent","p":"n.phr.","d":"the person in charge of all the schools in an area","c":"教育局長；學區總監","s":"The school superintendent visited our school yesterday to see how the new computer classrooms were being used by the students.","t":"教育局長昨天來我們學校，看學生如何使用新的電腦教室。"},{"w":"supervise","p":"v.","d":"to watch a person or activity to make sure everything is done correctly","c":"監督；管理","s":"A lifeguard must supervise the swimming pool at all times, so he cannot look at his phone even for a minute.","t":"救生員必須隨時監督游泳池，所以他連一分鐘都不能看手機。"},{"w":"supervisor","p":"n.","d":"a person who watches over workers or students","c":"主管；監督者","s":"My supervisor at the restaurant is strict about being on time, but she always praises us when customers leave happy.","t":"我在餐廳的主管對準時很嚴格，但每當顧客滿意離開時她總是稱讚我們。"},{"w":"superiority","p":"n.","d":"the state of being better, stronger, or more important than others","c":"優越（性）；優勢","s":"The team's superiority was clear from the first minute, and they led by twenty points before halftime.","t":"這支球隊的優勢從第一分鐘就很明顯，上半場結束前他們就領先了二十分。","h":1},{"w":"superior","p":"adj.","d":"better or higher in quality, rank, or position","c":"較好的；上級的","s":"This brand of running shoes is superior to the cheaper one because it lasts twice as long and protects your knees.","t":"這個牌子的跑鞋比較便宜的那款更好，因為它耐用兩倍，而且能保護膝蓋。"},{"w":"superior","p":"n.","d":"a person of higher rank, especially at work","c":"上司；上級","s":"Before signing the contract, the young clerk had to show it to his superior, who checked every line carefully.","t":"在簽約之前，年輕職員必須先給他的上司看，上司仔細檢查了每一行。"},{"w":"a sense of superiority","p":"n.phr.","d":"the feeling that you are better than other people","c":"優越感","s":"Winning a few contests gave him a sense of superiority, and his old friends soon grew tired of hearing about his prizes.","t":"贏了幾次比賽讓他有了優越感，他的老朋友很快就聽膩了他的獎項。"},{"w":"inferiority","p":"n.","d":"the state of being worse or lower than others","c":"自卑；低劣","s":"Growing up with a brilliant older sister gave her a feeling of inferiority that she only overcame at university.","t":"和一個聰明的姊姊一起長大讓她有一種自卑感，直到上了大學才克服。"},{"w":"superstitious","p":"adj.","d":"believing that some things bring good or bad luck","c":"迷信的","s":"My grandmother is very superstitious; she never lets anyone open an umbrella inside the house or sweep the floor on New Year's Day.","t":"我奶奶非常迷信；她從不讓任何人在屋裡撐傘，也不讓人在大年初一掃地。","h":1},{"w":"superstition","p":"n.","d":"a belief that some things bring good or bad luck","c":"迷信","s":"In Taiwan there is a superstition that the number four brings bad luck, so many buildings have no fourth floor.","t":"在台灣有一種迷信認為數字四會帶來厄運，所以許多大樓沒有四樓。"},{"w":"be superstitious about","p":"v.phr.","d":"to believe that a certain thing brings good or bad luck","c":"對…感到迷信","s":"Many athletes are superstitious about their clothes, and our goalkeeper wears the same old socks for every important match.","t":"許多運動員對自己的衣服很迷信，我們的守門員每場重要比賽都穿同一雙舊襪子。","a":"are superstitious about"},{"w":"supplement","p":"n.","d":"something added to make something larger or better","c":"補充（物）；補給品","s":"The doctor suggested a vitamin D supplement for my grandfather because he rarely goes outside during the winter.","t":"醫生建議我爺爺服用維他命D補充品，因為他冬天很少出門。","h":1},{"w":"supplement","p":"v.","d":"to add something to make it larger or better","c":"補充；增補","s":"Many teachers supplement their income by giving private lessons on weekends, since salaries have not risen for years.","t":"許多老師靠週末家教來補貼收入，因為薪水多年沒有調漲。"},{"w":"supplementary","p":"adj.","d":"added to something to improve or complete it","c":"補充的；附加的","s":"The textbook comes with supplementary exercises online, and students who finish them usually do better on the test.","t":"這本教科書附有線上補充練習，完成練習的學生通常考試表現較好。"},{"w":"dietary supplement","p":"n.phr.","d":"a pill or powder taken to add vitamins or minerals to your diet","c":"膳食補充品","s":"A dietary supplement cannot replace real food, so you should still eat vegetables even if you take vitamin pills every day.","t":"膳食補充品無法取代真正的食物，所以即使你每天吃維他命，還是應該吃蔬菜。"},{"w":"suppress","p":"v.","d":"to stop something by force; to hide a feeling","c":"鎮壓；壓抑；抑制","s":"The government sent soldiers to suppress the protest, but the pictures spread online and more people joined the next day.","t":"政府派士兵去鎮壓抗議活動，但照片在網路上傳開，第二天有更多人加入。","h":1},{"w":"suppress a yawn","p":"v.phr.","d":"to stop yourself from yawning","c":"忍住哈欠","s":"The speech was so long that I had to suppress a yawn every few minutes, hoping the speaker would not notice.","t":"演講太長了，我每隔幾分鐘就得忍住哈欠，希望演講者不會注意到。"},{"w":"suppress one's feelings","p":"v.phr.","d":"to hide what you really feel","c":"壓抑感情","s":"It is not healthy to suppress your feelings for years, so my counselor encourages me to talk about what makes me angry.","t":"多年壓抑感情對健康不好，所以我的輔導老師鼓勵我說出讓我生氣的事。","a":"suppress your feelings"},{"w":"suppression","p":"n.","d":"the act of stopping something by force or hiding it","c":"鎮壓；壓抑","s":"The suppression of free newspapers was one of the first signs that the new leader did not plan to allow any criticism.","t":"對自由報紙的壓制是新領導人不打算允許任何批評的最早跡象之一。"},{"w":"surge","p":"n.","d":"a sudden large increase; a sudden strong movement forward","c":"激增；洶湧","s":"There was a surge in ticket sales after the movie's trailer went viral, and every evening show sold out within hours.","t":"電影預告片爆紅後票房激增，每場晚間場次幾小時內就售罄。","h":1},{"w":"surge","p":"v.","d":"to increase suddenly; to move forward suddenly and powerfully","c":"激增；湧動","s":"Prices of vegetables tend to surge after a typhoon because so many farms are damaged by the wind and rain.","t":"颱風過後蔬菜價格往往會飆漲，因為許多農田被風雨損壞。"},{"w":"a surge in","p":"n.phr.","d":"a sudden large increase in something","c":"…的激增","s":"Hospitals reported a surge in flu cases this week, so the health department is asking everyone to wash their hands often.","t":"醫院通報本週流感病例激增，所以衛生單位呼籲大家勤洗手。"},{"w":"surge forward","p":"v.phr.","d":"to move forward suddenly as a group","c":"向前湧","s":"When the store opened its doors on sale day, the crowd surged forward and two people were nearly knocked down.","t":"特賣日商店開門時，人群向前湧，有兩個人差點被撞倒。","a":"surged forward"},{"w":"surgical","p":"adj.","d":"connected with medical operations","c":"外科的；手術的","s":"The nurse laid out the surgical tools on a clean cloth while the doctor washed his hands for the third time.","t":"護士把手術器具擺在乾淨的布上，醫生則第三次洗手。","h":1},{"w":"surgical mask","p":"n.phr.","d":"a thin mask worn over the nose and mouth to stop germs from spreading","c":"外科口罩","s":"During flu season, every visitor to the hospital must wear a surgical mask, which the front desk gives out for free.","t":"流感季節期間，每位到醫院的訪客都必須戴外科口罩，櫃檯會免費發放。"},{"w":"surgery","p":"n.","d":"medical treatment in which a doctor cuts open the body to repair or remove something","c":"手術","s":"My uncle needs surgery on his knee next month, and the doctor says he will walk normally again after six weeks.","t":"我叔叔下個月需要做膝蓋手術，醫生說六週後他就能正常走路。"},{"w":"surgeon","p":"n.","d":"a doctor who performs operations","c":"外科醫生","s":"The surgeon explained the operation to the family carefully and promised to call them as soon as it was finished.","t":"外科醫生仔細地向家屬說明手術，並承諾手術一結束就打電話給他們。"},{"w":"surname","p":"n.","d":"the name shared by all members of a family; last name","c":"姓","s":"In Chinese, the surname comes first, so Lin Mei-ling would be called Ms. Lin, not Ms. Mei-ling, in a formal letter.","t":"在中文裡姓放在前面，所以林美玲在正式信件中會被稱為林女士，而不是美玲女士。","h":1},{"w":"family name","p":"n.phr.","d":"the name shared by a family; surname","c":"姓氏","s":"Chen is the most common family name in Taiwan, so there are four students named Chen in my class alone.","t":"陳是台灣最常見的姓氏，光是我們班就有四個姓陳的學生。"},{"w":"first name","p":"n.phr.","d":"the name your parents gave you, which comes before your family name","c":"名字","s":"Americans often call each other by their first name at work, even when they are talking to the boss.","t":"美國人在工作時常常直呼彼此的名字，即使是跟老闆說話也一樣。"},{"w":"full name","p":"n.phr.","d":"your first name and your family name together","c":"全名","s":"Please write your full name and student number at the top of the test paper before you begin answering the questions.","t":"請在開始作答前，在試卷上方寫上你的全名和學號。"},{"w":"surpass","p":"v.","d":"to be better or greater than someone or something","c":"超越；勝過","s":"The young swimmer hopes to surpass her coach's old record this year, and she is already only one second behind it.","t":"這位年輕的游泳選手希望今年能超越她教練的舊紀錄，而且她現在只差一秒。","h":1},{"w":"surpass expectations","p":"v.phr.","d":"to be much better than people expected","c":"超出預期","s":"The new restaurant has surpassed expectations; it was supposed to serve fifty customers a day but now serves two hundred.","t":"新餐廳的表現超出預期；原本預計每天服務五十位顧客，現在卻服務兩百位。","a":"surpassed expectations"},{"w":"surpass oneself","p":"v.phr.","d":"to do something better than you have ever done before","c":"超越自我","s":"The pianist surpassed herself at last night's concert, and even her teacher said she had never heard her play so beautifully.","t":"這位鋼琴家在昨晚的音樂會上超越了自我，連她的老師都說從沒聽過她彈得這麼美。","a":"surpassed herself"},{"w":"unsurpassed","p":"adj.","d":"better than anything or anyone else","c":"無與倫比的","s":"The view from the top of Yushan is unsurpassed in Taiwan, and hikers often cry when they see the sunrise from there.","t":"從玉山頂上看到的景色在台灣是無與倫比的，登山客在那裡看到日出時常常會哭。"},{"w":"suspense","p":"n.","d":"a feeling of excited worry about what will happen next","c":"懸念；緊張感","s":"The movie keeps you in suspense until the last minute, when you finally learn who stole the painting from the museum.","t":"這部電影讓你一直處在懸念中，直到最後一分鐘你才知道是誰從博物館偷走那幅畫。","h":1},{"w":"keep sb in suspense","p":"v.phr.","d":"to make someone wait nervously to find out what will happen","c":"讓某人懸著一顆心","s":"Please do not keep me in suspense any longer; just tell me whether I passed the driving test or not.","t":"請不要再讓我懸著一顆心了；直接告訴我駕照考試到底過了沒。","a":"keep me in suspense","h":1},{"w":"suspension","p":"n.","d":"a punishment in which someone is not allowed to work or attend school for a time; stopping something for a while","c":"停學；停職；暫停","s":"The student received a three-day suspension for cheating on the exam, and his parents had to come to the school for a meeting.","t":"這名學生因為考試作弊被停學三天，他的父母必須到學校開會。"},{"w":"suspend","p":"v.","d":"to stop something for a short time; to hang something from above","c":"暫停；停學；懸掛","s":"The school had to suspend all outdoor classes because of the typhoon, and the sports day was moved to next month.","t":"因為颱風，學校必須暫停所有戶外課程，運動會也延到下個月。"},{"w":"suspension bridge","p":"n.phr.","d":"a bridge that hangs from strong cables fixed to towers","c":"吊橋","s":"The old suspension bridge swings a little when you walk across it, which scared my little sister but made my brother laugh.","t":"那座老吊橋在你走過時會稍微搖晃，這嚇壞了我妹妹，卻讓我弟弟大笑。"},{"w":"swamp","p":"n.","d":"an area of very wet, soft land","c":"沼澤","s":"The hikers lost their way and walked into a swamp, where the mud came up to their knees and the mosquitoes never stopped biting.","t":"登山客迷了路走進一片沼澤，泥巴淹到膝蓋，蚊子也不停地叮咬。","h":1},{"w":"swamp","p":"v.","d":"to give someone more work or things than they can deal with","c":"使應接不暇；淹沒","s":"After the TV show mentioned the tiny bakery, orders began to swamp the owner, and she had to hire two more helpers.","t":"電視節目提到這家小麵包店後，訂單開始淹沒店主，她必須再雇用兩個幫手。"},{"w":"be swamped with","p":"v.phr.","d":"to have too much of something to deal with","c":"忙得不可開交；被…淹沒","s":"Our teacher is swamped with essays to grade this week, so she asked us to wait a few more days for our scores.","t":"我們老師這週被要批改的作文淹沒了，所以她要我們再等幾天才能拿到分數。","a":"is swamped with"},{"w":"swampy","p":"adj.","d":"wet and soft like a swamp","c":"沼澤般的；泥濘的","s":"The field behind the school becomes swampy after heavy rain, so the soccer team practices in the gym instead.","t":"學校後面的操場在大雨後會變得泥濘不堪，所以足球隊改在體育館練習。"},{"w":"swarm","p":"n.","d":"a large group of insects moving together; a crowd","c":"一群（昆蟲）；一大群人","s":"A swarm of bees suddenly flew out of the old tree, and everyone at the picnic ran screaming toward the cars.","t":"一群蜜蜂突然從老樹裡飛出來，野餐的每個人都尖叫著跑向車子。","h":1},{"w":"swarm","p":"v.","d":"to move somewhere in a large group","c":"蜂擁；成群移動","s":"Fans began to swarm around the singer's car as soon as it stopped, and the police had to clear a path for her.","t":"歌手的車一停下來，粉絲就開始蜂擁圍住車子，警察必須為她清出一條路。"},{"w":"swarm with","p":"v.phr.","d":"to be full of people or animals moving around","c":"擠滿；充滿","s":"On the first warm weekend of spring, the night market swarmed with tourists, and it took us an hour to buy one bubble tea.","t":"春天第一個溫暖的週末，夜市擠滿了遊客，我們花了一個小時才買到一杯珍珠奶茶。","a":"swarmed with"},{"w":"a swarm of","p":"n.phr.","d":"a large group of flying insects or busy people","c":"一群（飛蟲或忙碌的人）","s":"When the farmer opened the barn door, a swarm of flies rushed out, and he quickly closed it again.","t":"農夫打開穀倉門時，一群蒼蠅衝了出來，他趕緊把門關上。"},{"w":"symbolize","p":"v.","d":"to be a sign of something; to represent an idea","c":"象徵；代表","s":"In many cultures, doves symbolize peace, which is why they are often released at the opening of the Olympic Games.","t":"在許多文化中，鴿子象徵和平，這就是為什麼奧運開幕時經常放飛鴿子。","h":1},{"w":"symbol","p":"n.","d":"a sign, shape, or object that represents something","c":"象徵；符號","s":"The red heart is a symbol of love around the world, and you will see it on cards everywhere in February.","t":"紅心在世界各地是愛的象徵，二月時你到處都能在卡片上看到它。"},{"w":"symbolic","p":"adj.","d":"representing something important; done as a sign rather than for real effect","c":"象徵性的","s":"Planting a tree at the school gate was a symbolic act that showed the students' promise to protect the environment.","t":"在校門口種一棵樹是一個象徵性的舉動，表現了學生保護環境的承諾。"},{"w":"symbolism","p":"n.","d":"the use of symbols to represent ideas, especially in art and literature","c":"象徵手法；象徵主義","s":"The poem is full of symbolism; the winter stands for sadness and the first flower for the hope of a new beginning.","t":"這首詩充滿象徵手法；冬天代表悲傷，第一朵花則代表新開始的希望。"},{"w":"symmetry","p":"n.","d":"the quality of having two halves that match exactly","c":"對稱","s":"The old temple was built with perfect symmetry, so the left side of the courtyard is an exact copy of the right.","t":"這座古廟以完美的對稱建造，所以庭院的左側是右側的完全複製。","h":1},{"w":"symmetrical","p":"adj.","d":"having two halves that are exactly the same","c":"對稱的","s":"A butterfly's wings are symmetrical, which means the pattern on the left wing matches the pattern on the right.","t":"蝴蝶的翅膀是對稱的，這表示左翅的圖案和右翅的圖案相同。"},{"w":"symmetrically","p":"adv.","d":"in a way that has two matching halves","c":"對稱地","s":"The gardener planted the roses symmetrically on both sides of the path, so visitors see the same flowers whichever way they look.","t":"園丁在小徑兩旁對稱地種植玫瑰，所以遊客無論往哪邊看都看到相同的花。"},{"w":"asymmetry","p":"n.","d":"the lack of matching halves","c":"不對稱","s":"The artist used asymmetry on purpose, painting one large tree on the left and nothing at all on the right side.","t":"這位藝術家刻意使用不對稱的手法，在左邊畫了一棵大樹，右邊什麼都沒畫。"}]},{"unit":37,"theme":"sympathize – transmit","cards":[{"w":"sympathize","p":"v.","d":"to feel sorry for someone and understand their problem","c":"同情；體諒","s":"When my friend failed her driving test for the second time, I could really sympathize with her because I had failed mine too.","t":"當我朋友第二次沒通過駕照考試時，我真的能體諒她，因為我自己也曾經沒考過。","h":1},{"w":"sympathize with","p":"v.phr.","d":"to show that you understand and feel sorry for someone","c":"同情…；體諒…","s":"Many people sympathize with the workers who lost their jobs when the factory closed suddenly last month.","t":"許多人同情上個月工廠突然關閉時失去工作的工人們。"},{"w":"sympathy","p":"n.","d":"the feeling of being sorry for someone who has a problem","c":"同情；慰問","s":"The whole class sent a card to show their sympathy after Kevin's grandfather passed away during the summer vacation.","t":"凱文的爺爺在暑假期間過世後，全班寄了一張卡片表達他們的慰問。"},{"w":"sympathetic","p":"adj.","d":"kind and understanding toward someone who has a problem","c":"有同情心的；體諒的","s":"The nurse was so sympathetic that she stayed after work to talk with the frightened little boy before his operation.","t":"那位護士非常有同情心，她下班後還留下來跟那個害怕的小男孩說話，陪他等手術。"},{"w":"symphony","p":"n.","d":"a long piece of music for a large orchestra","c":"交響樂；交響曲","s":"The city orchestra will perform a famous symphony by Beethoven on Saturday evening, and all the tickets sold out in two days.","t":"市立管弦樂團將在星期六晚上演出一首貝多芬著名的交響曲，所有的票兩天內就賣光了。","h":1},{"w":"symphony orchestra","p":"n.phr.","d":"a large group of musicians who play classical music together","c":"交響樂團","s":"My cousin plays the violin in a symphony orchestra, so she practices for at least four hours every single day.","t":"我表姐在一個交響樂團裡拉小提琴，所以她每天至少練習四個小時。"},{"w":"symphonic","p":"adj.","d":"connected with a symphony or a large orchestra","c":"交響樂的","s":"The movie's symphonic music was recorded by eighty musicians, and it made the final battle scene feel much more exciting.","t":"這部電影的交響配樂由八十位音樂家錄製，讓最後的戰鬥場面感覺更加刺激。"},{"w":"synonym","p":"n.","d":"a word that has the same meaning as another word","c":"同義字","s":"If you keep using the word \"good\" in your essay, try to find a synonym such as \"excellent\" or \"wonderful\" instead.","t":"如果你在作文裡一直用 good 這個字，試著找個同義字來代替，像是 excellent 或 wonderful。","h":1},{"w":"synonymous","p":"adj.","d":"having the same meaning; closely connected with something","c":"同義的；等同於…的","s":"For many people, the name of that small town has become synonymous with delicious pineapple cakes and friendly shop owners.","t":"對許多人來說，那個小鎮的名字已經等同於美味的鳳梨酥和友善的店家。"},{"w":"antonym","p":"n.","d":"a word that means the opposite of another word","c":"反義字","s":"The teacher asked us to write one antonym for each word on the list, so I wrote \"cheap\" next to \"expensive.\"","t":"老師要我們為表上的每個字寫一個反義字，所以我在 expensive 旁邊寫了 cheap。"},{"w":"synthetic","p":"adj.","d":"made by people from chemicals, not natural","c":"合成的；人造的","s":"This jacket is made of synthetic materials instead of real leather, so it is cheaper and much easier to clean.","t":"這件夾克是用合成材料做的，而不是真皮，所以比較便宜，也更容易清洗。","h":1},{"w":"synthetic","p":"n.","d":"a material made by people from chemicals","c":"合成物；合成纖維","s":"Natural fibers like cotton feel soft on the skin, while synthetics such as nylon dry faster after you wash them.","t":"像棉這樣的天然纖維穿起來柔軟，而像尼龍這類的合成纖維洗過後乾得比較快。","a":"synthetics"},{"w":"synthesize","p":"v.","d":"to make something by combining chemicals or ideas","c":"合成；綜合","s":"Scientists can now synthesize this medicine in a laboratory, so they no longer need to collect the rare plant from the forest.","t":"科學家現在可以在實驗室裡合成這種藥，所以他們不再需要到森林裡採集那種稀有植物。"},{"w":"synthesis","p":"n.","d":"the act of putting different ideas or things together","c":"綜合；合成","s":"Her final report was a clear synthesis of everything we had learned during the semester, so the teacher used it as an example.","t":"她的期末報告清楚地綜合了我們這學期學到的一切，所以老師把它當作範例。"},{"w":"syrup","p":"n.","d":"a thick sweet liquid made from sugar","c":"糖漿","s":"My little sister loves pancakes, but she always pours so much maple syrup on them that they become too sweet to eat.","t":"我小妹很愛吃鬆餅，但她總是倒太多楓糖糖漿在上面，結果甜到沒辦法吃。","h":1},{"w":"cough syrup","p":"n.phr.","d":"a sweet liquid medicine that you take for a cough","c":"咳嗽糖漿","s":"The doctor told me to take two spoons of cough syrup before bed, and my cough was much better the next morning.","t":"醫生要我睡前喝兩湯匙咳嗽糖漿，第二天早上我的咳嗽就好多了。"},{"w":"syrupy","p":"adj.","d":"thick and sweet like syrup; too sweet","c":"糖漿般的；過甜的","s":"The dessert was so syrupy that I could only finish half of it, even though I usually love sweet things.","t":"這道甜點太甜膩了，我只吃得下一半，雖然我平常很愛吃甜的。"},{"w":"tan","p":"n.","d":"the brown color your skin gets from the sun","c":"曬成的棕褐色；曬黑","s":"After a week at the beach in Kenting, Lisa came back with a deep tan that made all her classmates jealous.","t":"在墾丁海邊待了一週後，麗莎帶著一身深深的曬痕回來，讓同學們都很羨慕。","h":1},{"w":"tan","p":"v.","d":"to become brown because of the sun","c":"曬黑","s":"If you want to tan safely this summer, you should still put on sunscreen and avoid the sun at noon.","t":"如果你今年夏天想安全地曬黑，還是應該擦防曬乳，並且避開中午的太陽。"},{"w":"tan","p":"adj.","d":"light brown in color","c":"棕褐色的","s":"He wore a pair of tan leather shoes with his dark blue suit, and the colors looked great together at the wedding.","t":"他穿了一雙棕褐色的皮鞋搭配深藍色西裝，在婚禮上這兩個顏色搭起來很好看。"},{"w":"tanned","p":"adj.","d":"having brown skin because of the sun","c":"曬黑的","s":"The fisherman's tanned face showed that he had spent most of his life working outside under the hot sun.","t":"那位漁夫曬黑的臉顯示他一生大部分時間都在烈日下的戶外工作。"},{"w":"get a tan","p":"v.phr.","d":"to make your skin brown by staying in the sun","c":"曬黑；曬成古銅色","s":"Many tourists lie on the sand for hours just to get a tan, but doctors warn that too much sun can harm the skin.","t":"許多觀光客躺在沙灘上好幾個小時只為了曬黑，但醫生警告太多陽光會傷害皮膚。"},{"w":"tedious","p":"adj.","d":"boring and lasting too long","c":"乏味的；冗長無趣的","s":"Typing all three hundred names into the computer by hand was a tedious job, so we took turns to stay awake.","t":"把三百個名字一個一個打進電腦是件乏味的工作，所以我們輪流做，才不會睡著。","h":1},{"w":"tediously","p":"adv.","d":"in a boring way that lasts too long","c":"乏味地；冗長地","s":"The speaker went on tediously for over an hour, and half of the audience were checking their phones by the end.","t":"講者冗長乏味地講了超過一個小時，到最後有一半的聽眾都在看手機。"},{"w":"tedium","p":"n.","d":"the state of being boring and too long","c":"乏味；單調","s":"To break the tedium of the long train ride, we played card games and shared snacks with the family next to us.","t":"為了打破長途火車旅程的單調乏味，我們玩紙牌遊戲，還和旁邊的一家人分享零食。"},{"w":"telecommunications","p":"n.","d":"the sending of messages over long distances by phone, radio, or the Internet","c":"電信","s":"My uncle works for a telecommunications company, so he knows a lot about mobile networks and how phone signals travel.","t":"我叔叔在一家電信公司工作，所以他很了解行動網路以及電話訊號是如何傳送的。","h":1},{"w":"telecommute","p":"v.","d":"to work from home using a computer and the Internet","c":"遠距上班","s":"Since the company allows employees to telecommute two days a week, Dad now saves nearly three hours of driving.","t":"自從公司允許員工每週遠距上班兩天，爸爸現在省下了將近三小時的開車時間。"},{"w":"telegram","p":"n.","d":"a short message sent by electric signals in the past","c":"電報","s":"Before telephones were common, people sent a telegram when they needed to share urgent news with family far away.","t":"在電話普及之前，人們需要跟遠方的家人分享緊急消息時會發電報。"},{"w":"communication","p":"n.","d":"the act of sharing information or talking with people","c":"溝通；通訊","s":"Good communication between parents and teachers helps children do better at school, so our school holds a meeting every month.","t":"父母和老師之間良好的溝通有助於孩子在學校表現更好，所以我們學校每個月都舉行一次會議。"},{"w":"teller","p":"n.","d":"a person who works in a bank and takes or gives out money","c":"銀行出納員","s":"The bank teller counted the money twice and then handed me a receipt with a friendly smile before I left.","t":"銀行出納員把錢數了兩遍，然後帶著親切的微笑把收據交給我，我才離開。","h":1},{"w":"tell, told, told","p":"v.","d":"to say something to someone; to know the difference","c":"告訴；分辨","s":"Can you tell the difference between the two twins, or do they look exactly the same to you after all these years?","t":"你能分辨這對雙胞胎的不同嗎？還是過了這麼多年他們在你眼裡看起來還是一模一樣？","a":"tell"},{"w":"fortune-teller","p":"n.","d":"a person who says what will happen to you in the future","c":"算命師","s":"The old fortune-teller at the night market looked at my palm and said that I would travel to a faraway country next year.","t":"夜市裡那位年老的算命師看了我的手掌，說我明年會到一個遙遠的國家旅行。"},{"w":"storyteller","p":"n.","d":"a person who tells stories well","c":"說故事的人","s":"Grandpa is a wonderful storyteller, and every night we beg him to tell us one more story before we go to bed.","t":"爺爺是個很棒的說故事的人，每天晚上我們都求他在睡前再講一個故事。"},{"w":"tempo","p":"n.","d":"the speed of a piece of music or of an activity","c":"速度；節奏","s":"The conductor asked the band to play the song at a faster tempo because the audience wanted to dance to it.","t":"指揮要樂隊用更快的速度演奏這首歌，因為觀眾想跟著跳舞。","h":1},{"w":"pick up the tempo","p":"v.phr.","d":"to start doing something faster","c":"加快速度／節奏","s":"In the second half of the game, our team began to pick up the tempo and scored three goals in only ten minutes.","t":"比賽下半場，我們的球隊開始加快節奏，在短短十分鐘內就進了三球。"},{"w":"temporary","p":"adj.","d":"lasting only for a short time","c":"暫時的；臨時的","s":"This is only a temporary job for the summer, so I will have to look for something else when school starts in September.","t":"這只是暑假的臨時工作，所以九月開學時我得再找別的工作。"},{"w":"temporarily","p":"adv.","d":"for a short time only","c":"暫時地","s":"The road near our school is temporarily closed for repairs, so the school bus has to take a longer way this week.","t":"我們學校附近的道路因為修路暫時封閉，所以這週校車得繞比較遠的路。"},{"w":"tenant","p":"n.","d":"a person who pays money to live in a house or use land","c":"房客；租戶","s":"The tenant on the third floor always pays his rent on time, so the landlord is happy to let him stay another year.","t":"三樓的房客總是準時付房租，所以房東很樂意讓他再住一年。","h":1},{"w":"landlord","p":"n.","d":"a person who owns a house or room and rents it to others","c":"房東","s":"When the air conditioner stopped working in July, we called our landlord and he sent a repairman the very next day.","t":"七月冷氣壞掉時，我們打電話給房東，他第二天就派了修理人員過來。"},{"w":"tenancy","p":"n.","d":"the right to live in a place that you rent; the period of renting","c":"租賃；租期","s":"Our tenancy agreement ends in March, so we need to decide soon whether we want to renew it or move out.","t":"我們的租賃合約三月到期，所以我們得趕快決定要續約還是搬走。"},{"w":"rent","p":"v.","d":"to pay money to live in or use something that belongs to someone else","c":"租用；租","s":"Students who cannot afford to rent an apartment near the university often share a room with two or three friends.","t":"付不起大學附近公寓租金的學生，常常和兩三個朋友合住一間房。"},{"w":"tentative","p":"adj.","d":"not certain or fixed; may be changed later","c":"暫定的；試驗性的","s":"We have made a tentative plan to visit Japan in April, but we will not buy the tickets until everyone confirms.","t":"我們已經暫定四月去日本的計畫，但要等到大家都確認才會買票。","h":1},{"w":"tentatively","p":"adv.","d":"in a way that is not certain or fixed yet","c":"暫定地；試探地","s":"The meeting has been tentatively scheduled for next Friday, so please keep that afternoon free until we send the final notice.","t":"會議暫定在下週五舉行，所以在我們發出正式通知之前，請先空下那個下午。"},{"w":"tentative","p":"adj.","d":"shy and not confident","c":"猶豫的；不確定的","s":"The shy boy gave a tentative smile when the teacher praised his drawing in front of the whole class.","t":"當老師在全班面前稱讚他的畫時，那個害羞的男孩露出了一個遲疑的微笑。"},{"w":"terrace","p":"n.","d":"a flat outdoor area next to a building where people sit","c":"露臺；陽台","s":"We had breakfast on the hotel terrace every morning, enjoying the view of the sea and the fresh ocean air.","t":"我們每天早上都在飯店的露臺吃早餐，欣賞海景並享受新鮮的海風。","h":1},{"w":"terrace","p":"n.","d":"one of several flat steps cut into a hill for farming","c":"梯田","s":"In the mountains of northern Taiwan, farmers built terraces on the steep hills so that they could grow rice and tea.","t":"在北台灣的山區，農民在陡峭的山坡上修築梯田，這樣才能種稻和茶。","a":"terraces"},{"w":"terraced","p":"adj.","d":"built in flat steps on a hill","c":"梯田式的；成階梯狀的","s":"The terraced fields looked like giant green steps climbing up the mountain, and tourists stopped to take photos.","t":"那些梯田式的田地看起來像爬上山的巨大綠色階梯，觀光客都停下來拍照。"},{"w":"terrace","p":"v.","d":"to cut flat steps into a hill","c":"使成梯田；築成階梯","s":"To stop the soil from washing away, the villagers decided to terrace the hillside before planting the new trees.","t":"為了防止土壤被沖走，村民們決定在種新樹之前先把山坡築成梯田。"},{"w":"textile","p":"n.","d":"cloth made by weaving or knitting; the business of making cloth","c":"紡織品；紡織業","s":"Taiwan was once famous for its textile industry, and many factories made cloth that was sold all around the world.","t":"台灣曾經以紡織業聞名，許多工廠生產的布料銷售到世界各地。","h":1},{"w":"textiles","p":"n.","d":"cloth products such as fabric, carpets, and clothes","c":"紡織品","s":"The museum has a large collection of traditional textiles made by indigenous people more than a hundred years ago.","t":"這座博物館收藏了大量原住民一百多年前製作的傳統紡織品。"},{"w":"textile","p":"adj.","d":"connected with making cloth","c":"紡織的","s":"Many textile workers lost their jobs when the company moved its factory to another country where labor was cheaper.","t":"當公司把工廠搬到勞力比較便宜的國家時，許多紡織工人失去了工作。"},{"w":"texture","p":"n.","d":"the way something feels when you touch it","c":"質地；觸感","s":"I love the soft texture of this sweater, but the bright pink color is not really my style at all.","t":"我很喜歡這件毛衣柔軟的質地，但亮粉紅色實在不是我的風格。"},{"w":"thereafter","p":"adv.","d":"after that time","c":"此後；之後","s":"He won his first chess tournament at the age of ten, and thereafter he practiced every day to become a champion.","t":"他十歲時贏得第一次西洋棋比賽，此後他每天練習，想要成為冠軍。","h":1},{"w":"shortly thereafter","p":"phr.","d":"a short time after that","c":"不久之後","s":"The company opened its first store in Taipei in 2010, and shortly thereafter it opened five more in other cities.","t":"這家公司 2010 年在台北開了第一家店，不久之後又在其他城市開了五家。"},{"w":"thereby","p":"adv.","d":"by doing that; in that way","c":"藉此；因此","s":"She took a part-time job during the summer, thereby earning enough money to pay for her own trip to Korea.","t":"她暑假找了一份打工，藉此賺到足夠的錢自己付去韓國旅行的費用。"},{"w":"therefore","p":"adv.","d":"for that reason; so","c":"因此；所以","s":"It rained heavily all night, and therefore the baseball game was moved to the following Saturday afternoon.","t":"整夜下著大雨，因此棒球比賽被改到下個星期六下午。"},{"w":"thermometer","p":"n.","d":"a tool used to measure how hot or cold something is","c":"溫度計；體溫計","s":"The nurse put a thermometer under my arm and told me that my temperature was a little higher than normal.","t":"護士把體溫計放在我的腋下，告訴我我的體溫比正常高了一點。","h":1},{"w":"thermos","p":"n.","d":"a bottle that keeps drinks hot or cold","c":"保溫瓶","s":"Mom always fills a thermos with hot tea for Dad before he leaves for his early morning shift at the factory.","t":"爸爸去工廠上早班之前，媽媽總是會在保溫瓶裡裝滿熱茶給他。"},{"w":"thermal","p":"adj.","d":"connected with heat; keeping you warm","c":"熱的；保暖的","s":"You should pack some thermal underwear for the trip to Hokkaido because the temperature can drop below zero at night.","t":"去北海道旅行你應該帶一些保暖內衣，因為晚上溫度可能降到零下。"},{"w":"temperature","p":"n.","d":"how hot or cold something is","c":"溫度；體溫","s":"The temperature in Taipei can reach thirty-six degrees in July, so remember to drink plenty of water when you go outside.","t":"七月台北的溫度可能高達三十六度，所以出門時記得多喝水。"},{"w":"tilt","p":"v.","d":"to move so that one side is higher than the other","c":"使傾斜；傾斜","s":"If you tilt your head a little to the left, you will be able to see the painting without the light shining on it.","t":"如果你把頭稍微向左傾斜，就能看到那幅畫而不會被燈光反射。","h":1},{"w":"tilt","p":"n.","d":"a position in which one side is higher than the other","c":"傾斜；斜度","s":"The old tower has a slight tilt, and engineers check it every year to make sure it is still safe for visitors.","t":"這座古塔有輕微的傾斜，工程師每年都會檢查，確保它對遊客仍然安全。"},{"w":"tilted","p":"adj.","d":"not straight; leaning to one side","c":"傾斜的；歪的","s":"The picture frame on the wall looked tilted after the earthquake, so I straightened it before the guests arrived.","t":"地震後牆上的相框看起來歪歪的，所以我在客人到之前把它扶正。"},{"w":"tiptoe","p":"v.","d":"to walk quietly on your toes","c":"踮著腳走","s":"I had to tiptoe past my parents' bedroom at midnight because I did not want them to know how late I came home.","t":"午夜時我必須踮著腳經過父母的房間，因為我不想讓他們知道我回家多晚。","h":1},{"w":"on tiptoe","p":"phr.","d":"standing on your toes to be taller or quieter","c":"踮著腳尖","s":"The little girl stood on tiptoe so that she could see the chocolate cakes on the top shelf of the bakery.","t":"小女孩踮著腳尖站著，這樣她才能看到麵包店最上層架子上的巧克力蛋糕。"},{"w":"tiptoe around","p":"v.phr.","d":"to avoid talking about a difficult subject directly","c":"小心迴避（敏感話題）","s":"Everyone in the office tends to tiptoe around the topic of the boss's divorce because nobody wants to upset her.","t":"辦公室裡每個人都傾向小心迴避老闆離婚的話題，因為沒有人想讓她難過。"},{"w":"tiresome","p":"adj.","d":"making you feel bored or annoyed","c":"令人厭煩的；討厭的","s":"It is tiresome to hear my brother complain about his homework every single night when he could simply start doing it.","t":"每天晚上聽我哥哥抱怨功課真令人厭煩，他明明可以直接開始寫。","h":1},{"w":"tire","p":"v.","d":"to make someone feel that they need to rest; to become bored with","c":"使疲倦；厭倦","s":"The long hike began to tire the younger children, so we stopped by the stream for a rest and some snacks.","t":"長途健行開始讓年紀較小的孩子們疲倦，所以我們在溪邊停下來休息並吃點零食。"},{"w":"tired of","p":"adj.phr.","d":"bored with something because it has happened too many times","c":"厭倦…的","s":"I am tired of eating the same lunch box every day, so tomorrow I want to try the new noodle shop near school.","t":"我厭倦了每天吃一樣的便當，所以明天我想試試學校附近新開的麵店。"},{"w":"tiring","p":"adj.","d":"making you feel very tired","c":"累人的","s":"Working at the night market from six in the evening until two in the morning is very tiring, but the pay is good.","t":"在夜市從晚上六點工作到凌晨兩點非常累人，但薪水不錯。"},{"w":"tireless","p":"adj.","d":"working very hard for a long time without stopping","c":"不倦的；孜孜不倦的","s":"The tireless volunteers worked for twenty hours without a break to help the families who lost their homes in the flood.","t":"不倦的志工們連續工作二十小時沒有休息，幫助在水災中失去家園的家庭。"},{"w":"token","p":"n.","d":"a round piece of metal or plastic used instead of money","c":"代幣","s":"You need to buy a token at the counter before you can use the washing machines in this laundry shop.","t":"你必須先在櫃檯買一個代幣，才能使用這家洗衣店的洗衣機。","h":1},{"w":"as a token of","p":"phr.","d":"as a sign or symbol of a feeling","c":"作為…的象徵／表示","s":"Please accept this small gift as a token of my thanks for all the help you gave me during my first year here.","t":"請收下這個小禮物，作為我對你在我來這裡第一年給我所有幫助的感謝表示。"},{"w":"by the same token","p":"phr.","d":"in the same way; for the same reason","c":"同樣地","s":"You expect your friends to listen to you, and by the same token, you should listen carefully when they want to talk.","t":"你希望朋友聽你說話，同樣地，當他們想說話時你也應該仔細聽。"},{"w":"token","p":"adj.","d":"done only as a small sign, not seriously","c":"象徵性的","s":"The company made only a token effort to reduce pollution, so the local people were still very angry about the dirty river.","t":"這家公司只做了象徵性的努力來減少污染，所以當地人對髒污的河流仍然非常生氣。"},{"w":"tornado","p":"n.","d":"a violent storm with strong winds that spin in a circle","c":"龍捲風","s":"The tornado tore the roofs off dozens of houses in less than five minutes, but luckily nobody in the town was killed.","t":"龍捲風在不到五分鐘內掀掉了幾十棟房子的屋頂，但幸運的是鎮上沒有人喪命。","h":1},{"w":"tornado warning","p":"n.phr.","d":"an official message that a tornado is coming","c":"龍捲風警報","s":"When the tornado warning appeared on TV, the whole family rushed down to the basement and waited there for an hour.","t":"當龍捲風警報出現在電視上時，全家人趕緊跑到地下室，在那裡等了一個小時。"},{"w":"typhoon","p":"n.","d":"a very strong tropical storm in the western Pacific","c":"颱風","s":"Schools and offices in Taipei were closed on Tuesday because a strong typhoon was expected to hit the island that afternoon.","t":"台北的學校和公司星期二停班停課，因為預計那天下午會有一個強烈颱風襲擊台灣。"},{"w":"hurricane","p":"n.","d":"a very strong tropical storm in the Atlantic Ocean","c":"颶風","s":"The hurricane that hit Florida last September caused heavy flooding, and thousands of people had to leave their homes.","t":"去年九月襲擊佛羅里達的颶風造成嚴重水災，成千上萬的人不得不離開家園。"},{"w":"torrent","p":"n.","d":"a large amount of water moving very fast","c":"激流；洪流","s":"After three days of heavy rain, the quiet mountain stream turned into a dangerous torrent that swept away the small bridge.","t":"連下三天大雨後，平靜的山間小溪變成了危險的激流，沖走了那座小橋。","h":1},{"w":"a torrent of","p":"n.phr.","d":"a large amount of something, such as words or questions","c":"一連串的…；大量的…","s":"The singer received a torrent of criticism online after she forgot the words of the national anthem at the game.","t":"那位歌手在球賽上忘了國歌歌詞之後，在網路上受到一連串的批評。"},{"w":"torrential","p":"adj.","d":"falling very heavily (rain)","c":"傾盆的；滂沱的","s":"The torrential rain lasted all night, and by morning several roads in the city were under half a meter of water.","t":"傾盆大雨下了整夜，到早上時市區好幾條路都淹在半公尺深的水下。"},{"w":"trademark","p":"n.","d":"a name or sign that only one company is allowed to use","c":"商標","s":"The company took the small shop to court because it had used a logo that looked almost the same as its famous trademark.","t":"這家公司把那間小店告上法院，因為小店使用的標誌和公司著名的商標幾乎一模一樣。","h":1},{"w":"trademark","p":"n.","d":"something special that a person is known for","c":"標誌性特徵；招牌","s":"Wearing a red cap on stage has become the singer's trademark, and his fans now wear red caps to every concert.","t":"在舞台上戴紅帽子已經成了這位歌手的招牌特徵，他的粉絲現在每場演唱會都戴紅帽子。"},{"w":"trade","p":"n.","d":"the buying and selling of goods between people or countries","c":"貿易","s":"Taiwan depends heavily on international trade, so changes in the world economy can quickly affect local businesses.","t":"台灣高度依賴國際貿易，所以世界經濟的變化會很快影響本地企業。"},{"w":"brand","p":"n.","d":"a product made by a particular company under a particular name","c":"品牌","s":"Many teenagers prefer to buy a famous brand of sneakers even though cheaper ones are often just as comfortable.","t":"許多青少年偏好買名牌品牌的運動鞋，即使比較便宜的鞋常常一樣舒服。"},{"w":"transcript","p":"n.","d":"an official record of a student's grades","c":"成績單","s":"To apply for the university in Canada, you need to send an official transcript that shows your grades from all three years of high school.","t":"要申請加拿大那所大學，你必須寄一份正式的成績單，上面要有高中三年的所有成績。","h":1},{"w":"transcript","p":"n.","d":"a written copy of words that were spoken","c":"逐字稿；文字記錄","s":"The reporter read the full transcript of the interview carefully to make sure she quoted the minister's words correctly.","t":"記者仔細閱讀整篇訪談的逐字稿，確保她正確引用了部長的話。"},{"w":"transcribe","p":"v.","d":"to write down exactly what someone said","c":"抄寫；轉錄成文字","s":"My job at the law office was to transcribe the recordings of long meetings, which took about three hours each day.","t":"我在法律事務所的工作是把長時間會議的錄音轉錄成文字，每天大約要花三小時。"},{"w":"transcription","p":"n.","d":"the act of writing down spoken words; the written copy","c":"轉錄；抄本","s":"The transcription of the old letters took the students a whole month because the handwriting was very hard to read.","t":"學生們花了整整一個月才完成那些舊信件的轉錄，因為字跡非常難以辨認。"},{"w":"transmit","p":"v.","d":"to send a signal, message, or disease from one place or person to another","c":"傳送；傳播；傳染","s":"Mosquitoes can transmit serious diseases such as dengue fever, so you should remove any standing water around your house.","t":"蚊子會傳播像登革熱這樣的嚴重疾病，所以你應該清除家裡周圍的積水。","h":1},{"w":"transmission","p":"n.","d":"the act of sending a signal or passing on a disease","c":"傳送；傳播；傳染","s":"Washing your hands often is one of the easiest ways to prevent the transmission of the flu virus during the winter.","t":"常洗手是冬天預防流感病毒傳播最簡單的方法之一。"},{"w":"transmitter","p":"n.","d":"a piece of equipment that sends out radio or TV signals","c":"發射器；發射台","s":"The radio station built a new transmitter on the mountain so that people in the valley could receive a clearer signal.","t":"廣播電台在山上建了一座新的發射台，讓山谷裡的人能收到更清楚的訊號。"}]},{"unit":38,"theme":"transplant – upwardupwards","cards":[{"w":"transplant","p":"v.","d":"to move an organ from one body into another; to move a plant to a new place","c":"移植","s":"Doctors were able to transplant a new kidney into the young patient, and she went home healthy only two weeks later.","t":"醫生成功地把一顆新的腎臟移植到那位年輕病人體內，兩週後她就健康地回家了。","h":1},{"w":"transplant","p":"n.","d":"an operation that moves an organ into another person's body","c":"移植手術","s":"After waiting three years for a heart transplant, Mr. Chen finally received the call from the hospital late last night.","t":"等了三年的心臟移植手術之後，陳先生昨天深夜終於接到了醫院的電話。"},{"w":"transplant","p":"v.","d":"to dig up a plant and put it in a new place","c":"移植（植物）","s":"It is best to transplant young tomato plants into the garden in the evening so the hot sun does not damage their roots.","t":"最好在傍晚把小番茄苗移植到花園裡，這樣烈日才不會傷到它們的根。"},{"w":"organ transplant","p":"n.phr.","d":"an operation to put a healthy organ into a sick person's body","c":"器官移植","s":"Thanks to organ transplant technology, thousands of patients with failing hearts or livers are given a second chance at life every year.","t":"多虧了器官移植技術，每年有成千上萬心臟或肝臟衰竭的病人獲得第二次生命的機會。"},{"w":"plant","p":"v.","d":"to put seeds or young plants into the ground to grow","c":"種植","s":"Every spring our class helps to plant trees on the hill behind the school, and some of them are now taller than we are.","t":"每年春天我們班都幫忙在學校後面的山坡上種樹，其中有些現在已經比我們還高了。"},{"w":"treasury","p":"n.","d":"the money that a government or organization has; the government department that controls it","c":"國庫；財政部","s":"The government's treasury was almost empty after the long war, so the king raised the taxes on salt and tea.","t":"漫長的戰爭之後，政府的國庫幾乎空了，所以國王提高了鹽和茶的稅。","h":1},{"w":"treasure","p":"n.","d":"gold, jewels, and other valuable things","c":"寶藏；財寶","s":"The children spent the whole afternoon digging in the sand because they believed a pirate's treasure was buried somewhere on the beach.","t":"孩子們整個下午都在沙裡挖，因為他們相信海盜的寶藏就埋在海灘的某個地方。"},{"w":"treasure","p":"v.","d":"to keep something carefully because it is very important to you","c":"珍藏；珍惜","s":"I will always treasure the letter my grandmother wrote me before she died, even though the paper is now yellow and torn.","t":"我會永遠珍藏奶奶過世前寫給我的那封信，即使紙已經泛黃破損了。"},{"w":"treasurer","p":"n.","d":"the person who looks after the money of a club or organization","c":"財務；出納","s":"As the treasurer of the student club, Amy keeps a careful record of every dollar that comes in and goes out.","t":"身為學生社團的財務，艾咪仔細記錄每一塊錢的收入和支出。"},{"w":"trek","p":"n.","d":"a long, difficult walk, usually in the mountains or countryside","c":"長途跋涉；徒步旅行","s":"The trek to the mountain village took us two full days, and we slept in a small tent beside the river.","t":"到山村的長途跋涉花了我們整整兩天，我們在河邊的小帳篷裡過夜。","h":1},{"w":"trek","p":"v.","d":"to make a long, difficult walk","c":"跋涉；徒步旅行","s":"Every year thousands of tourists trek through the Himalayas to see the sunrise over the highest peaks in the world.","t":"每年有成千上萬的觀光客徒步跋涉穿越喜馬拉雅山，去看世界最高峰上的日出。"},{"w":"trekking","p":"n.","d":"the activity of walking long distances in wild places for pleasure","c":"徒步旅行；健行","s":"My brother loves trekking, so he spent his whole summer vacation walking through the mountains of Nepal with a heavy backpack.","t":"我哥哥熱愛徒步旅行，所以他整個暑假都背著沉重的背包走在尼泊爾的山區裡。"},{"w":"trifle","p":"n.","d":"something that is not important","c":"瑣事；小事","s":"Do not argue with your sister over such a trifle as who sits in the front seat, because it is really not worth it.","t":"別為了誰坐前座這種小事跟你妹妹吵架，真的不值得。","h":1},{"w":"a trifle","p":"phr.","d":"a little; slightly","c":"有點；稍微","s":"Grandpa was a trifle annoyed when the restaurant forgot his order, but he smiled again as soon as the soup arrived.","t":"餐廳忘了爺爺的餐點時，他有點不高興，但湯一送來他就又笑了。"},{"w":"trifle with","p":"v.phr.","d":"to treat someone or something without the respect they deserve","c":"輕視；玩弄","s":"The coach warned the players not to trifle with the new rules, because anyone who broke them would be sent off the field.","t":"教練警告球員不要輕視新規則，因為任何違規的人都會被趕出球場。"},{"w":"trifling","p":"adj.","d":"small and not important","c":"微不足道的","s":"The repair cost was a trifling amount compared to the price of a new phone, so I decided to fix the old one.","t":"和新手機的價格比起來，修理費只是微不足道的數目，所以我決定修舊手機。"},{"w":"trillion","p":"n.","d":"the number 1,000,000,000,000","c":"兆","s":"The government plans to spend more than one trillion dollars on new roads and railways over the next ten years.","t":"政府計畫在未來十年投入超過一兆元興建新的道路和鐵路。","h":1},{"w":"trillions of","p":"n.phr.","d":"a very large number of something","c":"數以兆計的；無數的","s":"There are trillions of stars in the universe, so many scientists believe that life must exist somewhere beyond our planet.","t":"宇宙中有數以兆計的星星，所以許多科學家相信地球以外的某處一定存在生命。"},{"w":"billion","p":"n.","d":"the number 1,000,000,000","c":"十億","s":"The population of the world passed eight billion in 2022, and it is still growing by about seventy million people every year.","t":"世界人口在 2022 年超過八十億（八十億），而且每年仍以大約七千萬人的速度增加。"},{"w":"million","p":"n.","d":"the number 1,000,000","c":"百萬","s":"Taipei has a population of about two and a half million, and it feels even more crowded during the morning rush hour.","t":"台北的人口大約是兩百五十萬（兩個半百萬），在早上的尖峰時段感覺更加擁擠。"},{"w":"tropic","p":"n.","d":"one of the two imaginary lines around the earth north and south of the equator","c":"回歸線","s":"Taiwan is crossed by the Tropic of Cancer, and there is a large monument in Chiayi that marks the exact line.","t":"北回歸線穿過台灣，嘉義有一座大型紀念碑標示出確切的位置。","a":"Tropic","h":1},{"w":"the tropics","p":"n.","d":"the hottest part of the earth, near the equator","c":"熱帶地區","s":"Fruits like mangoes and bananas grow best in the tropics, where it is hot and wet all through the year.","t":"芒果和香蕉這類水果在熱帶地區長得最好，那裡一年到頭都又熱又潮濕。"},{"w":"tropical","p":"adj.","d":"coming from or found in the hottest parts of the world","c":"熱帶的","s":"Southern Taiwan has a tropical climate, so even in December you can still wear a T-shirt during the day.","t":"南台灣是熱帶氣候，所以即使在十二月，白天你還是可以穿短袖。"},{"w":"tropical rainforest","p":"n.phr.","d":"a thick forest in a hot, wet part of the world","c":"熱帶雨林","s":"Thousands of plants and animals live only in the tropical rainforest, and many of them have never been studied by scientists.","t":"成千上萬種動植物只生活在熱帶雨林裡，其中許多從未被科學家研究過。"},{"w":"trout","p":"n.","d":"a fish that lives in rivers and lakes and is good to eat","c":"鱒魚","s":"My father caught two large trout in the mountain stream, and we cooked them over the campfire for dinner that evening.","t":"我爸爸在山間小溪裡釣到兩條大鱒魚，那天晚上我們在營火上烤來當晚餐。","h":1},{"w":"salmon","p":"n.","d":"a large fish with pink meat that swims up rivers to lay eggs","c":"鮭魚","s":"Doctors say that eating salmon twice a week is good for your heart because it contains healthy oils.","t":"醫生說一週吃兩次鮭魚對心臟很好，因為它含有健康的油脂。"},{"w":"tuna","p":"n.","d":"a large sea fish that is often sold in cans","c":"鮪魚","s":"I made a quick sandwich with a can of tuna, some lettuce, and a little mayonnaise before I rushed to school.","t":"趕去學校前，我用一罐鮪魚、一些生菜和一點美乃滋快速做了一個三明治。"},{"w":"trustee","p":"n.","d":"a person who controls money or property for the benefit of others","c":"受託人；董事","s":"The university's board of trustees meets four times a year to decide how the school's money should be spent.","t":"這所大學的董事會每年開會四次，決定學校的經費該如何運用。","a":"trustees","h":1},{"w":"trust","p":"v.","d":"to believe that someone is honest and will not harm you","c":"信任","s":"You can trust Jack with your house keys because he has never let any of his friends down in all these years.","t":"你可以放心把家裡的鑰匙交給傑克，信任他，因為這麼多年來他從沒讓任何朋友失望。"},{"w":"trust","p":"n.","d":"the belief that someone is honest and will not harm you","c":"信任","s":"It takes years to build trust between a teacher and her students, but only one broken promise to destroy it.","t":"老師和學生之間的信任需要多年才能建立，但只要一次失信就能毀掉它。"},{"w":"trustworthy","p":"adj.","d":"able to be trusted; honest and reliable","c":"值得信賴的","s":"The company is looking for a trustworthy accountant who can handle large amounts of money without being watched all the time.","t":"這家公司正在尋找一位值得信賴的會計，能在無人時時監督的情況下處理大筆金錢。"},{"w":"tuck","p":"v.","d":"to push the edge of something into a place so that it is neat or safe","c":"塞進；塞好","s":"Please tuck your shirt into your pants before the ceremony begins, because the principal wants everyone to look neat.","t":"典禮開始前請把襯衫塞進褲子裡，因為校長希望每個人看起來都整齊。","h":1},{"w":"tuck in","p":"v.phr.","d":"to make a child comfortable in bed by pulling the covers around them","c":"替…蓋好被子","s":"Every night Dad comes upstairs to tuck in the twins and read them one short story before he turns off the light.","t":"每天晚上爸爸都會上樓替雙胞胎蓋好被子，關燈前再唸一個小故事給他們聽。"},{"w":"tuck away","p":"v.phr.","d":"to put something in a safe or hidden place","c":"藏起來；收好","s":"Grandma likes to tuck away a little money in an old tea box every month so that she can buy gifts for us at New Year.","t":"奶奶喜歡每個月在舊茶葉罐裡藏一點錢，這樣她過年時就能買禮物給我們。"},{"w":"turmoil","p":"n.","d":"a state of great confusion, worry, or disorder","c":"混亂；動盪","s":"The country was in turmoil after the president suddenly resigned, and nobody knew who would lead the government next.","t":"總統突然辭職後，國家陷入動盪，沒有人知道接下來誰會領導政府。","h":1},{"w":"in turmoil","p":"phr.","d":"in a state of confusion and worry","c":"處於混亂之中","s":"My mind was in turmoil the night before the big exam, so I could not fall asleep until almost three in the morning.","t":"大考前一晚我的腦子一片混亂，所以我到將近凌晨三點才睡著。"},{"w":"chaos","p":"n.","d":"a state of complete disorder","c":"混亂","s":"The sudden power cut caused chaos in the shopping mall, with people shouting and pushing in the dark to find the exits.","t":"突然停電讓購物中心陷入混亂，人們在黑暗中大喊推擠，想找到出口。"},{"w":"twilight","p":"n.","d":"the soft light just after the sun goes down","c":"暮色；黃昏","s":"We walked along the beach at twilight, when the sky turned purple and the first stars began to appear.","t":"我們在黃昏時沿著海灘散步，那時天空變成紫色，第一批星星開始出現。","h":1},{"w":"twilight","p":"n.","d":"the last period of something, such as a life or career","c":"晚期；衰落期","s":"In the twilight of his career, the old actor chose only small roles in films made by his young friends.","t":"在演藝生涯的晚期，這位老演員只接年輕朋友拍的電影裡的小角色。"},{"w":"dusk","p":"n.","d":"the time in the evening when it starts to get dark","c":"黃昏；傍晚","s":"The street lights come on automatically at dusk, so the park is never completely dark when people walk their dogs.","t":"路燈在黃昏時會自動亮起，所以人們遛狗時公園從來不會完全黑暗。"},{"w":"dawn","p":"n.","d":"the time in the morning when light first appears","c":"黎明；破曉","s":"The farmers get up before dawn every morning to feed the chickens and milk the cows before breakfast.","t":"農夫們每天早上在黎明前起床，在早餐前餵雞和擠牛奶。"},{"w":"twinkle","p":"v.","d":"to shine with a light that goes on and off quickly","c":"閃爍；閃耀","s":"On a clear winter night, you can see thousands of stars twinkle above the mountains far from the city lights.","t":"在晴朗的冬夜，你可以看到成千上萬顆星星在遠離城市燈光的山上閃爍。","h":1},{"w":"twinkle","p":"n.","d":"a bright, happy look in someone's eyes","c":"閃光；神采","s":"There was a twinkle in Grandpa's eye when he told us he had hidden a surprise gift somewhere in the house.","t":"爺爺告訴我們他在家裡某處藏了一份驚喜禮物時，眼裡閃著光芒。"},{"w":"twinkling","p":"adj.","d":"shining with a light that goes on and off","c":"閃爍的","s":"The twinkling lights on the Christmas tree made the whole living room feel warm and magical on that cold evening.","t":"在那個寒冷的夜晚，聖誕樹上閃爍的燈光讓整個客廳感覺溫暖又神奇。"},{"w":"in the twinkling of an eye","p":"phr.","d":"very quickly; in a moment","c":"一瞬間；轉眼間","s":"The magician made the coin disappear in the twinkling of an eye, and nobody in the audience could explain how he did it.","t":"魔術師一瞬間就讓硬幣消失了，觀眾中沒有人能解釋他是怎麼做到的。"},{"w":"unanimous","p":"adj.","d":"agreed by everyone","c":"一致同意的；全體一致的","s":"The decision to hold the school fair in May was unanimous, since every single teacher voted for it at the meeting.","t":"五月舉辦園遊會的決定是全體一致的，因為會議上每一位老師都投了贊成票。","h":1},{"w":"unanimously","p":"adv.","d":"with everyone agreeing","c":"一致地；全體同意地","s":"The committee unanimously agreed to give the prize to the youngest writer, whose story had made all of them cry.","t":"委員會一致同意把獎頒給最年輕的作者，她的故事讓他們全都哭了。"},{"w":"unanimity","p":"n.","d":"complete agreement among all the people in a group","c":"全體一致","s":"There was complete unanimity among the players about choosing Peter as the new captain of the basketball team.","t":"關於選彼得當籃球隊的新隊長，球員們全體一致贊成。"},{"w":"unconditional","p":"adj.","d":"without any limits or conditions","c":"無條件的","s":"A mother's love for her child is unconditional, which means she keeps loving him no matter what mistakes he makes.","t":"母親對孩子的愛是無條件的，也就是說不管他犯了什麼錯，她都會一直愛他。","h":1},{"w":"unconditionally","p":"adv.","d":"without any conditions","c":"無條件地","s":"The soldiers were told to surrender unconditionally, so they put down their weapons and walked out of the fort with their hands up.","t":"士兵們被要求無條件投降，所以他們放下武器，舉著雙手走出堡壘。"},{"w":"conditional","p":"adj.","d":"depending on something else happening first","c":"有條件的；視…而定的","s":"His offer to pay for my trip was conditional on my passing the final exam, so I studied harder than ever before.","t":"他答應出錢讓我去旅行是有條件的，要看我期末考有沒有及格，所以我讀得比以前更用功。"},{"w":"condition","p":"n.","d":"something that must happen before something else can happen","c":"條件","s":"I will lend you my bike on one condition: you must bring it back before dinner without a single scratch.","t":"我可以借你腳踏車，但有一個條件：你必須在晚餐前還回來，而且不能有任何刮痕。"},{"w":"underestimate","p":"v.","d":"to think that something or someone is smaller, weaker, or less important than they really are","c":"低估","s":"Never underestimate your opponent in a chess game, because even a beginner can surprise you with a clever move.","t":"下棋時絕對不要低估你的對手，因為即使是初學者也可能用一步妙棋讓你吃驚。","h":1},{"w":"underestimate","p":"n.","d":"a guess that is lower than the real amount","c":"低估；過低的估計","s":"Saying that only a hundred people came to the concert is a serious underestimate, since every seat in the hall was taken.","t":"說只有一百人來聽演唱會是嚴重的低估，因為大廳裡每個位子都坐滿了。"},{"w":"overestimate","p":"v.","d":"to think that something is bigger or better than it really is","c":"高估","s":"Students often overestimate how much they can study in one night, and then they panic when the exam comes.","t":"學生常常高估自己一個晚上能讀多少書，然後考試來臨時就慌了。"},{"w":"estimate","p":"v.","d":"to guess the size, amount, or cost of something","c":"估計","s":"The mechanic could not estimate how much the repair would cost until he had looked inside the engine carefully.","t":"技師在仔細檢查引擎內部之前，無法估計修理要花多少錢。"},{"w":"underneath","p":"prep.","d":"under or below something","c":"在…下面","s":"The cat likes to hide underneath the bed whenever strangers come to the house, and she will not come out for hours.","t":"每當有陌生人來家裡，貓就喜歡躲在床下面，好幾個小時都不肯出來。","h":1},{"w":"underneath","p":"adv.","d":"under or below something that covers it","c":"在下面；在底下","s":"The old painting was covered with dust, but when I wiped it clean, the bright colors underneath looked brand new.","t":"那幅舊畫蓋滿了灰塵，但當我把它擦乾淨時，底下鮮豔的顏色看起來像全新的一樣。"},{"w":"underneath","p":"n.","d":"the bottom part of something","c":"底部；下面","s":"The underneath of the car was covered with mud after we drove along the dirt road to the farm.","t":"我們沿著泥土路開到農場之後，車子的底部沾滿了泥巴。"},{"w":"beneath","p":"prep.","d":"under something; in a lower position","c":"在…之下","s":"We sat beneath the big tree to escape the hot sun and ate our sandwiches while the children played nearby.","t":"我們坐在大樹下躲太陽，一邊吃三明治，孩子們則在附近玩耍。"},{"w":"underpass","p":"n.","d":"a road or path that goes under another road or a railway","c":"地下道","s":"It is safer to use the underpass to cross the busy road near the station than to run between the cars.","t":"要穿越車站附近繁忙的馬路，走地下道比在車陣中奔跑安全多了。","h":1},{"w":"overpass","p":"n.","d":"a bridge that carries a road or path over another road","c":"天橋；高架道路","s":"A new overpass was built over the highway so that students no longer have to wait for the traffic lights.","t":"高速公路上方蓋了一座新的天橋，學生們再也不用等紅綠燈了。"},{"w":"pass","p":"v.","d":"to go past something or someone","c":"經過；通過","s":"Several buses pass this stop every ten minutes, so you will not have to wait long to get to the museum.","t":"每十分鐘就有好幾班公車經過這一站，所以你不用等很久就能到博物館。"},{"w":"underway","p":"adj.","d":"already started and happening now","c":"進行中的","s":"Preparations for the school anniversary are already underway, and the students are practicing their dance every afternoon.","t":"校慶的準備工作已經在進行中，學生們每天下午都在練舞。","h":1},{"w":"get underway","p":"v.phr.","d":"to start","c":"開始；啟動","s":"The race will get underway at eight o'clock sharp, so all the runners must be at the starting line by seven thirty.","t":"比賽將在八點整開始，所以所有跑者必須在七點半前到達起跑線。"},{"w":"ongoing","p":"adj.","d":"continuing to happen; not finished","c":"持續進行的","s":"The police investigation into the fire is still ongoing, so the officers cannot tell reporters what caused it yet.","t":"警方對那場火災的調查仍在持續進行，所以警員還不能告訴記者起火原因。"},{"w":"unification","p":"n.","d":"the act of joining separate parts into one","c":"統一","s":"The unification of Germany in 1990 brought together two countries that had been separated for more than forty years.","t":"1990 年德國的統一讓分隔了四十多年的兩個國家重新合而為一。","h":1},{"w":"unify","p":"v.","d":"to join separate parts or people into one group","c":"統一；使團結","s":"The new leader promised to unify the country after years of fighting between the north and the south.","t":"新領導人承諾在南北多年的戰爭之後統一國家。","h":1},{"w":"unified","p":"adj.","d":"joined together as one","c":"統一的；一致的","s":"The company needs a unified plan so that its offices in Taipei, Tokyo, and Seoul all work toward the same goals.","t":"這家公司需要一個統一的計畫，讓台北、東京和首爾的辦公室都朝同樣的目標努力。"},{"w":"unity","p":"n.","d":"the state of being joined together or in agreement","c":"團結；統一","s":"The coach always says that unity is more important than talent, because a team that works together can beat anyone.","t":"教練總是說團結比天分更重要，因為一支合作無間的隊伍可以打敗任何人。"},{"w":"unveil","p":"v.","d":"to show a new product or plan to the public for the first time","c":"公開；發表","s":"The car company will unveil its first electric sports car at the Tokyo Motor Show next month, and fans are very excited.","t":"這家汽車公司下個月將在東京車展發表它的第一輛電動跑車，車迷們都非常興奮。","h":1},{"w":"unveil","p":"v.","d":"to remove the cover from a statue or painting in a ceremony","c":"為…揭幕","s":"The mayor will unveil the statue of the famous poet in the park on Saturday, and the public is invited to watch.","t":"市長星期六將在公園為那位著名詩人的雕像揭幕，歡迎民眾前往觀禮。"},{"w":"veil","p":"n.","d":"a thin piece of cloth that covers a woman's face or head","c":"面紗","s":"The bride wore a long white veil that covered her face until the moment her husband lifted it to kiss her.","t":"新娘戴著長長的白色面紗遮住臉，直到她丈夫掀起面紗親吻她的那一刻。"},{"w":"reveal","p":"v.","d":"to let people know something that was secret","c":"揭露；透露","s":"The magician refused to reveal the secret of his best trick, even when the children begged him to tell them.","t":"魔術師拒絕透露他最拿手魔術的祕密，即使孩子們求他說出來。"},{"w":"upright","p":"adj.","d":"straight up; not bent or lying down","c":"直立的；挺直的","s":"The doctor told me to sit in an upright position while I work, instead of leaning over my desk all day.","t":"醫生要我工作時保持挺直的坐姿，而不是整天趴在桌上。","h":1},{"w":"upright","p":"adv.","d":"in a straight position","c":"直立地；筆直地","s":"Please put your seat upright and fasten your seat belt, because the plane will be landing in about fifteen minutes.","t":"請把座椅豎直並繫好安全帶，因為飛機大約十五分鐘後就要降落了。"},{"w":"upright","p":"adj.","d":"honest and fair","c":"正直的","s":"Everyone in the village respected the judge because he was an upright man who never accepted money to change his decisions.","t":"村裡每個人都尊敬那位法官，因為他是個正直的人，從不收錢改變判決。"},{"w":"upright","p":"n.","d":"a piano in which the strings stand straight up","c":"直立式鋼琴","s":"My parents bought a second-hand upright for the living room because a grand piano would never fit in our small apartment.","t":"我父母買了一台二手直立式鋼琴放在客廳，因為平台鋼琴絕對放不進我們的小公寓。"},{"w":"uprising","p":"n.","d":"an act of fighting against the people in power","c":"起義；暴動","s":"The uprising began when the farmers refused to pay the new tax, and within a week the whole province had joined them.","t":"起義從農民拒絕繳納新稅開始，不到一週整個省的人都加入了他們。","h":1},{"w":"rise, rose, risen","p":"v.","d":"to go up; to increase; to stand up","c":"上升；上漲；起身","s":"The price of eggs has risen so much this year that many breakfast shops have had to raise the price of their sandwiches.","t":"今年雞蛋的價格上漲了很多，許多早餐店不得不調高三明治的價格。","a":"risen"},{"w":"rebellion","p":"n.","d":"an organized attempt to change the government by fighting","c":"叛亂；反抗","s":"The rebellion against the cruel king lasted for three years before the people finally won their freedom.","t":"對抗殘暴國王的叛亂持續了三年，人民才終於贏得自由。"},{"w":"upward","p":"adj.","d":"moving or pointing toward a higher place or level","c":"向上的；上升的","s":"The chart shows an upward trend in bicycle sales, which means more people are choosing to ride to work.","t":"圖表顯示腳踏車銷量呈上升趨勢，這表示越來越多人選擇騎車上班。","h":1},{"w":"upward","p":"adv.","d":"toward a higher place or level","c":"向上地","s":"The rocket climbed upward into the clear blue sky, and the crowd cheered as it disappeared from sight.","t":"火箭向上衝進晴朗的藍天，當它消失在視線中時，群眾歡呼起來。"},{"w":"upwards","p":"adv.","d":"toward a higher place (British spelling of upward)","c":"向上（＝upward）","s":"Hold the map the right way up and look upwards along the river until you find the small red bridge.","t":"把地圖拿正，沿著河往上看，直到你找到那座小紅橋。"},{"w":"upwards of","p":"phr.","d":"more than a certain number","c":"超過；多於","s":"The new stadium can hold upwards of fifty thousand fans, which makes it the largest sports ground in the country.","t":"新體育場可以容納超過五萬名球迷，是全國最大的運動場。"},{"w":"downward","p":"adj.","d":"moving or pointing toward a lower place or level","c":"向下的；下降的","s":"After the scandal, the company's sales went into a downward spiral, and it had to close ten stores within a year.","t":"醜聞之後，公司的銷售陷入下降的惡性循環，一年內不得不關閉十家店。"}]},{"unit":39,"theme":"urgency – virgin","cards":[{"w":"urgency","p":"n.","d":"the need to do something very quickly","c":"緊急；急迫","s":"The doctor spoke with such urgency on the phone that we drove Grandpa to the hospital right away without even changing our clothes.","t":"醫生在電話裡的語氣如此急迫，我們連衣服都沒換就立刻開車送爺爺去醫院。","h":1},{"w":"a sense of urgency","p":"n.phr.","d":"the feeling that something must be done quickly","c":"急迫感","s":"With only two days left before the deadline, the whole team finally began to work with a sense of urgency on the project.","t":"離截止日只剩兩天，整個團隊終於帶著急迫感投入這個專案。"},{"w":"urgent","p":"adj.","d":"needing to be dealt with immediately","c":"緊急的","s":"Please call me back as soon as you get this message, because it is urgent and cannot wait until tomorrow morning.","t":"收到這則訊息請盡快回電給我，因為這件事很緊急，不能等到明天早上。"},{"w":"urgently","p":"adv.","d":"in a way that needs immediate action","c":"緊急地；急切地","s":"The hospital urgently needs blood donors of all types after the bus accident on the highway this morning.","t":"今天早上高速公路發生巴士事故後，醫院緊急需要各種血型的捐血者。"},{"w":"urge","p":"v.","d":"to strongly advise someone to do something","c":"敦促；力勸","s":"Teachers urge students to get at least eight hours of sleep before the exam instead of studying all night.","t":"老師力勸學生考試前至少睡八小時，而不是熬夜讀書。"},{"w":"usher","p":"v.","d":"to lead someone politely to a place","c":"引領；帶領","s":"A young man in a black suit came to usher us to our seats a few minutes before the concert began.","t":"音樂會開始前幾分鐘，一位穿黑西裝的年輕人來引領我們到座位上。","h":1},{"w":"usher","p":"n.","d":"a person who shows people to their seats in a theater or church","c":"引座員；招待員","s":"The usher checked our tickets with a small flashlight and led us down the dark aisle to the front row.","t":"引座員用小手電筒查看我們的票，然後帶我們沿著黑暗的走道走到前排。"},{"w":"usher in","p":"v.phr.","d":"to be the start of something new","c":"迎來；開創","s":"Many people believe that the invention of the smartphone helped to usher in a new age of communication around the world.","t":"許多人認為智慧型手機的發明幫助全世界迎來了一個溝通的新時代。"},{"w":"utensil","p":"n.","d":"a tool used in the kitchen for cooking or eating","c":"用具；餐具；器皿","s":"Please wash every utensil you used for cooking tonight, including the big wooden spoon and the cutting board.","t":"請把你今晚煮飯用過的每一件用具都洗乾淨，包括那支大木湯匙和砧板。","h":1},{"w":"kitchen utensils","p":"n.phr.","d":"tools such as spoons, knives, and pans used for cooking","c":"廚房用具","s":"The new department store sells all kinds of kitchen utensils, from cheap plastic spoons to expensive knives made in Japan.","t":"新開的百貨公司販賣各種廚房用具，從便宜的塑膠湯匙到昂貴的日本製刀具都有。"},{"w":"tool","p":"n.","d":"something you hold in your hand and use to do a job","c":"工具","s":"A hammer is the only tool you need to hang this picture, so you do not have to borrow a drill from the neighbor.","t":"掛這幅畫你只需要一把鐵鎚這個工具，所以不必向鄰居借電鑽。"},{"w":"utter","p":"adj.","d":"complete; total (used to make a statement stronger)","c":"完全的；徹底的","s":"The party was an utter failure because the music was too loud, the food ran out, and half of the guests left early.","t":"這場派對是徹底的失敗，因為音樂太大聲、食物吃完了，一半的客人還提早離開。","h":1},{"w":"utter","p":"v.","d":"to say something or make a sound with your voice","c":"說出；發出（聲音）","s":"The shy boy did not utter a single word during the whole dinner, even when his aunt asked him about school.","t":"那個害羞的男孩整頓晚餐沒說一個字，即使阿姨問他學校的事也一樣。"},{"w":"utterly","p":"adv.","d":"completely","c":"完全地；徹底地","s":"I was utterly exhausted after running the ten-kilometer race, so I fell asleep on the bus before it left the park.","t":"跑完十公里賽跑後我完全累壞了，公車還沒開出公園我就在車上睡著了。"},{"w":"utterance","p":"n.","d":"something that someone says","c":"言語；話語","s":"The baby's first utterance sounded like \"mama,\" and my mother was so happy that she recorded it on her phone.","t":"寶寶發出的第一句話語聽起來像「媽媽」，我媽媽高興得用手機把它錄了下來。"},{"w":"vaccine","p":"n.","d":"a substance put into the body to protect it against a disease","c":"疫苗","s":"Every child in Taiwan receives a vaccine against measles before starting elementary school, so the disease is now very rare.","t":"台灣每個孩子上小學前都會接種麻疹疫苗，所以這種疾病現在非常少見。","h":1},{"w":"vaccinate","p":"v.","d":"to give someone a vaccine","c":"為…接種疫苗","s":"Vets advise pet owners to vaccinate their dogs against rabies every year, especially if the animals often go outside.","t":"獸醫建議飼主每年為狗接種狂犬病疫苗，尤其是常常外出的狗。"},{"w":"vaccination","p":"n.","d":"the act of giving someone a vaccine","c":"接種疫苗；預防注射","s":"The school nurse gave every student a vaccination card to keep a record of all the shots they had received.","t":"學校護士給每位學生一張預防注射卡，用來記錄他們打過的所有疫苗。"},{"w":"get vaccinated","p":"v.phr.","d":"to receive a vaccine","c":"接種疫苗","s":"My grandparents went to the clinic to get vaccinated against the flu last week, because older people get sick more easily in winter.","t":"我的祖父母上週去診所接種流感疫苗，因為老年人冬天比較容易生病。"},{"w":"vanilla","p":"n.","d":"a sweet flavor that comes from the seeds of a tropical plant","c":"香草","s":"The cake smelled wonderful because my mother added a few drops of vanilla to the mix before she put it in the oven.","t":"蛋糕聞起來很香，因為我媽媽在放進烤箱前加了幾滴香草精到麵糊裡。","h":1},{"w":"vanilla ice cream","p":"n.phr.","d":"ice cream with a vanilla flavor","c":"香草冰淇淋","s":"On hot summer afternoons, Grandpa always buys two cones of vanilla ice cream from the little shop near the park and shares one with me.","t":"炎熱的夏日午後，爺爺總是在公園附近的小店買兩支香草冰淇淋，分一支給我。"},{"w":"vanilla","p":"adj.","d":"ordinary and not special or exciting","c":"平淡無奇的；普通的","s":"The new phone works well but looks rather vanilla, so the company added bright colors to make it more exciting.","t":"新手機很好用，但外型相當平淡無奇，所以公司加上了鮮豔的顏色讓它更吸引人。"},{"w":"vanity","p":"n.","d":"too much pride in your own appearance or abilities","c":"虛榮；虛榮心","s":"Out of pure vanity, the actor refused to wear glasses in public even though he could hardly read the menu without them.","t":"純粹出於虛榮心，那位演員拒絕在公開場合戴眼鏡，儘管不戴眼鏡他幾乎看不清菜單。","h":1},{"w":"vain","p":"adj.","d":"too proud of your own appearance or abilities","c":"愛慕虛榮的；自負的","s":"She is so vain that she checks her hair in every shop window she passes on the way to school.","t":"她太愛慕虛榮了，上學路上經過每一面商店櫥窗都要照照自己的頭髮。"},{"w":"in vain","p":"phr.","d":"without success","c":"徒勞地；白費力氣","s":"The firefighters tried in vain to save the old temple, but the fire had already spread to the wooden roof.","t":"消防員徒勞地試圖搶救那座古廟，但火勢已經蔓延到木造屋頂了。"},{"w":"vain","p":"adj.","d":"not successful; useless","c":"徒勞的；無用的","s":"After several vain attempts to start the old car, Dad finally gave up and called a taxi to take us to the station.","t":"幾次徒勞的發動舊車的嘗試之後，爸爸終於放棄，叫了計程車送我們去車站。"},{"w":"vapor","p":"n.","d":"a gas made of very small drops of liquid in the air","c":"蒸氣；水汽","s":"When you boil water in a kettle, the hot vapor rising from the spout can burn your hand if you get too close.","t":"用水壺燒開水時，從壺嘴冒出的熱蒸氣如果靠太近會燙傷你的手。","h":1},{"w":"water vapor","p":"n.phr.","d":"water in the form of a gas","c":"水蒸氣","s":"Clouds form when water vapor in the air cools down and turns into tiny drops of water high above the ground.","t":"當空氣中的水蒸氣冷卻並在高空變成微小的水滴時，雲就形成了。"},{"w":"evaporate","p":"v.","d":"to change from a liquid into a gas","c":"蒸發","s":"The small puddles on the playground will evaporate within an hour once the sun comes out after the rain.","t":"雨後太陽一出來，操場上的小水窪一小時內就會蒸發。"},{"w":"evaporation","p":"n.","d":"the process of a liquid changing into a gas","c":"蒸發","s":"Farmers cover the soil with straw in summer to slow down evaporation so that the plants do not dry out too quickly.","t":"農夫夏天在土壤上鋪稻草來減緩蒸發，這樣植物才不會太快乾枯。"},{"w":"veil","p":"n.","d":"a thin piece of cloth that covers a woman's face or head","c":"面紗","s":"In some countries, women wear a veil over their faces when they go out, and only their eyes can be seen.","t":"在某些國家，女性外出時會戴面紗遮住臉，只看得到眼睛。","h":1},{"w":"veil","p":"v.","d":"to cover or hide something","c":"遮掩；掩飾","s":"The politician tried to veil his anger with a polite smile, but everyone in the room could see that he was upset.","t":"那位政治人物試圖用禮貌的微笑掩飾他的憤怒，但房間裡每個人都看得出他很不高興。"},{"w":"a veil of","p":"n.phr.","d":"a thin layer of something that covers or hides","c":"一層…；…的面紗","s":"The whole valley was covered by a veil of mist in the early morning, so we could not see the river below.","t":"清晨整個山谷被一層薄霧籠罩，所以我們看不到下面的河流。"},{"w":"unveil","p":"v.","d":"to show something new to the public for the first time; to remove a cover","c":"揭幕；公開","s":"The museum will unveil a newly discovered painting by the famous artist at a special ceremony next Friday.","t":"博物館將在下週五的特別儀式上公開那位著名畫家新發現的畫作。"},{"w":"velvet","p":"n.","d":"a soft, thick cloth that feels smooth on one side","c":"天鵝絨；絲絨","s":"The queen's long dress was made of deep red velvet, which looked soft and shone beautifully under the lights.","t":"女王的長禮服是用深紅色天鵝絨做的，看起來柔軟，在燈光下閃閃發亮。","h":1},{"w":"velvet","p":"adj.","d":"made of velvet","c":"天鵝絨的","s":"My grandmother keeps her old jewelry in a small velvet box that her mother gave her more than sixty years ago.","t":"我奶奶把她的舊首飾放在一個小絨布盒裡，那是她母親六十多年前送給她的。"},{"w":"velvety","p":"adj.","d":"soft and smooth like velvet","c":"柔軟光滑的","s":"This chocolate cake has a velvety texture that melts in your mouth, so it is the most popular dessert at the café.","t":"這個巧克力蛋糕有柔滑的口感，入口即化，所以是這家咖啡館最受歡迎的甜點。"},{"w":"versatile","p":"adj.","d":"able to do many different things well","c":"多才多藝的","s":"Our drama teacher is a versatile performer who can sing, dance, and play three musical instruments on stage.","t":"我們的戲劇老師是位多才多藝的表演者，能在台上唱歌、跳舞，還會演奏三種樂器。","h":1},{"w":"versatile","p":"adj.","d":"having many different uses","c":"多用途的；用途廣泛的","s":"A rice cooker is a surprisingly versatile machine, since you can use it to steam vegetables and even bake a simple cake.","t":"電鍋是一種出乎意料多用途的機器，你可以用它蒸蔬菜，甚至烤一個簡單的蛋糕。"},{"w":"versatility","p":"n.","d":"the ability to do many different things well","c":"多才多藝；多功能性","s":"The actress is famous for her versatility; she can make the audience laugh in one film and cry in the next.","t":"這位女演員以她的多才多藝聞名；她能在一部片裡讓觀眾大笑，在下一部裡讓他們落淚。"},{"w":"veterinarian","p":"n.","d":"a doctor who takes care of animals","c":"獸醫","s":"We took our cat to the veterinarian this morning because she had not eaten anything for two whole days.","t":"我們今天早上帶貓去看獸醫，因為她已經整整兩天沒吃東西了。","h":1},{"w":"vet","p":"n.","d":"a veterinarian (short form)","c":"獸醫（簡稱）","s":"The vet gave our puppy an injection and told us to keep him indoors for a week until he felt better.","t":"獸醫幫我們的小狗打了一針，並要我們讓牠待在室內一週，直到牠好起來。"},{"w":"veterinary","p":"adj.","d":"connected with the medical care of animals","c":"獸醫的","s":"My cousin is studying veterinary medicine at university because she has loved taking care of animals since she was little.","t":"我表妹在大學讀獸醫學，因為她從小就喜歡照顧動物。"},{"w":"vet","p":"v.","d":"to check someone or something carefully to make sure they are suitable","c":"審查；仔細檢查","s":"The school will carefully vet every volunteer who wants to work with the children during the summer camp.","t":"學校會仔細審查每一位想在夏令營期間和孩子們一起工作的志工。"},{"w":"veto","p":"n.","d":"the official power to refuse to allow something","c":"否決權；否決","s":"The president used his veto to stop the new law, so it was sent back to the lawmakers for more discussion.","t":"總統動用否決權阻止了新法案，所以法案被退回給立法者再做討論。","h":1},{"w":"veto","p":"v.","d":"to officially refuse to allow something","c":"否決","s":"My parents decided to veto my plan to travel alone during the winter vacation because they thought I was too young.","t":"我父母決定否決我寒假一個人去旅行的計畫，因為他們認為我年紀太小。"},{"w":"veto a bill","p":"v.phr.","d":"to refuse to sign a new law so that it cannot take effect","c":"否決法案","s":"The governor threatened to veto a bill that would raise taxes on small businesses, so the lawmakers rewrote it.","t":"州長威脅要否決那項會提高小企業稅負的法案，所以立法者重新修改了它。"},{"w":"vibrate","p":"v.","d":"to shake with small, fast movements","c":"震動；顫動","s":"My phone began to vibrate in my pocket during the movie, so I quietly went outside to answer the call.","t":"看電影時我的手機在口袋裡開始震動，所以我悄悄走到外面接電話。","h":1},{"w":"vibration","p":"n.","d":"a small, fast shaking movement","c":"震動；振動","s":"People living near the train station can feel a slight vibration in their floors every time a fast train passes by.","t":"住在火車站附近的人每次快車經過時，都能感覺到地板輕微的震動。","h":1},{"w":"vibrant","p":"adj.","d":"full of energy and life; very bright","c":"充滿活力的；鮮豔的","s":"The night market is one of the most vibrant places in the city, full of bright lights, loud music, and delicious smells.","t":"夜市是這座城市最充滿活力的地方之一，到處是明亮的燈光、響亮的音樂和美食的香味。"},{"w":"vice","p":"n.","d":"a bad habit or a moral weakness","c":"惡習；壞毛病","s":"Smoking is the only vice my grandfather has, and he has tried to give it up at least ten times.","t":"抽菸是我爺爺唯一的惡習，他已經試著戒了至少十次。","h":1},{"w":"vice president","p":"n.phr.","d":"the person next in rank below the president","c":"副總統；副總裁；副校長","s":"The vice president will lead the company's meeting today because the president is on a business trip to Japan.","t":"今天的公司會議將由副總裁主持，因為總裁到日本出差了。"},{"w":"vice versa","p":"phr.","d":"the other way around","c":"反之亦然","s":"My sister helps me with English, and vice versa, I help her with math whenever she has a test.","t":"我姐姐幫我學英文，反過來也一樣，每當她要考試時我就幫她學數學。"},{"w":"vicious","p":"adj.","d":"violent and cruel; very unkind","c":"兇惡的；惡毒的","s":"The vicious dog next door barks and shows its teeth at everyone who walks past the gate.","t":"隔壁那隻兇惡的狗對每個經過大門的人都狂吠並露出牙齒。"},{"w":"victor","p":"n.","d":"the person who wins a fight, game, or competition","c":"勝利者；贏家","s":"After a long and exciting match, the young player from Taiwan became the victor and lifted the gold cup high above her head.","t":"經過一場漫長又刺激的比賽，這位來自台灣的年輕選手成為勝利者，把金盃高高舉過頭頂。","h":1},{"w":"victory","p":"n.","d":"success in a fight, game, or competition","c":"勝利","s":"The team celebrated their first victory of the season by eating pizza together in the school cafeteria.","t":"球隊在學校餐廳一起吃披薩，慶祝本季的第一場勝利。"},{"w":"victorious","p":"adj.","d":"having won a fight, game, or competition","c":"勝利的；獲勝的","s":"The victorious soldiers marched through the city gates while thousands of people cheered and waved flags from the windows.","t":"獲勝的士兵們穿過城門行進，成千上萬的人在窗邊歡呼揮旗。"},{"w":"vigor","p":"n.","d":"physical or mental strength and energy","c":"活力；精力","s":"Even at eighty, my grandmother still works in her garden with great vigor, digging and planting from morning until noon.","t":"即使八十歲了，我奶奶仍然精力充沛地在花園裡工作，從早上挖土、種植到中午。","h":1},{"w":"vigorous","p":"adj.","d":"strong and full of energy; needing a lot of effort","c":"精力充沛的；劇烈的","s":"Doctors recommend thirty minutes of vigorous exercise, such as running or swimming, at least three times a week.","t":"醫生建議每週至少三次、每次三十分鐘的劇烈運動，例如跑步或游泳。","h":1},{"w":"vigorously","p":"adv.","d":"with a lot of energy or force","c":"用力地；精力充沛地","s":"The coach shook his head vigorously when the reporter asked whether the team would give up before the final game.","t":"當記者問球隊是否會在決賽前放棄時，教練用力地搖了搖頭。"},{"w":"villa","p":"n.","d":"a large, expensive house, often used for holidays","c":"別墅","s":"My uncle rented a villa with a private swimming pool in Bali, and our whole family stayed there for a week.","t":"我叔叔在峇里島租了一棟附私人游泳池的別墅，我們全家在那裡住了一個星期。","h":1},{"w":"village","p":"n.","d":"a very small town in the countryside","c":"村莊","s":"The small fishing village where my grandparents live has only one convenience store and no traffic lights at all.","t":"我祖父母住的那個小漁村只有一家便利商店，完全沒有紅綠燈。"},{"w":"villager","p":"n.","d":"a person who lives in a village","c":"村民","s":"Every villager came out to help put out the fire, carrying buckets of water from the well in the square.","t":"每個村民都出來幫忙滅火，從廣場的水井提來一桶桶的水。"},{"w":"villain","p":"n.","d":"the bad person in a story or film; a criminal","c":"反派；惡棍","s":"In most superhero movies, the villain wants to destroy the city, and the hero has to stop him before the final scene.","t":"在大多數的超級英雄電影裡，反派想毀滅城市，而英雄必須在最後一幕前阻止他。","h":1},{"w":"villainous","p":"adj.","d":"evil; like a villain","c":"邪惡的；惡棍般的","s":"The actor is so good at playing villainous characters that children are sometimes afraid of him when they see him in the street.","t":"這位演員非常擅長扮演邪惡的角色，小孩子在街上看到他有時會害怕。"},{"w":"hero","p":"n.","d":"a person who is admired for doing something brave or good","c":"英雄","s":"The firefighter who carried three children out of the burning building was called a hero by everyone in the neighborhood.","t":"那位從燃燒的大樓裡救出三個孩子的消防員，被附近所有人稱為英雄。"},{"w":"vine","p":"n.","d":"a climbing plant, especially the one that grapes grow on","c":"藤蔓；葡萄藤","s":"Grapes grow on a vine that climbs along a wooden frame, and farmers cut it back every winter to keep it healthy.","t":"葡萄長在沿著木架攀爬的葡萄藤上，農夫每年冬天都會修剪它以保持健康。","h":1},{"w":"vineyard","p":"n.","d":"a piece of land where grapes are grown for making wine","c":"葡萄園","s":"The vineyard on the hillside produces grapes for wine, and visitors can taste it in the small shop at the gate.","t":"山坡上的葡萄園生產釀酒用的葡萄，遊客可以在門口的小店品嚐。","h":1},{"w":"grapevine","p":"n.","d":"a grape plant; the informal way news spreads from person to person","c":"葡萄藤；小道消息","s":"I heard through the grapevine that our math teacher is getting married next month, but nobody has told us officially.","t":"我從小道消息聽說我們的數學老師下個月要結婚了，但沒有人正式告訴我們。"},{"w":"violinist","p":"n.","d":"a person who plays the violin","c":"小提琴家；小提琴手","s":"The young violinist played so beautifully that the audience stood up and clapped for five full minutes after her performance.","t":"這位年輕的小提琴家演奏得如此動人，表演結束後觀眾起立鼓掌了整整五分鐘。","h":1},{"w":"violin","p":"n.","d":"a wooden musical instrument with four strings that you play with a bow","c":"小提琴","s":"My sister has been learning the violin since she was six, and now she plays in the school orchestra.","t":"我妹妹從六歲起就開始學小提琴，現在她在學校管弦樂團裡演奏。"},{"w":"pianist","p":"n.","d":"a person who plays the piano","c":"鋼琴家","s":"The famous pianist began learning to play at the age of three and gave his first concert when he was only eight.","t":"這位著名的鋼琴家三歲開始學琴，八歲時就舉辦了第一場音樂會。"},{"w":"virgin","p":"adj.","d":"in its natural state; not yet used or touched by people","c":"未開發的；原始的","s":"The explorers walked for days through virgin forest where no human being had ever set foot before.","t":"探險家們在原始森林裡走了好幾天，那裡從來沒有人類踏足過。","h":1},{"w":"virgin","p":"n.","d":"a person who has never had sex; a young unmarried woman in old stories","c":"處女；少女","s":"The ancient temple was built to honor a goddess, and only a virgin was allowed to light its sacred fire each year.","t":"這座古廟是為了供奉女神而建，每年只有處女才被允許點燃它的聖火。"},{"w":"virgin olive oil","p":"n.phr.","d":"high-quality olive oil from the first pressing of the olives","c":"初榨橄欖油","s":"Italian chefs recommend using extra virgin olive oil for salads because it has a richer taste than ordinary cooking oil.","t":"義大利廚師建議做沙拉時使用特級初榨橄欖油，因為它比一般食用油味道更濃郁。"}]},{"unit":40,"theme":"vitality – zoom","cards":[{"w":"vitality","p":"n.","d":"energy and strength; the state of being full of life","c":"活力；生命力","s":"Even at the age of eighty, my grandmother is full of vitality, and she still swims in the pool every morning before breakfast.","t":"即使八十歲了，我奶奶仍然充滿活力，她每天早餐前還是會去泳池游泳。","h":1},{"w":"vital","p":"adj.","d":"very important or necessary","c":"極重要的；必要的","s":"Clean drinking water is vital to everyone's health, so the government must check the water supply regularly and carefully.","t":"乾淨的飲用水對每個人的健康極為重要，所以政府必須定期且仔細地檢查供水系統。"},{"w":"play a vital role","p":"v.phr.","d":"to be very important in something","c":"扮演重要角色","s":"Teachers play a vital role in shaping how children think, because students spend most of their waking hours at school.","t":"老師在塑造孩子的思考方式上扮演重要角色，因為學生大部分清醒的時間都在學校。"},{"w":"vitally","p":"adv.","d":"in a very important way","c":"極其；至關重要地","s":"It is vitally important that you back up your files, or you may lose months of work when the computer breaks down.","t":"備份你的檔案是極其重要的，否則電腦壞掉時你可能會失去好幾個月的工作成果。"},{"w":"vitamin","p":"n.","d":"a natural substance in food that your body needs to stay healthy","c":"維他命；維生素","s":"Oranges and kiwis are rich in vitamin C, so eating them often can help you fight off colds during the winter.","t":"柳橙和奇異果富含維他命C，所以常吃它們可以幫助你在冬天抵抗感冒。"},{"w":"vocation","p":"n.","d":"a job that you feel you are meant to do, especially one that helps people","c":"天職；使命感的職業","s":"Nursing is more than a job for Amy; it is her vocation, and she says helping sick people makes every long shift worthwhile.","t":"對艾咪來說，護理不只是一份工作，而是她的天職，她說幫助病人讓每一次漫長的值班都值得。","h":1},{"w":"vocational","p":"adj.","d":"connected with the skills you need for a particular job","c":"職業的；職業訓練的","s":"After junior high, my cousin chose a vocational school where he learns to repair cars instead of studying only textbooks.","t":"國中畢業後，我表哥選擇了一所職業學校，在那裡他學習修車，而不只是讀課本。","h":1},{"w":"vocational training","p":"n.phr.","d":"classes that teach the practical skills for a job","c":"職業訓練","s":"The city offers free vocational training for people who lost their jobs, so they can learn cooking, computer repair, or hairdressing.","t":"市政府為失業的人提供免費的職業訓練，讓他們可以學習烹飪、電腦維修或美髮。"},{"w":"vocal","p":"adj.","d":"connected with the voice; expressing opinions loudly","c":"聲音的；直言的","s":"The singer rests her voice for two days before every concert because her vocal cords get tired easily after long practice.","t":"這位歌手每次演唱會前都讓聲音休息兩天，因為長時間練習後她的聲帶很容易疲勞。"},{"w":"vocabulary","p":"n.","d":"all the words a person knows or uses","c":"字彙；詞彙","s":"Reading English novels every night helped Kevin build a large vocabulary, so he now understands movies without any subtitles.","t":"每晚讀英文小說幫助凱文累積了大量的字彙，所以他現在不用字幕就能看懂電影。"},{"w":"vowel","p":"n.","d":"one of the speech sounds or letters a, e, i, o, u","c":"母音","s":"English has only five vowel letters, but they can be pronounced in many different ways, which confuses many learners.","t":"英文只有五個母音字母，但它們可以有許多不同的發音，這讓很多學習者感到困惑。","h":1},{"w":"vowel sound","p":"n.phr.","d":"the sound made by a vowel","c":"母音發音","s":"The teacher asked us to listen carefully to the vowel sound in \"ship\" and \"sheep\" because the difference changes the meaning.","t":"老師要我們仔細聽 ship 和 sheep 裡的母音發音，因為這個差別會改變字義。"},{"w":"short vowel","p":"n.phr.","d":"a vowel sound that is said quickly, like the a in cat","c":"短母音","s":"In the word \"bit,\" the i is a short vowel, so you should say it quickly instead of stretching it out like the ee in \"beat.\"","t":"在 bit 這個字裡，i 是一個短母音，所以你應該唸得短促，而不是像 beat 裡的 ee 那樣拉長。"},{"w":"wag","p":"v.","d":"to move something, especially a tail, quickly from side to side","c":"搖（尾巴）；搖動","s":"Our dog starts to wag his tail as soon as he hears my father's car pull into the driveway every evening.","t":"每天傍晚，我們的狗一聽到爸爸的車開進車道，就開始搖尾巴。","h":1},{"w":"wag","p":"n.","d":"a quick movement from side to side","c":"搖動","s":"The puppy greeted every visitor with a happy wag of its tail, so nobody could stay angry at it for very long.","t":"小狗用開心的搖尾巴迎接每一位客人，所以沒有人能對它生氣太久。"},{"w":"wag one's finger","p":"v.phr.","d":"to move your finger from side to side to warn someone","c":"搖手指警告","s":"The librarian wagged her finger at the noisy boys and reminded them that other people were trying to study quietly.","t":"圖書館員對那些吵鬧的男孩搖手指警告，並提醒他們其他人正在安靜地讀書。","a":"wagged her finger"},{"w":"wag its tail","p":"v.phr.","d":"(of a dog) to move its tail to show happiness","c":"搖尾巴","s":"When the children came home from school, the little dog ran to the front door and wagged its tail with joy.","t":"孩子們放學回家時，小狗跑到前門，開心地搖尾巴。","a":"wagged its tail"},{"w":"walnut","p":"n.","d":"a hard brown nut that you can eat","c":"核桃","s":"My grandmother adds chopped walnuts to her banana bread, and the whole house smells wonderful while it is baking.","t":"我奶奶會在她的香蕉麵包裡加入切碎的核桃，烤的時候整個房子都香氣四溢。","a":"walnuts","h":1},{"w":"walnut","p":"n.","d":"the dark hard wood of the walnut tree, used for furniture","c":"胡桃木","s":"This walnut table has been in our family for three generations, and its dark wood still looks beautiful after all these years.","t":"這張胡桃木桌子在我們家已經傳了三代，它深色的木頭過了這麼多年看起來依然很美。"},{"w":"walnut tree","p":"n.phr.","d":"the tall tree that walnuts grow on","c":"核桃樹","s":"The old walnut tree in our backyard drops hundreds of nuts every autumn, so the squirrels are always busy there.","t":"我們後院那棵老核桃樹每年秋天都會掉下數百顆核桃，所以松鼠總是在那裡忙個不停。"},{"w":"ward","p":"n.","d":"a large room in a hospital where patients stay","c":"病房","s":"After the operation, Grandpa was moved to a quiet ward on the fifth floor, where we could visit him every afternoon.","t":"手術後，爺爺被移到五樓一間安靜的病房，我們每天下午都可以去探望他。","h":1},{"w":"children's ward","p":"n.phr.","d":"the part of a hospital where sick children stay","c":"兒童病房","s":"The nurses in the children's ward painted the walls with cartoon animals so that the young patients would feel less afraid.","t":"兒童病房的護士在牆上畫了卡通動物，好讓小病患不那麼害怕。"},{"w":"ward off","p":"v.phr.","d":"to keep something bad away from you","c":"避開；擋開","s":"Many people drink hot ginger tea in winter because they believe it helps to ward off colds and keep the body warm.","t":"許多人在冬天喝熱薑茶，因為他們相信它有助於擋開感冒並讓身體保暖。"},{"w":"warden","p":"n.","d":"a person in charge of a place, such as a prison or a hostel","c":"管理員；典獄長","s":"The warden of the youth hostel locks the front door at midnight, so remember to come back before then.","t":"青年旅館的管理員會在午夜鎖上大門，所以記得在那之前回來。"},{"w":"wardrobe","p":"n.","d":"a tall cupboard where you hang your clothes","c":"衣櫃","s":"There is not enough space in my wardrobe for winter coats, so I keep them in boxes under the bed until December.","t":"我的衣櫃沒有足夠的空間放冬天的大衣，所以我把它們裝在箱子裡放在床下直到十二月。","h":1},{"w":"wardrobe","p":"n.","d":"all the clothes that a person owns","c":"（個人的）全部衣物","s":"Before she started her new job at the bank, Linda bought a few jackets and skirts to update her wardrobe for the office.","t":"在銀行開始新工作之前，琳達買了幾件外套和裙子來更新她上班用的衣物。"},{"w":"built-in wardrobe","p":"n.phr.","d":"a wardrobe that is fixed to the wall of a room","c":"嵌入式衣櫃","s":"The new apartment has a built-in wardrobe in every bedroom, so we will not need to buy any large furniture for our clothes.","t":"新公寓每間臥室都有嵌入式衣櫃，所以我們不需要再買任何大型家具來放衣服。"},{"w":"warrant","p":"n.","d":"an official paper that allows the police to search a place or arrest someone","c":"搜索令；拘捕令","s":"The police officers could not enter the apartment without a search warrant, so they waited outside until the judge signed it.","t":"警察沒有搜索令不能進入那間公寓，所以他們在外面等到法官簽署為止。","h":1},{"w":"warrant","p":"v.","d":"to make something necessary or right; to deserve","c":"使…有正當理由；值得","s":"A small mistake like this does not warrant such an angry response; a quiet word with the student would have been enough.","t":"像這樣的小錯誤不值得如此生氣的反應；和那位學生平靜地談一下就夠了。","h":1},{"w":"warranty","p":"n.","d":"a written promise to repair or replace a product if it breaks within a certain time","c":"保固（單）","s":"The washing machine comes with a two-year warranty, so the company will repair it for free if anything goes wrong.","t":"這台洗衣機附有兩年保固，所以如果出了任何問題，公司會免費維修。"},{"w":"under warranty","p":"phr.","d":"still covered by the maker's promise to repair it","c":"在保固期內","s":"Luckily, my laptop was still under warranty when the screen stopped working, so the repair did not cost me a single dollar.","t":"幸運的是，我的筆電螢幕壞掉時還在保固期內，所以維修一毛錢都沒花。"},{"w":"extended warranty","p":"n.phr.","d":"extra protection you pay for so that the product is covered for a longer time","c":"延長保固","s":"The salesman tried to sell us an extended warranty for the TV, but we decided that the standard one-year protection was enough.","t":"銷售員試著向我們推銷電視的延長保固，但我們認為標準的一年保障就足夠了。"},{"w":"waterproof","p":"adj.","d":"not letting water pass through","c":"防水的","s":"Make sure your hiking boots are waterproof before the trip, because the trail crosses several streams and it may rain.","t":"出發前請確認你的登山鞋是防水的，因為路線會穿過好幾條小溪，而且可能會下雨。","h":1},{"w":"waterproof","p":"v.","d":"to treat something so that water cannot pass through it","c":"使防水","s":"Before the rainy season, my father will waterproof the roof of the garden shed so that his tools stay dry inside.","t":"在雨季來臨前，我爸爸會把花園工具間的屋頂做防水處理，讓他的工具在裡面保持乾燥。"},{"w":"waterproof jacket","p":"n.phr.","d":"a coat that keeps the rain out","c":"防水外套","s":"Pack a light waterproof jacket in your bag, since the weather in the mountains can change from sunshine to rain within an hour.","t":"在包包裡放一件輕便的防水外套，因為山上的天氣可能在一小時內從晴天變成下雨。"},{"w":"water-resistant","p":"adj.","d":"able to keep some water out, but not completely","c":"抗水的；防潑水的","s":"This watch is water-resistant, so it is fine in the rain, but you should still take it off before you go swimming.","t":"這支手錶是防潑水的，所以下雨時沒問題，但你游泳前還是應該把它拿下來。"},{"w":"weary","p":"adj.","d":"very tired, especially after working or traveling for a long time","c":"疲倦的；厭倦的","s":"After a twelve-hour flight and a long wait at the airport, the weary travelers just wanted a hot shower and a bed.","t":"經過十二小時的飛行和在機場漫長的等待後，疲倦的旅客們只想洗個熱水澡然後睡覺。","h":1},{"w":"weary of","p":"adj.phr.","d":"tired of something because it has gone on too long","c":"對…感到厭倦","s":"The workers grew weary of the same excuses from the manager, so they finally decided to write a letter to the company owner.","t":"工人們對經理一再重複的藉口感到厭倦，所以最後決定寫信給公司老闆。"},{"w":"weary","p":"v.","d":"to make someone tired; to become tired","c":"使疲倦；感到厭倦","s":"The endless noise of the big city began to weary her, so she moved to a small town by the sea last year.","t":"大城市無止盡的噪音開始讓她感到厭倦，所以她去年搬到了一個海邊的小鎮。"},{"w":"wearily","p":"adv.","d":"in a very tired way","c":"疲倦地","s":"The old farmer sat down wearily under the big tree after planting rice all morning in the hot summer sun.","t":"老農夫在炎熱的夏日太陽下插了整個早上的秧後，疲倦地坐在大樹下。"},{"w":"weariness","p":"n.","d":"the feeling of being very tired","c":"疲倦；倦意","s":"You could see the weariness on the doctors' faces after they had worked through the night during the emergency.","t":"在緊急狀況中工作了整夜之後，你可以從醫生們的臉上看到疲倦。"},{"w":"wharf","p":"n.","d":"a flat structure at the edge of the sea or a river where ships stop to load and unload","c":"碼頭","s":"Early in the morning, the fishing boats return to the wharf, and buyers from local restaurants wait there to choose the freshest fish.","t":"一大早，漁船回到碼頭，當地餐廳的買家在那裡等著挑選最新鮮的魚。","h":1},{"w":"wharves","p":"n.","d":"the plural form of wharf","c":"碼頭（複數）","s":"The old wharves along the river have been turned into cafés and shops, so the area is now popular with tourists on weekends.","t":"河邊的舊碼頭已經改建成咖啡館和商店，所以這個區域現在週末很受觀光客歡迎。"},{"w":"wharf worker","p":"n.phr.","d":"a person who loads and unloads ships at a wharf","c":"碼頭工人","s":"My uncle was a wharf worker for thirty years, and he says the job became much easier after big machines replaced human strength.","t":"我叔叔當了三十年的碼頭工人，他說自從大型機器取代人力之後，這份工作變得輕鬆多了。"},{"w":"whiskey","p":"n.","d":"a strong alcoholic drink made from grain","c":"威士忌","s":"My grandfather keeps a bottle of Scottish whiskey in the cabinet, but he only opens it on New Year's Eve with old friends.","t":"我爺爺在櫃子裡放了一瓶蘇格蘭威士忌，但他只在除夕夜和老朋友一起時才打開。","h":1},{"w":"whisky","p":"n.","d":"another spelling of whiskey, used in Scotland and Canada","c":"威士忌（英式拼法）","s":"In Scotland, the word whisky is spelled without an e, and the country is famous for making it in small towns.","t":"在蘇格蘭，威士忌這個字的拼法沒有 e，而這個國家以在小鎮釀造威士忌聞名。"},{"w":"a glass of whiskey","p":"n.phr.","d":"one serving of whiskey in a glass","c":"一杯威士忌","s":"The tired businessman ordered a glass of whiskey at the hotel bar and sat quietly looking at the rain outside the window.","t":"疲憊的商人在飯店酒吧點了一杯威士忌，安靜地坐著看窗外的雨。"},{"w":"wholesale","p":"adj.","d":"sold in large amounts to shops, not to the public","c":"批發的","s":"The restaurant buys its vegetables at wholesale prices from the market at dawn, which is why its dishes are so cheap.","t":"這家餐廳在清晨以批發價從市場買蔬菜，這就是為什麼它的菜這麼便宜。","h":1},{"w":"wholesale","p":"n.","d":"the business of selling goods in large amounts to shops","c":"批發","s":"My aunt works in wholesale, so she sells boxes of toys to shops rather than single items to customers.","t":"我阿姨從事批發業，所以她把整箱的玩具賣給商店，而不是把單件商品賣給顧客。"},{"w":"wholesaler","p":"n.","d":"a person or company that sells goods in large amounts to shops","c":"批發商","s":"The small bookshop orders new titles from a wholesaler every month and then sells them to readers in the neighborhood.","t":"這家小書店每個月向批發商訂購新書，然後賣給附近的讀者。"},{"w":"wholesale","p":"adv.","d":"in large amounts; on a large scale","c":"大批地；大規模地","s":"The company decided to change its old computers wholesale rather than replace them one at a time over several years.","t":"公司決定大批更換舊電腦，而不是花好幾年一台一台地換。"},{"w":"wholesome","p":"adj.","d":"good for your health","c":"有益健康的","s":"My mother believes that a wholesome breakfast of eggs, fruit, and whole-grain bread is the best start to a school day.","t":"我媽媽認為一份有雞蛋、水果和全麥麵包的健康早餐，是上學日最好的開始。","h":1},{"w":"wholesome","p":"adj.","d":"good for your character; not containing anything bad","c":"健康正面的；有益身心的","s":"The movie is wholesome family fun, so parents can watch it with their young children without worrying about violence.","t":"這部電影是健康正面的家庭娛樂，所以父母可以和年幼的孩子一起看，不用擔心有暴力內容。"},{"w":"whole","p":"adj.","d":"complete; all of something","c":"整個的；完整的","s":"We spent the whole afternoon cleaning the garage, and we still found boxes that nobody had opened in ten years.","t":"我們花了整個下午打掃車庫，而且還找到了十年來沒有人打開過的箱子。"},{"w":"on the whole","p":"phr.","d":"in general; considering everything","c":"大體上；總的來說","s":"There were a few problems with the hotel room, but on the whole, we enjoyed our holiday in Kenting very much.","t":"飯店房間有一些小問題，但總的來說，我們非常享受在墾丁的假期。"},{"w":"wholly","p":"adv.","d":"completely","c":"完全地","s":"The accident was wholly the fault of the driver who ran the red light, as the traffic camera clearly showed.","t":"正如交通監視器清楚顯示的，這場事故完全是那位闖紅燈駕駛的錯。"},{"w":"widow","p":"n.","d":"a woman whose husband has died and who has not married again","c":"寡婦","s":"Mrs. Lin became a widow at forty, and she raised her three children alone by running a small breakfast shop.","t":"林太太四十歲時成了寡婦，她靠經營一家小早餐店獨自撫養三個孩子。","h":1},{"w":"widower","p":"n.","d":"a man whose wife has died and who has not married again","c":"鰥夫","s":"After his wife passed away, the old widower learned to cook for himself and now invites neighbors over for dinner every Sunday.","t":"妻子過世後，這位年老的鰥夫學會了自己做飯，現在每個星期日都邀請鄰居來吃晚餐。"},{"w":"widowed","p":"adj.","d":"having lost your husband or wife through death","c":"喪偶的","s":"My widowed aunt moved in with us last year, and the house feels livelier now that she bakes cookies with my little sister.","t":"我喪偶的阿姨去年搬來和我們一起住，現在她會和我妹妹一起烤餅乾，家裡感覺更熱鬧了。"},{"w":"withhold, withheld, withheld","p":"v.","d":"to refuse to give something; to keep something back","c":"保留；拒絕給予；扣住","s":"The company may withhold part of your pay if you leave the job without giving two weeks' notice, so read the contract carefully.","t":"如果你離職時沒有提前兩週通知，公司可能會扣住你部分的薪水，所以要仔細閱讀合約。","a":"withhold","h":1},{"w":"withhold information","p":"v.phr.","d":"to keep facts secret from someone who should know them","c":"隱瞞資訊","s":"The witness was warned that it is a crime to withhold information from the police during a murder investigation.","t":"證人被警告，在謀殺案調查期間對警方隱瞞資訊是一種犯罪。"},{"w":"hold back","p":"v.phr.","d":"to stop yourself from showing a feeling; to keep something back","c":"抑制；保留","s":"She tried to hold back her tears at the graduation ceremony, but she cried when her best friend hugged her goodbye.","t":"她在畢業典禮上努力忍住淚水，但當最好的朋友抱著她道別時，她還是哭了。"},{"w":"woe","p":"n.","d":"great sadness or trouble","c":"悲痛；苦難","s":"The old song tells a tale of woe: a sailor loses his ship, his money, and finally the woman he loves.","t":"這首老歌講述一個悲傷的故事：一位水手失去了他的船、他的錢，最後還失去了他愛的女人。","h":1},{"w":"woes","p":"n.","d":"problems and troubles","c":"（複數）困境；麻煩","s":"The city's traffic woes got worse after the new shopping mall opened, and drivers now wait thirty minutes to cross the bridge.","t":"新購物中心開幕後，這座城市的交通困境變得更糟，駕駛現在要等三十分鐘才能過橋。"},{"w":"woeful","p":"adj.","d":"very bad or very sad","c":"悲慘的；糟糕的","s":"The team's woeful performance in the final game disappointed the fans, who had traveled for hours to support them.","t":"球隊在決賽中糟糕的表現讓球迷很失望，他們可是坐了好幾個小時的車來支持球隊。"},{"w":"woefully","p":"adv.","d":"very badly; to a very bad degree","c":"糟糕地；嚴重地","s":"The small clinic is woefully short of doctors, so patients sometimes wait a whole day before anyone can see them.","t":"這家小診所嚴重缺乏醫生，所以病人有時要等上一整天才有人幫他們看診。"},{"w":"woodpecker","p":"n.","d":"a bird with a strong beak that it uses to make holes in trees","c":"啄木鳥","s":"If you hear a fast knocking sound in the forest, look up, because a woodpecker is probably searching for insects inside the tree.","t":"如果你在森林裡聽到快速的敲擊聲，往上看，因為一隻啄木鳥可能正在樹裡尋找昆蟲。","h":1},{"w":"wood","p":"n.","d":"the hard material that trees are made of","c":"木頭；木材","s":"This table is made of real wood, which is why it is much heavier than the plastic one we had before.","t":"這張桌子是用真木頭做的，這就是為什麼它比我們以前那張塑膠桌重很多。"},{"w":"woods","p":"n.","d":"a small forest","c":"森林；林地","s":"We used to play hide-and-seek in the woods behind my grandparents' house, where tall pine trees blocked out the sun.","t":"我們以前常在爺爺奶奶家後面的林子裡玩捉迷藏，那裡高大的松樹遮住了陽光。"},{"w":"wooden","p":"adj.","d":"made of wood","c":"木製的","s":"My grandfather carved a small wooden horse for me when I was five, and I still keep it on my desk today.","t":"我五歲時爺爺幫我刻了一隻小木馬，到今天我還把它放在書桌上。"},{"w":"peck","p":"v.","d":"(of a bird) to hit or bite something with its beak","c":"（鳥）啄","s":"The chickens ran across the yard to peck at the rice my grandmother had thrown on the ground for them.","t":"雞群跑過院子去啄奶奶丟在地上給它們的米。"},{"w":"workforce","p":"n.","d":"all the people who work in a company or a country","c":"勞動力；全體員工","s":"Nearly half of the company's workforce now works from home two days a week, so the office feels much quieter than before.","t":"這家公司將近一半的員工現在每週有兩天在家工作，所以辦公室感覺比以前安靜多了。","h":1},{"w":"join the workforce","p":"v.phr.","d":"to start working for the first time","c":"進入職場","s":"Many young people join the workforce right after high school, while others go to university first and start working at twenty-two.","t":"許多年輕人高中畢業後就直接進入職場，而其他人則先上大學，二十二歲才開始工作。"},{"w":"workload","p":"n.","d":"the amount of work a person has to do","c":"工作量","s":"The nurses complained that their workload had doubled since two colleagues left, and nobody had been hired to replace them.","t":"護士們抱怨自從兩位同事離職後，她們的工作量翻了一倍，而且沒有人被聘來接替。"},{"w":"workplace","p":"n.","d":"the place where you work","c":"工作場所","s":"Smoking is not allowed anywhere in the workplace, so employees who smoke have to go outside the building during their breaks.","t":"工作場所內任何地方都不准吸菸，所以吸菸的員工休息時必須到大樓外面。"},{"w":"wrestle","p":"v.","d":"to fight by holding and trying to push someone to the ground","c":"摔角；扭打","s":"The two brothers like to wrestle on the living room carpet after dinner, and their mother always worries that something will break.","t":"兩兄弟喜歡晚餐後在客廳地毯上扭打，他們的媽媽總是擔心會有東西被打破。","h":1},{"w":"wrestle with","p":"v.phr.","d":"to struggle with a difficult problem or decision","c":"努力解決；苦思","s":"Sarah spent the whole weekend wrestling with the decision about whether to study abroad or stay close to her family.","t":"莎拉整個週末都在苦思要出國留學還是留在家人身邊的決定。","a":"wrestling with"},{"w":"wrestler","p":"n.","d":"a person who wrestles as a sport","c":"摔角選手","s":"The wrestler lifted his opponent high in the air and threw him onto the mat, and the crowd screamed with excitement.","t":"那位摔角選手把對手高高舉起，然後把他摔到墊子上，觀眾興奮地大叫。"},{"w":"wrestling","p":"n.","d":"the sport of fighting by holding and throwing your opponent","c":"摔角運動","s":"My little brother watches wrestling on TV every Saturday night, even though my mother says it is too violent for him.","t":"我弟弟每個星期六晚上都看電視上的摔角，雖然媽媽說那對他來說太暴力了。"},{"w":"wrinkle","p":"n.","d":"a small line in your skin, especially on your face, that appears as you get older","c":"皺紋","s":"My grandmother says every wrinkle on her face tells a story, so she has never wanted to hide them with makeup.","t":"我奶奶說她臉上的每一條皺紋都在訴說一個故事，所以她從來不想用化妝品遮住它們。","h":1},{"w":"wrinkle","p":"n.","d":"a small fold in cloth or paper","c":"皺褶","s":"Hang your shirt up as soon as it is dry, or it will be full of wrinkles by the time you want to wear it tomorrow.","t":"襯衫一乾就把它掛起來，否則明天你想穿的時候它會滿是皺褶。","a":"wrinkles"},{"w":"wrinkle","p":"v.","d":"to form small lines or folds","c":"起皺；使起皺","s":"Do not sit on your school uniform in the car, because the skirt will wrinkle easily and look messy at the ceremony.","t":"在車上不要坐在你的制服上，因為裙子很容易起皺，在典禮上會看起來很亂。"},{"w":"wrinkled","p":"adj.","d":"having many small lines or folds","c":"有皺紋的；皺巴巴的","s":"He arrived at the job interview in a wrinkled shirt, and the manager noticed it before he had even said hello.","t":"他穿著一件皺巴巴的襯衫去面試，經理在他還沒開口打招呼前就注意到了。"},{"w":"wrinkle-free","p":"adj.","d":"made so that it does not wrinkle","c":"免燙的；不易皺的","s":"This travel shirt is wrinkle-free, so you can pack it in a small bag for a week and still look neat at meetings.","t":"這件旅行襯衫是不易皺的，所以你可以把它塞在小包包裡一週，開會時看起來還是很整齊。"},{"w":"yearn","p":"v.","d":"to want something very much, especially something that is hard to get","c":"渴望；嚮往","s":"Living in a tiny apartment in the busy city, Jack began to yearn for the quiet green hills of his hometown.","t":"住在繁忙城市的小公寓裡，傑克開始嚮往家鄉那片安靜的綠色山丘。","h":1},{"w":"yearn for","p":"v.phr.","d":"to want something very much","c":"渴望得到；思念","s":"After three months in the hospital, the little boy yearned for his own bed, his dog, and his mother's home cooking.","t":"在醫院住了三個月後，小男孩渴望回到自己的床、見到他的狗，還有吃到媽媽做的飯。","a":"yearned for"},{"w":"yearn to","p":"v.phr.","d":"to wish strongly to do something","c":"渴望做…","s":"As a child, she yearned to see the ocean, and she finally saw it for the first time on a school trip at fifteen.","t":"小時候她渴望看到大海，十五歲那年她終於在學校旅行中第一次看到了海。","a":"yearned to"},{"w":"yearning","p":"n.","d":"a strong wish for something","c":"渴望；思念","s":"The old photographs filled him with a deep yearning for the friends he had lost touch with after graduation.","t":"那些老照片讓他心中充滿了對畢業後失去聯絡的朋友們深深的思念。"},{"w":"yoga","p":"n.","d":"a form of exercise that uses slow movements, stretching, and breathing","c":"瑜珈","s":"My mother does yoga for half an hour every morning, and she says it keeps her back strong and her mind calm.","t":"我媽媽每天早上做半小時瑜珈，她說這讓她的背部強健、心情平靜。","h":1},{"w":"yoga class","p":"n.phr.","d":"a lesson where people do yoga together","c":"瑜珈課","s":"I signed up for a yoga class at the community center, and the teacher showed us how to breathe slowly to relax.","t":"我在社區中心報名了一堂瑜珈課，老師教我們如何慢慢呼吸來放鬆。"},{"w":"yoga mat","p":"n.phr.","d":"a thin soft mat that you lie or stand on to do yoga","c":"瑜珈墊","s":"Remember to bring your own yoga mat to the lesson, because the studio only has a few extra ones for new students.","t":"記得帶你自己的瑜珈墊來上課，因為教室只有幾張多的給新學生用。"},{"w":"yogurt","p":"n.","d":"a thick, slightly sour food made from milk","c":"優格","s":"For breakfast, I usually mix plain yogurt with honey and fresh fruit, which is much healthier than sweet cereal.","t":"早餐我通常把原味優格和蜂蜜、新鮮水果混在一起，這比甜麥片健康多了。","h":1},{"w":"yoghurt","p":"n.","d":"the British spelling of yogurt","c":"優格（英式拼法）","s":"On British menus you will often see yoghurt spelled with an h, but it is exactly the same creamy food we eat at home.","t":"在英國的菜單上你常會看到優格拼成帶有 h 的拼法，但它和我們在家吃的綿密食物完全一樣。"},{"w":"frozen yogurt","p":"n.phr.","d":"a cold sweet dessert like ice cream, made from yogurt","c":"冷凍優格","s":"On hot summer afternoons, the frozen yogurt shop near our school is always crowded with students looking for something cool.","t":"炎熱的夏日午後，我們學校附近的冷凍優格店總是擠滿了想找涼爽東西吃的學生。"},{"w":"Greek yogurt","p":"n.phr.","d":"a thick type of yogurt with less water in it","c":"希臘優格","s":"Many athletes eat Greek yogurt after training because it is thick, filling, and has more protein than regular types.","t":"許多運動員訓練後會吃希臘優格，因為它濃稠、有飽足感，而且蛋白質比一般優格多。"},{"w":"zoom","p":"v.","d":"to move very fast","c":"飛馳；疾行","s":"Motorcycles zoom past our school gate every afternoon, so the teachers always remind us to look both ways before crossing.","t":"每天下午都有機車飛馳經過我們校門口，所以老師總是提醒我們過馬路前要左右看。","h":1},{"w":"zoom in","p":"v.phr.","d":"to make the picture on a camera or screen look bigger and closer","c":"放大（鏡頭／畫面）","s":"If you zoom in on the photo, you can clearly see the tiny bird sitting on the branch behind my sister.","t":"如果你把照片放大，就可以清楚看到我姊姊後面樹枝上停著的小鳥。"},{"w":"zoom out","p":"v.phr.","d":"to make the picture smaller so that it shows more of the area","c":"縮小（鏡頭／畫面）","s":"Zoom out on the map a little so that we can see where the train station is in relation to our hotel.","t":"把地圖稍微縮小一點，這樣我們就能看到火車站相對於我們飯店的位置。","a":"Zoom out"},{"w":"zoom","p":"v.","d":"(of prices or numbers) to rise very quickly","c":"飛漲；暴增","s":"House prices in the city have zoomed over the past five years, so many young couples can no longer afford to buy a home.","t":"這座城市的房價在過去五年飛漲，所以許多年輕夫妻再也買不起房子了。","a":"zoomed"},{"w":"zoom lens","p":"n.phr.","d":"a camera lens that can make far things look closer","c":"變焦鏡頭","s":"With a good zoom lens, you can take clear pictures of birds in the trees without getting close enough to scare them.","t":"有了好的變焦鏡頭，你可以拍到樹上鳥兒的清晰照片，而不必靠得太近把它們嚇跑。"}]}];
